window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":701,"title":"Chapter 701: 701, Bai Jingchen Passes Away (Two-in-One) [Thanks to Yi Meng «Shang Shang Qian» for the Great God Certification]","paragraphs":["Successfully capturing Zhao Weixiang meant that Liu Yutong’s trip abroad wasn’t a waste.","Without wasting any time, she brought Zhao Weixiang straight to the hotel where she was staying, planning to rest for the night and set off tomorrow.","Once everything here was handled, she’d likely head back to her home country soon.","Back at the hotel, Liu Yutong immediately dialed her sister Gao Min’s number.","“Sis, Zhao Weixiang has been caught,” she stated directly as soon as the call connected.","On the other end, Gao Min was instantly thrilled: “Really? You caught him for real? Little sis, you’re not playing with me, are you?”","“For real!” Liu Yutong replied.","“So... does he admit his guilt?”","“Whether he admits it or not doesn’t matter. Once we’re back home, we’ll find plenty of ways to make him talk. But sis, keep this under wraps for now. Someone just tried to kill Zhao Weixiang to silence him, and I’m not sure if they can confirm whether he’s dead yet. This has to stay secret!”","“You mean we should announce his death?”","“Exactly. I need you to temporarily hold back any news, just say we’re still investigating. I’ll release some ‘evidence’ that Zhao Weixiang is dead, so the people hiding in the shadows will let their guard down.”","“Okay, I understand!” Gao Min said.","“Sis... thank you. My dad has waited eleven years, and so have I. Now we finally have a lead,” she said, her voice emotional.","“Sis, this isn’t just for our dad. Every single criminal—I won’t let any of them get away!” Liu Yutong declared.","“I’ll be waiting for you to come back! Together, we’ll bring them all to justice.”","“Good!” Liu Yutong replied.","“...”","After hanging up, Liu Yutong turned to face Yun Cheng.","“Yun Cheng, find a few trustworthy foreign-looking people and contact some underground tabloids and online forums—the kind that publish anything for money, no questions asked.”","Yun Cheng paused in surprise, then asked, “What news do you want to spread, Miss?”","Liu Yutong said: “Spread the word that Zhao Weixiang, a wanted fugitive from the Dragon Kingdom who fled overseas, got himself killed in a gang shootout in Los Angeles. Have Zhao Weixiang cooperate by taking a few ‘corpse’ photos to back it up.”","Yun Cheng nodded: “I’ll handle it right away. Should I spice it up with a story? Like he owed gambling debts and was hunted down by a gang?”","Liu Yutong: “Sure, the more cliché, the better. The more it fits people’s expectations of how a fugitive meets his end, the more convincing.”","“Also, have Jess spread some talk in his circle. Say there was some unlucky guy from the Dragon Kingdom who pissed off the wrong people and got dumped in the ocean. But don’t mention Zhao Weixiang’s name directly—let them guess and gossip on their own.”","“Understood!” Yun Cheng acknowledged, turning to leave.","But Liu Yutong suddenly remembered something and called him back: “Wait, Zhao Weixiang’s in a fragile state right now. Find a couple of people to watch him, and make sure he doesn’t try to kill himself.”","“Got it!” Yun Cheng said.","After Yun Cheng left, Liu Yutong stood alone by the window, staring out at the view.","Things were going smoothly in the States. Ordinarily, she should be happy, but for some reason, a sense of unease gnawed at her, as if something big was about to happen.","Ring, ring, ring~","Just then, her phone suddenly rang.","The unexpected noise made her heart jump.","And when she saw the caller ID—Bai Shisui—that bad feeling only grew stronger.","The moment she answered, she heard Bai Shisui’s heart-wrenching sobs.","\"Yutong... my dad... my dad... waaah...\"","Liu Yutong’s heart sank instantly. She quickly asked, \"What happened to Uncle Bai?\"","\"He’s gone... the doctor announced it ten minutes ago. Mom and my uncles are already discussing the funeral arrangements, but I... I don’t know what to do...\" Bai Shisui couldn’t stop sobbing on the other end of the line.","Liu Yutong closed her eyes. Even though she had mentally prepared herself, hearing the news still sent a sharp pang through her heart. It was an incredibly bitter feeling.","The elder who used to tie on an apron in the kitchen and kindly serve steamed buns with a smile. The chamber of commerce president who insisted on rescuing fellow countrymen in a foreign land. The helm of the Bai Group. In the end, he hadn’t managed to pull through; he was gone.","\"Shisui, I’m coming back right now. Until I get there, don’t agree to anything, don’t sign anything. Got it?\"","\"I... I remember... but my uncles say we have to follow the company’s articles of association and Dad’s will. They seem to have already contacted the lawyers.\"","A cold glint flashed in Liu Yutong’s eyes. \"Let them contact the lawyers. Shisui, your father’s body isn’t even cold yet, and some people can’t wait. Wait until I get back.\"","After hanging up, Liu Yutong immediately called Su Mansu. \"Prepare the plane. We’re going to San Francisco. Now!\"","\"Yes, boss!\"","The good thing about the States was the abundance of small planes and airports, and as long as you had the money, you could fly whenever you wanted.","Soon! Liu Yutong and her Wanlong Society entourage landed in San Francisco.","..........","San Francisco, Chinatown.","The news of Bai Jingchen’s death sent shockwaves through the Chinese community. Not only was there an undercurrent of turmoil within the Bai Group itself, but the entire overseas Chinese business circle could sense a gathering storm.","The Chinese Chamber of Commerce’s weekly meeting, originally scheduled for next week, had been moved up to the day after Bai Jingchen’s passing. The stated reason was to discuss the late president’s affairs and the chamber’s future development.","But anyone with a keen eye knew the real agenda of this meeting was only one thing—electing a new president.","As the chamber’s largest sponsor and driving force, Bai Jingchen’s death inevitably created a power vacuum. Whoever succeeded him would become a key figure shaping the future of the overseas Chinese business circle in San Francisco—and possibly even across the entire United States.","Overseas, when fighting for market share and establishing a foothold, many Chinese expats and their descendants naturally banded together to form alliances like chambers of commerce.","And this chamber held vast resources. Becoming its president came with undeniable benefits, and the title itself represented leadership in the business world. Whether for fame or fortune, there was no reason not to compete for it.","The meeting was held at Longteng Restaurant in Chinatown.","Outside the restaurant, news media vans had lined up early. Bai Jingchen’s high standing in both the local business and overseas Chinese communities made his death and the question of his successor media focal points.","On the second floor, in the largest banquet hall, more than thirty people sat around the long conference table. They were all members of the chamber’s board—business owners, community leaders, and neighborhood representatives.","The main seat remained empty. That was Bai Jingchen’s seat.","To the left of it sat Bai Shisui and her mother Zhou Meizhen, while Bai Shisui’s uncle Zhou Yan sat directly across from them.","Zhou Yan was wearing a dark gray suit today, his hair slicked back meticulously, and he was smiling as he chatted with a few business owners beside him about trade matters. On the same row were two middle-aged men, both members of the Zhou family, holding high positions in the Bai Group.","To the right of the main seat sat a few other influential business veterans from the chamber of commerce. Among them, two stood out the most. One was Old Master Li, with silver hair and leaning on a cane, over seventy years old—a highly respected figure in the Chinese community. The other was a man under forty named Zeng Jin, who had built his fortune in import-export trade, running a substantial business and representing the younger faction within the chamber.","The meeting had yet to begin, but murmurs of discussion never ceased.","“President Bai’s departure was so sudden... Ah, good people don’t get good rewards.”","“I heard he was shot twice—it’s already a miracle he held on for so many days.”","“Was the killer caught?”","“According to the news, it was the Snakehead Gang. They’ve all been arrested now.”","“Good, that’s some comfort for President Bai’s soul in heaven!”","“Those gangsters deserve to die!”","“Now that President Bai has passed, who do you think will take over his position?”","“It should be Miss Bai, right? After all, she’s the legitimate heir.”","“Could also be Mrs. Bai.”","“I’m not so sure. I think Zhou Yan’s stance today is that he wants to succeed President Bai.”","“Zhou Yan? I think he falls short—he’s not a blood relative by surname.”","“So what if he’s not a blood relative? He’s still her biological uncle!”","“I heard that before his death, President Bai intended to transfer part of his shares to an unrelated outsider.”","“Really? Who?”","“Not sure, but the Zhou family definitely won’t be happy about it. Look at the two Bai Group executives Zhou Yan brought today—both are his own family. That says a lot.”","“And the presidency? Is he going to aim for that too?”","“Hard to tell. There are plenty of people eyeing the chamber’s presidency. Zeng Jin is no pushover either—he has support from the Taiwan Province chamber of commerce and some Fujian merchants. He’s very strong.”","Just then, Zhou Yan looked at his watch, cleared his throat, and said, “Everyone, it’s about time. Master Li, shall we begin?”","Old Master Li slowly opened his eyes and nodded. “Let’s begin. President Bai’s departure was sudden. We’re gathered here today for two reasons: to mourn President Bai and to discuss the chamber’s next steps. Let’s first hear a few words from Mrs. Bai.”","Zhou Meizhen wiped the corner of her eyes, stood up, and gave a speech: “Thank you all for coming today. My husband spent his entire life working for the chamber and for our compatriots, only to end up like this. I only hope the chamber can continue his unfinished work and help more people in need.”","She broke down crying as she spoke, and Zhou Yan quickly rushed over to comfort her. “Sister, accept your loss! Brother-in-law’s spirit in heaven would surely want the chamber, you, and Suisui to be well.”","Zhou Meizhen nodded and sat down.","Zhou Yan then took a stance next to the main seat, not sitting, but his position made many things clear.","“Everyone, my brother-in-law’s case is still under police investigation. I believe the truth will come out. But our Chinese chamber of commerce cannot be left without a leader.”","\"According to the chamber's bylaws, if the chairman passes away unexpectedly, the vice-chairman should serve as acting chairman and hold a new election within one month. Elder Li is the honorary chairman, and President Zeng is the vice-chairman, so by rights, President Zeng should act as chairman temporarily. However, President Zeng has been very busy with business lately, and besides...\"","He paused for a moment, then turned to look at Zeng Jin: \"President Zeng, you mentioned before that you weren't very interested in the chairman position, correct?\"","Everyone's gaze shifted to Vice-Chairman Zeng Jin.","Zeng Jin gave a faint smile. \"President Zhou has an excellent memory. I did say that I'm more skilled at business and not very adept at administrative matters. But then again, these are unusual times. Chairman Bai has just passed away, and everyone inside and outside the chamber is watching us. If we elect someone without enough authority, I'm afraid it'll be difficult to command respect.\"","His words were practically a clear statement to everyone that he would also be running, and that he didn't think highly of Zhou Yan's chances.","The smile on Zhou Yan's face remained unchanged. \"I welcome President Zeng's candidacy. But given the urgency of the situation, I've already discussed it with several board members in advance, and they suggested that I serve as acting chairman to oversee the upcoming election. I've worked at the Bai Group for over a decade and am very familiar with chamber affairs. Most importantly, I'm now the head of the Bai Group. Forty percent of the chamber's annual operating funds come from donations by the Bai Group. Having me as acting chairman will ensure the chamber's funding doesn't dry up and projects don't stall. What does everyone think?\"","\"Of course, once things settle down, we'll hold a proper election for a new chairman.\"","The hall erupted in murmurs.","\"The head of the Bai Group? Has Chairman Bai's will been made public?\"","\"I haven't heard anything...\"","\"Is Zhou Yan trying to seize control?\"","Elder Li furrowed his brow. \"President Zhou, you say you're now the head of the Bai Group. Do you have Chairman Bai's will to prove it? If not, Mrs. Bai and Miss Bai, as his direct relatives, seem more suited for that role, don't you think?\"","Zhou Yan was well-prepared. He pulled a document from his briefcase. \"Elder Li, this is a copy of my brother-in-law's will. Everyone can take a look. He designated an executor for his estate, but regarding company management, it clearly states that in the event he is unable to fulfill his duties, I am to act as interim manager until my niece is capable of taking over.\"","He deliberately skipped over the part about transferring shares to Liu Yutong. That agreement was still with the lawyer, and as long as Bai Shisui didn't sign to confirm it, there was room to maneuver.","Several board members passed the will copy around, discussing it among themselves.","Zeng Jin glanced at the will briefly, a subtle shift in his expression, but he said nothing.","Zhou Yan seized the momentum. \"I know some might think I'm taking advantage of this crisis, but I swear to heaven that everything I'm doing is for the good of my sister and my niece. Bai Shisui is still young. The business world is a battlefield. How could a young girl like her handle it? I'll first help stabilize the situation for her, and once she matures, I will naturally hand everything back to her. Everyone here has watched her grow up. Would you really be willing to see her bullied by the wolves and tigers out there?\"","His words, spoken with such sincerity, combined with Zhou Meizhen quietly weeping beside him, indeed moved quite a few people.","\"President Zhou does make some sense.\"","\"Miss Bai is still too young.\"","\"But letting Zhou Yan serve as acting chairman—doesn't that bind the chamber to the Bai Group? Won't the chamber become Zhou's personal fiefdom in the future?\"","\"Then who do you suggest? Zeng Jin? Can we really trust him with those people from the Taiwanese Provincial Chamber behind him?\"","“Exactly!”","“It seems making Zhou Yan the acting chairman might be the safest choice for now...”","“.........”","Zhou Yan watched the room’s sentiment gradually sway in his favor, the smirk on his lips growing more pronounced. He was certain of victory. Control of the Bai Group, along with the future position of chamber president, were all but in his grasp.","“Everyone, since there are no objections, I shall—”","He had barely spoken halfway.","Boom!","The banquet hall’s door flew open with a kick, slamming against the wall with a thunderous crash.","Everyone in the hall jolted in fright and turned as one.","There, at the entrance, stood a long, slender silhouette. She wore a black trench coat, and on her left chest gleamed a golden dragon badge. Behind her were dozens of young men in black, each standing tall and sharp-eyed, framing her like a queen emerging from the darkness.","A faint smile curved her lips as she said:","“I object!”"]},{"number":702,"title":"Chapter 702: 702, I Have the Final Say in Everything (Two-in-One) [Thank you to the handsome uncle for the gift]","paragraphs":["\"I object!\"","At those words, the entire venue fell into dead silence. Everyone's gaze focused on the young woman standing at the doorway, dressed in a black trench coat and exuding an overwhelming presence.","Behind her stood dozens of men in black, several of whom were particularly striking.","One was a giant over two meters tall, like a door god, his appearance incredibly intimidating.","There were also two cold-faced young men—one with his hands casually in his pockets, the other scanning the crowd in the meeting hall with sharp eyes, like a wolf spotting a flock of sheep.","Just these three alone gave off an aura of being an unstoppable force!","Zhou Yan froze for a moment. When he recognized the girl he had seen at the hospital a few days ago, he erupted in fury: \"Miss Liu, this is an internal meeting of our chamber of commerce. Who allowed you to barge in here? Security! Where the hell are the security guards?\"","Outside, the few guards originally stationed at the entrance were being pinned firmly against the wall by the men in black, unable to move.","Liu Yutong completely ignored Zhou Yan's roar. She walked straight in, reached the conference table, and fixed her gaze directly on Old Mr. Li, who was seated beside the head of the table.","\"Old Li, Uncle Bai's body is still warm, and you're already rushing to elect a new president?\"","Old Mr. Li's hand, resting on his cane, trembled slightly. \"Who... who are you? This follows the chamber's bylaws. It seems to have nothing to do with an outsider like you, does it?\"","\"You say I'm an outsider? Heh...\"","Liu Yutong let out a soft, crisp laugh. The sound was clear and pleasant, yet for some reason, it sent an inexplicable chill down everyone's spines.","She said nothing more and walked straight toward the head seat that had belonged to Bai Jingchen.","Yun Cheng immediately stepped forward and pulled out the chair for her.","Liu Yutong didn't even glance at him. She turned and sat down gracefully, crossing her legs in one smooth motion.","The action was so natural, as if she had always belonged in that seat.","Smack!","Zhou Yan slammed the table, his face dark as iron. \"Liu Yutong, you're going too far! That's the president's seat. What gives you the right to sit there?\"","The others in the hall began to stir.","\"Too arrogant.\"","\"Who is this girl, anyway?\"","\"Even Old Mr. Li hasn't sat in that chair, and she just takes it.\"","\"Zhou Yan called her Liu Yutong. Who the hell is she? Has anyone heard of her?\"","\"...\"","Although the crowd was unhappy with Liu Yutong's actions, no one dared to openly accuse her. After all, those bodyguards behind her and the swarm of men in black outside were too terrifying—just looking at them sent a chill down your spine.","Bai Shisui's mother, Zhou Meizhen, also had her expression gradually change.","She had originally felt some goodwill toward Liu Yutong, thinking this young woman was accomplished at an early age and someone her late husband had valued.","But what was unfolding before her now made her feel that Liu Yutong was too domineering and utterly lacking in manners.","\"Miss Liu, this is an important chamber meeting. Is it really appropriate for you to be here? If you need to talk to Shisui, you can wait until after the meeting ends...\"","Liu Yutong looked at Zhou Meizhen, her gaze calm as still water. \"Mrs. Bai, I'm not here to see Shisui.\"","She paused, then added: \"I'm here to settle some accounts.\"","Settle accounts?","Everyone was taken aback.","Could it be that someone owed her money?","\"Damn, if someone owes money and doesn't pay, forcing the creditor to come knocking, that's the worst kind of scum,\" they cursed inwardly, glancing again at the men in black outside, who looked more like gangsters than actual gangsters.","Zhou Yan couldn't help but shout, \"Settle what accounts? Who here owes you money? Liu Yutong, I'm warning you—don't make trouble here! This is the U.S.! A society governed by law! You're trespassing on a private meeting, and I can call the cops to have you arrested!\"","Liu Yutong looked at him and made a \"go ahead\" gesture. \"Be my guest! If you want to call the police, go right ahead.\"","Zhou Yan: \"You...\"","Old Mr. Li leaned on his cane and stood up. \"Miss Liu, if anyone here owes you money, you can take it up with them privately. Please stop causing a disturbance here.\"","Liu Yutong uncrossed her long legs, sat up straight, and said seriously, \"Old Li, you're wronging me. I'm not here to cause trouble. I really am here to attend this meeting.\"","Old Mr. Li: \"But as far as I know, you don't seem to be a member of our chamber, so you...\"","\"Who says I'm not?\" Liu Yutong cut him off.","At that, the crowd exchanged bewildered glances and shook their heads, as if none of them knew anything about Liu Yutong joining the chamber.","Liu Yutong didn't keep them in suspense and revealed the truth.","\"Uncle Bai gave me thirty percent of the shares in the Bai Corporation before he died. That makes me the second-largest shareholder. So tell me—do I have the right to attend this meeting?\"","Boom!","The hall erupted instantly.","\"Thirty percent of the shares?\"","\"President Bai really gave shares to an outsider?\"","\"That can't be possible, right?\"","\"Sounds crazy. Thirty percent of the Bai Corporation is worth at least two billion dollars!\"","\"But look at the Bai family's faces—they don't look too good. Could it be true?\"","\"...\"","All kinds of speculation broke out.","Zhou Yan's face turned completely dark. \"Miss Liu, that agreement hasn't gone through final notarization and registration yet. Its legal validity is still open to question. Besides, what we're discussing now is the election of the chamber's president, not the equity issue of the Bai Corporation.\"","\"Mr. Zhou, you seem to be misunderstanding something.\"","Liu Yutong tilted her head slightly, a strand of hair sliding across her cold, sharp profile. Her clear, beautiful eyes held an undeniable dominance.","\"I'm sitting here to tell you the outcome, not to listen to your discussion!\"","\"Uncle Bai's matters—I have the final say! The future of the Bai Corporation—I have the final say! As for who has the final say in this chamber today...\"","Her gaze slowly swept across the faces of everyone seated. Those whose eyes met hers instinctively lowered their heads.","\"I have the final say!\"","\"Are we clear?\"","The hall was dead silent. No one dared to make a sound; they could only think to themselves, This girl is way too domineering!","Zhou Yan's face had turned the color of pickled pork liver, practically trembling with rage.","So arrogant!","She completely disregarded them!","Seeing everyone's reaction, Liu Yutong seemed satisfied.","\"Good. It looks like everyone understands.\"","\"Before we elect a new president, let me share a piece of news with you. The Snakehead Gang, which murdered President Bai, has been completely wiped out by me.\"","\"Of course, I'm not sure if you saw the news, so I'll just fill you in on the result.\"","At this, everyone was stunned. They couldn't believe their ears.","\"What? The Snakehead Gang was taken down by Miss Liu?\"","\"But didn't the news say the police did it?\"","\"Wait... I think I heard from some underground connections that they pissed off a woman known as the Black Phoenix from the East. She brought along the Hell Giant, the Black and White Devils—those deadly enforcers—and bulldozed them all. The cops were just there to clean up the mess.\"","\"Black Phoenix? Could it be...\"","\"...\"","As they talked about these nicknames, someone unconsciously looked toward the door at the giant of a man standing there like a guardian spirit, wondering how he perfectly fit the description of that hellish giant.","Then, the crowd turned their terrified gazes to Liu Yutong, seated at the head of the table. Could she be...?","Zeng Jin’s expression shifted as well. He had indeed heard a rumor that the Snakehead Gang was actually wiped out by a person nicknamed the Black Phoenix, and the police had only come to clean up the mess.","The Snakehead Gang had entrenched itself in the United States for years. The Chamber of Commerce had tried to crack down on them and had reported them to the police, but they still thrived, growing even bolder—even daring to assassinate President Bai.","Now, that gang had been completely taken down in a single night.","If these rumors were true, then the woman before them possessed terrifying power!","Zhou Yan’s heart was pounding. He had heard this rumor too, and especially recalling the secret actions he had arranged, his fear intensified.","Still, he stiffened his spine and said, “Ridiculous! Miss Liu, are you making up this lie just to polish your own image? Do you think everyone here is a three-year-old? The Snakehead Gang has been entrenched in the U.S. for years; the police have raided them countless times and they still came out fine. And you, an outsider, claim you wiped them out overnight? Absolutely absurd!”","Liu Yutong chuckled lightly. “Whether it’s true or not, Mr. Zhou knows better than anyone in his heart.”","“Besides, now that the Snakehead Gang is gone, it’s a dead-end for evidence. Isn’t that right?”","Zhou Yan’s heart skipped another beat, but he feigned ignorance. “What are you talking about? I don’t understand. Are you suggesting I was in league with the Snakehead Gang?”","On the surface, he said this, but inside, he was panicking.","Could this woman have actually found something?","Impossible.","They had been extremely discreet; it shouldn’t have been exposed. She was just trying to bluff him.","Yes! That had to be it!","As the scene grew increasingly chaotic and loud, Old Man Li tapped his cane heavily on the floor and spoke again: “Miss Liu, you claim to hold thirty percent of the Bai Group’s shares. I really want to believe you, but without seeing the evidence, I must still ask you to leave—even if it costs me my life!”","The old man had backbone. Among the crowd, aside from a guilty Zhou Yan, he was the only one daring enough to confront her despite the black-suited men outside.","“Old Man Li wants evidence; then I’ll give you that courtesy.”","Liu Yutong sat down again, crossing her legs, and looked toward Bai Shisui.","“Sui Sui.”","Bai Shisui trembled. “Sister Yutong.”","“What’s your surname?” Liu Yutong asked.","“I... my surname is Bai,” Bai Shisui answered instinctively.","“Yes, the Bai of Bai Jingchen.”","Liu Yutong’s gaze swept over Zhou Yan and the two Zhou family executives beside him.","“In this room, besides you, who else truly carries the surname Bai?”","“Your father built the Bai Group from scratch, making it bear his name. Now that his body is barely cold, the people here clamoring to take over the company and the Chamber of Commerce—do any of them have the surname Bai?”","“Zhou Yan, Mr. General Manager, what’s your surname?”","“And you two—what are your surnames?”","She pointed her finger one by one at each person. Every time she pointed, the victims’ faces turned paler.","Finally, she looked at the grim-faced Zhou Meizhen, paused for a moment, but ultimately didn’t ask her.","Liu Yutong’s words were straightforward: she wanted to awaken Bai Shisui with this simple truth—she was the only one present who shared her father’s surname.","They were indeed blood relatives, but in reality, as long as the surname was different, they were ultimately outsiders!","Gradually, a terrifying thought that Bai Shisui had never dared to entertain emerged uncontrollably.","If her father were alive, the Bai Group would always carry the Bai name.","If he were gone, and power fell into her uncle’s hands, in a few years... would it still be surnamed Bai?","As for Liu Yutong, though she was also an outsider, Bai Shisui had already made enough profit from investing with her to almost buy thirty percent of the Bai Group’s shares.","From that perspective, Liu Yutong was far more trustworthy than the Zhou family.","Seeing the situation rapidly deteriorate, with Liu Yutong’s few words shaking Bai Shisui’s resolve, Zhou Yan knew that if Bai Shisui actually acknowledged the share transfer, things would become a huge mess.","With this woman around, they would only face endless trouble. He couldn’t let her keep talking!","“Liu Yutong, stop spreading your lies here and driving a wedge in our family relationships!”","“Sis! Sui Sui! Don’t listen to her! Sui Sui, I’m your own uncle—how could I harm you? Everything I do is to keep the Bai Group out of outsiders’ hands, for the sake of your and Sis’s future. This woman is the real outsider! She’s the one coveting the Bai family’s property!”","The two Zhou executives chimed in, “Mr. Zhou is right—she’s the outsider, the one with wolfish ambition!”","“...”","But no matter how much they tried to smear Liu Yutong, she acted as if she hadn’t heard, simply gazing quietly at Bai Shisui, waiting for her answer.","Bai Shisui took a deep breath, stood up, and looked at her mother and uncle. “Mom, Uncle, I believe in Dad’s choice.”","“Before he died, Dad did say he would transfer thirty percent of the Bai Group’s shares to Sister Yutong as the basis for our cooperation. The intent agreement and signed documents are all with my lawyer.”","Boom!","Those words exploded like thunder in the banquet hall.","“So there really is a share transfer—Miss Bai just admitted it herself!”","“No way! Shares worth two billion U.S. dollars, just given away like that? President Bai really trusted Miss Liu that much?”","“Then everything Miss Liu said is true. She really is the second-largest shareholder of the Bai Group!”","“That means she does qualify to participate in this meeting—even more so than Zhou Yan.”","“...”","Zhou Yan’s face went completely pale. He rushed forward and grabbed Bai Shisui’s arm. “Sui Sui, you’ve lost your mind! That’s thirty percent of the shares—worth two billion dollars! How could you admit to this? She’s an outsider, here to steal our Bai family’s assets!”","Bai Shisui shook him off forcefully. “Uncle, Sister Yutong is not an outsider! My father trusted her, and I trust her. Besides, it was my father’s decision. I have no right to deny it!”","“You!” Zhou Yan fumed, heartbroken.","Zhou Meizhen grew anxious too. “Sui Sui, listen to me—these shares cannot be given to an outsider. Your father must have been confused when he made that decision. We can simply refuse to acknowledge it!”","“Mom!”","Bai Shisui looked at her mother with disappointment in her eyes. “Dad discussed this with me before. He said Sister Yutong has the ability to lead the Bai Group further. And before this, any money I made investing with her had already nearly bought me these thirty percent of the shares. She had no need to deceive me!”","“You’re just a young girl. What do you know about investing? That was all luck,” Zhou Meizhen scoffed, refusing to believe it.","A nearby vice-director with the surname Zhou chimed in to back him up: “Shuisui, you can’t be fooled by outsiders. Your uncle truly has your best interests and the Bai Group at heart. Miss Liu probably just sweet-talked you to get you on her side, only to swallow up the entire Bai Group later.”","“Exactly! We’ve been loyal to Chairman Bai for years. You can’t let a stranger deceive you.”","Bai Shisui looked at these Zhou family members, their faces flushed with urgency, and suddenly felt a clarity dawn on her.","They kept saying it was for her and the Bai Group, but from start to finish, all they cared about was power and profit.","Her father had just passed away, and instead of focusing on his funeral arrangements properly, they were rushing to seize control. Now they were desperately trying to block the decisions he made before his death—ultimately, weren’t they just afraid that if she and Sister Yutong joined forces, it would cut off their revenue stream?","“Enough!”","Bai Shisui cut them off. “This was my father’s decision, and I won’t change it! Sister Yutong is a shareholder of the Bai Group, and no one can deny that!”","......"]},{"number":703,"title":"Chapter 703: 703, A Slap (Thank You, Tianwei Yuedu, for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["The entire room fell silent in an instant.","No one had expected that this seemingly indecisive young woman would so firmly defend an outsider, even going against her mother and the relatives from her maternal uncle's family.","Upon hearing this, Old Master Li said in a deep voice, \"Since Miss Bai has personally acknowledged it, I recognize Miss Liu's status as a shareholder. According to the chamber of commerce's bylaws, the Bai Group, as a core enterprise of the chamber, and its second-largest shareholder are entitled to participate in chamber affairs. Miss Liu, you may stay.\"","With Old Master Li's approval, the other directors nodded in agreement one after another.","\"Old Li is right; Miss Liu is qualified to stay.\"","\"Since it's President Bai's decision, we respect it.\"","\"Now we should properly discuss the candidate for president.\"","\"........\"","Liu Yutong, seated in the main chair, looked at Bai Shisui with a hint of relief in her eyes.","This girl still had some judgment, able to discern who truly had her best interests at heart and stood by her side.","Zeng Jin, the vice president, immediately seized the opportunity and said, \"Director Liu keeps a low profile—I admire that. President Bai has a keen eye for talent; it seems the Bai Group's future is bright.\"","He directly addressed her as Director Liu, his sudden shift in attitude drawing everyone's attention.","Zhou Yan and the Zhou family members beside him looked extremely grim.","To be honest, if it weren't for the presence of those fierce-looking men in black, they would never have let this slide.","A faint smile curled at the corner of Liu Yutong's mouth. This was exactly the effect she wanted—Bai Shisui had to stand up on her own to truly protect Bai Jingchen's hard work.","\"Since everyone acknowledges my status, let me say a few words. Regarding the selection of the chamber's president, I still hold the same view: Miss Bai Shisui is President Bai's only daughter and the heiress of the Bai Group. It is only fitting that she serve as the interim president.\"","Zhou Yan stepped forward to object again: \"Shisui is too young; she's not capable of managing the chamber!\"","Liu Yutong: \"Whether she's capable isn't for you to decide! And more importantly, you are the least qualified person here to voice an opinion!\"","Zhou Yan: \"You...\"","Liu Yutong: \"Shut up!\"","\"That's settled. Who agrees, and who opposes?\"","No one dared to respond.","Liu Yutong's assertiveness was unmistakable, and with the intimidating men in black she had brought, no one wanted to court trouble.","\"Alright, since no one opposes, it's passed.\"","Liu Yutong didn't give them time to hesitate; she made the decision on the spot: \"From now on, Miss Bai Shisui will serve as the interim president of the chamber, overseeing all its affairs.\"","Then she turned to Zhou Meizhen: \"Mrs. Bai, the rest of the meeting has nothing to do with you. It's inconvenient for you to stay here, so please excuse yourself first.\"","\"You... you're kicking me out?\"","Zhou Meizhen looked at Liu Yutong in disbelief, then turned to her daughter: \"Shisui! Are you just going to let her treat your mother like this?\"","Although Bai Shisui didn't know why Liu Yutong was doing this, she understood Liu Yutong's style—she never acted without reason.","Suddenly asking her mother to leave must mean there was important business to discuss, and it was not appropriate for her mother to know.","With this in mind, she hardened her heart and said, \"Mom, please go rest. With me and Sister Yutong here, that's enough.\"","Yun Cheng walked over to Zhou Meizhen and made a polite gesture to escort her out, his demeanor courteous yet carrying an undeniable force.","Zhou Meizhen looked at her daughter's resolute profile, her heart sinking like ashes. Accompanied by Yun Cheng, she silently left the conference room.","The door closed again, and the atmosphere in the room grew even heavier.","Everyone could sense that the real climax was about to come.","Liu Yutong became the absolute focus once more. She lightly tapped the table with one hand, drawing everyone's attention back.","\"Alright, now that the outsiders are gone, we can talk about serious matters.\"","Her icy gaze locked onto Zhou Yan, who was trying to appear calm.","\"Mr. Zhou, it's time for us to settle some accounts.\"","Zhou Yan's heart skipped a beat, a sense of foreboding washing over him: \"You... what do you want now?\"","\"What do I want?\"","Liu Yutong let out a cold laugh and said, \"Zhou Yan, do you think that just because the Snakehead Gang has been wiped out, there's no evidence left? Do you think you can hide your secret collusion with the Snakehead Gang to murder President Bai forever?\"","This statement landed like a bombshell, sending shockwaves through the room!","\"What? Zhou Yan colluded with the Snakehead Gang?\"","\"He killed President Bai?\"","\"Is it true or false? This is too horrifying!\"","\"No wonder he was so eager to seize power—he was afraid of being exposed.\"","\"President Bai treated his Zhou family so well, and yet he could commit such an ungrateful act!\"","\"........\"","Zeng Jin shot to his feet and stared at Zhou Yan: \"Zhou Yan, is what Miss Liu said true? Did you really collude with the Snakehead Gang to kill President Bai?\"","Old Master Li also looked at him in disbelief: \"Zhou Yan, explain this clearly to me!\"","Cold sweat broke out on Zhou Yan's forehead, his mind screaming that it was impossible!","But on the surface, he shook his head frantically in denial: \"No! I didn't! Liu Yutong, you're slandering me! You're just trying to frame me so you can seize control of the Bai Group!\"","Liu Yutong: \"You say I'm framing you? Then let me ask you—who is Chen Ming?\"","Chen Ming?","Zhou Yan's body stiffened, panic flashing in his eyes.","\"Chen Ming... I don't know him!\"","\"Don't know him?\"","Liu Yutong sneered: \"He's the husband of your Zhou family's niece, and also the deputy director of the logistics department at the Bai Group. Are you telling me you don't know him?\"","\"You... how do you know all this?\" Zhou Yan's voice was filled with fear.","\"I know far more than you imagine.\"","Liu Yutong's tone turned ice-cold: \"Chen Ming used multiple fake identities to contact the Snakehead Gang through an intermediary, promising them rewards to eliminate President Bai. Given the bad blood between the Snakehead Gang and President Bai, none of you here would have suspected the Zhou family of being behind it. The plan was clever enough, but his method of covering his tracks was sloppy. It didn't take much effort for me to track him down.\"","\"After the Snakehead Gang was destroyed, I already sent people to arrest him. Care to guess who he might implicate when he talks?\"","\"No! That's not true!\"","Zhou Yan was still fighting for his life: \"You're lying! You... you're fabricating this! Chen Ming is crazy! He must have been bribed by you!\"","\"Bai Jingchen was my brother-in-law! Why would I harm him!\"","\"Evidence! Yes, evidence! If you have the guts, show me the proof, or let Chen Ming confront me face to face!\"","Liu Yutong snorted coldly: \"Still trying to argue even at death's door!\"","The truth was, she didn't have solid evidence yet, but once Chen Ming was caught, everything would come to light.","But whether she had evidence or not didn't matter to her. As long as she was sure the Zhou family was behind it, that was enough.","\"Shisui, it's your call on what to do next.\"","Bai Shisui's mind was spinning, her world tilting.","She had guessed that Liu Yutong would announce something major, which was why she had sent her mother away.","But she never expected the truth Liu Yutong revealed to be this brutal.","Liu Yutong hadn't produced any evidence, but when she saw her uncle's reaction, she figured the truth was probably close enough.","How could her uncles and aunts be so ruthless as to harm their own family in a bid for inheritance?","How dared they?","At that moment, everyone's attention turned to Bai Shisui.","This was her first decision as acting chairperson, a trial of her resolve, or rather, a test of how much she truly trusted Liu Yutong.","After all, Liu Yutong had accused Zhou Yan and the Zhou family of conspiring with the Snakehead Gang to murder Chairman Bai, but without solid proof, many remained skeptical.","So, the power of choice now rested with Bai Shisui.","Only she was truly qualified to judge the truth of the matter.","Slowly, Bai Shisui pulled herself back from the depths of extreme grief. Though she wanted nothing more than to go home, sleep, and cry her eyes out, the image of her father's brutal death kept her going.","In a daze, she recalled a line her father had once said to her: \"Don't trust your mother's family too much. They're not like us—father and daughter.\"","She had never understood what was so different about them. After all, they were her own uncles from her mother's side.","Now, she finally grasped the meaning behind her father's words.","Raising her eyes, Bai Shisui fixed a cold, hate-filled gaze on Zhou Yan.","\"Uncle, do you have anything to say?\"","Zhou Yan's face twisted in panic. \"Shishui! Shishui, listen to me! That woman has ulterior motives—she wants to swallow up the Bai family's assets! Don't be fooled by her! You know how I've treated you, your mother, and your father all these years! How could I possibly harm my own family? You have to believe me!\"","\"Shut up!\"","Bai Shisui suddenly exploded. \"You're not worthy of mentioning my father!\"","Zhou Yan: \"You'd rather trust an outsider than your own uncle?\"","The two other Zhou family executives also chimed in, their voices choked with emotion.","\"That's right! We watched you grow up!\"","\"Shishui, you have to trust us!\"","\"...\"","\"How can I trust you?\"","Bai Shisui's voice trembled. \"My father taught me to judge people by their actions, not their words. You know what you've done. Are you still going to argue?\"","\"I...\" Zhou Yan was about to continue his denial.","But Bai Shisui cut him off. \"I, as the interim head of the Bai Corporation and acting chairperson of the Chinese Chamber of Commerce, hereby announce that, effective immediately, Zhou Yan is relieved of all his positions within the Bai Corporation. All his accounts and permissions related to the company are frozen.\"","\"At the same time, I authorize Ms. Liu Yutong and her team to conduct a full investigation into the attack on my father.\"","\"Anyone who obstructs this investigation, regardless of their status, will be treated as an accomplice!\"","Her words echoed through the room, shocking everyone present.","The crowd looked at this girl, who seemed to have transformed overnight. They could faintly see the shadow of Chairman Bai in her.","Then again, considering what she had been through, they understood.","When faced with such a situation, people usually had two outcomes: either completely collapse and choose to escape, or grow tough and cold-blooded.","Clearly, Bai Shisui was tougher than they had imagined.","Or rather, her hatred had taken absolute control.","Zhou Yan staggered back as if struck by lightning, bumping into the back of a chair. \"You... Bai Shisui! How dare you! I'm your own uncle! Your mother won't stand for this!\"","\"I'll explain things to my mother.\"","Bai Shisui's face was expressionless. In that moment, she seemed to have shed all her innocence overnight, her eyes icy cold. \"As for you... Brother Yun Cheng.\"","She turned to Yun Cheng, who had been standing guard behind Liu Yutong.","Yun Cheng stepped forward. \"Please give your orders, Miss Bai.\"","Bai Shisui took a deep breath. \"Brother Yun Cheng, please arrest them and deal with them according to the methods of the Wanlong Society.\"","\"Yes!\"","\"Seize them! Execute justice on the spot!\"","Yun Cheng waved his hand, and a group of men in black burst in from outside, rushing straight toward Zhou Yan and the two Zhou family executives he had brought with him, restraining them.","\"What are you doing! Let me go! This is illegal detention! I want to call the police! I want a lawyer!\" Zhou Yan struggled wildly, but it was futile. He was completely overpowered and dragged out.","Once he was hauled outside by two men in black, he completely lost his composure, screaming like a fishwife.","\"Let me go! You bastards! Bai Shisui! You little wretch! You're just like your deadbeat father—a traitor who helps outsiders screw over your own family!\"","\"Liu Yutong! You witch! You're a curse! You'll die a horrible death! All of you in the Wanlong Society are a bunch of thugs! Don't think I don't know your dirty secrets! You're a gang! You're not good people at all!\"","\"Murderers! Kidnapping and detaining people in broad daylight! Lawless!\"","\"They can do this to me today, and they'll do it to you tomorrow! Bai Shisui, you've invited wolves into your home! You'll regret this! The Bai family will be picked clean by that witch sooner or later, down to... uh?\"","Zhou Yan's cursing came to an abrupt halt. Not because he wanted to stop, but because he had run into a wall... a human-shaped one.","It was Ji Yu.","Ji Yu had been standing by the wall, snoring, until Zhou Yan's insults woke him up. When he heard the man cursing the young lady, his simple, sleepy face turned grim.","He stepped right in front of Zhou Yan and growled, \"You... cursing the young lady?\"","Zhou Yan, intimidated by the terrifying sight of the huge man looming over him up close, felt like he might pass out. But still, he persisted, \"So what if I curse her? She's a witch! And you're all her dogs! Freaks! You're all lawless gangsters...\"","Despite Ji Yu's slow wit, he could tell that this man was really cursing the young lady—and fiercely at that.","He remembered what Brother Yun Cheng had told him about making bad guys face justice. That meant making them pay for their wrongs. But as long as he didn't actually send the guy to join great-grandma, it should be fine.","If this guy was cursing the young lady, he must be a bad guy, right?","So, could he just make him see his ancestors?","Just as Ji Yu was struggling to process this with his big head, Zhou Yan kept on ranting without stopping.","Ji Yu looked at the face in front of him and suddenly felt annoyed. This guy was messing with his thinking!","It was like a fly buzzing in his ear—noisy and annoying.","So, instinctively, he raised his right hand, which was bigger than an average person's entire head. With a casual motion, as if trying to swat a fly, he swung it toward Zhou Yan's face.","Whoosh!","The wind from his palm was so strong that it lifted the hair of the men in black who were holding Zhou Yan.","Zhou Yan's pupils shrank in terror as he watched that giant hand fly toward his face, covering his view.","Smack!!!","A sharp, thunderous sound exploded in the hallway.","Zhou Yan’s head snapped violently to the side at a grotesque angle, his twisted expression freezing instantly as it warped. His cheekbone visibly caved in, his mouth twisted askew, and several bloody teeth flew out along with a spray of saliva...","His entire body looked as if he had been hit square-on by a sledgehammer. His feet left the ground, and he was sent flying sideways, slamming heavily into the wall three or four meters away. Then, he slid down limply and collapsed onto the floor, motionless.","Both inside and outside the room, a deathly silence fell!","The two black-clad men responsible for escorting Zhou Yan swallowed hard, staring at Ji Yu with awe.","Holy crap, that was brutal!","Ji Yu, however, awkwardly lowered his head, glanced at his own palm, then looked at Zhou Yan lying crumpled in the distance, and muttered under his breath, “Hmm... maybe I used a bit too much force?”","He scratched his head and asked the black-clad brother beside him uncertainly.","“He’s still breathing, right?”","The black-clad men: “...”"]},{"number":704,"title":"Chapter 704: 704, Dust Settles [Thanks to Ailuo who loves eating Nyonya dried meat for the generous \"Big Health\" gift]","paragraphs":["Zhou Yan’s entire face had twisted beyond human recognition—half of it was collapsed, with blood frothing from the corner of his mouth. If not for the occasional twitch of his body proving he was still alive, everyone present would have suspected that these black-clad men would simply drag his “corpse” out to sea and dispose of the evidence.","But even if he was still breathing, the way he looked now seemed far worse than death itself.","The other two members of the Zhou family were so terrified that their faces turned ashen. They shook off the black-clad men restraining them, dropped to their knees with a loud thud, and wailed with tears streaming down their faces.","“Sui Sui, please spare us! It was all Zhou Yan’s idea! We didn’t know anything!”","“Yes, yes! Please let us off, considering all the years we’ve worked for the group!”","“Your uncle Zhou Yan acted on his own—it has nothing to do with us!”","“......”","These two clearly weren’t tough nuts to crack. Before the men of the Wanlong Society had even started using their methods, they had already confessed everything.","Still, after seeing what had happened to Zhou Yan, it was easy to understand—after all, not everyone could withstand a slap from that giant.","Bai Shisui closed her eyes, unwilling to look at their pleading faces.","“Take them away!”","At Yun Cheng’s command, the black-clad men immediately stepped forward and forcibly dragged the two out as well.","The cries for mercy grew fainter and fainter until they finally faded completely from everyone’s ears.","In the banquet hall, silence fell over the crowd.","They secretly glanced at the towering, terrifyingly built man outside, then at the dent in the wall left by Zhou Yan’s impact, and shivered in unison.","Many people instinctively touched their own cheeks, feeling an imaginary ache.","Holy shit! What kind of monster possessed that kind of strength?","If they had had any doubts earlier about whether this was the legendary “Hell Giant,” that single slap had erased them completely.","Aside from the legendary brute who had once knocked out a foreigner nicknamed “The Steamroller” with just one slap, it was hard to imagine anyone else whose hand could deliver such devastating force.","A few who had been harboring secret schemes immediately abandoned their unrealistic ideas after witnessing this.","What were interests and factional struggles in the face of absolute violence? Utterly meaningless.","They were on a completely different level from these black-clad men!","If these people didn’t feel like reasoning with you, one slap was all it took to shut you up—permanently.","Liu Yutong also saw what had happened outside. The corner of her mouth twitched almost imperceptibly.","That idiot Ji Yu didn’t hold back at all. Hadn’t they agreed not to kill anyone? Sure, he technically hadn’t, but was there any real difference?","Given Zhou Yan’s current state, even if he survived, he’d probably spend the rest of his life in a hospital bed, drooling.","Still, the effect was unexpectedly good.","She scanned the room again at the terrified, silent crowd and sighed inwardly. Indeed, in many situations, reasoning with people was far less effective than a physical demonstration—especially in an overseas environment like this.","Of course, Liu Yutong considered herself a law-abiding businesswoman, and the Wanlong Society was a legitimate company. This was just an accidental incident—well, she’d have to have Zhao Tianyi carefully study the relevant American laws to see how this “accident” could be legally defined.","After all, she wasn’t sure if Ji Yu’s disability certificate would hold up here.","Zhou Yan had committed a crime, sure, but even criminals in America had human rights, right? You couldn’t just go around slapping people like that.","At that thought, she almost felt like laughing. Did criminals really have human rights in this place?","“Ahem.” Liu Yutong cleared her throat lightly, breaking the silence in the meeting room.","All eyes immediately locked onto her, and their expressions had become noticeably more respectful.","“Ji Yu, be more careful next time. We’re civilized people—we rely on reason. Don’t kill anyone. Quickly, send him to the hospital.”","“Oh, got it, Miss.” Ji Yu scratched his head and responded in a deep, gruff voice.","Then, like picking up a chick, he lifted the unconscious Zhou Yan and handed him to one of the black-clad men: “Find a doctor. Don’t let him go meet his great-grandmother.”","“Yes, sir!” The man took him quickly, handling him far more delicately than before, as if afraid of causing any further trouble.","The door closed again.","Liu Yutong turned back to the crowd and spoke slowly: “Alright, just a little interruption. Sorry for the show, everyone. The Wanlong Society has always abided by the law, loved peace, and opposed violence. That was nothing but a minor accident.”","Everyone: “......”","Right, right. You do “love” peace, you really don’t “like” using violence. We all saw that hallucination.","And yeah, that slap was just a “minor accident”—one that happened to crush half of Zhou Yan’s face into nothing.","Despite their internal sarcasm, the smiles on their faces grew even more sycophantic.","“Of course, of course, I could tell at a glance that Chairman Liu is a peace-loving person!”","“Not only that, but I think Chairman Liu is also very compassionate—someone’s face ran into a slap, and she even sent him to the hospital for free.”","“Zhou Yan dared to insult Chairman Liu and slander the Wanlong Society. Getting just a light slap was already far too merciful for him.”","“......”","Flattery erupted from all sides. It might have been clumsy, but the attitude was unmistakable.","Zeng Jin, the businessman from Taiwan, suppressed the shock in his heart and spoke with a respectful tone: “Chairman Liu, you are wise and decisive. I admire you. With your support, Miss Bai’s appointment as acting chairperson is truly the will of the people and a blessing for the Chamber of Commerce! I, on behalf of myself and my companies, fully support Miss Bai!”","Old Master Li trembled slightly as he said, “Miss Liu... your methods are extraordinary. I have no objections. Shi Sui, from now on, the Chamber of Commerce will depend on your and Miss Liu’s efforts.”","Even he, the toughest honorary chairman, had been frightened by that scene.","Earlier, he had relied on his seniority, thinking the black-clad men wouldn’t dare touch him. But now it was clear—their black suits weren’t just for show. They played for keeps.","Seeing this, the other directors didn’t dare hesitate. One by one, they voiced their support.","“I support Miss Bai!”","“I support Chairman Liu!”","“Under Chairman Liu and Miss Bai’s leadership, the Chamber of Commerce will surely reach new heights!”","“......”","Bai Shisui watched this dramatic turn of events with a storm of emotions—hatred toward her uncle’s possible involvement in her father’s murder, awe at Liu Yutong’s thunderous methods, and bewilderment at the heavy burden suddenly placed on her shoulders. But above all, there was a firm determination.","Her father was gone. Some had shown their fangs.","Now she had to grow up and protect the legacy he had left behind.","As for Yutong—she was now the one person she could trust and rely on completely.","\"Thank you all for your support, uncles and elders. I will do my utmost to live up to my father's expectations and earn your trust. My first priority is to thoroughly investigate the truth behind my father's murder and bring the real culprit and the mastermind to justice! Secondly, I will stabilize the operations of the White Group and the Chamber of Commerce, ensuring that all business and charitable projects remain unaffected. I will discuss specific matters in detail with Sister Yutong and all the directors.\"","Liu Yutong nodded approvingly. This girl was tougher than she had imagined, which put her at ease.","She immediately made her stance clear: \"What happened to President Bai is my concern as well. I hereby guarantee to everyone here—regardless of who is involved, no matter how powerful the forces behind them—that the Wanlong Society and I will pursue this to the end. We will seek justice for President Bai and for all our compatriots!","\"At the same time, I also promise that since I myself have become a member of the Overseas Chamber of Commerce, I will fulfill my duty of mutual assistance from now on. If any of you need help in the United States—whether for business matters or personal safety issues—you can come to me.","\"Lastly, I want to emphasize once more: we are all sons and daughters of the Dragon Country drifting overseas. We should stand together and look out for one another!\"","After Liu Yutong's speech, the atmosphere in the banquet hall grew far more spirited than before.","If the previous statements had been made under pressure or threat, now many people's eyes truly lit up—a spark of excitement born from toiling in a foreign land and suddenly finding a powerful ally.","\"Chairman Liu, those words are incredibly uplifting!\" exclaimed a burly middle-aged man in the construction material business, standing abruptly with emotion. \"To be honest, my warehouse in South Bay was extorted for protection money by a local gang last month. The police response was slow, and I didn't dare to fight back myself—it was humiliating. Now that I've heard you, I feel a solid foundation beneath me!\"","A female business owner chimed in, \"Exactly, Chairman Liu. When we do business abroad, we seek both profit and peace. But in the West, obeying the law doesn't guarantee safety. Take the Snakeheads, for example. When President Bai was alive, we could at least bargain and intimidate them. But once he was gone, many of us couldn't sleep soundly at night, afraid we'd be their next target.","\"Now, with you personally taking action and uprooting the Snakeheads completely, you've not only avenged President Bai but also eliminated a major threat for all of us Dragon Country merchants! The gentleman who acted earlier must be the legendary Hell Giant, right? With him and the Wanlong Society's big brothers here, what do we have to fear?\"","These words immediately resonated with others.","\"That's right! Black Phoenix—oh, I mean Chairman Liu! We've all heard about how you wiped out the Snakeheads. They say you led those black-clad heroes and razed their lair overnight. We thought it was just rumor before, but seeing it today, I believe it!\"","\"Yes, absolutely! It has to be Chairman Liu! Who else could have such strength and audacity?\"","\"The name Black Phoenix is truly well-deserved!\"","\"With Chairman Liu at the helm of the Chamber of Commerce, no one will dare look down on us Dragon Country merchants anymore!\"","\"...\"","Zeng Jin, the most perceptive—and the most sycophantic—among those present, seized the moment to address the crowd: \"Ladies and gentlemen! Chairman Liu has not only set things right today, stabilizing the White Group and the Chamber of Commerce, but has also given us all a promise. What is this? It's a sense of responsibility! Boldness! And a pillar of support for us overseas Dragon Country people!\"","He turned to Liu Yutong and bowed deeply: \"Chairman Liu, I may not be talented, but after years of doing business in the bay area, I've accumulated some connections and resources. From today onward, I, Zeng Jin, and all my enterprises will follow your lead! We wandering sons abroad have long needed a leader like you to unite us.\"","Liu Yutong's words had also struck a chord with Elder Li, who couldn't help but sigh: \"I have lived long enough to have seen storms and read people's hearts. Today, Miss Liu has shown me what it means to be a heroine and a true chivalrous person. President Bai devoted his life to benevolence and uniting overseas compatriots. Miss Liu carries on his legacy and even surpasses him—this is truly a blessing for us Dragon Country people wandering abroad! Ladies and gentlemen, since Miss Liu has spoken, let us cherish this moment and work in solidarity. No one should do anything underhanded!\"","With these two heavyweights setting the tone, the other directors had no hesitation left. They vied to express their support, anxious not to seem insincere.","\"Chairman Liu, our company's future security consulting services will be entirely contracted to your team—name your price!\"","\"Chairman Liu, I have a logistics center in San Jose in a great location. Would the Wanlong Society need a base there? I'll offer it at cost!\"","\"Chairman Liu, my son isn't studying well and hangs around with bad company. Could you let him come to your place for training under your heroes? He can endure any hardship—it's better than going astray!\"","\"...\"","As Liu Yutong made her stance unmistakably clear, everyone's perception of her grew increasingly favorable.","Their earlier fear of her—even disgust at her being too ruthless and intimidating—stemmed from the uncertainty of distrust.","But now that she had explicitly declared she would share their fortunes and hardships, everything changed.","Now, they were people with a powerful protectors in the United States. A group that could obliterate the Snakeheads overnight, whose strength was formidable, whose terrifying reputation alone brought instant security!","Liu Yutong was pleased with the reaction. Earlier, Ji Yu had wielded a heavy stick, and now she offered a sweet carrot—the effect was immediate.","\"Rest assured, everyone. I, Liu Yutong, always keep my word and deliver on my promises. I also hope that all of you will stay united, support Miss Bai, and support the Chamber of Commerce.","\"But I will say this bluntly: If I discover anyone trying to play petty tricks, hold us back, or act recklessly in the future, don't blame me for showing no mercy!\"","The crowd once again enthusiastically responded.","\"Never, never!\"","\"Chairman Liu, rest assured—we will fully cooperate!\"","\"Anyone who stirs up trouble at a time like this will be an enemy of us all!\"","\"...\"","The remainder of the meeting went exceptionally smoothly.","Bai Shisui's position as acting president was officially confirmed, and in time, she would be formally promoted.","Liu Yutong was elected Honorary President after another round of voting.","As the meeting adjourned, every director stepped over to Liu Yutong and Bai Shisui to bid farewell with utmost respect, their attitudes far more humble than when they arrived.","Zeng Jin was the last to leave, but just as he finished his farewell, Liu Yutong called him back.","\"President Zeng, hold on a moment.\"","Zeng Jin stopped in his tracks and smiled respectfully, asking, \"Chairman Liu, do you have further instructions?\"","Liu Yutong didn't answer immediately. Instead, she gestured toward the door of a nearby lounge. \"Let's talk privately.\"","Zeng Jin extended his hand. \"After you, Chairman Liu.\"","The two entered the rest lounge one after the other, and the door was gently closed behind them by Yun Cheng, who then stood behind Liu Yutong.","After sitting down, Liu Yutong first expressed her gratitude to him.","“President Zeng, thank you for your support today.”","“Chairwoman Liu, you flatter me!”","Zeng Jin quickly clasped his hands in a respectful gesture. “I merely said what needed to be said and did what needed to be done. You and Ms. Bai are deserving of the recognition. And I’m truly honored to have had the chance to meet you today, Ms. Liu.”","Liu Yutong smiled faintly. “No need for formalities. I asked you to stay because I want to discuss some practical cooperation.”","Zeng Jin’s spirits lifted. “Please go ahead, Chairwoman Liu. I’m all ears.”","..."]},{"number":705,"title":"Chapter 705: 705, Responsibility and Dream. (Two in One)","paragraphs":["After the two sat down,","Zeng Jin proactively poured her a cup of tea and said, \"President Liu, feel free to speak your mind. If there's anything I can do, I won't refuse.\"","Although he didn't know the purpose of Liu Yutong calling him aside for a private talk, he was well aware of one thing: if she could wipe out the Snake Head Gang overnight and ruin Zhou Yan's reputation, dealing with him would likely take no effort at all.","Liu Yutong said, \"Let's skip the pleasantries. I kept you here to discuss a practical collaboration.\"","Zeng Jin perked up. \"Please go ahead, President Liu. I'm all ears.\"","Liu Yutong picked up the teacup but didn't drink, just gently swirling the tea inside. \"President Zeng, I heard that your Zeng family got its start in Taiwan Province, formerly as the notorious society Xinghe Association, didn't it? Are you still in touch with those organizations in Taiwan Province now?\"","Zeng Jin's hand holding the teacup froze, and his smile instantly stiffened. \"President Liu, what exactly do you mean by that? Those are all old stories. The Zeng family has long since transitioned into legitimate business and completely cut ties with the past.\"","His family had indeed been part of a major society in Taiwan Province in the past, but as times changed, the family gradually cleaned up its image and transformed. By his father's generation and his own, they were already fully legitimate businessmen. However, some early connections and networks, especially ties to certain special circles, had not been completely severed.","This was a family secret, known to few, and he hadn't expected Liu Yutong to uncover it.","Could she be planning to use this to attack him?","\"Don't get so worked up, President Zeng. I'm not here to settle scores. I told you, I called you alone to ask for your help—or we could call it a collaboration.\"","Without further delay, Liu Yutong cut to the chase. \"I've invested in a chip manufacturing company domestically. As you should know, the biggest bottleneck in the chip industry is talent, especially top-tier experts in advanced process technology and chip architecture design. Our country has a weak foundation in this area, and training takes time, while Taiwan Province has deep accumulated expertise in this field.\"","Hearing her words, Zeng Jin seemed to guess what she was after. He felt a wave of relief and nodded. \"Companies like TSMC and MediaTek indeed have many world-class technical elites.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"I've heard that TSMC has a top technical expert named Liang Mengsong. His mastery in wafer manufacturing is exceptional across the entire Chinese-speaking world. But it seems he hasn't been happy at TSMC and has faced obstacles in promotion.\"","Zeng Jin frowned with some difficulty. \"President Liu, I'm not in the chip industry, so I really don't know about this Liang Mengsong's personal situation. However, I've heard that TSMC has extremely strict non-compete agreements and confidentiality clauses for core technical staff. Moreover, Taiwan Province has tight controls over the flow of such high-end talent.\"","\"That's why I came to you.\"","\"Recruiting him through formal headhunting channels would face some resistance. I need some 'special' connections and methods.\"","\"What exactly do you mean, President Liu?\"","\"Your Zeng family's early network—can it still reach some friends who 'get things done without sticking to the rules'?\" Liu Yutong asked.","Upon hearing this, Zeng Jin fell silent.","Liu Yutong’s words were practically an open invitation for him to leverage the darker, less-public networks of his family’s connections to poach talent—and if needed, resort to some unconventional methods.","But if that happened, wouldn’t all the Zeng family’s efforts to go legit be for nothing?","“President Liu, this kind of thing is highly risky. The Zeng family now runs a lawful business. I’m not sure I can...”","Liu Yutong cut him off immediately. “President Zeng, don’t be so quick to refuse!”","“There’s a saying: risk often goes hand in hand with reward. And I never said you had to use illegal means. I’ve never supported such things.”","“The reason I came to you is that I’ve thought this through. Your family is now a legitimate business, and that’s the kind of partner I feel comfortable with. If you were still tied to gangster life, I wouldn’t trust you, and I wouldn’t have approached you. Do you understand?”","Zeng Jin almost blurted out that he didn’t understand, and couldn’t help silently complaining: Wanlong Group is shady enough already... and you’re worried about my family being legit?","The way she builds her moral platform is just...","Of course, he only dared to think this.","On the surface, he barely managed to nod and force out two words: “I understand.”","Liu Yutong said, “What do you understand?”","Zeng Jin: “...”","What did he understand? How was he supposed to answer?","He could tell Liu Yutong seemed very concerned that no one questioned whether her company was clean, which is why she kept hammering the point.","Finally, after struggling for a while, he spoke up: “Is it because Wanlong Group is also a legitimate company? That cooperation between legit companies is the safest?”","Liu Yutong nodded. “Exactly.”","“If this goes through, the benefits for you and the Zeng family will be enormous.”","Zeng Jin said, “Please spell it out, President Liu.”","Liu Yutong replied, “Your family has some roots in Taiwan and among overseas Chinese business circles, but you lack a strong strategic ally. If this partnership goes smoothly, Wanlong Group can bring the Zeng family along in its future expansions into semiconductors, internet, consumer electronics, and other fields.”","“The potential of the mainland market—need I say more? If the Zeng family becomes an ally of Wanlong Group, you’ll have smoother access to the mainland market, and overseas, Wanlong Group will have your back. By then, a Zeng family backed by Wanlong, connecting capital markets across the strait—what kind of future do you think that would bring?”","“To be blunt, even if you offend some factions in Taiwan by poaching for me and lose the Taiwanese market, it won’t hurt much. Gains and losses—which weighs more? Chairman Zeng can surely figure that out.”","“Of course, if you doubt Wanlong Group’s influence on the mainland, feel free to investigate before deciding. I’ll wait for your answer.”","Zeng Jin’s breathing grew heavier.","The vision Liu Yutong had painted was too big, too tempting!","He didn’t fully understand Wanlong Group’s real power, but judging from Miss Liu’s presence and the way they had easily crushed the Snakehead Gang in the States, their mainland connections were probably far stronger.","If the Zeng family could truly leverage Wanlong’s might to break into the mainland market, the prospects would far surpass anything their current trade business in Taiwan could achieve.","Every business in Taiwan Province wanted to develop on the mainland, but due to certain restrictions, even if they could grow, it was very limited. If they had the help of a mainland giant, even if it meant losing the Taiwan Province market as a result, it would still be worth it!","Zeng Jinqiang suppressed the excitement in his heart and asked, \"President Liu, what do you want me to do?\"","Liu Yutong: \"It's simple. Have your people approach Liang Mengsong and find a way to get him to visit the mainland. Secondly, handle his non-compete agreement—use even some unconventional methods if necessary, but don't let the non-compete clause restrict him.\"","\"Of course, if some of the top executives at Taiji Electric don't play along, you can deal with them as you see fit, as long as you don't break the law.\"","\"President Liu, aren't you afraid of stirring things up and causing trouble?\"","\"Afraid? In Liu Yutong's dictionary, there is no such word as 'afraid'.\"","\"Besides, poaching just one technical talent isn't that big of a deal, is it? And as long as the job is done cleanly, who would know I did it?\"","Zeng Jin felt there was something odd about her last sentence, but he couldn't quite put his finger on it at the moment.","Then, looking at Liu Yutong's confident demeanor, he finally made up his mind.","Doing business sometimes meant taking risks—if it succeeded, the Zeng family's power would rise to another level; if it failed, with the Wanlong Association backing them up, it wouldn't lead to total ruin.","As long as Liu Yutong kept her word.","\"Alright, I agree!\"","\"I'll arrange for someone to handle Liang Mengsong as soon as possible. I hope you'll keep your promise, President Liu, and help the Zeng family break into the mainland market.\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"That's naturally not a problem. I'll return to the country in a couple of days. If you're skeptical, you can come back with me and visit the headquarters of the Wanlong Association on the mainland.\"","\"Can I?\"","\"Of course.\"","Zeng Jin felt more at ease. To be honest, he had been a bit worried that she might be a scammer—what if Miss Liu's Wanlong Association wasn't that powerful on the mainland and only had some influence in the States? Then the Zeng family would be finished!","Now that she had voluntarily invited him to visit the mainland for inspection, what did that mean? It meant she was absolutely confident in her own strength.","For one thing, those black-clad enforcers of the Wanlong Association—back in the country, their numbers had to be at least one or two times greater than they were in the States, right?","It wasn't that he didn't dare to think bigger; it was that the fighting power of those black-clad men was too terrifying. They simply couldn't be measured by ordinary gang members.","For example, back in the day when the Zeng family's predecessor was a gang, having a few top-tier fighters and about two hundred ordinary underlings was enough to make them a regional powerhouse.","So, based on his experience, even if the Wanlong Association was stronger, it definitely wouldn't be ridiculously over-the-top.","\"Alright! But I need to sort out matters here in the States first. I'll visit you on the mainland in a while.\"","\"Not a problem.\"","\"Oh, by the way!\"","As if she remembered something, Liu Yutong added: \"Besides Liang Mengsong, you should also try to poach top-tier technical talent from Taijidian and other related companies. Compensation won't be an issue. And of course, I won't forget your share of the benefits.\"","Zeng Jin nodded without hesitation. Poaching one person meant making enemies; poaching a whole group meant making even more enemies. So he might as well go all the way.","Once you're on board, there's no turning back.","\"Alright!\"","Zeng Jin extended his hand. \"President Liu, happy cooperation.\"","\"Pleasure doing business with you.\" Liu Yutong extended her hand as well, shaking his.","...........","A few days later.","At the Bai family villa in San Francisco.","Bai Jingchen’s ashes were temporarily placed in the home, awaiting the day when Bai Shisui would take them back to China for burial, so that his roots might return to the earth.","Liu Yutong, dressed entirely in black, stood alone before the memorial tablet. She lit a stick of incense and said nothing, simply gazing quietly at Bai Jingchen’s gentle smile in the photograph.","After an unknown stretch of time, soft footsteps sounded behind her.","Bai Shisui, also in black, walked slowly to her side.","The two stood shoulder to shoulder in silence for a long while before Bai Shisui spoke.","\"Sister Yutong, thank you for avenging my father.\"","\"It was the least I could do,\" Liu Yutong said softly.","\"Yesterday, my uncle... after Zhou Yan’s injuries improved, I arranged for them to be sent back to the country, including all the Zhou family members who were involved. As for my mother’s relatives, they moved out of San Francisco this morning and headed for the East Coast...\"","Liu Yutong nodded. By choosing to send them back to China, Bai Shisui clearly had no intention of letting Zhou Yan live.","A trial here would most likely not result in the death penalty; only by sending him back to China could she more easily ensure he was sent to the afterlife.","To be honest, making this decision must have caused Bai Shisui immense pain, especially regarding her mother, Madam Bai. How could she face her, how could she explain?","Perhaps the rift between mother and daughter could never be mended.","Bai Shisui looked up at her father’s smile in the photo and suddenly asked a question: \"Sister Yutong, do you think people have to give up what they love in order to take on their responsibilities?\"","Liu Yutong turned to look at her. \"Why do you ask?\"","\"I’ve loved fashion design since I was a child. My father supported me and sent me to the best schools. My dream was to have my own designer brand. But now that my father is gone, the conglomerate and the business association are such a huge weight bearing down on me. I’ve been thinking for days—my fledgling fashion design company probably can’t keep going. I’m planning to shut it down.\"","Liu Yutong paused for a moment and asked, \"Do you regret it?\"","Bai Shisui shook her head. \"No regrets. Just a bit sad. But I know this is a choice I have to make. The career my father built with his whole life can’t collapse in my hands. Hobbies and dreams can wait, but responsibility cannot be avoided.\"","\"Sister Yutong, do you think I’m doing the right thing?\"","Liu Yutong looked at this girl who had grown up overnight and felt a mix of emotions.","There was pity, but also relief.","\"There is no absolute right or wrong, Suisui.\"","\"In life, you often have to find balance among various choices, or make sacrifices. Being able to see what is most important at this moment and being willing to set aside your dreams for it—that itself is a sign of maturity and responsibility. Your father would be proud of you.\"","She paused, then added: \"But giving up doesn’t mean losing forever. Once you’ve steered the conglomerate and the business association onto the right track and nurtured a management team you can trust, you can always pick up your dream again. By then, your experience, resources, and vision might take your design brand even further and make it more renowned.\"","\"Responsibility and dreams don’t have to be forever at odds. Sometimes, you just need to decide which comes first.\"","Bai Shisui listened carefully as the haze in her eyes gradually cleared, and her expression brightened with understanding: “I see, Sister Yutong. You mean I should first do what I must do, then do what I want to do, right?”","Liu Yutong nodded. “Exactly.”","“Sister Yutong, can I ask you one more question? Isn’t it hard for you to bear such a heavy responsibility with the Wanlong Group? Does being so busy ever make you unhappy?” Bai Shisui asked curiously.","Many leaders of large conglomerates find themselves with no choice but to carry on, unable to rest, enjoy life, or slack off. It’s truly difficult because thousands of employees rely on them for their livelihoods. Bai Shisui now understood this from her own experience.","This was the first time anyone had asked Liu Yutong this question, but she didn’t have to think it over much before replying with a smile, “I have thousands of trustworthy family members. How could I be unhappy?”","“Haha... I really envy you, Sister Yutong!”","The two of them stood in silence for a while longer.","“Sister Yutong, are you planning to return to China?” Bai Shisui asked.","“Yes, there are many things in China that need my attention, especially pushing forward with my Loongxin project as soon as possible,” Liu Yutong said.","The first phase of the Loongxin factory was almost complete, and the ordered equipment had smoothly cleared customs. President Qiu was pushing full steam ahead with the preparations for equipment installation and commissioning, striving to start operations in the shortest time and achieve mass production of 90-nanometer chips as soon as possible.","Although the 90-nanometer process lagged behind the current mainstream 45-nanometer—and even more advanced processes—it had the advantage of being a mature technology with high success rates. It could also meet the current needs of partners like Qiming Electric Company.","Of course, this was only their first step.","As the saying goes, the hardest part is starting. Once the initial phases got ironed out, they would gradually introduce new processes, perhaps even quietly acquire advanced equipment, and then sprint toward world-class standards.","Beyond the impending launch of the chip factory, Uncle Li had also reported some special aspects of the Loongxin project to the relevant leaders in the capital.","Because the Loongxin project involved an overseas lithography equipment company, the situation was complex. The authorities in the capital took it very seriously. At that time, she would likely need to accompany Uncle Li to the capital for a detailed briefing and discuss how to mitigate potential risks and prevent certain unscrupulous entities from forcibly taking over a company that belonged to the Dragon Kingdom.","It was necessary to prepare for the worst-case scenario in advance.","But if it came to that, it wouldn’t just be her problem alone. There would be people above her to help bear the pressure.","Besides the chip matters, there were many other issues requiring her attention—such as the acquisition of a mobile phone project, and the case involving Zhao Weixiang, who had already been sent back to China by private jet. In short, there was too much waiting for her in the country.","Bai Shisui also knew that Liu Yutong was very busy. She had already spent too much time on her father’s affairs, leaving Bai Shisui feeling both grateful and apologetic.","“Sister Yutong, make sure you rest. Don’t wear yourself out,” she said.","“I will,” Liu Yutong nodded.","...","The next day, at San Francisco International Airport.","Bai Shisui came personally to see off Liu Yutong and her team.","Before this, a group of men in black had already escorted Zhao Weixiang in a private jet back to China ahead of time, to ensure confidentiality.","Now, the only core members accompanying Liu Yutong on the international flight back home were Lan Die, Yun Cheng, Chu Yang, and Su Mansu.","“This is far enough.”","In front of the terminal, Liu Yutong turned around and said to Bai Shisui, “Remember what I told you—stay calm when faced with trouble. If you’re ever unsure about something, you can reach out to me, but the final decision must be yours. And when you need to stand your ground, don’t hesitate.”","“I’ll remember, Yutong Jie.” Bai Shisui nodded firmly.","Liu Yutong extended her arms and gave her a gentle hug.","“You’ve got this, Suisui. You’re stronger than you think.”","Bai Shisui hugged her back tightly, then whispered a single word into Liu Yutong’s ear.","“Thank you.”"]},{"number":706,"title":"Chapter 706: 706、Chance Encounter (Two-in-One)","paragraphs":["In the business class cabin of a flight from San Francisco to the imperial capital, Liu Yutong chose a window seat and sat down.","She had originally planned to fly directly to Danancheng, but received a call from Uncle Li just before her departure. This elder, who had always supported the Longxin project, was going to the imperial capital for a meeting. Upon learning that she was about to return to China, he suggested they travel together so she could make an appearance before the relevant officials.","Of course, this appearance wasn’t a formal meeting—just a chance for the officials to get a first impression of her.","Liu Yutong understood the importance of this opportunity, so she changed her flight at the last moment and headed for the imperial capital.","Now, she was half-reclining in her seat, holding a copy of Semiconductor Physics and Devices, reading intently.","After all, the officials she was about to meet were completely different from those she had dealt with before. The more knowledge she absorbed, the better prepared she would be.","The plane had been flying smoothly for three hours when the cabin crew began serving meals.","“Miss, would you like something to eat?” a flight attendant asked softly, approaching with care.","Liu Yutong closed her book and rubbed her slightly tired eyes. “I’ll pass on the food for now. Just give me an Americano without sugar, please. Thank you.”","“Of course!”","Not long after, the flight attendant brought the coffee.","Liu Yutong took a sip and let her gaze wander around the cabin.","The people from the Yuncheng group surrounding her were scattered nearby, resting, while only a stranger sat in the seat to her left.","The woman wore a light gray Chanel suit with a pale purple silk scarf tied at her neck, quietly reading a finance magazine.","From her appearance alone, she looked quite young—around thirty, with an air of scholarly elegance, warm and refined, likely a woman from a wealthy family.","Liu Yutong’s eyes lingered on her face for a few seconds, feeling an inexplicable sense of familiarity.","Maybe it’s because she looks kind, she thought to herself.","Just then, as if sensing Liu Yutong’s gaze, the woman looked up, paused briefly, and then offered a polite smile with a gentle nod.","Liu Yutong nodded back with a smile, then turned her attention away, reopening her book to continue reading about the principles of bipolar junction transistors and MOS field-effect transistors.","A few minutes later, the plane hit some turbulence, jolting slightly.","Liu Yutong lost her grip briefly, and the coffee she was holding spilled onto her book.","She sighed, pulled out some tissues, and began wiping it up slowly.","Just then, a voice came from the woman on her left: “Need some help?”","Liu Yutong looked up to see the woman had stood up, offering a towel. “Use this—it’ll clean it better.”","“Thank you!” Liu Yutong took the towel, wiped the coffee stains off her book, and then pressed the call button to ask a flight attendant for a fresh towel for the woman.","Perhaps because of this small incident, or maybe because the fourteen-hour flight was too boring, the woman struck up a conversation with Liu Yutong.","“Semiconductor Physics and Devices—a very technical book. Are you a student in this field?”","Liu Yutong shook her head. “No, I just find it interesting and read it for fun. My major is business administration.”","“Business administration?”","A flicker of surprise crossed the woman’s eyes. “That’s rare. Most young people studying management seldom take an interest in such hardcore technical books.”","Liu Yutong smiled. “Just reading casually.”","“Many industries are deeply integrated with technology these days. If you don’t understand the basics, it’s easy to fall into pitfalls. Learning a bit more is never wrong.”","The woman nodded. “It’s surprising that someone so young has such insight. My husband’s company is also involved in some tech investments, and I often hear him say the rarest talent these days are those who understand both business and technology.”","The two naturally continued chatting, the conversation gradually drifting to the field of investments.","“Do you work in investments?” Liu Yutong asked.","The woman laughed. “Being called ‘big sister’ by someone as young as you makes me a bit shy. I’m actually forty-three.”","Liu Yutong was astonished, because the woman didn’t look a day over forty—she seemed around thirty and was quite beautiful.","“I really couldn’t tell. I feel like you’re not much older than me.”","“Really? Then I’ll take that as a compliment.”","The woman laughed even more heartily. “I rarely meet young people I connect with so well. This long flight, with you beside me to chat, has been truly pleasant.”","“Same here!”","Liu Yutong felt the same way—the conversation was remarkably easy and enjoyable.","From then on, they talked about tech trends and business logic, from studying and reading to clothes and skincare, chatting for about an hour.","“Little sister, although you’re very young, your perspective on issues is quite mature. I’ve met many young people your age, but it’s rare to find someone who combines business acumen with a focus on technology.”","“You’re too kind, big sister.”","Only then did the woman reveal the strange feeling she had had all along. “It’s weird—even though we’ve only just met, I feel especially close to you, as if I’ve known you for a long time.”","Liu Yutong: “I feel the same way.”","The woman smiled, and the warmth in it was bright. “Then it must be fate. Are you heading to the imperial capital this time to go back to school?”","Judging by Liu Yutong’s eloquence and demeanor, along with the flight’s destination, the woman naturally assumed she was a student at one of the top universities in the imperial capital, likely from a well-off family.","“This trip to the imperial capital is mainly because of an invitation from an elder,” Liu Yutong said.","“An elder? So are you from the imperial capital yourself?”","“No, I’m from Pearl City. I go to university there too. You might not have heard of it. This flight to the imperial capital is purely to broaden my horizons,” Liu Yutong explained.","“Pearl City? You’re in university in Pearl City?” At the mention of that name, the woman’s expression froze briefly, as if stirred by some unpleasant memory, and her face changed color.","“Yes, at Pearl City University of Finance and Economics. Do you know our city, big sister?” As soon as she spoke, Liu Yutong noticed the woman’s mood shift clearly—her face even turned slightly pale.","“Big sister, what’s wrong? Are you feeling unwell?”","“Should I call a flight attendant?”","“No, no need.”","The woman quickly waved her hand. “I just... suddenly remembered something from the past.”","Her gaze toward Liu Yutong grew complicated. “Pearl City is a wonderful place. I lived there in my youth.”","“Really? What a coincidence! So we’re practically from the same hometown. Haven’t you been back to visit in a long time?” Liu Yutong asked again.","The woman nodded. “I really haven’t been back for many years, and I don’t dare to go back. I lost too much there, including my daughter.”","Liu Yutong listened quietly, sensing that the woman’s mood had become low, as if she had touched on some painful memories.","After a long pause, the woman steadied herself and then said jokingly to Liu Yutong, “If my daughter were still with me, she’d probably be about your age.”","\"Is your daughter also in Bright Pearl City?\" Liu Yutong asked.","The woman nodded slowly. \"Many years ago, I left home for some reasons and left her behind. Over the years, I've always wanted to find her. I know roughly where she is, but I've never had the courage to go to her.\"","\"Why?\"","\"I owe her too much. I left her when she needed a mother's love the most. If I suddenly showed up now, saying I regret it and want to make amends—wouldn't it be too late? I'm terrified she'll hate me, even more afraid she won't want to acknowledge me.\"","Liu Yutong was silent for a moment.","She thought of her own mother, the woman who was a complete blur in her memory.","If her mother were still alive, if her mother suddenly appeared before her, what would her reaction be?","She didn't know either.","\"Sister, maybe you should give yourself a chance, and give her a chance too. You can't keep running away forever, can you?\"","\"Some regrets, if you never try to make up for them, may become permanent ones.\"","Perhaps moved by Liu Yutong's words, the woman gradually made up her mind.","\"You're right. I can't keep hiding from her. When I get back this time, I plan to go to Bright Pearl City and see her. Even if she hates me, I'll accept it. If I keep avoiding facing her, I'm afraid I'll regret it for the rest of my life.\"","\"I support you. Sister, when you arrive in Bright Pearl City, you can find me. I'll help you locate someone.\"","Liu Yutong truly felt a deep connection with the woman, and sensed that there must have been some unspeakable difficulty behind her leaving back then, or else she wouldn't be like this.","The woman wiped away her tears and forced a smile: \"Thank you. I don't know why, but talking to you about all this has made me feel much better.\"","\"You're welcome.\"","The two then chatted about other topics until they gradually grew sleepy, and each went to rest.","When Liu Yutong woke up, the plane's announcement was just playing, prompting that they were about to begin their descent.","The flight attendants began reminding passengers to fasten their seatbelts and adjust their seats.","Just before disembarking, Ms. Jiang suddenly asked, \"Little sister, how many days will you be staying in the Capital?\"","\"Probably a day or two. Once I've visited the elders, I'll head back to Bright Pearl City. There's a lot waiting for me there.\"","\"I see. If you have some free time while in the Capital, you're welcome to visit my home. It's out near Xishan, the environment is quite nice.\"","\"Thank you for the kind invitation, sister, but this trip is pretty packed. I probably won't have the time. Next time—if I ever come to the Capital again, I'll definitely pay a visit.\"","\"Alright, it's settled then. Next time you're in the Capital, be sure to contact me.\"","\"Absolutely.\"","The plane landed smoothly at Capital International Airport.","After getting off, they parted ways at the end of the jet bridge.","Walking out of the terminal, Liu Yutong quickly spotted Uncle Li's car—a very low-key black commercial vehicle.","Uncle Li personally got out to greet her: \"Yutong, you must have had a tiring journey.\"","\"Uncle Li, I feel bad making you come all the way to pick me up,\" Liu Yutong said with some humility.","\"Don't be so formal with your uncle. The Loongxin project is a high priority now. The leaders I'm taking you to meet today are all in charge of technology and industrial planning. Make a good impression and show them the potential of Loongxin,\" Uncle Li said.","\"I understand, Uncle Li,\" Liu Yutong nodded, and got into the car with him.","Meanwhile, at another exit of the airport's VIP channel.","The middle-aged woman had just stepped out when she saw a black Bentley parked at the entrance.","Standing beside the car was a man under fifty, with a refined, scholarly air. This was her current husband, Lin Dong, the head of the Capital's powerful Lin family.","Seeing Jiang Lu walk out, Lin Dong immediately got out of the car and personally opened the door for her.","\"Tired?\"","Jiang Lu smiled. \"Not too bad. Why did you come yourself? I told you the driver could have picked me up.\"","\"You've been abroad for half a month—I've missed you like crazy. If I hadn't come to get you myself, I'd have gone mad,\" Lin Dong said, his eyes full of affection as he took her suitcase and helped her into the car.","\"At our age, talking so cheesily,\" Jiang Lu laughed, her eyes filled with love.","\"Haha, young at heart! I always think we're still young,\" Lin Dong joked.","\"Come on, let's head home first.\"","\"Mm.\"","Just before getting into the car, Jiang Lu couldn't help but look back.","\"Lulu, what are you looking at?\" Lin Dong noticed her movement and asked curiously.","Jiang Lu: \"I met a girl on the plane. We talked the whole way, but I forgot to ask her name.\"","\"Do you want me to have someone look into it? The business class passenger list should have a record,\" Lin Dong said.","Jiang Lu shook her head: \"No need. Meeting someone you click with by chance doesn't have to lead anywhere. If fate wills it, we'll meet again.\"","\"Alright.\"","Once in the car, Lin Dong asked, \"How did the San Francisco negotiations go?\"","\"Pretty smoothly. The cooperation agreement with that biotech company has been signed. I'll have people follow up.\"","Lin Dong took her hand as he drove: \"You've worked hard. Actually, you could have let the subordinates handle these things. Why did you have to travel so far yourself?\"","\"This project is very important. I wasn't comfortable leaving it to others. Besides, I wanted to get out, to clear my head,\" Jiang Lu replied.","Lin Dong sensed a hint of unease in her tone: \"What's wrong? Did something happen on this trip? You seem a bit down.\"","Jiang Lu was silent for a while before shaking her head: \"It's nothing. Just tired from the long flight, I guess.\"","Lin Dong didn't press further: \"Then get some sleep. I'll wake you when we get home.\"","\"Mm.\" Jiang Lu nodded and closed her eyes.","Perhaps due to jet lag, even though she had slept for a few hours on the plane, she still felt sleepy.","Before she knew it, she had a nightmare.","In the dream, she was in a run-down little house. The air reeked of cigarette smoke, alcohol, and stale odors. A gambling addict was beating a very thin little girl with a belt.","The little girl was pitiful, curled up in a corner, crying heart-wrenchingly.","\"Stop hitting her! Don't hurt my daughter!\"","Jiang Lu rushed over like a madwoman, trying to shield the little girl, but her hands passed right through the girl's body again and again, unable to touch her.","\"You useless woman! What did you run away for?\"","The gambler turned his head, his face full of menace as he glared at her: \"If you hadn't run off, I wouldn't have lost so much money being unlucky! This brat is a jinx. I'll just beat her to death!\"","He raised his belt again and struck the little girl.","Jiang Lu could only watch helplessly as the belt fell on the child, powerless to stop it, crying in despair: \"Tongtong! My Tongtong!\"","\"...\"","\"Lulu! Lulu! What's wrong?\"","\"Jiang Lu! Wake up! Wake up!\"","\"...\"","After Lin Dong called out to her several times, Jiang Lu jolted awake from the nightmare, her face already soaked with tears.","The afterimages of the dream kept tearing at her nerves, making her body shake uncontrollably.","Lin Dong pulled the car over to the side of the road, reached over, and wrapped his arm tightly around her shoulders. \"Don't be afraid, don't be afraid. I'm here. It was just a dream.\"","Jiang Lu leaned against his shoulder, unable to hold it in any longer, and burst into tears. \"Lin Dong... I dreamed about Tongtong... She was so small and thin, and that man was hitting her with a belt. She was curled up in a corner, crying... I wanted to hold her, but I couldn't reach her... I couldn't save her... I couldn't do anything... Wuwuwu...\"","Seeing his wife like this, Lin Dong's heart ached deeply.","\"That wasn't your fault, Lu. It wasn't your fault. It was just a dream. Tongtong must be grown up now. She's your daughter, and she'll surely be as strong as you.\"","He knew about Jiang Lu's past, and he knew she had been thinking about that daughter all these years. But she rarely brought it up, perhaps because she was afraid to face her guilt for not being there for her daughter, or perhaps because she was worried he wouldn't be able to accept it. So she had kept it buried inside.","But they had known each other for over a decade and had been married for ten years this year. How could he possibly not accept his wife's daughter?","After a long while, Jiang Lu's sobbing finally began to subside.","Lin Dong comforted her some more, gently wiping away her tears with his hand, and then made a decision.","\"Lu, once I finish up what I'm working on, I'll personally go with you to Pearl City. We'll find Tongtong and bring her home. No matter what happened in the past, from now on, with me here, with us here, she will never suffer again. Your daughter is my daughter!\"","\"Really?\" Jiang Lu looked at her husband with tear-filled eyes.","\"Of course it's true. Three days from now. In three days, we'll go to Pearl City.\""]},{"number":707,"title":"Chapter 707: 707, Lin Family Gathering (Two-in-One)","paragraphs":["Imperial Capital, at the foot of the Western Hills, Lin Residence.","This traditional Chinese courtyard, covering nearly ten acres, was hidden behind layers of pine and cypress trees. If one did not approach closely, it would be hard to imagine that in this inch-of-gold, foot-of-silver Western Hills district, such a complete three-courtyard compound still existed.","The Imperial Capital had always been known as \"wealth in the east, nobility in the west.\" That the Lin family could own such an ancient residence here was enough to show that their ancestors were once a prominent and illustrious clan.","The car pulled into the Lin residence garage and stopped.","Jiang Lu's emotions had mostly calmed by now. Before her husband could unbuckle his seatbelt, she called out to him again.","\"Lin Dong, if we really bring Tongtong over, will your brothers and the rest of the family... will they agree?\"","Lin Dong had three brothers and one younger sister, and he was the third among them.","Logically, the position of head of the Lin family should never have fallen to Lin Dong, who had chosen the path of business. But misfortune struck unpredictably—many years ago, the old master Lin and his eldest son had met with tragedy one after another.","The eldest brother had been personally groomed by the old master as his successor. Had no accident occurred, he would likely have become a rising star in the political arena. With the old master backing him, his prospects would have been limitless.","But who could have known that this promising young man would rush to the front lines during a flood to rescue victims, only to be tragically killed, leaving behind a daughter. Shortly after, his wife took the girl back to her own family.","The old master himself had been in poor health, suffering from cancer. Struck by the blow of losing his son, he passed away in the hospital not long after.","It was because of the loss of both the eldest brother and the old master that the Lin family's fortunes plummeted.","Although the Lin family still wielded considerable influence, compared to when the old master and the eldest brother were alive, that influence was like heaven and earth apart. The family was in decline.","Among the remaining children, the second brother, Lin Liang, was easygoing by nature and had no ambition for power or wealth. He only loved walking his dogs and playing with his birds—a man without contention, utterly incapable of carrying the family's prestige.","The fourth brother had also taken the path of politics, working his way up the ranks in a certain ministry. After many years, he had only risen to a C-level position. While this rank might be considered someone high in local government, like a county leader, in the Imperial Capital, especially in the Western Hills district, there was a saying: throw a brick, and you could knock out a dozen people at the same level.","He was hardly enough to support the entire Lin family.","As for the youngest sister, the fifth child, there was no need to mention her—she was already married.","On his deathbed, the old master had seen through the Lin family's future. The eldest son had died young, the second son had no interest in the family business, and the youngest son's political career was mediocre. The family's glory could no longer be sustained.","Since the path to nobility was cut off, it was better to settle for second best and let his descendants live comfortably as wealthy commoners.","So he turned his gaze to his third son, Lin Dong, and appointed him the next head of the family.","However, Lin Dong's position as family head was not an easy one to bear.","In his early years, because of his relationship with Jiang Lu, his ties with the family had become very strained.","At that time, the old master and the eldest brother were still alive, and the entire family vehemently opposed him marrying a woman who had already given birth to a child. The Lin family was, after all, a wealthy and noble household. Let alone Jiang Lu, even many wealthy businessmen from the East District who wished to marry their daughters into the Lin family lacked the qualifications—let alone Jiang Lu, a woman without any background and with a previous marriage.","But after the old master passed away, Lin Dong used his authority as family head to forcefully marry Jiang Lu, which caused his relationship with the rest of the family to plunge almost to the freezing point.","They all felt that Lin Dong's actions had disgraced the Lin family and made them lose face in public. After all, Lin Dong was the head of the Lin family, the family's emblem of honor.","Moreover, ever since Jiang Lu married into the Lin family, she hadn't given birth to a single child, and her sisters-in-law and brothers had never treated her with any kindness.","In short, the complex dynamics within the family were also one of the reasons Jiang Lu had never dared to seek out her daughter.","As the saying goes, \"Entering a wealthy family is as deep as the sea\"—there were too many twists and turns inside. She was also worried that her daughter Tongtong wouldn't be able to handle this big, complicated household.","Additionally, as family head, Lin Dong had to take care of every family member, which put him under great pressure. Add to that his previous business setbacks, looming bankruptcy, and various other troubles... Jiang Lu had simply never brought up the matter of finding her daughter.","This sudden, intense urge to find her daughter was sparked by an accidental encounter on the plane with a like-minded young girl, which stirred the long-buried longing in her heart, now impossible to contain.","Seeing that her husband hadn't spoken, Jiang Lu hesitated and said, \"Lin Dong, if it's really too difficult, Tongtong doesn't have to join the Lin family. I... I could find a place outside and move out...\"","Before she could finish, Lin Dong cut her off.","\"Don't even think about moving out!\"","\"I told you, your daughter is my daughter too. This is my decision! I am the head of the Lin family now. When the old master entrusted the family property and this whole household to me on his deathbed, it wasn't so I could watch my wife suffer. I'll handle this matter—just don't worry about it!\"","Jiang Lu looked at him, deeply moved. But she knew all too well that the Lin family was never easy to manage.","Years ago, the old master had set a rule that the family would not be divided. Although it was meant to strengthen family unity, it also tied a heap of entanglements and disputes together.","Especially with the financial power firmly in Lin Dong’s hands, his sister-in-law and brother’s wife had long been discontented. Now, bringing in a granddaughter with no blood relation only made matters worse, and it was easy to imagine the fallout.","But she missed her daughter so much that in the end, she only whispered, “Thank you, husband.”","...","Two days later.","After handling urgent business at the company, Lin Dong called the family back ahead of schedule.","At six thirty in the evening, inside the dining hall adjacent to the main hall of the Lin residence, a redwood round table seating over twenty was already set with a full array of fine tableware.","The Lin family had to hold a family dinner every week—a rule set by the late patriarch. As long as a member of the Lin family was in the capital, they were required to return weekly for a meal to maintain family cohesion.","By the time Lin Dong and Jiang Lu entered the dining room, many were already seated.","The head seat was empty—it was Lin Dong’s seat.","To his immediate left sat the second brother, Lin Liang, in his early fifties, dressed in a loose cotton-linen Tang suit, spinning two walnuts in his hand while quietly chatting with his wife, Zhang Yu, beside him.","Zhang Yu was two years younger than Lin Liang and had kept herself quite well, but there was a pickiness in her eyes and brows.","Further down sat the fourth brother, Lin Zheng, with his wife, Wang Jiangyao.","Lin Zheng worked in a government ministry, just turned forty, wore gold-rimmed glasses, and always put on a stern expression—almost as if he were deliberately imitating the late patriarch.","Wang Jiangyao was the typical official’s wife, with a habit of speaking in a pretentious tone.","Across the table sat several of the younger generation.","Lin Liang’s son, Lin Shen, twenty-six, was coasting through a job at a foreign company; his daughter, Lin Yue, twenty-three, was still in graduate school.","Lin Zheng’s eldest son, Lin Feng, twenty-three, had entered the civil service; his second son, Lin Mian, eighteen, had just started college.","There was also a slightly withdrawn figure—Lin Feng, the son from Lin Dong’s deceased first wife. At twenty-two, he was a senior in college currently interning at the family company.","He sat a little farther from the head seat, looking down at his phone and sending messages. Seeing his father and Jiang Lu enter, he put away his phone and stood up along with the other younger members.","“Third Uncle, Third Aunt.”","“Dad...”","The juniors greeted them in a scattered manner.","Lin Dong nodded, took the head seat, and Jiang Lu sat beside him.","“Everyone’s here. Let’s start the meal,” Lin Dong instructed the servant waiting by the side.","Soon, one home-style dish after another was brought to the table, filling the entire spread.","At first, the dinner was relatively quiet—only the faint clatter of chopsticks and bowls, and soft sounds of chewing.","After a moment.","The more easygoing second brother, Lin Liang, slowly picked up a piece of fish with his chopsticks and was the first to speak: “Third Brother, I heard you invested in another new energy project last month?”","“Yeah, the prospects are good, and the government’s policies support it,” Lin Dong nodded, then had a servant serve Jiang Lu some soup.","“Business is getting bigger and bigger,” Lin Liang said with an ambiguous smile. “People like us, I guess we’ll just rely on you to keep us fed from now on.”","If someone else had said that, it would have sounded like deliberate sarcasm, but those who knew Lin Liang well understood he meant it literally—because he was content with his laid-back life and never wanted to worry about anything.","But his casual remark gave a few sharp-minded people an opening.","The fourth brother’s wife, Wang Jiangyao, seeing her chance, took over with a smile: “Third brother is capable, so of course we get to bask in the glory. By the way, Third Brother, your nephew Mian is going abroad for an exchange program next month, but the school only covers airfare. He has to pay for accommodation and living expenses himself—around forty to fifty thousand US dollars a month, right?”","Her meaning was obvious: she was asking for money.","In the past, Lin Dong would have at least asked about the expenses and immediately cut it in half—who needed that much every month just for an exchange program abroad?","The Lin family was indeed wealthy, but he didn’t approve of the younger generation squandering money. Forty to fifty thousand US dollars a month, converted, was over three hundred thousand yuan—far beyond necessary expenses.","But this time, Lin Dong broke his usual pattern. Without asking a single question, he agreed.","“It’s good for a child to go abroad and broaden his horizons. The expenses will come from the family fund.”","“Then thanks, Third Brother.” Wang Jiangyao smiled in satisfaction and shot a quick glance at her younger son.","She had been prepared to haggle with Lin Dong, but hadn’t expected things to go so smoothly.","Lin Mian promptly and obediently thanked him: “Thank you, Third Uncle.”","Lin Shen, seeing that their third uncle was in such an accommodating mood today, quickly chimed in: “Third Uncle, my car’s been running for five years and keeps breaking down. I’ve got my eye on a new Porsche—nothing too pricey, just a bit over a million. Do you think...”","He had long wanted a sports car. Without one, he couldn’t hold his head up among the younger circles in the capital. While those in the west side of the city were more low-key than the east side, constantly driving a beaten-up Audi A4 was really dragging him down.","However, every time he mentioned changing cars, Third Uncle would always refuse on the grounds of not being wasteful or indulgent, and none of the younger generation’s cars had ever cost more than five hundred thousand yuan, let alone owning a sports car. This time when he brought up the old topic, he didn’t really have much hope—he was just testing the waters since Third Uncle seemed in a good mood today. After all, he had thick skin.","To his surprise, Lin Dong agreed readily this time: “If you like it, buy it. Go find my secretary later to handle the paperwork.”","Lin Shen was stunned, thinking he had misheard: “Third Uncle, are you serious?”","“Mm.”","Lin Dong nodded and then looked at the other younger ones: “Xiao Yue, Xiao Feng, is there anything you want? Let’s settle it all today.”","At these words, everyone at the table froze.","Had the sun risen from the west today?","Even Lin Feng, who had been silent all along, looked up and gave his father a deep, searching glance.","Something was off—very off.","The first to speak was the only girl among the younger generation at the table, Lin Yue: “Third Uncle, I’ve had my eye on a Hermès bag, but it’s a bit pricey—over a hundred thousand...”","“Buy it.”","After Lin Yue’s successful test, the others grew bolder.","“I want to upgrade to a top-of-the-line gaming laptop, over fifty thousand...”","“Buy it.”","“I want the latest model phone...”","“Buy it.”","“...”","“Whatever you want today, my answer is just one word—buy!”","The younger ones cheered with excitement.","“Long live Third Uncle!”","“I love you, Third Uncle!”","“Thank you, Third Uncle... Third Uncle!”","“...”","Watching the giddy younger generation across the table, the second brother’s wife, Zhang Yu, couldn’t help muttering under her breath: “Third Brother is this generous today? Did the sun rise from the west?”","Lin Liang also set down his walnuts, squinting as he carefully studied his younger brother: “I reckon Third Brother has something on his mind.”","Lin Dong’s behavior today was indeed too unusual.","Lin Dong noticed his second brother and the others’ stares. Using his chopsticks, he placed a large shrimp on Jiang Lu’s plate, then calmly said to them: “We’re all family. If the kids have needs and I can meet them, of course I will. Last year during the financial crisis, business was tight on funds. Now that cash flow has eased up, money that needs to be spent should be spent.”","His words sounded noble enough, but everyone at the table was sharp; hardly anyone believed him.","The fourth brother’s wife, Wang Jiangyao, rolled her eyes thoughtfully and said with a smile: “Third Brother is right—we’re all family. But I think the kids are grown up now, and some things should be settled. For instance, the distribution of family shares. When the old man passed away, he only said you’d be in charge—he didn’t say all the shares belong to you alone, did he?”","Finally, they were getting to the real topic.","Lin Dong set down his chopsticks and wiped his mouth with a napkin: “What do you mean by that, Sister-in-law?”","“What could I mean?”","Wang Jiangyao said with feigned innocence: “I just think that now that the company has grown so big, with annual profits in the hundreds of millions, we uncles and aunts only get a monthly allowance and nothing else. The kids have to submit requests every time they want something—you’d think the Lin family is scraping by.”","Second sister-in-law Zhang Yu couldn’t help chiming in: “That’s right, Third Brother. It’s not that we’re greedy, but think about it—without the old man back then, without the family’s support, could you have built the company this big? Don’t take this the wrong way, but the company itself is the Lin family’s shared property. Now that you’re the head of the family, you can’t just hog it all, can you?”","The conversation was growing sharper.","The fourth brother, Lin Zheng, gave a soft cough, pretending to mediate: “Everyone, say less. Third Brother’s job running such a big company isn’t easy either.”","Just then, the silent Lin Feng let out a cold laugh.","“What are you laughing at?” Lin Shen, not far away, heard it and shot a dissatisfied glare at his cousin.","Lin Feng: “Nothing. I just find your words amusing. When my father’s company was on the verge of bankruptcy, no one said a word. Now that it’s making money, everyone wants a piece of the pie. Have some shame!”","“Lin Feng!”","Fourth Uncle Lin Zheng immediately scolded: “How dare you speak like that? Are you saying we’re all taking advantage of your family?”","“Did I say anything wrong?”","Lin Feng looked up, his face cold: “About ten years ago during the financial crisis, my father’s company had a cash flow break, and the banks were hounding us at home. Back then, why didn’t anyone mention shares? Why didn’t anyone say we should share the risk? After the company turned around, suddenly everyone remembers they’re part of the Lin family.","“If it weren’t for Aunt Jiang using her connections at the investment bank to broker an emergency loan for my father, landing a few big clients, and later securing a bank loan, the company would have collapsed long ago! You should count yourselves lucky you’re living this life of luxury and fine clothes!”","His words left no room for face, effectively calling them a bunch of ungrateful parasites and bloodsuckers.","Second Aunt Zhang Yu’s face turned crimson. \"What kind of talk is that, child? We tried to come up with ideas back then, didn’t we?\"","\"Ideas? What ideas? Second Aunt, if you had just opened your mouth back then to borrow some money from the Zhang family, my father wouldn’t have struggled so much! Ideas, my foot!\"","\"You!\"","\"Enough!\" Lin Dong slammed the table, cutting off the argument.","He looked at Lin Feng, a flicker of relief in his eyes. This kid had never liked his stepmother, but he never expected him to stand up for her at such a critical moment—this caught him off guard.","\"Let’s not dwell on the past.\"","\"The reason I called everyone here for dinner today is that I have something to say.\"","\"I want to bring Lu Lu’s daughter to the Lin family and have her formally entered into the Lin family lineage.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the entire room was stunned!"]},{"number":708,"title":"Chapter 708: 708, Looking for Someone (Two-in-One)","paragraphs":["Let's not dwell on the past.","The reason I called everyone here for dinner today is that there's something I need to discuss.","As soon as Lin Dong said this, everyone put down their chopsticks and fixed their eyes on him.","Jiang Lu nervously clasped Lin Dong's hand under the table, knowing exactly what her husband was about to say.","Lin Dong squeezed her hand back, signaling her to stay calm, and then spoke: \"Before I get to the main point, I want to ask you all: Is there anything unsatisfied with your current lives? Any requests? Bring them up today, and if I can resolve them, I will.\"","This left everyone exchanging glances.","Lin Liang was the first to react: \"Third brother, are you... planning to split the family?\"","\"It's not about splitting the family.\"","Lin Dong shook his head. \"Before he passed, Father instructed that the Lin family must not fall apart. I just want everyone to live better, with less resentment and more harmony.\"","Wang Jiangyao immediately cut in: \"What about the shares?\"","She still couldn't let go of that topic.","\"The company shares can't be touched for now.\"","Lin Dong left her no room for negotiation. Changing the shareholding structure would bring too much trouble and complexity.","But he hadn't come unprepared.","\"While the shares can't be moved, I can allocate more dividends to you from the annual profits. The exact proportion will be calculated by the finance department. Also, if the younger generation wants to join the company after college, I can arrange positions for them. If they want to start their own businesses instead, I'll support them with startup funds.\"","These terms were quite generous, essentially providing them with a safety net.","Though Zhang Yu, Wang Jiangyao, and the others still felt dissatisfied, they could grudgingly accept it—it was far better than before.","Second brother Lin Liang toyed with his walnuts, speaking slowly: \"Third brother, you're being so generous today. Is there something you want to say?\"","Finally, someone hit the key point.","Lin Dong didn't beat around the bush either. He stated his purpose directly: \"I want to bring Lu Lu's daughter back home.\"","The moment he said this, the dining room fell into dead silence.","A few seconds later.","Wang Jiangyao broke the silence first, voicing her opposition: \"What? Third brother, you want to bring Jiang Lu's daughter—that illegitimate child from outside—into the Lin family?\"","Lin Dong's temper flared at her words: \"Watch your mouth!\"","Wang Jiangyao was startled but still unconvinced: \"Did I say something wrong? That child Jiang Lu gave birth to before she married into our family has nothing to do with the Lin family! Why should we bring her back?\"","Second sister-in-law Zhang Yu also frowned: \"Third brother, this is inappropriate. What kind of standing does our Lin family have? Suddenly bringing in an outsider's surname—what will others think?\"","Fourth brother Lin Zheng pushed up his glasses and added: \"Third brother, it's not that we're being unreasonable, but you need to consider the Lin family. That child would be in an awkward position to begin with. And how old is she now? An adult, right? Having a sudden sister appear—don't you think Xiao Feng will have something to say?\"","Everyone's gaze shifted to Lin Feng. Though they didn't want to admit it, the fact was that Lin Feng was the most likely heir to Lin Dong's estate.","Lin Feng remained expressionless, continuing to fiddle with his phone and send text messages, adopting a detached attitude. His demeanor was much like his second uncle's—laid-back, but also shrewd. By not taking sides, he avoided being used as a pawn.","Jiang Lu wanted to say something, but she knew she wasn't well-liked among the Lin family. Speaking up might only add fuel to the fire.","Lin Dong was tired of wasting words. He took a firm stance: \"You all seem to have misunderstood something. I'm not here to ask for your consent today. I'm here to inform you!\"","\"Third brother!\"","Lin Liang slammed the table: \"Have you lost your mind? Are you willing to turn against the entire family for the sake of another person's daughter?\"","Though he was the most easygoing among them, that didn't mean he'd turn a blind eye to everything. Even he found it hard to agree to letting someone with no blood relation to the Lin family be brought into the fold.","Lin Dong didn't back down an inch: \"Second brother, she's not an outsider. She's Lu Lu's daughter, which means she's my daughter!\"","\"Your daughter?\"","Zhang Yu questioned skeptically: \"Have you raised her for even a single day? Changed her diaper? Taught her to talk? Now, out of nowhere, you want to claim her as your daughter. Do you even know if she'll accept you?\"","This struck a nerve with Jiang Lu. Indeed, it might be too soon to talk about all this.","Whether Tongtong would be willing to recognize her or accept Lin Dong as a stepfather was still uncertain.","It was very possible that this was just wishful thinking on their part.","Lin Dong: \"Precisely because I haven't raised her for a single day, I need to make it up to her even more. Do you all know what Lu Lu has endured all these years? She endured ten years of suffering for me, for this so-called dignity of the Lin family! I can't watch her continue to endure the pain of separation from her mother and daughter just because of your ridiculous notions of social standing!\"","\"And another thing—haven't you all been whispering behind her back, wondering why Lu Lu couldn't have children? Fine, today I'll tell you. It's because she felt guilty about Tongtong and was afraid it would upset Xiao Feng! Before we even got married, she voluntarily signed an agreement with me, in black and white, renouncing any right to inherit any of my assets. She married me never for the Lin family's money!\"","\"It's our Lin family that owes her!\"","Hearing his father's words, Lin Feng paused in his phone scrolling. This was the first time he'd learned the real reason behind it. He had always assumed that his stepmother Jiang Lu simply couldn't have children, or else she would have given birth to many sons to compete with him for favor and inheritance.","He never expected the truth to be like this.","Seeing the silence, Lin Dong continued: \"You keep going on about the Lin family's standing, the Lin family's face. Do you still think we're in the same position as when Father was alive? You all know damn well what state our family is in now! And when Father was alive, what did he teach us? 'If the household is not at peace, how can one settle the world?' And now? For the sake of your petty vanity, you've abandoned even the most basic familial bonds!\"","\"That's different!\"","Wang Jiangyao retorted: \"That was something that happened before Jiang Lu married in! It has nothing to do with the Lin family!\"","Lin Dong stared at her: \"How is it not related?\"","\"Lu Lu is my wife. Her matters are my matters, and they are the Lin family's matters! I'm laying it out clearly today: I've accepted this daughter. I will bring her back, and I'll even change her surname to Lin. She'll have her name entered into the family genealogy!\"","\"Don't you dare!\"","Fourth brother Lin Zheng slammed the table and stood up: \"Lin Dong, don't think that just because you're the head of the household, you can do whatever you want. We don't agree, and let's see if she can even step through this door!\"","\"Fourth brother, sister-in-law, and second brother, second sister-in-law.\"","Lin Dong recited each of their names and then let out a cold laugh: \"Do you have some kind of amnesia? Do I really need to repeat who's in charge of this household now?\"","Everyone's expressions froze.","\"The company's shares—though they haven't been divided—the controlling stake is in my hands. The family fund's management rights are mine. The deed to this ancestral house is also under my name.\"","\"From the very beginning, I wasn't negotiating with you. I was telling you my decision. If you agree, good. If not, you are free to move out.\"","\"Third Brother, what kind of talk is that? Are you threatening your own family?\" Lin Liang also put on a stern face.","\"You’re the ones forcing me. I’ve asked myself over the years—I’ve done right by every member of the Lin family. Most of the money the company made went to family expenses. The house you live in, the nice cars you drive, the elite schools your kids attend—none of that would have been possible without me. But now, Lu Lu and I just want to bring back a daughter we lost years ago, and you all put up obstacle after obstacle. On what ground?\"","\"Let me make this clear—none of you have the right to stop me!\"","The fourth brother, Lin Zheng, softened his tone, perhaps genuinely afraid that Lin Dong might impulsively kick them all out. \"Third Brother, don’t get so worked up. Everyone’s just having a hard time accepting it. After all, that child has no blood ties to the Lin family. Suddenly bringing her in really doesn’t seem right.\"","\"Fourth Brother, don’t talk to me about blood ties. Xiao Feng is blood-related to you—have any of you ever truly cared about him? After his mother passed away unexpectedly, who among you showed him genuine concern? Now you want to lecture me about blood relations?\"","Just then, Lin Feng suddenly stood up without warning.","The others all turned to look at him again. At this moment, his words carried the most weight. Lin Dong could be ruthless with other Lin family members, but he would never be heartless toward his only son, whom he had neglected for years.","Even Jiang Lu grew tense. She too feared that her stepson might suddenly blurt out, \"I oppose!\"","But Lin Feng’s answer caught everyone off guard.","\"I agree!\"","\"Xiao Feng, you—\" Lin Feng’s second uncle and aunt stared at him in disbelief.","Lin Feng couldn’t be bothered to look at them. He fixed his gaze on his father, Lin Dong. \"I agree to bring her back.\"","\"Why?\"","The eldest cousin, Lin Shen, couldn’t help but say, \"If she really joins the Lin family, that means she’ll get a share of your inheritance. Are you being stupid or what?\"","Lin Feng turned to him, his expression as if he were the one looking at a fool. \"You think everyone’s like you—only seeing money?\"","Then he walked over to Jiang Lu, the woman he had once hated, rejected, and never once called \"Mom.\" He pulled out a tissue and handed it to her.","The gesture made Jiang Lu tremble. She raised her tear-filled eyes to look at him.","\"Auntie,\" he said, still unable to bring himself to use the word that felt so awkward. \"Don’t cry. Bring her back. This home is too cold. Maybe with one more person, it’ll warm up a little.\"","Jiang Lu couldn’t hold back anymore. She threw her arms around him and sobbed loudly.","Lin Dong watched the scene with deep relief. To be honest, he had been afraid his son would oppose, and that would have made things truly difficult.","Since his son had no objection, everything became straightforward.","\"It’s settled. I’ll go to Pearl City tomorrow to bring my daughter back. Before she arrives, I want you all to think clearly—do you still want to be a family, or do we go our separate ways? Those who want to leave, I won’t stop you, and I’ll give you every penny you’re due. But those who stay—no more useless talk!\"","The dining room fell into dead silence.","Second Brother, Lin Liang, looked at his younger brother’s resolute expression, then at his sister-in-law Jiang Lu and nephew Lin Feng. Finally, he let out a long sigh and sat back down.","\"Whatever you say. After all, this household has long been run by you.\"","Seeing that the outcome was inevitable, the others swallowed their complaints for the time being, even if resentment lingered.","Lin Dong knew all too well that they were only temporarily compromising. The real conflict was yet to come.","But he didn’t care.","He helped Jiang Lu sit back down and said to the servant, \"The food’s cold. Heat it up.\"","Then he poured Jiang Lu a bowl of soup. \"Eat more. Rest well tonight and regain your strength. Tomorrow, we’ll head to Pearl City and bring our daughter home.\"","At that moment, Lin Feng spoke up: \"I’ll go too. It’ll be a nice break.\"","Jiang Lu looked at the father and son, tears turning into a smile, and nodded vigorously.","...........","The next afternoon.","A black Bentley entered the territory of Pearl City.","Jiang Lu sat in the car, staring at the rapidly passing scenery outside the window, her heartbeat quickening.","This city, which she had left nearly twenty years ago, had changed enormously. Although it was far from being as grand as the imperial capital, it was now filled with high-rises and thoroughly modernized.","And here, she saw many familiar red figures—the delivery riders for Wanhui Preferred. There were plenty of them in the imperial capital too.","The uniform of Wanhui Preferred riders was predominantly red, and so were the work clothes of employees in other Wanglong Group businesses, such as supermarkets, internet cafés, restaurants, and tea shops—mostly red in color, just with different styles and accents.","Aside from red, the other dominant color was naturally black.","Lin Dong, sitting beside Jiang Lu, also noticed these red figures and couldn’t help commenting, \"These Wanhui Preferred delivery guys are everywhere in Pearl City. They’re common in the imperial capital too, but not this dense.\"","Jiang Lu nodded. \"Yeah, it does feel like there are more here.\"","Lin Dong seemed to sense that his wife’s mind was elsewhere, so he didn’t press the topic. \"Lu Lu, take it easy. We’ll go slow.\"","Jiang Lu forced a smile. \"I’m not anxious.\"","But the slight sweat on her palms gave her away—how could she not be anxious?","The car finally stopped in front of a five-star hotel.","Lin Dong had already asked his secretary to arrange accommodations—a top-floor suite with an excellent view overlooking most of Pearl City.","Not long after they checked in.","The people Lin Dong had sent ahead to investigate in the countryside called with a rough report.","As soon as he hung up, Jiang Lu couldn’t wait to ask, \"Did you get news about Tongtong?\"","Lin Dong’s initially serious expression broke into a smile.","\"We did. This trip wasn’t in vain.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Tongtong isn’t in the countryside. She’s in Pearl City.\"","\"That girl has really made something of herself—very much so. She got into the Finance University in Pearl City, a key provincial school. That proves she’s smart and hardworking, and she’s managed to take care of herself well. You don’t need to worry too much.\"","\"And also, that gambler is behind bars. What goes around comes around!\"","He then relayed to his wife all the information his men had gathered.","After hearing it, Jiang Lu felt a huge weight lift off her heart. \"That’s good, that’s good... She grew up safe and sound and even got into such a good university. I... I really...\"","For a moment, she didn’t know what to say.","Lin Dong: \"Not worried anymore, are you?\"","Jiang Lu nodded. She had been terrified that the news would be about her daughter suffering miserably, being mistreated by that gambler.","Thankfully, all the reports were good.","The previously tense atmosphere lightened noticeably, and a smile appeared on Jiang Lu’s face.","Of course, this only strengthened her resolve to make up for her daughter in the future.","After all, for her daughter to get into university under those circumstances, she must have put in an unimaginable amount of effort.","\"But...\"","\"But what?\"","\"The person I arranged said that when they went to inquire about Tongtong's whereabouts, they always found that village very strange.\"","\"Strange?\" Jiang Lu was taken aback, her heart clenching again, afraid to hear any bad news.","\"It's not a bad kind of strange.\"","Lin Dong explained, \"My assistant, the one I sent to investigate, said that whenever the villagers mentioned Tongtong's name, they kept nodding and giving thumbs up, and they were constantly saying good things, emphasizing it heavily—almost like they were afraid my assistant wouldn't believe them. It was really eerie.\"","\"Ask one person, and it's the same. Ask ten people, and it's the same.\"","Just then, Lin Feng, who had been silent so far, couldn't help but say, \"Dad, you're overthinking it. Maybe she's the only university student from that village? Doesn't everyone say that in those rural areas, a college student is a rare gem? It's normal for a village that finally produces a university student to boast about her. And since she's only twenty years old, as Aunt Jiang said, she's just a young girl. It's not like she can eat people, right?\"","Lin Dong thought it over and found it reasonable. \"That's true—maybe I'm overthinking.\"","He then turned to Jiang Lu. \"Don't worry. Tomorrow, we'll go to the school to find her. We'll talk about everything when we see her.\"","..."]},{"number":709,"title":"Chapter 709: 709, Jiang Lu's Experience (Two-in-One) [Thanks to Zhizhi O for the Great God Certification]","paragraphs":["Lin Dong still had quite a few doubts lingering in his mind.","For example, when his assistant tried to ask the villagers for a photo of Tongtong, the villagers who lived there naturally wouldn’t have any pictures. Back then, phone functions weren’t powerful enough yet, and many villagers’ phones didn’t even have cameras.","Even if some did, why would they casually take pictures of the Liu family’s granddaughter?","Later, the assistant did find the Liu family home and was surprised to discover that the household actually owned a rather grand villa in the village. He figured he must have the wrong place, so he didn’t go in to ask—definitely not because two large wolfdogs were barking at the gate.","But when he went back to inquire more details about the young lady from the villagers, no one was willing to say anything more. In fact, the villagers grew wary.","Quite a few people had come to the village asking about the Liu family’s granddaughter—some were business owners, others were officials. But people like them, who knew almost nothing and even asked for a photo, were far too suspicious.","Especially since their excuse was so flimsy; they claimed they were searching for a lost relative.","The villagers naturally assumed they were some distant, maybe even completely unrelated, relatives hoping to latch onto the Liu family’s granddaughter, so they weren’t given any friendly treatment.","In the end, the assistant only managed to learn that the young lady studied at Mingzhu City, with no other information available.","When this news reached Lin Dong, although he found it strange, he later figured it might just be that the country folks were too exclusive and didn’t think much of it.","Like his son had said, the girl was at most twenty years old—perhaps even younger by her birthday. At that age, what kind of trouble could she cause?","More likely, the honest villagers were just protective of their village’s rising star and didn’t want to reveal too much.","That evening, the family of three dined at Yuyue Fang.","It was a restaurant recommended by their hotel’s concierge, said to be quite famous locally. The signature dish, Little Fish Guotie, was a must-try for outsiders, according to the staff.","Without a second thought, Lin Dong had the driver take them to the branch near the university district.","In fact, there was a branch near their hotel as well, but choosing the one by the university meant being nearer to the University of Finance and Economics. They could take a stroll around after dinner and get a sense of Tongtong’s living environment.","When they arrived, they realized just how popular the place was.","It was only a little past five in the afternoon, and the restaurant was nearly full.","Instead of opting for a quieter private room, they chose the main hall because they saw many university students dining there. They figured they could pick up some information about the university area from the students’ conversations.","The three of them were led by a waiter dressed in an antique-style red uniform and seated at a table for four.","When ordering, Lin Dong didn’t even glance at the menu. He simply told the waiter to bring out a few signature dishes, then began looking around the restaurant with interest.","“This restaurant is something special—not like ordinary places. The staff are full of energy, and the Chinese-style décor shows good taste.”","As a businessman who frequented high-end venues, he had a sharp eye for service quality.","The warmth of the Yuyue Fang staff didn’t feel like the mechanical, trained smiles typical of other places; instead, it carried a genuine sense of vitality and pride.","That was rare, and it showed that the owner managed things well.","Soon, several dishes arrived.","The most striking was the iron pot placed on a wooden base. When the lid was lifted, a rich, savory aroma burst forth—the signature Little Fish Guotie.","Golden, glossy little fish bubbled in the broth at the bottom of the pot, surrounded by a ring of hand-pressed flatbreads. Just looking at it was mouthwatering.","“Please, enjoy.”","The waiter thoughtfully used shared chopsticks to portion the flatbreads into each person’s plate and explained the best way to eat it—dipping the bread into the delicious fish broth.","In fact, this cooking method was more commonly associated with Guo Tie Ji (iron pot chicken), while Little Fish Guotie was rarely found in restaurants because sourcing the ingredients was a major challenge.","Chicken was far easier to get than those palm-sized fish. These small fish could only be obtained in large quantities in water-rich regions and at high costs.","When Jiang Lu saw the dish, she felt a pang of nostalgia, recalling the Little Fish Guotie she once made with freshly caught tiny fish in the countryside.","Lin Dong was the first to pick up a piece of flatbread, dipped it in the broth, and put it in his mouth. His eyes brightened slightly.","“The bread is crispy on the outside and soft on the inside, especially with that rich, salty fish broth. Great texture. Lu, you have to try it.”","Jiang Lu also took a piece of fish and tasted it. “The fish is very fresh—delicious.”","Lin Feng, too, praised the dish, saying it was the best fish stew he had ever eaten.","Besides the Little Fish Guotie, the other dishes were also excellent. Not a single one gave them anything to complain about.","That was rare in a small place like Mingzhu City.","What they didn’t know was that every dish at Yuyue Fang had to go through a tasting evaluation by all the local staff and chefs. Only those that gained approval from over ninety percent of the people could be added to the menu.","Apart from a few fixed signature dishes, the menu at each branch varied based on the chefs’ specialties, so every location had its own unique flair.","The only downside was that this model made opening new branches a very slow process.","During the meal, they experienced the meticulousness of Yuyue Fang’s service once again.","Their tea was refilled the moment it ran low, their bone china plates were changed promptly, and the staff kept a constant eye on every table’s needs without being intrusive.","A woman who seemed to be a shift supervisor noticed that Jiang Lu appeared to have a low tolerance for spicy food and proactively asked if she wanted the broth of the Little Fish Guotie adjusted to be milder. Soon, she brought over a small bowl of specially prepared, non-spicy clear broth for Jiang Lu to dip her food in.","“This service level has plenty to teach other restaurants. The best part is how natural it feels, so comfortable. To train the staff to this degree, the owner must be someone truly remarkable,” Lin Dong remarked again.","“Dad, do you think this restaurant belongs to some big group?” Lin Feng asked as he munched on his flatbread.","Before Lin Dong could reply, a group of students at the next table answered for him.","“Buddy, you guessed right. This restaurant is under the biggest local group, Wanlong Group.”","“Wanlong? Sounds like something from the underworld?” Lin Feng said instinctively when he heard the name.","The student immediately made a shushing gesture: “Hey! You can’t say that! Wanlong Group... ah no, Wanlong Corporation— it’s one of Mingzhu City’s top responsible enterprises. They’ve created a ton of jobs, done a lot of charity, and most importantly, they’re very law-abiding! Lots of seniors from our university want to join their company after graduation!”","Lin Feng felt there was something odd about the student’s tone and pressed further: “That impressive? The owner must be a big shot, right?”","Another student nodded: “More than a big shot— practically someone with connections in high places. And they started from scratch, white-handed... most importantly, they’re still a student in school.”","Lin Dong: “......”","Lin Feng: “......”","Heads in high places? Started from scratch?","Lin Feng leaned close to his father’s ear and whispered, “Dad, don’t you think the way they talk is weird?”","Even though those students had quickly corrected themselves, he was sure he hadn’t misheard—what they meant to say was “black,” not “white.”","“Mm, strange behavior hints at something unusual. This Wanlong Group is definitely not simple.”","Lin Dong, who had lived for over half a century, was well-traveled. He knew that some local enterprises had shady origins before gradually cleaning up their acts after becoming big.","This Wanlong Association was probably that kind of company.","Still, he didn’t pry further. They had no dealings with the Wanlong Association anyway—they were just here to find someone.","Even if they did end up clashing with them, he wasn’t afraid. Although the Lin family was no longer what it once was, the connections his father had left behind were still partly intact. If trouble arose, they could still call in a favor.","After finishing that topic, they dug into their meal.","About halfway through dinner, Jiang Lu suddenly remembered something. “Oh, that girl I met on the plane—I should have asked for her contact information back then.”","Lin Dong asked, “The one you mentioned earlier, that you got along so well with?”","Jiang Lu nodded. “Yeah, she’s in this city too, and she’s also studying at the University of Finance and Economics.”","“If I’d asked for her contact info, maybe I could have asked her for help. She might have run into Tongtong on campus, maybe they even know each other?”","As she said this, she really did regret it. First of all, she and that girl had hit it off so well. If the girl could have helped her out, it would have made getting closer to her daughter Tongtong much easier—at the very least, she could have gotten a sense of Tongtong’s campus life.","Lin Dong comforted her, “It’s okay. We’re going straight to the school to look for her tomorrow anyway. As long as Tongtong is at the University of Finance and Economics, we’re bound to find her.”","Jiang Lu nodded.","Just then, Lin Feng couldn’t help asking Jiang Lu a question. “Aunt Jiang, what exactly did you go through back then?”","Before, he had never been interested in his stepmother Jiang Lu’s past. But ever since his father had told him about the things she had done, his attitude had gradually changed. He now wanted to take the initiative to understand her history.","Lin Dong frowned. “Xiao Feng, that’s not something you should be asking about.”","“It’s fine.”","Jiang Lu interrupted her husband. “Xiao Feng, if you want to know, I can tell you. There are some things I couldn’t hide from you all forever.”","Seeing that his wife was willing, Lin Dong didn’t object.","But the very first thing Jiang Lu said stunned both father and son.","Jiang Lu said, “I actually have... two daughters.”","Lin Dong nearly dropped his teacup. “What? Two?”","In all ten years of marriage, he had never once heard his wife mention that she had another daughter!","Lin Feng was also taken aback. What was going on? Hadn’t it always been said that there was only that sister Tongtong, whom he had never met? How had it become two?","Jiang Lu explained, “Tongtong is my younger daughter. My older daughter, Niannian (meaning 'yearning'), went missing shortly after she was born. I suspect she was kidnapped.”","“I searched for her for a long time back then—I went to the police, posted missing person notices, used every connection I had, but I just couldn’t find her. I cried every day until I was nearly broken, and I could only keep going by relying on medication for my mental health.","My ex-husband was named Liu Lei. He used to be a police officer, but I don’t think he was a competent cop or a competent father.","As a father, he didn’t bother looking for our daughter. He always brushed me off with excuses about being too busy. As a police officer, he spent his time hanging around with gang members. Later, I found out he had been dismissed for misconduct and had become the boss of a powerful triad in Mingzhu City.","In the end, I was completely disappointed in him. A man who didn’t care that his own biological daughter was missing, who quit being a cop to join the underworld—a total scumbag. Why should I stay with him? So I asked for a divorce.","He agreed to it. After the paperwork was done, I left Mingzhu City. I was already pregnant with Tongtong at the time, but he didn’t know.","Later... I never expected to be targeted by human traffickers. When I woke up, I had been sold to some gambling addict in the countryside. He paid money to buy me, locked me up, and forced me to become his wife.","In the end, for the sake of the child in my belly, I gave in. I thought I could live out my life as an ordinary peasant. But what I didn’t expect was that he was hooked on gambling and beating people. His ex-wife had run away because of that.","After Tongtong was born, I couldn’t take it anymore. One night, when he went out to gamble again, I escaped overnight.","It’s ridiculous to say, but that gambling addict always believed Tongtong was the result of a drunken fling. Actually, I never had any physical relationship with him.","After I got away, my mental condition worsened. I kept having hallucinations, always hearing both of my children calling ‘Mommy,’ always feeling like someone was chasing me... Until I eventually made my way back to my parents’ home. I stayed there for three years, but both my parents passed away during that time...”","“After that, I went to the capital. There, I found a professional psychiatrist. I underwent treatment for a long time and slowly crawled out of the shadows.","Then I taught myself finance and got into an investment bank... and finally, I met your father.”","“Meeting your father has been the luckiest thing in my life from start to finish. He didn’t look down on my past, didn’t care about my history of mental illness, and even accepted the fact that I had a daughter...”","As she said this, her eyes were full of love for Lin Dong. If it weren’t for this man, she might never have made it.","Lin Dong reached out and held her hand. His voice was full of tenderness. “Lulu, you’ve been through so much. Why did you never tell me any of this?”","Although he had known some general things about his wife, he had never imagined her journey had been this hard.","Jiang Lu’s eyes welled up. “I was afraid you would look down on me, afraid you would think my past was too shameful... and besides, I really couldn’t bear to go back and relive those days.”","Lin Feng was silent for a long time before he spoke to apologize. “Auntie, I’m sorry.”","He genuinely hadn’t realized that his stepmother’s past had been so traumatic and painful. An unlucky marriage, a kidnapped daughter, imprisonment and domestic abuse, losing her parents early... It all read like a story of blood and tears.","At the same time, he was stunned by her incredible ability to learn and her resilience.","A woman who had endured so much misery, who had been almost entirely cut off from society until she hit thirty, who had once been on the verge of mental collapse—and yet she had managed to teach herself finance, work in an investment bank, and even help his father save the Lin Group from disaster.","Who knew how far she could have gone if she hadn’t married so early?","No wonder his dad was utterly devoted to her. Forget her looks and grace—he wasn’t being vulgar, okay? Without a decent appearance, his dad probably wouldn’t have fallen for his stepmother in the first place.","But what really mattered was her strength, her abilities, her gentleness and wisdom. Those were what made her truly rare.","If you didn’t consider her past, she could almost be called perfect.","It made sense that his father would be captivated.","“Xiao Feng, you don’t need to apologize.”","Jiang Lu said, \"You're part of this family too, so you have the right to know about our past. Maybe someday I'll even find my eldest daughter. The hope is slim... but I'll still do my best to search for her.\"","Lin Dong said, \"You can definitely do it!\"","Lin Feng said, \"Aunt, I'll help you look for her too!\"","At the same time,","in a private room upstairs at Yuyue Restaurant,","Liu Yutong and Gao Min were organizing the leads they'd dug up from Zhao Weixiang.","\"Sister, Zhao Weixiang confessed to a lot, including who really killed our dad back then.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"It was Jiang Yuan, right?\"","Gao Min nodded. \"This Jiang Yuan is no ordinary man. He's a well-known patriotic businessman in Hong Kong City, a regular at charity galas, and holds seven or eight titles like committee member of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference. On the surface, he looks very upright.","But behind the scenes, he does every dirty deal you can think of—smuggling, money laundering, fraud... and he might even be involved in espionage.\"","\"We've put together enough evidence by now, but the tricky part is how to catch him. The guy is extremely cunning. Every time he comes to the mainland, he rushes in and rushes out, staying at most one night before returning to Hong Kong City. And recently, he hasn't been back to the mainland at all. I'm wondering if he's gotten wind of something, or if he's sensed that something's up.\"","Liu Yutong naturally understood why. Jiang Yuan was lying low, probably uncertain whether Zhao Weixiang was truly gone and whether the evidence in Zhao's hands had fallen into someone else's. That was why he was being so cautious.","But she didn't necessarily have to wait for him to walk into a trap—there was an opportunity to catch him right now.","\"If he won't come to us, we can invite him here.\"","\"How?\"","\"Jiang Yuan has some connections with an elite family in the capital, the Jiang family of Di Du. I heard that in a few days, the Jiang family is hosting an eightieth birthday banquet for the matriarch. Jiang Yuan has always wanted to forge ties with a top-tier family like that, to be acknowledged by the clan—would he really want to miss an event like this?\"","\"Huh? How do you know all this?\"","\"Last time I was back in the capital, I overheard Uncle Li and the others talking about it. The Development and Reform Commission official I met then, whose surname is Jiang, he even sent me an invitation.\""]},{"number":710,"title":"Chapter 710: 710. A Brief Meeting (Two-in-One)","paragraphs":["After the two finished discussing those matters, Gao Min suddenly asked a question: \"Sister, do you hate our biological parents?\"","Liu Yutong was looking down at a text message on her phone and paused for a moment. \"Why the sudden question?\"","Gao Min said softly, \"It just came to me. I was just curious.\"","\"If we had grown up in a normal family, maybe our lives would be completely different now. Maybe we'd be happier.\"","Liu Yutong put away her phone and looked up at her. \"I don't hate them. Hate has no meaning. They chose their path, and we chose ours. I think the way things are now, I feel content and fulfilled.\"","Gao Min was momentarily stunned, then smiled. \"You're always like this — so calm it doesn't seem like you're a twenty-year-old girl. Sometimes I wonder who's really the older sister.\"","\"But you're right. Hate doesn't matter, and dwelling on the past doesn't change anything.\"","With Zhao Weixiang's capture, along with their own investigations over the past two years, they had essentially pieced together their origins.","Gao Min's foster father, Gao Shubai, and their biological father, Liu Lei, had once been close brothers who graduated from the same police academy.","After graduation, both found the loves of their lives and even planned a joint wedding.","But Gao Shubai's girlfriend later discovered she had acute leukemia and tragically passed away. He was a very devoted man; her death hit him hard, and he swore never to marry.","Later, Liu Lei was assigned a highly dangerous undercover mission where he could be exposed at any moment, making it impossible to care for his family or his newborn child. So he entrusted his infant daughter, Gao Min, to his good brother, Gao Shubai.","One reason was to give his daughter a relatively safe environment to grow up in, with a clean background.","The other was to provide Gao Shubai with a sense of purpose, to keep him from falling into despair.","That was how Gao Min's origins unfolded.","As for Liu Yutong, it was highly likely that Liu Lei had no idea she even existed.","Later, Gao Shubai was attacked and stabbed during an investigation. Liu Lei was present and could have saved his brother, but Gao Shubai used all his strength to stop him. If Liu Lei intervened, it would expose his undercover identity, rendering all their previous efforts meaningless.","Liu Lei ultimately chose to trust his brother, but Gao Shubai didn't survive...","After that, Liu Lei's personality changed drastically. Feeling he had nothing left to lose and nothing to hold him back, he launched a relentless campaign to crush other gangs, driving himself further down a path of no return.","Eventually, those in power decided he had become uncontrollable and arranged for his elimination...","After Liu Yutong and Gao Min fully understood their origins, they couldn't deny it was hard to accept. But the past was already set, beyond change.","A moment of silence passed.","Gao Min sniffled, suppressing the sadness in her heart, and asked again, \"What if our biological mother comes looking for us? What should we do?\"","As the one hidden figure in their origin story, their feelings toward that biological mother were far more complicated.","Of course, it wasn't impossible that she had her own difficult reasons.","Liu Yutong's answer was simple: \"She can look, but whether we acknowledge her or not is up to us.\"","Deep down, she held no hope of meeting their mother. Even in her previous life, she had never seen her. Of course, it was possible that in her past life, she left her hometown after getting into college and never returned, with no one knowing where she was, so they missed each other.","This time, her presence had already shifted things. For instance, she had never met Yun Cheng in her past life, but now she had. It was possible.","But even if their mother came looking for her now, she probably wouldn't acknowledge her.","From the moment her mother chose to leave her behind, something had already broken.","If she hadn't worked hard enough, if her grandparents hadn't supported her back then, her life might have ended up like so many other girls in rural towns — dropping out early, being forced into marriage at a young age, becoming a village woman, muddling through life.","Besides, before meeting each other, both sides only imagined the other's image, viewing it through a natural filter.","But once they met, that filter could easily shatter.","If she had really become a poorly educated, unemployed village woman with a child trailing behind her, her skin weathered, would her mother truly want to acknowledge her?","Probably not.","But those assumptions weren't important to her.","As she had said, the power was in their hands.","Gao Min looked at her sister and understood her stance. She nodded.","\"I get it now.\"","\"No matter what, we're sisters. Your decision is my decision.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Why waste time thinking about that? It's uncertain. I don't think she'll come looking. Right now, we should focus on how to arrange things for Jiang Yuan. The birthday banquet is an opportunity, and we need to plan carefully.\"","The two sisters talked for a while longer.","Seeing how late it was and that they had finished eating, they got ready to turn in.","Liu Yutong took the black coat that Lan Die handed her and put it on. The golden dragon emblem on the left chest glittered.","\"Let's go.\"","\"Yeah.\"","Gao Min stood up as well. The two walked side by side out of the private room, with Yun Cheng and Ma Da following behind.","They had just stepped out of the private room when they heard a sudden burst of cheers from the crowd downstairs.","Then, someone started leading a group in singing the birthday song. It turned out that some college students were celebrating a birthday party for a classmate in the restaurant.","\"Happy birthday to you! Happy birthday to you...\"","The singing was cheerful. Since there were a lot of college students dining in the main hall tonight and that group loves excitement, many people joined in clapping and singing, creating a lively scene.","From a corner, Lin Dong, Lin Feng, and Jiang Lu watched the spirited young people.","\"Look at these kids. So lively, so full of energy.\"","\"Yeah! At this age, carefree and spending time with friends — this is probably the happiest time of their lives.\"","Jiang Lu thought of her own daughter. \"When Tongtong's birthday comes, I wonder if she celebrates it like this with her classmates too?\"","Lin Feng tried to comfort her, \"Auntie, don't overthink it. For all we know, Tongtong might be popular and have an even more exciting birthday celebration than this.\"","\"When we find her, we can throw her a big party. We'll hire the best pastry chef and go all out.\"","\"Mm.\"","Just then, the birthday girl puffed up her cheeks and blew out all the candles on the cake in one breath. The surrounding group erupted in even louder cheers and applause.","Jiang Lu quietly applauded along, imagining her daughter making a wish in the candlelight, momentarily lost in thought.","Just as they were about to cut the cake, Liu Yutong and her group walked out of the private room and appeared at the top of the stairs.","The moment they appeared, the cheers in the hall came to an abrupt halt.","Some diners who were eating involuntarily put down their chopsticks and stood up, staring at the group of people in black on the stairs.","Lin Dong's family was taken aback by this sudden change in atmosphere.","A birthday party going so smoothly—why had it suddenly become so quiet? Was there some special ceremony about to take place?","But they soon understood why the students and guests had fallen silent—a group of people in black was descending the stairs.","The diners and college students who had been eating in the main hall looked at this group with awe, even a hint of tension in their eyes.","The two girls at the front were especially striking.","On the left was a tall young woman in a long black coat that accentuated her cold, aloof aura. She exuded an imposing presence, as if she were born to stand at the top of the hierarchy.","On the right was a young woman of similar height, with a sharp, short haircut that framed her handsome, assertive features. She, too, carried an undeniable air of authority.","Behind them followed several young men, all dressed in black suits with a dragon emblem pinned to the left chest. Their solemn expressions made it clear they were no ordinary people.","The diners' first reaction upon seeing them was, \"I didn't expect so many high-ranking members of the Ten Thousand Dragon Society to be dining here as well.\"","There was reverence in their faces, but also a barely contained excitement.","Lin Dong narrowed his eyes, carefully studying the two girls at the front—especially the one in the black coat. She looked no more than twenty years old, yet she had a commanding presence that felt deeply ingrained, as if she were destined for the pinnacle of power.","The people behind her were clearly no ordinary individuals either.","This Pearl City might not be big, but it was full of hidden talent.","Jiang Lu, meanwhile, was stunned. Her eyes widened in disbelief.","The girl in black walking on the left—the one with the powerful aura—was none other than the \"little sister\" she had chatted with so warmly on the plane and felt an instant connection to.","The girl's current image was a far cry from the quiet, bookish, girl-next-door type she had met on the plane, holding a stack of professional texts. Now, she was far more intimidating.","At that moment, Lin Feng couldn't help asking, \"Dad, who do you think that girl in black is? It feels like everyone here is afraid of her.\"","Lin Dong didn't answer. He just stared at the dragon-shaped emblem on the left chest of each person in the group. The symbol looked familiar... Ah, he remembered—the head waiter in black at the restaurant had worn the same emblem.","So, this must be the Ten Thousand Dragon Society those students had been talking about.","And these people were likely core members of the society, holding very high status, or else the students wouldn't have reacted this way.","But they were so young!","Young enough to be almost unbelievable.","Liu Yutong was long accustomed to this kind of scene. Her gaze fell on the birthday girl wearing a crown. She nodded slightly in her direction and offered a faint smile.","The girl, flustered that Liu Yutong had noticed her and even smiled and greeted her, blushed deeply and blurted out, \"Senior! I... I'm your idol! No, wait—you're my idol!\"","Liu Yutong hadn't expected the girl to dare speak to her. She smiled and asked, \"Are you from the University of Finance and Economics too?\"","The girl nodded vigorously. \"Senior, I'm in the same major as you—Business Administration. I really, truly admire you!\"","Liu Yutong offered her a blessing. \"Happy birthday, junior!\"","\"Thank you, Senior! Thank you!\" The girl's voice trembled with excitement.","The other students in the hall were incredibly envious, seeing that the legendary heiress of the Ten Thousand Dragon Society was so approachable and had even personally offered birthday wishes.","Liu Yutong called over a waiter and whispered something.","The waiter immediately understood and walked briskly to the table celebrating the birthday. Smiling, he announced to the entire hall:","\"Dear students and honored guests, and especially our birthday girl today. Our boss has said that tonight, this table—and the bills for all guests in the venue—are on the house! Consider this a birthday gift from Yuyue Fang to our birthday senior, and a token of thanks to all our student and customer friends for your continued support!\"","The hall fell silent for a moment, then erupted into cheers even more fervent and excited than before.","\"WOW——!!\"","\"Thank you, Liu Yutong! You're amazing!\"","\"Thank you, boss!\"","\"Yuyue Fang rules!\"","\"Birthday girl, you've got such clout! The senior really came through for you!\"","\"...\"","The birthday table in particular was bursting with excitement. The students' faces were flushed bright red, and a few boys even jumped up.","They might not have known Liu Yutong personally, but the name of the Ten Thousand Dragon Society's heiress was legendary throughout Pearl City, especially around the university district.","Getting a free meal and a blessing from this legendary senior was something they could brag about for years!","The birthday girl herself was so moved she was almost in tears, silently vowing to work hard and try to join the Ten Thousand Dragon Society.","Amid the lively atmosphere, Liu Yutong gave a light wave to the diners and guests, then turned and led her group out of the restaurant.","Just as they were about to get into their cars, an excited voice called out behind her.","\"Please wait a moment!\"","Liu Yutong paused and turned around. There, running out of the restaurant, was the \"big sister\" she had met on the plane, her face alight with surprise.","Behind Jiang Lu followed her husband and son, both of whom also had distinguished auras—clearly her family.","A flicker of surprise passed through Liu Yutong's eyes, and she greeted her politely, \"What a coincidence, big sister. I didn't expect to run into you here again.\"","Jiang Lu beamed. \"Yes! What a coincidence! Meeting again here—it must be fate!\"","The surprise and excitement on her face were genuine. Meeting the girl again here felt like destiny was helping her find her daughter.","\"By the way, last time we chatted, I forgot to introduce myself. I'm Jiang Lu, this is my husband Lin Dong, and this is my son Lin Feng.\" She introduced the father and son behind her.","But the moment Liu Yutong heard the name \"Jiang Lu,\" her gaze sharpened almost imperceptibly.","Jiang Lu?","Wasn't that the name of her biological mother?","In that instant, a flood of thoughts and complex emotions surged within her. She forcibly suppressed her inner turmoil, maintaining her polite composure, and asked calmly, \"Are you... here looking for someone?\"","Hearing this, Jiang Lu immediately abandoned any thought of asking for the girl's contact information or name, and eagerly said, \"Yes! I mentioned on the plane that I was searching for my long-lost daughter, and you encouraged me to keep looking. Now I've gotten a lead—she should be in Pearl City, studying at the University of Finance and Economics. My daughter's nickname is Tongtong, and her full name is Liu Yutong. Do you know her? If you do, could you...\"","She didn't get to finish her sentence.","Liu Yutong suddenly spoke, her tone icy as she cut her off: \"Sorry, I have something urgent to attend to, so I'll be going now.\"","She didn't give Jiang Lu any chance to respond or press further, and said to Yun Cheng and the others, \"Let's go.\"","Yun Cheng quickly walked to the roadside and pulled open the door of the Maybach.","Once Liu Yutong was seated inside, the others got into their respective cars and started up to leave immediately.","Lin Dong and the others watched the convoy of black cars drive away, their smiles gradually freezing on their faces.","What the hell.","Everything was going so well just now—why the sudden change of heart?","Are women always this fickle?","More importantly, even if she's busy, she could have at least left her contact information!"]},{"number":711,"title":"Chapter 711: 711, The Daughter of Legend (Two in One)","paragraphs":["\"She... why did she leave all of a sudden?\"","Jiang Lu watched the black motorcade gradually disappear into the distance, her face full of confusion. \"Just a moment ago, everything was fine. Could it be that I came across as too eager and annoyed her?\"","Lin Dong frowned deeply and comforted her. \"Don't overthink it. Maybe they really had some urgent business to attend to.\"","Though he said this, he couldn't shake a nagging feeling that something was off. That girl's reaction was far too strange. One second she was chatting and laughing with them all amicably, and the next, her attitude took a sharp turn, becoming distant and cold.","This suggested that the girl most likely knew Tongtong—might even be close to her. Otherwise, there was no way to explain such a sudden shift in demeanor. Also, he kept feeling that she looked vaguely familiar, but for the life of him, he couldn't recall where he had seen her before.","Lin Feng watched his stepmother's disappointed expression and couldn't help but say, \"Auntie, how about I have someone look into her? She seems pretty well-known in Bright Pearl City. It shouldn't be too hard to find information.\"","Jiang Lu immediately shook her head. \"No need. That would be too intrusive.\"","Even as she said this, she couldn't shake a vague sense of unease. Based on their conversation on the plane last time, that girl didn't seem like the type to be so fickle.","It was just too strange.","Seeing this, Lin Dong said, \"Don't dwell on it. Let's head back to the hotel first. Tomorrow we'll go straight to Finance University to find the person, and then everything will become clear.\"","\"Alright,\" Jiang Lu sighed, a trace of regret in her voice.","---------","In the back seat of the Maybach.","Liu Yutong leaned against her seat, her eyes closed, trying to mask the turmoil within her.","Gao Min, sitting beside her, keenly sensed her sister's unease and asked, \"What's wrong? Who were those people just now?\"","\"No one important. Just strangers I met once,\" Liu Yutong said, opening her eyes.","Gao Min looked at her suspiciously. \"Really just strangers? The way you were chatting with them earlier didn't seem like you were dealing with strangers. Is there something you're hiding from me?\"","A brief silence fell over the car.","Liu Yutong turned her head to look at the rapidly retreating street scenes outside the window. After a long pause, she finally spoke slowly. \"Sister, what if I told you that woman just now... is our biological mother? Would you believe me?\"","Gao Min's body jolted violently. She stared at her sister in disbelief. \"What did you say? Her... she's our mom?\"","Liu Yutong continued, \"The name matches, the age fits, and she said she was looking for her long-lost daughter... I should have realized it long ago.\"","In truth, she already had a feeling back on the plane, but she just hadn't let her mind go there. Mainly because in her previous life, her mother had never come looking for her. So she thought that in this life, the same would likely hold true, and she didn't dwell on it.","Gao Min took a deep breath, trying to process this sudden revelation.","That woman, with her gentle and refined aura who looked barely over thirty, was their birth mother?","\"Are you... are you sure?\"","\"I'm sure. But so what?\"","Liu Yutong turned to look at her. \"She chose to leave when we needed her most. What point is there in coming back now?\"","Gao Min looked at her sister's somewhat cold profile, a storm of conflicting emotions churning inside her.","She could understand her sister's feelings—the pain of abandonment, the hardship of growing up alone. None of this could be mended by a simple \"I'm sorry.\"","But deep down, she still held a faint, unspoken hope for the mother she had never known, the one who had only existed in her imagination.","\"Maybe... she really had no choice back then? And she's come looking for us now, hasn't she?\"","Liu Yutong let out a cold laugh. \"Even if she had her reasons, that's her business. There hasn't been a place for a mother in my life for a long time.\"","She paused, then added, \"Besides, she already has a new family now, a new life. Look at the man by her side—he's got a distinguished air, probably from some powerful family in the capital. And that young man, he must be her son.\"","\"They're a happy little family of three. If we barge in out of nowhere, what would that make us?\"","Gao Min fell silent.","True. If her mother already had a new family, their sudden appearance might not be a good thing either.","\"Then we just pretend we don't know?\" Gao Min's voice carried a hint of bitterness.","Liu Yutong was silent again for a moment before she said, \"Let's deal with Jiang Yuan's matter first. As for the rest... let things take their course. What's meant to come won't be avoided. But whether we accept it or not, that's up to us.\"","Gao Min nodded.","In her heart, she actually yearned more than Liu Yutong did to sit down calmly with their mother and ask what really happened back then.","Perhaps this was because of their different upbringings. She had grown up surrounded by love and care, and her father was a police officer—a profession she had always been proud of.","But her sister Liu Yutong's experience had been the complete opposite. Her foster father was a gambler who was also prone to domestic violence—he even once tried to sell her off.","It was only natural that her sister didn't want to acknowledge their mother.","But if she had to choose between her mother and her sister, she would choose her sister without a second thought.","\"Don't worry. I told you—your decision is my decision. I'll always support you.\"","\"Thank you, Sister.\"","-----------------","A sleepless night passed.","The next morning, just as the sky was beginning to lighten, Jiang Lu was already out of bed.","She stood in front of the dressing mirror in her hotel suite, having already changed into her fifth outfit—a light purple suit that looked dignified and proper. But after staring at herself from left to right, she still wasn't satisfied.","\"How does this one look?\"","\"Too formal. Makes you look like you're going to a business meeting,\" Lin Dong commented, leaning against the doorframe.","Jiang Lu frowned, her expression anxious. \"I want to come across as warm and approachable. I want to look like an ordinary mother, not some strong-willed career woman.\"","At this, Lin Dong walked into the room and picked out a light blue knee-length dress with lace trimming the hem. \"Try this one? I remember you look especially good in blue. It makes you appear more gentle, too.\"","Jiang Lu took the dress, hesitated for a moment, and then put it on.","The woman in the mirror was gentle and graceful. The blue made her skin look even fairer, softening the tension on her face.","\"I'll go with this one,\" she finally nodded.","Lin Feng knocked and came in. Seeing Jiang Lu's outfit, he deliberately teased her. \"Auntie Jiang, if you go out looking like that, people are going to think you're my older sister.\"","Though it was a joke, it eased some of the tension in Jiang Lu's heart.","\"Breakfast is ready. We'll head out after we eat. I've already had someone check—Finance University has no classes this morning. Most students should be in the dorms or the library. It'll be easier to find her.\"","\"Mm.\"","The three of them went downstairs to have breakfast.","Jiang Lu had little appetite and only managed to drink half a glass of milk.","Seeing this, Lin Feng encouraged her. \"Auntie Jiang, take it easy. The worst that can happen is she's not ready to acknowledge the relationship right now. In that case, we'll take it slow. Today, we'll just see her and leave a good first impression. We can set up another meeting another day. As they say, 'If you chip away with enough patience and sincerity, even metal and stone can be opened.' One day, she'll accept it.\"","Lin Dong also nodded in agreement. \"Xiaofeng is right, Lulu. We have plenty of time. Don't put too much pressure on yourself.\"","Jiang Lu nodded, forcing a faint smile, but the sweat in her palms betrayed her inner turmoil.","She really couldn’t help being nervous.","After breakfast, they got into the Bentley and headed toward Mingzhu City University of Finance and Economics.","On the way, Jiang Lu kept looking out the window, repeatedly rehearsing the words she would say when they met.","“Tongtong, I’m your mother...”","No, that was too direct.","“Hello, I’m Jiang Lu. You might not know me, but I’m your mother.”","That wouldn’t work either—too stiff.","“I’ve been looking for you for a long time...”","Would that sound too insincere?","The more she thought, the more flustered she became. Finally, she decided to stop overthinking and just go with the flow.","When the moment came, the right words would naturally follow.","About a dozen minutes later, the car arrived at the entrance of the university.","After registering, they followed the information they had gathered earlier and found the female dormitory building where Liu Yutong lived.","“Excuse me, is Tongtong... I mean, is Liu Yutong here?” Jiang Lu stopped a girl who was about to enter the building and asked politely.","The girl paused and looked them up and down. “You’re looking for Liu Yutong?”","“Yes, we’re her...”","Jiang Lu hesitated. “We’re her relatives, visiting from out of town, and we’d like to see her.”","The girl’s expression turned a bit strange. “Are you really her family?”","Lin Dong stepped forward and nodded. “Yes, we came all the way from the capital. This is my wife, and we have something very important to discuss with Liu Yutong.”","“From the capital, huh? That explains it, but you probably won’t find her on campus,” the girl said.","“Why? Did she go out?” Jiang Lu’s heart tightened.","“Not exactly,” the girl shook her head. “She rarely comes to school. If you want to find her, you’ll have to go to the Wanlonghui Group headquarters.”","Jiang Lu was taken aback. “Wanlonghui Group headquarters?”","The girl nodded. “That’s right. Liu Yutong is the big boss of Wanlonghui Group—she’s very busy, so she hardly ever shows up here.”","“If you’re really her relatives, you’d already know that, wouldn’t you?”","Boom!","That sentence struck the three of them like a thunderbolt!","Tongtong... was the big boss of Wanlonghui Group?","The same company that those students last night described as the all-powerful, self-made business empire of Mingzhu City?","Lin Dong suddenly recalled the black-clad girl with an imposing presence he had seen at Yuyuefang last night. A wild thought crossed his mind.","Could it be her?","“Excuse me, are you sure? Liu Yutong, about twenty years old, majoring in business administration at the university, a sophomore?” Lin Dong’s voice unconsciously grew tense.","The girl nodded firmly. “Of course I’m sure! Everyone on campus knows Liu Yutong. She’s a legend here, a role model for countless students. She founded Wanlonghui Group from scratch, and her net worth is said to be over ten billion.”","“See that bulletin board over there? Her full profile is on it—you can check it out yourselves.”","Jiang Lu felt her heart skip a beat.","Ten billion? Self-made?","Was this really her daughter?","“Can you tell us where the Wanlonghui Group headquarters is?” Lin Dong quickly asked.","The girl shot them another suspicious glance. “Are you really Liu Yutong’s relatives? You seem to know nothing—you’re not scammers, are you?”","“Of course we’re not scammers. It’s just our first time here, and we’re unfamiliar with the place.”","The girl nodded and gave them the address.","On Mingzhu City’s turf, anyone foolish enough to try to con Liu Yutong probably hadn’t been born yet.","Lin Dong thanked her and prepared to take his wife and son to that address.","As they passed the bulletin board, Lin Feng suddenly pointed at it and exclaimed, “Dad, Aunt Jiang! Look!”","Jiang Lu and Lin Dong followed his gaze. There, at the center of the board—a prominent display right in front of the dorm building—stood a personal profile taking up nearly half the space.","The profile was astonishing, with a long list of honors that seemed to stretch endlessly.","Recipient of the Dragon Nation Youth May Fourth Medal","National Annual College Student Figure","National College Student Model of Virtue","Mingzhu City Youth Outstanding Contribution Award","Mingzhu City College Student Entrepreneurial Leader","Mingzhu City Safety Exemplary","University Annual Figure","President’s Special Honorary Medal","Student Union Honorary Chair","University Outstanding Student Representative","Founder of the Wanlonghui Scholarship","...","The endless list of honors was followed by a commentary from the university president:","“She redefines the boundaries of what it means to be an ‘outstanding student.’ Her classroom is the world. Her exam is the age. Her answer is legend.”","—In solemn tribute from the University of Finance and Economics","This ridiculously overwhelming résumé left Lin Dong, Jiang Lu, and Lin Feng completely stunned. Even the first few awards alone were heavyweight honors.","For example, the Dragon Nation Youth May Fourth Medal was one of the highest honors the country bestowed on modern youth, given only to those who had made extraordinary contributions in fields like technology, culture, or national defense.","In fact, she had only recently received that award, thanks to Uncle Li’s strong recommendation and an assessment of the Dragon Core Project by the higher-ups.","The National Annual College Student Figure meant she had topped the ranks among tens of millions of college students nationwide.","The Mingzhu City Youth Outstanding Contribution Award was the highest local recognition possible.","The President’s Special Honorary Medal indicated she had been inscribed into the school’s history as a current student—meaning she was no longer merely a standout among students but had become part of the school’s legacy, even a symbol of an era.","Any single one of these honors would make anyone immensely proud, yet here they were listed together as just a small part of this student’s glory.","Lin Feng scanned all the way to the bottom and couldn’t help cursing.","“Holy shit! Holy shit! Holy shit!”","“Is this really a college student? That’s insane!”","“Dad, Aunt Jiang, look at that last line from the president: ‘Her answer is legend!’”","“So badass! So damn badass!”","Passing students noticed their stunned expressions and smiled with pride.","Clearly, every outsider who saw Liu Yutong’s profile for the first time had pretty much the same reaction.","After all, this résumé surpassed excellence—it was practically mythological!","Jiang Lu’s breathing grew faster and faster.","From each of these honors, she could almost see the path her daughter had walked over the past twenty years.","Starting from scratch, building a ten-billion-dollar fortune, earning the highest national youth honor, receiving a moral model commendation... every single accomplishment sounded like something out of a fictional script, yet there it was, carved into her daughter’s real life.","Her emotions grew even more complicated.","There was pride... and heartache. How much hardship had her daughter endured? How many dangers had she faced to become this extraordinary?","And besides that, she also felt a deep, overwhelming sense of fear.","Her daughter seemed to have grown, in the years of her absence, into someone entirely beyond her imagination—someone who had even ascended to heights she could never hope to reach.","“Wanlong Association, Wanlong Association...”","Lin Dong muttered the name over and over, the scenes from the restaurant the previous night replaying in his mind.","The students’ reverent and fearful attitude toward the Wanlong Association, the dragon emblem on the head waiter’s chest, and the imposing black-clad girl from the night before—all of it rushed back to him.","A terrifying thought exploded in his mind.","His gaze jerked away from the text, frantically scanning the bulletin board.","Usually, a profile like this would be accompanied by a photo.","And there it was!","Above the list of honors, beneath the title 【Liu Yutong | School of Business Administration | Class of ‘07】, a small but striking half-length portrait was displayed.","The girl in the photo wore an ordinary student uniform, photogenic and pretty, with a touch of youthful innocence—an innocence that came purely from her age.","This image merged seamlessly with the girl who, the night before, had offered a warm smile and birthday wishes to a younger schoolgirl at the restaurant, only to turn cold and distant toward them.","“It’s her! It really is her!” Even Lin Dong, the nearly fifty-year-old head of the Lin family, found his voice trembling.","The daughter they had been searching for so desperately had slipped right past them!","Jiang Lu followed her husband’s gaze to the photo.","In that moment, time stood still.","The young, beautiful face in the image—the “little sister” who had made her feel such a fond connection on the plane, and the imposing, awe-inspiring young girl from Yufang Restaurant—finally became one and the same.","So this was her youngest daughter—Liu Yutong.","..........."]},{"number":712,"title":"Chapter 712: 712, Refusing to Meet Loongson's Trial Production Successful Visit","paragraphs":["Jiang Lu's family stood in front of the notice board for a long time before finally coming to terms with the fact that their daughter Tongtong had become a major power in her own right.","Logically, they should have been happy about Tongtong's achievements, but at that moment, they couldn't muster an ounce of joy.","The reason was simple.","If their daughter Tongtong were just an ordinary girl, they could at least use money, resources, and everything they had to make up for the past, to dote on her, and slowly win back her heart.","There would always be a way, always an opening.","But now, they had to face an exceptionally accomplished daughter, the founder of a business empire. What could they possibly offer to make amends?","Wealth? Power?","Wealth was out of the question. If she was truly worth tens of billions, she could probably buy out the Lin family with ease.","As for power, the Lin family's influence had already waned significantly. Perhaps Tongtong held even more sway in Bright Pearl City than they did.","And trying to appeal to her through blood ties and emotions? That seemed even more laughable.","Missing the most critical twenty years of someone's life, then trying to rely on a thin connection of blood to make such an independent and formidable person accept them—it would feel more like an insult than anything else.","At the end of the day, they didn't even have the right to offer compensation anymore.","The more they thought about it, the more desperate they became—especially Jiang Lu.","Even Lin Dong didn't know how to comfort his wife. He could only sigh and say, \"This girl is no ordinary one.\"","Deep down, he also felt a pang of regret. Back when he first learned that his wife had a daughter, he should have been more resolute and decisive, bringing the girl directly into the Lin household instead of backing down at the first sign of resistance.","Now, none of the younger generation of the Lin family amounted to much. If he had brought this stepdaughter home earlier, how dazzling the next generation of the Lin family could have been. Just based on her resume, even if she were placed in a government position, her achievements would have been nothing short of remarkable. Perhaps the Lin family could have risen again because of her.","But what was missed was missed.","Lin Feng had also calmed down from the initial shock. He smacked his lips and said, \"Dad, Aunt Jiang, it seems like acknowledging this sister of ours is going to be no easy task.\"","Even as a young master from the capital, he had to admit that this sister of his was far too outstanding.","So outstanding that, looking across all the prestigious families in the capital, very few heirs could match her.","But precisely because she was so exceptional, reunion was all the more difficult.","Jiang Lu stared at her daughter's photo in the picture, feeling utterly powerless.","Yes, her daughter now lacked for nothing.","What could she, as a mother appearing only now, possibly bring to her daughter?","Joy? Her daughter probably didn't need it.","But she still didn't want to give up.","\"Lin Dong, I still want to see Tongtong. Even if she doesn't want anything from me, even if she hates me, I have to tell her in person that Mom is back, that Mom was wrong. Even if she tells me to disappear forever after she hears it, I'll accept it.\"","Lin Dong let out a heavy sigh. \"Then let's go see her. But Lu, we need to prepare for the worst.\"","Carrying this bleak feeling, they left the university and, based on the address given by the students, found the temporary headquarters of the Wanlonghui Group—Shunchang Tower.","\"Shunchang...\"","Lin Dong looked up at the golden, glittering sign that read \"Shunchang,\" then at the men in black entering and exiting through the main entrance. He couldn't help but mutter under his breath.","\"Shunchang, those who obey me shall prosper. It seems this stepdaughter of mine isn't just a business prodigy—she's got a streak of... well, a very unique kind of fierceness.\"","This only reinforced their belief that communicating with her would be as difficult as scaling the heavens.","Lin Feng couldn't help but click his tongue. \"Dad, Aunt Jiang, look at the name. 'Shunchang,' and 'Wanlonghui' too. Now I kind of believe what those students last night said about Tongtong having connections everywhere. This sister of ours—she seems to walk a rather wild path.\"","The name Wanlonghui sounded very much like an underworld organization, and \"Shunchang\" made that domineering attitude abundantly clear.","Jiang Lu was visibly nervous. \"Let's go. We have to face this sooner or later.\"","As expected, they were stopped at the front desk on the first floor.","\"Sorry, sirs and madam, without an appointment, we cannot let you through.\"","\"What do we need to do to see your boss?\"","\"To see our chairman, you must make an appointment in advance and obtain approval from either Assistant Su, or one of our CEOs, President Yun, President Ma, or President Yu.\"","\"We... we're not here on business.\"","\"I am your chairman's mother. We came from the capital. We just want to see her, to exchange a few words.\" Jiang Lu pleaded with the receptionist in an almost begging tone.","The receptionist's eyes flickered with a hint of suspicion. The chairman's mother? Was that some kind of joke?","If she really were the chairman's mother, wouldn't the chairman see them?","But despite her doubts, her professionalism kept her outwardly polite. \"Madam, please understand. Many people come every day trying to see our chairman for all sorts of reasons. If you truly are a family member of the chairman, you can contact her directly or reach out to Assistant Su. Without an appointment, we must adhere to protocol here.\"","Lin Dong knew arguing with the receptionist was futile. He pulled out his business card and handed it over. \"I am Lin Dong from the Lin Group in the capital. This is my wife. We do have very urgent personal matters. Could you please inform Assistant Su? Tell her we met your chairman last night at Yu Yue Fang.\"","The receptionist took the card, gave it a slightly more serious look upon seeing the mention of the Lin Group, but still shook her head. \"Mr. Lin, I'm sorry. Without an appointment, I truly cannot relay this. It's the rule.\"","She then handed the card back. \"If you really have urgent business, you can try reaching Assistant Su through her public email or send a formal letter via our business cooperation channels.\"","Rebuffed politely, the three of them retreated to the rest area outside the building.","\"What do we do now?\"","Lin Feng sounded irritated. \"We can't even get through the door. This company of our sister's has way too strict of a policy.\"","Lin Dong understood why. \"That's to be expected. If Tongtong doesn't want to see us, the people underneath will naturally block us at every turn. She already made her stance clear last night.\"","\"Lu, it seems Tongtong is more resolute than we imagined.\"","Jiang Lu bit her lip, tears welling up in her eyes. \"I wronged her. She has every right to hate me. But don't I even get a chance to explain? Even if she wants to curse me, hit me—I'd take it. Why won't she just see me?\"","\"Auntie, don't be like that. Let's think of another way.\"","After offering some words of comfort, Lin Feng turned to his father. \"Dad, do you have any connections here in Bright Pearl City? Can we get someone to put in a word for us?\"","Lin Dong shook his head. \"If it weren't for your mother, I might never have even heard the name Bright Pearl City. But even if I had connections, it wouldn't matter. This is Tongtong's territory.\"","Just moments ago, after learning at the university about his stepdaughter's identity, he had immediately contacted his assistant to look into the Wanlonghui Group—a company he had previously thought would never intersect with his own.","Though time was limited, the information the assistant managed to gather had startled him.","The Wanlonghui Group's rise to power was anything but clean; instead, it reeked of darkness.","Rumors said that in the past few years, several major gangs that had entrenched themselves in Pearl City for years had fallen one after another, with the Dragon Alliance's shadow behind it all. It was also said that the Dragon Alliance was extremely brutal in dealing with its enemies... In short, the waters were deep, the background was deep, and within Pearl City, the Dragon Alliance Group was practically an unchallenged force.","In such a situation, finding anyone would probably be useless.","After hearing these rumors, he even considered giving up on reclaiming their long-lost relative altogether.","The Lin family, after all, had a clean record. If this stepdaughter was so \"shady,\" would bringing her back drag the Lins down the same path?","Of course, these were just rumors, impossible to verify, but scary enough.","\"Th-then we just give up like this?\" Jiang Lu's heart sank halfway.","Lin Dong, seeing his wife's dejected expression, couldn't bear it and comforted her: \"Regardless, she is our daughter. What we must face, we must face. Since she won't see us now, we'll come a few more times, let her see our sincerity, and she'll eventually agree to meet.\"","\"Alright,\" Jiang Lu said, having no better ideas.","Over the next two days, they arrived at Shun Chang Mansion almost morning, noon, and night, but without exception, they were turned away for \"no appointment\" or \"appointment not approved.\"","Let alone seeing her, they couldn't even get through the front door.","What they didn't know was that Liu Yutong wasn't in Pearl City at all—she had already gone to the provincial capital. Perhaps she wanted to get it out of sight, out of mind. Additionally, there was the good news from President Qiu of Dragon Core that the production line was built and chip trial production had begun. So Liu Yutong had personally gone to the Dragon Core factory to oversee operations.","On the afternoon of the third day, after being politely asked to leave the building again by the receptionist, Lin Dong looked at his haggard wife Jiang Lu and let out a deep sigh.","\"Lu Lu, we have to go back to the imperial capital tomorrow.\"","\"Why? Give me a few more days, I'm sure I can meet our daughter.\" Jiang Lu grew anxious.","Lin Dong said: \"It's not that we can't afford the time; it's that Granny Jiang's eightieth birthday banquet invitations arrived long ago. Although the Lin family is no longer what it once was, we must attend on such an occasion. This isn't just about etiquette—it also concerns the future of Lin Feng and the younger generation. The Jiang family's roots are deep; even if we only maintain a sliver of their goodwill, it's a huge benefit to the Lins. Besides, I've heard that many big names will attend this banquet; it's an opportunity.\"","\"And most importantly, my sister-in-law and my niece are coming back to the Lin family. You know what that means, don't you?\"","Lin Feng's eyes widened: \"Dad, my cousin...\"","Lin Dong said meaningfully: \"You understand in your heart.\"","Since his elder brother passed away, his sister-in-law and niece had never set foot in the Lin family home. Their sudden decision to visit couldn't be as simple as it seemed.","Lin Feng nodded and turned to his stepmother: \"Aunt Jiang, let's take our time with recognizing my sister. Let's return to the imperial capital first to handle the matters we need to attend to. When we come next time, maybe things will turn around.\"","Jiang Lu fell silent.","She knew her husband was right. When it came to family and her son's future, she couldn't be willful.","But the thought of leaving again, possibly never seeing her daughter again, felt like her heart was being torn open.","\"I... I understand.\"","\"Tomorrow, I'll try one last time. If Tong Tong still won't see me, then we'll go back first.\"","Lin Dong replied: \"Alright, I'll accompany you tomorrow. If we still can't see her... Lu Lu, we need to prepare ourselves mentally. Maybe she just needs more time to accept the fact that you've appeared in her world. A little breathing room is good for everyone.\"","Though unwilling, Jiang Lu could only nod: \"Mm.\"","...","Provincial capital city, Lu City. Dragon Core Semiconductor Manufacturing Co., Ltd.","In the brand-new cleanroom, engineers dressed in white dust-proof suits were nervously conducting final equipment adjustments. Giant lithography machines, etching equipment, ion implanters... these precision instruments, costing hundreds of millions of dollars, now stood quietly in a temperature and humidity-controlled environment, awaiting the first trial production order.","Liu Yutong stood quietly, looking through the observation window at the scene inside the workshop.","\"Chairman, all equipment self-checks are complete, parameter calibration is done, we can proceed with the first trial run,\" came President Qiu's voice over the intercom, carrying an excitement hard to conceal.","Though technologically two to three generations behind international mainstream production, this 90nm process line was Dragon Core's first truly independent, controllable chip manufacturing line.","Its significance far outweighed commercial value—if the trial succeeded, it would mean Dragon Core had taken its first solid step forward.","\"Begin.\"","\"Understood! Start lithography machine one, load test pattern!\"","At the command, indicator lights in the workshop lit up in sequence, and the machinery hummed with a low operating sound. On the monitoring screen, extremely tiny circuit patterns began to appear on the silicon wafer—the most basic building blocks of a chip.","Time ticked by minute by minute.","All engineers held their breath, staring at the monitoring data in front of them.","Half an hour later.","\"Pattern transfer complete, accuracy within specs!\"","\"Etching process complete, slight line width errors, but within allowed range!\"","\"Ion implantation complete...\"","\"...\"","A series of reports came through the intercom, and Liu Yutong felt her heartbeat quicken.","She was no longer the clueless newbie about chip manufacturing she once was; she could roughly understand what they were saying.","When the green light for the final process lit up, the entire control room erupted in cheers.","\"We did it! First trial run successful!\"","\"Initial yield rate estimate exceeds 70%! Surpassing expectations!\"","\"We made it! We really made it!\"","President Qiu took off his dust cap, his eyes already red-rimmed.","This veteran, who had struggled in the semiconductor industry for decades, had been longing for Dragon Core to take its first step more than anyone else.","Through the intercom, he said to Liu Yutong: \"Chairman, we have successfully trial-produced our own chip production line.\"","Though the yield rate was low, though the process was still behind, the first step had finally been taken smoothly.","Qiu Ciyun, this expert in building factories, had lived up to his reputation.","\"Thank you all for the hard work! I may not understand the details as an outsider, but I still want to congratulate everyone!\"","\" The cafeteria has prepared a celebration banquet—please make sure to eat and drink well!\"","\"Thank you, Chairman!\"","A wave of cheers came through the intercom, the atmosphere heated and jubilant.","With the successful trial production, it was nearly evening. This historic first step certainly deserved a grand celebration.","Engineers and factory staff gradually left their posts for the changing room, preparing to attend the banquet in the cafeteria.","Liu Yutong had just changed her clothes and stepped out of the changing room when her phone buzzed.","It was Ma Da calling.","\"Miss, the family of three from the imperial capital came again today and waited all morning at the Shun Chang Mansion reception desk. They still want to see you. I turned them down according to your instructions, saying they didn't have an appointment.\"","\"They still haven't left?\"","\"No, I've heard that Ms. Jiang has been coming almost every day, and today is already the third day.\"","\"Miss, should I arrange for someone to ask them to leave Pearl City?\"","\"No need! If they want to wait, let them wait. Once they lose patience, they'll leave on their own.\"","\"I understand!\"","After Liu Yutong hung up the phone, she gazed out the window at the flags fluttering in the Longxin factory compound, her expression complicated.","She wasn't refusing to meet them out of hatred.","It was because she didn't know how to face them.","The \"sister\" on the plane who had made her feel a sense of warmth, the gentle and knowledgeable woman she had chatted so harmoniously with—turned out to be her biological mother.","Fate really could be cruel with its jokes sometimes.","\"Boss!\"","Su Mansu's voice interrupted her thoughts, reporting the situation outside the factory: \"There are many journalists outside, along with some local officials. They say they want to interview and inspect the test production of Longxin. Would you like to go and see them in person?\"","Liu Yutong frowned at the news, a flicker of impatience flashing in her eyes.","The Longxin factory was at a critical moment. The engineers were fully focused on preparing for the test production. The sudden arrival of these journalists and local officials would not only be unhelpful but would only waste time.","And she had long made it clear that she didn't want anyone disturbing the work rhythm of people like CEO Qiu, so they could concentrate on their tasks.","\"Send them all away!\"","\"But...\"","\"No buts. I already spoke with Uncle Li earlier—all unnecessary inspection procedures are to be declined.\"","\"Yes!\"","As Su Mansu was about to turn around, she received another message and reported again: \"Boss, CEO Zeng has also arrived. He's now at the main gate of the factory, being stopped by the security guards. He says he brought a guest with him.\"","Liu Yutong was about to say \"send him away too,\" but before she could speak, she realized who it was.","\"Are you talking about Zeng Jin? He came to the mainland?\"","Su Mansu nodded: \"Yes, it's him.\"","\"Let's go—quickly!\"","Without a second word, Liu Yutong turned and strode toward the main entrance.","Watching Liu Yutong's eager demeanor, Su Mansu suddenly thought of a historical figure from the Three Kingdoms period.","Indeed, a boss truly intent on doing great things is always this hungry for talent."]},{"number":713,"title":"Chapter 713: 713, Once You're Here, Don't Even Think About Leaving. (Two-in-One)","paragraphs":["Outside the gate of the Longxin Semiconductor factory, the scene was bustling.","Journalists from seven or eight media outlets had their interview vehicles parked at the entrance, with cameras and microphones all aimed squarely at the tightly closed factory gate.","A few men dressed in suits, looking like officials, were arguing with the head of the security team.","\"Is Longxin factory really about to start trial production?\"","\"Rumor has it that Longxin’s goal is to surpass international advanced levels. Is that true?\"","\"Longxin...\"","\"I’m from the Lucheng District Committee. I want to inspect the project progress. Why won’t you let me in?\"","\"...\"","The head of the security team was a young man in his twenties, wearing the black uniform of a core member of the Wanlong Society. He stood expressionless in front of the electric gate, with over a dozen young security guards in Longxin uniforms lined up behind him.","As soon as news of Longxin’s trial production spread, these reporters and some local officials flocked over like cats catching a whiff of fish.","However, Liu Yutong had already made it clear that she didn’t want pointless interviews and inspections to waste CEO Qiu’s and the engineers’ time, so she had issued strict orders.","No outsiders were allowed in without prior notice. Even Uncle Li had to check in advance.","To enforce these requirements strictly, the security team recruited mostly young former military personnel, and the team leader was a core member of the Wanlong Society. Only this way could orders be carried out without hesitation.","Otherwise, an ordinary security guard might buckle under pressure when faced with local officials.","\"I’m sorry. Without an appointment, no one is allowed in.\"","The security team leader repeated expressionlessly, \"Longxin is in the middle of key technical debugging. All visits and interviews are declined. This is a direct order from our Miss. Please leave, everyone.\"","\"Miss? Are you talking about your Longxin Chairwoman Liu? What does a young girl like her know?\"","A middle-aged leader with a beer belly grew angry: \"This is a standard inspection process. We’re inspecting an enterprise in our district, and a mere security guard dares to stop us?\"","The security team leader remained unmoved: \"I’ll say it one last time. Without an appointment, no one gets in!\"","Just then, a black Mercedes drove up to the factory gate.","The window rolled down, and Zeng Jin poked his head out. Seeing the crowd at the gate, he couldn’t help exclaiming, \"Whoa! So many media and officials. Did something major happen at Longxin?\"","He then signaled to Liang Mengsong, got out of the car to investigate, and learned that Longxin was starting trial production today, hence the swarm of reporters and leaders.","That wasn’t surprising—chip manufacturing was a key industry in China, and trial production at a new chip factory carried great significance, naturally attracting many curious visitors.","But to his surprise, even these people, including the officials, couldn’t get past the gate.","Without dwelling on it, he walked to the front of the crowd and handed his business card to the security team leader: \"Please inform them that Zeng Jin from Taiwan’s Zeng Group has come as invited by Chairwoman Liu.\"","The security guard took the card, glanced at it, and spoke more politely: \"Mr. Zeng, please wait. I need to verify this.\"","\"I understand, I understand.\" Zeng Jin smiled and nodded.","Liang Mengsong didn’t stay in the car long either and got out shortly after.","He was in his early fifties, with jet-black hair, looking quite spirited.","Once out of the car, he looked around at the so-called Longxin factory, his eyes filled with curiosity and surprise.","\"General Manager Zeng, this factory looks quite large,\" he said.","Zeng Jin nodded: \"What’s built now is probably less than a third of the total plan. Over there, large areas are still under construction. Once it’s all complete, it should be a super-factory that ranks on the international list.\"","Liang Mengsong was noncommittal about this. Unlike Zeng Jin, an outsider, he wasn’t so optimistic about Longxin.","Whether it could become an international giant was one thing, but whether this newly established Longxin could withstand foreign sanctions down the line was another question entirely.","But it was still too early to discuss that now.","Zeng Jin continued, \"Engineer Liang, let me give you some insider info. Longxin’s chairwoman is no ordinary person. Her influence in mainland China might be beyond your imagination. If you work for a boss like this, I guarantee you won’t regret it.\"","Although his words were somewhat exaggerated to praise Liu Yutong, part of it came from genuine belief.","Since Liu Yutong was already so formidable overseas, she couldn’t be bad in China, right?","His eagerness to visit was actually to get a deeper understanding of the Wanlong Society’s power.","Once he had a rough idea, he could decide which industries it was best for the Zeng family to expand into mainland China.","Liang Mengsong adjusted his glasses and said nothing.","He had agreed to come to mainland China for two reasons. First, the terms Zeng Jin offered were indeed generous—triple his salary, unlimited R&D funding, and a promise to help resolve his non-compete agreement with TSMC.","Second, he was indeed unhappy at TSMC. Originally, he had planned to try his luck at Samsung in South Korea, but he couldn’t resist Zeng Jin’s repeated invitations. To force him to come to the mainland, this guy even shamelessly hinted that the Zeng family used to be involved in organized crime.","Vaguely, the message was: either come with me, or I’ll take your family with me.","Having no other choice, Liang Mengsong agreed to come to the mainland. But now that he was actually here, he was still uneasy.","Besides Zhongxin, what other decent chip companies existed in mainland China?","He’d never even heard of this Longxin before.","Still, since he was already here, he thought he’d just take a casual look, go through the motions, and maybe tell this yet-unmet chairwoman about the situation in the hopes she’d stop Zeng Jin from bothering him.","Zeng Jin had told him earlier that this Chairwoman Liu was a young girl, with a clean background and a very legitimate company.","Surely she’d be easier to talk to than General Manager Zeng, right?","As he was thinking this, footsteps sounded from inside the factory gate.","Everyone turned to look.","Liu Yutong strode over in large steps, flanked by her assistant and several Wanlong Society bodyguards.","She wasn’t wearing a suit today—just a simple white shirt paired with black trousers, her long hair tied in a high ponytail. She looked less sharp and more fresh and capable.","\"Chairwoman Liu is out!\"","\"Hurry! Get ready for the interview!\"","\"...\"","The reporters stirred into action instantly.","The local officials also put on smiling faces and moved forward to greet her.","Liang Mengsong finally got a clear look at this alarmingly young chairwoman, and inwardly he was astonished.","Even though he had mentally prepared himself, seeing a twenty-year-old woman in charge of such a massive enterprise still felt hard to believe.","Even more admirable was the fact that someone so young had chosen to invest in the chip industry, which burned through money like water and had a long return cycle. Such a choice was extremely rare among young people today.","\"Chairwoman Liu, I’m from the High-Tech Zone Management Committee. Can I trouble you for a few minutes to discuss cooperation?\"","\"Chairwoman Liu! We’re from the Science and Technology Bureau. We’ve come specially for an inspection...\"","\"Chairwoman Liu, I’m from the District Government...\"","\"...\"","The officials gathered around, each introducing themselves.","Liu Yutong frowned, a hint of impatience flashing in her eyes.","\"Step aside, please.\"","\"Longxin factory will release information about trial production at an appropriate time through official channels. We are not accepting interviews at the moment. Leave immediately and do not disrupt the factory’s normal operations.\"","Then, she turned to those officials: \"We appreciate the goodwill from all of you, but this is a critical trial production phase, and the factory needs a quiet environment. If there are cooperation needs in the future, we will proactively contact the relevant departments. For now, please return as well.\"","The smile on the potbellied official's face froze, clearly not expecting Liu Yutong to be so dismissive.","\"Chairman Liu, this is non-cooperation with government work!\"","Liu Yutong looked at him. \"Cooperation? Do you have an official approval from Director Li of the provincial level? Or any formal correspondence from the relevant authorities? If not, please leave! The DragonCore project is a national key priority, not a tourist attraction!\"","\"You!\" The minor official's face flushed bright red.","Liu Yutong simply waved at the head of the security team. \"Escort unrelated personnel out.\"","\"Yes, Miss!\"","The security chief immediately led a group of guards, forcibly driving the reporters and those local officials away from the factory gate.","Zeng Jin stood to the side, watching in shock.","He had known Liu Yutong was assertive, but he never imagined she would be this assertive—even daring to expel local officials. In the province of Taiwan, businessmen treated officials with extreme deference, never acting like this!","After dealing with the trouble outside, Liu Yutong walked over to Zeng Jin and the others.","When she saw Liang Mengsong, a smile immediately spread across her face, and she extended her hand. \"Engineer Liang, you must have had a tiring journey! Please, come in!\"","The speed of her change in expression left everyone present stunned.","Those officials were particularly furious.","Why were these two outsiders treated politely and invited in, while they, the local officials, were rudely kept out?","The more they thought about it, the angrier they grew.","\"How dare she treat us like this!\"","\"I'm going back to file a report right now—environmental review for DragonCore, tax inspections... let's see how long she can keep up this bravado!\"","A young, bespectacled official chimed in indignantly.","\"Outrageous! We came on behalf of the government to care about corporate development, and this is her attitude? We must deal with this severely!\"","\"Exactly! She needs to be taught a lesson, so she won't be so arrogant!\"","The group cursed loudly.","Then, a middle-aged official who had remained mostly silent at the back tugged at the potbellied man's sleeve.","\"Old Liu, calm down. Have you forgotten what background this Chairman Liu has? I've heard that Leader Li at the provincial level has a relationship so close with her, they might as well be family.\"","\"Leader Li? Which Leader Li?\"","\"Which one? The top leader in our region. I heard he even brought this young lady's materials to meetings in the capital, citing her as a model young entrepreneur and emphasizing that she needs focused support and care.\"","The potbellied official's anger instantly vanished.","The others, who had just been so vocal, also fell silent, exchanging glances.","\"Ahem...\"","The potbellied man coughed and abruptly put on a serious expression. \"Actually... when you think about it, Chairman Liu's approach is perfectly understandable. The chip industry is high technology, and trial production requires absolute quiet. It's indeed unsuitable for too many visitors.\"","The others immediately nodded in agreement.","\"Exactly, exactly! We were inconsiderate and too presumptuous. We should have made an appointment—that's basic courtesy!\"","\"Chairman Liu, so young and already taking on such a big role, must have exceptional qualities. We should support great entrepreneurs like her, not cause trouble!\"","\"Right, right! Let's go, let's go, no need to interfere with their work here...\"","As they spoke, they hurried toward their cars and disappeared within moments.","The reporters who had remained nearby witnessed this and looked at one another in bewilderment.","\"What just happened? Why did they leave all of a sudden?\"","\"No idea—quick change of heart than turning a page.\"","A savvy reporter whispered to a colleague, \"I've heard this DragonCore project is deeply connected. That Chairman Liu seems to be... well, let's just say some things are better left unasked. Let's pack up and leave.\"","Inside the factory.","Seeing that Liu Yutong was not taking them to see the production line but heading in another direction, Liang Mengsong asked with some confusion, \"Aren't we going to the production line first?\"","Liu Yutong turned to him with a smile. \"Engineer Liang, let's go to the cafeteria for a meal first, rest a bit, and then tour the production line. Although DragonCore is just starting out, I can assure you that when it comes to employee benefits, we won't fall short of any major international corporation.\"","Liang Mengsong nodded and said nothing more.","He secretly wanted to go straight to the production line, but as a guest, he would follow their arrangements.","When they stepped through the cafeteria doors, they were stunned.","This... was this really a factory canteen?","The cafeteria was decorated like a five-star hotel, with crystal chandeliers and marble floors—extremely luxurious and beautifully appointed.","What was most impressive was the food station: a thirty-meter-long buffet table laid out with an array of dishes—lobster, king crab, wagyu, foie gras, Buddha Jumps Over the Wall, roast duck... everything from Chinese and international cuisines, even the signature dish from Yufang Restaurant—small fish pancakes.","\"This... Chairman Liu, are you sure this is the employee cafeteria?\" Zeng Jin's eyes widened. Giving employees such high-quality meals—wasn't this overly extravagant?","At that moment, employees carried trays as they moved around; someone had a whole lobster with noodles on their plate, another was cutting into a sizzling steak, while a group of young people sat around a table with steaming small fish pancakes and various seafood.","Frankly speaking, this meal standard was far more luxurious than many well-known large companies.","Liu Yutong smiled. \"Engineers at DragonCore work very hard, so the least we can do is supplement them with good food. Our restaurant is fully self-service; take whatever you like. The kitchen has over 20 chefs from starred hotels, capable of preparing both Chinese and Western cuisine. If there's something special you crave, you can tell the cafeteria manager in advance, and as long as conditions allow, we'll try our best to accommodate.\"","Liang Mengsong watched the relaxed engineers happily eating and had to admit that the food here was far better than what he had experienced at Taiwan Semiconductor.","The sight even made his stomach growl faintly.","\"Engineer Liang, President Zeng, help yourselves. I reserved a private room, but I think dining in the main hall has a better atmosphere.\" Liu Yutong personally handed them two trays.","Liang Mengsong took the tray, a bit dazed, and walked to the food station.","He picked two salmon sushi rolls, a serving of Buddha Jumps Over the Wall, and a portion of pan-seared foie gras...","By the time he sat down, his tray was full.","Also in front of them was inevitably a pot of small fish pancakes.","\"Engineer Liang, this small fish pancake is the signature dish of my restaurant chain. I'm not sure if it will suit your taste.\"","Liang Mengsong tried these for the first time. He picked up a small fish and put it into his mouth—the tender fish meat burst with flavor, unexpectedly delicious.","\"How is it?\" Liu Yutong asked.","\"Very good,\" Liang Mengsong answered honestly. He picked up another fish and a piece of griddle cake and began to eat with gusto.","Just as he was eating with relish, a middle-aged man in work clothes hurried into the cafeteria.","“Engineer Qiu!”","“Director Qiu!” some engineers greeted the newcomer.","“Everyone, enjoy your meal!” Qiu Ciyun greeted them cheerfully as well.","Then he briskly walked over to Liu Yutong’s table.","“Chairman, why didn’t you inform me when Engineer Liang arrived?” It was clear he knew Liang Mengsong.","The semiconductor industry was a small circle; top technical talents mostly knew each other, or at least had heard of one another.","“I thought you’d come to the cafeteria first and was about to tell you,” Liu Yutong said with a smile.","Liang Mengsong stood up at that moment and extended his hand: “Engineer Qiu, I’ve long admired you.”","Qiu Ciyun grasped Liang Mengsong’s hand tightly and shook it vigorously: “Engineer Liang, I really didn’t expect Chairman Liu to recruit you. This is fantastic! Fantastic! With you here, we have hope for quickly breaking through the 65-nanometer process and then the 45-nanometer!”","Liang Mengsong felt a bit overwhelmed by his enthusiasm: “Director Qiu, you’re too kind. I haven’t decided yet...”","“Decide? What’s there to decide!”","Qiu Ciyun waved his hand grandly: “Once you’re here, you won’t leave... I mean, don’t go. We’ve got everything you need here. R&D funding is more than enough! Whatever equipment you need, as long as it’s not banned, the chairman can get it for you!”","“By the way, has your family come? Should we bring them over as well? Our chairman’s hometown, Pearl City, has a particularly great environment! It’s also extremely safe! Very livable! I guarantee that once you and your family visit, you’ll never want to leave.”","“Am I right, Chairman?” he said, turning to Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong nodded: “I’ll do my best to meet whatever you need.”","But as Liang Mengsong listened to their exchange, he felt a strange unease creep up on him. How come it sounded like he’d stumbled into a den of thieves? And he couldn’t leave?"]},{"number":714,"title":"Chapter 714: 714: Talent is the Most Valuable Asset","paragraphs":["Liang Mengsong had a very complicated mood during this meal at the Loongson cafeteria.","On the one hand, Qiu Ciyun's enthusiasm and Liu Yutong's display of financial resources really showed him a platform that was completely different from TSMC, a platform full of vitality and ambition.","When Qiu Ciyun talked with him about the technical route, the light in his eyes was something he hadn't seen in some senior executives of TSMC for a long time.","He thought that working with such people should be a rather enjoyable and passionate thing.","On the other hand, the strange remarks from President Qiu and Director Liu, hinting that once he came, he wouldn't be able to leave, made him feel a bit uneasy.","He even felt that he was not here for an inspection, but rather like a hostage being detained.","After the meal.","Liu Yutong noticed that Liang Mengsong needed time to have a more in - depth exchange with Qiu Ciyun, so she arranged for President Qiu to accompany Engineer Liang to visit the partially debugged production lines and the R & D center.","\"Engineer Liang, in terms of technology, President Qiu is an expert. You can have a slow chat. If you have any requirements, you can come to me directly.\"","\"President Qiu, I'm leaving Engineer Liang in your care. Treat him well and make sure Engineer Liang feels at home at Loongson.\"","Qiu Ciyun understood what she meant: \"Don't worry, Chairman. Once Engineer Liang is here, he's one of us. I'll definitely make him feel welcome and let him deeply experience the cohesion of our Loongson family!\"","As he said that, he gave Liang Mengsong a hard pat on the shoulder. This pat made Engineer Liang stagger, and the smile on his face became a bit stiff.","Then Liu Yutong turned to Zeng Jin: \"President Zeng, shall we go somewhere else to talk?\"","\"Couldn't be better!\" Zeng Jin nodded quickly.","The two left the cafeteria and went to the office of the Loongson chairman.","Liu Yutong had only been to this office a few times since it was renovated.","Su Mansu brewed tea for them and then retreated, gently closing the door.","\"Director Liu, this trip has really been worthwhile for me,\" Zeng Jin said first, still in a respectful tone. \"Loongson's grandeur and strength far exceed my imagination. Especially the execution ability of the people under your command is really remarkable!\"","He thought of the security guards at the entrance. Even the security guards under her dared to confront leaders and the media. This showed that the Wanlong Association really had the confidence.","It was also enough to show how powerful the Wanlong Association was on the Chinese mainland. Otherwise, under normal circumstances, how could any security guards dare to confront leaders like this?","Liu Yutong smiled faintly and didn't comment: \"For an enterprise to develop and become a world - class one, the prerequisite is to ensure that the working environment of employees is not disturbed by irrelevant people. Only in this way can everyone focus on their work without distractions.\"","Look! Look! This is what a person with strength and confidence sounds like! The way she talks is different!","Leaders became irrelevant people in her words.","But Zeng Jin deeply agreed with her words: \"What Director Liu said really makes me feel ashamed. I've really witnessed your way of running the enterprise today, which is really worth learning from for people like me!\"","Liu Yutong didn't want to engage in mutual flattery, so she got straight to the point: \"President Zeng came here in such a hurry. You want to talk about cooperation, right? Tell me, which sector does your Zeng family want to enter and what are your ideas?\"","Zeng Jin sat up straight and said seriously: \"You're perceptive, Director Liu. I really came here this time to hear your opinion first.","\"First, it's about our Zeng family's investment direction on the Chinese mainland. In addition to cooperating with your chip talent introduction plan, we also hope to catch the fast - moving train of the mainland's economic development. Our Zeng family is mainly involved in trade, real estate, and some cultural and entertainment industries in Taiwan. This time, I'm primarily considering the entertainment sector. I have a newly - established brokerage company under my name, which has signed some artists.","\"These artists want to develop on the Chinese mainland. But as you know, there are a lot of twists and turns in the entertainment circle, and the water is very deep. Especially for young artists, without some backing, they are easily bullied, and things like unspoken rules are very common.\"","He paused for a moment and continued: \"I heard that in the early days, many artists in Hong Kong relied on gangster backgrounds to gain a foothold and become famous. So when they come to the Chinese mainland to develop this time, they want to ask Director Liu to... take care of them a bit.\"","He said this to test the real strength of the Wanlong Association, such as how much influence it really had and whether it could really protect his people.","In his opinion, having a \"dark\" background in this industry was actually a good thing. The \"darker\" it was, the more it would make people afraid, and the artists would suffer less grievances and be more likely to get resources.","Liu Yutong also had a general understanding of some inside stories in the entertainment circle. It could be said that the entertainment circle was the industry with the most strict seniority - based hierarchy.","Moreover, the entertainment circle was also an industry that capital liked to get involved in these days, so there were bound to be all kinds of interest disputes and even dirty deeds.","For example, the media company under the control of her company currently had the singer Xue Qian as its star attraction.","Now, with the resource support of the Wanlonghui Group, such as endorsements for its products, Weibo endorsements, and group - buying website endorsements, Xue Qian's popularity and commercial value have far exceeded those of the past. He has firmly entered the ranks of first - tier singers.","Even so, in some occasions, Xue Qian still inevitably encounters some intentional or unintentional difficulties.","As for those unknown new artists, in many cases, they are even forced to socialize and accompany guests in drinking, and humble themselves to beg others.","It is quite normal for Zeng Jin to have such concerns.","This is mainly because most of the artists under his management are not well - known. Nowadays, the entertainment circle in Taiwan Province is much more competitive than before. Those with opportunities and resources have all flocked to the Chinese mainland.","Of course, the most important purpose for Zeng Jin to use an entertainment company to break into the mainland market is to test the real strength of the Wanlonghui Group.","Because this industry is most likely to attract some troubles. If you can easily solve them, your strength must be no less. If you can't, it's estimated that other industries of the Zeng family will also have a hard time entering the mainland.","I have to say that this guy is really shrewd!","Liu Yutong took a sip of tea and then slowly stated her attitude: \"Mr. Zeng, the Wanlonghui Group is a regular corporate group, and this will never change.\"","\"As for what you're worried about, there's no need to worry at all.\"","\"The Wanlonghui is a regular company and group, but it doesn't mean we're easy to bully. As long as it's someone we protect, no one dares to lay a finger on them. As for our strength, you'll soon see it with your own eyes.\"","\"The artists under your management want to enter the mainland market. They can just cooperate with my industries. There is a video website called [Longkan Vision] under the Wanlonghui Group. It is currently competing with platforms like Doudou, Kuku, and Leshi and is in urgent need of high - quality artist resources.","There is also the Weibo platform under the group, which is currently the largest social promotion channel in the country. Your artists can first join Weibo, and I'll have people give you enough traffic support.","In addition, one of my media companies is investing in self - produced online dramas, and your artists can participate in them on a priority basis.","Just the internal resources I've mentioned above are enough to give your company's artists sufficient exposure. This is the first cooperation gift I'm giving you.\"","After hearing this, Zeng Jin was shocked. He just wanted to test the strength of the Wanlonghui Group, but he didn't expect to be almost overwhelmed by the entertainment resources in Liu Yutong's hands.","Originally, he thought that the main businesses of the Wanlonghui Group were real estate and the like, because these industries are very suitable for companies similar to gangs.","However, he didn't expect that the Wanlonghui Group was playing at such a high - end level. On one hand, it was involved in chips, and on the other hand, in the Internet and entertainment industries, and all of them were booming.","What a blow it was to him, a former gangster!","He also uses Weibo. Weibo is indeed the leader in the social media sector on the mainland. It has top - notch users and traffic. In particular, it is said that its user scale has exceeded 100 million, which is extremely exaggerated.","As for why he uses Weibo, it's actually because he's addicted to the game of \"Stealing Vegetables\".","This little game seems to be addictive. He sets so many alarms every day for fear that someone will steal his vegetables.","Now that he hears that Weibo also belongs to Liu Yutong, he really wants to ask if she can give him some rare seeds.","Of course, he also knows that Liu Yutong is so generous and offers so many resources right from the start mainly because he has brought a talent that the other side really wants.","If the other side is so generous with just one talent, will they offer even more resources if he brings more talents in the future?","The more Zeng Jin thought about it, the more excited he became. He really didn't expect that a Liang Mengsong could make Liu Yutong attach so much importance. If he could package and bring over all the talents from Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company...","Hey, wait a minute. Doesn't it feel a bit like being a human trafficker?","However, these are not important. The most important thing is to successfully break into the mainland market and establish a foothold to make money.","Thinking of this, Zeng Jin excitedly slapped the table, stood up, and reached out his hand: \"Thank you, Director Liu, for your care.\"","As he said this, he looked at a calligraphy hanging behind Liu Yutong that read, \"Talent is the most precious asset.\"","Director Liu is really a person who practices what she preaches and is truly extraordinary!","Liu Yutong also stood up and shook hands with him: \"You're welcome, Mr. Zeng. This is a cooperation, and cooperation should naturally achieve mutual benefit and win - win results.\"","Zeng Jin: \"What you said really hits the nail on the head, Director Liu. You're absolutely right. Cooperation is all about win - win!\"","\"To be honest, I've brought detailed information about several artists this time. I'd like you to take a look...\"","Just as he was speaking, there was a gentle knock on the office door.","\"Come in.\"","Su Mansu pushed the door open and quickly walked to Liu Yutong's side. She leaned over and whispered the latest news in her ear, which happened to be about their group - controlled video website.","\"Boss, President Lin is in some trouble. He's being jointly besieged by several competitors.\"","After hearing this, Liu Yutong just nodded. There was no particular expression on her face. She only said, \"I got it. Arrange a car to go back to Mingzhu City.\""]},{"number":715,"title":"Chapter 715: 715, Can It Scare Someone to Death","paragraphs":["After listening to Su Mansu's report, Liu Yutong gently set down her teacup and said to Zeng Jin, \"President Zeng, it seems we need to find another place for our discussion. There's a minor issue at Pearl City that needs my attention. How about we head there together? This also gives you the opportunity to see Wanlong Group in person.\"","Zeng Jin, who had been eager for a deeper understanding, nodded immediately. \"I'll follow President Liu's arrangement!\"","Just as the two stepped out of the office, they ran into Qiu Ciyun and Liang Mengsong, who had just returned from the production line at the corridor corner.","\"Chairman, are you going out?\" Qiu Ciyun asked hastily upon seeing Liu Yutong seemingly ready to leave.","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Yes, there are some urgent matters at Pearl City that require my attention.\"","Then she turned to Liang Mengsong. \"Engineer Liang, how was the visit? Is everything satisfactory?\"","Liang Mengsong was a straight shooter who disliked empty flattery, so he answered honestly, \"The production line was led by President Qiu herself, so there's little to criticize. Plus, the LongChip team has great drive, with clear plans and technical roadmaps for the future.\"","He paused before continuing, \"However, the overall manufacturing process still lags far behind international standards. Catching up will be difficult, and the investment won't be small.\"","\"Don't worry about that. We have time on our side, and investment is hardly a concern.\"","Liu Yutong suddenly shifted the topic. \"By the way, Engineer Liang, would you be interested in visiting Pearl City? The headquarters of my Wanlong Group is there, and it’ll give you a more comprehensive view of our company's strength. When choosing a new platform, you can't just focus on the technology—corporate culture and team atmosphere matter just as much.\"","Qiu Ciyun's eyes lit up, and he immediately chimed in, \"Exactly! Engineer Liang, you must go! Pearl City is the Chairman's home base. It’s a place blessed with talent and a favorable environment, and it ranks first in security nationwide—no, globally! And the corporate culture at the Chairman's company is truly unique. You’ll regret it if you don’t see it for yourself!\"","He himself had been quite intimidated by the densely packed, mafia-like black-suited security guards of Wanlong Group, so he deliberately exaggerated to let Liang Mengsong have a similar experience—a little mischievousness on his part.","More importantly, he wanted to remind Liu Yutong that they needed to pull out all the stops to make Liang Mengsong feel \"reassured\" enough to stay, just like he had been back then.","After all, once anyone witnessed the \"real face\" of Wanlong Group, no one ever wanted to leave.","In fact, he was now quite looking forward to seeing the expression on Liang Mengsong's face when confronted with the spectacle of the black-suited guards.","Liu Yutong nodded and extended the invitation once more. \"Let's go, Engineer Liang. President Zeng will join us too.\"","Liang Mengsong was initially inclined to decline—he was a technical man at heart and had little interest in so-called corporate culture.","But Zeng Jin was extremely curious. He very much wanted to see what the legendary Wanlong Group headquarters looked like.","Seeing that Liang Mengsong seemed unwilling to go, Zeng Jin quickly stepped forward, grabbed Liang Mengsong's arm, and put on a face that said, \"If you don’t go, I’ll throw a fit.\"","Left with no choice, Liang Mengsong reluctantly nodded. \"Then it’ll be a trouble to President Liu.\"","\"No trouble at all.\"","Liu Yutong turned to Su Mansu and instructed, \"Arrange the cars. We’re heading straight back to Pearl City. Also, notify Mada to get ready.\"","\"Yes, boss,\" Su Mansu replied.","Soon after, a black Maybach and several Mercedes-Benz vehicles sped out of the LongChip factory, racing toward Pearl City.","Sitting in the front passenger seat of the Maybach, Su Mansu dialed Mada’s number.","\"Brother Ma, the boss will arrive in Pearl City in an hour. By the way, do we have any promotion ceremony for core members today?\"","On the other end of the line came Mada’s boisterous voice.","\"Promotion ceremony? No, the underlings haven’t finished their probation period yet.\"","\"Brother Ma, this could happen.\"","\"Huh? Assistant Su, it really can’t—the procedures aren’t right...\"","\"Brother Ma, this really could happen.\"","\"We have guests coming.\"","The line fell silent for two seconds.","Then, Mada caught on and said excitedly, \"Oh! I get it! Got it! Yes, yes, yes! Absolutely! I’ll arrange it right away! I’ll make sure the show is grand, so the guests will never forget it! Hehehe...\"","Click.","The call ended.","Su Mansu turned around to Liu Yutong. \"Boss, everything is arranged.\"","Liu Yutong nodded with a quiet \"mm.\"","Sitting next to her in the back seat, Zeng Jin was utterly confused. What was this talk of \"having it\" or \"not having it\"? Why all the mystery?","Still, he could roughly guess that they were preparing some kind of special welcome ceremony for their visit—likely something out of the ordinary, or on a large scale.","But how big could it really be? Back in Taiwan Province, he had seen everything—fights involving hundreds of people in gangs, and he had even participated in a few.","Wanlong Group might be powerful, but was a welcome ceremony supposed to scare him to death?","Ridiculous!"]},{"number":716,"title":"Chapter 716: 716, Doesn't the art style seem a bit off","paragraphs":["Although Zeng Jin was eager to see the true strength of the Wanlong Hui, he was still confident that no matter how grand the scene might be, it wouldn’t exceed his expectations.","Thinking back to his youth in Taiwan Province, when he was just a green, hotheaded rookie, he had followed his family’s elders into turf wars and witnessed a thrilling street fight on a night market road.","That night, the two sides combined must have numbered at least three or four hundred people. He hid behind a trash can by the roadside, watched from start to finish, and wasn’t even scared.","As for why he was more cautious now, it was probably because he was older...","Later, the family went legitimate, gradually distancing themselves from the days of fighting and killing. But the air of the underworld in his bones had never faded.","In his view, this so-called reception by the Wanlong Hui would amount to nothing more than sending extra people, lining them up neatly, shouting a few catchy slogans, or at best, putting on some show with a few nice cars to make an impression.","He had seen too much of this sort of thing.","No matter how powerful the Wanlong Hui was, could they really conjure up over a thousand men in black?","Back in the States, those twenty-some men in black had already been formidable enough. If there were really a thousand of that caliber...","Impossible! Absolutely impossible!","Over an hour later, the convoy entered Mingzhu City and finally stopped in front of a building called Shunchang Tower.","Zeng Jin got out of the car, looked up, and silently recited the name to himself.","Shunchang... “Those who obey me prosper, those who defy me perish.” It was certainly domineering enough, just like Liu Yutong’s style.","In truth, the actual owner of the building—the landlord—had originally chosen the name “Shunchang” purely for its literal meaning, hoping for smooth and prosperous business.","But everyone who came here thought of that phrase, “Those who obey me prosper, those who defy me perish.” It was really just the Wanlong Hui’s influence at play.","After getting out of the car, Zeng Jin saw two neat rows of men in black at the main entrance, about seven or eight in total, all standing upright and full of energy.","When Liu Yutong appeared, they greeted her in unison: “Miss!”","Zeng Jin let out a mental “Oh.”","Sure enough, it was just as he guessed: the men in black were limited, maybe even fewer than he had expected.","“President Zeng, Master Liang, please come in.” Liu Yutong gestured slightly to them, then led the way into the building.","Inside the first-floor lobby, Zeng Jin looked around but didn’t notice anything special.","The decor was modern and minimalist: a reception desk, a lounge area, potted plants—it looked much like the headquarters lobby of an ordinary company.","Except of course for the extra men in black suits.","“Chairman Liu, should we head to the meeting room first, or...?” Zeng Jin asked.","“No rush.”","Liu Yutong waved over one of the men in black: “Cheng Gang, come here.”","Cheng Gang, who had been standing by at a distance, immediately jogged over and greeted her respectfully: “Miss!”","Liu Yutong looked him over and then asked, “Have your gunshot wounds fully healed?”","Cheng Gang nodded. “Yes, miss. Thank you for your concern!”","Hearing this, Zeng Jin’s eyelids twitched.","What? Gunshot wounds?","Good heavens, the Wanlong Hui was certainly no ordinary group... With mainland China’s strict gun control, they still dared to use firearms in clashes?","Badass! Truly badass!","At that moment, he silently raised his assessment of the Wanlong Hui’s strength by another notch.","Using such things wasn’t unusual in Taiwan Province, Hong Kong, or even less so in the States. But in mainland China, it was a whole different story.","Then Liu Yutong asked about everyday matters—how his younger brother was adjusting after transferring schools, whether his grades were keeping up. Her tone didn’t sound like a boss talking to a subordinate, but more like a family member.","Cheng Gang felt a warmth in his heart as he answered every question from the miss.","With the company’s help, his brother had already transferred to a school in the city and was currently staying in Cheng Gang’s rented apartment. Of course, the company provided a housing subsidy, so he didn’t actually have to pay a cent.","Moreover, the new apartment the miss had awarded him was almost ready for delivery. It was located not far from the Wanlong Hui’s main headquarters under construction, on the same piece of land Liu Yutong had won at an auction.","The residential development was being built in tandem with the Wanlong Hui headquarters, and it was expected to be topped off and handed over by the end of the year.","As for the Wanlong Hui headquarters, it would take a bit longer to move in, with completion expected between the end of 2010 or early 2011—about a year later than the residential complex.","That pace wasn’t slow at all; it was actually quite fast, since building a corporate headquarters and a residential community were entirely different matters.","Just a quick render of the Wanlong Hui headquarters done in Doubao!","After Liu Yutong finished chatting with Cheng Gang—an ordinary core member of the Wanlong Hui—she instructed him, “First, take President Zeng and Master Liang on a tour of the company, then bring them to my office.”","Cheng Gang immediately nodded. “Yes, miss!”","Once Liu Yutong turned and left, he walked straight up to Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong, gesturing with a hand: “President Zeng, Master Liang, this way, please.”","Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong exchanged a glance, then followed Cheng Gang toward the elevator.","The elevator first stopped on the third floor.","In the early days, Wanlong Company only rented the top ten floors of this building. Later, as its personnel expanded significantly, it simply rented the entire building.","The martial arts hall and training grounds originally located on the upper floors were also moved to the second and third floors.","As soon as the elevator doors opened, Zeng Jin and his group heard a series of low, rhythmic shouts.","Three professional boxing rings of standard size appeared before them. At that moment, several pairs of men in black, wearing helmets and protective gear, were engaged in high-intensity sparring on the rings.","The visual impact of fist hitting flesh was palpable even from several meters away, exuding a strong sense of pressure.","On the other side was a spacious fitness equipment area. Treadmills, rowing machines, squat racks, barbells—all the equipment was available, and the specifications and professionalism rivaled any top-tier commercial gym.","Some men in black were working out there as well, shirtless, each displaying a set of eight-pack abs. Even without touching them, one could sense the explosive power contained within their bodies.","Zeng Jin quietly watched those figures training and suddenly understood a little why, in Cloud City in the States, those twenty men in black under Chu Yang had been able to grind down those foreigners, even professional boxers, and rub their faces into the ground.","Given this level of training intensity and professionalism, they were likely on par with—if not exceeding—many professional fighters.","It was incredibly professional!","\"Strengthening the body and staying fit is part of our corporate culture,\"","Cheng Gang explained calmly beside him. \"Having a healthy physique benefits both the individual and the work. Of course, all training emphasizes discipline and control. Private fights are strictly prohibited, and bullying the weak is forbidden.\"","Zeng Jin silently nodded.","To be honest, Wanlong Company was far more professional than many of the gangs he had seen, and even stronger than the Zeng family at its peak.","Just looking at their training intensity confirmed it. Back in the day, what they did was called \"running the streets,\" but this—this was the real deal!","It seemed his guess was right: every man in black at Wanlong Company was a formidable fighter.","After touring the boxing gym and fitness area, Cheng Gang led them to the floor where the law firm was located.","The law firm occupied two floors: one for offices and one for studying. They arrived at the study area.","This place was completely different from the boxing gym. The atmosphere here was intensely academic and much quieter.","The first thing that caught the eye was a large plaque displaying the words: \"Cautious, meticulous, bold, knowledgeable in the law, and united in knowledge and action.\"","Just reading those words was enough to inspire solemn respect. What a proper attitude toward learning!","No wonder it was a law firm!","However, the layout here puzzled them a bit. The corridor was flanked by rooms of varying sizes, each filled with dozens of desks and chairs, resembling school classrooms.","Most rooms were empty at the moment, except for the first classroom, which still had its lights on. Inside, seven or eight men in black sat scattered.","If the boxing gym and fitness area had seemed somewhat normal to Zeng Jin—after all, he had seen the fighting ability of these men in black in the States, and such strength had to come from training, so it made sense for Wanlong Company to have a boxing gym and fitness center—","But this so-called study area completely baffled him. It left him in awe.","In the still-occupied classroom, the people sitting there were not the lawyers he had imagined, but men in black from Wanlong Company.","And they were not smoking, playing cards, or chatting idly like the thugs he had imagined. Instead, they were... reading?","Yes, really reading!","The scene felt utterly surreal.","Why would proper gang members be reading books?","Especially since the books seemed completely out of place with their rough-and-tumble image and temperament.","Those books turned out to be things like Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure Law, and Public Security Administration Punishments Law—all legal texts. This was absurd!","And that wasn’t the end of it. The real shock was that they not only read the books but also analyzed them.","But their interpretations were entirely different from what one might expect.","For instance, on the whiteboard at the front of the classroom, someone had written a problem.","Next to it, there was a simple diagram of the human skeleton, with key body parts labeled.","After Zeng Jin read the text clearly, his eyes went wide.","It was a case analysis:","Case Analysis: If an enemy charges at you with a weapon, you dodge to the side and then strike the side of his knee from behind with a baton, does this constitute legitimate self-defense? Please analyze based on Article 20 of the Criminal Law and the principles of human biomechanics.","Below it were a few lines of small-print annotations:","Note 1: Striking the side of the knee can instantly incapacitate the opponent without causing permanent disability, meeting the necessary limits of self-defense.","Note 2: Remember to avoid the back of the head, neck, spine, and other vital areas to prevent excessive force.","Note 3: In practice, it is recommended to first shout, \"Don’t come any closer!\" to strengthen the on-site evidence of defensive intent.","???","Zeng Jin completely lost it.","What the hell was this?","He couldn’t help himself and turned to ask Cheng Gang, \"You... you study like this on a regular basis?\"","Cheng Gang’s expression remained calm as he nodded. \"Yes, this is our daily legal study session. There are fewer people here today.\"","Upon hearing this, Zeng Jin couldn’t help but grumble to himself: “Was I asking about the lack of people? The way you guys study the law—are you aiming to follow it, or to find loopholes? Every single one of you knows the law so well that you shout out warnings before a fight just to leave evidence. Is this a gang of thugs or a pack of legal maniacs?”","Cheng Gang seemed to pick up on Zeng Jin’s confusion and explained again: “Our Wanlong Association is a legitimate enterprise. Abiding by the law is our bottom line. All core members must regularly undergo legal knowledge training and exams to ensure that everyone’s actions stay within the legal framework. Only by understanding the law can we better obey it, and better strike back—uh, protect our rights and act bravely for justice.”","Zeng Jin: “...”","Liang Mengsong: “...”"]},{"number":717,"title":"Chapter 717: 717, So Arrogant","paragraphs":["After leaving the study room with its whiteboard covered in legal case analyses, Zeng Jin felt like his entire understanding had been repeatedly ground down.","A gang... no, the people of the Wanlong Association had taken their study of law to such a level that he didn’t even know what to say anymore.","He even had a strange illusion—that he hadn’t come to visit some gang headquarters, but had stumbled into some bizarre, otherworldly base.","But what he never expected was that what he saw next would truly make him understand why the Wanlong Association could rule the roost in Bright Pearl City with an iron fist.","Cheng Gang led them away from the study area, took the elevator up a few more floors, and entered the Wanlong Association’s normal office zone.","This floor looked completely ordinary—exactly like any legitimate corporate office.","Zeng Jin breathed a sigh of relief, thinking he could finally see something normal. But when his gaze shifted to the walls, he froze again.","Almost every wall in the office was covered with something that looked like silk banners of commendation.","[Upholding Justice, Serving the People with Warmth]—signed by a local precinct of the Bright Pearl City Police.","[Model of Police-Community Cooperation]—signed by the Bright Pearl City General Police Headquarters.","[Brave and Righteous, Noble Character]—signed by the Bright Pearl City Office of Social Security and Comprehensive Management.","Zeng Jin’s eyelid twitched. He took a few more steps forward and peered into another meeting room with its door open.","That wall was even more over-the-top.","Aside from the banners, it was hung with several framed group photos.","He recognized some of the people in the photos—they seemed to be high-ranking members of the Wanlong Association’s men in black.","In the photos, they were dressed in black, smiling, shaking hands with several middle-aged leaders in police uniforms.","Zeng Jin: “...”","Wait, what... is this for real?","You’re a syndicate. I could accept you having enforcers, training in martial arts, even studying those outrageous criminal laws.","But hanging police-given commendation banners all over your office and having chummy photo ops with top cops? What kind of game is this?","Has collusion between gangs and authorities on the mainland really gotten so blatant? The protection umbrella isn’t even hidden anymore? You just show it off to outsiders like this?","Isn’t this way too audacious?","The sheer absurd contrast was beyond words. He wasn’t afraid—he just couldn’t hold back his laughter, really couldn’t hold it back!","Cheng Gang, long accustomed to this reaction, explained matter-of-factly: “The Wanlong Association has always adhered to the principle of actively participating in social welfare, assisting the police in maintaining public order, and cracking down on illegal and criminal activities. These banners and awards are merely part of our fulfillment of social responsibility and contribution to building a harmonious society. There’s really no need to be so surprised.”","Zeng Jin coughed dryly and nodded repeatedly: “Right, right, right. Your company’s level of social awareness is truly impressive. No wonder Director Liu always says the Wanlong Association is a legitimate business. I’ve seen it for myself today. This is indeed, indeed very... very unique.”","Even as he spoke, his mind was exploding with silent sarcasm.","No wonder your Wanlong Association could grow this big, could expand your businesses this far—your connections must be this rock-solid.","This isn’t even about playing both sides of the law anymore. You’ve literally moved the table into broad daylight.","Before seeing the Wanlong Association headquarters with his own eyes, he never imagined such a... bizarre and brazen syndicate could exist.","He practiced boxing, studied law, and even had his picture taken with police leaders with his arm around their shoulders, showing it off openly.","When you're in the underworld and can pull off something like this, you're no longer just a part of the underworld.","That's just way too impressive!","Liang Mengsong, who had been quiet all this while, kept nodding as he looked at these honors. \"Not bad! Not bad! There aren't many companies this dedicated to public welfare and so responsible.\"","Zeng Jin: \"???\"","Wait, Liang, what are you saying?","You don't actually think Wanlong Society is some kind of public-spirited, police-civilian partnership model enterprise, do you?","He opened his mouth, ready to say something, but swallowed the words back down.","It suddenly hit him—Liang Mengsong had never known the true nature of Wanlong Society from start to finish.","Then it was fine."]},{"number":718,"title":"Chapter 718: 718, Problems Faced by Video Websites and Artists.","paragraphs":["After almost finishing the tour of the Wanlong Association’s headquarters, Zeng Jin couldn’t help but voice the question that had been on his mind to Cheng Gang.","“Brother Cheng, someone as capable as you—are there many like you in the Wanlong Association?”","He had long speculated that there were at most a hundred or eighty black-clad men at the top of the organization, but it was just a guess.","So he wanted to get a clearer picture.","Cheng Gang smiled a little awkwardly at the question. “Mr. Zeng, you flatter me. I’m nothing special, just an ordinary member in the company. There are plenty of brothers stronger than me.”","“Oh?”","Zeng Jin raised an eyebrow. “Plenty? How many exactly?”","Cheng Gang thought seriously for a moment. “Well... quite a few. I’m not exactly sure of the number, but definitely a lot.”","He truly didn’t know the exact count.","There were still large numbers of core members scattered in other regions, with branches, projects, and outposts spread out everywhere. Cheng Gang wasn’t in charge of personnel, so he only had a rough idea and could only answer vaguely.","But how many is “a lot”?","A hundred? Two hundred?","For a large organization, having over a hundred well-trained black-clad men was already terrifying.","That number alone would make them dominant across the entire province, arguably invincible anywhere. The heads of local gangs and factions were mostly street-level thugs, nowhere near the level of these professionally trained operatives.","No matter how many street thugs they had, they couldn’t match such high-caliber enforcers.","Yet, judging from the subtle expression on Cheng Gang’s face, the number might be even higher?","Could it be five hundred?","Impossible.","It wasn’t that Wanlong couldn’t afford to maintain five hundred black-clad men—it simply wasn’t necessary.","Zeng Jin shook his head, thinking he was overthinking it, and didn’t press further. Instead, he followed Cheng Gang up to the top floor—to Liu Yutong’s office.","By then, quite a few people had already gathered inside.","Lin Muyang, CEO of Longkan Vision, the prominent lawyer Zhao Tianyi, Yu Xin, Yun Cheng, Zhang Dalong, and even the singer Xue Qian were all present.","They were in the middle of discussing the joint crackdown by industry competitors on Longkan Vision.","“Director Liu, according to the plan drafted by Lawyer Zhao, we’ve completed the net closure.”","“The undercover tech personnel we planted in several competing platforms have been uploading large amounts of exclusive copyrighted film and TV content. Once these were put online on their platforms, the viewing numbers skyrocketed. Some top series even saw pirated views exceeding tens of millions.”","“Our legal department, after securing the evidence, sent out cease-and-desist letters demanding takedowns and compensation. We currently have over a hundred lawsuits underway, with total damages exceeding five hundred million yuan. And we’ve basically won all of them, applying for asset preservation and freezing part of their assets.”","“But they’ve been pushed to the brink.”","“Right now, Longkan Vision can’t obtain network broadcast rights for any mainstream variety shows. Whether it’s the established hit shows or the new weekend prime-time programs this year, we’re completely excluded. The variety section on our platform is suffering a severe shortage of content, and daily active users have dropped by nearly eight percent in the past week.”","“And that’s not even the worst part.”","“We started focusing on producing our own web dramas last year. A few have already wrapped filming and are awaiting review, and two more are in post-production. But suddenly, the censorship bureau blocked all our submissions. The official reason for rejection was that the content didn’t meet regulations.”","“But the same themes, the same level of explicitness, were passing reviews just fine not long ago. I made some inquiries and heard that several of the platforms’ major shareholders are connected to a few influential young masters in the capital. It seems they used their connections at the bureau to deliberately choke us...”","“...”","After Lin Muyang finished explaining, Xue Qian also shared the difficulties their side was facing.","“Besides what Lin told you, our media company is running into some trouble too.”","“Huang Guotai has officially sent a notice stating that none of our artists are allowed to participate in any self-produced variety shows anymore. Whether it’s the long-running classic ‘The Big Camp’ or the phenomenally popular new show ‘Upward’ launched just last year, our artists’ names have been completely removed from the lineup.”","“At first, it was only Huang Guotai. But then even Litchi and Blueberry, those satellite TV stations, followed suit. Although no official documents were issued, when our people tried to coordinate with them, all they got were vague evasions and endless delays until nothing came of it.”","“Now, in the entire company, not a single recognizable artist can get on any mainstream satellite TV variety show. It feels like we’ve been completely isolated from the industry, and it’s a huge problem.”","This era isn’t like the future. The popularity, national reach, and buzz-generating power of variety shows back then were on a whole other level—far beyond what later times could compare to. Especially for young artists, without exposure on variety shows, their careers would take a serious hit.","Only a handful of top-tier stars and big-name actors could afford to skip variety shows without suffering consequences. But that’s just a small minority.","“...”","After quietly listening to the challenges they were facing, Liu Yutong couldn’t help but think, “No wonder the entertainment industry is so murky.”","All because they refused to pay a few hundred million, they got so worked up they even dragged in connections from the capital—blocking reviews and blacklisting artists.","She picked up her teacup and took a sip.","But when you break down the problem, it wasn’t as complicated as Lin Muyang and Xue Qian made it sound.","There was only one core issue: the review channel for web dramas and related content had to be cleared.","They couldn’t let the bureau keep blocking them.","If the lifeline of self-produced content was strangled, video streaming sites would be left with only one option: buying copyrights. But many high-profile copyrights had long been cornered by a few leading platforms working together. If this kept up, these sites were heading for a dead end.","This knot had to be untied at its root.","As for Xue Qian’s side, their problem was the easiest to fix.","Not allowed to appear on variety shows?","Perfect.","She never liked squeezing around the same table with others anyway.","If they wouldn’t let her artists on those shows, then she’d just create a variety show even hotter than those old stalwarts.","When that time came, those TV stations would probably be begging her to send their artists over."]},{"number":719,"title":"Chapter 719: 719, Planning a Variety Show.","paragraphs":["At that moment, everyone in the office turned their gaze toward Liu Yutong, waiting for her decision. After a moment of thought, Liu Yutong named someone: \"Xue Qian.\"","\"Here,\" Xue Qian said, sitting up straight immediately.","\"What's your take on not being allowed on variety shows?\" Liu Yutong asked.","Xue Qian pondered briefly and replied earnestly, \"Chairman, to be honest, the impact is definitely there. Several of our company's artists were really hoping to get some exposure on the popular stage of 'Base Camp,' but they all got cut. For me personally, it's not a big deal—I rarely go on variety shows anyway—but...\"","\"But you feel frustrated, right?\"","Xue Qian gave a wry smile and nodded. \"Yeah, a little.\"","Liu Yutong nodded, then abruptly shifted the topic with a seemingly unrelated question: \"Do you like singing?\"","Without hesitation, Xue Qian replied, \"Of course I do. If I didn't love singing, I wouldn't have chosen this path.\"","\"Then would you be willing to be a mentor on a music show?\"","\"Huh? Me, a mentor? I've only been in the industry a few years.\"","Without elaborating, Liu Yutong turned to Lin Muyang. \"Muyang, what does Longkan Vision need most right now?\"","Lin Muyang answered without missing a beat, \"Content—especially popular content that can be produced steadily long-term, spark discussions, and draw in new users. Right now, major TV stations are holding onto variety show copyrights tightly. Even if we're willing to spend big money, it's hard to buy suitable programs.\"","\"Then we'll make our own.\"","The moment Liu Yutong said this, everyone in the office felt a familiar rhythm. A thought crossed their minds in unison: The young lady/chairman is about to stir things up again.","Lin Muyang paused for a second, then confirmed, \"Chairman, do you mean we develop our own variety show?\"","\"Yes.\"","Liu Yutong nodded lightly. She then asked Yu Xin for a notepad and pen and began writing as she spoke.","\"The name will be 'The Voice of Dragon Country'—a music talent show. It'll air primarily on Longkan Vision, with simultaneous syndication on Lucheng Satellite TV. The core concept of this show is two words: blind selection.\"","\"Blind selection?\"","The term stoked everyone's curiosity.","Liu Yutong explained, \"Four mentors sit with their backs to the stage, listening only to the voice, not the appearance. If a mentor feels moved by the voice, they press the button in front of them, and their chair spins around. If multiple mentors turn around, the power shifts—the contestant gets to choose which mentor's team to join.\"","\"Remember, this isn't a beauty contest; it's a voice contest. Contestants don't need to be handsome or pretty, they don't need to flatter others, and they don't even need to be articulate. As long as they have a great voice, they deserve a spot on that stage.\"","Upon hearing this, Xue Qian started thinking seriously.","He understood too well what this meant.","Talent shows in the Dragon Country's music scene had been around for over a decade, from early shows like 'Super Girl' to various later incarnations—all essentially picking idols rather than real singers.","Most of the time, factors like contestants' looks, stage presence, popularity, and buzz mattered far more than the voice itself. Many truly talented singers couldn't even get past the preliminary auditions, simply because their appearance didn't meet the standard.","The blind selection model proposed by the chairman completely overturned the traditional talent show logic.","But would this really work?","However, when Lin Muyang and the others heard about the format of this new music variety show, their reactions were completely different from Xue Qian, who was an industry insider.","“Genius!”","“Absolute genius!”","“Chairman, this model feels incredibly fresh to me. Right now, whether it’s cover songs or competitive performances, the audience has already figured out all the tricks. With blind selection, just the setup of the mentors turning their backs to the contestants can max out anticipation.”","“Plus, the buzz will definitely be huge—which contestant gets fought over by multiple mentors, which one doesn’t get a single turn, why a mentor turned around, why a contestant picked one mentor over another... these are all hot topics. As long as the production isn’t a letdown, this is bound to become a blockbuster hit!”","The others nodded in agreement, their thoughts aligned with Lin Muyang’s.","The key was picking the right mentors, because in this blind selection format, the mentors were the real stars.","Liu Yutong seemed to have already thought of this and scribbled a few names on her notepad.","Xue Qian leaned in curiously to take a look, and when he did, he couldn’t help but exclaim, “Holy crap!”","“Jay Chou, Faye Wong, Han Hong... and me?”","Liu Yutong looked up at him and asked, “What do you think?”","“Chairman, this lineup is too stacked. A pop king, a diva, a legendary singer... with my current status, sitting alongside them as a mentor—I’m afraid I don’t quite measure up.” Xue Qian wasn’t being modest; he was stating facts.","“None of that matters. Whether you’re qualified is up to us to decide. We’re the money behind this.”","Liu Yutong then said to Lin Muyang, “Get those three to come on board as mentors. Money isn’t an issue. Also, let them know this is a purely music-oriented program with no behind-the-scenes manipulation—we can guarantee that.”","“And as for Lucheng Satellite TV, I’ll personally give them a heads-up. Haven’t they always wanted to create a phenomenal variety show? If we fully fund the production and just borrow their broadcasting platform, there’s no way they’ll refuse.”","“As for the show’s budget—four words: no ceiling at all!”","“President Zhang, make sure Weibo is fully involved to maximize buzz. The finals’ voting will be hosted on Weibo, but it needs strict control. No vote rigging, and no links that could easily be tampered with.”","Zhang Dalong replied, “Got it. I’ll have my team coordinate with President Lin.”","Liu Yutong then turned to Zhao Tianyi: “Tianyi, as for those platforms trying to surround us, keep hitting them hard. Also, the legal contracts for the new variety show will be handled by your law firm.”","Zhao Tianyi nodded. “Understood!”","“Miss Liu, since this variety show is self-produced, should we include a clause for a ‘pre-competition exclusive artist management contract’? Every contestant who passes the auditions and enters the blind selection recording must sign a five-year full contract with Longyu Entertainment. If they breach it, the penalty fee will be set at the industry’s maximum.”","“Isn’t that clause too harsh? What if contestants think it’s a predatory contract and refuse to sign?” Yu Xin suddenly interjected.","“This contract is indeed necessary. It won’t be mandatory during the audition stage—they can choose not to sign. But if they don’t, they can’t proceed to the blind selection recording. We’re putting up the money, building the stage, and using our resources to make stars. We’re not going to let other agencies swoop in and reap the benefits after we’ve done the work,” Liu Yutong said.","For the first season of this show, the Wanlonghui Group was definitely the sole funder. Not to mention costs like venue rental and equipment purchases, just inviting those three mentors alone probably required half a small target.","When you add up the entire production and promotional costs of the show, one small target was definitely necessary.","In such a situation, if they didn’t sign contracts with the contestants, what difference would it make from doing charity?","Xue Qian also nodded in agreement: “Signing contracts is indeed necessary, and signing for just five years is already very reasonable.”","Having come from being an unknown himself, he knew the industry’s unspoken rules all too well.","In most talent shows, contracts lasting eight or ten years were common, and contestants had no right to refuse. Their decision to sign for only five years was anything but ordinary—it was incredibly fair.","Moreover, the big boss of Longyu Entertainment was Liu Yutong.","Based on his understanding of her, she definitely wouldn’t stoop to underhanded schemes or deliberately exploit artists.","Even if an artist wanted to leave someday, as long as they followed the contract terms, she would never intentionally hold them back.","Incidentally, Longyu Entertainment was formerly Xue Qian’s studio. It was only renamed Longyu Media after the Wanlonghui Group took a controlling stake.","Sure enough.","Just as Xue Qian thought of this, Liu Yutong made it clear in public.","“Tianyi, all the signing contracts for the show must be clear and transparent. No hidden clauses. We don’t exploit people, and there’s no need to. Also, any form of backroom deals must be prohibited, as well as any pre-determined advancement slots or winners. If discovered, strict penalties will be enforced!”","In truth, she emphasized this not just because she disliked underhanded practices, but also because she personally enjoyed watching music variety shows. In her previous life, she had watched a few seasons of The Voice, though she stopped after that.","From her perspective as an audience member, if she found out the show had backroom deals or a pre-determined winner, she would definitely feel upset.","If it upset her as a viewer, then others would also be upset.","Zhao Tianyi: “Understood! Miss!”","Liu Yutong then turned to Xue Qian: “Teacher Xue Qian, among these four mentors, you have the least seniority, but you’re one of us. During the audition stage, pay close attention. Make sure those truly talented but unknown individuals get their chance. Also, we’re creating content. The premise of good content is that it must be real.”","Xue Qian nodded firmly: “Understood, Chairwoman!”","Lin Muyang then raised another question: “Chairwoman, who will host the show?”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment and said, “Find someone who talks fast.”","“Huh?”","“The blind selection format requires a tight pace. When mentors turn their chairs and compete for contestants, the host needs to quickly guide the segments, control the flow, and cue the procedures. Don’t pick someone who drags out commercial lines. We need someone quick-witted, able to riff, and unafraid of the stage.”","“Got it.”","“Chairwoman, when will we launch the show?”","“As soon as possible, as long as it hits the summer schedule.”","“Also, record and archive all judging segments for review.”","“Understood!”","After finalizing most of the show’s details, Lin Muyang brought up the thorny issue again: “Chairwoman, you’ve arranged the new variety show, but we still have that deadly censorship problem on our end.”","“The web series got blocked. If our variety show also gets blocked, what do we do? If those aristocratic young masters in the capital are determined to mess with us, we won’t be able to handle it.”","This was the real crux of the problem.","No matter how strong one’s local connections were, once they reached the capital, it was a whole different set of rules.","If they couldn’t win over that group, then all the planning would be nothing but a waste of time.","Yet Liu Yutong never seemed worried about it: “I’ll handle this matter. I happen to need to go to the capital again in a couple of days.”","The moment Lin Muyang and the others heard that, they all felt relieved.","It was as if, in their minds, there was nothing Liu Yutong couldn’t solve.","Just then, a knock came at the door.","“Come in!”","Cheng Gang pushed the door open from outside. Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong, who had just finished touring the Wanlonghui Company, stepped inside.","Seeing this, Liu Yutong turned to Su Mansu and asked, “Is Mata ready?”","Su Mansu replied immediately, “Boss, Brother Ma sent a message ten minutes ago saying everything is set and he’s just waiting for you to bring the guests over.”","“Good.”","Liu Yutong stood up, casually grabbed the black trench coat draped over the back of her chair, and threw it over her shoulders as she walked straight toward Zeng Jin and the others.","Everyone else in the office also rose and followed behind her.","“President Zeng, Engineer Liang, since you’ve finished touring the company, it’s the perfect time for some late-night snacks. This hour, the food stalls are quite lively.”","For some reason, when Zeng Jin heard her say that, his heart tightened inexplicably."]},{"number":720,"title":"Chapter 720: 720, Directly Enclosing an Entire Street, a Stunning Scene","paragraphs":["“President Zeng, Liang Mengsong, after a tour around the company, you must be hungry. The night view of Pearl City may not compare to those big cities, but the night market snacks are quite distinctive. I’ll take you to try some local late-night eats.”","Zeng Jin responded politely, but his heart was pounding with unease.","Just now, inside Shunchang Tower, he’d seen a boxing gym, a criminal law study room, and walls covered with silk banners and group photos—everything he’d known for half a lifetime had been turned upside down.","He honestly couldn’t imagine what kind of scene this Chairman Liu’s simple offer of a late-night snack might create that would blow his mind yet again.","Liang Mengsong, however, didn’t overthink it. To him, this was just a normal part of hosting.","He nodded and said, “Then we’ll trouble you, Chairman Liu. I actually enjoy strolling through night markets too.”","Liu Yutong smiled faintly without adding much and headed straight for the elevator.","By the time they reached the ground floor, a group of black-suited men had already gathered behind them.","Zeng Jin kept sneaking glances back, silently counting the numbers.","In just that short time, at least thirty black-clad men had fallen in behind Liu Yutong.","And every single one of them stood tall and upright, with sharp eyes and an aura of pressure that made your skin crawl.","Back in his days in Taiwan Province, he’d seen plenty of so-called underworld big shots making their grand entrances.","The men around them were either rakish thugs reeking of hoodlum energy or loudmouthed enforcers who couldn’t wait to show off their criminal ties.","But Wanlong Corporation’s people were completely different.","Quiet, straight-backed, and well-drilled—like blades sheathed in their scabbards, no threat at rest, but guaranteed to draw blood the moment they were unleashed.","The more you watched them, the more unsettling they became.","When they stepped out of the building, a dozen shiny black Mercedes-Benz cars were already lined up outside in a row.","A black-suited man stood rigidly beside each vehicle. At the sight of Liu, they all bowed in unison and greeted her.","“Miss!”","Zeng Jin stopped short and instinctively moved closer to Liang Mengsong.","Liang Mengsong, still unruffled, simply thought how disciplined the company’s employees were—truly high-class.","Liu Yutong gave a slight nod, then walked straight to the black Maybach at the center.","The man beside the car smoothly opened the door for her.","Once Liu was inside, the others got into their own vehicles, and the convoy set off for the night market.","Their destination wasn’t any of Pearl City’s most famous old-school night markets, but a fairly new commercial street.","Right at the entrance stood a massive sign: Wanlong Plaza.","The plaza itself was already closed for the night, but only an adjacent side street remained brightly lit.","This was a pedestrian street built behind the plaza, which turned into a night market after dark.","The whole street was strung with red lanterns, and warm yellow light spilled from every shop; cooking smoke curled upward, and the aroma of cumin and chili mixed with the smell of charcoal drifted far away.","At first glance, it looked just like any ordinary night market.","Seeing this through the car window, Zeng Jin breathed a slight sigh of relief.","Well, this matched his guesses—it’s just eating some street food. At least they wouldn’t create another epic spectacle, right?","There had already been plenty of black-suited men back in the building. Surely they couldn’t be so over-the-top as to rent out an entire street.","But the next second, Zeng Jin sensed something wrong.","A night market on any normal night should be bustling with people.","Yet now, aside from the drifting cooking smoke he could see, it was eerily quiet—was that right?","And for some reason, even though from the car the whole street appeared lit up, the closer the convoy got, the more it seemed darker—an illusion, maybe.","It was just strange.","However, when Zeng Jin’s party got out and turned into the pedestrian street at the corner, a single glance inside made their blood run cold.","From the entrance, stretching deep into the street, were rows upon rows of ordinary plastic round tables, packed tight together like a black dragon coiling through the middle of the road, its head and tail invisible.","The black wasn’t the color of the tables or chairs—it came from the people seated at every one, all dressed in identical black suits!","The crowd sprawled as far as the eye could see.","Warm yellow streetlights spilled down over that sea of black figures. Though the lights were clear and bright, it felt as if the day had truly turned black.","A wave of pressure, like tidewater, surged from all sides and instantly swallowed Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong, leaving them almost unable to breathe.","In their decades of life, this was the first time they’d fully witnessed a physical phenomenon—it turned out that black really does absorb light.","The most terrifying part was that despite the vast number of people, nobody spoke. The silence was oppressive.","Even all the shop owners and waitstaff along the street dared not say a word; they just buried themselves in grilling skewers and preparing snacks, working much faster than usual.","Of course, though they were nervous and uneasy, inside they were delighted—at least today’s turnover would be all but guaranteed.","Zeng Jin's hair stood on end, his scalp tingled, and his legs uncontrollably trembled.","He blinked hard, thinking his eyes were playing tricks on him.","Who would believe it? In all his years, he'd never seen someone rent out an entire street before.","He had witnessed countless spectacles in his life—street brawls in the back alleys of Taiwan Province, lavish banquets at the Chamber of Commerce, gatherings of both the underworld and the elite... but never had any scene made him tremble from the depths of his soul like this one.","He had been wrong!","And spectacularly so!","What did he think? That the Black Dragon Society only had a hundred or so men in black? The formation before him was ten times that, at least!","Just from what he could see, there had to be no fewer than a thousand people!","And this street stretched at least a kilometer long, making it impossible to see how many were seated farther back. It only gave him one impression—that this black dragon had no end.","Liang Mengsong was also completely dumbfounded, his mind wiped blank.","An engineer working with chips, his whole life had been spent dealing with labs, machines, and code—how could he have ever witnessed something like this!","He had genuinely believed the Black Dragon Society was a legitimate, socially responsible company dedicated to public welfare.","But what did this scene in front of him mean?","Was he really just too naive?","Liang Mengsong stiffly turned his head, looking at the calm-faced Liu Yutong beside him. His lips moved, but no words came out.","Who on Earth was this unsettlingly young chairman?","Zeng Jin swallowed hard, his voice trembling as he asked, \"Mis... Miss Liu, if I may ask, how many brothers are here tonight?\"","Liu Yutong casually said a number: \"Probably... less than three thousand.\"","Zeng Jin: \"...\"","Liang Mengsong: \"...\""]},{"number":721,"title":"Chapter 721: 721, Completely Convinced","paragraphs":["Zeng Jin sucked in a sharp breath when he heard that number.","What did she mean... fewer than three thousand people?","Before arriving at the Wanlong Society headquarters, he had been estimating in his head that the organization had at most a hundred or so men in black.","But now, just this night market street alone was densely packed with two to three thousand people sitting there.","That meant the tough guys he had seen before weren’t even a drop in the bucket?","At that moment, he really wanted to muster the courage to ask Liu Yutong one more question: “Are you raising all these people to take over the universe or what?”","It was too absurd!","So absurd that he had started to wonder if he had been living in a parallel universe for the past half of his life.","Liang Mengsong stared at the street, completely swallowed by a sea of black figures, and his expression shifted. From initial bewilderment, it slowly turned into confusion, and finally, with belated awareness, a sliver of fear surfaced.","He slowly turned his head to look at Zeng Jin, his eyes seemingly asking:","“President Zeng, what kind of place have you brought me to?”","“You’ve really screwed me over!”","Liu Yutong, as if she hadn’t noticed how terrified the two men were, wore a perfectly calm expression.","She had seen this kind of scene more than once; she was long used to it.","Then, she spoke to the crowd of men in black, her tone casual.","“Is everyone here?”","Just four simple words.","The next second—","Boom!!!","A thunderclap erupted from the ground!","The thousands of men in black, who had been sitting quietly a moment before, immediately snapped to their feet in unison.","In an instant, the light along the street seemed to be swallowed by that surging tide of black figures, and the pressure shot straight through the roof.","Zeng Jin was so startled his heart clenched painfully, and he almost went weak in the knees, nearly collapsing to the ground.","Then, all eyes from the black-clad men locked onto the slender figure standing at the head of the street—Liu Yutong.","In the next moment, a deafening roar swept through the entire street:","“Greetings, Miss!!!” X thousands of voices.","A thousand voices shouted as one, the sound waves rising straight into the clouds, as if they would tear the sky apart.","That overwhelming clamor violently shook the red lanterns hanging from the shop doors, and even the glass windows along the street vibrated, emitting a low humming sound.","Zeng Jin felt his eardrums ringing, his heart thumping wildly.","He had lived for half a lifetime, but this was the first time he truly understood what it meant to be crushed by sheer presence.","What it meant to speak one sentence and have a thousand respond!","Those so-called big shots, gang leaders, and godfathers from Taiwan Province—compared to this Miss Liu, they weren’t even fit to polish her shoes!","This was what a real boss looked like!","Liu Yutong gently raised one hand, her pale white fingers pressing downward slightly.","The next second!","Whoosh!","The thousands of men in black sat back down in perfect unison.","The whole street immediately returned to its previous silence.","Zeng Jin: “...”","Liang Mengsong: “...”","The two men were completely dumbfounded, their minds blank, as if all ability to think had been stripped away. They just stood there frozen, unable to snap out of it for a long time.","What kind of execution was this?","What kind of commanding presence was this?","One word, one gesture, and thousands moved like an extension of her own arms, stopping when she stopped and moving when she moved!","If Liu Yutong said she wanted to go fight the U.S. military right now, Zeng Jin would actually believe it.","This was just too incredible!","“Today, I’m inviting these two guests for a simple meal. Everyone, please don’t hold back; eat normally,” Liu Yutong’s voice rang out again.","“Understood, Miss!” X thousands of voices.","Then, the previously silent street gradually came alive, as if waking up.","The sounds of chopsticks and bowls clinking, bottles pouring drinks, shop owners serving food, all mixed with lively chatter and laughter slowly built up. The warmth of everyday life returned bit by bit, giving the street back its ‘vitality.’","By the time Liang Mengsong finally shook off his state of mental shutdown, he couldn’t help but ask Zeng Jin a soul-searching question.","“President Zeng... can we still... still leave here now?”","Zeng Jin: “...”","What do you think?","Liu Yutong seemed to have overheard Liang Mengsong’s words. She turned around, glanced at him, and smiled.","“Engineer Liang, you must be joking. You’re our honored guest at Wanlong Society, not some suspect. You’re free to come and go as you please. Why would you think you can’t leave?”","She paused, then added, “Of course, that’s only if you want to leave.”","Liang Mengsong: “...”","Zeng Jin: “...”","Somehow, that sounded even more ominous!","After taking a while to compose himself, Zeng Jin mustered the courage to ask again, “Miss Liu, are all the people from your company here?”","Liu Yutong didn’t want to scare him any further, so she answered casually, “Pretty much. It just so happened we were having a little gathering today, so we’re just having a simple bite here.”","A simple bite?","Zeng Jin nearly coughed up blood. Thousands of people, taking over an entire street, and she called that a simple bite?","In all his life, he had never heard a more ridiculously arrogant statement than this one!","But despite his inner grumbling, his mind was finally crystal clear—this young Miss Liu, in her twenties, was exactly the reason she could rule this city with an iron fist.","With power like this, in ancient times, she could have raised an army and led a rebellion.","Liang Mengsong also finally understood why Qiu Ciyun had insisted he come along to broaden his horizons. He had certainly seen it now.","The only thing was, he wanted someone to buy him a bottle of cardiac emergency pills!","That so-called company of Miss Liu’s was nothing like the legitimate enterprise he had imagined earlier.","It was clearly a hidden empire, wrapped in a legal shell, wielding terrifying power, crossing both the underworld and legitimate society, dominating everything with absolute control.","And the young girl in front of him, who didn’t look even twenty years old, was the—Empress of this empire!","“President Zeng, Engineer Liang, don’t just stand there. Let’s go sit down,” Liu Yutong said, and then led the way forward.","The two men dared not linger; they quickly followed, nervously making their way along behind her.","As they walked, every table they passed sent them a wave of invisible, focused attention.","It wasn’t a hostile glares. On the contrary, the men in black looked at Liu Yutong with something closer to reverence and fanaticism, as if she were their guiding deity.","But when they sized up Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong, their gazes turned appraising.","Zeng Jin felt as if he had been scanned head to toe by some kind of X-ray machine thousands of times, putting immense pressure on him.","Liu Yutong seemed to sense their discomfort and said over her shoulder without turning back,","“They’re all our own people, very friendly. Don’t worry about it, you two.”","Zeng Jin forced a dry laugh. “No worries, no worries.”","How could he not worry? The pressure was suffocating.","Finally, amidst a sensation of cold sweat running down their backs, they arrived at a pre-reserved round table in the middle of the street.","The positioning was subtle.","Neither too far up front nor too far back.","It sat right in the middle of that long black dragon—looking forward and backward, there was just an endless stretch of men in black as far as the eye could see.","The table had already been laid out with food. It wasn’t any lavish, high-class meal, but the kind of snacks you’d get from a night market.","Things like crawfish, barbecue, seafood, stir-fried noodles, beer, and soft drinks—all steaming hot, fragrant, and enough to make anyone start salivating.","Liu Yutong took the center seat and gestured for them to sit.","“President Zeng, Engineer Liang, make yourselves comfortable. No need to stand on ceremony.”","The two men finally sat down, though their movements carried an unmistakable sense of unease.","Then, the drinks arrived.","Zeng Jin, as if he had made some sort of decision, grabbed a freshly opened bottle of beer. Holding it with both hands, his demeanor utterly respectful, he gave Liu Yutong a deep bow.","“Chairman Liu, I, Zeng, admit defeat.”","“From this day forward, the Zeng family will follow wherever Chairman Liu leads. We’ll go through fire and water without a second thought! As for the talent at Taiji Electric, I’ll do everything in my power to recruit them for you. I won’t let you down!”","He was truly beaten, wholeheartedly and utterly convinced—the kind of submission where you’d prostrate yourself on the ground. After all, anyone who witnessed a spectacle on par with the world’s most formidable syndicate would feel the same way.","Liu Yutong raised the glass in front of her and clinked it against the bottle in his hand.","“Work with us at Wanlong Hui, and you won’t be treated poorly.”","“Thank you, Chairman Liu!”","After expressing his gratitude, Zeng Jin tipped his head back and downed the entire bottle of beer in one go."]},{"number":722,"title":"Chapter 722: 722, Born Leader","paragraphs":["Zeng Jin finished a bottle of beer, and once he made his stance clear, he visibly relaxed. After all, he had admitted he was willing to become a human trafficker—no wait, he meant her lackey—and with Liu Yutong’s personal guarantee, his initial fear naturally subsided.","As for Liang Gong, under Zhang Dalong’s enthusiastic hospitality, he had already drunk quite a bit with this younger brother, who was the closest to him in age at the gathering.","Sometimes, you have to admit that circumstances can truly change a person. Compared to his days before joining the Wanlong Society, Zhang Dalong had become noticeably more bold and generous.","If this were his past life, he would never have been this unrestrained or this capable of holding his liquor.","After a few rounds of drinks, Liang Mengsong finally started talking more.","“Chairman Liu.”","“Please go ahead, Liang Gong.”","“Why did you choose to go into the chip industry?”","“The chip industry requires massive investment, yields slow returns, has high technical barriers, and is dominated by international giants. Patent walls are insurmountable, and equipment is strangled by restrictions. The whole world knows chips are the future, but the only ones daring to invest heavily are either national teams or people who are crazy.”","Liang Mengsong put down his glass and looked seriously at Liu Yutong.","“You’re not a national team, and you don’t seem crazy either.”","He asked this question because it felt too contradictory. A person so involved in the underworld, with so many lucrative industries to choose from, had picked one of the hardest to crack. It was truly baffling.","Liu Yutong’s expression turned serious, and she asked him a question in return.","“Liang Gong, do you know how much Dragon Country spends on importing chips every year?”","Liang Mengsong paused, then nodded. “Over a hundred billion US dollars. That’s already surpassed oil, making it the largest import.”","Liu Yutong continued, “And do you know how much of that profit ends up in the hands of Dragon Country’s companies?”","Liang Mengsong fell silent. He knew the answer: a painful number—zero.","No, it wasn’t even zero; it was negative. Because the chips sold to you not only take your money but also use technical barriers, patent licensing, and supply chain control to firmly grip you by the throat, making you suffer with no way out.","Liu Yutong’s gaze shifted to the serpentine black river stretching in the distance.","“When I first started in the chip business, someone asked me the same question: why choose such a difficult path.”","“Some said, you’re just handing money to the US, buying equipment and patents, and when they impose an embargo, you’ll be finished.”","“Some said, a twenty-year-old girl like you could do anything else, why take on an industry that even the country spent tens of billions on and still failed at? It’s a waste of money.”","“And some said, chips are the crown jewel of industry. Even if you manage 90 nanometers, others are already working on 45 and 32 nanometers. You’ll never catch up—why bother?”","“I heard all of that early on, and plenty of it.”","Liang Mengsong listened quietly, waiting to hear how she would answer.","Liu Yutong suddenly gave a slight smile and finally spoke seven words.","“But I just wanted to try.”","When these words came out, Liang Mengsong felt a jolt in his heart, as if something had stirred him.","“Liang Gong, you spent many years at TSMC, didn’t you?”","“Back in the earliest days, what was TSMC’s scale? And what were Intel, Samsung, and Toshiba like?”","Liang Mengsong opened his mouth but didn’t answer. He knew it all, inside and out.","Twenty years ago, TSMC was just one obscure foundry among many, while Intel was an unshakable titan, lofty and looking down on everyone.","Yet twenty years later, Intel was still stuck in one place, while TSMC had risen to become the global king of wafer foundry.","“So, no one is born a king,” she said.","“They’re all chased down step by step, then trampled underfoot.”","In the middle of her speech, Liu Yutong had someone pour a beer, then raised her glass again and downed it in one gulp. With a sharp thud, she slammed the glass onto the table.","“So we can do it too!”","Liang Mengsong stared at her, silent for a long, long time.","So long that Zeng Jin thought he might never speak again.","Then, suddenly, he raised the glass in front of him, tilted his head back, and drained it dry.","When he set the glass down, his eyes were slightly red.","“Chairman Liu, I haven’t heard words like that in so many years.”","This time, he didn’t say he would stay, nor did he say he would leave.","But Zeng Jin knew—Liang Mengsong wasn’t going anywhere anymore.","Not because of the street teeming with those terrifying men in black.","But because of Liu Yutong’s words just now.","Zeng Jin looked at Liang Mengsong, then at Liu Yutong.","The night wind gently stirred the loose strands of hair by her ears, and the streetlamp cast faint shadows across her face, adding an air of mystery and depth.","She was just a twenty-year-old girl, yet at this moment, she gave off an intangible, indescribable... weightiness.","Zeng Jin suddenly understood something.","All his previous perceptions of Liu Yutong were built on the foundation that she was ruthless, cold-blooded, and cunning.","In America, she had crippled Rossi with a single kick.","In San Francisco, she had wiped out the Snakehead Gang overnight.","Here, she had her thousands of men in black.","He had thought that was the sum of Liu Yutong—a female overlord with limitless means.","But now, he realized he had missed one crucial thing.","Why did those men in black willingly follow her? Was it really just for money? Or because she was ruthless?","If it were only money and ruthlessness, you could at most raise a bunch of hired thugs, not so many loyal subordinates.","How do you measure loyalty? It’s simple—look in their eyes.","Those men in black had light in their eyes.","That same light, he had only ever seen in the eyes of the old-timers in the Taiwan underworld who lived by brotherhood.","That was true loyalty.","The kind of loyalty that made a man willing to take a blade for you.","But those old-timers had taken decades to forge that bond.","And Liu Yutong?","Twenty years old.","How did she earn it?","What did she have, to command such dedicated loyalty?","Now, he had his answer.","This woman was a born leader, and she carried that irresistible charm that made people willing to follow her and go through fire and water for her."]},{"number":723,"title":"Chapter 723: 723. Message (Thank you, Sōgetsu Kei, for the God Certification)","paragraphs":["Time passed little by little, and the streets grew livelier.","In the middle of everyone eating skewers, a person suddenly appeared at the street corner, walking straight toward Liu Yutong’s table.","It was a young woman, seemingly just over twenty years old. Her facial features bore a slight resemblance to Liu Yutong’s, but there was a touch more boldness in her brow.","But that wasn’t the main point.","The main point was that she was wearing a police uniform, and on her shoulder epaulette was clearly a rank insignia of one bar and three flowers.","First-class Superintendent!","Many people might have a vague idea of police rank levels, but they only needed to know this much:","Under normal circumstances, after graduating from the police academy, an officer first undergoes an internship, which usually lasts at least a year. After passing the internship evaluation, the first rank awarded is Third-class Superintendent. Based on the typical three-year promotion cycle, from the end of the internship to promotion to First-class Superintendent, it takes at least six years.","In other words, under normal and smooth conditions, a person would be around twenty-eight or twenty-nine years old before reaching this rank.","Yet this young woman, who looked as if she had just graduated, was already a First-class Superintendent.","The speed of her promotion was practically like riding a rocket!","“This Pearl City really is a land of outstanding talent. Not only is there Liu Yutong, but even a random police officer we see is so young and accomplished. Amazing!” Zeng Jin couldn’t help exclaiming.","However, what truly blew his mind was yet to come.","This policewoman walked boldly into the street.","Remember, this street was where thousands of men in black were having a feast!","And what’s more, those men in black didn’t show the slightest panic or hostility upon seeing her. Instead, they were very enthusiastic, greeting her one after another.","“Officer Gao!”","“Officer Gao is here!”","“Sister Min is here!”","“Make way for Sister Min!”","“Sister Min, want a drink?”","The men in black along the way all stood up and greeted her warmly, without any sign of wariness or deliberate distance because of her identity as a police officer.","The policewoman smiled back at them continuously, acting very familiar.","“Enjoy your meal and drinks!”","“I won’t have any alcohol—I still have official business with your young lady. You all eat and drink well.”","“Got it!”","The expressions on those men in black’s faces were genuinely happy.","It wasn’t fake!","It wasn’t just polite formality!","They were truly welcoming this police officer!","“They really don’t keep any distance!” Zeng Jin couldn’t help muttering under his breath.","Fortunately, he quickly recalled the group photos hanging on the walls of the Wanlong Association headquarters, and his mind immediately relaxed.","No problem, this is just their usual routine.","Gao Min quickly arrived at the main table.","Liu Yutong had already stood up, a smile appearing on her face: “Sis, why are you here?”","Sis?","Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong were stunned.","This policewoman was actually Liu Yutong’s older sister?","Wow, the young lady of the Wanlong Association really does have connections everywhere—she even managed to get her own sister arranged to work in the police department!","“I was just finishing up a shift, and I heard you were hosting a dinner here, so I came to grab a meal.” Gao Min said, looking toward Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong.","It was her first time meeting these two, so she was naturally a bit curious.","After all, anyone dining at the same table as her younger sister must have a notable background.","Liu Yutong introduced them: “This is Mr. Zeng Jin, President from Taiwan Province, and this is Mr. Liang Mengsong, a chip expert I’ve been eagerly waiting for.”","Gao Min nodded, extended her hand politely, and said, “Mr. Zeng, Mr. Liang, nice to meet you. I’m Gao Min.”","Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong shook hands with her courteously, quietly sizing her up.","No wonder she’s Chairman Liu’s older sister—with that background, she has a bright future ahead!","After Gao Min sat down, Liu Yutong asked the restaurant owner to bring some more barbecue.","Gao Min ate a few skewers to fill her stomach, then deliberately winked at her younger sister.","Liu Yutong caught on and turned to Zeng Jin and Liang Mengsong: “Mr. Zeng, Mr. Liang, please take your time eating. My sister and I need to discuss something.”","“Of course, of course, Chairman Liu, go ahead!”","“We’re fine here.”","Liu Yutong stood up and walked into the restaurant with Gao Min, finding a private booth to sit down.","Once the door was closed, Gao Min dropped her casual expression and became serious.","“Scarface sent a new piece of information.”","Scarface was the last boss of the Justice Alliance, though the organization was completely dissolved shortly after he took over.","After all, in Pearl City, the influential gang leaders had either died, ended up in prison, or gone on the run... In this environment, keeping the Justice Alliance wasn’t necessary, so it was disbanded.","After the dissolution, Scarface didn’t switch careers or leave Pearl City.","He didn’t have much ambition, or maybe he just liked the thug life. He gathered a few old brothers, opened a few bars and some poker rooms, and lived a low-key life, practically invisible.","Of course, even though he still hung around in that scene, he continued to act as an informant for Liu Yutong and Gao Min.","Because he often dealt with all sorts of people from the underworld, he was always well-informed.","Whenever someone wanted to stir up trouble, form gangs to establish a group, or open a gambling den... Scarface would always be the first to know.","Then, those people would mysteriously get noticed by either the Wanlong Society or the police station, only to be wiped out in one fell swoop.","Why was the public security in Pearl City so good?","Not because no one wanted to cause trouble, but because once anyone surfaced, they were crushed at the source.","\"One of Scarface’s underlings was drinking at a bar in the north of the city when he overheard some people talking. Those two were well-disguised, but you could hear a foreign accent in their speech. After getting drunk, they bragged to a bar hostess and let it slip that they were secretly asking around about Zhao Weixiang and also about you. Scarface’s guy heard it all by chance.","Unfortunately, he tried to tail them to find their hideout, but he lost them.\"","Liu Yutong finished listening to her sister’s words and nodded.","As expected.","Someone was asking about Zhao Weixiang and about her—what did that mean?","It meant that old dog Jiang Yuan still wasn’t giving up.","Earlier, she had spread the false news that Zhao Weixiang had been killed in a gang shootout to make Jiang Yuan lower his guard.","Now, it seemed Jiang Yuan wasn’t that easy to fool.","Or rather, he was too cautious.","So cautious that even after hearing about Zhao Weixiang’s death, he still sent people to Pearl City to scout things out.","He just underestimated Liu Yutong’s influence in Pearl City.","To put it bluntly, in Pearl City, no ripple could escape Liu Yutong’s notice—she had run it as tightly as an iron bucket.","Still, since Jiang Yuan only sent a few low-level lackeys to test the waters, they probably weren’t major players.","\"Sis, tell Scarface’s people to keep watching, but don’t alert them. If they come again, find a way to pinpoint their hideout and see if anyone’s meeting up with them.\"","\"Got it.\"","Gao Min nodded, then thought of something: \"Oh, there’s another piece of news.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"It came from Whitey.\"","Whitey was a code name—the same Hua Muying who had once been chased for several blocks by Liu Yutong’s people.","Later, he was sent to Hong Kong to gather intelligence.","That guy, true to his nature as a professional broker, thrived in Hong Kong like a fish in water.","Liu Yutong provided him with funds to operate there as an investor, and he had actually become quite successful, even making connections with big names in Hong Kong circles.","In his own words: \"Miss, I almost forgot I’m a spy!\"","\"What did he say?\" Liu Yutong asked.","Gao Min’s expression turned serious: \"He said Jiang Yuan probably won’t go to the capital for Old Lady Jiang’s birthday banquet.\"","Liu Yutong frowned slightly: \"Is the intel reliable?\"","Gao Min: \"He heard it from a Hong Kong businessman. That businessman has business dealings with Jiang Yuan, and during a dinner a few days ago, Jiang Yuan casually mentioned that the capital was too cold, saying he’s old and doesn’t want to bother with the trip, so he’d just send a representative to make an appearance.\"","Liu Yutong fell silent.","Jiang Yuan not going to the capital? That was a problem.","Her original plan was to find an opportunity at Old Lady Jiang’s birthday banquet to \"invite\" Jiang Yuan for a chat.","But now this old fox was backing off?","\"Could it be a smokescreen?\"","Gao Min nodded: \"That’s possible. Whitey also said Jiang Yuan is too cunning—nine out of ten things he says are false. Maybe he’s deliberately spreading word that he won’t go, but he actually will.\"","Liu Yutong thought for a moment.","That was a possibility.","For a sly old fox like Jiang Yuan to survive all these years and still thrive, if it weren’t for his past life’s funding of certain thugs exposing his identity, he might never have been caught.","Could it be that they really couldn’t grab him on the mainland this time?","But if they acted in Hong Kong, neither she nor her sister Gao Min would be satisfied. Hong Kong didn’t have the death penalty—wouldn’t it be too easy on that scumbag if he didn’t get what he deserved?","Just as Liu Yutong was pondering what to do next, a commotion suddenly erupted outside.","Soon,","the Blue Butterfly guarding the door came in to tell them the reason, her expression odd.","\"Boss, a guy being chased by a bunch of thugs has barged into our gathering spot.\"","Liu Yutong: \"???\"","Gao Min: \"???\"","Come on, was Pearl City’s public security really this bad now?","Someone dared to launch a chase during a gathering of thousands of Wanlong Society members? And actually chased them here?"]},{"number":724,"title":"Chapter 724: 724. Suffocating Sense of Oppression (Thanks to the Great God Certification from Yu Qingjue of Yien Hou Mansion)","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong and Gao Min exchanged a glance, both seeing a flicker of surprise in each other’s eyes.","Pearl City’s public security was arguably the safest in the entire country—especially on the turf controlled by the Ten Thousand Dragons Society. Open street chases were unheard of, and even scuffles among petty thugs were rare.","It wasn’t a question of courage; anyone bold enough to try would face only two outcomes: either get invited for tea by the police, or get taken away for “legal education” by the Ten Thousand Dragons brothers.","Let alone the fact that today, nearly three thousand core members of the Ten Thousand Dragons Society had gathered here.","So they really wanted to know who was foolish enough to barge in here.","“Come on, let’s go check it out.” Liu Yutong stood up.","“Alright!” Gao Min nodded, finding the whole thing absurd.","In all her years on duty, she had never encountered such a ridiculous scene—chasing someone down right under the noses of the Ten Thousand Dragons?","And on top of that, in front of thousands of people.","What was the difference between that and daring to make trouble on the doorstep of a god?","The noise of shouting and fighting grew closer.","“Stop right there! Don’t run!”","“Damn, he’s quick!”","“Grab him and kill him!”","“......”","Just as they stepped out of the private room, Liu Yutong and the others saw a young man sprinting desperately toward the street, running for his life.","That man was Lin Feng.","That night, he had been bored stiff alone in the hotel. Since he hadn’t had a chance to explore Pearl City properly over the past few days, he decided to sneak out to buy some local specialties to take back to the imperial capital—as a little hometown keepsake for Aunt Jiang.","He had shopped for about two hours and bought a lot of stuff.","Just as he was standing by the roadside, waiting for a taxi to return to the hotel, he happened to notice a few suspicious characters lurking in an alley behind him, muttering something he couldn’t make out.","He hadn’t thought much of it at first, but while waiting for the cab, he instinctively glanced in their direction.","That single glance changed everything.","Among those men, one wearing a duckbill cap happened to look up, locking eyes with Lin Feng.","Their gazes met.","Lin Feng froze for a second, muttering to himself that the guy must be crazy—why wear a hat so late at night?","Just as he turned to hail a cab, the man suddenly pointed a finger at him and barked, “What are you staring at?!”","Lin Feng hesitated, turning back with an innocent look. “I wasn’t staring at you guys.”","“Not staring? Then what were you looking at over here?”","“I was just taking a look.”","“Taking a look? You’re ‘just taking a look’ this late at night?”","Lin Feng was irritated by this unreasonable attitude. After all, he was the young master of the Lin family in the imperial capital. How could he swallow such an insult? Acting on impulse, he shot back, “Yeah, I was staring at you. So what?”","But the moment the words left his mouth, he regretted them.","Because those men all stood up at once, their faces fierce as they zeroed in on him, muttering things he couldn’t fully understand.","“Damn it, this kid is trouble!”","“He must have overheard what we were saying!”","“If that gets to Liu Yutong’s ears, we’re finished.”","“Grab him! Don’t let him get away!”","“Take him down!”","Seeing the danger, Lin Feng turned and bolted.","As he ran, he cursed himself: Lin Feng, you idiot! Are you brain dead? Picking a fight with a bunch of thugs this late at night?","Lin Feng sprinted for his life, thinking that after a bit of running, they’d give up. But when he glanced back, he realized he had seriously underestimated how vengeful these people were.","Not only did they refuse to give up the chase, they even called in reinforcements and armed themselves with machetes, looking determined to chop him into pieces.","Terrified, he even dumped the tens of thousands worth of local products he had just bought.","At the same time, he cursed inwardly: What the hell? Are people in Pearl City this petty? Is the local temperament this brutal?","All because of a glance? And they pull out machetes over it?","The chase dragged on for who knows how long. Lin Feng fled in panicked confusion, zigzagging like a headless fly, until—by some bizarre twist of fate—he ended up near the Ten Thousand Dragons Plaza.","By then, several cuts had opened up on his body, blood seeping out. He had clearly been injured during the escape.","But even after being wounded, he managed to break free again and run even faster.","Maybe it was the adrenaline pumping wildly in a life-or-death situation, temporarily numbing the pain and unleashing his survival instinct, that kept him going.","When Lin Feng spotted a brightly lit street up ahead, still bustling with the smell of barbecue and showing no signs of shutting down, he almost cried tears of joy.","Salvation was at hand!","As long as he reached that crowded area, those pursuers wouldn’t dare follow him. He could even get someone to call the police and an ambulance.","But just as he reached the street entrance and was about to scream “Help!” he froze like he had been struck by lightning.","He didn’t even feel the pain from his wounds anymore.","What... what was that?","That pitch-black mass—was that people?","He rubbed his eyes instinctively and looked again.","They were people!","All people!","One long street was packed with men in black suits, seated densely from end to end—a sea of them so vast he couldn’t even see the other side.","Lin Feng’s jaw dropped, his mind reeling.","His only thought was: Have I stumbled into a super gang’s gathering?","Or are they filming a sequel to Kung Fu Hustle and The Godfather right here?","The group chasing him had finally caught up to the street entrance.","Leading them was the man in the duckbill cap, panting heavily, still cursing, “Run! Run all you want! I’ll make you learn what—(⊙o⊙)!”","His words died halfway as he froze, his mouth still hanging open but no sound coming out.","The few accomplices behind him caught up one by one, equally stunned.","The once noisy street had fallen silent.","One after another, the men in black who had been eating skewers and drinking looked up, their gazes turning in unison toward them.","Several thousand pairs of eyes bore down on Lin Feng and the thugs holding their machetes.","And those thousands of eyes gradually shifted from their normal color to... green.","Like starving wolves spotting a fat sheep.","“Yesss! A chance for merit delivered to our doorstep!”","“I might actually get that commendation flag for bravery!”","“Let me have it—I’m newly promoted and haven’t gotten one yet.”","“It’s only six or seven of them, not enough to go around. What do we do?”","“Simple—whoever’s fastest gets it.”","“......”","Getting a commendation flag in Pearl City these days was getting tougher. Everyone knew why: the crime rate was too low, so there was no work to be done.","Now that a bunch of clueless criminals had practically walked into their laps, they were as excited as wolves spotting meat... their eyes glowing green.","At that moment,","Even though their target was right in front of them, the leader in the duckbill cap had no desire left to seize him—only an overwhelming, bone-deep fear.","I freaking tried to chase someone, and how did I end up in their gang’s hideout?","He stiffly turned his head to look at his accomplices.","His accomplices were also terrified, frantically signaling him with their eyes: Boss, run!","But no matter how hard they—or the ringleader in the baseball cap—tried, they realized their legs wouldn’t obey.","Just then, in the middle of the crowd, a man in black slowly stood up.","Then a second, a third, a fourth... countless men in black rose from their seats, their eyes fixed on them, the green glint in their gaze growing ever brighter.","The baseball cap and his thugs finally couldn’t bear the overwhelming pressure bearing down on them. They dropped to their knees in unison, their cleavers clattering to the ground.","“G-Gentlemen... w-we’re not here to cause trouble.”","“We’re just after that kid... he’s got a beef with us... we’re just chasing him... that’s really all it is!”","No one answered him.","Thousands of men in black simply cracked their knuckles and flashed “friendly” grins, ready to strike at any moment.","The sheer weight of their presence was suffocating.","Lin Feng felt the same way. His mind went blank, and his legs were shaking too.","Just as he was about to kneel down and beg for mercy—wait, no, plead that he was just an innocent bystander—a cool, clear voice rang out beside his ear.","“Lin Feng, are you so bored in the capital that you had to come to my turf and play a real-life game of escape?”"]},{"number":725,"title":"Chapter 725: 725、Too Scary (Thanks to the Vital and Vigorous Bith Star for the Great Healthcare)","paragraphs":["Hearing the sound, Lin Feng’s body jolted as he turned to look in the direction it came from.","The crowd parted on its own, clearing a path.","That path wasn’t wide—barely enough for two people to walk side by side—but it cut straight through the entire black-clad street, stretching from the far end all the way to where Lin Feng stood.","On both sides of the path, countless black-clad men stood packed together, the scene so oppressive it felt suffocating.","Then, Lin Feng saw her.","A slender yet imposing figure in black was walking slowly toward him along the path.","Black trousers, a black trench coat, a golden badge on her chest... His eyes traveled upward until he saw her face—a face so young it was almost unbelievable.","Her features were as delicate as if painted, her brow tinged with the cool aloofness of a young girl.","But it was precisely that youthful face that now sent Lin Feng’s heart pounding wildly.","Her presence was overwhelming.","Though she did nothing, she seemed to stand above ten thousand people, looking down from a great height at the ants beneath her feet.","Just as Lin Feng felt he might suffocate under that pressure, the girl stopped in front of him.","In that moment, Lin Feng finally saw her face clearly, as well as the badge pinned to her left breast.","A dark golden dragon, coiling and soaring, so vivid it seemed alive.","It was the emblem of the Dragon Union!","That name he had heard endlessly over the past few days.","About how fearsome the Dragon Union was, how they ruled with power reaching the heavens, how in Bright Pearl City the Dragon Union was the law... and so on.","It was terrifying, absolutely bone-chilling.","Lin Feng had dismissed it as exaggeration before, after all, he was the young master of the Lin family in the imperial capital—what grand spectacles hadn’t he seen?","But only now, witnessing this scene with his own eyes, did he truly understand that those rumors weren’t just understated—they were actually conservative.","The legendary self-made billionaire who ruled Bright Pearl City with an iron grip, the chairman of the Dragon Empire Group—Liu Yutong.","Also, his so-called foster sister.","She was a hundred times darker, ten thousand times more terrifying than he had imagined.","In all his life, he had never seen such a dark and frightening scene, never encountered so many underworld figures.","And yet, these men in black were all subordinates of his own “sister.”","It was utterly absurd.","Meanwhile, the thugs who had been kneeling on the ground finally snapped out of it, their hearts sinking like stones.","The... the Dragon Union?","Why had they come to Bright Pearl City?","To dig up information on Liu Yutong.","To probe the Dragon Union’s background.","They were here on a special mission.","And now?","They were chasing someone, and the chase had led them straight into Dragon Union territory.","Chasing and chasing, until they stood before countless Dragon Union men in black.","Chasing and chasing, until that legendary young lady of the Dragon Union, feared by countless on both sides of the law, appeared right before their eyes.","What insane luck was this?","Thinking of what was coming, the gangsters’ faces turned pale, one by one, and a few had already wet their pants.","“B-Boss... a-are we... stepping right into trouble?” one of them stammered.","The man in the cap swallowed hard, unable to speak.","Stepping into trouble?","They had just walked straight into an ammo depot!","Just then, the girl spoke.","“Who gave you the guts to make trouble in Bright Pearl City?”","The cap-wearing man opened his mouth to explain, but it felt like his throat was sealed. Not a word came out.","The girl didn’t seem impatient. She just watched them calmly.","But that gaze, fixed on him, felt like a mountain pressing down on him, making even breathing a struggle.","His mind was racing.","What now? What the hell do we do?","If he told the truth and gave up their employer, he’d be dead for sure—and it wouldn’t be a quick death.","But if he kept silent, would he even survive this moment?","Looking at the countless men around him, crushing them would be like squashing an ant.","Sweat streamed down the man’s forehead, soaking his collar. The back of his shirt was drenched through.","The girl seemed to lose patience when no one answered. She casually waved her hand.","“Take them away for a proper questioning. Follow the rules.”","“Yes, Miss Liu!”","No sooner had she spoken than a dozen men in black rushed forward, grabbing the cap-wearing man and his crew, dragging them off.","As they were hauled away, the gangsters finally broke down.","“Mercy! We didn’t do anything! We were just chasing that kid...”","“We were wrong! We swear we won’t do it again!”","“...”","Their pleas faded into the distance, swallowed by the night.","Lin Feng stood there blankly, his mind still foggy.","Those thugs who had been ready to tear him apart a moment ago were now being dragged off like chickens to slaughter.","And judging by the Dragon Union’s attitude, their fate would likely be worse than death.","Lin Feng swallowed hard. Just as he was about to say something to try and connect with his “sister,”","Liu Yutong spoke first.","“Lin Feng, you’ve been away from the imperial capital so long, and you came to my turf to play a real-life game of escape? Is that amusing?”","Her tone carried a hint of teasing, but to Lin Feng’s ears, it still sent a chill down his spine.","“Hiss—”","The sweat seeped into his fresh wounds, making him wince.","Liu Yutong glanced at the gashes still oozing blood on his back. She immediately ordered one of her men, “Take him to get that cleaned up. After that, send him away.”","One of the men in black gave a nod, motioning for Lin Feng to follow.","Lin Feng froze, then quickly waved his hands. “No, no! I’m fine, it’s just a few scrapes...”","Liu Yutong didn’t say a word. She just looked at him silently.","Just one look.","Lin Feng immediately changed his tune. “Alright, alright, I’ll get it cleaned up. I’ll go.”","As soon as the words left his mouth, he wanted to slap himself.","Lin Feng, you’re the young master of the Lin family in the imperial capital! How can you be such a coward in front of your “sister”?","But after another glance at the sea of black-clad figures, he quickly made peace with it.","She was the leader of the largest gang in Bright Pearl City, the Dragon Union. He wasn’t even in the same league. A little cowardice wasn’t so bad.","Lin Feng obediently followed the man in black toward a pharmacy that hadn’t yet closed for the night.","After a few steps, he couldn’t help glancing back again, his heart a mess of complex feelings.","This was the daughter Aunt Jiang had pined for all this time.","This was his sworn “sister.”","And she was...","Way too damn terrifying!",". . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ."]},{"number":726,"title":"Chapter 726: 727, Seeking a Chance (Thanks to Qianmo Liuhen for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["A dozen minutes later, Lin Feng walked out of the pharmacy after having his wounds treated.","The cuts weren't deep—just a few bloody gashes that needed disinfecting and bandaging.","He originally planned to make a quick escape.","After all, tonight’s experience had been way too intense. From being chased by thugs with knives to stumbling into the Wanlong Society gathering, his adrenaline still hadn’t calmed down. He urgently needed to get back to his hotel and digest everything.","But just as he was about to take a step, he saw a scene that would shock him for the rest of his life.","The usually lively street had somehow fallen silent.","The black-clad men who had been drinking and eating skewers were now all lined up neatly on both sides of the street, their eyes fixed on a simple makeshift stage in the center.","To call it a stage was generous—it was really just a few steps covered with a red carpet, looking a bit shabby. But that didn’t matter.","What mattered was the ceremony they were holding.","At that moment, Liu Yutong stood on the stage, followed by a squad of black-clad men holding clothes, red books, and badges.","Beside her, a fat man acting as the master of ceremonies called out names one by one, and each time, a young man stepped onto the stage and approached Liu Yutong.","Then they did something that sent chills down Lin Feng’s spine.","The young man, with a near-worshipful and excited expression, greeted her.","“Greetings, Miss!”","Liu Yutong smiled and nodded, then took the black suit and the book and handed them to him.","After he put on the suit jacket, she picked up a silver dragon badge and personally pinned it to the left chest of the young man.","The action was simple, yet it carried an indescribable solemnity.","The moment the dragon badge was fastened, the young man straightened up like a soldier receiving an inspection, clenched his right fist, and slammed it heavily against his left chest.","“I will follow Miss to the death!”","After shouting that, he turned and walked off the stage without hesitation.","Then came the third, fourth, fifth...","Each person who stepped onto the stage shouted a slogan that stirred the blood.","“Born a member of Wanlong, dead a spirit of Wanlong!”","“I dedicate my youth to build Wanlong’s glory!”","“Faith never fades, Wanlong endures forever!”","“Law as my sword, reason as my shield! Unity of knowledge and action!”","“Women are no less than men, Wanlong makes no distinction!”","“Girls of Wanlong can hold up half the sky!”","“Miss’s will is my direction!”","“...”","More than two hundred core members to be inducted stepped onto the stage one after another.","They punched their chests and made their vows before Liu Yutong.","Every vow was different.","Every vow came from the heart, filled with fervor.","Every vow was a pledge of total devotion to Miss, to the Wanlong Society.","When the last member’s induction was complete, Liu Yutong stepped forward. Her black trench coat fluttered in the wind.","She swept her gaze over the nearly three thousand black-clad men below, as well as those newly badged core members still brimming with excitement.","Then she spoke slowly.","“The Wanlong Society will never betray anyone loyal to it.”","“I, Liu Yutong, will never betray anyone who follows me!”","The crowd fell silent for two seconds.","Then...","“Long live Miss!” someone shouted first.","Instantly, the entire street erupted.","“Long live Miss!”","“Long live the Wanlong Society!”","“Long live Miss!”","“I would die for Miss!”","“...”","The waves of cheers grew louder and louder, making the glass on nearby storefronts buzz and rattle.","Lin Feng stood by the side of the street, watching it all unfold, completely frozen.","He finally understood one thing:","—The authorities really should crack down on this.","Just as Lin Feng was still reeling from the shock, a hand landed on his shoulder.","“Come on, Miss ordered us to escort you away.”","Lin Feng was about to say “wait a minute,” but when he saw the look in the black-clad man’s eyes, he wisely shut his mouth and followed them toward the road.","By the roadside, the black-clad man stopped.","“Alright, you’re safe now. Call yourself a cab and get out of here.”","Lin Feng nodded, thanked him, and raised his hand to hail a taxi.","But just as his hand went up, Aunt Jiang’s haggard face suddenly flashed through his mind.","For so many days, rain or shine, Aunt Jiang had been waiting outside the Wanlong Society building every day, just to see Liu Yutong once.","But they couldn’t even get through the front door.","Tomorrow, they were heading back to the capital.","If he missed this chance, he had no idea when—if ever—she’d get to meet her again. Maybe never in this lifetime.","Thinking of this, Lin Feng’s fists slowly tightened.","He knew he had no right.","He knew he was just an outsider.","But dammit... Screw it!","Lin Feng spun around and sprinted back toward the black-clad street!","“Hey!”","The black-clad man, who was about to turn back, froze, then his face changed drastically as he chased after him: “What are you doing? Stop!”","Lin Feng had already charged into the crowd’s outer edge.","The black-clad men on both sides stopped their cheering, turned their heads, and fixed their stares on this clueless idiot daring to barge in.","Lin Feng ran desperately, weaving past tables and black-clad men.","But he didn’t get far. Once the others snapped out of it, someone blocked his way.","“Stop right there!”","“Take one more step and see what happens!”","A group of men grabbed him immediately and pinned him down.","Cornered and frantic, Lin Feng jumped in desperation, fear forgotten. He screamed at the top of his lungs toward the center of the crowd, toward the woman surrounded by her followers.","“Liu Yutong! Liu Yutong! I need to talk to you!”","No one paid him any attention.","A few black-clad men stepped forward, grabbed his arms, and started dragging him away.","Lin Feng struggled wildly, his feet kicking at the ground, but his strength was nothing compared to these men. He could only watch helplessly as he was pulled farther and farther from her.","He panicked. He threw all caution to the wind and roared again.","“Aunt Jiang really misses you!”","The shout made the men dragging him pause.","“She dreams of you every night! She wants to find you, but she can never reach you!”","“She cries every time she wakes up, sometimes for half the night!”","“She hasn’t had a good life all these years! She regrets it every single day, regrets that she didn’t take you with her back then!”","“She didn’t abandon you on purpose! She was just too broken! She was sold to the countryside, and after she gave birth to you, her mind went. Sometimes she couldn’t even remember who she was!”","“She wanted to go back for you so many times, but she was scared... scared that gambler would catch her again!”","“She never stopped wanting to find you! She really had no choice!”","Lin Feng’s voice echoed through the street, growing louder and hoarser with each word.","The black-clad men holding him hesitated, unsure whether to keep dragging him or let go.","Seizing their moment of distraction, Lin Feng wrenched himself free with a sudden burst of energy, then dropped to his knees with a heavy thud.","He raised his head, gazing at the aloof girl in black standing high above in the distance, and continued shouting loudly.","“I know I have no right to speak for Aunt Jiang!”","“I know you’re strong, and I know you don’t need anyone! You’re the heiress of the Wanlong Society!”","“But could you... could you possibly give her a chance?”","“Just one chance!”","“Let her see you, let her apologize to you in person! Is that too much to ask?!”","After shouting this, Lin Feng was completely drained, gasping heavily for air.","He had done everything he could. If she still refused to see Aunt Jiang, then he would have to go back and persuade Aunt Jiang to give up hope.","The entire street fell silent.","Thousands of black-clad figures stood in unison, staring at this young man kneeling on the ground, their gazes complex.","Some were surprised, some admired him, others were puzzled, but most looked at him as if he were already dead.","This kid had some nerve, daring to speak to the young mistress like that, at a time like this, in such a manner.","Liu Yutong stood on the high platform, separated by a sea of people, her eyes fixed on the kneeling figure, a hint of amusement in her gaze.","She hadn’t expected Jiang Lu to have such charisma—this reckless stepson of hers actually dared to risk his life to speak for her.","Just then, footsteps suddenly echoed from the direction of the street entrance.","“Move aside, move aside! Police!”","“Over here! Hurry up!”","“Nobody move! Hands on your heads, get down...”","A few figures in police uniforms rushed in impatiently, but when they saw the scene before them, they froze in shock."]},{"number":727,"title":"Chapter 727: 728, A Belated Apology (Thanks to Kite for the Big Health Gift)","paragraphs":["“Nobody move!”","A sharp shout suddenly rang out at the entrance of the street.","Immediately after, several figures in police uniforms rushed in urgently. Behind them followed a man and a woman—exactly Lin Dong and Jiang Lu.","The couple had been terrified after receiving Lin Feng’s distress call, so they panicked, called the police, and followed the police car all the way here.","But when they reached the street corner and took in the scene before them, they froze.","What was that?","That vast, pitch-black mass—were those people?","All people!","The entire long street was packed densely with men in black.","Stretching as far as the eye could see, there was no end in sight.","Before Lin Dong and the others could even snap out of the suffocating pressure of that exaggerated sight, an even more surreal scene unfolded.","After the leading officer clearly recognized the dragon-shaped badges on the chests of those men in black, he let out a long sigh of relief and casually holstered his gun.","“Oh, it’s the Wanlong Association having a gathering. That’s fine, no problem.”","The several police officers behind him also nodded one after another, their expressions instantly relaxing.","“If it’s Wanlong Association’s turf? Then there’s definitely no issue.”","“With them around, criminals can’t get away.”","“Come on, come on, let’s head back.”","“Pack it up, pack it up.”","With that, the few of them turned around and were about to leave.","Lin Dong: “???”","He grabbed one of the police officers. “Comrade... comrade, aren’t you going in to take a look? My son might be inside! He’s being chased by someone trying to kill him!”","The officer turned back, patted Lin Dong on the shoulder, and comforted him.","“Mr. Lin, don’t worry. In Bright Pearl City, as long as you’re on Wanlong Association turf, no one can harm your son. If any reckless criminal really did crash in there, they’ve probably already been ‘cleaned up’ and sent to the station by now.”","“Here’s the plan: we’ll head back first. If you still haven’t found your son, give us a call, alright?”","Having said that, the officers really did just swagger off like that.","They left.","Just like that...","Lin Dong stood there dumbfounded, watching those officers get into their car and drive away, completely lost.","What the hell was going on?","Police see a mob of black-clad gangsters, and instead of arresting them, they leave at ease?","And they even say, “With them around, criminals can’t get away”?","Wasn’t this way too surreal?","If cops in the capital saw thousands of men in black gathered together, they’d probably call in the anti-terrorism unit.","But here? They just casually packed up and left?","Jiang Lu had sharp eyes. The first thing she spotted was Lin Feng kneeling among the crowd, and she immediately rushed toward him.","“Xiaofeng...”","The men in black on both sides glanced at her but didn’t stop her.","Lin Dong quickly followed.","The couple passed through the crowd, step by step, making their way deeper into the street.","The further they went, the stronger the invisible pressure became. It felt like walking into a massive black hole, surrounded by terror—incredibly frightening!","Finally, they reached the spot where Lin Feng was kneeling.","Lin Feng’s knees were probably numb by now, but he still kept his back straight, staring intently ahead.","About a dozen meters in front of him, the girl in black stood silently, her cold, stunning face expressionless.","When Jiang Lu followed Lin Feng’s gaze and saw her, it was as if she’d been struck by lightning. She instantly froze in place.","That was the daughter she had thought of day and night for nearly twenty years.","Lin Dong helped his kneeling son to his feet and stood beside his wife.","After helping his son up, Lin Dong stood next to his wife, his eyes darting between Liu Yutong and the dense crowd of men in black behind her, unable to stop himself from muttering.","“Hey... Lulu, is it too late to say I don’t want to claim the family ties now?”","Jiang Lu: “...”","Lin Feng: “...”","Lin Dong quickly waved his hands. “Kidding! Just kidding! Don’t take it seriously!”","Then he wiped the non-existent cold sweat from his forehead, silently screaming inside.","What kind of nightmare scene was this?","The biggest spectacle he’d ever seen in his life was a company annual meeting with a few hundred people—he’d never witnessed anything like this ‘gangster pilgrimage’ of thousands!","It seemed he had seriously underestimated just how “dark” this “daughter” of theirs was.","He was genuinely afraid that after reclaiming this daughter, one day the authorities would launch a crackdown on organized crime and sweep the entire Lin family clean.","Just as Lin Dong’s thoughts were spiraling, Liu Yutong moved. She walked toward them, all the way up to Lin Feng, and looked at this young man who had shown some backbone.","“I heard everything you said.”","Though Lin Feng was scared to death inside, seeing Jiang Lu still crying, he gritted his teeth and spoke again. “Please give Aunt Jiang a chance!”","Liu Yutong was silent for a few seconds.","Then she turned her head and looked at Jiang Lu.","Mother and daughter’s eyes met in the air.","Jiang Lu’s tears flowed even harder. Her lips trembled, and she wanted to say something but couldn’t get the words out.","After looking at her for a few seconds, Liu Yutong turned back to Lin Feng.","“Too bad you seem to have gotten one thing wrong.”","Lin Feng was startled. “What?”","Liu Yutong: “Your Aunt Jiang’s hardships are her business. How I’ve lived all these years is my business. There’s no direct cause and effect between the two.”","“Just because she suffered doesn’t mean I have to forgive her. Just because she regrets doesn’t mean I have to accept her. In this world, not every ‘I’m sorry’ is met with an ‘it’s okay.’”","Lin Feng grew anxious. “But... she’s your mother! She really didn’t mean it!”","“Xiaofeng, stop it.”","Jiang Lu suddenly spoke up, cutting Lin Feng off, shaking her head at him.","“Tongtong is right.”","Lin Feng was frantic. “Aunt Jiang...”","Jiang Lu took the initiative to step forward, standing face to face with Liu Yutong.","The two stood there, mother and daughter, one drenched in tears, the other cold as frost.","After a moment, Jiang Lu spoke first.","“Tongtong, I’m not asking for your forgiveness.”","“I truly don’t expect it.”","“I’m standing here today because I wanted to say this to you in person—I’m sorry!”","“Not so you’ll forgive me, but because I owe you this.”","“For nearly twenty years now, every single night, I’ve dreamed of you. I dream of you as a little girl. I dream of you being bullied. I dream of you wanting your mom and no one being there for you. Every time I wake up, I want to slap myself over and over.”","“I know, saying all this might make you think I’m playing the victim, trying to win sympathy, but I’m really not... I just... I just wanted you to know that all these years, I’ve never once let you go in my heart.”","“When you were doing well, I was happy for you. When you were hurting, it hurt me more than anyone.”","“But I know—I don’t have the right to feel hurt for you. Because the suffering you went through wasn’t supposed to be yours to bear alone.”","“I’m the one who couldn’t carry it. I’m the one who ran away first.”","By this point, Jiang Lu was sobbing uncontrollably.","She raised her hand, clumsily wiped her tears, and struggled to calm herself down.","“I didn’t come today to claim our family bond, or to disrupt the life you have now.”","“I just wanted you to know that Mom... no... I... I have never forgotten you.”","“Even if you never recognize me for the rest of your life, even if you have your people throw me out right now—I’ll accept it.”","\"As long as you're okay, that's enough... truly enough.\"","After saying these words, she turned around, ready to leave.","Being able to say these things to her daughter had already filled her heart with satisfaction.","Just as Jiang Lu turned, Liu Yutong felt someone gently tug at her from behind.","It was her sister, Gao Min.","Liu Yutong didn't look back, but she already understood Gao Min's meaning.","After two seconds of silence,","she spoke.","\"Wait!\"","Jiang Lu's footsteps suddenly halted. Trembling, she turned around, a glimmer of hope in her eyes as she looked at Liu Yutong.","Could it be that her daughter had forgiven her?","But Liu Yutong’s next words dashed her hopes again.","\"Tomorrow at nine in the morning, Shunchang Tower, my office.\"","\"And don’t misunderstand.\"","\"I just want to have a word with the head of the Lin family standing beside you.\""]},{"number":728,"title":"Chapter 728: 729, A Tough Nut to Crack (Thanks to Yi Meng «Shang Shang Qian» for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Although Jiang Lu felt a little disappointed, she still nodded vigorously: “Okay... okay! We’ll be there tomorrow, for sure! For sure!”","She didn’t dare to ask for too much. She truly didn’t.","As long as she could see her daughter again, even if it was just to sit quietly by her side for a while and steal another glance at her, that would be more than enough.","As for Liu Yutong saying she wanted to talk alone with her husband Lin Dong, she didn’t care at all. It didn’t even cross her mind.","At that moment, only one thought kept repeating in her head: she’d see Tongtong again tomorrow. She’d see her tomorrow.","Lin Dong nodded as well. “Tomorrow at nine in the morning—we’ll be there on time!”","Though he said it, his heart was pounding.","What the hell did this little girl suddenly want to talk to him about? Was she planning to take over or even swallow up the Lin family?","After all, the Lin family was a shadow of its former glory—down and out now.","On the other hand, Liu Yutong held such a terrifyingly massive force in her hands.","If she wanted to break out of Bright Pearl City and expand elsewhere, their family—though declining but still with some foundation—would indeed be her best option.","But he didn’t dare to refuse. Never mind speaking up to reject her—he didn’t even have the guts to ask what they’d be talking about.","Given tonight’s spectacle, even if his biological father showed up, he’d probably be kneeling and listening, let alone a stepfather like him with no real standing.","Lin Dong by now had completely forgotten his earlier vows at the Lin family estate about inducting this “stepdaughter” into the family registry.","In the face of absolute power, a person’s memory always seems to conveniently fade away.","The black-clad men nearby had also gradually loosened up, glancing at Lin Feng and his family with less hostility and more curiosity.","They could tell that Mr. Lin, Ms. Jiang, and that young guy who’d been chased through the streets had some kind of connection with the young lady.","But nobody dared to pry. The young lady’s personal affairs were never theirs to discuss. All they had to do was mind their own duties and keep her safe.","–––––","Lin Dong and his family didn’t head back to the hotel. They went straight to the hospital.","Even though Lin Feng kept insisting he was fine and only had minor scratches, Jiang Lu and Lin Dong refused to let it go. They wouldn’t be able to sleep without getting him checked out.","Only after the doctor confirmed with the X-rays that Lin Feng really wasn’t hurt badly did they finally breathe easy.","After all that running around until the dead of night, they were finally ready to head back and rest.","In the car.","Lin Dong couldn’t help but say to his wife, “Lu, do you know what I was thinking earlier?”","“I was thinking, if this were ancient times, with Tongtong’s abilities, she’d probably be at least a regional warlord.”","Jiang Lu blinked, surprised by where her husband’s mind had wandered.","Lin Feng also turned around, curious about what his father would say next.","“Look at tonight’s show—thousands of black-clad men filling an entire street. The cops showed up, took one look, and left without a word. What kind of power is that? That’s true control, ruling with an iron fist.”","“I’ve spent decades in the capital, always thought I’d seen it all, been through every big scene. But tonight? I’ve never seen anything like it.”","Lin Feng cut in, “Dad, you’re right. You should have seen it when I was being chased down that street. Those thousands of guys stood up in unison—I almost had a heart attack. Even now, I can’t believe they’re all her men. It was like a damn movie.”","Lin Dong nodded in agreement. “That’s authority. Tongtong is truly something special.”","Lin Feng asked, “Dad, Auntie Jiang, how do you think she did it?”","“How does a twenty-year-old girl get so many people to follow her and risk their lives for her?”","“Those thousands of black-clad men—the way they looked at her wasn’t fake. It was fervor, like believers looking at a shrine.”","Lin Dong fell silent.","He couldn’t figure it out either.","How did she do it?","After a long pause, he came up with a half-decent explanation.","“There are always people in this world who are natural-born leaders. They have an indescribable charisma that makes others willingly submit. Tongtong is probably one of those people.”","Lin Feng nodded thoughtfully.","This trip to Bright Pearl City had been worth it.","At the very least, it had opened their eyes.","For folks from the capital to see something like that was just... damn thrilling. Almost surreal.","–––––","On the other side.","Yun Cheng and Chu Yang, along with a few black-clad men, were surrounding the group of thugs.","They’d already gotten one key piece of intel: these thugs were the same bunch that Scarface had reported earlier—possible forerunners sent by Jiang Yuan to scout for info.","Of course, thugs at the bottom rungs of the underworld had no idea that their real boss was someone as big as Jiang Yuan. There had to be a middleman in between.","But no matter how much the Wanlong Society men used their infamous “special methods” that made people’s blood run cold, the leader in the cap never spilled who his contact was.","The Wanlong Society thugs carrying out the interrogation were genuinely surprised.","“Whoa, Yun, this guy’s tough—real stubborn.”","“First time any of our methods haven’t worked after almost an hour.”","“Gotta admit, he’s not wasted his time on the streets. Loyal as hell.”","“What do we do? If we can’t break him, we can’t report back to the young lady.”","“Maybe we call Brother Ji?”","“Good idea. Where is he?”","“I think he’s asleep...”","“...”","Yun Cheng was getting impatient. If the young lady hadn’t ordered them to stay within the law, he’d have already broken some bones.","He grabbed the cap leader by the collar and yanked his head up.","“Talk. Who sent you? Last chance!”","The man in the cap just shook his head. “We... we really just didn’t like that guy and decided to teach him a lesson. Everything I’ve said is true... Please, stop pushing me.”","In his heart, he knew that if he gave up his boss, he’d die an even worse death.","His boss was ruthless and would stop at nothing.","These Wanlong Society people looked even scarier, but either way, he was doomed. Holding out might be his only hope of a way out.","Just as Yun Cheng was about to put them back in their special vests, Yu Xin walked over.","She was wearing a black business suit, her hair loose over her shoulders. Her cheeks were slightly flushed from the wine she’d had, giving her a subtly alluring look. She was holding a bottle of red wine.","“Yun, hit a wall with a tough one?”","\"Yu Xin, why don't you give it a try? This guy's got a hard mouth. We've been grilling him for an hour and haven't gotten a thing out of him.\"","Yu Xin nodded, walked over to the man in the cap, and looked him up and down from above.","The man in the cap felt a chill under her gaze but still gritted his teeth, putting on a defiant \"I'd rather die than surrender\" attitude.","Yu Xin didn't rush to speak. Instead, she pulled over a stool and sat down across from him.","\"Big brother, what's your surname?\"","The man in the cap was taken aback. He hadn't expected her first question to be that, and he answered instinctively, \"Liu.\"","\"Brother Liu, your accent sounds like you're from the south, right?\" Yu Xin asked.","The man in the cap hesitated for a moment, then nodded.","Yu Xin smiled. Her smile, set against her slightly flushed face, seemed especially genuine. \"Brother Liu, I can tell you're a smart man. Let's put our cards on the table. Did you really chase after that kid tonight just because you didn't like the look of him?\"","The man in the cap stuck to his story. \"Yes!\"","Yu Xin nodded, then unhurriedly twisted open the stopper of the red wine bottle. She poured herself a glass, swirled it gently, and took a sip.","\"Brother Liu, that watch you're wearing is nice.\"","The man in the cap instinctively pulled his hand back, but the guy in black beside him held it down.","Yu Xin looked at him with a half-smile. \"A Rolex—market price must be over a hundred thousand, right? Your boss sure is generous to you, isn't he?\""]},{"number":729,"title":"Chapter 729: 730, The Most Likely CEO Candidate (Thanks to the Old Tree at the Alley for the Grandmaster Certification)","paragraphs":["The guy in the cap was completely baffled by what this seemingly alluring girl was up to.","Weren't they supposed to be interrogating him?","Why had she suddenly started talking about his watch?","And what did how generous his boss was have to do with her anyway?","But he had already made up his mind. No matter what sweet-talk or seduction tactics she used—even if it was a honey trap—he would never, ever rat out his boss.","He still had some professional integrity.","Yu Xin, however, couldn't care less about what he thought and kept sizing up his outfit with obvious interest.","And sure enough, the guy might look unremarkable, but everything he wore was top-tier designer stuff.","His sneakers were a limited-edition pair, and the watch on his wrist was worth a small fortune. That told her he wasn't just some reckless thug—he was also a flashy, money-hungry type.","Well, who didn't love money, though?","Once she'd sized him up, she spoke in a serious, measured tone.","\"Brother Liu, the way I see it, people like you are out here for two reasons only: loyalty or money. But have you ever thought about this—when you screwed up tonight, do you really think your big-shot boss, no matter how generous, would let you off easy?\"","The guy in the cap shifted his eyes but said nothing.","\"You know exactly who you pissed off tonight. In all of Bright Pearl City, crossing our Dragon’s Legion—you really think your skulking boss can protect you?\"","\"You don't seriously underestimate what Dragon’s Legion can do, do you?\"","Yu Xin leaned in closer as she said that, her delicate face less than ten centimeters from his.","Then, in a secretive whisper, she told him a story.","\"Let me tell you something, just between us. This morning, the Bright Pearl City police pulled a body out of the river. I heard the fish had eaten half its face... absolutely brutal.","Brother Liu, why do people have to go and commit suicide these days? There's still so much beauty in the world—why go down that road?\"","What Yu Xin was saying was actually true. Last night, someone couldn't handle it anymore and jumped into the river. They got pulled out this morning. One of the Dragon’s Legion members saw it as they passed the bridge on their way to work. She was just repeating what she'd heard.","But to the guy in the cap and his henchmen, that story sounded completely different.","Especially the man in the cap—his face went white, and even his lips started trembling.","He had, in fact, heard the same rumor: someone was dragged out of the river. Could it be that Dragon’s Legion was behind that?","It had to be!","Dragon’s Legion was so powerful in Bright Pearl City; they wouldn't think twice about dumping a person in the river for the fish to eat and then making it look like suicide.","Was she giving him an ultimatum by bringing this up?","The thought made him shudder.","Yu Xin: \"Brother Liu, I'm not trying to scare you. And Dragon’s Legion is a legitimate company. We don’t engage in anything illegal, and we definitely don’t go around killing people. Don't overthink it, okay?\"","The more she denied it, the more suspicious he became. He muttered inwardly, \"Like I'd believe that!\"","Still, what could he do? Could he really sell out his boss?","Wouldn't that be a death sentence anyway?","Yu Xin pressed on. \"I’m just being straight with you. Right now, you’re holding out and playing the loyal soldier. But do you think your boss will actually appreciate that?\"","\"He hasn’t even shown his face. He sent you and your little crew ahead like cannon fodder. Do you honestly think he cares whether you live or die?\"","The man's expression twisted. His eyes showed clear signs of doubt.","Yu Xin then poured herself another glass of wine and slid the bottle toward him.","\"Take a drink to calm your nerves.\"","He froze for a moment, staring at the red wine bottle as his throat bobbed.","Yu Xin smiled. \"Relax, it's not poisoned. Drink this, and we're friends.\"","He hesitated, then took the bottle and chugged a good part of it.","Seeing that the moment was right, Yu Xin had someone bring in a stack of cash and slammed it onto the table.","\"We've talked enough. Right now, just tell me who sent you, and this ten grand is yours.\"","The guy's eyes gleamed with greed at the sight of the money.","He had borrowed a ton from loan sharks just to buy his expensive watch and show off. His plan was to pay off that debt with the final payment from this job—only he'd fallen right into Dragon’s Legion’s hands. And weirdly, they were offering him money, too. But this wasn't enough. If only he could squeeze more...","\"Save your breath. I don't need money,\" he said.","Yu Xin raised an eyebrow and threw another stack onto the table.","\"Twenty thousand!\"","\"I live on loyalty! Think twenty grand is gonna turn me into a rat? No chance!\"","\"Fifty thousand!\"","\"Forget it! Would you sell out your own boss?\"","\"A hundred thousand!\"","\"And to make it clear, just give me the truth. I, Yu Xin, will keep you safe and get you to a secure place. Deal?\"","\"A hundred grand? Hah! Stop dreaming! I’m Liu San. I stand tall with my head high. Don't insult me with your money!\"","The surrounding men in black were stunned. Was this guy crazy or just stupid?","\"Miss Xin went as high as a hundred grand plus protection, and he’s still not talking. Is he really not afraid of dying?\"","Yun Cheng, however, shook his head, signaling them to wait. He knew Yu Xin well enough—she was a master of psychological warfare. This was probably just the opening act.","And just as he'd guessed.","Yu Xin's smile faded. She reached over and grabbed a stack of cash, weighing it in her hand, then tossed it into the hands of one of her men.","\"Ninety thousand.\"","Liu San blinked, not quite processing, but still stubborn. \"I'm not that kind of guy—\"","Yu Xin grabbed another stack and tossed it away too.","\"Eighty thousand.\"","\"You think you can scare me? I don't care!\"","\"Seventy thousand.\"","\"I-I'm a loyal kind of guy...\"","She kept going, throwing each bundle away without a hint of mercy.","\"Sixty thousand.\"","\"W-well, truth be told...\"","\"Fifty thousand. Say any more and you'll get nothing.\"","Liu San couldn't take it anymore. That mental torture of watching the amount plummet from a hundred grand to just fifty broke him completely. He lunged up from his chair and shouted, \"Stop! Stop cutting my money!\"","Yu Xin smirked. \"So now you admit it’s your money?\"","His face red. \"Will that hundred grand you mentioned still count?\"","Yu Xin looked at him sarcastically. \"What, you don't care about loyalty now?\"","Liu San stammered, \"Loyalty won’t feed me! And you’d better guarantee my safety!\"","Yu Xin shot a triumphant glance at Yun Cheng and then rose from her seat.","\"You’ve got my word. A hundred grand, not a penny less. Finish the rest of the wine at your leisure, because you’re going to be off the bottle for a while.\"","With that, she clicked her heels and strode out without looking back. The rest—verifying the info he’d spill—could be left to Brother Yun and his crew.","The Dragon’s Legion men all stared at the back of Yu Xin as she left, their faces filled with newfound awe and caution.","I never imagined the young lady’s high school classmate would have grown to such a level!","No wonder there’s talk that she’s the top candidate to become the CEO of the Wanlong Group.","Truly incredible!","..................","As the night deepened, the long street’s banquet was also winding down.","The throng of black-clad men began to disperse one after another, until that suffocating pressure finally lifted. Only then did the restaurant owners along the street dare to smile, cheerfully starting to clear away the tables and chairs.","They had made a killing today.","Though the Wanlong Group was intimidating, they were remarkably generous. Not only had they paid extra for the venue booking, but they had also handed out generous red envelopes to the street’s sanitation workers separately.","“Let’s go. Time to head back,” Liu Yutong said, walking toward the black Maybach parked by the roadside.","Gao Min silently followed.","After getting into the car, neither of them spoke.","They remained silent throughout the entire drive.","Back at the residence, Liu Yutong changed her shoes and made her way to the living room sofa, sinking into the soft leather.","Gao Min followed and sat down across from her.","They sat in silence for another moment before Liu Yutong finally spoke.","“Sis.”","Gao Min looked up and gazed at her steadily.","Liu Yutong opened her eyes, staring at the ornate crystal chandelier on the ceiling, and asked,","“You still really want to acknowledge her, don’t you?”"]},{"number":730,"title":"Chapter 730: 731, Heart-to-Heart Between Sisters. (Thanks to Mr. Jinpeng for the God-tier Certification)","paragraphs":["Gao Min didn’t know how to answer that question for a moment.","Did she want to acknowledge her? Yes.","From the moment she learned that woman was their birth mother, a vague, indescribable feeling had risen in her heart.","It was a complex emotion—curiosity, longing, and... anticipation.","She had grown up beside her adoptive father, Gao Shubai, who treated her like his own daughter, giving her his complete love and even remaining unmarried for her sake. Yet, there had always been a void in her heart—the void left by the absence of a mother.","As a child, she had asked him countless times: “Dad, where’s my mom? All the other kids have one.”","Gao Shubai would fall silent for a long time before patting her head and saying vaguely, “Mom went somewhere far away. Maybe when you’re older, you’ll get to see her.”","As she grew older, she stopped asking.","Because she had learned to be sensible.","But deep down, she had always held an image of her mother—was she gentle or strict?","She wondered if her life would have been different if her mother had been there. Would she no longer have to envy other children?","Now that she knew the truth about her origins and had even seen her mother with her own eyes, that longing had taken root like a seed buried in her heart, quietly sprouting.","But she also knew her sister was different from her.","Liu Yutong had grown up in the home of that gambling addict, enduring scolding, beatings, and domestic violence.","She dared not imagine, nor could she bear to think about, the suffering her younger sister had endured over those years.","Her sister had every right to hate, every right to refuse forgiveness, every right to shut that woman out.","But she herself... did not.","Gao Min took a deep breath and looked seriously at Liu Yutong. “Little sister, I told you—your decision is my decision. I’ll stand by you, always. If you don’t want to acknowledge her, I’ll treat her like a stranger. Only if you want to, then I will too.”","Liu Yutong turned her head and looked at her sister.","Gao Min’s eyes were resolute, as if she had made up her mind completely.","Liu Yutong sat up and said, with a hint of resignation, “You don’t have to say that. You’re my sister; of course I know what you’re thinking.”","“Little sister—”","“Alright, alright. We’re close, you and me. You really don’t have to worry so much about my feelings, because you and I are different.”","Liu Yutong leaned back, finding a comfortable position. “You were raised by Uncle Gao. He treated you like his own daughter, so you never lacked love when you were young. It’s only natural you want to acknowledge her. I’m not unreasonable, and I’m certainly not selfish enough to take away your right to reconnect with her.”","Gao Min bit her lip. “But... I’m afraid it might make you uncomfortable, given how she treated us back then—”","Liu Yutong cut her off with a wave. “You’re my sister. If you want to acknowledge her, go ahead. If that woman—our ‘mother’—actually treats you well and sincerely tries to make it up to you, I’d be happy for you. Why would I stop you?”","Gao Min stared at her sister, her eyes slowly reddening, tears misting over them.","She hadn’t expected her sister to be so understanding. It filled her with both gratitude and guilt.","“Stop right there!”","Seeing that Gao Min was about to cry again, Liu Yutong raised her hand in a “halt” gesture, looking disdainful. “Don’t get all mushy on me. I’m not falling for that. If you dare to cry, I’ll throw you out.”","Gao Min couldn’t help but laugh. “You little rascal, who said I was going to cry?”","“Enough, enough. Let’s talk business.”","Liu Yutong dropped the playful expression and spoke seriously. “If you want to acknowledge her, I won’t stop you. But you need to promise me one thing.”","Gao Min: “What is it?”","Liu Yutong: “Come to my office tomorrow morning and act as my assistant. Let me probe her a little first. Don’t reveal your identity yet; just listen to what she has to say.”","“After you’ve heard her out, you can make your decision.”","“If you want to acknowledge her then, go ahead. If not, don’t. In the end, it’s your choice. Don’t worry about me, and don’t worry about how I feel.”","Gao Min was silent for a few seconds before asking, “And what about you?”","Liu Yutong didn’t answer right away.","She stood up, walked to the French window, and pushed it open.","The night wind rushed in, carrying the chill of early autumn, stirring her hair and dispelling the stuffiness in the room.","Beyond the window lay the nightscape of Pearl City—countless lights glimmering like a cascading river of stars scattered across the ground.","This was the empire she had built piece by piece, the very foundation of her organization, the Dragon Alliance.","“Me?”","“I’ve told you before—I’ve long passed the age where I need a mother.”","To be honest, did she hate Jiang Lu?","Not really.","After all, how could you hate someone you had no memory of from childhood? That kind of feeling was too abstract for her.","Was she lacking in familial love?","No, she wasn’t. If anything, she had more of it than most.","Her grandparents, Yaya, Gao Min, Yuncheng, Mada, Yu Xin, Li Xiaohui... and the thousands of brothers and sisters in the Dragon Alliance—they were all her family.","So whether she acknowledged her mother or not didn’t really matter.","Of course, deep down, she still leaned toward keeping her distance from Jiang Lu.","After all, her mother was now the wife of the Lin family, and Liu Yutong didn’t carry the Lin surname.","Of course, she didn’t intend to acknowledge the family bond, but the Lin family connection could still be exploited.","After all, the Lin family was once a noble and wealthy house. Even if they had fallen from grace, a lean camel is bigger than a horse. They might still have some value to be used when the time came.","As long as Jiang Lu didn’t cause trouble in the future, maintaining a surface-level harmony or even cooperation wouldn’t be out of the question.","Gao Min walked over and stood shoulder to shoulder with her.","“Little sister.”","“Hmm?”","“No matter what, I’ll always be your sister. That’s something no one can change.”","Liu Yutong turned to look at her sister’s earnest expression and suddenly joked, “Maybe in the next life, you can be my younger sister instead.”","Unexpectedly, Gao Min seriously tilted her head, thought about it, and then nodded solemnly.","“That works too!”","Liu Yutong: “???”","Gao Min: “Then I could accept you looking out for me without feeling guilty.”","Liu Yutong was thrown off by that. It took her a couple of seconds to process before she responded, “Wait a minute—how does that logic work? You know I’ve always had your back even when you’re the older sister.","“It’s not the same.”","Gao Min said matter-of-factly. “When you’re the older sister, you have to keep up appearances, you know? Being taken care of by you makes me feel like a failure as an older sister. If I were the younger sister, it’d be completely natural to be looked after by you.”","Liu Yutong: “...”","She stared at Gao Min for a long moment, then said darkly, “Are you tricking me? And in a really sneaky way, too.”","Gao Min looked completely innocent. “What are you talking about? I’m just telling the truth.”","Liu Yutong: “Fine, you win. This life you’re the older sister, but next life you want to be the younger one. You’re trying to have it both ways, aren’t you?”","Gao Min smiled so hard her eyes turned into crescent moons. “Want to switch? You can be the older sister next life, and I’ll stay the younger sister in this one. Then we’ll be even, and no one’s losing out.”","Liu Yutong: “Alright... wait, it feels like you’re messing with my head again!”","Gao Min: “Hahaha...”"]},{"number":731,"title":"Chapter 731: 732, Two Beauties in One Family (Thanks to Xunle Duku for the God Certification)","paragraphs":["The two sisters chatted for a while and gradually began to feel drowsy.","\"Sis, you go upstairs and rest first. You still need to come with me to the office tomorrow.\"","\"Mm, you should get to bed early too. Don’t stay up too late.\"","Gao Min didn’t say anything more. She turned and went upstairs to wash up.","Liu Yutong walked over to the sofa and had just picked up her phone to check her messages when the doorbell rang.","It had to be Yun Cheng.","After she opened the door, he walked in.","\"Miss, I have the confessions from those thugs, plus the verified information. It’s all sorted out.\"","Liu Yutong pointed to the sofa across from her. \"Have a seat. Tell me, what’s the situation?\"","Yun Cheng sat down and started reporting directly.","\"The ringleader is called Liu San. He’s likely a pawn sent by Hu Ge, who works under Wu Kun, Jiang Yuan’s white glove. This bunch basically took money for the job. They have no clue their real boss is Jiang Yuan. They only know it was Hu Ge who paid them and sent them to Mingzhu City to find out two things. First, the whereabouts of Zhao Weixiang and to confirm if he’s dead. Second, whether there’s anything unusual on your side.","Oh, by the way, this Hu Ge is a building materials merchant from the south.\"","\"Go on.\"","\"Hu Ge also set them rules: don’t expose your identity, quietly relay any info back to Gangcheng, don’t do anything else, and especially don’t stir up trouble locally. Too bad Liu San and his guys completely forgot that. When they saw Lin Feng lurking near the alley, they thought he’d overheard their conversation, so they impulsively chased after him. Little did they know they’d land right in our hands, like fish trapped in a net.\"","\"...\"","After hearing the report, Liu Yutong fell into thought.","Jiang Yuan was indeed cautious. Having to go through so many layers just to gather information clearly showed he still doubted Zhao Weixiang’s death and was wary of the evidence she might hold.","An old fox like him—any slight disturbance would make him retreat into his shell.","\"Did they mention if Wu Kun has any other plans?\"","\"No. Liu San and his crew are just low-level runners. They don’t have access to core information. However, I relayed the situation here to Hua Muying, and he told me Wu Kun has been frequently contacting several major families in Gangcheng lately, apparently preparing some capital operations. The exact purpose is still unclear.\"","Contacting major families in Gangcheng, huh? That really is a bit unusual. Could he be planning to sell off assets and make a run for it?","Does he have to be this cautious?","A plan began to form in Liu Yutong’s mind. \"Since Jiang Yuan is so cautious, let’s feed him some good news and get him to let his guard down.\"","\"What kind of news?\"","\"First, have Liu San’s people send a message that Zhao Weixiang is indeed dead, killed cleanly, but there’s no confirmation on whether he left anything behind. Let them guess for themselves.\"","\"Second, send word that everything is normal in Mingzhu City. But let it slip that the Wanlong Society is up to something—like hint that, through bribed employees, we’ve learned the society’s Weibo platform has plans to go public in Gangcheng.\"","\"Will that work? Can an old fox like Jiang Yuan buy it?\"","\"Whether he believes it or not isn’t the point. The key is to give him a reason to believe. And Weibo’s IPO plan is that reason.\"","\"That’ll need some coordination. Later, have Yu Xin contact Mrs. Ji and Mr. Chu from Qixing Capital and AEG Capital. Tell them we have plans for Weibo to go public next year, so they can start preparing their funds.\"","Weibo had never raised funds before—first, because Liu Yutong wanted to maximize profits, and second, because she genuinely wasn’t short on cash.","But thinking it over, she decided to throw those two a bone.","Because the Wanhui Premium Selection, which they’d been eagerly looking forward to, she planned to postpone its IPO.","Her original plan was to take it public next year, but she now intended to delay it—or even scrap the idea altogether.","After careful deliberation, she realized that while Wanhui Premium Selection had great potential to become a corporation worth hundreds of billions, its business chain was too singular. Its profit model relied heavily on commissions and similar streams, making it vulnerable to capital attacks. If any capital wanted to mess with her, they could simply pour money into taking over her market share.","So instead, it might be better to use it as bargaining chips to swap interests with a certain Chairman Ma.","Timing was key—pretty soon, he’d need to push through a delisting plan and relist. If before that, she used Wanhui Premium Selection, along with a hefty chunk of cash, to help him speed up the delisting, wouldn’t that carve out a place for her in the future of e-commerce?","That would be far easier than building an e-commerce platform from scratch.","But before that, she had to either crush or cripple all the emerging competitors out there. Only then would her hand be worth more, and the chips on the negotiation table heavy enough.","Of course, this was just a rough idea. Whether it actually worked remained to be seen.","Yun Cheng’s eyes lit up as he instantly grasped the Miss’s intention.","\"You mean, by using Weibo’s Gangcheng IPO as a pretext, make Jiang Yuan think our focus is on business expansion, so we have no time to bother with his shady dealings?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Right. When Liu San and his crew go back to report, they can let slip this irrelevant news: that I’m busy with chips and busy with IPOs, so why would I have the energy to care about Zhao Weixiang? That will make it seem perfectly reasonable to Jiang Yuan.","After all, with the massive business empire I run, focusing on making money and expanding is only logical. If I were glued to the death of a dead man like Zhao Weixiang, that would look strange—and put him on alert.\"","\"And, we can throw in a rumor: that I was so money-hungry I had my father in the countryside thrown into jail, utterly devoid of family loyalty.\"","After hearing this, Yun Cheng couldn’t help but nod. The reasoning seemed quite feasible.","Jiang Yuan, that old fox, was always paranoid. The Miss’s approach was a good one.","After all, the Miss’s lack of family loyalty was a \"fact.\" With a little embellishment—like how she’d even jailed the head of a rival company competing for stock—she’d look like someone who only cares about money, a true capitalist.","And would a capitalist still care about how her biological father died back in the day?","At any rate, the Miss was wealthy, busy, and focused on IPOs and cashing out. She had no time to obsess over Zhao Weixiang.","\"Miss, I’ll take care of it.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Good. But handle Liu San personally. Don’t leave any clues.\"","\"Understood,\" Yun Cheng said.","As Yun Cheng was about to leave, he seemed to think of something and hesitated before speaking. \"Miss, there’s something I’m not sure if I should ask.\"","Liu Yutong looked at him, signaling him to go ahead.","Yun Cheng: \"It’s about Miss Gao’s family reunion matter. Are you really going to let her go through with it?\"","As the one who had been with Liu Yutong the longest and had always been her personal bodyguard, he couldn’t have missed Liu Yutong’s attitude toward this.","Liu Yutong showed no surprise at his question. Apparently, she’d already considered it long ago.","\"I’m not going to decide for her. I’ll let her make her own choice. But before that, I’ll test Jiang Lu to see if she has ever truly searched for her eldest daughter all these years.\"","\"She never came looking for me, and maybe I could understand her a little—after all, she might have been afraid or had her reasons, or perhaps she thought that since I had grandparents who loved me, she could rest easy.\"","\"But there's no excuse for her not to go looking for Big Sister. Even if she didn't know she was kept in the dark, I refuse to believe that, given her status after marrying into the Lin family, with the Lin family's resources and her own, she wouldn't have searched. If she didn't, then I can only conclude that she's been lying all along—or worse, that she never really cared about Big Sister.\"","\"Coming to claim kinship now is either a sudden attack of conscience or she has some other agenda.","And when that happens, I think Big Sister will know whether or not to acknowledge her, won't she?\"","Yuncheng nodded upon hearing this. \"I understand.\"","Of course, he had no idea that there was more to Liu Yutong's considerations.","To be precise, the reason she even wanted Gao Min to acknowledge the kinship was to pave a path for her—a path that could reach the heavens.","If everything went smoothly, the two sisters would truly be a formidable alliance: one ruling a commercial empire, the other wielding political power.","A true pair of dual prodigies from the same family!"]},{"number":732,"title":"Chapter 732: 733, The Path Is Paved. (Thanks to Li Xindi for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Actually, after learning about Jiang Lu’s identity, Liu Yutong had already had the Lin family investigated.","The Lin family of the imperial capital had once been aristocrats among the city’s elite. When the old Lin patriarch was alive, a single stomp of his foot could shake the entire Fourth and Ninth Ring Road. Unfortunately, he passed away early, leaving no worthy successor, and over the years, the family had declined steadily.","But as the saying goes, a starved camel is still larger than a horse.","Though the Lin family no longer enjoyed its former glory, its foundations remained. In particular, the Lin family’s marital alliances, though now less visible on the surface, still carried unbreakable bonds of kinship.","The most typical example was Lin Yi, the only daughter of the late eldest Lin brother.","Lin Yi was the only child of Lin Dong’s elder brother. After her father died, she followed her mother back to her maternal family.","Her mother’s maiden name was Shen, hailing from the Shen family of the imperial capital.","The Shen family was true top-tier aristocracy. Old Mr. Shen was a legitimate descendant of revolutionary founders; though long retired from the front lines, his former students and subordinates were scattered across the country.","The current generation of the Shen family was especially accomplished: the eldest served in a ministry commission, the second in the military, and the third in a state-owned enterprise—each holding real power.","Lin Yi, as the Shen family’s granddaughter, had grown up under their roof and was said to be deeply favored by Old Mr. Shen.","At just twenty-six or twenty-seven, she was already a department-level director.","More crucially, Lin Yi was the head of content regulation at the main bureau—a chokehold department that could strangle countless entertainment companies, a position of genuine authority.","This time, when Dragon View Media’s web series got blocked, the connections moved by those young masters from the imperial capital might well have been coordinated with Lin Yi’s approval.","Of course, this was just speculation.","But one thing was certain: if this Lin Yi connection could be established, the blockage would cease to be a problem.","The other was the Zhou family, the clan of Lin Feng’s late mother.","Lin Feng’s biological mother was born a Zhou, from the Zhou family of the imperial capital.","Though the Zhou family was not as eminent as the Shen family, they were an old-school established lineage with generations of influence, their network deeply rooted and intricate within the imperial capital.","Unfortunately, Lin Feng’s mother died young, and his father, Lin Dong, remarried an outsider, Jiang Lu, who came from a second marriage. This provoked the Zhou family’s displeasure, and over the years, they had virtually cut ties with the Lin family.","But that didn’t mean the Zhou family would completely abandon Lin Feng.","After all, Lin Feng carried half the Zhou family’s blood. If something truly serious happened, the Zhou family couldn’t stand idly by.","Of course, this also showed how pragmatic those big families were. Once the Lin family declined, they gradually kept their distance.","Still, the Lin family could still be leveraged now.","Gao Min was currently a first-grade police inspector.","At her age, having reached that rank in Bright Pearl City was exceptionally rare.","But to climb higher, ability and merit alone were far from enough; one needed a patron to pave the way with connections.","Any single thread connected to the top-tier circles of the imperial capital was worth more than ten years of hard grind in the provinces.","As for herself, she didn’t need such things.","Her own empire she had built with her own hands, relying on no one.","Her sister Gao Min was different.","Gao Min operated within the bureaucratic system, where resources were essentially about who you knew.","Uncle Li’s connection, to be blunt, had any direct relation to Gao Min?","He had given Gao Min opportunities only because of Liu Yutong’s influence.","She couldn’t keep running to Uncle Li every time.","If the Lin family’s connections could still be used, then use them now.","The younger generation of the Lin family seemed destined to achieve nothing notable—except for that Lin Feng from yesterday, who at least showed some courage and responsibility.","Since the Lin family was bound to fade, it was better to take their relational resources, rather than waste them, and use them to benefit her sister Gao Min.","After all, Jiang Lu owed them; come to think of it, that could be counted as the Lin family’s debt.","As for herself, she still maintained: she had no intention of acknowledging family ties.","The Lin family was the Lin family; she was just herself.","The Dragon Alliance was the Dragon Alliance, needing no one’s backing.","Yun Cheng, standing nearby, seemed to instantly grasp his boss’s intention, and couldn’t help but feel moved inside.","His boss had never been as cold-hearted as the rumors made her out to be. Her softness was always reserved only for those closest to her.","Miss Gao Min was her biological sister, one of the few blood relatives she had. Though she said she wouldn’t claim family ties, she had already paved the way for Gao Min.","It wasn’t just Gao Min—all of them, who had followed her from the beginning, had never been treated stingily.","That was why, whether it was him or anyone else in the Dragon Alliance, they were unwaveringly loyal to her.","A faint trace of relief stirred in Yun Cheng’s heart.","Sometimes he wondered: if he had never taken his brothers to seek out the boss, what would he be now?","He had actually had that dream.","In the dream, there was no boss. He still had his dyed yellow hair, leading his brothers in street fights over territory, drifting day after day, until he got caught in some crackdown and ended up in prison. When he came out, the world had changed, and he knew nothing, becoming like a lump of mud, a discarded piece of scrap society had left behind.","That kind of hopeless life—he didn’t want a single day of it.","Luckily, it had only been a dream.","The boss was right in front of him, hadn’t disappeared.","“Alright, I’m getting sleepy. Yun Cheng, you should rest early too. There’s work tomorrow.”","“Okay.”","Yun Cheng turned to leave. Just as he reached the door, Liu Yutong’s voice came again from behind.","“Oh, one more thing.”","He looked back.","Liu Yutong looked at him. “You really don’t want to go to BS Province?”","Yun Cheng paused briefly, then shook his head.","“Boss, I’m not leaving, and I don’t want to leave.","“I don’t have grand ambitions. Being by your side gives me peace of mind. Let the other brothers expand the territory; I just want to stay here and be your bodyguard.”","Liu Yutong nodded.","“Understood.”","“Then take some time to hand over your duties. I’ll send someone else.”","In her heart, she felt a little sorry for Yun Cheng.","Strictly speaking, he was the de facto second-in-command of the Dragon Alliance. In terms of seniority and prestige, he could have filled a key role, like the deputy head of the group.","But on second thought, maybe this was for the best.","Without too much ambition or too many desires, such people often lasted the longest.","Since he wouldn’t leave, the future arrangements would have to fall on Yu Xin.","The Dragon Alliance Group was expanding rapidly, even becoming somewhat bloated.","She was also planning to restructure the organization.","By then, she would gradually step back from day-to-day matters, only controlling the overall direction. For the person responsible for executing specific tasks, she had originally had two candidates in mind: Yun Cheng and Yu Xin.","In terms of ability, Yu Xin was indeed superior, but Yun Cheng was the founding contributor. With proper training, he might have stood on his own.","Now that Yun Cheng had explicitly declined, it saved her from having to agonize over that choice.","“Alright, you may go now.”","“Goodnight, boss.”"]},{"number":733,"title":"Chapter 733: 734, Become a Vassal of the Lin Family (Thanks to Li Xindi for the Great God Certification X2)","paragraphs":["The next morning, at ShunChang Tower.","A black Bentley pulled up at the entrance of the building.","The car door opened, and Lin Dong stepped out first, then helped his wife, Jiang Lu, out.","Lin Feng followed last. The wounds on his body were still wrapped in bandages, but his spirits were clearly much better than the night before.","The three stood at the main entrance, looking up at a tower they had visited many times before, their emotions tangled.","As soon as Lin Feng saw this building, images from the previous night flooded his mind unbidden—the street filled with men in black. It was one of the most oppressive scenes he had ever witnessed in his life.","Even now, the memory still made his heart race.","He couldn’t help but recall his father’s words: if that girl Tongtong had been born in chaotic times, she might very well have carved out her own kingdom.","Jiang Lu was still visibly nervous.","Seeing this, Lin Feng teased her, “Aunt Jiang, don’t be so tense. We’re just here to chat, not walk to the execution ground. Besides, after what we saw last night, how could today be any scarier?”","Jiang Lu forced a faint smile and nodded.","“Let’s go.”","The three walked into the building side by side.","Unlike their previous visits, the front desk didn’t stop them this time.","A short-haired woman in a black suit came up to greet them.","She was quite pretty, with sharp, determined features and a brisk, confident stride—clearly a very capable person.","But for some reason, they all felt she looked oddly familiar.","Before they could dwell on it, she spoke.","“I’m Miss’s assistant, my surname is Gao. Please follow me. Miss is waiting for you in her office.”","Lin Dong and the others felt a subtle stir in their hearts.","Miss...","They had been hearing this title since last night, and it still struck them as odd.","They were fairly familiar with Liu Yutong’s background. She wasn’t from some prominent family. So why did everyone call her that?","The elevator rose all the way to the top floor.","The short-haired woman led them down a corridor and finally stopped before a dark wooden door. She knocked twice, lightly.","“Come in.”","A cool female voice came from inside—neither loud nor soft, but it somehow made their nerves tighten.","“Please, go ahead.”","The woman pushed the door open and stepped in first.","Lin Dong and the others quickly followed.","The office was large, simply decorated but tasteful. A floor-to-ceiling window offered a view of Pearl City’s skyline, and sunlight streamed in, coating the space in a warm glow.","But Lin Dong and the others felt no warmth at all.","Because behind that broad desk sat a young girl.","Today, she wore a black suit jacket over a simple white blouse, her long hair draped over her shoulders. She had light makeup on, and at first glance, she looked like an exceptionally pretty young woman.","Yet her eyes carried a cold, distant aloofness that sent a chill through anyone who met her gaze.","Seeing them enter, she stood and gestured toward the sofa area in the lounge.","“Sit.”","Lin Dong, Jiang Lu, and Lin Feng took their seats on the sofa. Liu Yutong walked over and sat down on the single sofa across from them.","She dispensed with pleasantries or polite chatter and looked directly at Jiang Lu.","“Ms. Jiang, before we discuss anything else, I have a question for you. You had better think carefully before answering. Don’t bother trying to lie. You should know whether I have the patience to hear your lies.”","Jiang Lu stiffened slightly, then quickly nodded. “Go ahead. I’ll tell the truth.”","Liu Yutong asked, “I’ve heard you have an older daughter, who went missing shortly after she was born. Is that right?”","Jiang Lu’s whole body trembled. She looked up at Liu Yutong in disbelief.","“How... how do you know about that?”","She had never mentioned this to anyone outside the family—not even her husband Lin Dong had known until recently.","How did her daughter find out?","Liu Yutong didn’t answer. She continued, “Don’t worry about how I know. I only have one question: Over all these years, did you ever look for her?”","Jiang Lu nodded frantically. “I did. I really did look. I...”","Liu Yutong cut her off again. “You say you looked. Then where’s the proof?”","Jiang Lu froze. “What?”","Lin Dong couldn’t hold back. “All of that was so many years ago. How could there still be any evidence...”","Liu Yutong cast a cool glance at him. “Mr. Lin, I wasn’t asking you.”","Lin Dong choked, swallowing the rest of his words.","Jiang Lu bit her lip. Then, as if a thought struck her, she frantically rummaged through her bag. She pulled out a wallet, opened it, and carefully retrieved something from an inner compartment.","It was a photograph. The edges had yellowed and grown brittle, but it was well preserved inside a plastic sleeve.","She handed the photo to Liu Yutong.","“This was taken after I escaped. I had no documents then. I had this photo taken at a town photo studio to get a temporary ID.”","Liu Yutong took it and looked down.","The woman in the photo was very young, barely past twenty. She was gaunt, her hair slightly messy, wearing a worn, faded old dress. Standing in front of a simple studio backdrop, she radiated a heartbreaking fragility.","“This was two years after I escaped. I had just recovered my health and wanted to go back to find Niannian. I used this photo to get a temporary ID, then traveled east to look for her.”","She went on, pulling a notebook from her bag and handing it to Liu Yutong with both hands.","“Later, after I settled down in the capital, I hired people to check the archives from that province. I searched everything I could, but... there was no news of Niannian. I also filed a report with the police’s missing persons system, but after so many years, nothing came of it.”","She paused and opened the notebook.","“This is what I wrote down back then when I was searching for Niannian—every place I went, everyone I asked, every lead I found... I recorded it all.”","Liu Yutong took the notebook and began flipping through it seriously.","It was densely filled with information about abducted children, especially girls whose birth dates were close to what she was looking for, each entry carefully noting time and place.","She read page by page, thoroughly. When she finished, she handed the notebook to Assistant Gao behind her.","In truth, after seeing all this, she wanted to ask, “If you looked for my sister, why didn’t you ever come back for me?”","But she didn’t say it.","Jiang Lu said, “I know... this might not prove anything. You might think I made it up or filled it in later, but I really did...”","“I believe you.”","Jiang Lu jerked her head up, staring at Liu Yutong in disbelief.","“Then... Tongtong...”","But Liu Yutong didn’t stay on the topic. “We’re done with your matter. Now it’s Mr. Lin’s turn.”","Lin Dong stiffened.","From the moment he walked into the room, he had witnessed his stepdaughter’s decisiveness. She wasted no words, pressed hard, and gave no room to breathe.","“Tongtong, if your Wanlong Society wants to cooperate with the Lin Group, as long as the terms aren’t unreasonable, I can agree on behalf of the company.”","Even as he said this, he had already braced himself for the worst.","He still felt that this stepdaughter was probably trying to use the Lin family as a springboard. After all, the only thing she might really care about were those major projects of his in the imperial capital.","At worst, he could even give her one at a low price, or for free.","Liu Yutong: \"You can think of it that way too. Consider it a transaction.\"","Lin Dong’s heart sank—just as he had suspected.","But he also knew that on her turf, he probably had no right to refuse.","\"Then state your conditions. As long as I can do it, I will.\"","But what Liu Yutong said next made him leap to his feet in shock.","\"Mr. Lin, I need your entire Lin family to mobilize all your resources and connections to elevate an outsider. Is that possible?\"","These words hit Lin Dong like a thunderbolt.","His face instantly turned ghastly as he stared at Liu Yutong in disbelief.","\"Miss Liu, what do you mean by that? What exactly are you trying to do?\"","In his panic, his form of address changed, and a terrible premonition surged in his heart—this stepdaughter’s ambition was far greater than he had imagined.","She wasn’t just asking for compensation; she was opening her mouth wide like a lion—someone about to devour everything!","To mobilize the entire Lin family’s strength and all their connections to elevate her? In other words, was she asking for the Lin family to become her vassal?","That was utterly impossible, and could never be done!!!","............."]},{"number":734,"title":"Chapter 734: 735, Tough.","paragraphs":["\"Miss Liu, you're being far too greedy!\"","Lin Dong's face had darkened to its extreme.","To mobilize the entire Lin family's strength and utilize all their connections to prop up someone who wasn't even a blood relative?","The words sounded simple enough, but Lin Dong knew better than anyone the weight they carried.","Though the Lin family was no longer what it once was, the goodwill from the late patriarch's time, the marriage ties, and the lingering connections with families like the Shen and Zhou families were the foundation of the Lin family's standing in the imperial capital.","This was what still allowed the Lin family to be called \"noble,\" not merely \"wealthy.\"","If he actually followed Liu Yutong's suggestion, wouldn't that be handing the Lin family over to an outsider?","From then on, would every Lin family descendant have to kowtow to this outsider?","And what would be the difference between that and the Lin family becoming her subordinate, being legitimately swallowed up by her?","Jiang Lu was also stunned when she heard her daughter's conditions, her face filled with disbelief.","She had come to see her daughter to make up for eighteen years of neglect, to acknowledge her as her own child. Even if it meant paying any amount of material compensation, she was willing without hesitation.","But the condition her daughter proposed was far too sensitive—it practically touched the taboo of a family like the Lin family.","To prop up someone outside the clan, using the entire family's resources—what did that even mean?","It was like dismantling the Lin family's ancestral tomb to fill someone else's foundation.","How could her husband possibly agree? And she couldn't force him to agree, either.","Besides, Tongtong—clearly controlling the massive Dragon Union's power, with thousands of armed enforcers under her command, a ruler in Pearl City by sheer force—could it be that she still wasn't satisfied and wanted to extend her reach into...","Thinking this, Jiang Lu shuddered violently and dared not continue.","Setting aside her daughter's identity, Jiang Lu felt her daughter was a bit \"dark\" herself. If something really went wrong, once exposed, not only would Tongtong be irredeemably ruined, but the entire Lin family would be dragged down with her.","At this thought, she couldn't help but speak.","\"Tong... Tongtong, why don't you think this over again?\"","\"In terms of material compensation, I'll give you whatever you want, and the Lin family will give you whatever they can... but this condition really is too harsh.\"","Beside them, \"Assistant Gao\" was also stunned that her sister would make such a sharp demand. It genuinely shocked her.","Though she knew her sister was doing it for her sake, the method itself, the terms—wasn't it all too transactional?","She was a senior inspector, reaching this point through her own efforts, with some help from her sister, of course, but she truly didn't want to turn a sincere family reunion into a cold, profit-driven exchange.","Even less did she want to put her sister and the Lin family in a bind.","If she'd known her sister would come down this hard, she might not have even come to acknowledge her parents.","At worst, both sides would part bitterly, or even fall apart altogether.","With that in mind, Gao Min, while pouring them tea, deliberately hinted for her sister to ease up.","But Liu Yutong remained unmoved, directly dismissing her. \"If you have nothing else to do, get out. No need for you to pour tea here.\"","Gao Min: \"...\"","She was about to speak when Yun Cheng came over, gesturing to Gao Min. \"This way, please.\"","It was the first time Gao Min felt so powerless and suffocated in front of her sister. When her sister was assertive, even she, as an older sister, couldn't get a word in.","Finally, she obediently followed Yun Cheng out of the office.","Watching Gao Min's figure disappear through the doorway, Liu Yutong shook her head slightly.","Her sister was good in every way, but too soft-hearted, with a naive, dogmatic streak.","Why shouldn't they take what they could get?","Since her sister couldn't bring herself to do it, she would play the villain instead.","At least her sister had already heard the important parts.","Lin Dong and the others were surprised to see Liu Yutong treat her own assistant like that. Before they could recover, Liu Yutong spoke again, her tone even harsher.","\"Mr. Lin, let me ask you one more time: can this deal be done or not?\"","\"To be blunt, how much is the Lin family's remaining influence really worth? The old patriarch passed away years ago. Is there anyone in the third generation of the Lin family capable of shouldering the family?\"","\"Your nephews and grandsons—either they're lost in pleasure, have no ambition, or are mediocre in ability. Not one of them is worth a damn, let alone capable of reviving or maintaining those complicated relationships.\"","\"In a few more years, when those who owe favors to your patriarch grow old and pass on, who among their descendants will remember the Lin family?","The Shen and Zhou families are already distancing themselves from you because of the Lin family's decline. In a few more years, they may not even bother meeting you.\"","\"When that happens, what will the Lin family still be? Even if you have a bit of money, you won't be able to hold your place in the imperial capital's elite circles. By then, the family's pride in being a great noble house will be nothing but a joke.\"","\"What I'm asking you to do—prop up one person—is not asking you to work for free. It's to let those nearly expired connections realize their final worth.","Perhaps, if I'm in a good mood and grateful for the Lin family's contribution, I might even give you a helping hand.\"","\"Think it over. Don't give me any nonsense about the honor of a capital family. Honor doesn't put food on the table.\"","Lin Dong opened his mouth to argue but found he didn't know how to refute.","The connections left by his father, the accumulated goodwill, the relationships that could tip the scales at critical moments—was there anyone in the Lin family's current generation who could carry that burden?","His son, Lin Feng, though loyal and kind-hearted, was too straightforward, too impulsive, like a kid who hadn't grown up—he couldn't lead the way.","As for the younger generation, Lin Shen, Lin Zheng, and others—they only schemed over family wealth, bickering among themselves. Put them on the real stage, and none of them could hold their own.","Liu Yutong's words were harsh, but true.","The current generation of the Lin family indeed had no one capable of carrying the torch.","Those connections, those relationships, everything the old patriarch had spent his life building—if no one took over, within ten years, even less, they'd amount to nothing.","By then, the Lin family would no longer be able to call itself a great noble house. Without a single person in the system who could speak up, what \"nobility\" would remain?","Of course, there was one exception: Lin Dong's brother's daughter, Lin Yi.","But Lin Yi didn't need the Lin family's support. She had the Shen family behind her, and she was excellent enough on her own.","It was even questionable whether Lin Yi still considered herself part of the Lin family.","Lin Dong hadn't expected this twenty-year-old girl to have such a thorough grasp of their family's situation in such a short time.","Her words hit the nail on the head, without mercy.","But having the entire family's strength used to prop up someone else... he still couldn't get past that mental hurdle.","After all, she didn't bear the Lin surname!","Of course, if she were willing to change her surname and be entered into the Lin family genealogy as a descendant, he might consider—perhaps treat her as the next generation's leader and cultivate her accordingly.","After all, he had seen firsthand just how capable and resourceful she was. She truly was impressive.","But before he could even voice that condition,","Liu Yutong seemed to see right through him, speaking up in advance. \"As for changing my surname and things like that, forget it. My surname is Liu. I like it just fine, and I'm used to it. As for the Lin family genealogy, we're not interested in it, so don't try to use that as a bargaining chip with me.\""]},{"number":735,"title":"Chapter 735: 736 (Thank you, Sensentianxiadiyi, for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Lin Dong was caught off guard by her words, the words on the tip of his tongue forcibly stuck in his throat.","This stepdaughter really left no room for negotiation!","But after all, he was an old fox who had weathered storms in the capital for years. Once the initial frustration passed, he gradually sensed something was off.","“Miss Liu, who exactly are you trying to lift up? It can’t be yourself, can it?” He suddenly asked a key question.","As soon as he said that, the office fell silent for a moment.","Jiang Lu was stunned.","Just moments ago, her mind had been entirely consumed by the excitement and anxiety of reuniting with her daughter, and she hadn’t thought about it deeply.","Now, hearing her husband’s question, she suddenly realized something.","Yes, Tongtong herself was already the head of the Wanlong Society, commanding thousands of people and controlling tens of billions in assets. How could she possibly give all that up to enter the civil service?","Lin Feng was also stunned. He scratched his head, looking confused.","If it wasn’t Liu Yutong, then who could it be?","Who else was qualified?","Liu Yutong looked at Lin Dong, a hint of amusement in her eyes.","As expected of the head of the Lin family—even though the family had declined, he still had his wits about him.","“Mr. Lin, go on.”","Lin Dong took a deep breath, his mind racing as he recalled every detail since arriving at Shunzheng Tower.","From the very beginning, Tongtong had asked Jiang Lu if she had ever looked for her eldest daughter. This proved she not only knew of her elder sister’s existence but might even know where she was.","Then she had made that extremely forceful demand—for the entire Lin family to dedicate all its resources to lifting up someone outside the family.","At the time, he had instinctively assumed that this outsider was Liu Yutong herself, that she wanted to use the Lin family as a springboard into the capital, even into the political system.","But now that he thought about it carefully, it made no sense at all.","If she truly wanted to enter that circle in the capital, with the power and tactics she already wielded as the head of the Wanlong Society, she wouldn’t need the Lin family as a stepping stone. She could do it on her own.","Yet she had chosen this method of forcing him to take a stand, insisting on using the Lin family’s resources to lift someone up.","Why?","Because what she truly cared about wasn’t whether the Lin family was willing to lift her up.","What she cared about was whether the Lin family was willing to lift up... that person.","That person must be extremely important to her.","Lin Dong suddenly thought of the somewhat unusual assistant.","Earlier, when Liu Yutong had told her to leave, the assistant had clearly wanted to say something but was sent out without explanation.","Lin Dong hadn’t thought much of it at the time, but now, connecting these details, the truth was practically right in front of him.","That assistant was likely Liu Yutong’s sister, his wife Jiang Lu’s eldest daughter!","And what’s more, the eldest daughter was a police officer!","No wonder he had found her familiar from the start. Wasn’t she the girl in a police uniform from last night?","Once he had it all sorted out, Lin Dong suddenly stood up.","“The person you want us to lift up isn’t you—it’s Assistant Gao outside, isn’t it?”","Liu Yutong was silent for a few seconds. Then she smiled softly.","“Mr. Lin, you’re sharper than I expected.”","“Since you’ve figured it out, I won’t beat around the bush.”","“The one I want the Lin family to lift up is indeed not me.”","Lin Feng was completely lost.","Wait, what was going on here?","How had it suddenly become connected to an assistant?","He looked at his father, then at Liu Yutong, feeling as if his brain had completely short-circuited.","Jiang Lu was also stunned.","Because her mind had been entirely focused on how to make up for her shortcomings toward Liu Yutong, how to mend their mother-daughter relationship, she hadn’t looked at things from any other angle.","Hearing her husband and daughter’s conversation, she was utterly bewildered.","“Tongtong, what are you talking about?”","“If it’s not you, then who is it?”","“Or do you want me to do something? If there’s anything I can do, I’ll agree to it!”","She still thought Liu Yutong was using this to negotiate conditions with them, assuming it was some kind of test.","But Liu Yutong didn’t even glance at her. Her gaze was fixed on Lin Dong.","“Mr. Lin, I’ll ask you just one question. Can you accept this deal or not?”","Lin Dong took a deep breath, and asked in a heavy tone, “You have to at least let me know exactly who I’m supposed to be lifting. What’s her name? What’s her background? What’s her resume? What are her skills? Is she worth the Lin family betting everything on her?”","Liu Yutong nodded.","“That’s fair.”","“Her name is Gao Min, 23 years old, a local of Pearl City. She graduated from XXX Police Academy and is the daughter of a fallen hero.”","“After graduation, she served in Pearl City as a trainee officer, sergeant, and senior sergeant... Not long ago, she earned a personal second-class merit and was promoted ahead of schedule to first-level senior sergeant.”","“To date, she has handled dozens of cases with a 100% solve rate, arrested over a thousand suspects, and has had zero wrongful convictions, zero unjust cases, and zero complaints.”","“Her record is spotless and can stand up to any scrutiny...”","After briefly introducing the situation, Liu Yutong asked again.","“Mr. Lin, what do you think of this person?”","Lin Dong sucked in a breath of cold air.","Twenty-three years old, daughter of a fallen hero, first-level senior sergeant, 100% solve rate, personal second-class merit...","Holy moly!","This resume was so solid, so undeniably impressive!","Even compared with Lin Yi, his elder brother’s daughter, it was in no way inferior.","Lin Yi had only recently been promoted to C-level, while this girl, at such a young age, was already a first-level senior sergeant, just one step away from deputy C-level, and she’d earned her stripes at the grassroots level through real accomplishments.","And that 100% solve rate, zero wrongful convictions or complaints—what did that mean?","It meant this young woman was extremely capable, very outstanding, and no mere ornament.","If someone like that could truly join the Lin family, it would be...","Lin Dong’s heart beat a little faster.","Seeing that he remained silent for a long time, Liu Yutong grew impatient.","“Mr. Lin, I’ll give you one minute to think it over.”","“One minute from now, if you still can’t give me a clear answer, then today’s conversation is over!”","She had essentially issued an ultimatum, leaving no room for bargaining.","Lin Dong suddenly started laughing too.","He laughed with a kind of helplessness, a sense of relief, and... genuine admiration.","“I’ve met many people in my life—sharp ones, foolish ones, kind ones... but I’ve never met anyone like you, Tongtong.”","Liu Yutong looked at him, not saying a word, simply waiting for his answer.","Lin Dong took another deep breath, looked her squarely in the eye, and spoke solemnly.","“Alright, I agree.”","“The Lin family will dedicate the full force of the clan to lift her up.”","“We’ll use all our connections and resources to help open up the path for her advancement.”","“As long as she’s willing, the Lin family will be her backing.”","“No matter how far she goes, the Lin family will support her every step of the way.”","As soon as he made this decision, both Jiang Lu and Lin Feng were dumbfounded.","Lin Feng, in particular, as the most likely successor to his father and the next head of the Lin family, definitely had his own reservations.","If it weren’t for the fact that his stepsister was so domineering, with such an intimidating presence, he would have immediately objected. Why should the family’s resources be given to an outsider?","And, crucially, that outsider wasn’t even his stepsister in front of him.","Of course, he had originally thought it impossible for his father to agree to such harsh terms from the other side, but the result turned out to be a real shock.","It was even unacceptable.","Jiang Lu was stunned for a long time as well. She never expected her husband to actually agree.","Would the rest of the Lin family be willing to accept this?","None of those sisters-in-law were easy to deal with. Once news of this got out, they would surely turn the Lin household upside down.","Liu Yutong hadn't expected Lin Dong to be so straightforward either.","To be honest, she herself had thought the chances of him agreeing were very low, and she hadn't held out much hope.","But since this was the case...","\"Mr. Lin, you've made a wise decision. I hope you won't regret it later.\"","Lin Dong gave a bitter smile.","\"Honestly, I really didn't want to agree. But seeing what you did for someone else today made up my mind.\"","\"You're a person with loyalty and heart. With a sister like you, yours can't be much different.\"","\"Besides, you said it yourself—this is a transaction. The Lin family's sacrifice should come with some return, shouldn't it?\"","A faint smile curled at the corner of Liu Yutong's lips as she called out toward the door.","\"Come in, sister!\""]},{"number":736,"title":"Chapter 736: 737, Place Hope on the Next Generation","paragraphs":["\"Come in, sister!\"","As Liu Yutong spoke, Jiang Lu turned at the sound of her voice, not even having a chance to ask anything before her gaze eagerly fixed on the door.","With a soft click, the door pushed open.","That short-haired girl—the Senior Assistant who had been sent out by Liu Yutong earlier—walked back in.","She stood there, her posture straight and tall, her features carrying a hint of valor and righteousness.","Jiang Lu's gaze moved from her face to Liu Yutong's, then back again.","The two faces were four or five parts alike.","Especially those eyes—they seemed cast from the same mold.","\"You... you are... Nian Nian?\"","Upon hearing this, Gao Min looked over at Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong gave her a slight nod.","With that silent signal, Gao Min stepped forward to stand before Jiang Lu, looking at the tearful woman in front of her.","\"My father was Gao Shubai.\"","\"My name is Gao Min. My father—my adoptive father, that is—gave me this name.\"","Jiang Lu's whole body shook.","Gao Shubai...","Wasn't that the name of Liu Lei's best brother?","\"So that's it... so that's it! Liu Lei, you kept this from me so cruelly!\"","Jiang Lu's tears burst forth instantly.","Her eldest daughter, who had gone missing shortly after birth. The daughter she had searched for so many years.","So she had been alive all along.","So Liu Lei had secretly given her away to his best brother, Gao Shubai.","So she had been right here in Bright Pearl City, right beside her own biological sister.","And she, as the mother, had known nothing.","Jiang Lu could no longer hold back her longing. She rushed forward and threw her arms around Gao Min.","\"I'm sorry, I'm sorry, Nian Nian. Mommy sorry—I've let you suffer...\"","Gao Min's body stiffened slightly. She stood there, not moving, letting herself be held.","After a moment, she raised her hand and gently patted Jiang Lu on the back.","\"Don't cry.\"","Jiang Lu slowly lifted her head, wiped away her tears, and carefully studied Gao Min's features.","Gao Min looked back at her, her expression complex.","\"You... well... take it slow... we'll talk later.\"","She didn't directly call her \"Mom\"—she held back at the crucial moment—but she didn't refuse to acknowledge her either. It was, in a way, a tacit acceptance.","Jiang Lu looked at her, then turned to glance at the younger daughter she truly wanted to hug but dared not, nodded desperately, and choked out: \"Good... good... Mommy will wait for you both... Mommy can wait.\"","She knew it was unrealistic to expect to be called \"Mom\" on the first meeting, especially since both daughters were so independent and outstanding.","Standing to one side, Lin Dong's gaze swept back and forth between Gao Min and Liu Yutong. His heart was churning with mixed emotions.","One was the child of a martyr, a First-Class Police Inspector, upright and honorable, with limitless prospects.","One was dressed in black as dark as ink, exuding overwhelming presence, commanding a hundred-billion-dollar commercial empire, with thousands of subordinates in black, holding absolute sway over Bright Pearl City.","One burned bright red, thoroughly class-conscious.","One was black to the extreme, inscrutably deep.","And they were blood sisters after all.","Lin Dong then looked at his own son, who still hadn't snapped out of his daze, and felt a surge of envy.","Look at those two daughters of hers!","It's not about comparing goods, but about comparing people!","His own reckless kid, compared to them, was practically worthless.","In the end, neither Liu Yutong nor Gao Min uttered that word \"Mom.\"","The family reunion concluded rather hastily.","However, Jiang Lu's mood had clearly improved. At the very least, the boulder that had weighed on her heart for twenty years was lifted. She knew her two daughters were alive and well.","As for formal recognition, there would always be time. Tomorrow was another day.","\"Alright, that concludes today's conversation.\"","\"Mr. Lin, remember your promise,\" Liu Yutong said.","Lin Dong snapped out of his thoughts and nodded.","\"Don't worry. I, Lin Dong, keep my word.\"","\"I'll arrange things for Miss Gao as soon as possible. Next week is the eightieth birthday celebration of the old lady of the Jiang family in the Imperial Capital. I'll take Miss Gao there to make an appearance. I'll introduce her under the Lin family's name, so some of the key people can get to know her.\"","Liu Yutong gave a slight nod, indicating her satisfaction. \"Then I'll be counting on you, Mr. Lin.\"","Lin Feng, overhearing their conversation, was still dazed and confused.","Wait, that's it?","He looked at Gao Min, then at Liu Yutong, and suddenly felt like he—the young master of the Imperial Capital Lin family—was nothing more than a little brother before them.","No, not even a little brother. At best, a background prop.","...","The three of them—Lin Dong, Lin Feng, and Jiang Lu—left Shunchang Tower and got into the car.","Jiang Lu gazed out the window at the building of Shunchang, receding into the distance. Her heart was a tangle of emotions, but mostly comfort.","Both daughters were so outstanding. She really should be grateful.","Lin Feng sat in the front passenger seat, turning his head back every now and then, looking as if he wanted to say something. Several times he opened his mouth, but didn't know how to begin.","Lin Dong noticed all of this.","\"Xiao Feng, I know what you want to say. Is it because Auntie Jiang is here that some things are hard to speak about?\"","Lin Feng: \"Dad, were you really not just being impulsive? That Liu Yutong... no, sister... she...\"","Lin Dong: \"To be honest, I wasn't acting on impulse.\"","\"I truly think that Tongtong isn't the kind of person we imagined her to be. She must be deeply loyal. If it weren't for that, I wouldn't have agreed to her.\"","Upon hearing this, Lin Feng couldn't help muttering: \"She's loyal? I find her terrifying...\"","Lin Dong: \"Xiao Feng, use your head. Why are those thousands of men in black under her so devoted to her?\"","\"If she really were just a profit-driven, ruthless person, so many people wouldn't truly follow her. Loyalty—that's never something you can buy with money alone.\"","\"And didn't you notice? She didn't actually want to acknowledge our family ties. Yet for her sister Gao Min, for others, she still compromised. What does that tell you? It means she places great value on loyalty!\"","\"A person who values loyalty—no matter how dark she may be—rarely does things like burning bridges or repaying kindness with enmity.\"","\"We helped her sister today, and she will remember this debt in the future.\"","\"That's why I dared to agree to her...\"","Of course, there was one most important reason that Lin Dong didn't mention: Gao Min was sufficiently \"red.\"","If it had been just about Liu Yutong, he would actually have worried about possibly being dragged down with her someday.","That girl was formidable, no doubt. But there was something unsettling about her.","After hearing his father's analysis, Lin Feng nodded thoughtfully.","He had to admit, the old ginger is indeed spicier. What his father said made a lot of sense.","But deep down, he still felt somewhat unconvinced. After all, he was the son of the Lin family head...","Just then, Lin Dong suddenly changed the subject.","\"By the way, Xiao Feng, there's something you need to get on top of.\"","Lin Feng blinked: \"Dad, what is it?\"","Lin Dong said in all seriousness: \"Find a partner, get married, have kids. This is urgent.\"","Lin Feng: \"???\"","What do you mean?","Lin Dong: \"You saw it. That girl Gao Min, she's already a First-Class Police Inspector at twenty-three. Unbounded future. And Tongtong, twenty years old, worth tens of billions. Look at yourself. Other than spending money and getting into trouble, what can you do?\"","\"I don’t expect much from your generation, so hurry up and produce a few outstanding offspring for me. If we’re lucky enough to raise someone like Niannian or Tongtong, wouldn’t the Lin family have hope again?\"","Lin Feng: \"...\"","The corner of his mouth twitched, \"Dad, have you forgotten? Gao Min and Tongtong were born to Aunt Jiang.\"","Lin Tong’s eyes widened: \"You think I don’t know that? That’s exactly why it proves the importance of genetics. If you find a woman with good genes, how could the child be bad? When I get home, I’ll have your mother arrange blind dates for you. That second daughter of the Li family isn’t bad, and the third girl from the Wang family, and the one from the Zhao family...\"","Lin Tong rattled off the names of seven or eight marriageable daughters from wealthy families in the imperial capital.","Of course, his own mind was also working. His son’s words had actually reminded him—since his wife Jiang Lu had such excellent genes, shouldn’t he consider having another child himself?","Lin Feng: \"...\"","Suddenly, his sense of self-esteem took a massive hit, and his face flushed red.","\"Come on, Dad! Are you treating me like a stud pig? Don’t I have any human rights at all?\""]},{"number":737,"title":"Chapter 737: 738, Building Rockets in the Future","paragraphs":["Top Floor of Shunchang Building.","Liu Yutong stood by the floor-to-ceiling window, watching the black Bentley gradually disappear into the flow of traffic.","Gao Min walked over to her, standing shoulder to shoulder with her.","\"Honestly, just now I thought I had enough courage to say that word, but when it was actually on the tip of my tongue, I couldn't get it out.\"","Liu Yutong withdrew her gaze, glanced at her sideways, and said, \"Normal. It's only human.\"","Gao Min said, \"Actually... I did want to acknowledge her. Seeing her cry like that made me feel really bad inside.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"I know. Good thing you didn't.\"","Gao Min replied, \"???\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Don't look at me with that strange expression. If you had really acknowledged her on the spot, I might have started to wonder: Did I do the wrong thing? Was I too heartless? Should I have taken that opening and acknowledged her too? That would have put me in a very passive position. Luckily you didn't, which saved me from having to second-guess myself.\"","Gao Min was stunned for a moment, then let out a relieved laugh.","\"You're right. After all, we're sisters. I could never put you in a bind.\"","Liu Yutong snorted softly. \"At least you have a conscience.\"","\"By the way, I've already arranged everything for our trip to the imperial capital the day after tomorrow.\"","Gao Min was slightly startled. \"The imperial capital?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Lin Dong mentioned that the Jiang family's matriarch is celebrating her eightieth birthday, right? This is a good opportunity.\"","\"You'll make an appearance through the Lin family's connections and let those so-called big shots get to know you as the 'Lin family's cousin' first. That way, when you actually need to use those relationships later, it won't seem too abrupt.\"","Gao Min was silent for a few seconds, then suddenly asked,","\"Sis, have you been planning all of this from the very beginning?\"","\"From the moment you had Lin Dong start boosting my profile, you'd already made up your mind to go to the imperial capital, hadn't you?\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"I'm just helping you crack your big case. I had to get you into that circle first so you could get close to the person you need to investigate. If you can't even get into the banquet, how are you going to solve the case? How will you make contact with that Jiang Yuan?\"","Gao Min asked, \"Couldn't you just take me in? With your status, you should have an invitation, right?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"I do, but it's a personal invitation. The Jiang family is one of those old, established aristocratic clans with a lot of rules. If the invitation is issued to me, it doesn't mean I can just bring anyone I want inside.\"","\"But the Lin family is different.\"","\"Even though the Lin family has declined, they're still a gentry family with generations of friendship with the Jiangs. It's only natural for Lin Dong to bring a couple of juniors along. No one would say a thing.\"","\"So, using the Lin family's identity to get in is much more proper than if I brought you.\"","When Gao Min heard this, she couldn't help but let out a long sigh.","\"You really... put so much thought into everything. It feels like there's nothing in this world that escapes your calculations.\"","Sometimes she really didn't know what to say. It always seemed like her younger sister did everything with a strong sense of purpose. It was the same in business, and even something as emotional as a family reunion had been turned into part of her master plan.","\"Honestly, doesn't it wear you out?\"","Liu Yutong smiled. \"The thrill of matching wits with others—there's nothing quite like it!\"","Gao Min looked at her, and a sudden pang of sympathy hit her.","Outsiders only saw the splendor of the Wanlonghui heiress: the thousands of people under her command, her tens of billions in assets, how a single word from her could make countless people bow down.","But who would ever guess that she was barely twenty years old?","At twenty, she should have been in the ivory tower of college, dating, shopping, binge-watching dramas, worrying about finals and a secret crush.","Instead, she had to scheme in this dog-eat-dog world, plotting step by step and matching wits with old foxes who had decades of experience.","\"Sis...\"","Liu Yutong looked at her and curled her lips in disdain. \"What? Don't look at me like that. It's creepy.\"","\"Besides, I'm not going to live like this forever. I've already thought it through. In another ten years or so, once Wanlonghui is completely stable, I'll retire and start enjoying life.\"","Gao Min was taken aback. \"Ten years? You'd be, what, thirty at most? Isn't that too early?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Early? I think it's perfect.\"","\"At thirty, while I still have energy, I'll first travel around the world and hit all the places I want to go. After that, I'll buy a big house in the most scenic spot in China, keep a few big dogs, wake up naturally every day, and do whatever I want.\"","\"Doesn't that sound great?\"","Gao Min, listening to her paint that picture of the future, was also filled with longing. \"It does sound nice, but are you sure you can stand being idle?\"","Liu Yutong asked, \"What do you mean?\"","Gao Min laughed. \"I know you too well. With your personality, if you actually had to slow down, you'd go stir-crazy. I bet you'd come up with some new scheme to keep yourself busy.\"","Liu Yutong thought about it seriously and nodded. \"You have a point. Maybe when I have so much money I can't spend it all, I'll try building rockets. I want to fly to Mars on one I made myself while I'm still alive.\"","Gao Min was stunned for a second, then burst into laughter, nearly doubling over. \"Mars? You're serious? Don't kid me. If you could actually build a rocket that flies to Mars, count me in!\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Really? Don't go back on your word!\"","Gao Min replied, \"Of course! We're sisters after all. Sisters stay together through thick and thin—we go to heaven and earth together.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Then it's settled. Tomorrow I'll have someone register an aerospace technology company first.\"","\"When the time comes, the two of us will go up there together and be neighbors on Mars. You can keep being a cop, and specialize in arresting aliens on Mars, while I'll build houses next door and be a Martian real estate developer collecting rent from the extraterrestrials.\"","Gao Min laughed uncontrollably. \"Haha... I've got to say, I'm actually looking forward to that day.\"","Of course, even as she laughed, she just thought Liu Yutong was joking.","What she didn't know was that Liu Yutong had already started thinking seriously about it.","Retiring at thirty had always been her plan, since her precognitive ability only extended about ten or fifteen years into the future. By then, Wanlonghui should be stable and running normally.","Most importantly, by that time she would definitely have a huge amount of money—more than she could spend. With nothing else to do, she might as well look into rockets and race those foreigners to see who gets to Mars first.","Of course, building rockets in China would require policy support. She'd still have to report to the higher-ups.","Once Gao Min had finished laughing, she looked at her sister and said with sudden emotion, \"Honestly, sometimes I feel like you're not really my sister.\"","Liu Yutong asked, \"Then what do I look like?\"","Gao Min thought for a moment and said, \"Like... someone who traveled back in time from the future.\"","\"You know everything, can do everything, and calculate everything so clearly, as if all things are within your predictions. You can even dodge risks that haven't happened yet. This feeling... it's just not real.\"","Liu Yutong was silent for a few seconds, then she smiled too.","\"Maybe it's real.\""]},{"number":738,"title":"Chapter 738: 739. Arriving in the Imperial Capital Again","paragraphs":["Two days later, at the Imperial Capital International Airport.","As Liu Yutong stepped off the aerobridge, a warm breeze swept toward her, gently lifting the stray hairs on her forehead.","She had deliberately chosen a light apricot-colored cotton and linen dress today, the hem falling just above her knees, revealing a section of fair and slender calves. A thin belt in the same shade cinched her waist, accentuating her delicate figure, and she wore a pair of white canvas shoes.","Her makeup was minimal—just a touch of clear lip gloss and a faint hint of blush. She looked fresh and understated.","But her face was simply too beautiful.","So beautiful that it was hard to look away.","Her beauty was like a gardenia flower damp with morning dew.","Beside her, Gao Min was dressed in a light blue cotton shirt, sleeves casually rolled to her elbows, revealing toned forearms. She paired it with a slim-fit pair of dark blue jeans, her shoulder-length hair tucked behind her ears, radiating a sharp, confident air.","Standing together, the two of them looked like a pair of enviable sisters.","“Miss, the Lin family’s welcoming party has arrived at the airport.”","“Quite a few people. Besides Lin Feng, there are several young men and women—looks like the younger generation of the Lin family. They seem to have come specifically to... see Miss Gao.” Yun Cheng had left the terminal early and reported the situation by phone.","Hearing this, a playful smile curled at the corner of Liu Yutong’s mouth.","“Come to see my sister? That’s fine. Let me take a good look at these children of the Imperial Capital’s noble families and see what they’re really made of.”","Gao Min looked a little worried. “Sis, you’d better...”","“Don’t worry. Although I’m playing your best friend today, here to broaden my horizons with you, if they try any tricks in front of me, they’re not up to par.”","“You don’t need to worry about me.”","Gao Min opened her mouth, but what she really wanted to say was: I’m not worried about you, sis—I’m worried about them.","Having spent so long in Pearl City, she knew her younger sister’s capabilities too well.","If those arrogant young masters from noble families thought Liu Yutong was just some naive country girl to be bullied, they wouldn’t even know how they died.","She just wanted to remind her sister not to go too far.","“Let’s go.”","They headed toward the exit.","From afar, Liu Yutong spotted the group waiting at the arrival gate.","Lin Feng stood at the front, wearing a white T-shirt under a light gray thin jacket. His hair was neatly styled, giving him a slightly handsome look.","Behind him stood four young men and women—three men and one woman, all dressed in stylish clothes with haughty expressions, whispering among themselves and occasionally glancing toward the arrivals area.","“Lin Feng!”","Gao Min raised her hand first.","Lin Feng hurried over. “Sister Min, Tongtong, you’re here. Uh... my parents asked me to pick you up, and I brought a few cousins along. They said... they wanted to get to know you both.”","Liu Yutong looked at him with an amused smile. “Get to know us? Or are they here to see what we look like?”","Lin Feng: “...”","He opened his mouth, trying to explain, but didn’t know what to say.","Because Liu Yutong was right.","This morning, those Lin family members had insisted on coming to pick them up. Fourth Aunt Wang Jiangyao said something about “since she’s Jiang Lu’s daughter, we Lin family members need to show sincerity,” but in the end, she didn’t come herself and instead sent all the younger generation.","She even told them specifically: “Take a good look and see just what kind of goods that girl really is.”","Lin Feng had wanted to curse right then.","What kind of goods?","She was the descendant of a martyr and a first-level police superintendent—a hundred times better than these useless partygoers!","But he couldn’t say that out loud.","After all, they were his elders, and he didn’t want to create an awkward situation right from the start.","“Let’s go. Don’t just stand here.” Liu Yutong walked straight ahead.","When those four saw Liu Yutong, their expressions shifted.","Especially the three young men. Their gazes lingered on Liu Yutong for several seconds, undisguised admiration flickering in their eyes.","This girl... was she really that beautiful?","Her outfit looked ordinary, not any famous brand, but her face and her aura were simply unmatched.","Even at the Imperial Capital Film Academy, where beauties were everywhere, it would be hard to find a girl with such an ethereal temperament.","Lin Feng unconsciously swallowed, his eyes slightly dazed.","The eldest, Lin Shen, quickly withdrew his gaze, pushed up his glasses, and put on a warm smile.","As for Lin Yue, the moment she saw Liu Yutong, a hint of hostility rose in her—this girl was stealing the spotlight a bit too much.","But seeing her simple outfit, Lin Yue figured her whole look probably cost less than a thousand yuan.","A country bumpkin.","That’s what she thought, but her face bloomed with an enthusiastic smile as she quickly stepped up and naturally took Gao Min’s arm.","“Sister Min, right? I’m Lin Yue. We’re about the same age, just call me Yueyue!”","“I’ve been so excited since I heard you were coming. You must have had a tiring journey, right? It’s been a bit hot in the Imperial Capital these past two days. How about I take you shopping for some cooler clothes later? I know a few stores at the International Trade Center that would really suit you...”","She chattered on without stopping, her warmth as if they were long-lost sisters.","But her eyes secretly scanned Gao Min’s clothes, and when she saw she was also wearing ordinary street-market stuff, a barely noticeable sneer flickered in her gaze.","Gao Min, uncomfortable with such excessive enthusiasm, declined. “Thanks, but no need. I brought a few changes of clothes.”","“Sister Min, we’re all family now, why be so polite with me?”","Then Lin Yue pointed at Liu Yutong. “Oh, and who’s this?”","Up close, the girl was even more beautiful.","Too beautiful.","An inexplicable discomfort welled up in Lin Yue’s heart.","She had grown up as the jewel of this generation in the Lin family. Pretty enough, she was always the center of attention wherever she went.","But now, with this girl standing there, everyone’s eyes turned to her.","Why should they?","Some country girl from who knows where—what right did she have to steal her spotlight?","“She’s my... well, my best friend. She happened to be coming to the Imperial Capital for fun, so I asked her to keep me company for a few days,” Gao Min explained.","Though a bit jealous of Liu Yutong’s looks, Lin Yue still extended a hand with a bright smile. “Welcome, welcome! Since you’re Sister Min’s friend, you’re a friend of the Lin family too! Later, let’s hang out together—my treat! First time in the Imperial Capital, right? You’ve got to have some fun!”","Liu Yutong shook her hand, her tone neither warm nor cold. “Liu Yutong.”","The other three also gathered around.","Lin Shen introduced himself first, maintaining a proper demeanor. “Xiao Min, I’m Lin Shen, your eldest cousin. My father is your second uncle. We’ve heard you were coming, and it’s great to finally meet you. You must have had a tiring journey.”","“Hello, Brother Lin Shen,” Gao Min replied politely.","Lin Shen gave Liu Yutong a brief nod as a form of greeting, his eyes lingering on her face for a moment before looking away.","Lin Feng kept his hands in his pockets, all nonchalant and cocky, his eyes constantly drifting toward Liu Yutong, a smirk playing at his lips as if he thought he looked charming.","“Hey there, beauty. I’m Lin Feng,” he said.","Liu Yutong took one look at his slick, borderline aggressive attitude and decided to ignore him.","Lin Feng’s smile faltered, a flicker of awkwardness and irritation flashing in his eyes.","The last boy stepped forward. He looked the youngest—maybe eighteen or nineteen—his face still carrying a hint of innocence, his eyes clear and honest.","“Hi, Sister Min... I’m Lin Mian.”","He greeted her a bit shyly, then glanced quickly at Liu Yutong and whispered, “Hello, miss.”","His voice was soft, a touch embarrassed.","Liu Yutong’s gaze lingered on his face for a moment longer before she nodded at him.","This kid was a bit interesting, much more pleasant than the others.","After Gao Min exchanged all the polite formalities with them, she walked back toward the car.","“Come on, come on! The car’s waiting outside!”","Lin Yue immediately latched onto Gao Min’s arm, bubbling with enthusiasm.","“Sister Min Min, let me tell you, there are so many fun places in the capital! Wangfujing, Sanlitun, Houhai... and that new shopping mall. In the next few days, I’ll take you out to see the sights, show you what real metropolitan life is all about...”","She paused, then threw a pointed glance at Liu Yutong. “And this best friend of yours, she’s coming too. First time in the capital, right? She’s got to open her eyes wide and soak it in—wouldn’t want her going back without seeing anything.”","Liu Yutong gave a faint smile. “Sure, thanks for the trouble.”","That calm smile unsettled Lin Yue more than she’d like to admit.","What was up with this small-town girl? No reaction at all?","By all rights, a first-time visitor to the capital like her should be thrilled to be greeted so warmly by the Lin family. Shouldn’t she be overwhelmed?","But this girl’s face showed nothing.","Fine. Maybe she hadn’t cottoned on yet, or maybe she was just pretending to be cool.","Once they reached those places, there’d be plenty of chances to open her eyes."]},{"number":739,"title":"Chapter 739: 740, Playing the Pig to Eat the Tiger","paragraphs":["A group of people arrived at the pickup point.","Lin Yue pulled Gao Min straight toward a brand-new Porsche. \"Sister Min, ride in this car. Big Brother just got it, and now it's mine to drive. We can chat along the way, and I'll tell you about all the fun places in the Imperial Capital!\"","Gao Min instinctively glanced back at Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong gave a slight nod, signaling her to go ahead without worry.","So, Gao Min was pulled into the Porsche by Lin Yue, while Liu Yutong was naturally arranged into the family minivan behind.","In the van, besides the driver Lin Feng, there were Lin Shen, Lin Feng, and Lin Mian—three male members of the Lin family.","Lin Feng and Lin Mian sat in the back row, while Lin Shen and Liu Yutong occupied the two seats in the middle row.","Once the van started moving, Lin Feng couldn't hold back. He leaned over the seatback, grinning at Liu Yutong.","\"Miss Liu, first time in the Imperial Capital?\"","Liu Yutong gave a faint \"mm-hmm,\" clearly not wanting to engage with him.","Lin Feng, thick-skinned as ever, pressed on enthusiastically: \"Then you've got to look around properly! The Imperial Capital is huge, with tons of great places to visit. The Four-Nine City has countless historical sites. How about I act as your guide these next few days? I promise you'll have a blast!\"","Liu Yutong finally turned her head and looked at him.","\"Do you know what you look like right now?\"","Lin Feng was startled. \"What do I look like?\"","Liu Yutong: \"A dog.\"","Lin Feng's face darkened instantly. \"You—\"","But before he could finish, Liu Yutong leaned back in her seat and closed her eyes.","Lin Feng's curse got stuck in his throat, his face flushed red.","Lin Shen adjusted his glasses, the corner of his mouth twitching as if stifling a laugh. He cleared his throat to smooth things over. \"Miss Liu, don't mind him. My younger brother is just a bit overenthusiastic, no harm meant. By the way, Miss Liu, what kind of work do you do in Pearl City?\"","\"Just a small business,\" Liu Yutong reopened her eyes.","\"Oh, running a business—that's good. How's the economic development over in Pearl City?\"","\"It's alright.\"","Lin Feng, perhaps trying to save face after hearing her tepid reply, leaned in again with a sense of superiority. \"'Alright'—what kind of standard is that? Can it compare to our Imperial Capital? The GDP of any single district here beats an entire city like yours, right?\"","Liu Yutong didn't turn her head. \"It can't compare.\"","Lin Feng smirked smugly. \"Of course. A small place like yours is far off from our Imperial Capital. But that's normal—this is the Four-Nine City, after all.\"","Lin Mian, sitting in the back row, couldn't help muttering quietly, \"Second Brother, don't say that...\"","Lin Feng spun around and glared at him. \"Did I say anything wrong? It's the truth; what's wrong with saying it?\"","He turned back to Liu Yutong. \"But, to be fair, small cities have their perks—slower pace of life, fresher air, less stress. When I have time, I'll drop by Pearl City for a visit. Miss Liu, you'll have to be my tour guide then!\"","Liu Yutong: \"You'd better not come. I'm afraid you won't get used to it.\"","Lin Feng scoffed. \"How could that be? Sure, small cities have poorer infrastructure than the Imperial Capital, but I'm not that delicate—I can handle a bit of hardship. Don't worry!\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Well then, when you do come, I'll make sure to have someone take good care of you.\"","Lin Feng didn't catch the hidden meaning in her words and instead nodded eagerly. \"Great, great, it's settled! I'll definitely come another day. Don't get annoyed with me then!\"","Liu Yutong said nothing more, only cursing inwardly: \"You idiot! Just don't come crying and begging me to let you go.\"","About half an hour later,","the van passed through several bustling streets and finally pulled into a quiet old neighborhood, stopping in front of a three-courtyard mansion.","Liu Yutong got out, her gaze sweeping over the property with subtle assessment.","Grey bricks and black tiles, upturned eaves and carved ridges, a pair of stone lions flanking the gate, and gleaming brass studs on the vermilion door.","For the Lin family to own a three-courtyard estate here in the Western Hills of the Imperial Capital—their background was indeed deep.","This estate, put on the market, would be worth at least a hundred million, and even then, it might not be up for sale.","The main hall was a typical Ming and Qing style building: a seven-purlin, hard-peaked roof, with a front veranda and a rear extension. Six large red lanterns hung under the eaves, casting a festive glow over the entire courtyard.","The lacquer on the corridor pillars was deep and shiny, clearly well-maintained.","Inside the hall, rosewood furniture was neatly arranged—purple sandalwood tables and armchairs. Famous calligraphy and paintings adorned the walls, and a curio cabinet displayed a variety of antique ceramics: blue-and-white, famille rose, and several pieces that looked like fine Ming and Qing imperial ware.","Around the central table, several people were seated.","\"Young Master Lin, the young ladies and gentlemen are back.\"","With the steward Uncle Liu's announcement, Lin Feng led Liu Yutong, Gao Min, Lin Shen, and the others into the main hall.","Everyone inside turned their gazes toward them.","At the head of the table sat a woman in her fifties, well-preserved, wearing a dark red embroidered cheongsam and a high-quality jadeite bangle on her wrist. This was Lin Dong’s second sister-in-law, Zhang Yu.","Beside her sat a man in his forties, with gold-rimmed glasses and a dark grey shirt, looking refined—this was Lin Zheng.","On the other armchair sat a heavily made-up woman with big permed curls in a bright yellow dress, holding a cup of black tea, her fingernails painted a vivid red. This was Lin Zheng’s wife, Wang Jiangyao.","As they entered, everyone’s eyes fell on them.","In those gazes, there was curiosity, scrutiny, and superiority—but very little goodwill.","Lin Feng stepped forward to introduce Gao Min. \"Second Aunt, Fourth Uncle, Fourth Aunt, this is Aunt Jiang's daughter, Gao Min.\"","He paused, then gestured to Liu Yutong. \"And this is Sister Min's... good friend, Miss Liu, who came with her to tour the Imperial Capital.\"","Zhang Yu set down her blue-and-white teacup, lifted her eyelids, and sized up Gao Min, her face breaking into a warm smile.","\"Oh my, so this is LuLu’s daughter? Come closer and let Second Aunt have a look.\"","Gao Min stepped forward and bowed slightly. \"Greetings, Second Aunt.\"","Zhang Yu took her hand, inspecting her from all angles, muttering, \"Mm, pretty features, and there’s indeed a bit of LuLu in her brow and eyes. But as for temperament—well, growing up in a small place does leave its mark. There's a certain... wildness, not quite like our girls from the Imperial Capital.\"","The words sounded like praise, but anyone could sense the condescending superiority dripping from them.","Wang Jiangyao picked up the thread, smiling kindly, but her tone was like that of a mentor instructing a junior. \"Second Sister-in-law, don’t say that. It’s her first time in the Imperial Capital—it’s normal not to know the rules. She can learn gradually.\"","\"Minmin, since you're now part of the Lin family, you'll have to follow the Lin family's rules. Later, ask Uncle Liu to explain the family's dos and don'ts: what to wear on what occasion, what to say to whom, how to walk, how to eat, how to serve tea—every little thing has its own proper way. You must study hard and not embarrass Third Sister-in-law. After all, your mother back then... well, let's not go there. Anyway, the more you learn, the better off you'll be.\"","Gao Min said, \"I understand. Thank you for your advice, Fourth Aunt.\"","Then Wang Jiangyao turned to Liu Yutong and asked, \"And what does your friend here do for a living?\"","Gao Min replied, \"My little... um, my best friend runs a small business in Mingzhu City.\"","\"Running a business, is it?\"","\"Someone in business coming to the Imperial Capital—looking for opportunities to grow, I suppose? You should make the most of it. The Imperial Capital isn't like your small-town backwater. There are plenty of opportunities here, but the competition is fierce. Not everyone can find their footing...\"","Wang Jiangyao had already decided in her mind that this girl was just someone who knew Gao Min had latched onto the Lin family and was trying to ride on her coattails. She felt even more contempt. She had seen plenty of these little gold diggers trying to climb the social ladder—the kind that weren't even fit to polish the Lin family's shoes.","As the conversation strayed further and further off-topic, with more and more barbs being thrown, Lin Feng, who was listening on the sidelines, felt his face turn red.","Small business?","The money that woman had could buy up the entire Lin manor and the land it sat on, several times over!","Finally, he couldn't take it anymore and interrupted their chat. \"Alright, alright. Sister Min and her friend just got off the plane—they must be exhausted from the trip. Let them rest for now. We can talk more later.\"","Wang Jiangyao said, \"Xiaofeng is right. Minmin and Miss Liu, please go upstairs and rest. Oh, Uncle Liu, have the rooms for them been prepared?\"","The butler, Uncle Liu, stepped forward and bowed slightly. \"Yes, Fourth Mistress. The rooms are ready, in the guest rooms at the back courtyard.\"","\"This way, please, young ladies.\"","Uncle Liu gestured and led the two of them through a long corridor. On both sides of the corridor were a few side rooms. They passed a decorative gate and finally arrived at a row of single-story houses in the back courtyard.","This area was clearly much more remote and shabby than the main courtyard.","Then Uncle Liu pushed open a door. The room inside was clean and tidy, with a double bed, a simple sofa set, a wardrobe, and a small bathroom. Compared to what ordinary people had, the conditions were actually quite decent.","But in a grand household like the Lin family's, it was very humble.","The butler offered no explanation, just said with a smile, \"Young ladies, please get some rest. Dinner will start at half past six. Someone will come to fetch you then.\"","With that, he left.","After Liu Yutong looked around the room and its furnishings, she suddenly laughed.","She could tell at a glance that this wasn't a guest room at all—it was clearly a servant's quarters, and a double-occupancy one at that.","\"Sister, the Lin family really does treat us like a couple of country bumpkins. They've put us in the maid's room, and a shared one at that.\"","Gao Min's expression didn't look too good either. She didn't care about material comforts, but this obvious insult made her uncomfortable. \"This is bullying. Maybe I should talk to Uncle Lin...\"","Liu Yutong waved her hand. \"No need. This is fine. They look down on you because they think you're from the countryside—naive and easy to push around. Just wait until they realize you're not what they imagined. That'll be interesting.\"","When Gao Min heard this, she could guess what her sister was up to. She couldn't help but say, \"You really are a schemer. Speaking of which, are you really going to keep using the identity of my best friend? You're not going to tell them who you really are?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"I told you, I'm here to keep you company. You came back to the Lin family to reconnect with your relatives, and I'm just tagging along. That's all.\"","\"Besides, if I gave away my identity, it would be boring.\"","\"I want to see what kind of tricks these young masters and ladies of the Imperial Capital are capable of.\"","Gao Min looked at her sister, who wore that effortless, carefree expression, and suddenly felt a bit sorry for the Lin family.","Who could have known that her own little sister had such an odd habit of playing the fool to catch the wise!"]},{"number":740,"title":"Chapter 740: 741, A Small Dining Incident.","paragraphs":["Half past six in the evening.","The main hall of the Lin family was brightly lit. The usual square table had been removed and replaced by a massive long table, bedecked with a dozen or so cold appetizers and hot dishes, steaming and fragrant.","Lin Dong, his second brother, and his wife Jiang Lu hadn't returned yet. Rumor had it they were off preparing a birthday gift for the Jiang family matriarch and wouldn't be back until later.","Zhang Yu sat rightfully at the head of the table, with Wang Jiangyao beside her. On the other side sat Lin Zheng.","The younger generation—Lin Shen, Lin Feng, Lin Feng (the third), Lin Yue, and Lin Mian—took their seats in order.","As for Gao Min and Liu Yutong...","They were relegated to the very back, the farthest corner seats. The kind of spots where you'd have to stretch your arm to its limit just to reach the main dishes, and had to stand up and walk over if you wanted to snag something from the other end.","\"Little Min, don't mind us,\" Wang Jiangyao said with a syrupy smile. \"Our family's big—the head seats are for the elders. You young folks should sit on the side, where it's livelier and easier to grab food.\"","The words sounded pleasant enough, but the underlying meaning was clear to everyone present.","You two are outsiders at the end of the day. Even being allowed at the table is an honor.","Gao Min nodded without a word. She'd been prepared for this.","But Liu Yutong? She was a different story. The moment her backside hit the chair, she didn't even look up. She just pulled out her phone and started fiddling with it, apparently texting someone.","The smile on Wang Jiangyao's face froze for a split second.","This uncouth country girl—didn't she have any basic manners at all?","Eating while on her phone, and when an elder hadn't even finished speaking!","\"Ahem.\"","Zhang Yu cleared her throat, striking a senior's authoritative pose. \"Since everyone's here, let's start the meal. By the way, Minmin, since this is your first time at the Lin residence, there are some rules your second aunt needs to tell you.\"","Gao Min set down her chopsticks and looked up at her, expression earnest.","\"Although the Lin family may not rival the top-tier rich clans, we're still a family of several generations' standing. We value order—elders before juniors. At the table, elders must eat first; juniors must never pick up their chopsticks before. You can't rummage through the dishes, can't stand up to reach food from afar, can't tap your chopsticks or bowl, and definitely can't slurp your soup... Got all those basic manners?\"","Gao Min: \"Got it, Second Aunt.\"","Zhang Yu nodded with satisfaction, then finally picked up her own chopsticks, helped herself to a bite of stir-fried greens, and began to eat.","Only after she started did the others reach for their chopsticks.","Wang Jiangyao picked up a piece of braised pork belly. Suddenly, as if reminded of something, she turned her head toward Liu Yutong in the corner.","\"By the way, Miss Liu, you're our guest—don't be shy. Help yourself to whatever you'd like. Make yourself at home.\"","Liu Yutong didn't even lift her head, just grunted an \"Mm.\"","Wang Jiangyao: \"...\"","How come it felt like this girl was brushing her off like a beggar?","Whatever. A small-town gal—no breeding, no manners. Not worth arguing with.","Elsewhere at the table.","Lin Yue, on the other hand, was warm-hearted. She used her chopsticks to pick up a piece of squirrel-shaped mandarin fish and placed it in Gao Min's bowl. \"Sister Min, try this. It's our chef's specialty—you won't find many places in the capital that can match it.\"","Gao Min looked up and smiled. \"Thanks.\"","Lin Yue then put a piece into Liu Yutong's bowl. \"Miss Liu, you should try it too. It's delicious.\"","Finally, Liu Yutong lifted her head.","She glanced at Lin Yue, then looked down at the piece of fish glazed in sauce in her bowl.","She paused for two seconds.","\"I don't eat food served by other people's chopsticks.\"","Lin Yue: \"Huh?\"","Liu Yutong picked up the serving chopsticks and, with a blank face, moved the fish to the side plate. \"Unhygienic.\"","\"... \"","The entire table stared at one another, the atmosphere dropping into an abyss of awkwardness.","Lin Yue's smile collapsed visibly. Her eyes reddened almost immediately, and she looked at her mother, Zhang Yu, with a pained, aggrieved expression.","Zhang Yu furrowed her brows and slammed her chopsticks down. \"Miss Liu, what's the meaning of this? Yueyue was being kind, serving you food. And you reject it publicly like this? That's just cruel!\"","Liu Yutong: \"I didn't ask her to serve me.\"","Zhang Yu: \"You—\"","Wang Jiangyao quickly stepped in to smooth things over. \"Oh, Second Sister-in-law, forget it, forget it. Calm down. Miss Liu is a first-time guest—she doesn't know our customs yet. It's understandable.\"","Then she turned to Gao Min, speaking with clear innuendo. \"Minmin, you'll have to teach Miss Liu properly when you get back. After all, if she's going to mingle with us in the future, being clueless about manners... People might think the Lin family's guests are utterly uncivilized.\"","Liu Yutong cast a glance at Wang Jiangyao and suddenly broke into a smile.","\"Auntie Wang, you're trying to say I'm uncivilized, aren't you? No need to beat around the bush. You could have just said it to my face.\"","\"Also, I heard someone earlier recite the Lin family's dining rules—don't pick and choose, keep it quiet, be refined. But I couldn't help noticing how you went digging through that kung pao chicken dish just now. Seven or eight times, at least, just to fish out a few peanuts.\"","Wang Jiangyao's smile instantly curdled.","\"And that bird's nest soup you were sipping? The slurping sound was so loud, I bet the neighbors could hear it. Anyone listening would think there was a pig farm running in the Lin residence.\"","\"Pfft!\"","Lin Feng nearly spewed the rice out of his mouth. He ducked his head, desperately covering his mouth, his shoulders shaking violently and his face turning red.","Lin Shen pushed up his glasses, the corner of his mouth twitching.","The other young members also lowered their heads.","Wang Jiangyao's face had turned the color of liver.","\"You... Who are you calling a pig?!\"","She—a country bumpkin—had just insulted her to her face!","Second sister-in-law Zhang Yu's face darkened as well. She slammed the table. \"Miss Liu, you've gone too far! If it weren't for the fact that Minmin is here for her first visit, I'd have the servants throw you out already!\"","Liu Yutong turned to Zhang Yu, her expression the picture of innocence.","\"Auntie Zhang, why are you saying that? I never called anyone a pig. I just made an innocent little analogy.\"","\"You were just teaching Minmin the rules—'Don't rummage through the dishes,' 'Don't slurp your soup.' I thought those were sacred commandments of the Lin family. Then I looked over and saw Auntie Wang rummaging away happily and slurping up her soup like a drain, albeit a bit louder than usual. So I thought to myself... Huh? Are the rules at the Lin family selective? Elders can break them, but the youngsters can't? Or are these rules just a show for outsiders?\"","\"You—\"","Zhang Yu was left speechless by the barrage of questions.","Just then, Lin Zheng, who was getting a headache from the commotion, spoke up.","\"Alright, alright, that's enough. Miss Liu is a guest. As hosts, we should be warm and welcoming. No need to sour the mood over a trivial matter.\"","Liu Yutong immediately nodded. \"Fourth Uncle Lin is absolutely right. I'm a guest—guests don't know the rules, it's natural. You hosts should be a little more understanding, don't you think?\"","And with that, she fixed her gaze on the massive king crab sitting at the center of the table.","\"Oh, that king crab is too far away for me to reach. Lin Feng, you're sitting close. Could you please pass it over here? As a guest, I get priority.\"","Lin Feng: \"...\"","He froze for a moment, taking in Liu Yutong’s utterly self-assured expression, then glanced at the ashen faces of the older relatives around him.","In the end, he reluctantly stood up, moved the plate of king crab to a different spot, and placed it directly in front of Liu Yutong.","Then, amid the heavy silence of the Lin family, he watched as this utterly unorthodox young woman pulled on gloves and, as if no one else were there, began to dig in with gusto.","She ate with pure relish, crab meat dripping with sauce, bite after bite—and of course, she didn’t forget to stuff some into her sister Gao Min’s mouth.","Every single member of the Lin family fell silent.","And yet, she kept muttering, “I’m just a guest, I don’t know the rules,” lowering her posture so much that no one could find a pretext to lose their temper.","They couldn’t exactly throw her out, could they?","But that meal certainly opened their eyes.","In all their years, this was the first time they had met someone with such thick skin, the first time they had seen a guest behave this way.","Originally, they had planned to use this chance to lay down the law and put Gao Min in her place.","But now, with Liu Yutong stirring things up like this, everyone had lost their appetite. They no longer had any mood to lecture Gao Min."]},{"number":741,"title":"Chapter 741: 742, Having Designs on Liu Yutong","paragraphs":["The dinner ended on a sour note.","To be precise, it was sour for the Lin family members alone—Liu Yutong had a great time eating.","She devoured most of a king crab, downed two bowls of matsutake chicken soup, and finally wiped her mouth, saying with satisfaction: \"The Lins' chef really knows his stuff. That money wasn't wasted.\"","Lin Feng's face was practically green.","Sis, were you actually complimenting the chef? You were clearly implying that aside from the chef, the Lin family had nothing else worth showing off.","But he couldn't say a thing. This little madam seemed to be doing it on purpose.","The older relatives left one by one, their faces dark.","Of course, they were determined to have a serious word with Lin Dong when he got back—he shouldn't bring just any riffraff into the house. Where were the manners?","The remaining younger generation exchanged awkward glances.","Finally, Lin Shen cleared his throat, breaking the silence: \"Um... Yueyue, didn't you say earlier you wanted to take Minmin and the others out for a look around?\"","Lin Yue's eyes lit up.","Right!","At home, with the elders around, she couldn't do much.","But outside, on her own turf, she was sure she could deal with that country bumpkin.","She immediately put on a fake, overly warm smile and hooked her arm around Gao Min's: \"Minmin, you're free tonight, right? I'll take you to a great place. The capital isn't just about the Forbidden City and the Great Wall—the nightlife is the real highlight. I guarantee you and your bestie will have your eyes opened!\"","Gao Min instinctively looked at Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong yawned: \"Whatever, I can't sleep anyway.\"","Lin Yue sneered inwardly: Can't sleep? Just wait—you'll have plenty to keep you awake tonight!","\"Then let's go. Afeng, come with us!\"","Lin Feng, always eager for an outing, flocked over like a cat smelling fish: \"Miss Liu, I'll show you some things you don't get to see every day!\"","Liu Yutong looked at him with a half-smile: \"Sure, then I'll trouble you, Master Lin.\"","Lin Feng felt his bones go weak at that look, his soul almost fleeing his body, completely missing the hidden meaning behind her smile.","Lin Feng opened his mouth to say something, but Lin Shen pulled him aside: \"Lin Feng, you stay home. Keep Uncle and Aunt company—they'll be back soon.\"","Lin Feng: \"But...\"","Lin Shen patted his shoulder: \"Don't worry. We'll be there. Nothing'll go wrong.\"","Lin Feng thought to himself: That's exactly what I'm worried about—things going wrong because she's there!","But Lin Shen had already shut him down, firmly pushing him back into his chair.","As the black van drove out of the Lin family's gate, an uneasy feeling stirred in Lin Feng's gut—a sense that something major was about to happen tonight.","......","The van cut through the neon-lit streets, finally stopping at the entrance of a quiet lane.","The lane was narrow, flanked by old, mottled gray-walled, black-tiled buildings. The cobblestone path glistened faintly under the ground lights.","At the lane's mouth stood an inconspicuous wooden sign carved with two ancient, bold characters—[Yun Lu].","No neon signs, no advertisements, no greeters at the door—just two yellow lanterns hanging under the eaves, swaying gently in the wind, exuding an air of mysterious sophistication.","Lin Yue pushed open the van door, casting a smug glance at Liu Yutong: \"We're here.\"","Gao Min looked at the surroundings and frowned slightly: \"Where is this?\"","\"One of the capital's top private clubs—members only. Without an introduction from an acquaintance, you can't get in even with money.\"","\"Minmin, let me show you what real high society looks like. This isn't a place where just any stray cat or dog can sneak in.\"","As she said this, Lin Yue swept a condescending gaze over Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong stepped out of the van, her eyes skimming over the narrow door. A barely perceptible smile curled at the corner of her lips.","Stray cat or dog?","Interesting.","The group passed through the narrow door, and the view suddenly opened up.","Inside was a completely different world.","It was a standard three-courtyard siheyuan, with carved beams and painted rafters, brightly lit. A stream of living water wound through the yard, adorned with exquisite rockeries. The babbling water instantly drowned out the noise of the outside world.","Beneath the eaves stood several young women in designer qipaos, each with a slender figure and delicate makeup, wearing precisely calibrated professional smiles. They bowed in unison as the guests entered.","\"Miss Lin is here!\"","A middle-aged man in a deep gray long gown quickly approached, his smile perfectly appropriate: \"Miss Lin, your usual room, 'Rain Listening Pavilion,' is still empty. You distinguished guests, please come in!\"","Lin Yue basked in this star-studded treatment, glancing triumphantly at Liu Yutong, as if to say: See this? This is Miss Lin giving you a taste of status.","Liu Yutong followed inside without expression.","The private room was spacious, exuding an antique charm.","At the center stood a massive round table of yellow rosewood, adorned with delicate pastries and fresh fruit. Against the wall was a set of red sandalwood sofas, and the walls were hung with several well-aged calligraphy paintings from famous figures. The air was thick with the faint scent of agarwood.","Lin Yue sat down in the main seat without ceremony, casually tossing her bag onto the table: \"The usual. Start with a bottle of Louis XIII, then bring out a few of your signature dishes.\"","The middle-aged man smiled warmly as he answered: \"Coming right up,\" and then bowed as he withdrew.","Only then did Lin Yue look at Liu Yutong: \"Miss Liu, first time in a place like this, right?\"","Liu Yutong picked up the celadon teacup, took a sip, and nodded: \"Mm.\"","Lin Yue grew even more smug. Leaning back, she said: \"Don't be nervous. Think of this as your own home. The capital isn't like your little town—here, it's all about circles and status. Just setting foot in Yun Lu is a symbol of identity in itself. Do you know the annual membership fee here?\"","Liu Yutong: \"How much?\"","Lin Yue held up one hand, fingers spread wide: \"Five hundred thousand. And that's just for a basic membership. For a family like ours with a reserved room, it's at least two million a year.\"","\"Two million—enough to buy quite a decent apartment in a place like Mingzhu City, right?\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"Mm.\"","Lin Yue waited for a long while, only to get another \"Mm\"?","She frowned, irritation brewing inside her.","Was this country girl not right in the head? Couldn't she understand plain speech, or was she just stunned into numbness? Why no reaction at all? Even a hint of envy or inferiority would do!","Lin Feng leaned in, unable to resist showing off: \"Miss Liu, you might not really grasp what two million means.\"","He pointed to Liu Yutong's clothes: \"Let me put it this way—everything you're wearing now costs less than a thousand, right? Two million would buy you two thousand sets of these clothes. Wearing a different one every day, you wouldn't repeat for six or seven years.\"","Liu Yutong looked down at her outfit, then lifted her gaze to him: \"So?\"","Lin Feng choked. He opened his mouth but couldn't find the words.","This girl just wouldn't follow the script!","Anyone listening would think he was the country bumpkin here!","Lin Yue shot him a dirty look, thinking her cousin was useless—and also disgusted by how much he was groveling.","So she stopped beating around the bush.","Getting straight to the point, she said to Liu Yutong, “Miss Liu, to be honest, with looks like yours, you must be pretty popular back in that little hometown of yours, right?”","Liu Yutong looked up at her.","Lin Yue smiled meaningfully. “Don’t get me wrong—I mean it as a compliment. You’re beautiful. But here’s the thing: beauty is an asset in a small town. In the capital, though... it’s just average. You know what the capital never runs out of? Beautiful women.”","She extended a finger and tapped the air. “The Film Academy, the Central Academy of Drama, all kinds of art schools—thousands of beautiful women come out every year. Every single one is young, pretty, has a great figure, and knows how to play the game. Someone like you, from out of town, with no connections and no resources, trying to make a name for yourself here? Good luck with that.”","With that, Lin Yue took a sip from her glass, her gaze becoming bolder and more unbridled.","“But don’t lose heart. You’re lucky you ran into me today. Since you’re Sister Min’s close friend, I can give you a hand.”","On hearing this, Liu Yutong finally understood why Lin Yue had been so generous with the invitation.","So that was her angle.","She was trying to use her as a gift to curry favor with some ‘big shot,’ wasn’t she?","Liu Tong looked at Lin Yue’s smug face and sneered inwardly.","Interesting. Very interesting indeed.","..."]},{"number":742,"title":"Chapter 742: 743, Want to Join the Cloud Mountain Gathering","paragraphs":["“Miss Liu, don’t take offense at what we’re saying. That’s just how society works—different levels see things differently. You being able to come here today is me, Lin Yue, doing you a favor. Under normal circumstances, someone like you, from out of town, probably wouldn’t even get past the front door.” Lin Yue’s tone still carried that air of superiority.","Gao Min frowned and couldn’t help speaking up: “Yueyue, Liu Yutong is my... friend. She’s just visiting the capital for sightseeing and doesn’t need any help. Thanks for your kindness, though.”","Lin Yue glanced at Gao Min, a flicker of disdain in her eyes, though she kept a fake smile on her lips: “Min Min, I’m only thinking about what’s best for Miss Liu. Think about it—running a small business in Pearl City, when’s she ever going to get ahead? There are so many opportunities in the capital. If she can get to know a few important people, she could strike it rich and make a real name for herself, wouldn’t that be much better than struggling in some small town?”","With that, she deliberately sized up Liu Yutong: “There’s an important guest coming later—a real big shot in the capital. Zhou Heng. You know the Zhou family, right? True aristocracy in the capital, a step above even our Lin family.”","“If you can just get in good with Mr. Zhou, forget about making a name for yourself here—even if you want to open a shop or start a business, one word from him, and the funds and connections will all be arranged for you, plain and simple.”","Her words were extremely blunt, clearly treating Liu Yutong as someone to cling to the powerful or, worse, as a gift.","Liu Yutong thought to herself: The Lin family really is beyond saving. Even the younger generation is already playing matchmaker.","“Miss Lin, are you saying you want me to be a drinking companion?” Liu Yutong asked.","Lin Yue waved dismissively: “Oh, don’t put it so harshly. What do you mean, a drinking companion? It’s just making a friend, getting acquainted. Mr. Zhou is a very nice guy and generous, too. If you stick with him, you’ll have someone to look out for you in the capital.”","Liu Yutong: “And if I don’t want to?”","Lin Yue’s smile stiffened slightly before returning to normal, but her eyes turned colder.","“Miss Liu, you better think this through. This kind of opportunity doesn’t come along often. Do you know how many women line up just for a chance to get close to Mr. Zhou? And he doesn’t even give them a second glance. Today, it’s only out of respect for me that he’s willing to meet you. If you pass this up, you’ll never get a chance like this again for the rest of your life.”","Lin Feng, seeing her unmoved, couldn’t help chiming in: “Miss Liu, my sister really means well. Mr. Zhou is a good guy. Getting to know him can only help you, not hurt. Besides, it’s just a few drinks—it’s not like you’re losing a piece of meat. Why are you being so stubborn?”","Liu Yutong turned to look at Lin Feng.","“What did you just say?”","Lin Feng felt a strange knot in his stomach under her gaze but still forced himself: “I said... isn’t it just a few drinks?”","Liu Yutong: “Mr. Lin, how old are you?”","Lin Feng blinked: “Twenty-three. Why?”","Liu Yutong: “Twenty-three, and still this clueless—that’s quite a feat.”","“Your sister wants me to be a drinking companion, and instead of stopping her, you egg her on. What, is this how the Lin family raises its kids—by pushing guests into a trap?”","Lin Feng’s face flushed red, and he pointed at her: “You...”","Lin Yue slammed the table and stood up: “Liu Yutong, don’t be ungrateful! I went out of my way to take you out and show you a good time, and instead of being thankful, you’re being petty. Who do you think you are? A wild girl from some backwater. I could snap my fingers and make sure you can’t stay in the capital. Believe me?”","Liu Yutong looked up at her, a hint of amusement and defiance in her eyes.","“Oh? Snap your fingers and make me leave the capital? Go ahead, Miss Lin. Show me.”","“You—!”","Just then, Gao Min jumped up too. “Lin Yue, say that again if you dare!”","Her sudden outburst startled everyone in the room.","Lin Yue’s tone softened immediately: “Min Min, don’t get upset. We were just kidding...”","“Joking? Lin Yue, every word you said just now—what part of that sounded like a joke? Making my... best friend be a drinking companion—is that how the Lin family treats its guests? If that’s what high-class manners look like, then we’d better not go back to the Lin family at all!”","Lin Yue’s face changed, and she quickly put on a placating smile: “Min Min, you’ve misunderstood. Really, it’s just a few drinks and making friends...”","“My sister doesn’t drink with strangers, and she doesn’t need to meet any Mr. Zhou or Mr. Wang. This ends here. We’re leaving now.”","Gao Min grabbed Liu Yutong’s arm to pull her up.","“Hey, hey, don’t go!” Lin Yue rushed forward to block them.","She had been so eager to invite them out because she’d had an ulterior motive all along.","Although this Liu Yutong was clueless about etiquette and spoke irritatingly, there was no denying she had a stunning face.","If she could talk her into having a few drinks with Zhou Heng, she might be able to use that connection to get a foot in the door with the Cloud Mountain Circle.","This all went back to her older brother, Lin Shen.","As the eldest grandson of the Lin family, Lin Shen was unwilling to just coast on the family’s fading glory. In other words, he didn’t want to keep living under their third uncle’s thumb. He was determined to start his own business and investments, make a name for himself, and restore the Lin family’s reputation.","Unfortunately, his capital was limited, and he was a marginal figure in the west side of the capital’s social circle. No one was willing to let him in on their games.","For months, Lin Shen had run around, pulled every connection he could to get projects, only to be brushed off or openly humiliated. He couldn’t secure a single decent investment deal.","Just when he was about to give up, he happened to hear about the Cloud Mountain Circle.","The Cloud Mountain Circle was a secret group formed by top-tier wealthy heirs from the central-southern region. They kept a very low profile and rarely interacted with outsiders.","The group’s existence wasn’t unusual—both the capital and places like Magic City had their own circles; it was normal.","What really put the Cloud Mountain Circle on the map was their incredible knack for making money."]},{"number":743,"title":"Chapter 743: 744, Young Master Zhou.","paragraphs":["It was said that the Cloud Mountain Society had been established for only about a year, yet the capital under its control had grown from zero to over sixty billion yuan.","Some claimed that the Cloud Mountain Society might become a second Tai Shan Society, but one even younger and more promising, a gathering of second-generation elites like themselves that would outshine their predecessors.","As this talk spread, the reputation of the Cloud Mountain Society grew louder.","For second-generation heirs like Lin Shen, from prominent families, the most scarce resource was high-quality investment opportunities, especially those with clean backgrounds and legitimate origins.","Thus, after the Cloud Mountain Society's astonishing track record became known, its allure for them was immense.","If those second-generation scions from the central and southern regions could make such waves, couldn't he, by joining them, also get a piece of the pie? Or even use resource synergy to catapult himself to the top?","But the entry threshold for the Cloud Mountain Society was also terrifyingly high.","To join, one not only needed a strong family background endorsement but also at least one billion yuan in liquid cash assets as entry capital — and by \"cash,\" they meant exactly that; many so-called billionaires might not even have that much liquid cash.","And that wasn't all. One had to be personally recommended by an existing member, pass a vote by all members, and then undergo a one-year probationary period.","At first, they thought this threshold would be enough to scare people off, but unexpectedly, it made more people flock to it.","In their eyes, the higher the threshold, the more valuable the circle, and the greater its influence.","The Lin family's current wealth could barely scrape together one billion in cash if they squeezed.","As for younger members like Lin Shen and Lin Yue, they couldn't even touch the edges, let alone find a Cloud Mountain Society member to recommend them. The people in the Beijing circles who were truly qualified to join were completely out of their reach socially.","Lin Shen was unwilling to accept this, and Lin Yue was even more so.","She had known for a long time that the Lin family was no longer what it used to be.","When she was a child, attending others' birthday parties, she was a guest of honor; now, when she went, people wouldn't even give her a second glance.","This contrast was harder to bear than poverty.","If only her big brother Lin Shen could join the Cloud Mountain Society, she could escape this awkward situation, break into the truly top-tier second-generation circles in the country, and never have to watch others' expressions again.","It wasn't really surprising that they were so obsessed with the Cloud Mountain Society. Every age group craves a stage to voice their own opinions, and the second-generation heirs were no exception.","They, too, longed to find a platform where they could showcase their own value, and clearly, the Cloud Mountain Society had that quality.","Later, through various channels, Lin Yue learned that the head of the Cloud Mountain Society was Zhu Silin, the daughter of a high-ranking local official, with close ties to the Zhu family in Beijing. She was also the CEO of Cloud Mountain Capital, young, beautiful, and highly capable.","But Lin Yue had also vaguely heard that behind Zhu Silin there was a true mastermind, a mysterious figure who was the real controller of both the Cloud Mountain Society and Cloud Mountain Capital, while Zhu Silin only handled the daily affairs.","As for who that mysterious mastermind was, she didn't yet know his identity, only that he was very low-key.","In short, Lin Yue was well aware that with their current strength, they had no chance of directly contacting the Cloud Mountain Society, let alone joining it.","Just when they were at a loss, Lin Yue thought of Zhou Heng, the young master of the Zhou family.","Zhou Heng, the most favored youngest son of the current Zhou generation, was said to know one of the Cloud Mountain Society's members. She had also heard from Zhou Heng that they were currently raising funds to join, and the money was almost fully collected.","If she could introduce Liu Yutong to him now and make him happy, maybe she could even buy into it and become a peripheral member.","She thought that Liu Yutong, shamelessly following Gao Min to reconnect with the family, was just trying to suck up to the Lin family, wasn't she? So introducing her to a sugar daddy would be even better.","The key point was that this Zhou Heng was also a playboy and a scumbag.","If something happened to Liu Yutong at his hands, it would be her own fault. Who told her to be so arrogant in the Lin family? She deserved it!","Just as Lin Yue was blocking Gao Min and the others from leaving,","a lazy male voice came from the doorway.","\"Oh, so lively? Lin Yue, are you setting up a Hongmen Banquet for me?\"","The newcomer was about twenty-five or twenty-six, wearing a dark gray shirt, with features that could be considered handsome. But his peach-blossom eyes and frivolous mouth immediately marked him as no good.","Zhou Heng, the notorious playboy of the Beijing circle.","Of course, Liu Yutong had never seen this Zhou Heng before, but when she saw the two friends behind him, she froze.","Those two young men were dressed flashily, clearly from the entertainment industry.","The one on the left had silver-gray hair and regular features, but his eyes were shifty, exuding a sense of frivolity.","The one on the right wore a pair of gold-rimmed glasses and looked refined, but the smile at the corner of his mouth seemed fake no matter how you looked at it.","Liu Yutong recognized them.","Good heavens, weren't these those two jerks from her previous life?","In her past life, while scrolling through the news, she had seen reports about them. They were rising stars heavily promoted by a video platform. One was called Chen Xinhuai, and the other, Sun Mo. At the time, they were incredibly popular, with endless endorsements and countless fans.","Then, they were turned in by the mysterious \"Chaoyang citizens.\"","They were involved in selecting girls, group orgies, and drug use — the whole package.","The news had caused a huge uproar, and the boss of the video platform that was promoting them even ended up going to jail along with them.","That platform, in this life, happened to be one of Dragonview's rivals, K-Video.","For some reason, Liu Yutong had a strange feeling again. Could it be that certain events from her past life were about to happen early?","But none of that mattered now.","She turned sideways, leaned close to Gao Min, and whispered, \"Sis, look at those two on the left. The one with the gray hair is Chen Xinhuai, and the one with the glasses is Sun Mo.\"","Gao Min was startled, not understanding why her younger sister was suddenly mentioning this.","Liu Yutong continued, \"Those two have problems, big problems. Later, you can check where they're staying. This is a gift-wrapped opportunity for you.\"","Gao Min's eyes lit up slightly.","She was in the police, and the word \"opportunity\" was the most sensitive to her.","If her sister said so, then those two definitely had problems, and big ones at that.","She nodded subtly, letting her gaze linger on the two men a moment longer, memorizing their faces firmly.","Lin Yue smiled as she stepped forward to greet them: \"Brother Heng, you finally made it. Please, have a seat, have a seat!\"","Zhou Heng swaggered over and plopped himself into the seat of honor. His eyes swept around the private room and finally landed on Gao Min and Liu Yutong.","Then, his eyes lit up.","\"Lin Yue, who are these two?\"","Lin Yue quickly leaned in and murmured a few words.","After hearing what she said, Zhou Heng's gaze paused on Gao Min for a moment, then skipped over her. Her aura was too righteous; she wasn't his type.","Then he stared directly at Liu Yutong.","This girl might be dressed plainly, but her face and temperament were absolutely stunning.","She was even more pure and captivating than the models and entertainers waiting at their community for them to start a party. This contrast kindled his male desire to conquer.","\"Miss Liu, I presume? My name is Zhou Heng, from the Zhou family in the imperial capital. Lin Yue told me you're from out of town, first time in the capital?\"","Liu Yutong ignored him.","Zhou Heng wasn't bothered; instead, he laughed. \"Quite a personality. I like it.\"","Then he sat directly down in the chair next to Liu Yutong—the one that had originally been Gao Min's.","Gao Min, by now, had also started chatting up the two celebrities, trying to fish for information about them.","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo, upon hearing Gao Min mention her connection to the Lin family, let their guard down and chatted casually with her. They even took the initiative to invite her to the party that evening.","Gao Min happily agreed.","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo were also thrilled and excited. They hadn't expected that tagging along with Young Master Zhou to meet a friend on a whim would lead them to inviting a short-haired beauty to the party.","Tonight was going to be a wild ride!",".........."]},{"number":744,"title":"Chapter 744: 745. What if you misjudged it","paragraphs":["\"Miss Liu, since you've come to the imperial capital, that's fate. As the host, I have to fulfill my duties as a proper host.\"","Zhou Heng raised his glass: \"Come on, let's have a drink.\"","Liu Yutong looked down at the glass in front of her without moving.","Seeing this, Zhou Heng's smile faded a bit.","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo, two popular young actors, exchanged glances at this scene.","In all of the imperial capital, they had never seen anyone dare to disrespect Young Master Zhou like this.","\"Miss Liu, Young Master Zhou is one of the top figures in the imperial capital. Getting to know him is your blessing.\"","\"That's right, that's right. With one word from Young Master Zhou, you can walk sideways in the imperial capital. Just give him some face and have a drink.\"","Liu Yutong glanced at them and said unhurriedly, \"Walking sideways is for crabs. But the two of you really do resemble crabs.\"","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo's faces instantly darkened.","Zhou Heng paused for a moment, then burst into loud laughter.","\"Interesting! Truly interesting!\"","\"Miss Liu, with a mouth like yours, you absolutely have to drink this glass.\"","Liu Yutong still didn't budge.","Lin Yue cursed Liu Yutong inwardly for being clueless and quickly stepped in to smooth things over: \"Brother Heng, Yutong is here for the first time and a bit nervous. Please don't mind...\"","Zhou Heng waved his hand, cutting her off, his eyes still fixed on Liu Yutong.","\"Not drinking?\"","Liu Yutong shook her head. \"I'm not drinking.\"","Everyone in the private room fell silent.","This girl had no idea what she was doing.","If she kept talking to Young Master Zhou like this, things wouldn't end well for her.","Zhou Heng's gaze turned cold: \"Miss Liu, do you know who I am?\"","Liu Yutong: \"Didn't you just say? From the Zhou family.\"","Zhou Heng: \"Knowing I'm from the Zhou family, you still dare to disrespect me like this?\"","Liu Yutong: \"So what if you're from the Zhou family? Does that mean I have to be your drinking companion?\"","Zhou Heng's smile froze slightly.","Chen Xinhuai couldn't help but speak up: \"Miss Liu, that's not right. Young Master Zhou's status in the imperial capital is unmatched. Countless people would kill for a chance to suck up to him. Sitting here today is a stroke of luck for you.\"","Sun Mo added: \"Yeah, don't be ungrateful.\"","Liu Yutong turned to look at the two of them.","\"You two work in entertainment, right? Seems like you're pretty famous.\"","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo were taken aback, then puffed up with pride.","\"Oh, Miss Liu recognizes us? Well, we are quite popular.\"","\"We've been on shows like 'Star Light' and 'The Base' twice each. If you want an autograph, we can give you one later—just as long as you have that drink with Young Master Zhou.\"","Liu Yutong: \"I won't need the autograph.\"","\"I just want to ask: if you two soft-skinned pretty boys ended up in a safe place, do you think you'd last?\"","Chen Xinhuai: ???","Sun Mo: ???","A safe place? Was this place unsafe? What was this woman babbling about?","Just then, Gao Min, who hadn't said much, stretched lazily and interjected: \"Hey, big stars, I'm getting sleepy. Know any places that could wake me up?\"","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo's eyes lit up immediately, and they nodded eagerly.","\"Yes, yes! There's a private party tonight—super exhilarating, all kinds of fun. Want us to take you?\"","Gao Min agreed readily: \"Sure!\"","Chen Xinhuai then looked at Zhou Heng: \"Young Master Zhou, we'll head off then?\"","Zhou Heng, whose mind was entirely focused on how to conquer Liu Yutong, knew exactly what those two were up to, and since his target was this woman surnamed Liu, he didn't want any interruptions. He waved them off impatiently.","\"You two, settle it with Miss Lin.\"","After all, this Gao Min was connected to the Lin family, so he couldn't make the call himself.","Lin Yue naturally didn't object: \"Sister Min wants to go, so take her then.\"","In truth, she looked down on this country bumpkin from the start.","If it weren't for her connection to her third aunt, she might have sold them both out already.","Now that she wanted to go 'chase stars' and get into those shady places, it worked out perfectly. If some scandal happened, it wouldn't be on her hands.","Lin Feng was burning with curiosity and desperately wanted to check out that kind of party. He quickly raised his hand: \"Can you take me along?\"","Chen Xinhuai and the others had no reason to refuse—he was from the Lin family after all—so they nodded: \"Sure, come along. We'll show you the ropes.\"","Gao Min then winked at Liu Yutong: \"I'm off first.\"","And she discreetly made an OK gesture, as if to say: Can you handle this scene on your own? Call for help if you can't.","Liu Yutong nodded slightly, signaling for her to be at ease.","After Gao Min and the others left the private room.","\"Well, your friend here sure knows when to make herself scarce.\"","Zhou Heng leaned back in his chair, crossed his legs, and looked at Liu Yutong again, his gaze growing bolder.","\"The question is, do you know when to play along?\"","He pointed once more at the glass in front of Liu Yutong.","\"Miss Liu, I'm a man of limited patience. Now that your friend's gone, isn't it a bit much to keep acting so high and mighty?\"","Lin Yue chimed in again: \"Yutong, just give Young Master Zhou a break! One drink, and it's all good. After that, you'll have Young Master Zhou's protection in the imperial capital. What a great deal!\"","Liu Yutong: \"Lin Yue, do you think every woman in the world should be falling all over this guy surnamed Zhou?\"","Lin Yue's face stiffened: \"Yutong, I'm saying this for your own good! Do you know who Young Master Zhou is? So many people would kill to get close to him! You're from out of town—if you can latch onto a big tree like him, you'll have everything you want in the imperial capital!\"","Liu Yutong genuinely felt this girl was beyond help, and turned back to Zhou Heng.","\"Young Master Zhou, right? Let me ask you something.\"","Zhou Heng: \"Go ahead.\"","Liu Yutong: \"If the person sitting here right now were the daughter of some top-tier imperial capital family, would you still dare to talk to her like this?\"","Zhou Heng froze.","Liu Yutong continued: \"You wouldn't. Because you know there are some people you can't afford to offend.\"","\"But you dare to talk to me like this. Why?\"","\"Because in your eyes, I'm just some outsider from the countryside—no connections, no backing, an easy pushover. Drinking with you is me doing you a favor; refusing is me being ungrateful. Am I right?\"","Zhou Heng's expression twisted.","Liu Yutong stood up and looked down at him from above.","\"But what if you've misjudged your mark?\""]},{"number":745,"title":"Chapter 745: 746, I Know a Little Kung Fu.","paragraphs":["\"But what if you misjudged her?\"","The moment Liu Yutong said this, the private room fell into a dead silence.","The flippant expression on Zhou Heng's face slowly froze. He stared at the girl in front of him, dressed in a light apricot cotton-linen dress, looking as pure as a blank sheet of paper.","She really did have a presence that didn't seem ordinary.","Was he wrong? Could Lin Yue have been mistaken? Was this girl not just some average student from Pearl City trying to use Gao Min to climb the social ladder and latch onto the Lin family?","The circle in the capital—well, it was big but also small. The truly top-tier families, even if he didn't know them well, he'd at least heard of their names.","Surnamed Liu... he'd never heard of any heiress from the top elite families with that surname.","But her aura didn't lie. That calm, unhurried demeanor wasn't something you could fake.","These days, a lot of top-tier big shots liked to keep their kids low-key, keeping them out of the public eye to avoid being targeted. Maybe she was like that—someone who looked ordinary on the surface but came from a family with connections that reached the heavens.","The more Zhou Heng thought about it, the more plausible it seemed. After all, this was the capital! A place full of hidden dragons and crouching tigers; anything was possible.","He'd been an idiot earlier, thinking about pressuring her to drink, thinking about taking her down. If he had actually stepped on a landmine and crossed the wrong person, he would be in deep trouble.","On the other side, Lin Yue couldn't help feeling uneasy too.","Had she really been wrong? Was the other girl not here to cling to the Lin family's wealth by accompanying Gao Min to find her birth relatives?","She thought back to Liu Yutong's words and actions that day. Originally, she'd just thought Liu Yutong was a rude bumpkin.","But now, looking back, everything seemed different.","No wonder she hadn't been scared at all during dinner at the Lin family's old mansion. She had dared to talk back to Second Aunt and Fourth Aunt, and had the nerve to take the king crab and eat it all by herself. It wasn't that she was lacking manners—it was that she simply didn't care about the Lin family's rules!","No wonder she had shown no reaction to the Cloud Dew Club and its two-million annual fee. It wasn't that she was an inexperienced nobody—it was that a place like that meant nothing to her!","If her background was much bigger than Lin Yue's, then everything made sense.","Realizing this, all of Lin Yue's previous sense of superiority and haughty demeanor vanished, replaced by sheer terror and regret.","She had actually tried to offer someone like that to Zhou Heng as a gift! And she had even dared to threaten Liu Yutong, saying she would make her life in the capital impossible!","If she had truly angered Liu Yutong, not only she, but the entire Lin family would suffer the consequences!","Just as the two were frantically second-guessing themselves, thinking about how to defuse the tension and pump Liu Yutong for more information about her true identity—","Suddenly!","\"Ha ha ha...\"","Liu Yutong, seeing both of them looking so nervous, burst into uncontrollable laughter.","\"Wait, wait... you actually believed me? Ha ha ha... I can't breathe...\"","Zhou Heng's face instantly turned black.","Lin Yue's face froze too.","What did this mean? She was teasing them?","Liu Yutong laughed until she had to wipe tears from her eyes, then looked at them mockingly.","\"I'm telling you, Master Zhou, you're way too gullible. I just said that off the top of my head, and you really fell for it, thinking I'm some family heiress?\"","Zhou Heng's face cycled from black to red, then from red to green—a truly spectacular sight.","Lin Yue wished she could crawl into a hole. She had actually been fooled by this country girl! She had actually believed Liu Yutong had some impressive background! And she had actually been afraid of crossing someone untouchable!","Watching their expressions, Liu Yutong laughed even harder.","\"Master Zhou, looks like you're the type who bullies the weak and fears the strong. The moment you hear someone has connections, you fold like a coward.\"","\"And you, Miss Lin, now I finally get why the Lin family is going downhill. You all in this generation are total losers!\"","Zhou Heng's face darkened completely, his expression grim enough to drip venom.","He had been played—by a wild girl from some backwater town!","He slammed the table. The wine glass crashed onto the surface, splashing alcohol everywhere.","\"You dare mess with me?!\"","\"You little bitch, you have no idea what death means! In the capital, no one has ever dared to talk to me like that, much less play me for a fool!\"","Lin Yue was furious too, pointing at Liu Yutong and cursing, \"Liu Yutong, you've gone too far! I treated you to good food and drinks, and you dare to toy with us! Don't think you can get away with this just by kneeling and begging for forgiveness!\"","Zhou Heng stepped closer to Liu Yutong, radiating a violent energy.","\"I'll give you one last chance. Kneel down, drink this wine in front of me, and I'll let this slide.\"","\"Otherwise, I'll show you exactly what happens when you cross Zhou Heng in the capital!\"","With that, he picked up the bottle of Louis XIII and shoved it toward her.","Liu Yutong obediently took the bottle, weighing it in her hand.","\"Master Zhou, don't get so worked up. I didn't really trick you, you know. I may not have much of a background, but that sister—I mean, that best friend of mine, Gao Min—she's got one hell of a connection.\"","Zhou Heng paused. \"Gao Min? That short-haired woman?\"","Lin Yue was also taken aback. \"Sister Min? What background could she have? Isn't she just the daughter Third Aunt found in the countryside?\"","Liu Yutong shook her head, raising a finger and wagging it between them.","\"No, no, no. You've both got it wrong.\"","\"My best friend isn't some ordinary country girl.\"","Zhou Heng frowned, his patience wearing thin. \"Then what is she?\"","Liu Yutong leaned in. \"She is a proud—\"","She paused deliberately, watching their reactions, then said the four words slowly, one by one: \"Peo-ple's Po-lice Officer!\"","The room went dead silent for three full seconds.","And then...","\"Pfft ha ha ha ha ha...\"","Zhou Heng nearly spat out his drink. Lin Yue also burst into laughter.","\"A cop? Ha ha ha ha... you're saying Sister Min is a cop? Ha ha ha... I'm dying!\"","\"And here I thought she was some big shot. Turns out she's just a regular beat cop! Ha ha ha...\"","\"Liu Yutong, do you even know what 'one hell of a connection' means? In the capital, a nobody cop doesn't count for anything! Do you know what kind of background the Zhou family has? Do you know where my uncle works? A lowly police officer is supposed to be some big shot?\"","\"Sister Min is a cop? Oh my God, I thought she actually had some serious clout, and that's it?\"","Seeing them laughing and mocking her, Liu Yutong calmly delivered the final blow.","\"You don't see my best friend's status as anything special—that's fine.\"","\"But she just left with Master Zhou's two friends. Do you know what they're up to?\"","The instant she said that, the smiles on Zhou Heng's and Lin Yue's faces froze.","Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo... those two idiots. What were they up to tonight? How could he have forgotten about that!","Of course he knew what those two idiots were doing tonight!","A party!","But it was no ordinary party!","Damn it! If Gao Min really was a cop, then she'd be walking right into a trap—offering up a ready-made bust!","The most critical thing was, if they were caught red-handed, then Zhou Heng would also be in trouble...","Zhou Heng didn't dare to think further.","He abruptly turned his head to look at Lin Yue.","Lin Yue stammered, panicked, \"I... I don't know... I really didn't know Sister Min was a cop... I thought she just wanted to be a fan...\"","Liu Yutong was still holding the bottle of wine, twirling it slowly in her hand.","\"What, now you're not mocking my best friend's identity? Not calling her a 'mere cop' anymore?\"","\"Though this identity is ordinary, it's specifically... for catching bad guys.\"","Zhou Heng's eyes practically shot fire.","He, the prestigious young master of the Zhou family, had been toyed with by a country girl!","First, she pretended to be supernatural to scare him, and then she used the cops to threaten him!","The most infuriating part was—he actually got scared!","No, it was really possible he'd end up in trouble too!","\"You bitch, I'll kill you first...\"","Unable to hold back any longer, Zhou Heng lunged at Liu Yutong, trying to hit her.","But the next second...","A loud bang exploded.","A wine bottle shattered—no, fully burst—right on Zhou Heng's head.","\"Ahhh!!!\"","Zhou Heng let out a piercing scream, but before he could even clutch his head, Liu Yutong grabbed his hair, raised her leg, and delivered a clean, sharp knee strike straight into his stomach.","\"Pfft!\"","Zhou Heng curled up like a cooked shrimp, darkness swimming before his eyes from the pain. He nearly passed out, feeling like his stomach acid was about to spew out.","Liu Yutong then shoved him with momentum, sending his bulky body flying backward, crashing heavily into the rosewood chair behind him.","Crash!","The chair splintered on impact. Zhou Heng collapsed on the floor, curled up clutching his stomach, whimpering and groaning, unable to get up.","All of this happened so fast.","Lin Yue stood frozen, utterly dumbfounded, not even reacting. She just stared blankly at the scene, at a loss.","A moment ago, Zhou Heng was charging at someone with murderous rage. The next second, the arrogant young master of the imperial capital was taken down cleanly by the seemingly fragile girl in front of her.","She never imagined that this quiet, gentle-looking girl could be so skilled—and her moves so ruthless!","Just then, Liu Yutong patted the glass shards that had accidentally splashed onto her hands, looking calmly at the groaning Zhou Heng on the floor.","\"Oh, I forgot to mention earlier—I also happen to know a little bit of martial arts.\""]},{"number":746,"title":"Chapter 746: 747, A Kick in Public","paragraphs":["Lin Yue stood there, completely stunned.","She stared blankly at Zhou Heng writhing on the floor, then looked up at the calm, composed Liu Yutong standing before her, her mind an utter blank.","This girl she’d dismissed as a country bumpkin with no background and no class—she’d actually laid out Zhou Heng?","That was Zhou Heng!","The youngest and most doted-upon son of the Zhou clan in the imperial capital!","In the circles of Beijing’s elite, the people bold enough to lay a finger on a Zhou family member could be counted on one hand!","And now, this young master of the Zhou family was lying on the ground like a beaten dog.","“Are you... are you insane?!”","Lin Yue’s voice was trembling. “Do you even know who you just hit? Zhou Heng! A Zhou family man!”","“You’re... you’re finished, Liu Yutong! Doomed! The Zhou family will hunt you down...”","Before she could finish, her words died in her throat.","Because Liu Yutong was walking toward her.","“You... what are you doing?” Lin Yue shouted, panicked, instinctively backing up a few steps.","Liu Yutong: “Lin Yue, you know what? From the moment you set foot in the Lin family home, you’ve been asking for it.”","“First, you put your sister and me in the servants’ quarters, and I didn’t say a word.”","“Then you made snide remarks over dinner, and I still kept my mouth shut.”","“Then you lured me to this seedy dive, and I still said nothing.”","“You know why?”","Liu Yutong reached out and patted Lin Yue’s cheeks gently twice. “Because I wanted to see just how far you could go with your stupidity.”","“Now I get it. You’re a fool—hopelessly stupid.”","“Do you even know what you’ve done tonight?”","“You handed a police officer over to two drug-dealing, porn-actor losers to take to their party—that’s pandering and harboring drug users right there. Plus the rest of the charges stacking up, and you’ll be rotting in jail for a long, long time.”","“And you tried to sell me off to this so-called Young Master Zhou. But didn’t it occur to you, before you sold me, to check exactly who you’re trying to sell?!”","“Tsk, Lin Yue, your stupidity makes me embarrassed for you.”","Lin Yue: “I... I...”","“I what? Cat got your tongue?”","Liu Yutong: “Since you’re a member of the Lin family, I’ll go easy on you this once. Now, you’re going to slap yourself across the face until I say stop.”","Lin Yue froze, rigid.","She was the acknowledged Miss Lin, always cherished and pampered. How had she ever been humiliated like this?","“What’s wrong? Can’t do it?” Liu Yutong’s gaze grew icy when she saw no movement.","The invisible pressure crushed Lin Yue instantly.","“I’ll do it! I’ll do it!”","Lin Yue flinched, and immediately raised a trembling hand to slap her own cheek.","Slap!","The crisp sound of a slap filled the room, and a vivid red handprint bloomed on Lin Yue’s face, stinging with fire.","But she dared not stop or slacken. She kept raising her hand, smacking her pampered face again and again.","Slap! Slap! Slap!","Liu Yutong stood to the side, expressionless, watching Lin Yue beat her own face without an ounce of pity in her eyes.","She had never been soft-hearted.","I don’t start trouble, but when trouble comes to me, my payback is a hundred times worse. Lin Yue and Zhou Heng had dared to cross her, and now they’d reap the consequences.","It felt like an eternity before Lin Yue’s cheeks were swollen like steamed buns, her hands numb, barely able to lift them anymore.","She sobbed, pleading, “Miss Liu... I... I can’t take it anymore... Please, tell me to stop...”","Liu Yutong saw it was enough and was about to speak...","Suddenly, the door to the private room was slammed open from outside.","“What’s going on?”","Several figures rushed in.","Leading them was the middle-aged man who’d first received Lin Yue earlier—the manager of the Cloud Dew Club, Han Yi.","Behind him came a few security guards, brandishing rubber batons.","Han Yi stepped in, took in the scene, and his face changed in an instant.","The room was a wreck. A man lay on the floor, curled up, his face bloody and unrecognizable.","He took a closer look and his heart dropped.","Zhou Heng!","The young master of the Zhou family!","On the other side stood a young woman, her hand cupping her swollen face, smeared mascara making her look a mess—Lin Yue.","Han Yi’s mind exploded.","On the Cloud Dew’s turf, the Zhou family’s young master and Lin’s heiress had been roughed up?","If word got out, Cloud Dew’s reputation would be destroyed!","“What happened here?”","Han Yi turned to Liu Yutong in disbelief.","The entire room, only she was untouched—even unnervingly composed.","“Was it you who did this?”","Frankly, even he didn’t fully believe it.","Only the three of them were in the room—nobody else. But imagining that a delicate-looking girl like her could beat a grown man like Zhou Heng bloody was hard to swallow.","Liu Yutong admitted calmly: “It was me. What about it?”","Han Yi stared at her defiance, rumors churning in his mind.","Could this girl also have overwhelming connections?","Despite her plain clothes, her unruffled presence wasn’t an act amateurs could fake.","He didn’t act recklessly. First he went to Zhou Heng, crouching down to check his injuries.","When he caught sight of the damage, he drew a sharp breath.","Zhou Heng’s once-passable face was a wreck. A gash cut across his forehead from a broken bottle, blood caking half his face. His lips were mangled, swollen like sausages.","“Young Master Zhou, how are you feeling?”","Zhou Heng struggled to sit up. “Call me an ambulance.”","Han Yi nodded quickly. “I’ll call one now.”","Zhou Heng wiped blood from his face, still shooting venomous looks at Liu Yutong.","“Manager Han, seize that bitch! I want her dead!”","Han Yi hesitated but waved to his security guards.","The men surrounded Liu Yutong.","“Miss, since you indulged in violence at my Cloud Dew, you’ll have to give an explanation.”","Liu Yutong regarded him: “An explanation? What kind?”","Han Yi took a deep breath, trying to keep his tone calm.","Business was business; peace and money were better than trouble.","“According to Club rules, you’ve injured someone here. We can call the police to handle this. Young Master Zhou and this young lady’s wounds amount to aggravated assault.”","“Young Master Zhou, young lady, should I call the police for you?”","At the mention of police, Zhou Heng’s expression stiffened.","His two fox friends were off with the policewoman, about to join that party. If cops came nosing around, traced it all back, those two would be caught red-handed, and they’d pin it on him. Zhou Heng couldn’t escape blame.","And on top of that, he had been planning to get that girl surnamed Liu tonight, but instead of succeeding, he had gotten his head bashed in. If news of this humiliation got out, where would he, Young Master Zhou, hang his face? Where would the Zhou family’s face be?","“Call the police? No, don’t call the police!”","“We’ll handle this ourselves! No need for the cops to get involved!”","Han Yi was taken aback.","Zhou Heng didn’t want to call the police?","That was unusual.","But he could roughly understand why.","Since the guest himself was unwilling to involve the authorities, Han Yi figured he’d better not say anything else—after all, even he couldn’t afford to offend the Zhou family.","“Then, Young Master Zhou, what’s your intention...”","Zhou Heng fixed his gaze on Liu Yutong, his expression twisted and vicious.","“You little slut, you said you’re pretty tough, didn’t you?”","“Fine, I’ll let you know today that in this city of the capital, being tough means shit!”","“You hit me today, and this debt—we’re going to settle it properly!”","“Pretty soon, I’ll have you on your knees begging for mercy! You’ll learn exactly what it means to cross me, Zhou Heng! I’ll make you experience what it’s like to be worse than dead! Tonight, I’ll use you up, wreck you, and then sell you off to Southeast Asia...”","He didn’t get to finish.","Bang!","A foot slammed violently into his chest.","The whole person of Zhou Heng flew backward, crashing heavily into a load-bearing wall with a dull thud.","“Ahhh!!!”","This scream was several times more miserable than the ones before.","Zhou Heng clutched his chest, barely able to breathe, feeling like at least three of his ribs were broken.","Liu Yutong lowered her long leg and said expressionlessly, “Your mouth is so dirty—better keep it shut.”"]},{"number":747,"title":"Chapter 747: 748, Repeatedly Fooled. (Thanks to Good Qing, Good Mood, Good Sunshine for the Spa Treatment)","paragraphs":["The security guards were all stunned.","Was this girl really this fierce?","She dared to throw a punch right in front of all of them. And not just a light one either—she was brutal, completely disregarding the fact that they were the security at Yulu.","Manager Han had turned pale.","No matter who this girl was, he had to step in today. Otherwise, Yulu’s reputation would be completely ruined.","“Men! Take her down!”","The security guards moved to grab Liu Yutong.","By then, Lin Yue had finally caught her breath and sobbed toward Han Yi: “Manager Han, she hit Young Master Zhou! She even made me slap myself! You have to arrest her! She must pay for today!”","“Don’t worry, I’ll make sure...”","Han Yi had only half-finished his sentence when Liu Yutong cut him off.","“Hold on!”","“Manager Han, are you sure you want to offend someone whose background you know nothing about, just for these two idiots?”","It was the same tactic she had used before, and the effect was just as immediate.","Han Yi flinched and immediately ordered the guards to stop.","He studied the young girl before him. Surrounded by five or six security guards, there wasn’t a hint of fear on her face.","That calmness, that composure—it couldn’t be faked.","She might really be the heiress of some influential family.","Han Yi’s heart began to waver. For a moment, he didn’t know what to do.","Zhou Heng and Lin Yue panicked when they saw Han Yi hesitating.","They knew this routine all too well.","This girl had used the exact same line to bluff them.","“She’s a fraud! She tricked us the same way! She has no real background—don’t let her fool you, Manager Han!”","“Yeah! She’s a fake! Do something already!”","Han Yi still hesitated. He couldn’t trust just one side’s story.","Sure, Young Master Zhou and Miss Lin had a grudge against her, their families from Zhou and Lin might not fear offending her, but Yulu couldn’t afford that risk!","Just as he was wavering, Zhou Heng yelled out.","“Han Yi! What the hell are you waiting for? Take her down! I’m telling you now—if you let her go, I’ll make Yulu regret it! I’ll make sure you can’t stay in Four-Nine City any longer!”","“Go ahead and act! I’ll take full responsibility for whatever happens!”","Hearing this, Han Yi gritted his teeth, stopped hesitating, and nodded to the guards behind him: “Move!”","But the moment he gave the order, something unexpected happened again.","Bang!","A loud crash came from the courtyard outside. The heavy solid-wood doors had been kicked in from the outside.","Everyone froze in shock at this sudden turn of events.","Han Yi’s face changed, and he spun around to shout: “Who dares to cause trouble at Yulu?! Do you have a death wish?!”","Before he could finish, he saw something he would never forget.","A group of men in black suits, looking like underworld enforcers, surged into the courtyard.","Han Yi and the security guards were caught off guard and immediately surrounded by these men.","Then, a tall, cold-faced young man in black walked up to him. It was Yun Cheng.","Without a word, Yun Cheng slapped Han Yi to the ground, sending stars spinning before his eyes.","“Who did you say has a death wish?”","Trembling, Han Yi dared not speak.","Yun Cheng stepped over him and walked straight to Liu Yutong. Everyone watched in shock as he slightly bowed and addressed her with extreme respect.","“Miss! We were late. Please punish us!”","That single word—“Miss”—stunned the entire room.","Han Yi’s eyes went wide.","Zhou Heng’s mouth hung open.","Lin Yue was dumbfounded again, staring at the scene.","Miss... Miss?","Wait, didn’t she just say she had no background? Then why were these men in black calling her “Miss”?","Liu Yutong looked like she had just realized something, and spoke again, as if slow on the uptake: “Oh, sorry, sorry. I forgot to tell you—I also called over a few people. You don’t mind, do you?”","Zhou Heng and the others: “......”","A few people?! That was a gross understatement!","When Yun Cheng saw that the security guards were still surrounding Liu Yutong and noticed the marks from the scuffle inside, his face darkened.","“Arrest them all!”","His men dispersed instantly, subduing every one of Yulu’s security guards with swift, clean moves.","Two guards tried to resist and were promptly kicked in the back of the knees, dropping to the ground, faces pressed against the floor, unable to move.","Han Yi’s face alternated between red and pale.","Now he finally understood why this girl had been so bold.","She had every right to be.","“May I ask... miss, who exactly are you?”","Liu Yutong said nothing.","Yun Cheng answered for her.","“You’re not qualified to know.”","Though annoyed, Han Yi dared not argue or make any move.","He knew that things had gone far beyond what he could handle.","Zhou Heng finally snapped out of his shock, pointing at Liu Yutong: “You... didn’t you say you were ordinary? Didn’t you say you were messing with us? Then what about these people? Who the hell are you?!”","Liu Yutong looked at him with a half-smile.","“You believe everything I say? Zhou, how have you survived this long with such a low IQ?”","Zhou Heng nearly spat blood.","He had been played!","This girl had played him from start to finish!","Was he a circus monkey to be toyed with like this?","First, she scared him with talk of connections, then claimed it was all a lie, lulling him into complacency—and now this group of men in black calling her “Miss”! What game was this woman playing? Did she get a kick out of messing with people’s heads?","Lin Yue, who had just been ready to gloat, now regretted ever crossing this devil.","Yun Cheng looked at Liu Yutong, waiting for her orders.","Her gaze swept across the room and finally landed on Han Yi.","“Manager Han, right?”","Han Yi trembled. “Y-yes, miss. What are your orders?”","Liu Yutong smiled brightly, but that smile made Han Yi’s skin crawl.","“Relax, I’m not here to tear the place down.”","“These two wastes asked for it. They have no one to blame but themselves.”","“As for you, you’re just doing business. I understand. Today’s incident has nothing to do with you, and I won’t make things hard for you.”","Han Yi let out a sigh of relief. He started to thank her, but before he could finish, Liu Yutong continued.","“However, you’ll have to testify for me.”","Han Yi’s heart sank. “Testify?”","Liu Yutong: “Simple. Young Master Zhou and Miss Lin tried to attack me, and I was only defending myself. It’s self-defense.”","“Then you can call the police and hand them over. That’ll wrap things up.”","Han Yi: “......”","Really, miss? You beat them until their ribs are broken and their faces look like meat platters, and now you want them sent to jail? Is that even fitting? It’s like selling them into slavery and making them count the money!","But he didn’t dare argue. He just nodded repeatedly. “Yes, yes, yes, I’ll definitely testify truthfully!”","Liu Yutong nodded with satisfaction, then turned to look at the utterly stunned Zhou Heng and Lin Yue. A suddenly meaningful smile spread across her face.","\"By the way, let me tell you the truth. I really don't have any connections. 'Miss' is just... what they call me, that's all. If you want to get back at me later, feel free to do so.\"","\"I'm not lying to you this time.\"","Zhou Heng: \"...\"","Lin Yue: \"...\"","Yeah, right, like we'd believe you! This woman doesn't speak a single word of truth!"]},{"number":748,"title":"Chapter 748: 749, Why Is This Grand Lady Here","paragraphs":["The commotion coming from the courtyard of Cloud Dew Club was so loud that, even with excellent soundproofing, it disturbed guests in other private rooms.","On the second floor, in a room called Guanlan Pavilion, four heavyweights from the business world sat around a rosewood tea table.","The fragrance of tea curled through the air, and the atmosphere was quite relaxed.","Seated at the head was a man in his forties, wearing a dark gray polo shirt, with a gentle and refined demeanor.","He was Lei Yun, former CEO and founder of Yinshan Technology.","Across from him sat two people. One was Huang Zhangming, founder of Meizu Electronics, who made his start in MP3 players and had recently transitioned into smartphones. He had a somewhat proud, aloof personality.","The other was a man named Lin Bing, formerly a technical director at a major international company and a genuine top-tier expert in operating systems and software architecture. Lei Yun had gone to great lengths to bring him on board.","The last person was Chu Hai, founder and president of AEG Capital, a top power player in the capital circle.","Today’s gathering was organized by Lei Yun.","When the iPhone launched in 2007, Lei Yun had someone bring one back from the U.S. for him right away. He stayed up all night playing with it.","That night, he called every friend in his contact list, repeating the same thing: “The era of mobile internet is coming. The phone is the portal to the future.”","Many people heard him out, laughed it off, and moved on.","But not Lei Yun.","That was when he started studying the smartphone industry: the supply chain, operating systems, everything there was to learn—and in the process, he met Huang Zhangming.","Lei Yun had seen Huang Zhangming’s engineering prototype.","The moment he laid eyes on it, he was amazed.","The phone’s UI design, interaction logic, and system smoothness were completely on par with foreign brands at the time. What impressed him most was the F System, developed by Huang Zhangming’s team, deeply customized based on Android with many original and eye-catching features.","Lei Yun had wanted to invest in him from the start.","But he also knew that Huang Zhangming was not easy to deal with.","The man was not only proud but somewhat arrogant. He’d already turned down many investors showing up checks in hand.","So Lei Yun played it smart—no talk about money, just build a connection first.","Taking advantage of everyone being in the capital on business trips, he set up this gathering and even pulled in the tech guru Lin Bing and the capital titan Chu Hai.","Everyone was together, the tea smelled wonderful, and conversation flowed naturally.","This was Lei Yun’s style—let things come to fruition naturally, never forcing anything.","“Come, come, try this tea.”","Lei Yun lifted a purple clay pot and poured amber-colored tea into cups. “This is Wuyi Mountain’s Zhengyan Rougui. A friend who’s in the tea business gave it to me. I don’t usually bring it out, but today I’m breaking it open to treat you distinguished guests.”","Huang Zhangming raised his cup, took a sip, and nodded slightly.","Lin Bing, being polite, savored it carefully and praised, “Excellent tea. Rich aroma, and a good aftertaste too.”","Chu Hai smiled, set down his cup, and looked directly at Lei Yun. “President Lei, let’s cut to the chase. You didn’t gather us just for tea, did you?”","Lei Yun laughed heartily. “President Chu, you’re a man who knows how things work. Fine, I’ll stop beating around the bush.”","He turned to Huang Zhangming. “President Huang, when is that new phone of yours launching?”","Huang Zhangming placed the engineering prototype that was by his hand on the table. “Soon. About a month from now. But there’s a hold-up with the supply chain—battery supplies aren’t coming fast enough. Might have to delay a bit.”","Lei Yun nodded and looked at the prototype. “Mind if I take a look?”","Huang Zhangming hesitated for a moment, then handed it over.","Lei Yun took the phone, weighed it in his hand. The screen was small—around 3.5 inches—and the resolution was decent.","The design was indeed polished; it felt premium in the hand.","He pressed a few buttons, swiped the screen, and tested the system’s smoothness.","“Not bad. The feel, the UI—pretty interesting.”","“President Huang, what price range are you targeting for this model?”","Huang Zhangming thought for a moment. “Between 2,500 and 3,000 yuan, roughly.”","Lei Yun nodded thoughtfully. That price already positioned it as mid-to-high-end among current domestic phones.","Just then, Lin Bing, who had been quiet, suddenly spoke up. “President Huang, could I take a look too?”","Huang Zhangming glanced at him and nodded.","Lin Bing took the phone. Instead of looking at the appearance, he immediately went into the engineering mode, his fingers flying across the screen, then checking the background processes.","Slowly, his expression changed—from calm to surprise, and finally to excitement.","“This kernel... your team really modified it yourselves?”","A hint of pride showed on Huang Zhangming’s face. “That’s right. The F System, deeply customized from Android. We’ve been developing it since 2007.”","Lin Bing said, “The interaction logic is very intuitive, and the smoothness is high. It’s far beyond the cheap reskins of Android on the market. In some ways, it’s even more user-friendly than the iPhone.”","Getting recognition from an expert of Lin Bing’s caliber was genuinely satisfying for Huang Zhangming.","Chu Hai had been silent the whole time, just listening to their conversation and forming his own judgment.","Lei Yun’s insight was unquestionable, and Lin Bing was clearly a talent. If both of them thought this highly of the product, it meant this company was definitely worth investing in.","When the discussion wound down, he finally spoke up.","“President Huang, how’s your company’s financial situation?”","Huang Zhangming’s smile stiffened slightly.","This was the question he least wanted to answer.","But Chu Hai was a guest Lei Yun had brought, a major figure in the capital world—he couldn’t just brush him off.","He paused, searching for words, then vaguely replied, “It’s okay. I saved up some money from the MP3 years, plus a few rounds of funding earlier. It’ll hold us for a while.”","Chu Hai smiled again. “And then what? After launch, you’ll need money for distribution channels, advertising, after-sales service, stocking inventory. The smartphone business is a bottomless pit—you know that better than I do, President Huang.”","Huang Zhangming went silent.","He knew it well.","Making phones meant burning money: R&D cost money, the supply chain cost money, marketing cost money—everything cost money.","The reason he had turned down investment firms before wasn’t that he didn’t need the cash. It was that his need for control was too strong. He was reluctant to part with equity.","In truth, he dreamed of building Meizu into a family business, keeping power firmly in his own hands.","Of course, he had guessed what Lei Yun’s gathering was really about. With a tech expert and an investor both here, the message was obvious—they wanted to buy in.","And sure enough, Lei Yun saw the moment was ripe. He stopped hinting and cut straight to the point.","“President Huang, I truly believe in your product. The hardware design and the software experience are top-tier for domestic phones, and even globally, it could hold its own.”","“But to succeed in smartphones, we need more than just a good product. Supply chain connections, distribution channels, brand identity, after-sales networks—all of that matters. President Chu and I have invested in many companies over the years. What we have in abundance is money and resources.”","\"I'm not going to mess around with you. AEG Capital, run by President Chu and me, is prepared to invest in Meizu. We can discuss the specific amount...\"","Then Lei Yun laid out his investment plan: the approximate amount, bringing in a tech expert like Lin Bing to serve as a senior executive, and restructuring Meizu into a joint-stock company with an eye toward an IPO in the future.","Huang Zhangming listened, falling into silence.","Lei Yun's terms were tempting—especially the addition of Lin Bing and access to supply chain resources, which were exactly what he needed most at the moment. But the cost came in the form of equity dilution... which made him hesitant.","To be honest, he really wanted Lei Yun to join Meizu. But he just couldn't let go of the equity. He was truly torn.","\"President Lei, I think I'll...\"","He was just about to say he'd go back and think it over when—","Suddenly!","Boom!","A loud crash came from downstairs, rattling the windows.","Lin Bing, who was sipping tea, jumped in surprise and nearly spilled it: \"What's going on? An earthquake?\"","Huang Zhangming frowned and glanced out the window.","\"Sounds like some kind of commotion down on the ground floor.\"","Then came a rapid series of footsteps from below.","Chu Hai was the first to stand up, walk over to the window, and open it to look down.","One glance, and his face instantly changed. He slammed the window shut without hesitation.","\"Oh no! Why is this woman here!\""]},{"number":749,"title":"Chapter 749: 750, Horror Story (Thanks to Shali'er for the Great God's Certification)","paragraphs":["Chu Hai stood up, walked over to the window, and glanced down.","Then his expression changed.","In the courtyard below, a group of men in black had appeared out of nowhere.","They wore matching black suits, each with a dragon-shaped pin on the chest.","All of Yunlu’s security guards had been dragged out, pinned to the ground, unable to move.","Chu Hai sucked in a sharp breath.","He knew that dragon-shaped pin all too well.","It was the emblem of the Wanlong Society.","Back when he was negotiating investments in Mingzhu City, he had personally witnessed how these lunatics—right in front of the authorities—had physically deleted a local crime boss.","That scene was still etched in his memory.","And now, with the men in black showing up here, it could only mean...","Chu Hai’s gaze followed the line of black-clad figures toward the entrance of the private room.","Sure enough, he spotted a figure he knew very well.","It was a girl in a light apricot-colored cotton and linen dress, her straight black hair casually draped over her shoulders, her figure graceful—like a lily swaying in the breeze.","She looked so gentle and pure, yet surrounded by those men in black, she radiated an almost unbearable pressure.","The moment he saw her, the girl below seemed to sense it too. She looked up.","Startled, Chu Hai quickly shut the window.","“Damn it, why did this little mistress have to show up too?”","Lin Bing and the others were thrown off by his sudden reaction.","“Chu, what’s wrong? What’s going on down there?”","Chu Hai forced himself to stay calm and waved it off. “Nothing, nothing. Just a few drunks causing trouble. Everyone, have some tea. Tea.”","The more he tried to cover it up, the more curious Lei Yun and the others became.","Everyone present was a tycoon worth billions—they had seen their share of storms.","If a man like Chu Hai, head of AEG Capital, was this shaken, it couldn’t just be a few drunks brawling.","Lei Yun exchanged a glance with Huang Zhangming. They stood up, walked to the window, and reached for the latch.","“Hey! Hey!” Chu Hai tried to stop them, but it was too late.","As soon as Lei Yun opened the window and looked down, he gasped.","“Holy hell! They’ve arrested everyone from Yunlu Club?”","“Who the heck are these guys in black?”","“No idea, but they look serious. Reminds me of some foreign gangs.”","“...”","Seeing them still gawking out the window, Chu Hai lunged over, yanked them back, and slammed the window shut.","“Stop looking! Do you have a death wish?”","Huang Zhangming was annoyed by his reaction.","“Chu, you’re overreacting. We’re on the second floor, door closed. What are they gonna do, storm in and bite us?”","“Besides, this is the capital!”","Chu Hai looked at these clueless fools and nearly lost it.","“Mr. Huang, Mr. Lei, you have no idea who these people are. If you did, you’d run faster than rabbits.”","That hooked everyone’s interest.","“Chu, isn’t that an exaggeration?”","“Who are they? What’s their story? Tell us why a big capitalist like you is so terrified?”","Chu Hai took a deep breath and uttered a single name: “The Wanlong Society. Ever heard of it?”","Lei Yun paused. The name did ring a bell.","“Wanlong Society? Isn’t that the parent company of Wanhui Preferred—the one you invested in? Based in Mingzhu City? Pretty strong enterprise, right?”","Chu Hai gave a bitter smile. “Enterprise? Ha... that’s just the surface.”","“The real Wanlong Society is deeply criminal. They have thousands of these thug-like thugs in black on their payroll.”","“Thousands!”","At that, every business tycoon in the room shot up from their seats.","“Chu, are you serious? Thousands? Are we hearing that right?”","Damn, the men downstairs didn’t look like corporate employees or security guards—they looked like mobsters.","And this outfit supposedly had thousands of them?","Their first thought was: Is this still Dragon Country? How such a huge fish slip through the net without getting wiped out?","What kind of protection would it take to sustain such a terrifying force?","Chu Hai nodded heavily. “Yes, thousands. And they’re not just many—they’re ruthless. I’m telling you, in Mingzhu City... no, in this whole country, you’re better off offending some rich second-generation heirs or even officials than crossing the Wanlong Society—especially... their young lady.”","Lei Yun’s mind flashed back to the girl in the apricot dress downstairs. “You mean... the girl in the dress?”","Chu Hai: “Exactly! That little mistress!”","“Don’t let her looks fool you. I’m telling you, she’s cold and merciless. Those old gang bosses in Mingzhu City—Brother Dragon, Brother Tiger, Brother Leopard—she uprooted them one by one. They were either physically deleted or sent to rot in prison. Not a single one walked away.”","\"I once went over there to sign an investment agreement, and I saw with my own eyes a very influential local crime boss. Just because he offended her, she brought in a few hundred people and took him out! The craziest thing is, the cops were standing right there watching, and they didn't do a thing—they even helped seal off the scene!\"","Lei Yun: \"!!!\"","Lin Bin: \"!!!\"","Huang Zhangming: \"!!!\"","They were all just dying to ask Chu Hai: \"Are you sure that isn't some horror story that happened overseas?\""]},{"number":750,"title":"Chapter 750: 751, Qin Yunlu, Lin Yi (Thank you, 'Jin Pengshi', for the King of Gifts)","paragraphs":["“President Chu, aren’t you exaggerating? Would anyone really be that shady these days?”","“No wonder I saw you looking so down when you came back from Bright Pearl City. I was wondering why you were frowning then, given the strong momentum of your Universal Select investment. Now I finally understand.”","Chu Hai sighed. “I didn’t even want to bring up these embarrassing things. Who would have thought that young lady would suddenly appear here?”","“I’m not sure if she saw me just now. If she did, I figure none of us are getting out of here today.”","With that, he glanced at the others at the table. “When the time comes, you’ll each have to look out for yourselves.”","“Oh, and let me tell you one more thing: the billionaire Huang got sent away because he crossed her. You’ve all heard about that, right?”","Lei Yun nodded. “I’ve heard it, but what I know is that the billionaire went down for economic crimes...”","Chu Hai cut him off. “That’s just the surface. I’ve actually confirmed it with the man himself. He admitted to me it was this young lady who made the move.”","“In short, whether you’re a crime boss in the underworld or a billionaire business magnate, if you provoke her, you won’t end well.”","The others remained silent.","These high-ranking business elites, long accustomed to power, now had obvious tension on their faces.","“President Chu, so... what should we do now? Should we go downstairs and say hello?”","“Yeah, maybe we should greet her, at least make ourselves known and leave a good impression.”","Chu Hai waved his hand quickly. “No! Absolutely not! I can’t figure out that young lady’s temper at all. If she ends up roping us into something, it’ll be trouble.”","“Besides, she’s here in the capital for her own reasons. Let’s just pretend we didn’t see anything.”","Lei Yun, Huang Zhangming, and Lin Bing all nodded in agreement.","Just as they were whispering among themselves...","A black Audi pulled up at the entrance of the courtyard.","Then, two strikingly beautiful women with refined auras stepped out of the car.","The one walking in front was a woman in her mid-to-late twenties, dressed in a deep blue business suit. Her demeanor was sharp and commanding, exuding an imposing presence that inspired awe without need for anger.","The other, in her thirties, wore a custom-made moon-white cheongsam. Her figure was graceful, and every move carried the charm of a classic Jiangnan beauty.","The executives upstairs recognized the two women at a glance.","The one in the cheongsam was Qin Yunlu, the owner of Cloud Dew Club.","She was a well-known socialite in the capital’s circles, smooth and resourceful, with extensive connections.","The younger one, who had an air of authority, was named Lin Yi.","She was the only daughter of the Lin family’s eldest son and a greatly favored granddaughter of the Shen family. Currently serving in a government department, she had already reached a C-level leadership position at a young age—a rising star in the political arena.","The group’s expressions turned subtle at the sight of them.","This was going to be interesting.","On one side was someone who had swept in from Bright Pearl City—a “dragon crossing the river” with, let’s say, “just a hint” of dark methods.","On the other were two figures: one from a deep-rooted capital dynasty and a political rising star, the other a well-known local power player.","No one knew what sparks would fly when they met.","...","Downstairs, in the courtyard.","Qin Yunlu stepped inside and saw the wreckage, along with the security guards and the manager pinned to the ground. She frowned slightly.","But as someone who had weathered many storms, she didn’t lose her composure. Instead, she first looked at the unfamiliar girl surrounded by men in black.","This girl had an extraordinary aura.","Even dressed in such gentle, elegant attire, standing before those men, she looked like a queen on high.","Qin Yunlu had mingled in the capital for years and met countless people, but among the younger generation, only a handful could give her such a sense of pressure.","Still, as the owner of Cloud Dew Club, she maintained impeccable composure. With a smile on her face, she walked directly toward the girl.","“Miss, how should I address you?”","Liu Yutong replied, “My surname is Liu.”","Qin Yunlu said, “Miss Liu, a pleasure. I’m Qin, and I own Cloud Dew Club.”","She paused, glancing at the security guards and the manager under the control of the men in black.","“I’ve already heard about tonight. Young Master Zhou and Miss Lin were thoughtless and offended you—that’s their fault. You’ve vented your anger and administered your lesson. Could you do me a favor and let this matter rest?”","Liu Yutong didn’t reply. She just calmly studied Qin Yunlu.","Qin Yunlu was in no hurry, standing quietly with her professional smile still in place.","At that moment, Lin Yi approached.","She saw Lin Yue sitting on the ground, her face swollen like a pig’s head, and frowned deeply.","Lin Yue spotted Lin Yi too, like seeing a lifeline, tears streaming down her face.","“Sister Yi... Sister Yi, save me...”","Lin Yi found her disappointing, but nevertheless, Lin Yue was a member of the Lin family. She couldn’t just ignore her.","“Miss Liu, Lin Yue is from the Lin family. She was thoughtless and offended you, which was wrong. I apologize on her behalf.”","Liu Yutong asked, “Are you Lin Yi? Lin Dong’s niece?”","Lin Yi nodded. “It seems my third uncle has mentioned me. That figures.”","“Since you already know, I’ll be straightforward. We’re practically family—there’s no need to go too far, is there? No matter how reckless Lin Yue is, she’s still a Lin. If you really do anything harsh, it won’t be easy for my third uncle and aunt to explain things, right?”","Liu Yutong understood immediately upon hearing this. It seemed Lin Yi knew she was Jiang Lu’s daughter—why else would she speak in such a tone?","Interesting.","This eldest Miss Lin was much smarter than the foolish Lin Yue.","“Family? Miss Lin, you make it sound like I’m closely tied to the Lin family. I am myself, and the Lin family is the Lin family. We have no connection.”","Lin Yi replied, “Regardless, your mother is my third uncle’s wife, and you are her daughter. That blood relationship can’t be erased.”","“Of course, I know you didn’t grow up in the Lin family and have no attachment to it. What Lin Yue did tonight was indeed over the top—I wouldn’t let her off easily either.”","She paused and changed her tone.","“Still, Miss Liu, you’ve taught her enough tonight. Her face won’t recover for at least ten days or two weeks. Could you do me a favor and let her off the hook?”","Liu Yutong looked at her and suddenly smiled.","“Miss Lin, since you’ve put it that way, it would seem unreasonable of me to refuse.”","Lin Yi said, “Miss Liu is a wise person.”","Liu Yutong nodded. “Fine, I’ll grant you this favor.”","“But I have one condition.”","Lin Yi said, “Go ahead.”","Liu Yutong replied, “You owe me one.”","Lin Yi was taken aback for a moment, then nodded readily. “Alright, I agree!”","Liu Yutong raised an eyebrow, somewhat surprised that the other woman had agreed so quickly.","She didn’t dwell on it. Instead, she turned to Qin Yunlu and reached out to take the gold card.","“Manager Qin, I’ll accept this card. Let’s call what happened tonight settled.”","Qin Yunlu, who had been anxiously holding her breath, finally relaxed. “Miss Liu, you’re very gracious. I’ll remember this favor.”","She then took an exquisite business card from her handbag and handed it to Liu Yutong with both hands.","“This is my private card. If you ever need anything in the capital, Miss Liu, feel free to reach out.”","Liu Yutong took the card and glanced at it.","The design was simple and elegant—just the name “Qin Yunlu” and a phone number, with no titles at all.","A card like this was usually only given to people she truly acknowledged.","“You’re too kind, Manager Qin.”","Liu Yutong put the card away, then lifted her gaze toward the second floor.","There, a curtain in one of the windows was still faintly swaying—clearly, someone had been watching from behind it.","“Manager Qin, let’s leave it at that for tonight. I happen to have a friend upstairs, so I’ll go say hello.”","Qin Yunlu was momentarily taken aback. She followed Liu Yutong’s gaze to the second floor.","A friend?","That private room upstairs was reserved tonight for General Manager Lei Yun, wasn’t it?","“Oh, so Miss Liu has a friend here. In that case, I won’t keep you. I’ll invite you for tea another day.”","Liu Yutong nodded and, accompanied by a few men in black from Cloud City, headed upstairs.","Qin Yunlu stood still, watching her retreating figure, a sharp glint flickering in her eyes.","By the time Liu Yutong disappeared at the top of the stairs, Qin Yunlu had already sent Zhou Dashao and Lin Yue to the hospital, then pulled Lin Yi into her office—clearly, she had something to discuss.","Meanwhile.","After seeing Zhou Dashao and Lin Yue onto the ambulance, Manager Han slipped into a corner and made a phone call.","“Boss, Liu Yutong has shown up in the capital...”"]},{"number":751,"title":"Chapter 751: 752, Want to Snatch It (Thanks for the Gift King from 'Jin Peng Shi')","paragraphs":["In the second-floor private room, Chu Hai, Lei Yun, Huang Zhangming, and Lin Bing were huddled by the window, watching the commotion downstairs.","\"How is it? Is that young mistress coming up?\"","\"She's coming up, she's coming up! Holy crap, those black-suited guys behind her are coming up too!\"","\"Is she here for President Chu?\"","\"Did she see President Chu?\"","\"Probably not. Maybe she's just passing by...\"","\"Stop with the nonsense! Close the door first! Close it!\"","They hurriedly shut the door to the private room, then leaned against it, hearts pounding.","After catching his breath, Lei Yun suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha...\"","His laughter caught the other three off guard.","\"President Lei, what are you laughing at?\"","Lei Yun pointed at them and said between laughs, \"No, look... look at us. We're big-shot bosses worth hundreds of millions, hiding behind a door scared of a twenty-year-old girl. If word gets out, how are we supposed to hold our heads up?\"","Lin Bing froze for a moment, then chuckled too. \"Now that you mention it, it is pretty embarrassing.\"","Huang Zhangming's mouth twitched as he tried to stay serious, but in the end, he couldn't help joining in the laughter.","Chu Hai looked at these three carefree fools and his face darkened. \"You still have the nerve to laugh? Wait until that young mistress really barges in here—let's see if you're still laughing then!\"","No sooner had he spoken.","Knock, knock, knock!","The sound of knocking rang out.","Their laughter stopped instantly!","All three turned to Chu Hai as if to say, \"You jinx!\"","But deep down, they clung to a sliver of hope that maybe it was a wrong door.","Until the girl's voice came from outside.","\"President Chu, since you've already seen me, aren't you going to come out and say hello?\"","Chu Hai, hearing her call him by name, knew there was no escape.","He sighed and opened the door.","In the hallway outside stood Liu Yutong.","She wore the same light apricot dress, had the same stunningly beautiful face, and carried the same calm, indifferent expression.","But for some reason, in Chu Hai's eyes, she was more terrifying than a demon summoner.","\"Miss... Miss Liu, what a coincidence. I didn't expect to run into you here.\"","Liu Yutong looked at him and couldn't help but smile.","\"President Chu, what's wrong? You look like you've seen a ghost. Am I that scary?\"","Chu Hai quickly waved his hands. \"No, no, absolutely not! I'm just surprised to see you in the capital. It's a pleasant surprise—a huge pleasant surprise!\"","Liu Yutong: \"A pleasant surprise? Then what were you guys chatting about when you spotted me through the window?\"","Chu Hai: \"...\"","What could he say?","That he was gossiping about how ruthless and scheming she was?","That would be asking for death.","Liu Yutong didn't press him further. She simply walked into the room.","Inside, Lei Yun, Huang Zhangming, and Lin Bing stood in a row like misbehaving schoolkids, their expressions a mix of tension, fear, bewilderment, and awkwardness.","Every single one of them was a heavyweight in the business world, commanding respect.","Now they were standing like they were being scolded in front of a twenty-year-old girl. If anyone heard about this, they'd never believe it.","When Liu Yutong realized all three were familiar faces, she paused. Then her eyes fell on the engineering prototype phone next to the tea table.","She quickly pieced together what they were discussing here.","She'd heard rumors from her past life many times.","They said Lei Yun once wanted to invest in Meizu and had long talks with Huang Zhangming. In the end, Huang Zhangming turned down the investment because he couldn't bear to part with equity and control.","Later, Lei Yun founded Xiaomi on his own, while Meizu fell behind under the siege of capital and eventually became just another \"other.\"","And right now, the people in this room happened to be the key players from those days.","Lei Yun, the future Lei Jun.","Huang Zhangming, the founder of Meizu.","Lin Bing, the future head of MU.","And Chu Hai—well, he was the real old acquaintance.","With this lineup, plus that prototype phone, it was clearly about investment and equity talks.","Liu Yutong understood.","At that moment, Lei Yun and the others snapped out of it, thinking: since they couldn't avoid her, they'd face her head-on.","Lei Yun was the first to greet Liu Yutong, extending his hand. \"Miss Liu, it's an honor.\"","Liu Yutong shook his hand politely. \"President Lei, you're too kind.\"","Then Huang Zhangming and the others shook hands with her too, marking a first acquaintance.","Seeing that she wasn't as terrifying as imagined—in fact, quite courteous—Lei Yun and Huang Zhangming relaxed a little, no longer as scared as before.","Chu Hai quickly invited Liu Yutong to sit down in the main seat.","The others then took their seats again one by one.","But the atmosphere was still a bit stiff, and no one spoke for a while.","Liu Yutong found it odd. Why were they so afraid of her when they first met?","Was it just because of the incident downstairs?","That couldn't be it, could it?","She didn't dwell on it and decided to break the ice.","\"President Lei, you're here to talk business, aren't you?\"","Lei Yun quickly waved his hand. \"No, no. Just friends hanging out, having tea, chatting. Nothing serious.\"","Liu Yutong looked at him with a knowing half-smile.","That look sent shivers down Lei Yun's spine.","He felt like this girl's eyes could see right through him.","Huang Zhangming watched too, feeling uneasy. For some reason, he had a bad feeling—like his precious company was being eyed by a venomous snake.","Liu Yutong cut straight to the chase.","\"President Lei, no need to hide it. I'd say you're discussing an investment in Meizu with President Huang, right?\"","At her words, the room fell dead silent.","Lei Yun's smile froze completely.","Huang Zhangming's expression changed too.","Chu Hai shrank into a corner, wishing the floor would swallow him up.","He wasn't really scared of meeting Liu Yutong; he was afraid she'd think he was trying to cut her out. Even though the investment had nothing to do with her, getting caught hiding it was bound to cause misunderstandings.","Lin Bing, meanwhile, stared at Liu Yutong in shock, wondering how she knew.","Lei Yun, seeing that the cat was out of the bag, sighed and came clean. \"Miss Liu, you're really sharp. You're right—we were talking about investing in Meizu, seeing if there's a chance to work together.\"","Liu Yutong nodded, then turned her gaze to Huang Zhangming.","\"President Huang, would you mind letting me take a look at your prototype phone?\"","Without waiting for an answer, Yun Cheng behind her grabbed the prototype and handed it to Liu Yutong.","Huang Zhangming: \"...\"","Did you even need to ask? Your subordinate already took it. And would I dare say no?","\"Miss Liu, please, go ahead.\"","\"Thanks.\"","Liu Yutong took the phone and examined it carefully.","A 3.5-inch screen, rounded body, exquisite craftsmanship—for its time, it was definitely top-tier.","She unlocked the screen, swiped a few times, and opened a couple of apps to test them.","The fluidity was pretty good, and the UI design was quite distinctive. The skeuomorphic icons were exquisite—far better than the shoddily made knockoff phones on the market. No wonder Lei Yun had taken a liking to this company in her past life. They really did have unique strengths.","After looking it over for a while, Liu Yutong handed the phone back to Huang Zhangming.","Then she turned to Lei Yun and said something that stunned everyone in the room.","\"Mr. Lei, save your efforts. MeiZu is not an investment you can make. I said so.\"","The moment she spoke, the expressions of everyone present changed.","What was this? Was this woman too domineering? Just one sentence, and they were supposed to give up on the investment? What did she mean by that?","Chu Hai, in particular, felt his heart sink: \"As I feared, what I dreaded most has happened. This young lady must be angry and planning to snatch it away directly!\"","......"]},{"number":752,"title":"Chapter 752: 753, Forced Buying and Selling","paragraphs":["“Damn it! This young lady has definitely set her sights on this fat piece of meat!” Chu Hai couldn’t help but rant inwardly.","Lei Yun’s mind was also flooded with a herd of grass-mud horses galloping through at that moment.","The Meizu project was something he’d been following for so long, and this woman wanted to cut in just as she arrived, even blocking him from investing—how domineering was that?","Huang Zhangming’s face didn’t look too good either.","He detested nothing more than having others meddle in his affairs, and he detested even more being treated like prey.","Earlier, when Chu Hai had said this woman was treacherous and ruthless, he had listened with only half a belief. But now, seeing her in action, it seemed to ring true.","Her first sentence had declared that Meizu would receive no investment—what exactly was that supposed to mean? Was she trying to spoil his investment?","Lei Yun, being someone with an easygoing temperament and calm demeanor, quickly pulled his emotions together.","“Miss Liu, you’re joking. We were just chatting casually—there’s no talk of investing or not. Besides, this company is built by President Huang himself. Whether to invest or not is entirely up to him, right, President Huang?”","He kicked the ball right over to Huang Zhangming.","Huang Zhangming nodded. “Miss Liu, Meizu was founded by me, and I hold absolute controlling shares. Messrs. Lei and Chu just came over for a friendly chat to exchange ideas and insights—we haven’t even reached the investment stage.”","Translated, that meant: The affairs of Meizu are none of an outsider’s business.","Seeing their reaction, Liu Yutong realized they had misunderstood. “President Huang, do you mind if I speak directly?”","Huang Zhangming showed no fear. “Go ahead.”","But Liu Yutong didn’t follow the usual script. She dropped a bombshell right from the start. “President Huang, you never intended to accept investment from the beginning, did you?”","Huang Zhangming’s face instantly changed.","She continued, “Or to put it another way, you simply can’t stomach the dilution of your equity. You want to turn Meizu into a family-run business, keeping full control in your own hands. The money, resources, and networks Mr. Lei brings—you really do want them, but you’d probably give at most a tiny share of equity, without letting go of much.”","Then she turned her gaze to Lin Bing, who was standing nearby.","“As for you, Engineer Lin, I’d guess Mr. Lei invited you to join Meizu. I think someone with your ability deserves no less than a 5% equity incentive, or even more. But I’d bet my money that President Huang won’t give it to you—because he’s too stingy to part with it.”","“Am I right, President Huang?” She asked him again.","Huang Zhangming opened his mouth to argue but found himself utterly at a loss for words. His heart was even tinged with alarm.","Did this woman have mind-reading abilities? How could she know exactly what he was thinking?","They’d only just met for the first time!","Seeing Huang Zhangming left speechless, Lei Yun knew that Liu Yutong had probably hit the mark.","He had invited Lin Bing precisely to introduce him to Huang Zhangming. A talent like that joining Meizu would be a powerful boost to the company, and offering some equity as incentive seemed only reasonable.","But now it was clear—that man had never planned to restructure the company into a more corporatized equity system.","No wonder every time equity came up, Huang Zhangming always been evasive and dragged his feet.","In his previous life, Lei Yun and Huang Zhangming had gone through a long negotiation period, only for Lei Yun to eventually launch Big Rice with Lin Bing. Huang Zhangming could only watch as Big Rice grew step by step, while he, short on funds and resources, backed the wrong horse, and stumbled relentlessly in the mobile phone market.","In the end, he ended up being acquired by others.","A former shining star of domestic phones was ruined by his own controlling nature and miserly ways.","“President Huang, do you know what that mindset of yours will lead to in the end?”","Looking him straight in the eyes, she said each word distinctly, “You will run Meizu into the ground!”","“Honestly, I feel sorry for you.”","“At least I think Mr. Lei came to you with capital, resources, and connections—this is a chance for you and Meizu alike. In my opinion, if you accept his investment now and bring him and Engineer Lin on board as top management, Meizu could become a super power in the future, capable of competing even with world-class famous brands.”","“But, President Huang, you don’t have the vision or the generosity for it.”","“It’s no wonder that Meizu is headed for decline under your leadership.”","Her words gave Huang Zhangming absolutely no face, practically belittling him as worthless.","Chu Hai looked at Huang Zhangming’s dark, furious expression and thought: Is this young lady here to pick a fight today? Will Huang die from sheer anger?","As expected.","Huang Zhangming finally exploded.","“Miss Liu, what gives you the right to judge me like that? Do you really think you know me?”","“And besides—Meizu is mine! How I run it is my own business! Aren’t you meddling too much?”","Liu Yutong, as if knowing he’d react that way, didn’t get angry. On the contrary, she nodded. “President Huang is right—Meizu is yours, and your way of handling it is your own business.”","“But still, I’d like to ask one more thing: Will you sell Meizu? If you do, just name your price. I won’t bargain.”","???","The sudden shift had everyone thrown off yet again.","What?","Acquisition?","Wait—she’d gone through all that just to reveal that her real goal was to buy out Meizu?","Lei Yun couldn’t help stealing glances at several men wearing black suits who hovered nearby like something out of a crime thriller. They got a chill thinking: Could this woman actually be planning to force President Huang to sign under duress?","This whole scene looked like something straight out of a gangster hostage drama.","Once again, their impression of this girl was being rewritten from the ground up.","No wonder Chairman Chu kept saying this young lady was a prankster running wild from start to finish. They had come to invest—she had come to ruin the whole show.","Huang Zhangming’s face flushed with steel-like fury.","After all Chu Hai had ranted earlier, his mind naturally guessed along the same lines as Lei Yun—this woman had ill intentions and likely planned to strong-arm him into selling, relying on shady connections behind her.","But he was a stubborn man, deeply headstrong about his independence. And besides, Meizu was his own “flesh and blood”—how could he ever just let it go?","Though he did have a very real fear of this woman’s presence, he clenched his teeth and refused.","“Miss Liu, Meizu is a company carved out by the hands that built it, my own life’s work. I will never yield it easily, no matter if you pulled a blade and put it to my throat—I wouldn’t give in!”","As he spoke, he actually stretched his neck out, putting on a dramatic face of certain-defiance.","Liu Yutong was flummoxed: “? ? ? ”","Wait, was this man crazy?","She only asked off-handedly; if he wasn’t selling, just say no—now he was stretching his neck out like he expected beheading?","And she couldn’t figure out why, from the moment she entered the room, several of these big men had looked at her with such a strange expression.","As if, in their eyes, she was some lawless female merciless brat.","And she had only just met them for the first time! Was her reputation really that fallen already?"]},{"number":753,"title":"Chapter 753: 754, Boss Huang Stormed Off in Anger","paragraphs":["Huang Zhangming stretched his neck like a goose, bobbing his head back and forth, his face filled with a look of unyielding defiance!","Liu Yutong found it utterly speechless.","She felt that this guy was missing a screw somewhere.","Like a complete lunatic!","Then she cast a suspicious glance at Chu Hai.","Cold sweat broke out on Chu Hai’s forehead. “Miss Liu... Chairwoman Liu, my admiration for you is like a mighty river flowing endlessly! How could I ever speak ill of you behind your back?”","Liu Yutong found his words strangely off, but she didn’t dwell on it. She spoke to Huang Zhangming again.","“President Huang, since you don’t want to sell, I won’t force you.”","“But I do want to give you one piece of advice: In business, the most important thing isn’t what you hold in your hands, but who stands by your side.”","Huang Zhangming snorted coldly, about to say something like “thanks for your concern.”","Just then, his phone rang.","He pulled it out impatiently and saw the caller ID was a trusted subordinate from the company. His brow furrowed as a sense of foreboding washed over him.","He gestured to the people in the room and walked to a corner to answer the call.","“Hello?”","“President Huang! It’s bad! Huge trouble!”","Huang Zhangming’s heart skipped a beat. He quickly asked.","“Old Zhou? What’s wrong? Why are you panicking? What happened?”","Old Zhou was his company’s vice president, a loyal confidant who had worked with him for years.","For him to call so frantically, it had to be serious.","“President Huang, a lot of people from our technical team are leaving!”","“What? Leaving? Talk clearly! Who’s leaving?”","“It’s our R&D team, including Engineer Liu from hardware, Engineer Wang from software, Team Leader Li from UI design... many core members. They’ve all been poached!”","“Just now, they submitted their resignations en masse, saying they’re jumping ship to a new company!”","Huang Zhangming’s mind went blank. It was like a bomb went off.","Engineer Liu, Engineer Wang, Team Leader Li... these were the core technical pillars of Meizu!","How could they leave? And why all at once?","“Who? Who poached them?”","“It’s... Long Yao Technology.”","“I looked into it. It’s a newly established company, reportedly backed by a large conglomerate from the eastern region. They’re loaded and throwing money around—offering double salaries plus stock options!”","“And... and they’ve promised Engineer Liu and the others a better R&D platform, greater room for growth, and... a full set of the latest experimental equipment...”","Huang Zhangming stopped listening to what Old Zhou said next. He felt the room spin, darkness closing in.","Long Yao Technology.","Long Yao... Long...","Wait!","He whipped his head around, glaring at Liu Yutong.","Long Yao... Wanlong Society... Liu Yutong... Long...","“You did this, didn’t you?”","Huang Zhangming pointed at Liu Yutong, furious. “Did you poach my people? Long Yao Technology is your company, right?”","Liu Yutong nodded calmly. “It is mine! A few of us are very optimistic about the smartphone market. Since you, President Huang, weren’t willing to sell your company, I had to start my own and poach a few talents along the way. Isn’t that fair enough?”","Huang Zhangming saw her shamelessly admit it, trembling with rage.","He really felt like he’d been made a fool of.","She must have known all along that he wouldn’t accept the acquisition offer. That’s why she asked.","Her real target was his technical team all along.","First, she blocked Lei Yun’s investment, then she tried to acquire Meizu—all just to distract him and enjoy his misery. Finally, she’d pull the rug out from under him!","Having pieced it all together, Huang Zhangming felt a tightness in his chest and a bitter taste in his throat. He nearly spat blood.","“You... you’ve gone too far!”","Seeing his distress, Lei Yun quickly stepped forward to support him. “President Huang, are you okay? Calm down, don’t get worked up!”","Huang Zhangming shook off Lei Yun’s hand, clutching his chest, his eyes locked onto Liu Yutong like he wanted to devour her.","“Fine... just fine, Liu Yutong! Today, I’ve seen what it means to stop at nothing! You’re a corporate bandit! Mafia tactics!”","Liu Yutong frowned at this. “President Huang, I don’t like what you’re saying. What mafia? In business competition, it’s every man for himself. Your people chose to jump ship. I offered more money, better conditions, and they came willingly. What’s the problem?”","“If you want to keep them, it’s simple—raise their pay, give them some equity, stop being so stingy, and they won’t leave.”","“Besides, weren’t you always reluctant to give up control? Now that your people are gone, you can hire a new batch from scratch, train them fresh—all compliant newcomers. That way, control stays firmly in your hands. Isn’t that perfect?”","“I... you...”","Huang Zhangming’s lips quivered, wanting to curse her out, but he held back.","Because he saw the black-suited man behind her, whose fists really were as big as a sack.","“Fine. I’ll remember you!”","Still fuming, he stormed out of the room in a huff.","After Huang Zhangming left, the room went quiet.","Lei Yun, Chu Hai, and Lin Bing stared dumbfounded at the scene.","What just happened?","Huang Zhangming’s core technical team had been poached?","The poacher was Long Yao Technology, and Long Yao Tech was Liu Yutong’s?","Wait, this woman moved fast and hard, didn’t she?","They were just discussing investment and acquisition a moment ago, and right after rejection, his people were gone?","This wasn’t a negotiation—it was outright robbery!","Chu Hai mentally screamed: I knew it! I fucking knew it! The moment she said she wanted to acquire Huang Zhangming’s company, I felt something was off!","And sure enough, she nearly ripped him apart root and branch!","The she-devil strikes again—ruthless, unpredictable, and sharp as a knife!","Lei Yun took a deep breath, trying to steady himself.","He looked at Liu Yutong again, a mix of emotions in his eyes—wariness, caution, and a hint of... admiration.","To be honest, he agreed with what Liu Yutong had said earlier.","The biggest problem with Meizu was Huang Zhangming’s narrow vision. If he kept clinging to a king-of-his-own-castle mentality, Meizu would never go far.","Better to let someone with strategic insight take the reins.","But he never expected Liu Yutong to just act on it.","She went ahead and nearly cleaned house!","Still, in business, poaching is common practice.","If your offer is worse, and your people get lured away, it’s your own fault.","Liu Yutong’s methods might rub people the wrong way, but she wasn’t technically in the wrong.","Still... Lei Yun looked at Liu Yutong’s alarmingly young face and a thought crept into his mind.","This woman—was she friend or foe to him?","Her earlier intervention to stop him from investing in Meizu—was it truly for his benefit, or did she have some other scheme?","And her poaching of Meizu's technical team—did she really intend to make phones, or was there a hidden agenda behind it?","Lei Yun kept thinking, and the more he thought, the more unfathomable this woman became.","To be honest, this was the first time he had encountered someone so utterly inscrutable—and a girl nearly twenty years his junior, no less. The whole thing felt absurd!","Since he couldn't figure her out, it was best to keep his distance.","Being around her made him feel transparent, as if he couldn't hide a single thing. It was far too unsettling.","But just as he was about to find an excuse to slip away,","Liu Yutong spoke up first, calling them back.","\"Now that President Huang has left, that's perfect timing.\"","\"Presidents Lei, Lin, and Chu, I think we can take this opportunity to discuss the investment in starting a new company.\""]},{"number":754,"title":"Chapter 754: 755, Invest in a New Company","paragraphs":["Invest in a new company?","What was she up to now?","After a moment of silence, Lei Yun spoke up first to ask, \"Miss Liu, what kind of company are you looking to invest in?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Smartphones, of course.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, everyone was stunned again.","Wait, didn't you already have a phone company called Long Yao? Why are you starting another new one?","Before they could voice their confusion, Liu Yutong turned the question back to Lei Yun.","\"President Lei, deep down, you've always wanted to make phones yourself, haven't you?\"","Lei Yun froze. He instinctively wanted to deny it, but the words died in his throat.","Liu Yutong continued, \"Let me guess. After the release of the iPhone, you started researching and choosing this industry. You saw early on that mobile internet was the future, and that phones would be the entry point to that future. You really wanted to jump in, to seize this opportunity.\"","\"But you didn't have the right starting point.\"","\"Doing it yourself—no experience, too much risk, issues with supply chains and systems. That's why you prioritized investing in a promising brand first, at least to learn the ropes. So you chose Meizu, hoping to leverage Huang Zhangming's team to quickly break into this market.\"","\"Unfortunately, Huang Zhangming isn't easy to deal with. His vision is too narrow.\"","\"Still, during your exchanges with him and your field research, you familiarized yourself with the entire phone manufacturing process and picked up some experience.\"","\"In fact, you've already decided not to invest in President Huang's Meizu anymore. You're planning to partner up with Engineer Lin to start your own venture. Partly because of me, but I don't think that's the main reason...\"","\"President Lei, am I right about all of this?\"","Lei Yun fell completely silent. In fact, he was utterly stunned—beyond words.","What was this? This woman was terrifying, almost supernatural, wasn't she?","Were they sure this wasn't their first meeting?","How could she have read every single thought in his head, even his half-formed plans, with such perfect accuracy?","No wonder President Chu, whenever he mentioned her, would occasionally have a look on his face like he'd seen a ghost. He was feeling that same way now. It truly felt like encountering a ghost.","Too terrifying. Absolutely terrifying.","As Chu Hai watched the shocked expression on Lei Yun's face, he felt a secret sense of satisfaction.","President Lei, President Lei—now you finally get to experience the dread of being bossed around by this heiress of the Wanlong Association, right?","As a seasoned investor, he had dealt with countless entrepreneurs and big shots, but only when facing this girl Liu Yutong did he feel an overwhelming sense of helplessness—completely led by the nose, dominated, unable to fight back. It was deeply frustrating.","Seeing Lei Yun's face now made him feel much better.","After his silence ended, Lei Yun admitted openly, \"Miss Liu, you guessed right. I do want to start my own business, but starting from scratch isn't easy. Even for me, I'm not sure I'd succeed.\"","Building a team from zero, developing a system, designing hardware, securing the supply chain, setting up distribution channels... every step required huge amounts of capital and time.","Even for someone like him, he couldn't just jump in recklessly. That was why he had chosen to invest in Huang Zhangming's Meizu instead.","Starting his own venture was only something he'd consider as a last resort.","Liu Yutong saw his hesitation and cut straight to the point. \"President Lei, I know what you're worried about. Starting from zero really is too hard, too risky.\"","\"But what if I told you I want to invest in you?\"","Lei Yun was jolted. He lifted his head sharply.","Invest in him?","So that was her angle?","Liu Yutong said, \"President Lei, I'm a straightforward person. I don't like beating around the bush. I really believe in you. In your judgment of mobile internet, in your understanding of products, and in your ability to execute.\"","\"If you're willing to get into the phone business yourself, I can invest—no, I will invest. And I won't take control. I'll even sign a unanimous shareholder agreement.\"","This statement landed like a bombshell in the private room.","Lei Yun was stunned.","Chu Hai was stunned.","Lin Bing was stunned, too.","No control? Was that for real?","A woman like her, who seemed so domineering and possessive, was willing to give up the absolute power to call the shots?","That didn't fit her persona at all!","Chu Hai looked at Liu Yutong in disbelief, wondering if the sun had started rising in the west.","Wait, since when had this young lady become so easygoing?","Back when he invested in the internet cafe chain and Wanhui Youxuan, he'd tried to bring in another board member, and she wouldn't have it. He and Old Ji could only throw money and resources around, without a single ounce of say in anything.","Now, suddenly, she'd had a change of heart?","Or was she setting a trap for President Lei to fall into?","Liu Yutong seemed to notice Chu Hai's doubt and gave him a cool glance. \"President Chu, don't look at me like that. I mean what I say. I won't take control. In the new company, President Lei can do whatever he wants. I won't meddle in day-to-day management.\"","\"I'll just provide the money, the resources, and the connections. President Lei handles the strategy, makes the phones, and sells them.\"","\"A win-win partnership.\"","Lei Yun fell silent again.","Honestly, the terms were too tempting.","So tempting that he couldn't believe it.","The helmswoman of a multi-billion-dollar business empire, the young mistress of the Wanlong Association with thousands of men at her command, was voluntarily offering to invest in him and giving up control?","This was way too abnormal.","So abnormal that he couldn't help wondering if she had ulterior motives, or maybe she planned to fatten him up before pulling the rug out from under him.","After all, Chu Hai had painted her as something terrifying. He couldn't help but overthink.","If Liu Yutong knew how Chu Hai had been spreading rumors about her, she'd definitely make him pay.","Seeing Lei Yun still hesitating, she asked again, \"President Lei, are you wondering why I trust you so much?\"","Lei Yun nodded. \"Miss Liu, we're total strangers. This really feels... I don't know, overwhelming—and honestly, a little frightening.\"","Liu Yutong let out a light laugh. \"President Lei, you're too modest. What do you mean strangers? Your name is legendary to me.\"","\"Kingsoft, Netease, UC... Every project you've invested in has paid off handsomely. I trust your ability to build products.\"","\"You're already this strong. Why would I fight you for control? That would be shooting myself in the foot. I'll leave professional matters to the professionals. Once the company grows and goes public, all I need to do is hold out a sack to collect the cash.\"","Hearing this, Lei Yun paused for a few seconds, then suddenly broke into a smile.","\"Miss Liu, you're the first person to make me feel truly unreadable, truly hard to figure out.\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"Is that so?\"","Lei Yun said, \"Yes. But none of that matters now. What matters is that you've definitely convinced me.\"","The truth was, he already had the idea of starting his own phone company. He wasn't short on money—he still had billions lying idle in his bank account.","But since he wanted to start a business, money was one thing, and another equally important factor was resources.","Although the woman before him might seem a bit shady, the resources under her company were indeed very helpful for his entrepreneurial venture.","For example, Wanhui Select, the largest group-buying platform in the country, had hundreds of thousands of delivery riders, making it suitable for both promotion and sales.","There was also Weibo, the largest social media platform in the country, which could generate massive traffic and trending topics for the company’s products.","In short, he needed all of these.","However, he still had one concern in his mind—this heiress had also founded her own mobile phone company. Would she use his newly established company as cannon fodder?","At that moment, Liu Yutong once again fully demonstrated her terrifying persona.","\"I think the world is vast, and the market is big enough. There’s no reason two mobile phone companies can’t coexist.\"","\"Mr. Lei, if you’re uneasy about this, we can sign a deep cooperation agreement. For instance, your newly established company and mine can share technological achievements, complement each other’s strengths, and work for mutual benefit. Maybe someday the two of us can even join forces to take down Samsung and Apple, monopolizing the domestic and even the global market.\"","Lei Yun couldn’t help but say, \"Miss Liu, your ambition is truly frightening!\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"I’ll take that as a compliment. So, Mr. Lei, what’s your answer?\"","Lei Yun didn’t respond immediately. Instead, he looked at Lin Bing, who was standing nearby.","\"Lin Bing, what do you think?\"","Lin Bing had been silent all this time.","But his gaze toward Liu Yutong had shifted from the initial shock to admiration, and even a sincere sense of awe.","This girl was truly remarkable.","Not just superficially impressive—her depth was unfathomable.","At their very first meeting, she had completely exposed Huang Zhangming, stripping him bare, humiliating him, and shattering his composure.","She had also laid her plans early, cleanly poaching Huang Zhangming’s technical team.","Most importantly, her ability to judge people was spot-on. She could almost flawlessly guess your thoughts, your concerns, and your desires.","Someone like that was truly terrifying!","He believed no one would want to face such an enemy.","Of course, if she were a partner or an investor, that was a different story. It would be a rare opportunity.","\"Mr. Lei, I think we should go for it.\"","\"Miss Liu has strength, vision, and a keen eye for people. With her as an investor in the new company, our products are bound to reach the world!\""]},{"number":755,"title":"Chapter 755: 756. Cooperation Achieved A New Era Is Coming.","paragraphs":["As Lin Bing made her stance clear, the atmosphere in the private room shifted noticeably.","Lei Yun's heart, which had only been restless before, now could barely be contained.","To be honest, the terms Liu Yutong offered were simply too tempting: no control, no interference in daily management, only providing capital and resources, and even willing to sign a unanimous action agreement.","An investor like this was harder to find than a lantern in broad daylight.","Not to mention she held top-tier traffic gateways like Weibo and Wanhui Preferred, plus those mysterious yet clearly powerful connections... it was hard not to be tempted!","Chu Hai watched Liu Yutong from the side, his emotions a tangled mess.","This woman really knew how to read people.","She first tore down Huang Zhangming, making him seem worthless, then poached his technical team, driving him into a frenzy, and finally played her real card—investing in Lei Yun.","And for Lei Yun, the shift from caution and wariness toward Liu Yutong at the start to now feeling eager and approving—the transformation happened so fast he probably hadn't even noticed it himself.","Chu Hai couldn't help but give Liu Yutong a mental thumbs-up.","Brilliant. Absolutely brilliant.","She was indeed the only woman he had ever met in his life who made him look up to her.","Liu Yutong asked Lei Yun again, \"President Lei, what do you think? I'm just waiting for your word.\"","Lei Yun didn't hesitate anymore. He stood up and extended his hand.","\"Miss Liu, let's work together.\"","Liu Yutong shook his hand.","\"Looking forward to our collaboration.\"","The moment their hands clasped, the gears of history silently turned, and a new business empire laid its foundation in that small private room.","Chu Hai, watching from the side, felt his eyes burn with envy. He quickly stepped closer, rubbing his hands together, and asked, \"Um... Miss Liu, can I get in on this new company investment too?\"","Liu Yutong looked at him with a knowing smile. \"President Chu, weren't you just hiding from me behind that window? Why aren't you hiding now?\"","Chu Hai's smile froze, and he scrambled to explain, \"Miss Liu, you misunderstand! It's a huge misunderstanding! I was just... that was...\"","\"That was what?\"","\"That was... I was afraid of disturbing your important business! Yes, that's it—afraid of getting in your way!\"","Liu Yutong was amused by his clumsy excuse. \"Alright, President Chu, if you want to invest, go ahead. But I'll lay it out straight: the management of the new company stays with President Lei. Do you have any objections?\"","Chu Hai quickly shook his head. \"None at all! I wholeheartedly agree! I'll just put in some money and be a quiet little shareholder. I won't interfere in management. Whatever President Lei says goes—if he says go east, I'll never go west!\"","Are you kidding? Just being allowed on this ship was lucky enough. He wouldn't dare object.","He had two hundred percent trust in Liu Yutong's judgment now.","Just look at the explosive success of Wanhui Preferred, the daily active users of Weibo, and even the chain of internet cafes he'd invested in earlier—all thriving.","Stick with her, and you followed the god of wealth.","Of course, the key was not to anger her.","Lin Bing watched this unfold from the side, emotions swirling within her.","That whole evening—from Huang Zhangming refusing investment and acquisition, to witnessing his technical team get poached, and then Liu Yutong decisively sealing the deal to invest in Lei Yun's new company—in just one hour, the plot twists and turns were more dramatic than any business negotiation she had ever seen.","And the driving force behind it all was just this young woman who looked barely twenty.","\"Miss Liu, I have a question I'd like to ask,\" Lin Bing suddenly said.","Liu Yutong replied, \"Feel free, Engineer Lin.\"","Lin Bing asked, \"You mentioned earlier that your companies are willing to share technology with President Lei. If both companies fully share technology, wouldn't they risk being in direct competition? From a business logic standpoint, that seems risky.\"","This question was sharp, and it hit on the very doubt lingering in Lei Yun's mind.","That's right.","If both companies had identical technology, wouldn't that create serious overlap?","Liu Yutong thought about the question for a moment before asking in return, \"Engineer Lin, how big do you think the future smartphone market will be?\"","Lin Bing paused to think and then gave a bold guess: \"With ongoing technological iteration, I believe global annual shipments will be at least over a billion units.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"A billion units. Even if China's market only accounts for ten percent of that, it's still a market worth hundreds of billions. Do you think someone like me can eat that entire pie by myself?\"","Lin Bing froze and shook her head instinctively.","Liu Yutong continued, \"Exactly. I can't, and industry monopolies are almost impossible in this sector.\"","\"The phones President Lei is about to make will likely differ from those my companies produce—in positioning, target audience, and even core selling points. We can engage in differentiated competition, complement each other's strengths, rather than tearing each other apart.\"","\"Besides, while the domestic market is huge, the overseas market is even bigger. Why waste time fighting among ourselves and draining energy internally, when we could join forces to drive out foreign brands and seize the global market? That’s the real sea of stars worth chasing.\"","After hearing this, Lin Bing felt a sudden clarity.","\"Miss Liu, I’ve learned a great deal.\"","\"Miss Liu, your vision truly humbles me!\"","Chu Hai nodded enthusiastically on the side: \"Exactly, exactly! Chairman Liu’s vision is absolutely top-tier! The first time I met her, I was deeply impressed by it! My admiration for Chairman Liu flows like an endless river, like a flood that can never be contained!\"","Lei Yun and Lin Bing couldn’t help but silently roast him in their minds.","Admiration? More like intimidation, right?","Liu Yutong then thought of something. \"Oh, by the way, President Lei, I have one small suggestion.\"","Lei Yun: \"Please, go ahead, Miss Liu.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Can we use the name 'Big Rice' for the new company?\"","\"Big Rice?\"","Lei Yun was taken aback, but the words \"Big Rice Phone\" immediately flashed in his mind.","It sounded quite catchy—simple, easy to remember, and oddly familiar.","\"Big Rice... Big Rice Phone... What a great name! Really, a fantastic name! Miss Liu, you’ve chosen it so skillfully—simple, memorable, and down-to-earth!\"","Liu Yutong smiled to herself, thinking: Of course it’s great. You came up with this name after much thought in your past life, I just borrowed it early.","Just then, her phone buzzed.","She pulled it out and saw a text from her older sister, Gao Min: [Evidence secured. Closing in soon.]","It seemed her sister’s side was progressing smoothly, so there was no need for her to worry further. She put the phone away and said to Lei Yun and the others, \"President Lei, Engineer Lin, President Chu, that’s all for tonight. I’ll arrange for someone to handle the details with you tomorrow.\"","Lei Yun quickly stood up. \"Of course, of course. Take care, Miss Liu.\"","Liu Yutong nodded, turned, and walked toward the door, followed closely by Yun Cheng and Lan Die.","As her figure disappeared at the top of the staircase, Lei Yun let out a long breath, as if releasing all the tension and stress of the evening.","\"President Chu, when you first told me this Miss Liu was formidable, I’ll be honest—I didn’t quite believe you. But now, I do.\"","Chu Hai replied, \"President Lei, you haven’t seen anything yet. Wait until you witness her methods for handling enemies—then you’ll know what truly formidable means.\"","At that moment, Lin Bing spoke up with a different perspective: \"I think Miss Liu is actually quite interesting.\"","Lei Yun and Chu Hai both turned to look at him.","Lin Bing shrugged, leaning back in his chair. \"Don’t you think so? She has vision, courage, skill, and most importantly... a very young and pretty face. A boss like that is hard to find, even with a lantern.\"","Lei Yun paused, then laughed. \"Lin Bing, if Miss Liu heard that, she’d probably be pretty happy.\"","Lin Bing: \"Happy or not, I don’t know. But I’m pretty happy, at least. No more having to look at Huang Zhangming’s dark face over at Meizu.\"","At the mention of Huang Zhangming, the three of them wore mixed expressions.","To be fair, that guy was indeed a genius. But probably because of his educational background, his vision was limited—his perspective just wasn’t broad enough.","Still, it didn’t matter now.","That poor fellow was probably hiding in some corner somewhere, crying over his shattered technical team.","Of course, none of that had anything to do with them anymore.","Because a new era had already arrived!"]},{"number":756,"title":"Chapter 756: 757, Lin Yi's Invitation.","paragraphs":["As Liu Yutong stepped out of the main gate, the window of the black Audi parked by the roadside rolled down, revealing a young, pretty face.","It was Lin Yi.","\"Miss Liu, got a moment to chat?\"","Liu Yutong paused mid-step and asked, \"Miss Lin, is there something you need?\"","Lin Yi pointed to the passenger seat. \"Get in, let's talk while we drive.\"","Liu Yutong turned back to say a few quick words to Yun Cheng, then opened the car door and slid into the passenger seat.","The car slowly pulled away from the Yunlu Club, heading west toward Xishan.","The night scenery of the imperial capital was ablaze with lights. Lin Yi drove steadily, her eyes fixed on the road ahead as she casually started the conversation.","\"Miss Liu, I'm curious—was coming to Yunlu tonight a coincidence, or deliberate?\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"Aren't you asking that knowing the answer already, Miss Lin?\"","Lin Yi smiled. \"I suppose I was overthinking it.\"","She paused, then shifted the topic. \"Miss Liu, we're practically family now, aren't we? Calling each other 'Miss Lin' and 'Miss Liu' feels too formal. Let me call you by your name, and you can call me Lin Yi, or Sister Yi if you like.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Alright, Sister Yi.\"","After all, Lin Yi was indeed a few years older, and she had been friendly from the start. At the very least, Liu Yutong had a decent impression of her.","At that moment, Lin Yi asked a question. \"The one Third Uncle agreed to back—was that you or your police officer sister?\"","Liu Yutong's gaze flickered with slight surprise.","She hadn't expected Lin Yi to know even this.","It seemed that this young woman, raised in the Shen family, still kept a close watch on the Lin family.","\"Sister Yi, you're really well-informed.\"","Lin Yi chuckled. \"I may not stay at the Lin family estate often, but I know a fair bit about what goes on. Third Uncle seems gentle and refined on the surface, but he's actually very stubborn. Whoever made him come to that decision definitely isn't an ordinary person.\"","\"So I figure it's either you or your sister. But my gut tells me your sister is the more likely candidate.\"","Liu Yutong neither confirmed nor denied it. Instead, she asked back, \"Does that bother you?\"","After all, Gao Min, to put it bluntly, had no blood ties to the Lin family.","Lin Yi shook her head. \"I grew up in the Shen family, and I know how important a successor is to a family. Third Uncle's decision is perfectly understandable.\"","She was actually quite disappointed with the other younger Lin family members. None of them seemed capable of carrying the family's banner.","That was until Liu Yutong and Gao Min suddenly appeared, bringing a glimmer of hope.","\"Still, I want to warn you—the circles in the imperial capital are much murkier than you think. You slapped Zhou Heng tonight, and the Zhou family won't let it go easily. Sure, Zhou Heng is a useless waste, but the Zhou family isn't. That old patriarch of theirs is notoriously protective and holds grudges over the smallest things.\"","\"Also, Lin Yue may be stupid, but her mother, Wang Jiangyao, is no pushover. Once Wang Jiangyao finds out you hit Lin Yue, given her personality, she'll definitely come after you. So, Yutong, you'll need to be careful for a while.\"","After hearing this, Liu Yutong asked, \"Is that you showing concern for me?\"","\"Still, a little advice like this doesn't count as you repaying your debt to me.\"","Lin Yi replied, \"Of course not. At least we're barely family, right?\"","Liu Yutong looked at her, a hint of amusement in her eyes.","This Lin Yi was quite interesting—smart, smooth, knew when to compromise, and handled things well. She was far better than a fool like Lin Yue.","No wonder someone so young could become a C-level leader.","\"Sister Yi, you didn't come to me tonight just to warn me, did you? Is there something else?\" Liu Yutong asked directly.","Lin Yi nodded. \"Sharp as always. I do have a favor to ask of you, Yutong.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Next week is Old Madam Jiang's eightieth birthday. Every influential figure in the imperial capital will be there. I'd like you to come with me and help me hold my own.\"","Liu Yutong was taken aback. \"Hold your own? I'm an outsider—how can I help you, a proper young lady of both the Lin and Shen families?\"","Lin Yi explained, \"You might not know this, but I have some trouble with the Jiang family. There are two younger Jiang family members I've had conflicts with. I'm afraid I won't be able to handle things alone if I go, but I can't afford not to show up. If you come with me, it'll be a different story.\"","Liu Yutong fell into thought.","Wasn't this practically asking her to actively offend the Jiang family?","But then again, if her sister Gao Min couldn't hold back and took down Jiang Yuan directly at the banquet, wouldn't that also offend the Jiang family?","She had already confirmed that Jiang Yuan was in the imperial capital, but she still hadn't located his exact hideout.","If she teamed up with Lin Yi, it would be easier to uncover Jiang Yuan's arrangements in the capital. Lin Yi also had the backing of the Shen family, and using her connections to dig up Jiang Yuan's whereabouts would be far simpler than doing it alone.","With that in mind, Liu Yutong had made up her mind.","\"Alright, I agree,\" she said.","Lin Yi's eyes lit up. \"Really?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Really. But, Sister Yi, you have to agree to one condition too.\"","Lin Yi asked, \"What condition?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"When we get to the Jiang family's place, don't ask me too many questions or pry into my affairs. What you need to know, I'll tell you. What you don't need to know, don't ask. And don't get clever and start investigating on your own.\"","Lin Yi paused for a moment, then burst out laughing.","\"Yutong, you really love keeping your mysteries, don't you?\"","\"Fine, I agree!\""]},{"number":757,"title":"Chapter 757: 758. Conspiracy. (Thank you 'username10654700' for the Gift King)","paragraphs":["In the study of a penthouse mansion located in the heart of the imperial capital, Wu Kun was reporting the latest information he had just obtained to the middle-aged man sitting at the desk.","The man, about sixty years old, had a refined and handsome face. He wore a dark gray Mao suit, holding a string of oily, smooth agarwood prayer beads in his hand, turning them slowly.","This man was Jiang Yuan.","He was the so-called patriotic businessman from Hong Kong, and also the true mastermind behind Zhao Weixiang's claim of murdering Gao Shubai.","\"Old Jiang, that Liu Yutong is not simple at all.\"","\"The people under her are all well-trained, acting swiftly and ruthlessly. The security guards at Yunlu had no chance to resist before they were subdued. She not only beat up the Zhou family's young master, Zhou Heng, but also forced Lin Yue to slap herself repeatedly. In the end, it was Qin Yunlu and Lin Yi who stepped in to get those two out.\"","Jiang Yuan's fingers, spinning the prayer beads, paused briefly.","\"What happened afterward?\"","\"After the incident was over, she went upstairs to meet with several business owners, including Lei Yun, Huang Zhangming, and Chu Hai, a partner of AEG... They seemed to be discussing investment matters.\"","Jiang Yuan squinted. \"Lei Yun? The Lei Yun from Yinshan Software?\"","Wu Kun nodded: \"Yes, that's him. A major figure in China's internet circle.\"","Jiang Yuan narrowed his eyes, lost in thought.","\"Anything else?\"","Wu Kun thought for a moment and said: \"Oh, by the way, earlier, Liu Yutong had a short-haired woman with her. She was said to be the long-lost daughter of the Lin family's matriarch, who had just been reunited with them. Her name is Gao Min.\"","\"Before the conflict broke out, Gao Min left with two of Zhou Heng's friends, a man named Chen Xinhuai and a woman named Sun Mo. They are two celebrities who have been popular lately. They said they were going to some party.\"","Hearing the name Gao Min, a terrifying, chilling glint suddenly burst from Jiang Yuan's usually calm eyes.","He still remembered that name—it seemed to be the daughter of that police officer, Gao Shubai.","Unexpected, truly unexpected. Even he had been kept in the dark.","He knew a little about the background of Lin Jia's matriarch, Jiang Lu. That woman was once Lei Yun's woman.","He had to admit, that woman was skilled—remarrying and still managing to climb up to the Lin family, a high branch. A formidable talent indeed.","If this information was true, then Gao Min's real identity would be Lei Yun's daughter.","In that case, what was her relationship with Liu Yutong...?","\" What is the relationship between Liu Yutong and Gao Min?\" Jiang Yuan then asked.","Wu Kun replied: \"As far as I know, they are friends. Liu Yutong seems to have come to accompany Gao Min for the family reunion, and also to discuss business on the side.\"","\"Understood. You may leave now.\" Jiang Yuan waved his hand.","Wu Kun bowed and retreated, leaving the study.","As the study door closed, only Jiang Yuan remained in the room.","He put down his prayer beads, slowly stood up, and walked to the huge floor-to-ceiling window. He gazed at the bustling, brilliant nightscape of the imperial capital outside, his eyes darkened with a terrifying gloom.","Gao Min... was actually Lei Yun's daughter.","This was truly unexpected.","And she had come to the imperial capital with Liu Yutong from the Wanlong Society.","Liu Yutong was a name he had long heard like thunder.","He had already learned about this person through various channels. He had heard she was an extremely ruthless character, directly forcing Zhao Weixiang to flee abroad before successfully hunting him down to kill him.","Of course, in truth, that was actually done by people he had arranged.","That girl, Liu Yutong, had just arrived and dared to beat up members of the Zhou and Lin families—truly as domineering as the rumors said.","Additionally, the fact that she was discussing business with those bosses showed that, like recent rumors suggested, she was busy expanding the Wanlong Society's commercial empire. Under such circumstances, how could she have the energy to investigate those old, dusty cases?","He also felt that this girl was cut from the same cloth as him—greedy and ruthless.","She had even sent her own father to prison. Wasn't that enough ruthlessness?","Someone like that probably wouldn't care what evidence Zhao Weixiang had.","Between them, it should just be an ordinary revenge killing.","Moreover, neither Lei Yun nor Gao Shubai had any connection to her, Liu Yutong, so there was no reason for her to look into things, right?","But the fact that she was with Gao Min, the daughter of Gao Shubai, did stir within him a vague sense of unease.","He then picked up his phone and dialed a number.","\"Wu Kun.\"","Wu Kun, who had just reached downstairs, immediately turned back and knocked on the study door again. \"Old Jiang, what's the matter?\"","\"Have someone keep tabs on that Liu Yutong. Watch her closely! Report every move she makes, everyone she meets, and every word she says to me.\"","Wu Kun promptly nodded: \"Understood.\"","Jiang Yuan thought for a moment and added: \"Also, send a message to the Zhou family. I know they won't let the matter of Zhou Heng being beaten rest easily, but tell them to hold their horses. We'll settle everything together when the time comes!\"","\"Isn't the Jiang family matriarch's birthday banquet coming up soon?\"","Wu Kun asked tentatively: \"Boss, do you mean...\"","A cold smile curled at the corner of Jiang Yuan's mouth: \"Let that insolent girl 'shine' properly at the banquet. At the right moment, raise her up high, and then expose her real identity, including all those shady things she did in Pearl City and abroad.\"","Wu Kun felt a chill run down his spine as he instantly understood Jiang Yuan's intentions.","As they say, red and black never go together. The aristocratic families in the imperial capital all had some degree of red, political background. What they detested most was being associated with shady, unsavory people. Even if the younger generations of these families were arrogant and overbearing, they dared not openly associate with those with a dark, criminal background.","If Liu Yutong's identity were publicly exposed in such a setting, including those appalling deeds she had done both domestically and abroad, they wouldn't even need to make a move. She would be in deep trouble all by herself.","Brilliant, truly brilliant.","Wu Kun silently admired Jiang Yuan's tactics and immediately nodded: \"Understood, Old Jiang. Rest assured, I will make sure she reveals her true colors at the banquet!\""]},{"number":758,"title":"Chapter 758: 759. Argument (Thanks again to 'Username10654700' for the Gift of the King)","paragraphs":["The Lin Family Mansion.","By the time Lin Dong and Jiang Lu returned from outside, it was already past nine in the evening.","They had spent almost the entire day traversing the entire Imperial Capital.","Aside from preparing the birthday gift, they also visited the old comrades and former subordinates of the family patriarch, as well as some allied noble families they had previously been on good terms with.","“The elders we visited today were all quite accommodating. The groundwork for Nian Nian’s matter is basically laid,” Lin Dong said.","A flicker of warmth passed through Jiang Lu’s eyes. “You’ve worked hard. But is it really okay to keep this from the family? After all, Second Sister-in-law and the others have always been suspicious. If they catch wind of anything, they might try to stir up trouble.”","“It’s fine.”","Lin Dong waved his hand dismissively. “For the Lin family to thrive in the long run, we need someone capable of carrying the banner. Nian Nian has great potential—far more than those worthless boys in the family. As for Second Brother and his wife, even if they find out, it won’t change anything. Once Granny Jiang’s birthday banquet is over, I’ll inform them slowly.”","As the two stepped through the main gate, the butler hurried over with an anxious expression.","“Patriarch, Madam, you’re finally back!”","“Something’s happened at home. Second Master and the others are waiting for you in the living room.”","Lin Dong frowned. “What happened?”","The butler quickly summarized the situation. “It’s... Second Miss was beaten up, and Young Master Lin Feng has gone missing. He hasn’t returned, and his phone is unreachable.”","Lin Dong and Jiang Lu’s expressions changed instantly as they rushed toward the living room.","The living room was crowded with people, and the atmosphere was tense.","Lin Liang sat in a rosewood armchair beside the main seat, idly spinning a pair of walnuts in his hand, his face dark and gloomy.","Second Sister-in-law Zhang Yu sat on the couch, holding an ice pack to her daughter Lin Yue’s swollen face, muttering curses under her breath.","Wang Jiangyao, on the other hand, paced around the living room like a cat on a hot tin roof, frantic with worry.","The moment she saw Jiang Lu walk in, Wang Jiangyao immediately pointed at her and began to shout.","“Jiang Lu! Tell me where that bastard daughter of yours has taken my son!”","“Xiao Feng is missing now, and his phone’s dead! Xiao Yue said Xiao Feng was taken by your daughter!”","“And look at Xiao Yue’s face—it’s swollen like a pig’s head! The doctor said it’ll take at least ten days to half a month for the swelling to go down—all because of that Liu Yutong!”","“She even beat up Young Master Zhou from the Zhou family! Broke three of his ribs! She’s simply lawless!”","“Who is this person you’ve brought back? She’s nothing but trouble for the Lin family!”","“You have to give us an explanation today, or this isn’t over!”","Lin Dong’s face changed color instantly.","More than anything, he felt a headache coming on.","He hadn’t expected Liu Yutong to stir up such a huge mess on her very first day at the Lin mansion.","First, the niece gets slapped, the nephew gets taken away, and then Young Master Zhou has his ribs broken. He’d always known Liu Yutong wasn’t one to be trifled with, but this girl was way too reckless, wasn’t she?","Still, as the head of the family, he quickly composed himself and looked at his wife, Jiang Lu.","His gaze clearly said: “I dare not provoke this little mistress. What do you think we should do?”","Jiang Lu was still processing all this information.","Her youngest daughter had hit Lin Yue and Zhou Heng?","Her first thought was that it was probably true.","After all, she knew something about her youngest daughter’s nature—even she herself was a bit intimidated by that girl.","But she also believed that given her youngest daughter’s status and position, she would never act without reason. The other party must have done something that crossed a line to provoke her.","With that in mind, she asked, “Second Sister-in-law, Fourth Sister-in-law, don’t get worked up just yet. Tell me clearly what happened.”","Zhang Yu exploded at that, slamming the ice pack onto the table. “What else is there to say?! Your daughter and that little wretch beat up my daughter and took Xiao Feng away somewhere! Are you trying to cover for them?”","Jiang Lu took a deep breath to calm herself. “Second Sister-in-law, before the facts are clear, is it appropriate for you to keep calling someone a ‘little wretch’?”","Zhang Yu’s temper flared even more at being confronted. “What do you mean by that? Are you defending that little wretch? Jiang Lu, don’t forget you married into the Lin family! And now you’re siding with an outsider!”","Jiang Lu replied calmly but firmly. “I’m just stating the facts, not taking anyone’s side. Yue Yue was hurt, and Xiao Feng is missing—of course we need to find out the cause and let whoever is responsible take the blame. But until then, please watch your words. ‘Little wretch’ is unnecessary—she has a name!”","“You—”","Second Sister-in-law Zhang Yu was about to retort when Lin Liang raised his hand to stop her.","“Alright, that’s enough, both of you,” he said, standing up and turning to Jiang Lu.","“Sister-in-law, no matter what, the facts are clear. My daughter was indeed beaten, and Xiao Feng was taken by your daughter. Instead of dwelling on what happened, you should be giving us an answer first.”","“After all, Xiao Yue and Xiao Feng are your niece and nephew, aren’t they?”","Jiang Lu replied, “Second Brother, let me ask Tong Tong about the situation when she gets back. If it’s her fault, we’ll pay the medical bills and apologize—whatever’s needed. Fair enough?”","Just then, footsteps were heard from outside.","Everyone turned toward the doorway.","Liu Yutong and Gao Min walked in side by side, chatting and laughing, each holding a cup of milk tea—a stark contrast to the oppressive atmosphere inside.","Behind them shuffled a young man with a limp, none other than Lin Feng.","His eyes were vacant, as if he’d lost his soul, muttering over and over, “I’ll never do it again... I’ll never do it again... I don’t want to go back to that place...”","The moment Wang Jiangyao saw her son like this, she rushed over.","“Xiao Feng! Xiao Feng, what’s wrong? Don’t scare Mom!”","Lin Feng snapped out of his daze at her shaking, saw his mother, and burst into loud sobs like a wronged child.","“Mom! Mom, save me! I won’t do it again! I swear!”","Wang Jiangyao’s heart ached. She turned to glare at Gao Min and Liu Yutong, her eyes burning with fury.","“What did you do to my son?!”","“I swear, if you—”","Just as she was about to lose control and lash out, Liu Yutong raised a finger and wagged it.","“Auntie, don’t say I didn’t warn you. Better not try anything physical with us, or you’ll regret it.”","Wang Jiangyao choked on her words, the rest dying in her throat.","For some reason, despite the girl looking young, the aura she exuded inexplicably made her feel intimidated.","Just then, Lin Dong cleared his throat loudly and stepped in front of Liu Yutong, cutting through the tense standoff.","“Yu Tong, what exactly happened here?”","He discreetly winked at her, his eyes signaling: “This is still Lin family territory, little mistress. At least give me, the patriarch, some face and don’t make things too ugly.”","Liu Yutong then briefly recounted the whole story.","\"Lin Yue introduced me to that young master from the Zhou family, but they didn't know I know a little martial arts...\"","\"Zhou Heng brought two friends, Chen Xinhuai and Sun Mo, who are minor celebrities. Lin Feng went to a party with them, and those two got caught up in drug use and group sex. The police raided the place and rounded everyone up. If Gao Min hadn't casually pulled him out, he'd be spending the New Year in lockup.\"","\"Of course, to teach him a lesson, we gave him a little scolding. Don't worry, he's perfectly fine.\"","After Liu Yutong finished explaining the situation, the living room fell silent.","Wang Jiangyao was the first to react, shouting angrily at Liu Yutong.","\"You're full of crap! How could my son possibly go to a place like that? Don't slander him like that!\"","\"And even if Xiao Feng did go, it's because you two led him astray!\"","Liu Yutong shot back, \"Auntie, hearing you say that makes me blush for your son.\"","\"How old is he now? Twenty-two? Twenty-three? He's a grown man with his own legs and his own brain. If someone told him to jump off a bridge, would he do it? If someone told him to eat crap, would he?\"","\"He lacks self-control. He followed those two scumbags to that kind of place of his own free will. Now that something's happened, you want to blame us?\"","\"Tsk, tsk. No wonder the Lin family has been going downhill. With elders like you, what good could you ever raise?\""]},{"number":759,"title":"Chapter 759: 760, The Contest for the Candidate.","paragraphs":["Wang Jiangyao was left red-faced by Liu Yutong’s sharp retort, but she couldn’t find any grounds to argue back.","Lin Dong’s expression also darkened. He knew his niece was domineering, but he hadn’t expected her to be so vicious at heart. And of all people to provoke, why did she have to pick this young lady whom even he dared not offend?","“Yueyue, you tell us! What really happened?”","Lin Yue covered her face, swollen like a pig’s head, and looked tearfully at her father, Lin Liang, then at her second uncle, Lin Dong, her lips moving but unable to utter a word for a long time.","How could she explain?","Was she supposed to admit that she tried to gift Liu Yutong to Zhou Heng, only to be turned around and nearly land her cousin in prison?","If that came out, how could she ever hold her head up in the Lin family again?","Lin Liang saw his daughter’s reaction and basically confirmed that what the other side had said was true. He had a rough idea of his daughter’s character.","She was usually spoiled, willful, with her nose in the air, looking down on everyone. Today, she had finally bitten off more than she could chew.","He sighed, stepped forward, and said, “Alright, the matter’s been cleared up. Let’s leave it at that.”","Zhang Yu immediately grew anxious. “Cleared up? How is it cleared up? Look, Xiaoyue’s face is still swollen! And what about the Zhou family? Zhou Heng has three broken ribs—how can this just be let go? What if they come looking for trouble with the Lin family?”","Lin Liang frowned. “I said it’s over. This was entirely Lin Yue’s own fault. The other side hasn’t pursued her for it, and that’s already lucky. What more do you want?”","Zhang Yu was choked into silence by her husband.","But deep down, she still couldn’t accept it. Why should her daughter be beaten like this while the other side got off scot-free?","Lin Liang turned to Liu Yutong. Though he was secretly annoyed, he was still a reasonable man and offered an apology: “Miss Liu, this matter was Yueyue’s fault. I apologize on her behalf. From now on, I’ll discipline her strictly and won’t let her stir up trouble again.”","Liu Yutong glanced at Lin Yue and smiled. “It’s fine. I’m usually very generous and never hold grudges over things like this.”","Seeing that the tension had eased somewhat, Lin Dong quickly stepped in to mediate. “Alright, alright. Since everything’s been clarified, let’s put this to rest.”","“Yueyue was in the wrong first, but she’s acknowledged her mistake. As for the Zhou family, how dare they plot against a guest of the Lin family? Breaking a few ribs is nothing serious. If the Zhou family dares to come looking for trouble, I, Lin Dong, will handle them!”","Zhang Yu still felt resentful but couldn’t argue further.","As for Wang Jiangyao, she was now looking at Lin Yue with displeasure. If not for Lin Yue’s instigation to go to that club, Xiaofeng would never have followed that kind of person to such a place—it nearly ruined his future!","But since both her second and third brothers had spoken, she had to swallow her anger.","Just then, Lin Dong, sensing this was an opportunity, made a decision that stunned everyone present.","“Now that we’re all here tonight, I have an announcement to make.”","Everyone turned their attention to him.","Lin Dong walked over to Gao Min and said solemnly,","“From today onward, Gao Min will be my daughter. She will appear in all settings as a member of the Lin family, and I will use all of the Lin family’s connections and resources to fully cultivate her.”","These words were like a bombshell dropped among the Lin family.","The living room instantly erupted in chaos.","“What?!”","“Have you lost your mind? She’s an outsider—why should our Lin family put all its efforts into her?”","“Third Brother, what do you mean by this? Xiaofeng, Xiaoshen, Xiaomian, Xiaofeng, Yueyue—they are the bloodline of the Lin family! Why are you neglecting them to groom an outsider?”","“Third Brother, this isn’t right. Gao Min doesn’t even bear the Lin name. Our family is a prestigious clan. If word gets out, people will think the Lin family has run out of talent.”","Even the normally mild-tempered Lin Liang frowned and spoke up, “Third Brother, you haven’t fully thought this through. Gao Min is a good girl, I can see that, but she’s not a Lin by birth. No matter how much we cultivate her, what can she do for the Lin family in the future?”","Zhang Yu was even more blunt, pointing at Jiang Lu and saying, “Third Brother, has Jiang Lu completely bewitched you? All these years you’ve indulged her every whim, and now you’re pushing her daughter to the forefront—are you trying to drive the Lin family into a trap?”","Hearing her sister-in-law’s words, Jiang Lu was immediately displeased. “Sister-in-law, what do you mean by that? Are you calling me a fox spirit?”","Zhang Yu curled her lips. “Even if you’re not, you’re close enough. Who knows what you’re really up to...”","Jiang Lu: “You—”","“Enough! Everyone shut up!”","Lin Dong slammed the table, cutting them off.","Then, taking a deep breath, he looked at everyone.","“Second Brother, Second Sister-in-law, Fourth Brother, Fourth Sister-in-law, hear me out first.”","“I’ve thought this through carefully.”","“Why is the Lin family declining year after year? It’s not because Grandfather left us too early—it’s because our generation is lacking, and the next generation is even worse!”","Lin Dong’s gaze swept over every young member of the Lin family present, critiquing them one by one.","“Xiaoshen, you’re the eldest grandson. Look at yourself—all these years, besides eating, drinking, and hanging out with disreputable friends, what have you accomplished?”","“Xiaoyue, you’ve always been spoiled and arrogant, looking down on others. Today, you nearly brought shame to the Lin family.”","“Xiaofeng, your self-control is far too weak. Even as a civil servant, will you forget your principles the moment temptation comes? At this rate, you’ll end up behind bars sooner or later.”","“Son, you may be steady, but your abilities are limited. You can hold the fort, but you lack initiative.”","“Xiaomian, you... just focus on your studies for now.”","The younger Lins who were singled out hung their heads, faces flushing red.","Some were resentful inside but dared not show it.","Only the newly adult Lin Mian looked at his third uncle with clear eyes, lost in thought.","After speaking, Lin Dong let out a long sigh.","“Tell me, among all of you, who can take up the mantle now?”","The entire living room fell silent.","Even if they didn’t want to admit it, they all knew Lin Dong was telling the truth. Neither their generation nor the next had anyone truly capable.","Seeing that he had set the stage, Lin Dong finally formally introduced Gao Min’s credentials.","“Gao Min is Lulu’s daughter, so that makes her my daughter. Though she grew up in a small town, she is remarkably outstanding—a first-class police commissioner at the age of twenty-three, with a perfect case-solving record, a personal second-class merit, and the child of a martyr—impeccable background!”","“I believe her future achievements will be no lower than Lin Yi’s.”","“I have chosen her as the heir to the Lin family not out of personal bias, but because she is exceptionally capable. Moreover, Grandfather left us many old connections and friendships. If we don’t use them now, they’ll only fade away and eventually break off. Then where will the Lin family be? No different from those upstart nouveau riche families in the eastern city.”","Lin Liang was silent for a moment before speaking again. \"Third Brother, I admit it—Gao Min is indeed an outstanding girl, no argument there. But she doesn't carry the Lin surname after all. If you dump all our family's resources into her, what can she possibly give back to the Lin family?\"","\"Yeah, if she makes it big one day, will she even remember our Lin family?\"","\"Isn't this decision too hasty? No matter how far our Lin family has fallen, we shouldn't have to rely on an outsider to save face.\"","\"Don't forget, we still have Lin Yi in the Lin family.\"","\"That's right. If we're going to groom someone, it should be Lin Yi. She's the one with our Lin family's true bloodline!\"","\"...\"","Seeing everyone voicing their objections in a flurry, Lin Dong slammed the table hard.","\"Lin Yi is indeed a member of the Lin family, but she was raised entirely by the Shen family. Can we really compete with the Shen family for her?\"","\"Also, I believe my daughter Gao Min is not someone who would forget a favor.\"","But the crowd still wouldn't back down, ready to rebut again.","Suddenly, a particularly sharp, mocking voice cut through the noise.","\"A bunch of frogs at the bottom of a well, still nitpicking. How ridiculous!\""]},{"number":760,"title":"Chapter 760: 761, Then Let Me Show You What I Really Am","paragraphs":["\"A bunch of frogs at the bottom of a well, still picking and choosing here—how ridiculous!\"","Everyone turned their heads in unison, looking toward the source of the voice.","Liu Yutong leaned against the armrest of the sofa, still holding the unfinished milk tea in her hand, her eyes dripping with undisguised sarcasm and disdain.","\"What does the Lin family have left now? Just an empty shell, right?\"","\"A bunch of losers who can't even live off their inheritance, and you're still nitpicking here.\"","\"Sister Min agreeing to this marriage is already giving you face—you should be thankful! Don't be ungrateful!\"","Her words were harsh, and the Lin family members immediately erupted in anger.","\"Who do you think you are! This is the Lin family, the Lin family of the imperial capital, not some backwater village of yours—who gave you the right to speak!\"","\"That's right! When the host is talking, what business do you have butting in? No manners at all!\"","\"Get out now!\"","\"Yes! Throw her out!\"","\"Where's the butler? Butler! Throw her out!\"","\"......\"","Yet facing this chorus of condemnation, Liu Yutong showed no sign of fear. She swept her sharp gaze across every Lin family member present.","Anyone she fixed her eyes on—whether it was elders like Zhang Yu and Wang Jiangyao, or younger ones like Lin Shen and Lin Feng—involuntarily shuddered and averted their gaze.","\"Throw me out?\"","\"Is the Lin family really so impressive?\" Liu Yutong said as she walked toward Lin Liang.","\"What do you think you're doing?\"","Lin Liang watched her approach step by step, instinctively narrowing his eyes.","The dignified Second Master of the Lin family, a notable figure in the imperial capital, felt uneasy—and even a faint fear—before a twenty-year-old girl.","Liu Yutong walked up to the coffee table, casually picked up a blue-and-white porcelain teacup, and toyed with it absentmindedly.","It was Lin Liang's favorite teacup, a Ming Dynasty Chenghua doucai piece, worth at least a million on the market—he usually wouldn't even let anyone touch it.","\"This tea isn't bad, Mingqian Longjing, right?\"","Liu Yutong examined the teacup, her tone light and indifferent. \"Too bad the person who brewed it has no skill, completely wasting the tea's essence.\"","No sooner had she spoken.","She let go.","Crack!","That priceless blue-and-white porcelain teacup shattered on the floor, splitting into pieces and startling everyone.","\"Ah! What have you done!\"","\"Are you crazy! That was an antique!\"","\"......\"","\"It's just a broken cup—don't make such a fuss.\"","Liu Yutong dusted off her hands and said bluntly, \"And in my eyes, you're no different from clowns putting on a show. You still feel so smug—what a joke!\"","\"What did you say!\"","Lin Liang, too pained to mourn his teacup, pointed at Liu Yutong and cursed, \"Arrogant! Too arrogant! Guards! Now! Seize her!\"","\"Who dares!\"","Liu Yutong sneered coldly. \"I've been too generous with you.\"","\"From the moment I walked into your Lin family, I saw you all putting on airs, looking down your noses. Not only do you lack any hospitality, but you keep calling me a wild girl, a country bumpkin, uncultured. So what, do you think you're superior? A bunch of frogs sitting in a well, thinking you're something special!\"","Liu Yutong's onslaught of curses nearly blew the top off the whole group.","\"You... you worthless thing! A wild girl from God knows what gutter, daring to make a scene in the Lin family!\"","\"Exactly! A piece of trash like you trying to marry into the Lin family? Why don't you take a good look at yourself first—do you even deserve it!\"","\"You low-class country bastard, don't ever set foot in our Lin family again!\"","\"Country folk will always be country folk—don't paint yourself gold!\"","\"Arrest her! Throw her out!\"","\"......\"","Hearing their self-righteous insults, Liu Yutong didn't get angry—she laughed instead.","\"Fine, since you look down on me as a country girl so much, let me open your eyes! Let me show you who I really am!\"","As her words faded.","The redwood door of the living room was violently pushed open from outside.","Bang!","The deafening noise made every Lin family member present jolt.","Everyone instinctively turned their heads, and then they saw a sight they would never forget.","A crowd of men in black suits, looking like tough guys, poured in like a flood, instantly surrounding the courtyard and corridors outside the living room.","A dense sea of people—at least a hundred of them.","The butler scrambled in, sobbing, \"Second Master, Third Master, it's terrible—there are people everywhere outside! I couldn't stop them!\"","The Lin family members stood frozen, dumbstruck.","When they came to their senses, they retreated in terror, terrified.","\"You... who are you people?\"","\"What do you want! This is trespassing!\"","\"Call the police! Call the police now!\"","\".......\"","The leader, Yun Cheng, stepped forward and sneered, \"Stop shouting, you country hicks! If you want to know who we are, just ask your family head.\"","At that, the Lin family all turned to stare at Lin Dong.","Lin Dong smiled bitterly and sighed in his heart: That girl is still so domineering... Ah, can't she just stay low-key? She always has to make a scene.","Then he said to his son, Lin Feng, \"Son, explain it to your uncles and aunts.\"","Lin Feng nodded and stepped forward.","\"Second Uncle, Second Aunt, Fourth Uncle, Fourth Aunt... the truth is, you've really made clowns of yourselves.\"","\"These men in black are all Miss Liu's subordinates.\"","The whole room exploded in shock.","\"What do you mean? These... these gangsters are all her underlings?\"","Lin Feng quickly waved his hands. \"Don't say that! They're from the legitimate company Wanlong Group—they're not gangsters!\"","\"Wanlong Group?\"","\"What's Wanlong Group?\" someone asked.","Lin Feng: \"It's the Wanlong Group Corporation from Pearl City. I saw it with my own eyes in Pearl City—they have... thousands of men like this.\"","\"Thousands!\"","The Lin family gasped again.","Lin Feng nodded and drove the point home, \"And Miss Liu is their heiress—or rather, their boss.\"","\"With one word from her, she could have you meeting your ancestors... well, that's beside the point.\"","\"And the assets of the Wanlong Group are conservatively estimated at over thirty billion—that's richer than our Lin family.\"","The living room fell into utter silence.","Thirty billion?","This girl, who looked no older than twenty, was worth thirty billion?","What kind of freak was she?","And the worst part was—they had been calling her a wild girl, uncultured, telling her to get out, and saying she was beneath the Lin family.","They now truly wished they could find a rat hole to crawl into. Who on earth was the one reaching above their station here?","They finally understood why this girl had been so calm and so arrogant from the moment she entered the Lin family home.","She really did have the capital to be cocky.","The crowd looked again at the dense crowd of black-clad men outside and couldn’t help swallowing hard.","Lin Yue, in particular, had witnessed firsthand how ruthless these thugs were, but she never imagined that these underworld figures were just the tip of the iceberg under Liu Yutong’s command.","This was too terrifying!","Lin Liang took a deep breath, suppressing the shock in his heart, and spoke with difficulty, “Miss Liu, we were wrong just now. We were blind and failed to see the truth. On behalf of the Lin family, I apologize to you.”","Liu Yutong looked at him with a faint, knowing smile. “Second Master Lin, you don’t need to apologize.”","“I didn’t come here to cause trouble. I just wanted to tell you one thing: if Sister Min is willing to acknowledge this family connection, it’s because she’s giving the Lin family face. If she doesn’t want to, then what is the Lin family? You’re not even worthy of polishing her shoes!”","“Also, let’s let today’s matter slide. But from now on, anyone who dares to cause trouble behind the scenes or look down on others with their eyes on top of their heads will face the consequences!”","As soon as she said this, the black-clad men outside suddenly shouted in unison.","“Anyone who dares disrespect the eldest young lady will be executed on the spot!” A hundred voices roared.","The shout was so sudden and so shocking that it nearly scared the souls out of the Lin family members.","Only then did the Lin family truly face reality: Liu Yutong was not someone they could afford to mess with. Even the entire Lin family combined wasn’t enough to play with her.","Lin Yue, covering her face swollen like a pig’s head, trembled. She finally understood just what kind of person she had provoked today.","And Lin Mian, the youngest of the Lin family’s younger generation, stood in the corner watching Liu Yutong, his eyes growing brighter and brighter.","He suddenly felt that this older sister was really cool."]},{"number":761,"title":"Chapter 761: 762, No One Is Allowed to Go","paragraphs":["Seeing that everyone had stopped objecting, Lin Dong finally breathed a sigh of relief.","He thought to himself: As expected, a fist still works best in this day and age.","The moment those men in black showed up, everyone fell into line.","“Alright, let’s drop this matter here. Yutong, you—”","He was about to tell Liu Yutong to call off her people when a woman’s voice suddenly rang out from outside the courtyard.","“What’s going on here? What are you all doing in the middle of the night?”","The interruption broke the suffocating tension, and everyone turned their heads toward the entrance.","Lin Yi walked into the courtyard. Frowning slightly at the sight of the imposing black-clad men gathered there, she didn’t linger on them long. Instead, her gaze immediately locked onto Liu Yutong.","She had noticed the dragon-shaped insignia on the chests of the men in black.","The Ten Thousand Dragons Society.","That meant they were Liu Yutong’s people. And given the situation, something unpleasant had clearly occurred.","“Yiyi, thank goodness you’re back!”","Zhang Yu and Wang Jiangyao rushed over as if they’d seen their salvation, clamoring to pour out their grievances.","“Yiyi, you have to stand up for us! Your younger cousin was bullied, and that Liu Yutong—she brought all these people to the Lin family home like this! What nonsense is this? You need to deal with her!”","“Look at them! Look at these people! Trespassing on private property! Lawless!”","“That’s right! Yiyi, you’re the most accomplished of the younger generation in our Lin family. You have to get us justice!”","“And your Third Uncle—he wants to give all the Lin family’s resources to an outsider! If anyone should get them, it should be you! You’re the one most qualified to inherit the family’s assets.”","“Yiyi, you can’t just watch your Third Uncle hand over everything our family has built!”","They spoke over each other, treating Lin Yi like their last hope.","After all, Lin Yi was a Class C leader within the government system and had the backing of the Shen family. Even a formidable force like Liu Yutong wouldn’t dare to cross her.","Lin Yi listened without making any response at first. Instead, she turned to her Third Uncle, Lin Dong.","“Third Uncle, is what they said true?”","Lin Dong nodded. “More or less.”","Lin Yi then looked at Liu Yutong, a hint of resignation in her eyes.","Was it really necessary to call in so many people over such a minor conflict?","This is the capital city. If the commotion gets too big and the authorities catch wind of it, none of your Ten Thousand Dragons Society members will get away easily.","Liu Yutong met Lin Yi’s gaze and simply shrugged, as if to say, It’s up to you now.","What Lin Yi did next, however, caught the Lin family completely off guard.","She walked straight up to Gao Min and extended her hand.","“Xiao Min, I’m Lin Yi. You can call me Sister Yi.”","Gao Min hesitated briefly, then took her hand. “Hello, Sister Yi.”","Lin Yi smiled, then turned to face the entire Lin family.","“Second Aunt, Fourth Aunt, I heard everything you said just now.”","“You claim that Third Uncle is giving our family’s resources to an outsider. I don’t think that’s true.”","Zhang Yu blinked in confusion. “Why not? Isn’t Gao Min an outsider?”","Lin Yi shook her head. “Xiao Min is Third Aunt’s daughter. That makes her part of the Lin family. I believe she’s fully entitled to our family’s resources.”","Wang Jiangyao grew frantic. “But, Xiao Yi, she has no blood relation to us! Haven’t you heard the saying: ‘Those not of our kin are bound to have different hearts’? Besides, you’re the most accomplished child in the Lin family, our pride and joy! You can’t side with outsiders!”","Lin Yi replied, “Fourth Aunt, have you forgotten? The reason I’m considered the most accomplished in the Lin family is because of the resources and connections the Shen family gave me. So by your logic, shouldn’t my maternal grandfather not have invested in me either? After all, my surname is Lin, not Shen.”","Wang Jiangyao was rendered speechless.","Though Lin Yi was related to the Shen family by blood, she wasn’t as close to them as the Shen children were. Yet Old Master Shen had spared no effort in cultivating her, even spending more resources on her than on his own grandchildren.","Ultimately, it wasn’t just his affection for his granddaughter—it was also because her ability and character had earned his approval.","Lin Yi continued, “I support Third Uncle’s decision regarding Xiao Min!”","“And there’s something else. I’m here to let everyone know: for Old Lady Jiang’s birthday banquet this time, aside from Gao Min, none of the younger generation in the Lin family should attend.”","“What?!”","These words caused an even bigger uproar than before.","Lin Yue was the first to jump up and protest. “Sister Yi, why won’t you let us go? We want to see the world too!”","Lin Shen and the others were equally stunned.","“Yeah, Sister Yi, why can’t we go?”","“This is too much!”","“You’re taking away our rights! We want to offer our birthday wishes to Old Lady Jiang!”","Lin Yi cast a cold gaze over them.","“And what for? To embarrass yourselves?”","“Going there would only make you look like extras for the other families. Why bother humiliating yourselves?”","Lin Yi showed them no mercy, and her words left them red-faced with shame.","Before they could refute her, she laid down several rules for her wayward younger siblings.","“From now on, as the eldest sister, I’m setting a few rules. All of you will remember them well.”","“First, no one is to speak a word about what happened tonight—especially anything concerning Miss Liu. Not a single word!”","“Second, from today onward, you must treat Xiao Min as one of our own!”","“Third, during the birthday banquet period, everyone is to behave. Stick to your own business. No causing trouble, no embarrassing yourself, and no scheming behind anyone’s back. If I find out anyone is stirring up trouble, you will face the consequences!”","The Lin family members present felt their hearts sink.","They had hoped Lin Yi’s arrival would help them get justice, but instead, she had sided with Gao Min, imposed three strict rules on the younger generation, and stripped them all of their right to attend the Jiang family’s birthday banquet.","This turn of events left not only the elders and the younger ones stunned but even the family head, Lin Dong, utterly baffled.","Wait—am I the head of the Lin family, or is she?","Though he knew that Lin Yi had grown up in the Shen household, personally mentored by Old Master Shen, and that her vision and capability far surpassed the Lin family’s mediocre descendants, banning everyone—wasn’t that going too far?","And more importantly, would her Second Uncle, Lin Liang, and the others agree to this?","“Yiyi, what do you mean by this?”","Zhang Yu could no longer hold back. “They’re your younger cousins, after all. Fine, even if you’re giving all the family’s resources to an outsider—but why won’t you even let them attend the birthday banquet?”","\"Not to mention anything else, if your sister Yueyue could just show her face and get acquainted with a few young masters from noble families, she could marry into a good household—that would be a great thing for both her and the Lin family.\"","\"Exactly! You can't just dismiss it out of hand, can you?\"","\"And besides, what about Lin Shen, Lin Feng, and Lin Mian? They haven't done anything wrong, so why should they be barred from going?\"","\"Yiyi, we admit you're the most accomplished among our generation, but you can't look down on people like this.\"","The group spoke one after another, their emotions growing more intense.","Even Second Uncle Lin Liang, who rarely meddled in such trivial matters, couldn't help but speak up.","\"Yiyi, you're really going too far with this. Regardless of anything else, Lin Shen and the others are still children of the Lin family—they should attend the birthday banquet. Besides, so many prominent families will be there. What will they think if they see not a single young member of the Lin family show up?\""]},{"number":762,"title":"Chapter 762: 763, Lin Yi's Considerations.","paragraphs":["Lin Yi listened quietly to the accusations and complaints from the crowd, neither getting angry, interrupting, nor explaining.","She could fully understand why they were so agitated and confused.","But there was no way she could tell them the real truth.","If Old Madam Jiang’s birthday banquet were just an ordinary celebration, she definitely wouldn’t have stopped anyone from going.","But some time ago, she had obtained insider information, which she confirmed through her maternal grandfather’s side. This time, a heavyweight guest would be attending Old Madam Jiang’s birthday banquet.","A certain Madam was coming.","God knew how shocked she was when she heard this news. She even had trouble sleeping for several days because of it.","Later, she found out why that Madam would attend the banquet. It was because, in her youth, Old Madam Jiang had worked in the Madam’s household for a few years, caring for the Madam when she was young.","It was precisely out of consideration for this old connection that the Madam made an exception to personally offer birthday congratulations to Old Madam Jiang.","If the Madam were just making a brief appearance, giving a gift, and leaving, she might not have cared so much.","What truly concerned her was another piece of news: the position of the Madam’s personal secretary had been vacant for over a month.","Over a month.","She knew full well how many eyes were fixed on that position.","The Shen family was watching, the Jiang family was watching, the Zhou family was watching, the Zhu family... every notable family in the capital that had any standing wanted to squeeze their most outstanding young member into that role.","That was the Madam’s secretary.","Although it didn’t carry much real power, only handling some schedule and daily trivial matters, spending even two years by the Madam’s side would gild your résumé, allowing you to rise through the ranks far faster than others.","More importantly, you also gained the network and rapport with the Madam.","A true once-in-a-lifetime leap!","Lin Yi herself had been stuck at the C-level position for a year—not too long, not too short.","But she knew that to move up quickly from here, relying solely on the Shen family’s resources was no longer enough.","The Shen family was her backing, but also her ceiling.","Old Master Shen doted on her, but the Shen family still had its own direct descendants. The resources they could allocate to her were ultimately limited.","She needed a real catalyst for rapid advancement.","The Madam’s secretary was that catalyst.","But this opportunity wasn’t easy to seize.","In the current generation of the Jiang family, there were two people she had to be cautious about, even wary of.","One was Jiang Chao, the eldest son of the Jiang family’s head.","Twenty-eight years old, a young core member of a key central ministry, fluent in four languages, handsome, and articulate. He was the pillar of the Jiang family’s younger generation. Word had it that for this Madam’s banquet, the Jiang family planned to have him accompany the Madam throughout, serving as her guide.","The other was Jiang Lan, the daughter of the Jiang family’s third son.","Twenty-four years old, a graduate from a prestigious university, already a deputy C-level at a young age—half a step faster than Lin Yi back in the day. According to others’ evaluations, this young woman was meticulous and thorough, well-suited for a personal secretary role.","These two were Lin Yi’s strong competitors.","And they had an advantage that Lin Yi didn’t: they were members of the Jiang family.","The Madam’s visit this time was out of respect for Old Madam Jiang.","As hosts, Jiang Chao and Jiang Lan would naturally have more chances to appear before the Madam and showcase themselves.","And what about Lin Yi?","She could only attend as a member of the Lin family.","She was very clear about the Lin family’s situation these days.","Ever since the old master passed away, the Lin family had been declining day by day.","Her second uncle, Lin Liang, was unambitious, only keeping birds and sipping tea.","Her third uncle, Lin Dong, had the desire to revive the family legacy, but he was taking the business route.","As for the younger generation of the Lin family, none of them were presentable.","How could she possibly let these people attend the banquet?","Bringing them along would only lower the Madam’s overall impression of their Lin generation.","Sometimes, the performance of a single family member was enough to influence the perception of the entire family. Bringing along someone embarrassing could drag down everyone’s image.","She needed teammates who could help her hold the line, who could step up at critical moments, who could add points rather than subtract them.","Not these Lin family losers who only fought among themselves.","So she chose to first win over Liu Yutong because she knew the chip project Liu Yutong was working on was a huge bonus.","And what Liu Yutong had done in BS Province—though she stayed low-key and didn’t mention it—Lin Yi had to make sure that story came to light at the right time. Those were massive advantages too.","Gao Min was the same.","Gao Min’s résumé was perfectly suited to the Madam’s tastes. The Madam had also served in the military in the past, and she naturally had a soft spot for the descendants of fallen martyrs.","If the Lin family accepted her, it would also show that the Lin family had vision and magnanimity.","These two sisters had talent, skill, strength, and faces that no one could find fault with.","Where else could she find teammates this good?","Honestly, after learning that the Madam was coming, she had been worried about how to find strong support. But she never expected her third uncle to bring Gao Min and Liu Yutong to the capital.","It was a huge surprise.","Also, what she said to Liu Yutong at Yunluo Club today, asking her to help her save face, claiming there was a conflict with some younger Jiang family members—that was all fabricated.","What were those younger Jiang members worth?","Even if Jiang Chao and Jiang Lan were powerful, they were still her peers. Who would be afraid of whom was still up in the air.","Her real target was the Madam.","She wasn’t just looking to save face; she wanted to make the Madam take an extra look at her in the crowd, to exchange a few more words with her.","But on her own, that wasn’t enough.","She needed someone who could draw attention, someone who could spark conversation, someone who could arouse the Madam’s curiosity.","Liu Yutong and Gao Min were those people, especially Liu Yutong.","She had a feeling that Liu Yutong would likely make a splash at the banquet.","She was looking forward to it.","...........","At that moment, the Lin family members were still fuming over Lin Yi’s earlier words.","“Yi Yi, you’re overstepping! You can go yourself, so why can’t they?”","“Exactly! You’ve been away from the Lin family for so long, and now you’re butting into family affairs? You’re stretching your hand too far!”","“.........”","Lin Yi waited until they were all done before speaking.","“Are you all finished?”","Everyone was taken aback.","Lin Yi’s gaze swept across their faces one by one. “Do you really think I was asking for your opinion?”","“Today, I’m laying down the rules. Anyone who dares to oppose me, don’t blame me for being ruthless.”","With those words, the entire room fell silent.","Though they were still deeply dissatisfied, since Lin Yi had put it that way, what more could they say?","No one really dared to break ties completely with the daughter left behind by the late head of the family.","After a moment.","Lin Dong cleared his throat, breaking the silence. “Well... Xiao Yi, it’s not that your third uncle doesn’t understand. But if we don’t bring a single male member, isn’t that a bit inappropriate?”","“How about this: pick two more, or at least one. You have to let me, as the head of the family, save face, right?”","He deliberately emphasized the word \"head of the family.\"","Lin Yi thought it was reasonable. After all, having no men at all didn't seem right either.","Then she looked at Liu Yutong and Gao Min, wanting them to pick one—this would prevent someone who didn't get along with them from causing trouble.","Gao Min glanced at Liu Yutong as well, then spoke up, pointing at two of the men.","\"Then let it be Lin Feng and Lin Mian.\"","As soon as the words were spoken, Second Aunt Zhang Yu grew anxious. Her son and daughter would have no chance now. She was about to say something again, but Lin Yi directly cut her off.","\"If anyone has objections, swallow them back down!\"","\"Third Uncle, let's finalize it just like that!\"","Lin Dong nodded. \"Alright!\"","That pretty much sealed the deal.","The rest of the Lin family, no matter how dissatisfied, could only grit their teeth and accept it."]},{"number":763,"title":"Chapter 763: 764. Preparations.","paragraphs":["Two days later, at daybreak, the entire Lin family household was bustling with activity.","Today marked the eightieth birthday of Old Madam Jiang. Although the celebratory feast wouldn't begin until the evening, there was no shortage of preparations to be made.","This was especially true for Gao Min, as this would be her first public appearance as a member of the Lin family, so nothing could be left to chance.","Jiang Lu had prepared several custom-made gowns for her to choose from, covering everything from head to toe, inside and out.","As for Liu Yutong, she had already prepared her own gown, so she didn't need Jiang Lu's help.","At that moment, she was curled up alone on the sofa in her room, handling company matters.","For this operation to capture Jiang Yuan, she had mobilised nearly five hundred core members of the Wanlong Society, deploying them all across the imperial capital, just waiting for that big fish, Jiang Yuan, to show himself.","From Qiu Ciyun, another report of success came in: the 90-nanometre production line for the LoongCore chip was running steadily, with a yield rate exceeding eighty percent. Full-scale mass production was within reach.","Su Mansu also sent an update, saying that Zeng Jin had poached two more engineers from Taiji Electric and was currently negotiating the terms of their contracts.","Lin Muyang's project was likewise progressing smoothly. The preparations for The Voice of Loong were in their final stages, all four judges had been confirmed and signed, and the auditions were about to begin.","The imperial capital would be one of the first cities to hold auditions, after all, it was home to numerous arts schools and many singers.","Just as Liu Yutong finished processing a personnel deployment list, her phone vibrated. It was a call from Cloud City.","\"Young Lady, we've spotted a tail.\"","\"For the past few days, someone's been following us. They're very cunning, switching shifts with three or four different teams. They have strong counter-surveillance skills—they must be old hands.\"","Upon hearing this report, Liu Yutong's first thought was Jiang Yuan.","That old fox was certainly cautious, sending people to watch her so quickly.","But thinking about it, it made sense.","She had caused quite a stir at Yuntu a couple of days ago, and given Jiang Yuan's paranoid nature, there was no way he would ignore her sudden appearance in the imperial capital.","What's more, she was with Gao Min. Even if he didn't care about Liu Yutong, he would certainly care about Gao Min.","After all, in name, he was the man who had killed Gao Min's father.","\"Keep watching them, but don't alert them.\"","\"Understood.\"","After hanging up, Liu Yutong began to think.","Jiang Yuan, Jiang Yuan. Do you really think you can figure me out by sending a few flies to keep an eye on me?","You probably never dreamed that in Pearl City, on my own turf of the Wanlong Society, the thugs you sent were already under my control.","By now, the smoke bombs that Liu San and the others set off should have reached your ears, haven't they?","Whether you believe them or not, you'll have to show your face at tonight's banquet.","As long as you dare to come, I'll make sure you can't escape even if you had wings!","Out of those five hundred Wanlong Society members, aside from a few assigned to tail Jiang Yuan's men, most were deployed at places like the airport, train stations, and bus depots.","To prevent anyone from slipping away by chance, she even coordinated with delivery riders in the city. If any target was spotted at those locations, they were to notify her team immediately.","It was a fallback plan she had kept in reserve.","If that guy was shameless enough to just cut and run, and she hadn't prepared for it, then things would really be a mess.","The other reason she arranged things this way was that it wouldn't be easy to make a move during the banquet itself.","After all, it was Old Madam Jiang's eightieth birthday, attended by numerous dignitaries and influential figures. Making trouble at the banquet would have terrible consequences.","Even she might end up in serious trouble.","Just as she was wondering if there were any other weak points in her plan, there was a knock at the door from Gao Min.","\"Yutong, we're here.\"","The door opened, and Gao Min walked in together with Lin Yi.","Gao Min was already dressed in her custom-made gown.","It was a white silk long dress, the fabric impossibly smooth. The collar was a modified high Mandarin collar, and the hem trailed slightly on the floor. Around her waist was tied a sash of the same colour, perfectly accentuating her slender waist.","Her shoulder-length hair was pinned up, secured by a white jade hairpin, revealing her long, fair neck.","She exuded both the gentle elegance of a southern woman and a certain spirited air of a martial artist.","\"How do I look in this?\" Gao Min asked, turning around in front of Liu Yutong.","After a careful look, Liu Yutong praised her generously, \"Sis, this dress really suits you. You look incredibly beautiful!\"","\"I think you should try wearing this style more often.\"","Gao Min was also very fond of the dress. \"I'd like to, but it's hard to find the chance on ordinary days.\"","Lin Yi laughed from the side. \"Xiao Min's dress was specially custom-made by Third Aunt. The fabric was hand-woven. I heard that only two pieces were ever made from this material—one was sent abroad for an exhibition, and the other is the one Xiao Min is wearing.\"","\"Third Aunt really went all out for this dress.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. She thought to herself that her so-called obliging mother had certainly put in the effort.","\"Speaking of which, Yutong, where's your dress? Hurry up and show us.\" Lin Yi suddenly remembered.","Liu Yutong pointed to her wardrobe. \"It's in the wardrobe.\"","\"Well, take it out and let us see!\"","Liu Yutong walked over to the wardrobe, opened the door, and took out a dress wrapped in a dust cover.","When the dress was revealed, the room fell silent.","It was a gown of mist-green, the colour so pale it seemed like the early morning mist of the south in March, or the sky just after a spring rain.","The material was top-grade silk gauze, light and ethereal. Thanks to a cleverly layered design, it was elegant without being revealing.","The collar was a simple crew neck, perfectly showcasing the collarbone. The sleeves were a modified wide design that would gently ripple when moving, like drifting mist.","The skirt had no unnecessary adornments, only a wide sash of the same colour at the waist. Embroidered upon the sash were extremely subtle dark patterns that took close inspection to discern as trailing clouds.","This dress was simple to the extreme, yet also conceived to the extreme in its beauty.","Lin Yi's eyes lit up.","\"Mist-green.\"","'After the rain, the sky clears to blue; what a colour for a robe to inherit anew.' Lin Yi couldn't help reciting a line of poetry.","\"Yutong, was this dress custom-made too? It's so full of atmosphere! But this colour is hard to pull off. Anyone with even slightly darker skin would look sickly. With your complexion, though, it will be perfect.\"","Even Gao Min was stunned. \"Yutong, your dress is absolutely beautiful, and it's so understated. I wish I'd asked you to get one made for me too. Suddenly, my own dress doesn't feel so special anymore.\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"If you like it, I'll have another one made for you.\"","She had chosen this gown mainly because she wanted to keep a low profile for tonight's occasion.","Besides, she would be attending as the Chairwoman of the Board of both the Wanlong Society and LoongCore. Being too flashy would be inappropriate, so she had opted for a more understated, neo-literati style.","This was, in fact, her first time trying such an elegant look.","In the past, she most often wore black.","\"By the way, have you prepared your birthday gift?\" Lin Yi asked again.","Liu Yutong nodded. She turned and took out a long, slender box made of rosewood from a corner of the wardrobe.","The box was exquisitely crafted and seemed to contain a scroll of calligraphy or painting.","Lin Yi and Gao Min looked at the wooden box and couldn't help asking, \"What is this? It looks like a painting? Is it some ancient calligraphy or artwork by a master?\"","Liu Yutong shook her head. \"It's not any antique, just a piece of calligraphy.\"","Upon hearing this, Gao Min and Lin Yi were both a little puzzled.","Old Madam Jiang's eightieth birthday—such a grand banquet for a top-tier aristocratic family—and they were giving just an ordinary piece of calligraphy?","Wasn't that too casual?","Liu Yutong didn't explain, just smiled mysteriously and kept them in suspense for now.","Last year's devastating earthquake that shocked the entire country—the Wanlong Group was one of the first companies to respond and donate.","Moreover, Liu Yutong's contribution was substantial, donating nearly two billion yuan.","This two billion yuan, without passing through any intermediary organizations, was entirely used for post-disaster reconstruction and designated specifically for building schools.","The children who had lost their school campuses had long since resumed classes in the new schools funded by the Wanlong Group's donation.","This piece of calligraphy was tied to those children.","Though it wasn't an antique, it was more meaningful than any antique.","Because it was a blessing from tens of thousands of students across hundreds of schools.","This was also a choice Liu Yutong had made after careful consideration.","For a family like the Jiangs, giving an expensive gift would not only be tacky but also easily invite criticism, especially given the number of high-ranking officials present.","Besides that, she had also found out that Old Madam Jiang had been a teacher in the countryside in her younger days.","That's why she chose this gift, whose significance far outweighed its monetary value.","Of course, she also hoped that this very meaningful gift would help minimize the Jiang family's hostility toward her when the time came, since she might stir up trouble at the banquet.","Seeing that Liu Yutong didn't want to say more, Lin Yi wisely stopped asking.","\"By the way, Yutong, you have a separate invitation, right?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"That's right.\"","\"Then we'll have to go separately later,\" Lin Yi said. \"It's not convenient for you to go with us. Tonight, you're attending as the chairwoman of the Wanlong Group, so your seating arrangement will definitely be different from us Lin family members.\"","She paused, her tone turning slightly meaningful. \"From what I know, tonight's seating at the Jiangs is arranged by rank. The children of aristocratic families will be seated in the side hall, but you'll probably be placed in the main hall at the VIP table.\"","That was where the truly influential people sat.","Top tycoons, key officials, celebrities from all walks of life...","Even she, Lin Yi, might not get a seat in that spot.","Liu Yutong didn't care much about that. \"It doesn't matter where I sit; I'm there to offer birthday wishes anyway.\"","Of course, she had one thing she didn't say out loud: as long as that old bastard Jiang Yuan showed up, it didn't matter where she was seated.","Gao Min seemed to read her mind and nodded. \"Exactly, it doesn't matter where we sit.\"","Then she added in a low voice, \"Tonight, it's time to settle the score!\""]},{"number":764,"title":"Chapter 764: 765, Seeing Jiang Yuan.","paragraphs":["Evening, at the Jiang family estate.","The old Jiang residence was also located on West Mountain, an equally imposing and grand mansion.","With vermillion gates, high walls, and sweeping eaves decorated with intricate carvings, it exuded the deep-rooted heritage of a top-tier aristocratic family.","At this moment, the front courtyard was bustling with traffic, filled with all kinds of luxury cars.","A single glance at the license plates revealed numbers like A88888, A66666, or vehicles with special permits—any one of them was enough to astonish ordinary people.","When the Lin family’s car arrived, it was directed by the reception staff to a designated VIP parking area.","The car doors opened, and Lin Dong and Jiang Lu were the first to step out.","Then, Lin Yi, Gao Min, as well as the younger generation members Lin Feng and Lin Mian, appeared one after another.","As soon as the Lin family group made its entrance, it began drawing the attention of many guests already present.","“Is that the Lin family’s car?”","“The Lin family? Which Lin family?”","“Which else could it be? The Lin family of West City.”","“I heard the Lin family has been in decline these past years, practically being held up by the women.”","“Shh, keep your voice down. Lin Dong may be a businessman, but his elder brother’s daughter, Lin Yi, is now a genuine C-level executive with real authority, and she’s connected to the Shen family.”","“Oh, that Lin Yi? She’s indeed something special.”","“Hey, who’s that unfamiliar girl in the white dress?”","“She’s quite beautiful, with a good presence. Does anyone know her?”","“No idea. I’ve never seen her before.”","“People always say the younger generation of the Lin family is worthless, but now, looking at these young Lins, they all carry themselves pretty strongly—not the useless wastrels the rumors suggest.”","“Could it be we’ve underestimated the Lin family?”","“...”","Amid the whispered chatter, Lin Dong, arm in arm with his wife Jiang Lu, led the four young Lin family members through the main entrance.","Along the way, they encountered more and more acquaintances, and many people took the initiative to greet Lin Yi.","“Director Lin, long time no see! You look younger every day.”","“Director Lin, you’re really glowing tonight.”","“Lin Yi, who’s this beside you?” someone finally couldn’t resist asking about Gao Min’s background.","Lin Yi, her arm linked with Gao Min’s, graciously introduced her to everyone. “This is my younger sister, Gao Min. She just came back into the family recently. She’s one of us.”","As soon as she said this, the surrounding crowd fell noticeably silent for a moment.","Lin Yi’s sister?","When did Lin Yi get a sister?","Could she be an illegitimate daughter of the Lin family who had been living away?","In an instant, the name Gao Min, along with various speculations, began spreading quickly among the guests.","Of course, eagle-eyed observers also noticed that of this generation of male heirs, only Lin Feng and Lin Mian had shown up.","“Hey, what about the other younger Lins? Why didn’t they come?”","“Probably brought here to avoid embarrassment, I guess.”","“Who knows?”","“...”","Soon, the Lin family reached the banquet hall.","The hall was decorated in an antique style.","Redwood tables and chairs, palace lanterns hanging high—it all exuded an air of opulence.","The seat of honor was reserved for Old Madam Jiang, still empty at that moment, but the nearby VIP seats were already occupied by many guests.","These people all had distinguished bearing, clearly individuals of status and prestige.","As more guests filed in, they were directed by the reception staff to their seats based on their name cards.","The seating for the younger generation was arranged in the right-side annex hall, separated from the main table by a corridor.","Lin Yi led Gao Min and the others toward the right-side seating area.","As they passed by the VIP seats, Gao Min’s eyes quickly scanned the faces of the people there.","Suddenly, her gaze froze.","In a corner of the VIP seating sat a man around sixty years old.","He was wearing a dark gray Mao suit, holding a string of glossy agarwood prayer beads in his hand. With his head tilted, he was quietly chatting with the person next to him, occasionally letting out hearty laughs. He had a kind and benevolent appearance.","The man was Jiang Yuan.","Even if he were reduced to ashes, Gao Min would still recognize that face.","In that instant, her heartbeat quickened sharply, and her fists clenched involuntarily.","But in the end, she managed to suppress the fierce urge to charge over and take him down, following Lin Yi to their seats.","Just as she turned her head, Jiang Yuan seemed to sense something too. He glanced slightly sideways and cast a look at her.","That gaze carried an unreadable, profound significance.","Then, as if nothing had happened, he quickly turned back and resumed talking and laughing with the person beside him.","When Lin Yi and the others reached the right-side area, it was already filled with elegantly dressed young men and women.","Seeing Lin Yi approach, many stood up to greet her.","“Sister Yi!”","“Hello, Sister Yi!”","“...”","Lin Yi returned their greetings one by one.","Once they were seated, the surrounding eyes began to drift discreetly toward Gao Min.","“Who’s that? Haven’t seen her before.”","“No idea. Is she some heiress?”","“She’s quite pretty, and she has good poise.”","“I heard outside that she’s Lin Yi’s sister, name’s Gao Min.”","“Gao Min? With a last name like Gao, she can’t be from the main Lin family.”","“Maybe a distant relative?”","“Hmm, she’s beautiful, and there’s something spirited about her.”","“...”","Facing these brazen stares and evaluations from the aristocratic heirs, Gao Min chose to ignore the noise.","She hadn’t come to the capital to climb the social ladder or to fit into this circle.","She had come to catch her enemy.","Just then, a sudden commotion and gasps erupted from the entrance.","“Look!”","“Who’s that?”","“Holy crap—that presence, that face... this is amazing!”"]},{"number":765,"title":"Chapter 765: 766, Everyone's Acting.","paragraphs":["“Look!”","“Who is that?”","“Damn, that aura... that face... stunning!”","Gao Min heard the exclamations and couldn’t help but curl the corners of her mouth slightly.","She was here.","Her younger sister.","At the entrance, a figure in misty blue walked in gracefully.","She was a very young girl, no more than twenty years old, dressed in a misty blue long gown. Her long hair, dark as ink, cascaded over her shoulders, curling slightly at the ends. Her delicate face bore only a hint of makeup, yet it was enough to make her breathtakingly beautiful.","But what truly set her apart was her aura.","Though dressed in such simple, understated clothing, the moment she appeared, the richly adorned socialites and wealthy ladies around her instantly seemed vulgar.","Even the entire hall fell silent for a moment because of her presence.","Who was this girl?","Where did she come from?","Lin Yi’s eyes flickered.","She knew Liu Yutong was beautiful, but she hadn’t expected that, when fully dressed up, Liu Yutong could reach such ethereal heights.","That misty blue gown seemed alive on her, carrying an otherworldly, fairy-like grace.","On the right side of the hall, where the young elite men from prominent families were seated, many had their eyes wide and fixed on her.","Suddenly, family alliances through marriage didn’t seem so bad. They were no longer resisting the idea—after all, this girl was clearly no ordinary person.","“Who is she? She’s gorgeous! Like a fairy descending to earth!”","“Never seen her before. Which family is she from?”","“I haven’t heard of any family having someone like this.”","“Whoever she is, I’m definitely going to get to know her later.”","“I suddenly think my dad’s idea of marrying into a big family is a brilliant strategic move. For the sake of our family’s interests, I’m willing to sacrifice myself and just barely make do with getting to know this girl.”","“Get lost! You’re a toad dreaming of eating swan meat!”","“...”","Lin Feng, sitting in a corner, heard these idiots spouting their ridiculous fantasies and couldn’t help laughing inside.","You bunch of lowlifes think you’re worthy?","That’s the young mistress of the Wanlong Group. She commands thousands of men in black, and she once broke three of Zhou Heng’s ribs without a second thought.","If you go messing with her, you’d better hope you don’t end up like Zhou Heng.","Lin Mian, on the other hand, kept staring at the misty blue figure, his eyes shining brightly.","Big sis is so cool!","Big sis is so beautiful!","“Miss Liu, this way, please.”","Under the gaze of the crowd, Liu Yutong followed the attendant toward the VIP section in the left hall and sat down in one of the seats.","The young men on the right side erupted immediately.","“What? She went to the VIP section?”","“How is that possible? Isn’t she like us, from a prominent family?”","“The VIP seats are for real big shots!”","“This doesn’t make sense!”","“Who exactly is she?”","“...”","In the eastern main hall, there were eight tables.","Those seated here were either incredibly wealthy, held real power, or were well-known figures from various fields. Every single person here was someone ordinary people could only look up to.","Amid curious stares, Liu Yutong followed the attendant to the east side of the hall, to a table roughly in the center.","“Miss Liu, this is your seat.” The attendant gestured.","Liu Yutong nodded silently and looked at the people already seated.","There weren’t many at this table—eight in total, including her.","To her left was a man in his forties, wearing an administrative jacket, with a refined demeanor. He was likely a senior official from some department in the capital. To her right was another man in his forties, in a suit and tie, looking every bit like the head of a major state-owned enterprise.","There were also two women, both with sharp, professional auras, probably from influential circles.","Finally, sitting directly across from her was a man around sixty.","He wore a dark gray Zhongshan suit and held a string of sandalwood prayer beads, looking kind and gentle.","He was Jiang Yuan.","Liu Yutong’s gaze lingered on Jiang Yuan’s face for less than a second before she naturally looked away, as if seeing a stranger.","As she observed them, the others at the table were also sizing up this unexpected young girl.","Their first reactions were similar: Had she wandered into the wrong place? The younger generation was supposed to be in the right side hall—shouldn’t she be there?","The middle-aged official from the Investment Promotion Bureau spoke first. “Miss, you seem unfamiliar. May I ask your name?”","Liu Yutong bowed slightly and replied politely, “Hello, sir. My surname is Liu, Liu Yutong. I’m the chairman of the Wanlong Group from Pearl City.”","“The Wanlong Group?”","The people at the table were a bit surprised.","Not because of the name—but because this young girl was actually the chairman of a group.","Unexpected.","“So you’re Director Liu.”","The Investment Promotion Bureau official extended his hand, his tone much more respectful. “Director Liu, you’re so young and already leading a group. Truly impressive. I work for the Capital Investment Promotion Bureau. My surname is Fang.”","Liu Yutong shook his hand. “Hello, Director Fang.”","At that moment, the man who had been silently rubbing his prayer beads, Jiang Yuan, suddenly spoke.","“Wanlong... I think I’ve heard that name. Sounds like a very big group. For Miss Liu to build such an enterprise at such a young age is truly remarkable.”","Liu Yutong turned to him, her expression unchanged. She replied humbly, “You flatter me, sir. My little efforts are nothing worth mentioning. May I ask how I should address you?”","Jiang Yuan chuckled. “My surname is Jiang. Jiang Yuan. I’m from Harbour City, doing some small business. Nothing compared to everyone here.”","“You’re too modest, Mr. Jiang.” Liu Yutong said politely.","On the surface, she was calm.","But inside, she was sneering.","This old fox really knows how to play pretend.","That’s fine. She could play pretend too.","After the brief pleasantries, Jiang Yuan turned back to chat with the state-own enterprise executive beside him, but his peripheral vision kept subtly observing Liu Yutong.","So this girl really doesn’t recognize him.","Her eyes and reactions didn’t seem fake.","If she were really investigating that old incident, if she actually had the evidence Zhao Weixiang left behind, she wouldn’t be this calm when seeing him.","Unless her acting was so good that even he couldn’t see through it.","But was that possible?","She was still so young. Her mind couldn’t be that deep.","For now, it seemed his earlier worries were probably unnecessary.","The taut string in Jiang Yuan’s heart loosened a little.","But he was an old fox. He didn’t let his guard down entirely.","He still planned to carry out that strategy.","Better to kill a thousand by mistake than let one slip through.","Liu Yutong lifted the celadon teacup in front of her and took a gentle sip. The fragrant steam curled upward, perfectly concealing the faint, almost imperceptible sneer at the corners of her mouth.","Old fool, no matter how cautious you are, now that you’ve shown your face, there’s no way you’re slipping out of my grasp!","Just as she was mapping out her next move in her mind, a sudden commotion erupted from the right side hall.","\"Lin Yi, you... you’ve gone too far!\"","Hearing the noise, Liu Yutong turned her head to look.","In the side hall, a young woman in a rose-red gown stood before Lin Yi, her face ashen as she pointed at her and hurled accusations. Behind her stood several other young men and women, all wearing hostile expressions—clearly, they had come looking for trouble.","They were from the Zhou family."]},{"number":766,"title":"Chapter 766: 767, Undermining Each Other (Thanks to Mr. Chen Who Loves Oranges for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Ten minutes earlier, the side hall where the scions of the elite families had gathered was quite lively.","As soon as Lin Yi took her seat with Gao Min, Lin Feng, and Lin Mian, many tactful people immediately surrounded them with wine glasses in hand. After all, Lin Yi was a prominent figure in the capital's social circles, holding a real power position at a C-level at such a young age. Everyone wanted to seize the chance to build a good relationship with her and get on her good side.","\"Sister Yi, long time no see.\"","\"Sister Yi, you look stunning today. Which designer is that dress from?\"","\"Sister Yi, and this is...\"","Lin Yi graciously introduced Gao Min: \"This is my sister, Gao Min. Please take good care of her in the future.\"","Although everyone was privately wondering how someone with the surname Gao became a member of the Lin family—having never heard of it before—since she was Lin Yi's sister, it was only proper to give her the face she deserved. They all greeted Gao Min with smiles.","Gao Min responded politely, but her eyes kept drifting toward the VIP seats on the left.","She also saw Liu Yutong sitting opposite Jiang Yuan, and saw her smiling and shaking hands with him as if nothing was wrong.","Honestly, in this regard, she couldn't compare to her sister.","If she were in her sister's place, she would have probably lost her cool long ago.","It must take incredible mental strength to smile so naturally at the murderer of one's father.","Just as she was about to secretly send a text message to ask her sister when it would be convenient to make a move, a harsh voice rang in her ears.","\"Well, well, if it isn't Miss Lin! What, bringing so many people today—are you here to wish Old Madam Jiang a happy birthday or just to freeload?\"","Hearing this voice, Gao Min frowned slightly and turned to look.","A young girl in a rose-red gown, followed by several young men, sauntered toward them with an air of arrogance.","The girl was about twenty-three or twenty-four, with passable features, but the arrogance and sharpness on her face dragged down her appearance significantly, making even her looks seem unpleasant. This was Zhou Yun, the daughter of the Zhou family's second branch and the younger sister of Zhou Heng.","Lin Yi furrowed her brows: \"Miss Zhou, today is Old Madam Jiang's birthday banquet. You'd better not cause trouble.\"","Zhou Yun completely ignored Lin Yi's warning, instead turning her gaze to Gao Min: \"Oh, this one looks unfamiliar. Miss Lin, when did your Lin family add such a character? I had no idea. She couldn't be some poor distant relative here to beg for handouts, could she?\"","Lin Yi said flatly: \"She's my sister.\"","Zhou Yun let out a snicker: \"Lin Yi, is your Lin family really that desperate for people? You bring in any random cat or dog and drag them into this circle? Haven't you seen what kind of occasion this is? Does she deserve to sit here?\"","The expression on Gao Min's face immediately darkened.","Seriously, what was wrong with this person? Biting people out of nowhere!","Lin Feng couldn't hold back anymore and jumped up: \"Zhou Yun, watch your mouth! She's my sister!\"","Zhou Yun shot him a sidelong glance: \"Lin Feng, what are you shouting about? Who gave you the right to speak here? I really don't get it—how can you even have the nerve to show up at an occasion like this? Do you even deserve to? Does the Lin family now rank high enough to be at the same table as us?\"","Lin Feng's face turned ashen with anger, but he couldn't find a good retort.","Although Zhou Yun's words were harsh, some of it was true. The Lin family indeed wasn't what it used to be, and compared to the top-tier families present, it fell far short.","Seeing him seeth but dare not speak, Zhou Yun grew even more smug and turned her focus to Lin Mian.","Lin Mian kept his head down, trying to make himself as inconspicuous as possible.","At only eighteen, he knew he was no match for Zhou Yun in a war of words, so naturally he wanted to avoid unwarranted trouble.","But Zhou Yun had no intention of letting him off: \"Oh, we've got a little kid here too! Is this Lin Mian? I hear you have good grades in school. What, are you here today to recite Tang poems for Old Madam Jiang?\"","\"Why don't you start with 'Quack, Quack, Quack' for big sister here and let me judge how well you perform?\"","\"Ha ha ha...\"","As she said this, the young men from the Zhou family behind her burst into laughter.","Lin Mian's head sank even lower, his face turning crimson, his ears burning.","Lin Feng: \"Zhou Yun, that's enough! If you've got guts, take it out on me!\"","Zhou Yun spun around to face him and pointed at Lin Mian: \"He's of age now, it's not like he's that fragile! And by the way, why don't I see Lin Shen or Lin Yue? Oh, I get it. Looks like they had sense enough to know they'd embarrass themselves here, so they didn't come.\"","Her words were incredibly cutting, effectively trampling all the younger generation of the Lin family's dignity.","Lin Yi's face also darkened.","She had long expected the Zhou family to stir up trouble, but she hadn't anticipated Zhou Yun being so blatant.","She looked at Lin Feng and Lin Mian, feeling a pang of regret.","She should have insisted they not come in the first place. These two teammates were just dead weight, completely overpowered by Zhou Yun.","The other young elites in the area had all quietly settled in to watch the drama unfold.","Zhou Yun kept on relentlessly, delivering taunts and insults.","\"Lin Yi, your Lin family has truly opened my eyes today. The old ones have nothing to show for, and the young ones can't hold themselves with any dignity. And you still dare to come wish Old Madam Jiang a happy birthday? If I were you, I'd have crawled into a mouse hole a long time ago!\"","The young men from the Zhou family behind her again burst into laughter.","Amidst this chorus of ridicule, Lin Yi slowly stood up.","She didn't explode in fury or become flustered as everyone expected. Instead, she looked at Zhou Yun calmly.","\"Miss Zhou, are you done?\"","Zhou Yun met her gaze, a flicker of unease stirring inside her, but her mouth remained sharp: \"So what if I'm done? So what if I'm not? Lin Yi, your Lin family just aren't up to scratch. Did I say anything wrong?\"","\"No, you didn't.\"","Lin Yi nodded, even admitting it: \"You're right. The Lin family hasn't been what it once was these past few years.\"","Zhou Yun was taken aback. She hadn't expected the other woman to agree. Just as she was about to gloat with further mockery, Lin Yi's next words froze her smile in place.","\"Miss Zhou, if you think this kind of insult can actually humiliate me, I'm really disappointed.\"","\"I heard your Zhou family is said to be the top preeminent family in the capital. But no matter how closely I look, I just can't see it.\"","Zhou Yun's face changed: \"You—\"","\"Hold on, I'm not finished.\"","Lin Yi didn't give her a chance to interrupt. She took another step forward, and Zhou Yun subconsciously stepped back.","\"You say my Lin family doesn't measure up. Fine, I admit it.\"","\"But where has your Zhou family excelled?\"","\"Your grandfather, Old Master Zhou, was quite a renowned figure in his day. Unfortunately, he lost face in the end—going to such lengths, at his age, to beg favors for a good-for-nothing grandson. Your eldest uncle managed to get a decent position, but not only is he incompetent, he loves showing off. Your father...\"","Lin Yi gave a scathing assessment from top to bottom, and finally turned her attention to Zhou Yun herself.","\"And as for your generation, not one of them is worth mentioning.\"","“Take you, for example.”","“Zhou Yun, you graduated from the Imperial College of Art, majoring in acting. It’s been two or three years since you graduated—what roles have you played? A third female lead in a web drama, and even that you bought your way into. I happened to watch the final cut your crew submitted, and honestly, with your acting skills, it’s a total waste of such good resources.”","“And do you know what people in the industry say about you? No talent, no integrity—useless except for having a rich father. If it weren’t for how pitiful your crew looked, I would have rejected your film outright.”","“That’s enough!”","Zhou Yun was on the verge of a breakdown, shrieking, “Lin Yi! You’re talking nonsense! You—”","“Don’t rush!”","Lin Yi cut her off again. “I’m not done yet. It’s one thing for a girl like you to be a disappointment, but your brother is the real piece of work—the one who’s truly brought shame to your family.”","Zhou Yun: “Stop it!”","“Weren’t you the one who wanted to hear me out? Let me finish!”","Lin Yi turned to the members of wealthy families gathered around, eavesdropping, and said loudly, “You all might not know this yet. Zhou Heng, Zhou Yun’s biological brother, recently made friends with two drug addicts. As luck would have it, those friends got caught by my little sister. And here’s the kicker—he, a grown man, tried to make a move on a girl because he was attracted to her. Want to guess what happened? She knocked him out cold with one punch, and he’s still lying in the hospital now.”","“I seriously have to laugh. The men in the Zhou family can’t even beat a woman, pure losers, aren’t they? Does the Zhou family even have a future?!”","At these words, the crowd burst into an uproar.","The young heirs from those wealthy families really hadn’t expected to stumble upon such juicy gossip.","So Zhou Heng tried to flirt with some girl, failed, and got beaten up instead?","No wonder he wasn’t showing his face today—he must be too ashamed to come out."]},{"number":767,"title":"Chapter 767: 768, If You Curse at Me, My Hands Will Itch.","paragraphs":["“Really? Zhou Heng got beaten up? By a woman?”","“Holy shit, that’s so embarrassing! The great Zhou Dashao got taken down by a girl.”","“I really want to know who that woman is. She’s fierce.”","“So that’s why Zhou Heng didn’t show up today—he’s lying in the hospital, huh.”","“Tsk, this generation of the Zhou family really made a name for themselves—all of it bad.”","“...”","Zhou Yun’s face turned ugly as she heard the sneers from the crowd around her.","She never imagined that Lin Yi, that bitch, would actually air her brother’s disgraceful secret in public!","Even worse, those rich kids from other families had started mocking the Zhou family outright.","“Lin Yi! How dare you slander my brother!”","Lin Yi: “Slander? If Miss Zhou doesn’t believe me, you’re welcome to go to the hospital right now and ask your brother how he broke those three ribs.”","“Also, didn’t I warn you before not to run your mouth? But you completely ignored me.”","“Now you’ve made a fool of yourself in public—you brought this on yourself. Don’t blame anyone else!”","Zhou Yun shook with rage: “Lin Yi, don’t get too cocky! You Lin family losers aren’t even fit to polish the Zhou family’s shoes!”","The more she spoke, the more agitated she became, her eyes darting around the room in search of a target.","Sure enough, on the VIP guest seating in the main hall, she spotted the figure in misty blue.","That girl so beautiful it made her jealous.","That was her!","She was the one who beat up her brother!","The fire in Zhou Yun’s heart instantly found an outlet. She raised her hand and pointed at Liu Yutong.","“And you, you bitch!”","“That bitch in the blue dress, flaunting herself! How dare you sit in the VIP seats!”","As soon as these words left her mouth, the entire side hall fell silent.","Everyone followed the direction of her finger and looked at the girl in misty blue, their minds a little stunned.","Seriously, was Zhou Yun losing her mind?","That girl was nowhere near you and hadn’t provoked you at all. To curse her out of nowhere—wasn’t that a bit much?","Of course, some speculated that this woman might be connected to Zhou Heng. Maybe she was the one who beat him up.","Soon, their guesses were confirmed.","Right then, the girl in the misty-blue dress—who had been smiling—wiped the smile off her face, stood up, and walked toward their direction.","Lin Feng saw her coming and seemed to already know what was about to happen.","Oh no, oh no. Zhou Yun was asking for death!","Why did she have to provoke this demon god?","Liu Yutong walked toward Zhou Yun one step at a time, the invisible pressure radiating from her growing stronger by the second.","Zhou Yun instinctively stepped back, about to say something.","She saw Liu Yutong raise her hand.","Smack!","A sharp, ringing slap landed squarely on Zhou Yun’s face, sending her crashing to the ground.","Dead silence fell over the entire hall.","Everyone stood there, mouths wide open, staring at the scene.","That girl who looked like a fairy just now—she actually struck someone without a second thought, right at Old Madam Jiang’s birthday banquet, in front of all those guests.","Zhou Yun sat on the ground, clutching her face, completely stunned.","In all her years, this was the first time someone had slapped her in public.","And it had to be at Old Madam Jiang’s birthday banquet, in front of so many elite families.","Soon, a wave of sharp pain and humiliation hit her.","“You... how dare you hit me!”","Liu Yutong looked down at her, her expression icy: “So what if I hit you? Got a problem with that?”","Zhou Yun whipped her head around and shouted at the Zhou family members behind her: “What are you all staring at? She hit me! Get her! Beat her to death!”","The young Zhou family members snapped out of their daze, fury rising in them as they rolled up their sleeves and prepared to charge.","“Stupid bitch, you’re asking for it!”","“How dare you lay a hand on my sister! You’ve got a death wish!”","“No more talk! Break her arms first!”","“...”","Liu Yutong casually flexed her wrists, eyeing them: “Didn’t Zhou Heng tell you? I know a little martial arts. Are you sure you want to fight me?”","Just then, Gao Min came up beside her, assumed a fighting stance: “Want a brawl? Come on, all of you at once. We can take you.”","Though they were just two very young women, the fierce aura they gave off made the burly Zhou men’s hair stand on end. They dared not step forward.","They remembered Zhou Heng, who was still in the hospital—wasn’t he beaten up by this girl in the blue dress?","Besides, if they beat up two girls, it would be shameful.","And if they lost, it would be even more embarrassing.","Seeing the Zhou family cowering, the onlookers could only think one thing: Holy crap.","Seriously, were girls nowadays so ferocious?","They actually managed to scare the Zhou family into backing down. That was rare.","And weirdly, the two girls looked somewhat alike.","Seeing that the Zhou family still didn’t dare make a move, Liu Yutong spat out two words: “Pathetic.”","That was the last straw. It utterly enraged the Zhou men.","Just as they were about to charge in regardless, several Zhou family elders rushed over upon hearing the commotion.","Leading them was an old man with a dignified square face, thick eyebrows, and big eyes, dressed in a traditional Tang suit, carrying a commanding presence from long years in power.","It was Zhou Liren, the current head of the Zhou family.","“What’s going on?”","When Zhou Liren saw the bright red handprint on his granddaughter’s face, his expression instantly darkened.","“Yun’er, who hit you?”","Seeing her grandfather, Zhou Yun finally felt a backbone. She pointed at Liu Yutong, sobbing: “Grandfather, it was her! This bitch! She hit me! You must get justice for me!”","Zhou Liren’s gaze snapped to Liu Yutong, his eyes sharp as knives.","“Whose child are you? How dare you strike my granddaughter at the Jiang family’s banquet? Who gave you the nerve?”","Liu Yutong looked straight at the Zhou family leader, unflinching.","“Old Master Zhou, right? Your granddaughter just now publicly insulted my sister, insulted the Lin family, and called me a flaunting street girl. I was simply teaching her a lesson on how to mind her tongue. Do you have a problem with that?”","“Or is this how it is—when the little one loses, the old one steps in to settle the score?”","Zhou Liren’s face stiffened. He turned to Zhou Yun: “Is what she says true?”","Zhou Yun looked a little guilty: “I—I just said it casually...”","But halfway through, she suddenly regained her confidence and pointed at Liu Yutong: “Grandfather, she beat my brother! I was only trying to get justice for him, and then she hit me!”","Zhou Liren turned back to Liu Yutong: “So you’re the one who injured my grandson Zhou Heng.”","Liu Yutong nodded: “Old Master Zhou, I do have to take some responsibility for your grandson’s condition—I was too lenient. I should have crippled him instead.”","“You!”","Zhou Liren’s face went livid with rage, his beard quivering.","This girl was way too arrogant!","The young Zhou family members behind him glared with murderous fury, as if they wanted to tear Liu Yutong apart.","“Grandfather, did you hear what she said? She beat my brother and now she’s this cocky! Today, she has to answer to the Zhou family! Otherwise, where do we put our face?”","Liu Yutong looked at Zhou Yun again. “What kind of explanation do you want? How about I let you experience what it’s like to have three ribs broken, just like your brother? Then you’ll know exactly how useless he really is.”","“You!” Zhou Yun was speechless with rage.","Zhou Liren, being the old hand he was, still managed to keep his composure even now. “Little girl, I don’t care whose daughter you are, but in the capital, no one dares speak to the Zhou family like this. Today, you must apologize to my family in front of everyone, or face the consequences!”","“Face the consequences?”","Liu Yutong laughed. “Well then, old sir, you’d better be careful. I don’t know my own strength, and if I accidentally rough you up too, the Zhou family’s reputation might just go down with you.”","“How dare you!”","Zhou Liren was furious. “Arrogant! Absolutely arrogant!”","Just as the situation was about to spiral out of control, Jiang Yuan stepped forward to play the peacemaker.","“Old Master Zhou, calm down, calm down. Today is my cousin’s eightieth birthday celebration, a joyous occasion. Let’s talk things out and not ruin the harmony.”","Jiang Yuan, eager to boost his own status and curry favor with the Jiang family, shamelessly claimed that Old Madam Jiang was his distant cousin.","He positioned himself between the Lin and Zhou families, who were at each other’s throats, and first cupped his hands to Zhou Liren. “Old Master Zhou, I understand how you feel. Having your grandchildren humiliated one after another would upset anyone. It’s true that Director Liu was a bit impulsive and shouldn’t have struck her.”","Then he turned to Liu Yutong. “Director Liu, although we’ve only just met, I must advise you not to be too rash. That slap may have put you in the wrong. For my sake, let’s just drop the matter.”","Liu Yutong looked at his sanctimonious demeanor and sneered inwardly.","This old fox is trying to play both sides.","“Mr. Jiang is right. I was indeed impulsive,” Liu Yutong said.","But then her tone shifted. “However, I have a bad habit: I can’t stand being cursed at. The moment someone cusses me out, my hands get itchy. That slap was just a reflex—I couldn’t hold back.”","Jiang Yuan paused for a moment, then gave a dry chuckle. “Regardless, for my sake today, let’s put this aside for now, shall we? After all, this is my cousin’s birthday banquet. Making too big a scene would be a slap in the Jiang family’s face.”","Zhou Liren snorted coldly, unconvinced. “Brother Jiang, that’s easy for you to say. What about the slap my granddaughter took? Are we just supposed to let it slide?”","Jiang Yuan sighed, leaned in close to Zhou Liren’s ear, and whispered a few quick words.","After hearing them, Zhou Liren’s face flickered with uncertainty as he glanced at Liu Yutong. Finally, he gave a heavy huff. “Fine, for Brother Jiang’s sake and for the old lady’s, I’ll let it go for now. But girl, you remember this—this isn’t over!”","With that, he led the Zhou family away in a huff."]},{"number":768,"title":"Chapter 768: 769, Sending Gifts, the Lady Arrives. (Thanks to 'Mingming Yang' for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong didn’t immediately return to the VIP section. Instead, she sat down right next to Lin Yi.","She still didn’t enjoy sitting with a bunch of older men and women—there was too much distance. She felt more comfortable at a table with young people.","By now, the people around them were looking at Liu Yutong and the Lin family members with noticeably different attitudes than before.","There was curiosity, surprise, and even a hint of awe.","After all, someone who dared to slap the eldest daughter of the Zhou family in front of everyone at the Jiang family’s birthday banquet and walk away unscathed was a rare sight in the capital.","And judging by how Lin Yi and the others were calling each other “sis” and “bro,” people seemed to be realizing something belatedly.","This Lin family didn’t seem as useless as the rumors suggested.","Lin Yi didn’t need much explanation. Though she grew up in the Shen family, she still had Lin blood in her veins.","As for Gao Min, someone had already found out that she was the daughter of the Lin family matriarch and also a first-level police inspector.","No wonder she showed no fear in front of the Zhou family.","And Liu Yutong was even more impressive—young as she was, she was already the chairman of a major corporation. On top of that, it seemed she had countless ties to the Lin family.","Looking at it that way, the Lin family was nothing to sneeze at.","Every single one of them was no pushover—they were all ruthless in their own way.","The only thing was, there were far more strong women than strong men.","Just look at Lin Feng and Lin Mian—those two were nowhere near the same level as the three female powerhouses.","Of course, Lin Feng and Lin Mian didn’t feel embarrassed at all. In fact, they felt proud.","So this was what it felt like to have powerful backers!","These sisters were awesome! Too cool!","Not long after the commotion had died down, a stir suddenly arose at the entrance of the banquet hall.","“Old Madam Jiang is here!”","“Old Madam Jiang has arrived!”","Everyone turned to look. An elderly woman with silver-white hair, wearing a dark red embroidered gown with floral patterns, walked in slowly, supported by several younger family members.","Though advanced in years, the old lady was in good spirits and exuded an air of nobility.","Flanking her were a young man and woman—one handsome and refined, the other elegant and graceful. They were Jiang Chao and Jiang Lan, the two most outstanding members of the Jiang family’s younger generation.","As soon as Old Madam Jiang appeared, all the guests rose to pay their respects.","“Wishing Old Madam Jiang boundless happiness and longevity!”","“May you stay healthy and vivacious, Old Madam!”","“...”","Old Madam Jiang smiled warmly and nodded to the crowd, taking her seat at the head table.","Only then did everyone else sit down, and the birthday banquet officially began.","Soon, the various families had their younger members present their gifts.","The Zhou family brought a jade artifact.","“Grandma Jiang, this is a small token from the Zhou family. Please accept it,” Zhou Yun said, handing over a gift box.","When the box was opened, inside lay a jade Buddha statue, smooth and lustrous, about the size of a palm. Its intricate craftsmanship made it clearly a rare treasure.","“This is a Hetian jade Buddha statue from the Qing imperial collection. My grandfather acquired it by chance years ago and treasured it ever since. Today, I offer it to you, Old Madam. May you enjoy good fortune, health, and the Buddha’s blessings.”","The crowd let out a wave of admiration.","That was no small gesture—it had to be worth at least seven figures.","Old Madam Jiang smiled and nodded. “Your grandfather is very thoughtful. Thank him for me.”","After presenting her gift, Zhou Yun deliberately rolled her eyes at Lin Yi’s table as she passed by, trying to provoke her.","Next came gifts from the other prominent families.","Some gave famous calligraphy and paintings, others antique porcelain, and a few presented jade and jewelry—every item was extremely valuable.","Old Madam Jiang accepted each one with a smile, though her expression didn’t reveal any particular reaction to any of them.","When it was the Lin family’s turn, Zhou Yun spoke up again.","“Lin Yi, what gift has your family prepared? Don’t tell me it’s some cheap junk picked up from a street stall? After all, everyone knows about the Lin family’s situation these days.”","At her words, the people around couldn’t help but roll their eyes inwardly.","Seriously? Didn’t you learn your lesson? You just got slapped, and now you’re provoking her again? Aren’t you afraid of getting another smack?","Lin Yi replied, “Miss Zhou, rest assured. No matter how down-and-out the Lin family may be, we wouldn’t embarrass ourselves with street stall junk.”","With that, she stood up, took a silk brocade box from Lin Feng, and walked over to Old Madam Jiang.","“Grandma Jiang, this is a piece of calligraphy my third uncle obtained from Master Qingyu. In celebration of your eightieth birthday, I present it on behalf of the Lin family. May you enjoy good fortune, good health, and a peaceful life.”","Once again, the crowd buzzed with amazement.","Master Qingyu’s calligraphy.","He was the undisputed master of contemporary calligraphy—a single piece from him was incredibly hard to come by.","Most importantly, this wasn’t an antique, nor did it have any quantifiable monetary value. The Jiang family could accept it without any awkwardness.","Old Madam Jiang’s smile became noticeably warmer. “You’re very thoughtful. I really like this gift.”","Lin Yi stepped back with a smile. As she passed Zhou Yun, she paused slightly and curled the corner of her mouth. “Miss Zhou, sorry to disappoint you.”","Zhou Yun’s face stiffened, and she gritted her teeth in fury.","Time passed, one moment after another, until it was finally Liu Yutong’s turn to present her gift.","She held a slender wooden box in her hands and walked toward Old Madam Jiang.","Everyone watched her, eager to see what treasure this woman—who had dared to slap the Zhou family’s face—could possibly offer.","Zhou Yun couldn’t resist sneering again. “Oh, so Miss Liu is finally presenting her gift? Let’s take a guess—what’s in the box? Another piece of calligraphy? If it’s another one by Master Qingyu, isn’t that a bit lazy?”","Several other Zhou family members chimed in with laughter.","“Maybe it’s a painting by Tang Bohu? Hahaha...”","“If it really turns out to be by Tang Bohu, I’ll eat this cup on the spot.”","“Come on, Miss Liu is from out of town. Maybe she brought some local specialty—like a basket of free-range eggs? Hahaha...”","Liu Yutong ignored their mockery and walked straight up to Old Madam Jiang.","“Grandma Jiang, I’m Liu Yutong, from Mingzhu City. This is my birthday gift for you. Please accept it.”","With that, she opened the wooden box.","Inside was neither a famous painting, nor an antique, nor any local specialty.","Instead, it was a framed piece of calligraphy.","The characters were written with a brush in a very childish hand—crooked and uneven, clearly the work of a beginner or a child.","It read: “Wishing Grandma Jiang good health and a long, long life.”","The signature consisted of a long list of names, densely packed—over a thousand of them, like a guestbook of signatures.","The banquet hall fell silent for a moment, then erupted in laughter.","“Hahaha... That’s it? A basket of free-range eggs would be worth more!”","“Which kindergarten kid wrote that? Miss Liu, this is way too careless!”","The younger members of the Zhou family laughed the loudest.","“That gift might just be the weirdest I’ve ever seen!”","“Isn’t she just trying to brush off the old lady?”","“...”","Even some neutral onlookers couldn’t hide their odd expressions and shook their heads.","This gift really was... hard to justify.","Although giving something too valuable to Old Madam Jiang might have been inappropriate, as she might return it all later, surely one couldn’t be this dismissive.","At the very least, she should have shown some sincerity.","Just as Zhou Yun was about to speak again with a sarcastic tone, a gentle yet piercing voice came from the doorway.","\"What gift has made you all laugh so much? I'd like to see it too.\"","Then they saw a particularly dignified middle-aged woman, surrounded by a group of core members of the Jiang family, walk in.","The woman appeared to be in her fifties, exceptionally well-preserved, with a gentle and graceful demeanor, yet radiating an authoritative air that inspired respect without anger.","Everyone present froze at the sight of her.","After a moment of realization, they all stood up abruptly, their expressions turning extremely respectful.","\"Madam, good to see you!\""]},{"number":769,"title":"Chapter 769: 770, Causing Trouble Again.","paragraphs":["\"What gift made you all laugh so happily? I’d like to see it too.\"","Suddenly, a very magnetic voice came from outside the door.","Everyone instinctively turned their heads.","They saw an elegant, noble-looking middle-aged woman, who appeared to be in her fifties, slowly walking in, surrounded by a group of members from the Jiang family.","The people present were momentarily stunned.","Once they recognized who it was, they all stood up abruptly, their expressions turning extremely respectful.","\"Greetings, Madam!\"","\"Madam has arrived!\"","\"......\"","Liu Yutong was also taken aback.","Though she had never been one to fear much of anything, facing someone of Madam’s stature instinctively made her feel a sense of pressure.","Beyond that, there was also a deep, heartfelt respect.","She had only ever seen this person on television news before. She never expected the real figure to appear at such an occasion.","She knew full well what Madam represented behind the scenes.","To put it simply, even if Uncle Li were here, he would have to greet her respectfully.","Old Madam Jiang saw Madam arriving and quickly rose, excitedly stepping forward to welcome her.","\"Madam, why did you come in person? This... this is too much of an honor.\"","Though she had known in advance that Madam would come, actually seeing her in the flesh still left her flustered with excitement.","Madam smiled and gently supported Old Madam Jiang’s hand, speaking warmly: \"Aunt Jiang, what are you saying? It’s your eightieth birthday—how could I not come? Back in the day, if it weren’t for you looking after me, I wouldn’t have been able to study and work so peacefully.\"","Hearing this, Old Madam Jiang’s eyes reddened: \"Madam still remembers those old stories. I... I really don’t know what to say anymore.\"","Everyone listening suddenly understood.","So this was the bond between Madam and Old Madam Jiang.","No wonder Madam had come personally to celebrate the birthday.","After Madam helped Old Madam Jiang to the seat of honor, her gaze fell on the calligraphy piece that everyone had been mocking.","\"Whose gift is this? May I take a look?\"","Liu Yutong was about to say it was hers, but before she could get the words out, Zhou Yun sprang forward like she had been injected with adrenaline. She darted out from the crowd and rushed up to Madam in a few quick steps, moving so fast that no one had time to react.","\"Madam, I know! It’s her gift!\" she said, pointing at Liu Yutong.","The moment Zhou Liren saw his granddaughter jump out, his face instantly darkened.","This foolish girl, what did she think she was doing!","This was the Jiang residence, and Madam was present. You jump out to point fingers—are you trying to court death!","He was just about to call his granddaughter back, but Zhou Yun had already lost all restraint. Pointing at Liu Yutong, she launched into a tirade of humiliation.","\"Madam, her gift to Grandma Jiang clearly shows she has no respect for her at all. Just look at the writing—all crooked and sloppy, like something a kindergartner would do. And she dares to offer this to Grandma Jiang!\"","\"A person like her doesn't even deserve to be at an occasion like this. She's dragging down the whole standard!\"","At these words, the guests were all stunned.","Was this girl out of her mind, publicly tearing down someone in such a setting?","Causing trouble earlier was one thing—since Old Madam Jiang wasn’t present, everyone just laughed it off as a joke.","But now?","Madam was here, and you still dare to make such a scene!","For the Zhou family to have such a granddaughter—that was a disaster for the entire household!","Some of those who had grudges against the Zhou family started sneering quietly, waiting to see how the Zhou family would clean up this mess.","Old Madam Jiang’s expression also turned visibly displeased.","Though she had a good relationship with Zhou Yun’s grandfather, Zhou Yun causing trouble like this in the Jiang residence reflected badly on her as the host.","And with Madam present, it was an even greater insult to her face.","She was about to speak up to stop it, but her granddaughter Jiang Lan stepped forward first.","\"Miss Zhou, please be mindful of the occasion!\"","\"This is the Jiang family’s birthday banquet, and Madam is here. Do not speak irresponsibly!\"","Jiang Chao also spoke coldly: \"Miss Zhou, Miss Liu is a guest of the Jiang family. Please show her some respect!\"","Even after being warned by the Jiang family, Zhou Yun still refused to back down. \"I’m... I’m just telling the truth! And she’s a female thug! She beat up my brother, and she beat me too. Look at my face—it’s still swollen!\"","She pointed at the red marks on her own face, looking as if she had suffered a great injustice.","Zhou Liren could finally take it no longer. He stepped forward and barked: \"Enough! Shut your mouth!\"","But Zhou Yun was already too far gone. She wouldn’t listen to anyone. In her mind, Madam’s arrival was a perfect opportunity to humiliate Liu Yutong, even to make her lose face completely.","What she failed to realize was that she was the one truly embarrassing herself.","Of course, she couldn’t see that. Some people are not just foolish but also stubbornly single-minded.","\"Grandfather, why are you defending her? She hit me! She—\"","\"Shut up!\"","Zhou Liren’s beard trembled with rage. He wanted nothing more than to slap his stupid granddaughter right then and there.","First, he was furious at her lack of brains, disgracing the Zhou family.","Second, he was angry that her impulsiveness had ruined the Zhou family’s image in front of Madam.","And third, he and Jiang Yuan had set a trap for Liu Yutong. With his granddaughter’s scene, everything might collapse.","Zhou Liren turned to face Madam and bowed deeply.","\"Madam, this old man has failed in discipline. My granddaughter has offended you. I will have her removed immediately and punish her harshly at home.\"","With that, he ordered the younger members of the Zhou family to drag her away, not giving her any chance to speak further.","Jiang Yuan stood in a corner, watching, and inwardly cursed the Zhou family to hell.","The Zhou family was utterly unreliable. How could they jump out and ruin things at this critical moment? It was pure stupidity.","Useless troublemakers!","He began recalculating in his mind, considering whether to just give up.","After all, he hadn’t expected Madam to show up. If she sensed anything amiss, he would be in real trouble—unable to escape blame.","But just as he was pondering whether to expose Liu Yutong’s identity, his phone vibrated in his pocket.","He discreetly pulled it out and glanced at the text message. His face instantly changed.","The message was from an unknown number.","The content was a single short line:","[Over a dozen unidentified vehicles have appeared on the outskirts of the Jiang residence, suspected to be from the Wanlong Society. It is recommended to leave early.]","After reading the message, Jiang Yuan raised his head and looked at the girl who, even when being accused by Zhou Yun, remained calm and composed.","That girl surnamed Liu—what exactly was she planning?","She had actually stationed over a dozen vehicles outside the Jiang residence!","Could it be that he had misjudged her? Was she really coming for him?","He didn’t believe in coincidences, and he didn’t dare gamble that Liu Yutong would dare to start something at the Jiang residence.","But he also couldn’t take the risk.","Leave now.","He had to leave immediately!","Once he was away from this dangerous place, he could think things through.","But as soon as he took two steps back, a younger member of the Jiang family blocked his way.","\"Uncle Jiang Yuan, where are you going? You still need to toast later.\"","Jiang Yuan barely kept the smile on his face: \"I... I need to go to the restroom. My stomach’s a bit uncomfortable. I’ll be right back.\"","With that, he walked around the younger family member and quickened his pace toward the side door.","But just as he reached the doorway, he spotted Zhou Yun arguing with her own family.","Clearly, she refused to let the matter slide and was unwilling to leave.","Jiang Yuan had no intention of having any further dealings with her and was about to leave.","Just as he was about to go, Zhou Yun caught sight of him and rushed over, grabbing his sleeve.","“Grandpa Jiang, you can’t leave.”","“You said before that you had a way for me to avenge my brother and ruin Liu Yutong’s reputation.”","Jiang Yuan had discussed and planned this matter with the Zhou family, and Zhou Yun was aware of it—it was just that she couldn’t keep her composure and messed everything up.","Yet she had no self-awareness and continued to speak.","“That Liu Yutong isn’t a legitimate businesswoman at all—she’s a shady character!”","“Didn’t you say the truth had to come out? Now Madam is still inside. This is the perfect chance to expose her!”"]},{"number":770,"title":"Chapter 770: 771. Is She the Social Boss (Thanks to Golden Pattern Dao Pill Who Likes Crayfish for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Jiang Yuan looked at the visibly excited Zhou Yun in front of him, fury bubbling inside him. He wanted nothing more than to kick her to death.","This idiot—why did she have to show up at the worst possible moment?","He had just received a text message saying that more than a dozen unidentified vehicles had appeared on the outskirts of the Jiang family estate, suspected to be from the Wànlóng Society.","Though it was only a dozen cars, who knew how many people that girl had actually brought with her?","What if they were really coming for him?","He didn't dare to take that gamble.","But Zhou Yun's outburst had now put him directly in the hot seat.","People nearby had already started to notice them. If he tried to leave now, it might draw Liu Yutong's attention, and then he wouldn't be able to escape even if he wanted to.","Jiang Yuan forced down his panic and plastered a kind, grandfatherly smile on his face.","\"Miss Zhou, what are you saying? When did I ever say those things? Are you sure you haven't misremembered? You shouldn't say such things lightly.\"","Zhou Yun hadn't expected him to deny it. She became anxious. \"Grandpa Jiang, how can you be like this? Back when you came to the Zhou residence, you said you had evidence that could ruin Liu Yutong. You even said she had thousands of thugs under her command, that she was running a black-market gang—you—\"","\"Zhou Yun!\"","Jiang Yuan quickly cut her off, his smile vanishing completely, replaced by a cold, grim expression.","\"I've been polite to you only because you're the young miss of the Zhou family. But if you keep spouting nonsense and slandering me, don't blame me for losing all courtesy!\"","Zhou Yun was stunned by his sudden change in demeanor.","She stared blankly at Jiang Yuan, unable to understand why the kindly Grandpa Jiang from earlier had suddenly turned into this menacing figure, refusing to acknowledge what he had said before.","Seizing her moment of hesitation, Jiang Yuan quickly pulled out a brown paper envelope and stuffed it into her pocket.","\"Take this and stop bothering me!\"","With that, he shook off her hand and hurried away.","Zhou Yun stood frozen for a few seconds before pulling out the envelope.","Opening it, she found a stack of photos inside.","She barely glanced at the first one before her eyes lit up.","The photo showed a long street.","It was packed, row after row, with people in black suits, seated at tables, eating skewers of grilled meat. The scene was massive—almost stretching endlessly into the distance.","What was most striking was that all the black-clad figures were staring in the same direction, their expressions fervent.","She flipped through more photos.","There was one of thousands of people standing up at once, and another of Liu Yutong standing in the center of the crowd, surrounded like a queen by her devoted followers.","Seeing this, her heartbeat quickened.","This... this was just like a mafia organization, wasn't it?","Thousands of people, dressed like gangsters, gathered together drinking. If Madam saw this, Liu Yutong wouldn't be able to talk her way out of it even with a hundred mouths.","This was a major crime—involvement in organized crime and underworld activities!","Zhou Yun clutched the photos, her smile growing more excited.","\"Liu Yutong, let's see how you get out of this one!\"","And with that, she turned and ran toward the banquet hall, clutching the photos in her hands.","... ...","Inside the banquet hall,","Lin Yi stood among the crowd, her gaze never straying far from Madam.","This was her only chance—a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to get noticed in front of Madam.","Zhou Yun's earlier outburst had been an accident, but it had given Lin Yi a way to approach Madam.","She took a breath, steadied her expression, and stepped forward to greet her.","\"Madam, Grandma Jiang.\"","Old Madam Jiang smiled and nodded. \"Ah, Lin Yi's here. Come, come, you're a good girl.\"","Lin Yi stepped closer, naturally positioning herself beside Old Madam Jiang.","Madam seemed to recognize her and asked, \"Are you Old Shen's granddaughter?\"","Lin Yi nodded, her expression even more respectful. \"Yes, Madam. My grandfather often speaks of you. He says you were immensely talented and brilliant when you were young!\"","Madam laughed at this. \"Your grandfather is just flattering me. When it comes to talent, he's far more accomplished than I am. He was a famous scholar back in the day—I remember his poems even won awards.\"","Lin Yi looked genuinely surprised. \"Madam, you even know about that? My grandfather did write many poems, but he always said they were just youthful scribbles.\"","Madam replied, \"That's him being too modest. Old Shen's brilliance is something everyone in our generation acknowledges.\"","A few brief exchanges, and the atmosphere became warm and relaxed.","The guests nearby looked on with some admiration—Lin Yi really knew how to seize an opportunity and work a room.","Just as they thought this, Lin Yi smoothly introduced Liu Yutong, who was still standing off to the side.","\"Madam, this is my younger sister, Liu Yutong. The birthday gift you just received—that was from her.\"","Madam turned her gaze back to Liu Yutong.","She had already noticed this girl earlier.","It wasn't because of the gift that everyone had been mocking, but because of her aura.","Too pure.","Even dressed in such simple, plain clothes, she stood out among the crowd. It was hard not to notice her.","And besides, there was something familiar about her face—like Madam had seen her somewhere before.","\"What's your name?\"","Liu Yutong answered respectfully, \"Madam, my name is Liu Yutong.\"","Madam nodded, her attention shifting again to the calligraphy piece.","The writing was crooked, childlike, but clearly done with great care.","\"Were these characters written by children?\"","Lin Yi quickly jumped in to answer. \"You have a sharp eye, Madam. Yes, this scroll was written by children. Sister Yutong has always been passionate about charitable work. These signatures come from children she has helped in BS province—their blessings. It's nothing extravagant, but every character carries their heartfelt gratitude.\"","Lin Yi was clever. She had guessed from the childish handwriting the origin of Liu Yutong's gift—and she admired Liu Yutong for thinking of such a unique present.","After hearing Lin Yi's explanation, Madam seemed to recall something. \"So you're that young woman—the one who led outdoor activities for children in BS and saved many students?\"","Liu Yutong was surprised. \"Madam, you know about me?\"","Madam shook her head. \"I don't know you, but I've heard your name.\"","\"My husband came back and mentioned a young person to me. He said in BS province, he met a very young girl—only nineteen—but composed, thoughtful, and kind-hearted. A rare, good seed. He said if there were more young people like her, he wouldn't worry about the country's future.\"","As soon as Madam said this, the entire hall fell silent.","Everyone stared in disbelief at Madam, then at Liu Yutong.","Had they heard that right?","The top leader had actually met Liu Yutong—and had given her such high praise?","In that moment, the contempt many had felt for Liu Yutong melted away. They silently resolved to take this girl more seriously.","Lin Yi, for her part, gave herself a mental pat on the back.","She had gambled right!","Wasn't it precisely by bringing Liu Yutong along that she had used her as a stepping stone to get close to Madam? And it was working!","Only then did Old Madam Jiang fully grasp the weight behind that scroll—it was a blessing from children in a disaster-stricken area. With Madam’s own endorsement, this gift instantly became the most precious and sincere offering of the evening.","“Little one, this gift of yours Grandma likes very much! Thank you!”","She then ordered that the calligraphy be framed, carefully preserved, and hung in the most prominent place in her bedroom.","Liu Yutong: “As long as you like it, Grandma Jiang. I was worried it might not meet your expectations.”","Old Madam Jiang: “How could that be? This is the most valuable and favorite gift I’ve received today.”","After all, it had Madam’s approval, and the collective blessing from the children of the disaster area added layers of meaning—making its worth soar.","Madam gazed at the strikingly beautiful and elegant young woman before her, liking her more and more with each passing moment. Then, to the astonishment of the guests, she took Liu Yutong’s hand and invited her to sit at the main table.","“Come, child, sit with me. Let’s have a chat.”","That simple gesture sent shockwaves through everyone present. Jealousy flickered in many eyes.","“Wow! She actually took her hand!”","“Am I seeing things? Since when does Madam ever get close to a junior at an event like this?”","“Just who is this girl? Who said her gift was cheap?”","“No one can call a gift cheap when a leader has personally praised it.”","“Looks like this girl is about to skyrocket.”","“More than skyrocket—she’s being sent straight to the heavens! With Madam holding her hand like that, from now on, everyone in the capital will treat her with respect.”","“...”","In an instant, all the guests—whether from old noble families, high society, or leadership circles—knew better than to underestimate this young woman again.","Those who had mocked her gift now wished they could slap themselves for running their mouths.","And none more so than the members of the Zhou family, whose faces turned especially sour.","Just as they were considering finding a moment to apologize and mend fences—","Suddenly!","Zhou Yun burst back into the room, having been escorted out earlier. She held a stack of photos high above her head and shouted for all to hear: “Don’t let her fool you! She’s no business tycoon! She’s a mob boss—a gangland queenpin!”","“She commands thousands of thugs! They’ve done every evil imaginable! I’ve got proof!”","At those words, the guests were dumbstruck.","What?","She... what did she just say?","That girl holding Madam’s hand is a crime lord?","This has to be a joke!"]},{"number":771,"title":"Chapter 771: 772, Awaiting Results.","paragraphs":["Zhou Yun’s outburst was so sudden that the brains of the guests in the banquet hall momentarily short-circuited.","“Wait, what did she just say? Miss Liu is a gang boss?”","“What a ridiculous joke! The Madam personally endorsed her—how could she be involved in organized crime?”","“Has that Zhou girl lost her mind? To dare spout such nonsense at a time like this, is she asking for trouble?”","“......”","Voices of doubt and ridicule grew louder, with everyone staring at Zhou Yun as if she were insane.","It wasn’t that they didn’t believe her—it was that they simply dared not believe.","Just moments ago, the Madam herself had said that even a high-ranking leader had praised Liu Yutong.","How could someone remembered and complimented by such an important figure possibly be a criminal?","Unless Zhou Yun could produce irrefutable proof, the chaos she was causing today was nothing short of walking to her own doom.","And on top of that, having a granddaughter like Zhou Yun was nothing less than a disaster for the Zhou family!","Lin Dong and the other Lin family members began to panic upon hearing Zhou Yun’s words.","Lin Feng, in particular, had witnessed Liu Yutong’s influence in Pearl City firsthand. That kind of scene would make anyone doubt that Liu Yutong was a harmless woman.","Could Zhou Yun actually have real evidence?","If she did, they were in serious trouble.","Of course, Lin Dong shared similar worries, his heart pounding with anxiety.","Earlier, when he heard the Madam say she knew Liu Yutong and thought highly of her, he had been ecstatic.","He never imagined that his seemingly unremarkable stepdaughter possessed such immense clout, valued by the Madam and even praised by a top leader.","He felt more and more that agreeing to back Gao Min in Pearl City had been an incredibly wise decision.","After all, everyone present understood just how valuable the Madam’s approval was.","Simply put, from now on in the capital, no one—whether from the most elite noble families or the newly rich and powerful—would dare look down on you.","Such was the Madam’s influence.","But now, this seemingly unbeatable ally was being accused of being a gangster.","Did he know whether Liu Yutong was shady?","Sure, she had a dark side.","But that didn’t matter. From this moment on, she had to be seen as clean!","Seeing the situation spiral out of control, Lin Dong stepped forward to strike preemptively.","“Zhou Yun, shut your mouth!”","“You’ve been picking fights since you walked in here, first insulting my Lin family, and now slandering Miss Liu as a criminal. Have you gone too far!”","He then turned to Old Master Zhou.","“Elder Zhou, you’ve seen what your granddaughter has done today, haven’t you? Is this the Zhou family’s upbringing? If you don’t give us an explanation today, the Lin family will not let this slide!”","Old Madam Jiang also spoke with a stern expression.","“Today is my eightieth birthday, with the Madam’s presence—it was supposed to be a joyful occasion. Old Zhou, your granddaughter has been causing trouble since she arrived, first insulting my guests and now publicly defaming someone. Don’t you owe me—and everyone here—an account of this?”","Her words prompted other family elders to join in condemnation.","“Elder Zhou, dragging this out will only hurt everyone. Better take her home now.”","“Exactly! To act so recklessly in front of the Madam is utterly brazen and disrespectful!”","“......”","In an instant, everyone’s accusations targeted Zhou Yun and the Zhou family.","Even the families that were usually on good terms with the Zhou family now stood against them.","It wasn’t that they were heartless—it was that circumstances demanded it.","Because the Madam was present.","Where the Madam was, there was absolute authority and correctness.","Anyone who spoke up for Zhou Yun would be seen as opposing the Madam.","So which side to choose was obvious—you could figure it out without thinking.","Zhou Liren’s face darkened to an extreme.","He had just ordered his granddaughter Zhou Yun to be taken away, only for her to return and blather on in front of the Madam, sealing their fate.","Even worse, this had completely made the Zhou family lose face in front of the Madam and all the assembled nobles.","“Zhou Yun, get out of here! Get as far away as possible!”","“Take her away! Now! Stop making a spectacle of yourself!”","The old man Zhou Liren had completely lost his composure.","Standing there, Zhou Yun felt utterly aggrieved as everyone pointed fingers at her.","She was telling the truth!","Why wouldn’t anyone believe her?","Why?! Why was everyone siding with that wretched woman?","Why?!","The more she thought about it, the more wronged and defiant she became. She steeled herself and decided to go all in.","“I’m not lying! I’m not!”","“I have proof!”","She raised the brown paper bag in her hand high. “Here! These are the proofs! She leads thousands of black-suited men—all gangsters. There are photos in here to prove it. She’s a gang boss!”","“And I also know what she did in Pearl City. She fought with the underworld there, took out several crime lords, and forced a boss named Zhao Weixiang to flee abroad, only for her to hunt him down and have him killed.”","“This is all true. I’m not lying. Why won’t you believe me?”","“I swear, if I’m lying, may I be struck by lightning and die a miserable death!”","Hearing such a vicious oath and so many sensational revelations, some guests finally began to waver.","Could Zhou Yun be telling the truth?","If so, then this girl the Madam was holding hands with was truly...","They dared not think further.","The atmosphere grew tense once more.","Those who had been condemning Zhou Yun gradually fell silent, observing the situation before continuing.","At the very least, they needed to verify whether Zhou Yun’s evidence was real before speaking, lest they pick the wrong side.","Lin Yi, standing not far from Liu Yutong, felt her heart leap into her throat.","Did Zhou Yun really have photos?","If they were genuine, what then?","Not only would Liu Yutong be finished, but Lin Yi’s own future would also be ruined.","She had been so close to Liu Yutong, even proudly emphasizing their relationship in front of the Madam, taking pride in it.","If Liu Yutong truly were a criminal, what would Madam think of Lin Yi?","A C-level official colluding with a gang boss?","Her political career would be over, and she might even face a purge.","Yet rationally, she still preferred to trust Liu Yutong. She had conducted a private background check on her; though there were some wild rumors, there was no solid evidence of any wrongdoing.","Zhou Liren, too, felt uncertain.","He didn’t know whether to believe his granddaughter or the documents she held.","He had also learned some details about Liu Yutong from Jiang Yuan before; that girl did seem quite shady.","If what his granddaughter had in her hands was genuine, then Liu Yutong was finished, and the Lin family would suffer as well.","As for his Zhou family, this could turn the tables and restore their dignity.","With this thought, he suppressed his inner agitation and no longer stopped Zhou Yun.","Gambling on this!","If the gamble paid off, once Madam was enraged, neither Liu Yutong nor the Lin family would escape.","Perhaps because everyone present harbored their own ulterior motives, the atmosphere fell into an eerie silence.","Everyone was waiting for a verdict.","Madam had been silently observing everything from the start, never uttering a word throughout the unfolding commotion.","Of course, given her status, she would not easily meddle in such trivial matters.","Only after everyone had quieted down did Madam finally turn to Liu Yutong beside her and ask,","“Girl.”","“Given what she said, what do you think?”"]},{"number":772,"title":"Chapter 772: 773, I'll Be Damned","paragraphs":["Madam turned to look at Liu Yutong, who had been standing by her side without starting to explain herself.","“Girl,” she said.","“What do you think of what she just said?”","Liu Yutong’s expression was calm. She showed no panic, no urgent desire to defend herself, and certainly didn’t cling to Madam crying out for mercy.","But what she said next left everyone stunned.","“Madam, would you like to see the evidence she has?”","“If you wish, I don’t mind letting her present it. In fact, I’m curious myself—how dark do you all really think I am?”","The moment these words left her mouth, the entire room was shocked.","“She’s not afraid?”","“Not afraid? It’s all an act, right? But pretending to be this calm under such pressure requires some serious composure.”","“I don’t think it’s an act. If she’s faking this level of cool, her scheme runs deep.”","“...”","Madam watched Liu Yutong with an enigmatic smile, as if pleased with her response.","This girl, heh, she really is bold and straightforward.","“Let’s take a look, then.”","Hearing Madam give the go-ahead, Zhou Yun couldn’t contain her excitement. She rushed forward clutching the photos, nearly tripping over herself in her eagerness.","But she didn’t care.","Her mind was consumed by a single thought: make Madam see this bitch’s true face!","Make everyone see it!","Ruin her reputation!","Drag her into the abyss!","“Madam, look! These are the pieces of evidence I mentioned. All these men in black are her underlings. Look at this scene—thousands of them gathered together. Isn’t that the hallmark of a gang boss?”","Madam took the photos and flipped through them one by one.","The first showed a long street lined densely with men in black suits, stretching endlessly into the distance.","The second captured them all standing at once, their chilling aura palpable even through the image.","The third featured Liu Yutong standing in the center of the crowd, looking exactly like a underworld overlord surrounded by her men.","The fourth, fifth, sixth...","Each photo was more shocking than the last, each more visually imposing than the previous.","Zhou Yun continued fanning the flames beside Madam.","“Madam, I also know what she did in Pearl City. She clashed with the underground forces there, took out several gang leaders, and supposedly had their bodies thrown into the river to feed the fish.”","“She even cruelly locked her own father behind bars—defying all morality and filial piety!”","“She’s a complete gang chieftain, a heartless female demon!”","“And she beat up my brother and assaulted me! Madam, look at my face!”","“Madam, you must seek justice for us!”","“...”","Hearing Zhou Yun’s accusations, everyone present felt their hearts pound.","If what she said was true, then this stunningly beautiful girl was far too sinister!","She sent her own father to prison and didn’t flinch at violence? Absolutely lawless!","But no one spoke up.","They waited.","They waited for Madam’s final verdict.","If Madam said she was guilty, they would all gang up on her.","If Madam said she wasn’t, then even if she was guilty, she’d be deemed innocent.","Madam finished looking through the last photo, raised her head, and gazed at Zhou Yun.","“Done? Anything else to add?”","Zhou Yun shook her head. “Madam, I’m done. Nothing more.”","Madam nodded, then signaled a hand.","A bodyguard dressed in plain clothes stepped forward immediately.","He was in his mid-thirties, with a rugged face and sharp eyes—clearly an elite guard of the highest caliber. Even Liu Yutong could tell at a glance that this man could outmatch even Cloud City’s Chu Yang.","Most frighteningly, at least four or five guards of this same caliber were present today.","Madam whispered something to the bodyguard, who then replied in a highly respectful tone.","Because of the low volume, no one nearby could make out what was said.","All they saw was Madam’s expression shift from calm to mild surprise, and then from surprise to thoughtful contemplation.","Everyone was baffled, unable to guess what Madam was thinking or planning.","After the guard finished his report, he stepped back to his original position.","Madam then rose to her feet.","As she stood, everyone in the room followed suit in unison.","Madam walked over to Old Madam Jiang, took her hand, and said, “Aunt Jiang, today is your eightieth birthday. I came to wish you well. Seeing you in such good health puts my mind at ease. I have some urgent matters to attend to, so I must leave now. Take care.”","Old Madam Jiang felt both flattered and nervous. She quickly replied, “Madam, you’re busy, you’re busy. I’m already honored that you came.”","Madam nodded, then turned to Liu Yutong and said, “Girl, come visit me at my place when you have time.”","With that, she departed in a grand procession, surrounded by her security team.","The crowd wanted to see her off but were stopped by the guards, left standing on tiptoes, straining their necks to watch her leave.","Only after Madam had gone did they all exchange bewildered glances.","Wait, that’s it?","What exactly did Madam mean?","No one could decipher Madam’s intentions.","All they witnessed was her reviewing the evidence, hearing the accusations, asking nothing and pronouncing no punishment—then leaving without fanfare.","Oh, and she also invited that girl over for a visit.","This...","Lin Dong and Jiang Lu were just as dumbfounded.","In fact, moments earlier, Lin Dong had been thinking about how he could speak up for Liu Yutong if Madam really pressed the matter. He’d even steeled himself for the worst—ready to throw caution to the wind and invoke his long-deceased elder to plead with Madam.","But after all his mental preparation, Madam just... left?","Still, for Lin Dong and his family, this was incredibly good news.","At the very least, Madam showed no intention of punishing anyone. On the contrary, she invited Liu Yutong to her residence.","What did that mean?","It meant Madam still acknowledged Liu Yutong!","It meant Madam did not see Liu Yutong as a gang boss’s daughter.","Lin Dong was now profoundly grateful he had agreed to Liu Yutong’s terms in Pearl City and latched onto this powerful ally.","The Lin family’s revival was looking bright!","Zhou Yun stood frozen in place. Seeing Madam leave, she felt a wave of panic.","“Madam... Madam, why are you leaving?”","“You haven’t punished her yet! She’s a gangster! She’s evil!”","No one answered her.","No one paid her any attention.","She was like a clown who had screamed and performed on stage, only to realize that the audience had either left or didn’t care about her act in the slightest.","Meanwhile, after watching Madam depart, Liu Yutong walked over to her, took the photos from Zhou Yun’s hands, and looked through them once more.","Then, holding them up to the crowd, she said, “I’m sure you’re all wondering whether these photos are real.”","“Let me tell you—they are real.”","The moment she said this, the entire room erupted into chaos.","“Wait, she confessed?”","“What the hell is she doing? Pulling a kamikaze?”","“Could she really be a gang leader?”","“But Madam didn’t say anything. Why is she admitting it? Isn’t that suicide?”","“...”","When they first saw those photos, everyone present instinctively thought the girl was definitely “in the underworld.”","Because people tend to be easily deceived by their own eyes when they don’t know the full story—especially when the figures in black in the photos looked so intimidating!","But since Madam hadn’t done anything to her, they couldn’t just label her as shady.","What they didn’t expect, however, was that the girl would just blow herself up on the spot, not even afraid that Madam might turn around and arrest her again.","Anyway, they couldn’t make heads or tails of her move.","When Zhou Yun heard this, her eyes, which had been on the verge of despair, instantly lit up.","“Did you hear that? She admitted it herself! She confessed! She’s a gangster! She’s in the underworld!”","But Liu Yutong’s next sentence made Zhou Yun’s smile freeze on her face.","“Everyone, I’d like to ask you a question.”","“If the employees of a legitimate company have a gathering, and it just so happens there are a lot of them, and they just so happen to be wearing the company’s uniform, and they just so happen to sit together... does that make them gangsters?”","When she asked that question, no one answered. They all fell into deep thought.","What she said made sense, didn’t it?","Who said a company can’t have everyone wear the same uniform?","Who said employees can’t sit together for a meal?","Judging someone as a gangster based solely on a photo of an employee gathering was indeed hard to justify.","They would need much more solid evidence.","Just as they were about to say something,","Suddenly!","A chaotic and noisy commotion erupted from outside, along with someone’s screams.","“Stop! Don’t run!”","“Catch him for me! Beat him to death!”","“Ahhh!”","The people in the banquet hall instinctively looked outside to see what was happening.","“What’s going on?”","“What’s happening out there?”","“Sounds like someone’s fighting.”","“Fighting? Who? Are they out of their minds? Daring to start a fight at the Jiang family’s doorstep—must be tired of living.”","“...”","Before they could react, a figure came crawling and stumbling toward them.","It was Jiang Yuan.","As he ran, he shouted at them.","“Help! Help!”","“Someone’s trying to kill me!”","“Cousin, someone’s trying to kill me! Help!”","Before anyone could figure out what was happening, a crowd of fierce-looking men rushed in behind Jiang Yuan.","They were all in black suits with dragon-shaped badges on their chests, wielding batons, looking menacing and murderous.","Over a hundred people surged into the Jiang family courtyard, caught up with Jiang Yuan, knocked him down with a single swing of a baton, and surrounded him, beating him like a stray dog.","“Run! Go ahead and run now, you bastard!”","“Dammit, once the Wanlong Society sets its sights on you, you think you can get away? Do you have what it takes?!”","The leading girl kicked Jiang Yuan hard again, and he let out a scream like a pig being slaughtered.","“Ahhh!!!!”","The banquet hall fell dead silent.","Everyone stood there stunned, gaping at the scene.","Soon, someone noticed that the black-clad figures looked familiar—they seemed to be dressed exactly like the people in the photos someone was holding.","When it clicked, they all turned to look in the same direction.","Liu Yutong.","The girl in the smoke-green dress was still holding the photos of the black-clad people gathering.","Then, as if to confirm they weren’t seeing things, they looked again at the black-clad men beating Jiang Yuan, then back at Liu Yutong. Their minds went blank.","So much for it being an employee gathering?","So much for it being a legitimate company?","We really fell for that one, didn’t we!"]},{"number":773,"title":"Chapter 773: 774, Still beating good people","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong had just left with the photo in hand, confidently declaring that her Ten Thousand Dragons Society was a legitimate company and that those men in black were merely employees wearing the company’s uniform.","The next moment, the so-called \"employees\" she had spoken of stormed into the Jiang residence and ground a man in his sixties into the floor.","When the crowd finally snapped out of their shock at the scene, someone stared at the extremely ferocious purple-haired girl and couldn’t help but ask,","\"Miss Liu, these seem to be your people, right?\"","Liu Yutong looked at the men in black, then at Jiang Yuan being pinned to the ground, and said awkwardly, \"It seems... yes.\"","She admitted it!","She actually admitted it just like that!","Every guest in the room suddenly felt a wave of dread wash over them. This girl had lost her mind—absolutely lost it!","Now let’s see how you explain yourself to the Jiang family!","Sure enough, Old Madam Jiang’s face turned extremely grim.","Just moments ago, she had looked kindly on the girl because of the Madam’s favor, but now the girl had given her such a \"wonderful surprise\"—having her men storm the Jiang residence and assault a guest of the Jiang family.","Even if the Madam thought well of her, even if the top leader had praised her, this matter had to be settled today.","\"Liu girl, what do you mean by this?\"","\"Today is my eightieth birthday banquet, and you send your men to break into my home and beat my guest. Do you take the Jiang family for some kind of doormat?\"","The other members of the Jiang family were also indignant, stepping forward one after another to demand an explanation.","\"Miss Liu, please explain yourself!\"","\"You must give the Jiang family an account of this today!\"","Lin Dong, Lin Yi, and the other members of the Lin family looked as though they had swallowed flies.","They had been overjoyed moments ago that the Madam favored Liu Yutong, only to have her spring this shocking surprise on them right afterward.","Right in front of all the elite families of the capital, she had her men charge into the Jiang residence and attack someone.","They wanted to blurt out: Miss, are you messing with us?","If you want to cause trouble, don’t do it at the Jiang residence!","The Jiang family was no ordinary household.","Old Madam Jiang was someone the Madam herself had called \"Auntie Jiang.\"","If this matter wasn’t handled well, not only would Liu Yutong be in trouble, but the Lin family would also suffer for it.","\"Yutong, you... you’ve taken this too far! Couldn’t you have dealt with this somewhere else? Hurry up and apologize to Old Madam Jiang—\"","Before Lin Dong could finish his sentence, Liu Yutong raised her hand to stop him.","Addressing the crowd with an apologetic tone, she said, \"Grandma Jiang, and everyone here, I’m sorry. This really was an accident.\"","\"Would you believe me if I said we really are a legitimate company?\"","The people exchanged glances, then looked out at the sea of men in black and Jiang Yuan still groaning on the ground.","They silently asked themselves: Do we look like we believe you?","Just look at those men in black—they don’t resemble any legitimate company’s employees.","And that Jiang Yuan, who had been chatting so cheerfully with you just a moment ago and didn’t seem to have offended you, ended up beaten by you.","Aside from arrogant and lawless, the guests couldn’t think of any other words to describe her.","Old Madam Jiang and the Jiang family almost laughed out of sheer anger.","Hundreds of men in black storming the Jiang residence and beating someone like this, and you call it an accident?","\"Liu Yutong, do you take us for three-year-olds?!\"","\"You must give us an explanation today! Otherwise, even if the Madam thinks highly of you, the Jiang family will not let this go!\"","\"...\"","\"I’ll give you an explanation.\"","With that, Liu Yutong walked toward the girl who had just kicked Jiang Yuan to the ground.","This girl was about twenty years old, wearing a purple wig and carrying a large megaphone in her hand.","When she saw Liu Yutong approaching, she immediately ran over excitedly.","\"Whoa, whoa, whoa... Sis Yutong, how was my work? That old guy tried to run, but I caught him red-handed with my people!\"","Liu Yutong looked at this carefree girl and felt a headache coming on.","Li Xiaohui.","One of the founding members of the Ten Thousand Dragons Society, her college classmate, and her best friend.","The girl was great in every way except for being too impulsive.","More importantly, when had she arrived in the capital? And why hadn’t Liu Yutong known about it?","\"Xiaohui, what are you doing here?\"","Li Xiaohui replied smugly, \"I brought the Purple Lord team here for a competition, and I happened to hear you were in the capital trying to catch someone, so I came over.\"","\"Catching people is my specialty! And I even bought a special command tool.\" She shook the megaphone in her hand.","\"So, surprise or not? Exciting or not?\"","Liu Yutong: \"...\"","Surprise was an understatement.","Good thing the Madam had left early, or if she had run into this, Liu Yutong wouldn’t be able to clear her name even if she jumped into the Yellow River.","She might even have ended up surrounded by countless people in uniform.","Of course, that was an exaggeration.","Li Xiaohui then noticed the tense atmosphere in the room. A bunch of well-dressed people were staring at her like she was a monster, and she asked curiously, \"Sis Yutong, what’s going on here? Looks lively!\"","Liu Yutong briefly explained the situation and the identities of the people in the room.","As Li Xiaohui listened, her excited expression gradually froze.","\"Sis Yutong... did I mess up?\"","Before Liu Yutong could answer, she quickly comforted herself: \"It’s okay! Ignorance is not a crime. I’ll apologize and explain everything!\"","Then, gripping her megaphone, she walked toward Old Madam Jiang and the others, drawing terrified stares from the crowd.","Some of the more timid guests even took a few steps back, afraid of catching her attention.","After all, everyone had seen her heroic kick that sent Jiang Yuan to the ground just moments ago.","They feared they might suffer a similar misfortune if they stood too close.","From their perspective, if even a man of Jiang Yuan’s status could be beaten for no reason, what chance did they have?","Old Madam Jiang remained stone-faced, while the Jiang family members around her watched warily.","Li Xiaohui stopped about three meters away from Old Madam Jiang, cleared her throat, raised the megaphone to her mouth, and said,","\"Testing, testing...\"","\"Respected leaders, respected elders, respected—uh—everyone, hello!\"","Buzzzzz—","The megaphone suddenly let out a harsh screech of feedback.","Li Xiaohui was startled and quickly lowered the megaphone, muttering, \"What’s going on? I just bought this! The seller said it was the latest model with super loud sound. Why the feedback?\"","She smacked the megaphone a couple of times and raised it again.","\"Uh, I want to explain to everyone—just now, I... buzz... meant to do it!\"","She had wanted to say \"I didn’t mean to do it,\" but the key word \"didn’t\" was swallowed by the feedback.","The room fell dead silent.","Old Madam Jiang’s face darkened even further.","Seeing the misunderstanding, Li Xiaohui quickly waved her hands and tried again: \"No, no, I misspoke! I meant to say, the reason I beat that Jiang Yuan is because he... buzz... is a good person!\"","Once again, the word \"not\" was lost to the feedback.","The guests: \"...\"","So you beat a good person? Isn’t that a bit too unreasonable?","Or rather, it's lawlessness and utter defiance!"]},{"number":774,"title":"Chapter 774: 775, Untouchable","paragraphs":["Old Madam Jiang was furious.","This was provocation, blatant provocation!","In her eighty years of life, she had never met such an arrogant person!","She had hit someone, and then, using a loudspeaker, she shouted that she had beaten up a good person.","Too arrogant!!!","Old Madam Jiang pointed at Li Xiaohui, then at Liu Yutong, so angry she could barely speak.","Jiang Chao and Jiang Lan quickly stepped forward to support the old lady, rubbing her back to calm her while glaring at Liu Yutong and the others.","\"Miss Liu, what exactly are you trying to do?\"","\"If you don't give our Jiang family an explanation for this today, it's not over!\"","Liu Yutong: \"...\"","No, you've all got it wrong.","The loudspeaker in Xiaohui's hand is faulty.","That's not what she said.","Seeing that the Jiang family members were practically shooting flames from their eyes, Liu Yutong quickly went over to Li Xiaohui, took the loudspeaker, and threw it directly to Yun Cheng behind her.","\"Xiaohui, it's better if you don't talk. Let me handle this.\"","Li Xiaohui nodded pitifully and muttered softly, \"I didn't know the loudspeaker was broken. It's not my fault...\"","Liu Yutong turned back to face Old Madam Jiang and everyone present.","\"Grandma Jiang, and everyone here, I will give you all an explanation for what happened today.\"","\"Please give me some time first.\"","Seeing her sincere attitude, the crowd reluctantly held back their impatience, curious to see what explanation she could offer.","If she couldn't come up with a convincing reason, the Jiang family would definitely not let this go—after all, this was too serious!","Even worse than what Zhou Yun had done before.","Liu Yutong turned and looked down at Jiang Yuan, who was lying on the ground, his face battered and bruised.","\"Old Mr. Jiang, do you want to explain to the old lady why you tried to run away early?\"","Jiang Yuan struggled to lift his head, staring at the girl in the smoke-blue long dress, filled with resentment.","He had guessed Liu Yutong might come after him, guessed the Ten Thousand Dragons Society might be lying in ambush outside, so he had taken the opportunity to flee early when his wife was around.","But he never imagined this girl would be so bold.","With his wife barely gone, right under the noses of all the noble families of the capital, she dared to strike directly.","\"Do you... do you know what you're doing?\"","\"This is the Jiang family! This is the capital! You—\"","\"I know.\"","Liu Yutong coldly cut him off. \"Even if the Madam hadn't left, I would still have taken action!\"","\"Because our grudge must be settled today!\"","She then spun around and declared loudly to all the guests present,","\"Everyone, the reason I brought so many people to storm the Jiang residence is for your own safety—because Jiang Yuan is a murderer!\"","The entire hall erupted in uproar.","\"What? She says Jiang Yuan is a murderer?\"","\"How is that possible!\"","\"She's crazy! Accusing Jiang Yuan of murder in front of everyone!\"","\"Jiang Yuan is a well-known patriotic businessman from Hong Kong. How could he be a murderer?\"","\"Exactly!\"","\"...\"","Jiang Yuan, upon hearing this, struggled to lift his head, his face a mix of fear and fury.","\"You... you're slandering me! I'm not a murderer! I haven't killed anyone!\"","\"Miss Liu, I have no enmity with you! Why are you framing me like this?\"","Liu Yutong sneered at his reaction.","\"No enmity? Jiang Yuan, do you really think I don't know what you've done?\"","\"Eleven years ago, in Pearl City, a police officer named Gao—do you remember that case?\"","\"And Liu Lei—how did he die? Have you forgotten?\"","\"They were both killed by you!\"","Jiang Yuan's face turned deathly pale.","\"You... you're lying! That case was closed long ago. The murderer died by accident. What does that have to do with me? Don't try to pin it on me!\"","\"You... do you have evidence?\"","Liu Yutong said only three words: \"Zhao Weixiang.\"","Jiang Yuan's pupils suddenly contracted.","Zhao Weixiang!","Hadn't he already sent someone to kill Zhao Weixiang!","Could it be...","Jiang Yuan's heart raced faster and faster, his fear growing stronger, but he still refused to admit it.","\"I don't know what you're talking about. Zhao Weixiang? I have no idea who that is!\"","\"It doesn't matter if you don't know him, and it doesn't matter if you don't admit it.\"","\"Jiang Yuan, did you think you were being thorough? That by killing everyone involved, no one would know the truth?\"","\"Too bad for you—Zhao Weixiang survived. He didn't die.\"","Jiang Yuan's eyes widened in shock, and he quickly shook his head.","\"Impossible! Wasn't Zhao Weixiang killed in a gang shootout? The news reported it!\"","Liu Yutong: \"That was fake. I had a false story leaked.\"","\"The real Zhao Weixiang is now in Pearl City, hidden away by me. He has evidence of your murder orders, as well as all your evidence of smuggling, money laundering, and fraud over the years!\"","\"Jiang Yuan, your time is up!\"","Jiang Yuan's psychological defenses completely collapsed.","He struggled frantically, trying to break free from the men in black holding him down.","\"Let me go! Let me go!\"","\"I'm a patriotic businessman from Hong Kong! You have no right to arrest me!\"","\"I've donated so much money, invested in so many projects—you bunch of gangsters, you're lawless!\"","\"Cousin Aunt, save me!\"","Even now, he was still trying to beg Old Madam Jiang for help.","But what answered him first was Gao Min's fist. Eleven years of suppressed fury slammed into his face and body.","\"Ah! Stop! Stop hitting!\"","Jiang Yuan let out another pig-like scream, rolling on the ground.","Inside the banquet hall,","The Jiang family members and the guests hadn't quite heard everything Liu Yutong and Jiang Yuan had said, only to see another girl attacking Jiang Yuan wildly.","They couldn't help but look away in discomfort.","Was this the so-called explanation she offered?","From their perspective, the gist of things went like this:","Maybe Liu Yutong really did have a grudge against Jiang Yuan, but he seemed to sense trouble and tried to flee early, only to be chased down and intercepted by the men in black, even all the way back to the Jiang courtyard.","But since the matter was handled too aggressively, Liu Yutong had to give the Jiang family a reason.","So she claimed Jiang Yuan was a murderer—only such a label could barely justify her actions, or the Jiang family would never let it go.","Then Jiang Yuan, as if provoked, started struggling desperately and denied everything.","Then the short-haired girl rushed over to beat him again, trying to force a confession and pin the murder charge on him.","As for why the crowd didn't quite believe Liu Yutong—there were two reasons.","First, those men in black did look rather thuggish.","Second, that purple-haired girl had already slipped up, saying Jiang Yuan was a good person.","How could he turn into a murderer in Liu Yutong's mouth?","They decided Liu Yutong was just grasping at straws for an excuse.","They also noticed a terrifying pattern: these women all seemed a little crazy, a little brutal.","At the slightest disagreement, they resorted to violence, completely throwing honor out the window.","They were worried that if they spoke up for Jiang Yuan, these girls would target them for a beating, and then, like Jiang Yuan, they’d be labeled as murderers. If that happened, wouldn’t they die of sheer injustice?","In this situation, wasn’t it just whatever she said goes?","Just as they were nervously watching Gao Min scold Jiang Yuan, one of the Madam’s bodyguards returned and went straight to Liu Yutong.","“Miss Liu, the Madam asked me to tell you that in the imperial capital, you need to be mindful of the impact. Don’t go too far.”","Liu Yutong’s expression turned serious. “Please tell the Madam that I will handle things here quickly. It won’t escalate.”","At that moment, Jiang Yuan spotted the Madam’s bodyguard and, like he’d found his last lifeline, desperately reached out to the man for help.","“Help! I need to see the Madam! I’ve been wronged! I’ve been kidnapped by gangsters!”","“Madam! I want to see the Madam!”","The plainclothes man paused, turned to look at him, and then said something that sent chills down everyone’s spines.","“Jiang Yuan, if you confess early, you might get an early grave.”","With that, he turned and left.","The hearts of everyone present churned with shock.","Seriously, what kind of backing did Liu Yutong have?","She said Jiang Yuan was a murderer, and that made him one? She wasn’t even a cop!","And the most critical part was that the Madam’s bodyguard had accepted it and even directly handed down a death sentence for Jiang Yuan.","This coordination...","Someone couldn’t help but curse under their breath, “Damn, the world suddenly feels so dark.”","Would you believe those words came from the mouths of these children of wealthy and powerful families?","As everyone looked at Liu Yutong again, their expressions had completely changed.","If before they were only dazzled by her beauty and stunned by her boldness, now only one thought remained in their minds.","This woman could not be provoked.","Absolutely not."]},{"number":775,"title":"Chapter 775: Chapter 776: It's Over.","paragraphs":["With the Madam’s bodyguard’s words, it was enough to seal the deal. Jiang Yuan was most likely a murderer.","After all, given the Madam’s status, she would never speak without basis, nor would she have her bodyguard say such inexplicable things in that setting.","Yet, for some reason, the people present still found it hard to believe.","Mostly because Liu Yutong’s men in black looked far too menacing—they didn’t seem like employees at all, but more like underworld figures.","The most intimidating such figures they had ever seen.","Liu Yutong turned to face the crowd. “You’ve all seen it. I say he’s a murderer, so he’s a murderer.","As for my people, they’re just a group of good citizens who love to act bravely for justice.”","Everyone: “...”","Fine, Miss Liu says it is what it is.","We’ll believe you, alright?","Zhou Yun stood frozen in place, staring at the dramatic scene unfolding before her, still unwilling to accept it.","Just minutes ago, she had been shouting that Liu Yutong was a gangster, brandishing photos and threatening to ruin her reputation.","But now?","The Madam was gone, and the Madam’s bodyguard had even sided with Liu Yutong, testifying on her behalf.","From start to finish, she had been nothing but a clown, utterly ridiculous.","“No! It’s impossible!”","Zhou Yun staggered back two steps, unable to process this reality.","Then, as if grabbing at a final straw, she whipped around to look at her grandfather, Zhou Liren, still in the crowd.","“Grandfather, you saw it too! She really is shady—those men in black are her thugs! Say something! Expose her, now—”","“Shut up!”","Zhou Liren slapped her hard across the face, the sound cutting through the air.","If he had been clinging to a shred of hope before, wanting to gamble on this, now he understood completely: Liu Yutong was not someone the Zhou family could afford to provoke.","The Madam’s bodyguard spoke for the Madam herself, and his words were a clear signal to everyone: She backs Liu Yutong.","So this matter had to end here—it absolutely had to.","After delivering the slap, Zhou Liren clasped his hands toward Liu Yutong.","“Miss Liu, my granddaughter is young and ignorant. She has offended you. I apologize here and now. When we return, I will discipline her strictly, and she will never trouble you again.”","With that, he waved his hand, ordering his men to drag away the numb-faced Zhou Yun, who no longer resisted. She was utterly numbed.","After handling his granddaughter, Zhou Liren turned to Old Madam Jiang. “Old Madam Jiang, today’s incident was my clan’s rashness. I will come another day to formally apologize.”","His apologies done, he wasted no time and left with the Zhou family. The birthday banquet had only just begun, but they had lost all face to stay.","Liu Yutong did not stop him.","After all, there was no deep-seated enmity between her and the Zhou family. In fact, thanks to Zhou Yun’s outburst, she had firmly established her authority among the elite circles of the capital.","From now on, no one would dare underestimate her, and she could expect fewer obstacles in her business dealings here.","Liu Yutong turned her gaze to Jiang Yuan, sprawled on the ground.","The once kind-faced man was now battered and swollen, lying like a dead dog.","Gao Min’s punches had been brutal.","“Sis, that’s enough.” Liu Yutong reached out and stopped Gao Min from striking again.","Only then did Gao Min lower her fist, her eyes reddened.","Eleven years.","Since the day their father died, she had been waiting for this moment: to capture this beast and avenge him.","“Little sister... I... I just can’t hold it in... sob sob sob...”","Liu Yutong embraced her, offering comfort.","She understood.","If it were her, she might be even fiercer, even crazier.","But they were at the Jiang estate in the capital, not in Pearl City.","The Madam’s bodyguard had already hinted that here in the capital, one must act with restraint—they needed to respect the host’s dignity.","“Yun Cheng.”","“Here.”","“Have him taken away, sent to Pearl City overnight, and notify the people in Harbor City to act. Don’t let anyone escape.”","“Understood.”","Yun Cheng waved his hand, and several men in black stepped forward, dragging Jiang Yuan away.","Just then, the silent Old Madam Jiang spoke up.","“Hold on.”","Liu Yutong turned to face her.","Leaning on her cane, supported by Jiang Chao and Jiang Lan, Old Madam Jiang approached slowly.","“Young lady, don’t you owe me an explanation?”","Liu Yutong replied, “Grandma Jiang, I helped catch a vicious murderer and protected everyone’s safety. Isn’t that explanation enough?”","Old Madam Jiang shook her head. “Today’s events stirred up quite a stir, but I am willing to let it go—on one condition.”","“Please, speak. If it’s reasonable, I don’t mind apologizing.”","Old Madam Jiang waved dismissively. “No need for apologies. I’m not so senile as to demand that.”","“I have only one request: from now on, you and your sister must visit the Jiang family often.”","At this, everyone in the room was stunned.","What did Old Madam Jiang mean by that?","Was she actively trying to win over Liu Yutong?","No, not exactly—it was more like she was using this opportunity to bring Liu Yutong and Gao Min into the Jiang family’s orbit.","Truly a masterful move by the matriarch!","Liu Yutong paused briefly, then smiled and agreed. “Grandma Jiang, I’ll hold you to that. Whenever I come to the capital, I’ll definitely visit you.”","Finally, Old Madam Jiang’s face broke into a satisfied smile. She nodded and, with the support of her children, turned to head inside.","Lin Dong and Jiang Lu, standing in the crowd, watched with immense pride.","That girl had made them so proud!","Not only had she not failed, but she had also earned the favor of the Madam and Old Madam Jiang.","With her leading the way, the Lin family could surely revive!","Jiang Yuan was taken away.","After much back-and-forth, the birthday banquet regained its lively atmosphere.","Following the meal, the guests began to leave one by one.","Before departing, each of them deliberately approached Liu Yutong, offering polite greetings, handing over business cards, and exchanging pleasantries.","“Miss Liu, I’ve heard so much about you. Let’s stay in touch!”","“Miss Liu, here’s my card. If you ever need anything in the capital, don’t hesitate to ask.”","“Miss Liu, you truly surpass many men with your courage!”","“...”","Liu Yutong accepted each card graciously.","After all, these people were influential figures in the capital. Her sister Gao Min would need to interact with them to develop her business here.","More friends meant fewer enemies.","When most of the guests had left, Liu Yutong was about to get into her car when a timid voice came from nearby.","“Uh... Sister Yutong.”","She turned to see Lin Mian.","This eighteen-year-old boy was looking at her with sparkling eyes.","“What’s up?”","Lin Mian hesitated before summoning his courage. “Sister Yutong, can I... can I become as strong as you one day?”","Liu Yutong laughed upon hearing this. “Yes.”","“As long as you’re willing to work hard and keep at it, you’ll become a very capable person someday too.”","Lin Mian’s eyes grew even brighter. “Really?”","“Really.”","“Sister Yutong, I’ll remember that. I’m going to work hard.”","Standing nearby, Lin Feng felt a pang of jealousy.","That brat—usually so quiet and tight-lipped—had somehow picked the perfect moment to suck up.","No way. He had to suck up too!","But just as Lin Feng was about to step forward and say something, Liu Yutong shot him a glare, shutting him down instantly. He could only climb into the car with a look of pitiful grievance."]},{"number":776,"title":"Chapter 776: 777, Drinking, Watching the Game. (Thanks to 'Hazel's Dog' for the God-level Certification)","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong didn't go back with the Lin family. Instead, she and Gao Min took a separate car and left.","The two of them found a small bar that was open all night, ordered two cases of beer, and with a few small dishes, sat quietly in a corner booth, drinking slowly.","The speakers were playing folk music, and a young man with a guitar was sitting on the small stage in the center, singing a song Liu Yutong had never heard before.","His voice was unique—hoarse, yet with a hint of clarity. It was beautiful.","\"Sis, what are you thinking about?\"","Gao Min had been staring blankly at the singer on stage. After a long moment, she said, \"I don't even know what I'm thinking.\"","\"Just... my heart feels empty.\"","\"Every night before bed, I used to think: where's the person who killed my dad? What does he look like? When will I personally catch him? I thought about it for so many years. It became a habit.\"","\"Now that I've finally caught the real culprit behind it all, my heart feels a little uneasy.\"","Liu Yutong didn't know what to say, so she simply raised her glass and clinked it with Gao Min's.","Gao Min tipped her head back and downed it in one gulp.","\"But still, it's good.\"","\"At least my dad can rest in peace now.\"","The two of them carried on like this, drinking and chatting about the past and the future.","The singer on stage switched to another song—an old one this time, with a pleasant melody and a touch of melancholy.","Driven by the alcohol, Liu Yutong found herself listening more and more intently.","To be honest, she wasn't much of a music connoisseur, but she could tell this guy sang really well, with a lot of emotion.","Gao Min couldn't help but praise him too: \"This singer is really good. He's got something special.\"","Liu Yutong nodded and waved at the waiter. \"Is that guy singing over there your regular performer here?\"","The waiter smiled and nodded. \"Yeah, that's Xiao Zhou. He's been here for about six months now, and he sings great.\"","Liu Yutong took a stack of cash from her bag—around two to three thousand yuan—and handed it to the waiter. \"After he's done singing, give this to him. Tell him he sang really well. It's a tip.\"","The waiter took it with a smile. \"Got it. I'll thank him on your behalf, miss.\"","Gao Min watched this, a little surprised. \"What are you doing?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Just tipping him. Who knows, maybe one day he'll make it big, and we'll be the ones who discovered him first.\"","Gao Min laughed. \"So you're a talent scout now?\"","\"Just in a good mood.\"","They continued drinking and chatting.","When they were about to leave, having had enough, the young singer walked over to them.","He looked about twenty-three or twenty-four, wearing a ripped denim jacket and carrying an old guitar on his back.","\"Ladies, was that money just now from you two?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"What, not enough?\"","The young man quickly waved his hands. \"No, no! It's way too much! I just... wanted to thank you in person.\"","Liu Yutong smiled at his earnest demeanor. \"You sang well. You earned it.\"","The young man said, \"Then... let me toast you two first.\"","With that, he grabbed a bottle of beer from the waiter and chugged it straight from the bottle, no glass.","Liu Yutong and Gao Min, seeing how straightforward he was, raised their glasses and clinked with him.","\"Did you study music professionally?\" Gao Min asked curiously.","The young man shook his head. \"No, I just love singing. I've loved it since I was a kid. After high school, I didn't get into college, and my family wasn't well-off, so I started singing on the streets to make a living.\"","Liu Yutong suddenly thought of something. \"You're this good—have you thought about joining a talent show? I heard there's a 'Voice of Dragon Nation' holding auditions in the capital. You should give it a shot.\"","The young man said, \"I can't go now.\"","\"Why? Is someone pulling strings to block your application?\"","He shook his head. \"No, I just signed a contract for another show called 'Show Me.' I made it past the preliminaries. The contract has a penalty clause, so I can't join another talent show.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"That's still good. Congratulations.\"","The young man said, \"Thanks, sis. But honestly, I'd rather go to 'Voice of Dragon Nation.' I hear the mentors are amazing—all big names. Too bad I can't make it.\"","Liu Yutong didn't know what else to say, since it was his choice. \"Just keep singing well. As long as you've got the talent, you'll shine wherever you are.\"","The young man nodded firmly. \"Yeah, I'm going to sing my best! Thanks, sis!\"","He toasted them with another bottle of beer, then slung his guitar over his shoulder and left.","After this little interlude, the two paid their bill and went back to rest.","The next morning, Gao Min boarded a flight home.","Jiang Yuan's case was closing in. The evidence from that old bastard needed to be dug up... A mountain of things waited for her to handle.","Liu Yutong saw her off at the airport.","Before leaving, Gao Min suddenly turned around and hugged her.","\"Little sister, thank you.\"","\"Sis, you don't need to say that to me.\"","Gao Min let go, her eyes a little red, but a smile on her face. \"Alright, I'm off. Don't stir up trouble while you're alone in the capital.\"","\"When have I ever stirred up trouble? I only ever strike back in self-defense.\"","Gao Min rolled her eyes at her, then turned and walked through the security checkpoint.","Liu Yutong watched her figure disappear into the crowd before turning and leaving.","In the afternoon.","Liu Yutong showed up at a relatively small e-sports venue.","The venue wasn't big, but there was a decent crowd of spectators—mostly young people holding signs, glow sticks, with team stickers on their faces, shouting slogans excitedly. The atmosphere was lively.","Unnoticed, e-sports seemed to be sprouting up domestically. Some teams already had fans.","Take Li Xiaohui's [Lady Zi] team, for example.","When Li Xiaohui founded the club, she kept the name [Lady Zi] for the game team. Only the club itself was registered under the cheesy but powerful name [Purple Dragon].","Today was Lady Zi's match day, and they were even competing in the game League.","It seemed Pony Ma had been fast—faster than she'd anticipated.","It hadn't been long, and he'd already launched League, this MOBA game that would explode in popularity in the future.","And from the looks of it, the response was good. They'd even put together entry-level professional matches.","Counting it up, the game had launched at least two years earlier than in her previous life.","Two years!","She wondered what Pony Ma was thinking, rushing it out so quickly. Was he afraid she'd barge in again?","After all, if Warcraft could change distribution companies, League wasn't out of the question for poaching.","Liu Yutong had just sat down in the audience when she saw a flash of purple bouncing around in the players' rest area ahead.","\"Hurry, hurry! Little Fatty, move it! We're going on stage soon, don't drag your feet!\"","\"Woo-hoo! Lady Zi will win! Lady Zi is unstoppable!\"","\"Hey, someone, bring over the energy drinks! Oh yeah, where's my megaphone? Who saw my megaphone? I need to cheer them on!\"","Li Xiaohui was wearing a purple team jacket today, with a purple headband and two streaks of purple paint on her cheeks. She looked like a moving purple flame, utterly chuunibyou, rebellious, and flamboyant.","Liu Yutong: “...”","She felt she needed to give this girl a lesson on what it meant to keep a low profile.","“Xiaohui.”","Li Xiaohui turned around, and the moment she saw Liu Yutong, her eyes lit up. With a roar, she pounced over.","“Yutong Jie! You finally came to watch my team’s match! Woohoo... I knew you wouldn’t abandon me! I’m so moved!”","After Liu Yutong finally managed to get rid of her, she sat down to watch the game.","Halfway through the match, the conversation of two nearby spectators drifted into her ears.","“Whoa, Lady Zi’s team is on fire! That mid-laner Little Fatty’s moves are insane!”","“It’s in the bag. If they win today, they lock in a spot for the national tournament. I heard the national champion gets a prize of five hundred thousand.”","“Five hundred thousand? That much?”","“Yeah, who knew Goose Company would be so generous, offering that much prize money for a game that just launched.”","“I’ve got a feeling this ‘League’ game is going to blow up soon...”","Liu Yutong listened to their conversation, lost in thought.","Five hundred thousand in prize money was indeed a lot at the moment.","But in a few years, that number would multiply several times—maybe even a hundredfold.","The e-sports track had only just taken off; its future potential was enormous.","Of course, that wasn’t the main point she was focusing on.","Goose Company seemed to have surpassed Shengda and Wangyi this year, becoming the number one gaming company in the country.","It looked like she needed to have a serious talk with Pony Ma."]},{"number":777,"title":"Chapter 777: 778, Welcome Competition.","paragraphs":["From 2000 to 2008, that was the golden age of PC gaming.","Shanda shot straight to the top with \"The Legend of Mir 2,\" and Chen Qiao briefly became the richest man in China, enjoying unprecedented fame.","NetEase followed closely, with \"Fantasy Westward Journey\" becoming a phenomenon that stayed popular for over a decade.","The9 secured the agency rights for \"World of Warcraft,\" raking in huge profits as well.","The landscape back then was crystal clear: Shanda was first, NetEase second, The9 third, and Tencent could only pick up scraps from behind.","But from 2008 onward, the situation completely changed.","Thanks to its terrifying traffic gateway, QQ, Tencent began a frenzied takeover.","First, it struck in the casual game arena, beating down once-dominant titles like \"Audition\" and \"Crazy Kart\" until they were lost.","Then, the licensed games \"CrossFire\" and \"Dungeon & Fighter\" exploded upon launch, becoming the new darlings of internet cafes.","By 2009, Tencent’s gaming revenue had already surpassed Shanda and NetEase, officially taking the top spot among domestic game companies.","Liu Yutong watched the intense esports competition on stage and couldn’t help but think.","The truth was, Tencent’s success now wasn’t about how good its games were—it was that terrifying traffic gateway, QQ.","With hundreds of millions of users, simply channeling some traffic could push any product to the top.","But was that really a good thing?","She still believed that the complacency bred by traffic monopoly would eventually kill innovation.","Just as she was pondering this, her phone suddenly rang.","She glanced at it—it was actually Pony Ma calling.","Speak of the devil.","“President Ma, what made you think to call me?” Liu Yutong answered with a smile.","A gentle male voice came through the line.","“Director Liu, I hope I’m not disturbing you.”","“Not at all. I’m actually watching your ‘League of Legends’ tournament right now.”","“President Ma, just say what you need to say. No need for formalities between us.”","Pony Ma paused on the other end for two seconds before speaking.","“Director Liu, I’m calling today because I need to discuss something with you.”","“Go ahead.”","“Well... we at Tencent have been working on our own microblogging service lately, and the product is about to launch soon. So, some of our past advertising collaborations with Weibo may need to be readjusted.”","“Are you saying you won’t let Weibo place ads on Tencent’s platforms anymore?”","“It’s not that we won’t allow it, just that adjustments are needed.”","“Our partnership has always been pleasant, and I hope we can find a way that works for both of us.”","Hearing this, Liu Yutong wasn’t surprised at all.","Tencent had already copied her farm game before, and it was only natural for them to copy Weibo now.","But this time, it seemed to be happening earlier than in her previous life.","In her past life, Tencent’s microblogging service launched in 2010, but now it was only 2009—a full year ahead.","Apparently, Weibo’s rise had put pressure on Tencent, pushing them to accelerate their own social product to defend their traffic turf.","“President Ma, I think it’s a good thing that Tencent is launching a microblogging service.”","These words left Pony Ma on the other end momentarily baffled.","Wait, was this girl serious?","She actually thought it was good?","Wasn’t she afraid history would repeat itself? Or was she underestimating Tencent’s copycat prowess?","“Director Liu, honestly, are you angry? I...”","“I mean it, President Ma. Seriously, I welcome Tencent entering the microblogging space.”","“Why?”","“Because I believe the market needs competition.”","“Right now, Weibo dominates alone, and frankly, that makes me uneasy. All the users are on my side, all the traffic flows to me. What if one day I get carried away, or my team does, and we make a bad product? Users would curse me out.”","“Having a competitor to share the blame with wouldn’t be so bad.”","On the phone, Pony Ma fell silent.","He suddenly felt he couldn’t quite figure out this young woman anymore.","She had built Weibo from scratch, it was now the largest social media platform in China, and Tencent was about to poach her turf, users, and traffic—yet she said she welcomed the competition.","This level of vision... he felt a bit unworthy.","“Director Liu, what you said makes me a little ashamed.”","“President Ma, don’t be ashamed. I’m being sincere.”","“But...”","Pony Ma’s heart skipped a beat: “But what?”","“Do you remember a pretty big acquisition case this year?”","“You mean Coca-Cola wanting to buy Huiyuan Juice?”","“Exactly, that one.”","“Coca-Cola offered 17.9 billion to acquire Huiyuan, but the Ministry of Commerce blocked it, citing monopoly concerns.”","“I think that decision was absolutely right. No industry should allow monopolies—monopolies kill vitality. So, I’m genuinely happy that you’re entering the microblogging space.”","“Director Liu, I...”","Pony Ma didn’t know what to say anymore. It felt like he’d finally met someone who understood him.","In recent years, everyone had been bashing him for copying and imitating. Now, at last, someone got it.","He was doing this to prevent monopolies, right?","Sure, it sounded nice enough to be comforting.","Director Liu really was a perceptive person.","No, if Director Liu was being so magnanimous, he couldn’t just let it pass without reciprocating. He should at least show more support for Loongson as an apology for canceling the partnership.","Little did he know, he was completely misreading the situation.","Liu Yutong had said those words to plant an idea.","She had let him copy so much from her—Farm Game and Weibo—without losing her temper, right?","So, when her own instant messaging service launched, she hoped he wouldn’t lose his temper either, and would sincerely congratulate her.","“Thank you, Director Liu.”","“You’ve set a great example. Business competition may be fierce, but it doesn’t have to affect our personal friendship.”","“Well said, President Ma. No matter how fierce the competition, personal friendships shouldn’t suffer.”","“Then I wish Tencent’s microblogging service a smooth launch. When the time comes, I’ll make sure to send a big bouquet of flowers.”","“Thank you! Thank you!”","After hanging up, Liu Yutong turned her attention back to the match on stage.","Pony Ma’s call had only strengthened her resolve.","No industry should be monopolized, and she wouldn’t allow anyone to monopolize—not even herself.","The position of QQ was hard to shake, but a chance had emerged to change the landscape and prevent Tencent’s monopoly.","Instant messaging tools.","Why was QQ so dominant?","Because it was the earliest instant messaging tool in China, had the accumulated user base, and had formed the strongest social relationship network.","Hundreds of millions of people were on QQ. If you wanted to switch to another app, no one would chat with you there—so you couldn’t switch.","That was the most terrifying part of social software—the network effect.","The more users, the harder it was to replace.","But that didn’t mean QQ was forever unshakable.","When new technology, new scenarios, or new demands emerged, that was the opportunity to break the monopoly.","Mobile internet was that opportunity.","In her previous life, WeChat launched in 2011 and took less than two years to completely reshape the landscape of domestic social software.","Although QQ was still thriving, it was no longer the sole ruler.","It was only 2009 now, so she still had at least a one-year window.","One year.","That was more than enough."]},{"number":778,"title":"Chapter 778: 779, Reunion at Cloud Mountain.","paragraphs":["Purple Clan’s team won.","The game screen froze at the moment the opposing crystal shattered, and cheers erupted instantly in the arena. Li Xiaohui was bouncing with excitement, her thrilled shouts blasting through the speakers: “We won! We won! Woohoo...”","Liu Yutong stood up, a smile spreading across her face as she applauded.","She had to admit, that kid called Little Fatty really had some impressive moves. In the final team fight, he single-handedly took down three opponents, turning a losing game around.","As soon as the match ended, Li Xiaohui rushed over like a gust of wind, exclaiming excitedly.","“Sister Yutong, did you see that? Did you see that? Our team is amazing, right? Especially that play from Little Fatty—it was incredible!”","Liu Yutong smiled and said, “I saw it. That was really well played.”","“Sister Yutong, you have to come to the finals. I’ll save the best seat for you,” Li Xiaohui said.","“Alright, I’ll be there.”","Liu Yutong glanced at the other team members and gave them another promise.","“I’ll come for the finals. If you guys win the championship, I’ll give each of you an extra big red envelope.”","“Wow! Sister Yutong, you’re way too generous!”","Li Xiaohui quickly turned around and waved at the team members, shouting, “Why aren’t you thanking our boss and benefactor?”","Several team members immediately ran over and thanked her in unison.","“Thanks, boss!”","“Thanks, boss!”","“We’re definitely winning the championship!”","The team members were overjoyed.","After all, making money in esports these days was tough. Having such a generous boss—how could they not be thrilled?","Liu Yutong waved her hand. “Alright, that’s that. Little Hui, I still have some things to take care of. I need to head to an event tonight, so I’ll go now.”","“Got it! Sister Yutong, go do your thing. Don’t worry about us.”","After leaving the venue, Liu Yutong got into her car and immediately pulled out her phone to dial Zhu Silin’s number.","“I’m done here. Is everyone here?”","“Sister Yutong, all the founding members of Cloud Mountain Society are here—Lu Hong, Gu Yebai, and the others. The dozen or so reserve members will also arrive later.”","“Good, I’m on my way now.”","At 7:00 PM, Imperial Capital Club.","This top-tier club, hidden deep in an alley, looked unremarkable from the outside—just an old-style courtyard house, without even a proper sign at the entrance.","But anyone in the Imperial Capital who knew the ropes understood that getting through this door usually meant you were eitherrich or powerful.","Liu Yutong’s car stopped at the entrance of the alley. As she stepped out, she spotted Zhu Silin waiting at the door.","The CEO of Cloud Mountain Capital and the daughter of a BS province leader immediately rushed over happily when she saw Liu Yutong.","“Sister Yutong, you’re finally here.”","Liu Yutong nodded, scanning the area briefly. “Everyone here?”","“They’re here, just waiting for you.”","As Zhu Silin led the way, she updated her on the situation. “Gu Yebai, Lu Hong, Shen Hao, Bai Shisui, Zhou Muchen—they’ve all arrived. Plus, there are thirteen reserve members on their way, all from the Imperial Capital social circles.”","“We’ve verified the reserve members’ family backgrounds and assets—they meet the requirements. Tonight’s just a formality to get them to sign the membership agreement.”","Liu Yutong paused slightly in her step. “Thirteen? That many?”","With a hint of pride, Zhu Silin said, “Sister Yutong, you have no idea how big Cloud Mountain Society’s reputation has become. Ever since we released last year’s returns, people wanting to join could line up from Dongzhimen to Xizhimen. These thirteen were handpicked—we weeded out the ones who didn’t make the cut.”","Liu Yutong didn’t say anything more and followed her through the corridor.","The moment the private room door swung open, the lively chatter inside stopped instantly, and everyone stood up in unison.","“Sister Yutong!”","“Sister Yutong is here!”","“Sister Yutong, I’ve missed you!”","“......”","The first to rush over was Bai Shisui. Dressed in a vibrant red little dress, she was like a blaze of fire as she ran up and threw her arms around Liu Yutong for a hug.","“Sister Yutong, you’re finally here. I haven’t seen you in so long—I really missed you.”","Liu Yutong gave her a thorough once-over and relaxed a little seeing her in good spirits.","“How’s the group doing?”","Bai Shisui’s expression turned more serious. “Everything’s going smoothly for now. My uncle has been sent back to China to deal with things. My mom is still giving me the cold shoulder, but I understand she needs time. As for that business association group, they’re all keeping their heads down now—no one dares to pull any more tricks.”","Liu Yutong nodded. “That’s good. Remember, you’re the head of the Bai family now. When you need to be tough, don’t hesitate. If you’re ever unsure about anything, come to me anytime.”","Bai Shisui nodded firmly. “Sister Yutong, I remember. Oh, by the way, I practiced my dad’s old char siu bao recipe for a long time at home and finally got it right. I’ll make some for you to try another day.”","Liu Yutong paused slightly, then smiled. “Okay.”","After a quick chat with Bai Shisui, Gu Yebai, Lu Hong, Zhou Muchen, and Shen Hao—the other second-generation heirs—came over in turn to say hello.","With that, all seven founding members of Cloud Mountain Society were present.","Apart from Liu Yutong, every one of them was either a child of privilege from top political families or a chairman of a billion-dollar conglomerate. Any one of them could command respect and influence outside.","But now, they all gathered around Liu Yutong like stars around the moon, calling her “Sister” in unison.","There was no way around it—she had earned it.","In just one year since its founding, Cloud Mountain Society had managed assets exceeding sixty billion.","What did that mean?","These people had been born into privilege, but compared to Liu Yutong, they all felt like younger siblings.","Her ability to generate wealth went without saying, but her poise and vision alone were enough to win their absolute respect.","Even though Liu Yutong was younger than them, they willingly called her “Sister.”","As soon as Liu Yutong sat down on the sofa, Zhu Silin handed over a list.","“Sister Yutong, this is the list of reserve members coming tonight. There are thirteen in total, with detailed background information included.”","Liu Yutong took the list and skimmed through it quickly.","All thirteen were children of Imperial Capital’s prominent families—surnames like Wang, Li, Zhao, and Sun. Their family backgrounds were solid, and the capital they could bring in exceeded one billion each, meeting Cloud Mountain Society’s entry threshold.","But when she reached the last name on the list, her finger paused slightly.","Zhou Zhao.","Liu Yutong looked up at Zhu Silin. “Is this person from the Zhou family?”","Zhu Silin nodded. “Yes, he’s from the Zhou family’s main branch. He’s Zhou Heng’s cousin.”","She clearly knew about the friction between Zhou Heng and Liu Yutong.","“Did you verify the assets?” Liu Yutong asked again.","“Verified—1.2 billion, all in cash, with a clean source.”","Liu Yutong set the list down, deep in thought.","Someone from the Zhou family trying to join Cloud Mountain Society?","Interesting.","A few days ago, Zhou Yun caused a scene at the Jiang family’s birthday banquet, leaving the Zhou family utterly humiliated. Old Master Zhou slapped Zhou Yun on the spot and led his family away in disgrace.","Logically, the Zhou family should despise her now.","Yet now the Zhou family actually wants to join the Yunshan Society.","Either this person knows when to adapt, hoping to mend relations through this opportunity,","or they still refuse to give up and are planning something.","Liu Yutong’s lips curled into a faint smile, a smile so subtle that Zhu Silin, standing nearby, inexplicably felt a chill down his spine.","“Sister Yutong, should I weed him out?” Zhu Silin said.","He had heard about what happened with Zhou Yun and Zhou Heng, but the list had already been set before that. Unsure of Liu Yutong’s thoughts, he had kept it unchanged.","Upon hearing this, Liu Yutong shook her head. “No need. Let’s see what they’re really up to.”"]},{"number":779,"title":"Chapter 779: 780, Meeting of Both Parties.","paragraphs":["\"No need. I'm going to see what tricks they're up to.\"","Hearing Liu Yutong's words, Zhu Silin opened her mouth but hesitated to speak.","Seeing her like this, Lu Hong crossed his legs and said casually, \"Silin, you don't understand. Sister Yutong has seen all kinds of situations. That Zhou Zhao is just a clown. What waves can he make?\"","Gu Yebai also smiled and said, \"Let him come. I also want to see what kind of people the Zhou family's younger generation are.\"","The other founding members in the private room didn't take Zhou Zhao seriously either. Their faces were full of disdain.","The incident at the Jiang family's birthday banquet a few days ago had spread like wildfire in the circles of the imperial capital.","Everyone knew that Sister Yutong, in front of so many famous families and celebrities, led hundreds of black - suited men into the Jiang family and arrested Jiang Yuan, a well - known \"patriotic businessman\" in Hong Kong, right on the spot.","She was completely unreasonable and extremely domineering!","Normally, when you barge in with so many people in front of the host family, it's already good if the host family doesn't turn hostile on the spot.","However, incredibly, not only did the Jiang family not cause trouble for her, but the old lady of the Jiang family even took the initiative to show goodwill. Even the noble lady of the family took a fancy to her and invited her to visit.","In this imperial capital, a place full of hidden talents, rules have always been supreme. Even the children of top - notch families don't dare to make trouble in a family like the Jiangs and have to behave properly.","But Liu Yutong did it. Not only did she do it, but she also got away unscathed and even won the favor of the Jiang family and the lady. It was simply incredible.","If it had been in the past, they would have never imagined such a thing could happen in the imperial capital.","It wasn't until Liu Yutong appeared that she became the first one.","With such courage and charisma, not only among girls of the same age, but even for them, the children from influential families, they couldn't hold a candle to her.","Of course, only someone as brave and decisive as Liu Yutong was worthy of their followership and had the qualification to be their leader.","\"Sister Yutong, no matter what that Zhou family kid is up to, we're on your side.\"","\"Yes, Sister Yutong, we're on your side! The rules of the Cloud Mountain Club were set by you. Whether someone can join depends entirely on your will. If the people from the Zhou family really dare to cause trouble, we'll just throw them out and make the Zhou family lose face completely in the imperial capital. Let them know the consequences of offending us!\"","\"...\"","Hearing everyone's words, Liu Yutong smiled and said, \"Don't be in a hurry. Let's wait and see first. I also want to see what tricks they can play.\"","Gu Yebai threw the lighter on the table and said with a smile, \"Sister Yutong will surely have no problem dealing with such a small fry. Let's just wait and see!\"","\"Silin, when will the people arrive?\"","Zhu Silin looked at her watch and said, \"Soon. We made an appointment for 7:30. There are still ten minutes left.\"","Hearing this, Liu Yutong stood up and said, \"Okay, then let's go out and greet them. They're our guests, and we can't be impolite.\"","Hearing her, the others also stood up.","The seven of them walked out of the private room together.","Not long after Liu Yutong and the others arrived at the main hall, several luxury cars appeared in the parking area at the entrance of the club.","Then, one by one, well - dressed men and women with extraordinary temperaments got out of the cars and walked towards them.","At the front was a young man in his late twenties. He had a straight figure, a calm demeanor, and an innate air of arrogance.","Liu Yutong took a few more glances at this man.","She didn't know him, but she could tell at a glance that this guy's background was probably not simple.","Moreover, Zhou Zhao from the Zhou family and several other children from influential families were half a step behind the young man, seemingly regarding him as their leader.","As the nominal manager of the Cloud Mountain Club, Zhu Silin stepped forward to greet them first.","\"Young Master Chu, everyone, welcome!\"","The young man called Young Master Chu reached out and shook hands with Zhu Silin, showing a polite smile on his face. \"Mr. Zhu, you're too kind. I've long heard of the Cloud Mountain Club. I'm very honored to be here today.\"","Then the remaining twelve people shook hands with Zhu Silin one by one, and then briefly shook hands with Liu Yutong and the others. The two sides had greeted each other.","Zhu Silin made a gesture of invitation. \"Young Master Chu, everyone, please!\"","A large group of people walked towards the largest private room.","To be honest, if all of them could really unite, it was hard to imagine how much power they would have.","After entering the private room, everyone took their seats in turn.","Liu Yutong, Zhu Silin, Gu Yebai and the other seven founding members sat on one side, and naturally, Liu Yutong sat in the middle.","The thirteen prospective members sat on the other side. There was a long mahogany table between them, and this table was like a dividing line, separating them into two camps.","Sitting in the middle across from them was Young Master Chu.","Moreover, since he sat down, Young Master Chu's eyes had been lingering on Liu Yutong, with undisguised admiration in his eyes.","This girl was really nice. She was very beautiful and had a great temperament.","Most importantly, he saw in her the same kind of self - confidence and arrogance that he had in himself.","It was very rare.","\"Mr. Zhu, please introduce us first,\" Young Master Chu said first.","Zhu Silin nodded and began to introduce them one by one.","\"This is our founding member, Gu Yebai, from the Gu family. The Gu family is in JH Province...\"","\"Lu Hong, from the Lu family...\"","\"Shen Hao, the chairman of Qiming Electric Appliance...\"","\"Bai Shisui, a director of the Bai Group and the president of the Chinese - American Chamber of Commerce in the United States...\"","\"Zhou Muchen, from the Zhou family...\"","Zhu Silin named and introduced each of them. Every time she introduced someone, the prospective members across from them would nod in greeting.","Of course, she also emphasized their backgrounds.","It was probably to tell them that they were not soft targets to be bullied.","They had strength and money. They had every reason to be confident!","After introducing these people, Zhu Silin finally began to introduce the most important member of their Cloud Mountain Club.","\"This is Liu Yutong, also a founding member of our Cloud Mountain Club.\"","Hearing this name, the prospective members across were immediately surprised.","\"So she's the Liu Yutong who embarrassed the Zhou family at the Jiang family's birthday banquet!\"","\"She's really beautiful. Even more beautiful than the rumors.\"","\"I heard that she's the first person who dared to act so recklessly in front of the influential families and still get away with it. She's so amazing.\"","\"Really didn't expect that she's also a founding member of the Cloud Mountain Club. It seems that the Cloud Mountain Club is really not simple.\"","\"...\"","Hearing what those guys across said, Gu Yebai and the others felt proud.","This was their Sister Yutong, the soul of their Cloud Mountain Club, who could make these arrogant children from influential families show respect.","Of course, Zhou Zhao from the Zhou family across was different.","His face turned as black as coal, looking like he had eaten a fly.","Liu Yutong's glorious achievements were the Zhou family's dark history!","There was nothing he could do. Who asked his younger cousins to be so useless?","Moreover, he really didn't expect to meet Liu Yutong here today, let alone that she was actually one of the founding members of the Yunshan Society.","Didn't that mean he had no chance of joining the Yunshan Society?","Zhou Zhao was recommended by Shen Hao, one of the founding members.","Of course, when Shen Hao got to know the other person, there hadn't been those conflicts between the Zhou family and Liu Yutong. Otherwise, he would never have recommended this guy.","However, Shen Hao had also roughly told Zhou Zhao about the structure of the Yunshan Society.","The Yunshan Society was divided into three levels.","The core was the founding members, a total of seven people, who held all the decision - making power of Yunshan Capital and enjoyed the highest proportion of dividends.","The second level was the full - fledged members, who had the right to invest and receive dividends, but no decision - making power.","The third level was the probationary members, who had the right to invest but with restrictions on the investment amount. They had a one - year probationary period and could only be promoted after passing the examination.","Since this Liu Yutong was a founding member, it meant she had the right to vote against, which was very unfavorable to Zhou Zhao.","However, when he saw Young Master Chu, Chu Junlin, beside him, he immediately gained some confidence.","He was one of the few probationary members who knew that Young Master Chu would never be content to be an ordinary member.","Then he could break the deadlock through Young Master Chu and even take the opportunity to annoy that Liu Yutong."]},{"number":780,"title":"Chapter 780: 781, The Disruptor.","paragraphs":["Zhou Zhao was twenty-six this year, the second son of the main branch of the Zhou family, and among the younger generation of the Zhou family, he was considered relatively steady.","Compared to his cousins Zhou Heng and Zhou Yun—those two fools—he was far superior.","The recent disgrace the Zhou family had suffered was entirely due to those two worthless members who had squandered their reputation.","Now that he, someone who still had some promise, wanted to join the Cloud Mountain Society, he had to run into this woman who had made their family lose all face.","What a small world, and what an unfortunate encounter!","Zhou Zhao glanced at Chu Junlin, who was not far from him.","Chu Junlin was twenty-nine, the leading figure in the Chu family's business direction for this generation.","When it came to the Chu family, their background was immense. Tracing back, they stood among those who could enter the core decision-making circle.","Although the Chu family had kept a low profile in recent years, their influence was far stronger than that of anyone present, including the Zhou family.","Chu Junlin himself was formidable—he founded Shining Star Media at twenty-three, took it public on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange in four years, and later acquired several well-known companies, including Origin Real Estate and Color Light Paper. He owned three listed companies, with a total market value exceeding thirty billion.","His network was also extensive, making him stand out even among the elite younger generation in the capital.","Given Chu Junlin's standing, he would never stoop to becoming just a preparatory member—he surely aimed to be at least a founding member, or even the chairman.","If it weren't for Liu Yutong blocking the way, Chu Junlin might have held back and settled for a regular membership slot.","But now that he knew Liu Yutong was a founding member of the Cloud Mountain Society, he had to find a way to stir things up. Otherwise, slinking away would only bring more shame.","Better to take a gamble and let Young Master Chu confront Liu Yutong directly.","As for him, he was only creating an opportunity to probe Liu Yutong for Young Master Chu, thereby not only getting under Liu Yutong's skin, but also indirectly showing loyalty to Young Master Chu.","As for whether he would permanently offend Liu Yutong...","It no longer seemed to matter, did it?","Having thought all this through, Zhou Zhao made up his mind.","Then he quietly leaned over and whispered a few words into Chu Junlin's ear.","Chu Junlin leaned back in his chair, toying with a silver lighter. After listening to Zhou Zhao, he gave a slight nod.","\"Alright.\"","Hearing Chu Junlin's reply, Zhou Zhao felt greatly reassured.","Just then, Zhu Silin had finished introducing the founding members and began getting down to business.","\"We've all reviewed everyone's background materials, and you all meet the entry requirements for the Cloud Mountain Society. Today, we invited everyone mainly to get acquainted and go through the formalities of signing the membership agreement.\"","She then took over a dozen documents from her briefcase and handed one to each person.","\"This is the membership agreement. Please take a look, and if there are no issues, sign it.\"","In truth, everyone had already familiarized themselves with the contents of these agreements beforehand and understood the rules of the Cloud Mountain Society.","So, they simply skimmed through and were about to sign with their pens raised.","But just as they were about to sign, a voice suddenly rang out.","\"Hold on!\"","Everyone paused and turned to look—it was Zhou Zhao.","What was he up to?","Zhou Zhao placed the agreement on the table and looked at Zhu Silin. \"President Zhu, I have a question I'd like to ask.\"","Zhu Silin: \"Feel free to speak, Young Master Zhou.\"","Zhou Zhao: \"President Zhu, the thirteen of us are here today with sincere intentions. We've met the entry threshold of one billion in cash, and we've accepted the one-year probation period. The fact that we've agreed to such stringent conditions shows something—it shows we truly believe in the Cloud Mountain Society and genuinely want to work alongside all of you.\"","\"But...\"","He shifted his tone, and his voice suddenly turned forceful.","\"Since we're working together, there are some things that need to be clarified.\"","\"For instance, how exactly does the Cloud Mountain Society's investment decision-making process work? Where does our invested money go? How is the return rate guaranteed? And how is risk controlled?\"","\"According to the agreement, regular members only have dividend rights, not decision-making power. I can understand that—founding members contribute more and deserve greater authority.\"","\"But if an investment loses money someday, do we have the right to be informed? Do we have oversight or supervision rights? We can't just sink our money in and not be allowed to ask a single question, can we?\"","\"After all, one billion is no small amount. We put our trust in the Cloud Mountain Society and handed over the money, but trust has to go both ways.\"","As soon as these words were spoken.","Muttering broke out among the preparatory members.","Truth be told, they had been given some warnings before, but back then, their position was different—they had been the ones begging to join, so it was hard to ask too many questions, and they had to suppress their doubts.","Now that someone had stepped forward to raise these concerns, they naturally wanted to see how the Cloud Mountain Society would respond.","\"Young Master Zhou is right—one billion is no small sum; there should be some explanation.\"","\"Yeah, we may not want decision-making power, but we at least deserve the right to be informed.\"","\"What if it does go wrong? We can't just get nothing in return—that would be a huge loss for us...\"","Voices gradually grew louder, and the atmosphere in the private room began to shift in a subtle and delicate way.","A smug smile spread across Zhou Zhao's face as he heard the murmurs of discussion.","This was exactly the effect he wanted.","The role he had set for himself now was to represent all the provisional members, fight for their interests, and make them feel that he had their backs.","Even if Liu Yutong had a problem with him, she wouldn't dare call him out in front of so many people, would she?","After all, these people were all sons and daughters of noble families from the imperial capital. Offending one or two was one thing, but offending all of them was something she would have to think twice about.","Especially Young Master Chu, Chu Junlin.","Even if Liu Yutong had won the favor of the matriarch of the family, this guy probably wouldn't bat an eye.","As long as he could push Young Master Chu into the core circle, Liu Yutong's objections would be useless.","Both were founding members, and in a one-on-one vote, things would end in a tie.","After listening to Zhou Zhao's words, Gu Yebai was the first to speak.","\"Zhou Zhao, what are you trying to say? You don't trust us? If you don't, then pack your bags and get out!\"","Zhou Zhao immediately waved his hand, putting on an innocent expression. \"Young Master Gu, don't misunderstand. It's not that I don't trust you. I just want to get things straight. We're all businessmen, and it's better to lay all the cards on the table upfront than to haggle over things later, right?\"","Lu Hong let out a cold laugh. \"Haggle? Who's haggling with you? The agreement clearly states that regular members only have profit-sharing rights, no decision-making or oversight powers. Didn't you read that clearly before signing? And now you're asking!\"","Zhou Zhao replied, \"Young Master Lu, agreements are written in stone, but people are flexible. I just wanted to hear the thoughts of the founding members. Since we're going to be working together from now on, it can't be that we're not even allowed to speak, right?\"","Shen Hao, who had been listening all along, also had an unpleasant look on his face.","Zhou Zhao was his recommendation, and now this guy was stirring up trouble, making him look bad.","He couldn't hold back any longer and stood up. \"Zhou Zhao, are you here today to join the organization or to pick a fight?\"","Zhou Zhao said, \"President Shen, I'm here to join, and I come with full sincerity.\"","\"But as for this Yunshan Society of yours, I only asked a few perfectly reasonable questions, and you've already turned hostile. That makes it hard for me not to wonder if you're feeling guilty or if you're deliberately setting up a trap to fleece us new members.\"","After this exchange, the atmosphere in the room grew increasingly tense.","The probationary members looked at one another, unsure which side to take.","Still, Zhou Zhao's words had struck a chord with them.","A billion dollars was no small sum, and none of them had money that grew on trees.","While they were all eager to join the Yunshan Society, it was only right to clear up any uncertainties.","Liu Yutong hadn't said a single word throughout the whole discussion. She simply watched the expressions on everyone's faces quietly.","Zhou Zhao's true intentions had become clear to her, or so it seemed."]},{"number":781,"title":"Chapter 781: 782, Then Eat the Contract","paragraphs":["The atmosphere in the private room froze instantly, thick with the smell of gunpowder.","The mahogany long table in the middle now seemed like an insurmountable divide, splitting the two sides apart.","Zhou Zhao stood on what he believed to be the moral high ground, confidently arguing for the rights of their probationary members.","After all, every one of these thirteen probationary members had brought massive funds with them—at least ten billion in cash each. Together, their total capital exceeded fifteen billion.","Such a huge sum was undoubtedly a weighty bargaining chip.","Zhou Zhao didn’t trust the Cloud Mountain Society, nor did he believe Liu Yutong would remain indifferent to such a large amount of money.","Money—no one ever had too much of it.","So, he was certain Liu Yutong wouldn’t simply reject their demands.","Even if Liu Yutong took a strong personal stance, what about the other members of the Cloud Mountain Society?","It wasn’t as if Liu Yutong ruled the society alone. Would the other members just let her do whatever she wanted?","Once he had applied enough pressure, Chu Junlin could step in and play the good cop, securing himself a founding member position, or even the role of president.","If Chu Junlin succeeded, Zhou Zhao would be the chief contributor—not only earning his own membership but also getting a chance to spite Liu Yutong, settling the score for the embarrassment she had caused the Zhou family earlier.","Chu Junlin had been thinking the same thing.","In truth, from the very beginning, he had never intended to be some mere probationary member of the Cloud Mountain Society.","What was his status?","A man commanding thirty billion in assets, a scion of the Chu family in the imperial capital—his identity was nothing short of noble.","Even if the backgrounds of the Cloud Mountain Society’s members weren’t shabby, did they really deserve to have him as their subordinate?","If it weren’t for the society’s tens of billions in capital, he wouldn’t have even considered joining.","In Chu Junlin’s view, the Cloud Mountain Society’s rapid growth to over sixty billion in assets within a single year was merely the result of pooling their respective resources to achieve such eye-catching performance.","If he could take control of the society, leveraging the Chu family’s influence and his own business acumen, he could definitely take things even further.","So, he wanted not just a founding member position, but also the presidency itself.","Only that title was worthy of him, Chu Junlin.","The more Zhou Zhao stirred up trouble, the more leverage he gained.","This group of probationary members was his trump card for forcing a confrontation, and the more than fifteen billion in capital was his hard bargaining chip in negotiations with the Cloud Mountain Society.","He didn’t believe anyone would turn away such a massive sum.","“Miss Liu, you’re a founding member of the Cloud Mountain Society, so you must have some say around here. How about you answer our questions?” Zhou Zhao shifted his focus onto Liu Yutong.","At that, nearly everyone turned to look at the woman who had humiliated the Zhou family just days ago.","They all understood why Zhou Zhao was doing this—it was simply an attempt to reclaim some of the lost face for the Zhou family.","Chu Junlin, too, wanted to see whether this woman, who had caused such a stir at the Jiang family banquet, would yield.","Finally, Liu Yutong reacted.","Not with anger, not with accusation—just a calm expression. Yet the oppressive aura she exuded made Zhou Zhao’s heart tighten for no reason.","“Anything else?”","Zhou Zhao felt a chill under her gaze, but with Chu Junlin backing him and that fifteen billion worth of leverage, he refused to back down.","“No... nothing else.”","Liu Yutong nodded, then crooked her finger at him. “Bring me your contract.”","Zhou Zhao was briefly stunned, but a wave of joy quickly washed over him.","Sure enough—she was giving in, ready to revise the agreement.","The Eldest Miss of the Wanlong Association, the new socialite of the imperial capital—even she had to bow before his silver tongue.","He hurriedly handed the contract over to Liu Yutong.","“Miss Liu, I knew you were a reasonable person. The terms in this contract were simply unfair—”","Before he could finish, a tearing sound rang out.","Rip!","Rip!","Liu Yutong grabbed his contract without hesitation, and right in front of everyone, tore it in two right before their eyes.","Zhou Zhao’s smile froze instantly.","What—what was she doing?","Had she gone mad?!","That was a contract worth over a billion!","Chu Junlin paused his lighter and narrowed his eyes at Liu Yutong.","Looks like this woman wasn’t going to give an inch.","After several seconds of shock, Zhou Zhao finally came to his senses and pointed a finger at Liu Yutong.","“Liu Yutong! Are you insane?! Do you even know what you just tore up? That’s a contract worth a billion! Are you trying to pick a fight with all of us? Believe me, we can pull our funding right now and collapse your Cloud Mountain Society! Then let’s see how you answer to the other members!”","Liu Yutong couldn’t be bothered to waste words on him. She simply called out, “Send someone in.”","A group of men in black suits from the Wanlong Association poured into the room.","Seeing this, Zhou Zhao panicked. “You—what do you think you’re doing?! I’m just fighting for my reasonable rights! You wouldn’t resort to violence, would you? Is this how you do business?”","Liu Yutong waved her hand. “Pin him down.”","On her command, the men in black moved in, seizing Zhou Zhao and pressing him onto the mahogany table.","“Let me go! Young Master Chu, save me!” Zhou Zhao screamed desperately.","But hands were already resting on Chu Junlin’s and the others’ shoulders. Any slightest move would land them in the same predicament as Zhou Zhao.","None of them dared to move. None dared to plead for leniency.","Liu Yutong stood up, walked around the table, and came face to face with Zhou Zhao.","Bending down, she looked at him. “Zhou Zhao, don’t think I don’t know what you’re up to.”","“You know what? What I hate most is someone going back on their word—and even more, I hate being threatened.” As she said this, she deliberately glanced at Chu Junlin, who remained expressionless.","Zhou Zhao was about to beg for mercy when Liu Yutong simply said to Yun Cheng, “Since that contract is so valuable, make him eat it. Don’t waste it.”","“Yes, ma’am!”","Without hesitation, Yun Cheng grabbed the torn halves of the contract and shoved them directly into Zhou Zhao’s mouth.","“Mmph... mmph...”","Zhou Zhao struggled furiously, but to no avail.","Soon, shredded paper filled his puffed-out cheeks, making him look as though he had gained several pounds.","Watching this horrifying scene, the thirteen reserve members all fell silent.","They had only heard rumors about Liu Yutong’s ruthlessness before. Now, they were witnessing it firsthand.","Truly merciless.","Once the entire contract had been forced down Zhou Zhao’s throat, Yun Cheng and his men finally let him go.","As soon as he was freed, the man collapsed to the ground, vomiting uncontrollably—a horrific sight.","Liu Yutong pointed at Zhou Zhao, who was still coughing and retching on the floor, and addressed the remaining probationary members. “Now, apart from him, does anyone else want to withdraw? Step forward!”","The entire room fell dead silent.","Every single one of them was intimidated by Liu Yutong’s ruthless methods.","All except for one person—Chu Junlin."]},{"number":782,"title":"Chapter 782: 783. A Ten-Billion Bet, Dare You Take It","paragraphs":["Slap! Slap! Slap!","Chu Junlin leaned back in his chair and clapped slowly.","“Brilliant, truly brilliant.”","“Miss Liu lives up to her reputation—decisive and ruthless. Today, I’ve seen it all firsthand.”","“This act of yours, killing the chicken to scare the monkeys, is certainly impressive. Look how frightened they are.”","Liu Yutong turned to look at him. “Does Young Master Chu have some advice? Or would you like a taste of the contract yourself?”","Chu Junlin shook his head with a smile. “No, I’d rather not. I just wanted to speak my mind.”","“As the old saying goes, in business, harmony brings wealth. Zhou Zhao merely asked a few reasonable questions. Even if his words were a bit off, your approach today was far too overbearing. Word gets out, and soon no one will want to deal with Cloud Mountain Consortium.”","Liu Yutong said, “I don’t need an outsider to teach me how to do business. As for you, you seem to think too highly of yourselves.”","“Cloud Mountain Consortium has never begged anyone to join. Young Master Chu, if you have something to say, say it directly. Sending some pawn to test the waters only brings humiliation.”","At this, Chu Junlin’s smile slowly faded.","“Miss Liu gets straight to the point. Then let’s not beat around the bush. I’m not here for some low-tier membership.”","Gu Yebai sneered, “Chu Junlin, what do you mean? Don’t tell me you want a founding member spot?”","Chu Junlin nodded, then shook his head.","“You’ve built Cloud Mountain Consortium into a massive six hundred billion operation in just a year—that’s impressive, really. It makes people sit up and take notice.”","“But I suspect your success comes from pooling resources among the seven of you, right?”","“Don’t get me wrong—it’s a clever and effective strategy.”","He refused to believe anyone could go from zero to a terrifying six hundred billion in a single year.","If that were true, they’d be better than the stock market gods themselves.","So he guessed these Cloud Mountain Consortium players must have leveraged their insider knowledge and coordinated their moves to build such a massive business.","After all, with multiple families pooling their resources and ensuring complete information sharing, they’d have a considerable advantage.","As for why no similar consortium had risen so fast in the imperial capital, it was because others couldn’t achieve the same level of coordination—too many conflicting interests.","Otherwise, Cloud Mountain Consortium wouldn’t even exist.","Seeing that everyone in Cloud Mountain Consortium remained silent, he felt more certain of his judgment.","He pressed on, “Have you ever thought what this operation could become if someone with stronger connections led it? Reaching a trillion might be just around the corner, and then we’d be true business giants.”","Gu Yebai said, “Are you saying you want to take the credit for yourself?”","Chu Junlin raised a finger and wagged it. “No! No! It’s about mutual benefit. Everyone gains—why not?”","“Miss Liu, you’re a clever woman. You know what I’m getting at.”","“I may not have many other skills, but when it comes to resource integration and capital management, I dare say I’m second to none.”","“So why can’t I become a founding member of Cloud Mountain Consortium, or even its chairman?”","“Let me lay it out plainly. Either you seven founding members accept my terms—let me be chairman and join the core group—and from now on, I’ll bring Chu family resources and capital to grow this to a trillion or even more...”","“Or... I’ll rally the like-minded people here and start a new consortium from scratch.”","“I refuse to believe that with the Chu family’s background and the funds and connections of the imperial capital’s elite, I can’t outdo your Cloud Mountain Consortium. When that day comes, let’s see how you compete with me for projects and resources.”","“I’ll crush you so hard you won’t know what hit you.”","Chu Junlin’s words were no longer a power play—they were a barefaced threat.","A threat to Cloud Mountain Consortium: if Liu Yutong and the others didn’t agree, he’d immediately form a new consortium and target them specifically.","Chu Junlin believed he had fully grasped the secret behind Cloud Mountain Consortium’s rapid rise, so he dared to threaten them like this.","And indeed, with the Chu family’s foundation and his capital, forming a rival consortium and luring away the prospective members could pose a minor threat to them.","A minor one.","They had no idea what kind of person they would face. If things got dirty, he’d strip them clean down to their underwear.","Chu Junlin’s words did make some prospective members waver.","On one hand, there was Cloud Mountain Consortium’s founder, who had strict rules and a habit of feeding people contracts.","On the other hand, there was Chu Junlin, equally backed by deep resources and capital.","If Chu Junlin was really starting a new consortium, they might consider joining him.","Still, unless absolutely necessary, Chu Junlin preferred not to go that far and establish a new consortium.","What he really coveted was Cloud Mountain Consortium’s six hundred billion capital pool.","“Miss Liu, I’ll give you and the others three days to think it over.”","“In three days, either let me be chairman and grow Cloud Mountain Consortium even bigger... or...”","He paused before continuing, “...or I’ll form my own group. Once the new consortium is established, you’d better be prepared.”","“Especially you, Liu Yutong.”","With that, he stood up and prepared to leave.","“Wait.” Liu Yutong called out to him.","Chu Junlin stopped and turned around, a smile spreading across his face.","“What, Miss Liu, has had a change of heart so soon?”","Liu Yutong shook her head. “Young Master Chu, you’re overthinking it. I can give you the answer right now: no way.”","Chu Junlin narrowed his eyes. “So you really want to go head-to-head with me.”","He then looked at the other founding members. “And you all? Are you going to let a woman run the show? Don’t you have anything to say?”","“President Zhu, what about you?” He deliberately singled out Zhu Silin.","After all, she was the CEO of Cloud Mountain Capital.","Without hesitation, Zhu Silin said, “Young Master Chu, you don’t need to test us. Sister Yutong’s word is our word.”","“Also, I want you to know something. Sister Yutong is the chairman of Cloud Mountain Consortium and the chairwoman of Cloud Mountain Capital—she is the core of our consortium.”","“What you said earlier about Cloud Mountain Consortium succeeding only through resource integration and information sharing is wrong.”","“Without Sister Yutong, Cloud Mountain Consortium would never have achieved such glory in just one year.”","At her words, the prospective members looked shocked.","“What does she mean—that Cloud Mountain Consortium’s success is all thanks to Liu Yutong alone?”","“Is that for real?”","“If that’s true, then it’s terrifying...”","Chu Junlin sneered in response. “You think you can fool me? You expect me to believe that?”","A twenty-year-old woman, no matter how gifted, couldn't possibly create sixty billion in capital on her own.","Zhu Silin: \"Believe it or not, if any of you want to leave, you can go now.\"","Chu Junlin didn't stand on ceremony either. He turned directly to face the twelve provisional members and said, \"Who wants to come with me? I promise that anyone who joins my guild will be a founding member, entitled to a larger share of the profits and a greater say than they had in the Cloud Mountain Society.\"","The twelve provisional members hesitated for a moment, then someone quickly stood up.","One, two, three...","One after another, they rose and walked over to stand behind Chu Junlin.","In the end, of those twelve people, aside from Zhou Zhao, who had been force-fed paper earlier, seven of the remaining eleven stood up.","Only four remained seated.","Chu Junlin looked at the eight people behind him and grinned broadly.","\"Miss Liu, it seems my appeal is stronger. This proves I'm more suited to be the leader.\"","Liu Yutong glanced at the nine people, including Chu Junlin, and suddenly changed the subject. \"Young Master Chu, you just said you wanted to start from scratch and beat the Cloud Mountain Society until it couldn't find its way back, didn't you?\"","Chu Junlin raised his chin and said arrogantly, \"What, scared? It's not too late to regret it now, as long as you agree to my terms.\"","Liu Yutong smiled, a smile laced with undisguised mockery. \"Young Master Chu, since you're so confident, let's make a bet.\"","Chu Junlin was taken aback, not expecting Liu Yutong to propose a wager.","\"A bet? What kind of bet?\"","Liu Yutong: \"You said you wanted to beat us into submission, right? Then let's see who beats whom into submission!\"","With that, she had someone bring out a checkbook, scribbled a few lines, tore the check off, and slapped it on the table.","\"One hundred billion!\"","The entire room fell silent instantly.","Everyone's eyes widened as they stared at the check with its long string of zeros on the table.","One hundred billion?","What was she doing?","The expression on Chu Junlin's face gradually froze.","Seeing that he wasn't speaking, Liu Yutong pointed at the check again. \"Young Master Chu, cat got your tongue? Didn't you want to beat the Cloud Mountain Society until it couldn't find its way back? There, I'm giving you the chance.\"","\"This is a check for one hundred billion. I'm betting it in the name of the Cloud Mountain Society.\"","\"From now on, we'll set a one-year term. We'll see who ends up with the higher rate of return. The loser pays the winner one hundred billion and must also bow down and worship the winner, prostrating on the ground.\"","\"So, Young Master Chu, do you dare to accept this bet?\""]},{"number":783,"title":"Chapter 783: 784. Bet Takes Effect.","paragraphs":["The proud expression on Chu Junlin's face completely froze.","He stared fixedly at the check on the table, praying that his eyes were deceiving him.","Ten billion.","Not one billion, not ten billion—ten billion!","Chu Junlin's corporation might have a market value of thirty billion, but that was only a valuation, not all belonging to him personally. The liquid cash he could actually mobilize was at most three to four billion.","Yet this woman, Liu Yutong, casually slapped down a check for ten billion, just as a bet.","If she dared to do that, either she had so much cash flow he couldn’t imagine, enough not to care about losing ten billion, or she was bluffing, trying to scare him with this move.","Whether it was real or not, he had to admit he was shaken by it.","The seven reserve members who had just arrayed themselves behind Chu Junlin also wore extremely interesting expressions.","They had chosen to side with Chu Junlin earlier because they thought Chu family’s foundation was deeper, Chu Junlin was stronger, and he was something of a business prodigy. Following him would definitely be better than staying a reserve member in Cloud Mountain Society.","But now, for some reason, they suddenly felt a pang of regret.","They regretted committing so early. They should have waited to see how things played out.","Liu Yutong watched Chu Junlin, who hadn’t yet spoken, and asked again.","“Young Master Chu, cat got your tongue?”","“Or are you afraid to take the bet?”","Chu Junlin’s face flickered with uncertainty; he still couldn’t make up his mind. But one of the men behind him couldn’t help speaking up first.","“Young Master Chu, the stakes are too high. Maybe we should...”","“Shut up!” Chu Junlin abruptly cut the man off.","Then he stared hard at Liu Yutong, trying to read any clue from her expression.","But he stared for a full minute and couldn’t find the slightest crack.","If there was any imperfection on her face, it was that the lipstick on the corner of her mouth was applied just a little unevenly.","No, wait—why was he even paying attention to her lipstick?","Regardless, he had already made his bold claims about setting up his own rival organization to crush Cloud Mountain Society. Now she was putting up ten billion for a duel bet. If he didn’t take it, those earlier boasts would become a complete joke.","From then on, his reputation in the capital’s elite circles would essentially be ruined.","But if he took it...","Ten billion!","If he lost, he’d be bankrupt.","“Miss Liu, are you trying to force me?” Chu Junlin said through gritted teeth.","Liu Yutong sighed lightly.","“Looks like Young Master Chu is going to play the turtledove and hide his head today.”","“Fine, I won’t make things difficult for you.”","“You can choose not to bet, but I have one condition: you kneel down in front of me right now and perform an act of humble worship, and from now on, wherever I, Liu Yutong, appear, you, Chu Junlin, must give way and keep your distance.”","“If you do that, this matter is settled.”","Such a humiliating condition made Chu Junlin fly into a rage. He pointed a finger at her: “Liu Yutong, you’re going too far!”","Liu Yutong spread her hands with an innocent expression: “How am I going too far? I gave you a choice. Or do you think two choices aren’t enough? Fine, I’ll add a third option—just run out of here stark naked, and I’ll pretend I never saw you today, like nothing happened.”","The reserve members standing behind Chu Junlin exchanged glances at Liu Yutong’s words.","This woman was clearly determined to humiliate Chu Junlin today!","They had grown up in the capital and witnessed no small number of power struggles and schemes in these elite circles. But they had never seen anyone dare to humiliate Chu Junlin like this.","This was Chu Junlin!","The business spearhead of the top-tier wealthy Chu family in the capital, the helmsman of three listed companies.","When he usually went out, everyone addressed him respectfully as “Young Master Chu,” wore smiling faces, even some who would be eager to kneel and lick his shoes.","But now Chu Junlin was being publicly humiliated by a girl nearly ten years younger than him.","Someone had already noticed Chu Junlin’s face. The always arrogant young master of the Chu household looked not just grim—it was twisted.","To be honest, some of them already regretted siding with Chu Junlin.","If this guy actually agreed to this century’s biggest bet, they’d definitely get dragged in too.","If Chu Junlin lost, would they also go bankrupt?","If Chu Junlin won...","But judging by this woman’s attitude, could Chu Junlin even win?","They seriously doubted it.","At that moment, one of the four remaining reserve members—a young woman—was staring at Liu Yutong with something close to worship.","Since childhood, she had been taught by her family that girls should be gentle, sensible, not too sharp, and should use subtle, soft tactics.","But she had never liked that philosophy.","Why should girls have to show weakness?","Why should girls rely on soft tactics?","She wanted to be like Liu Yutong—insult people when she felt like it, fight when she wanted, humiliate whoever she pleased, and after humiliating them, the other party wouldn’t even dare to talk back.","So satisfying!","So cool!","That was the kind of woman she wanted to become.","She made up her mind—she was going to follow Liu Yutong from now on!","Even if her family objected, she would!","Liu Yutong glanced at her watch and asked again: “Young Master Chu, have you decided? My patience has its limits.”","Chu Junlin looked left and right, then finally made his decision. With a clenched jaw, he said, “Fine! I’ll take the bet!”","He couldn’t back down, and he couldn’t show a white feather. If he really cowered, she probably would make him crawl on the ground and bark like a dog, or run naked.","That would finish him completely.","Hearing this, Liu Yutong’s face broke into a brilliant smile: “Young Master Chu, you’re truly decisive!”","Then she turned to Zhu Silin and said, “Silin, draft a betting agreement, two copies. Young Master Chu, let’s sign the contract first, so no one reneges later.”","Chu Junlin nodded. Even if his heart was full of reluctance, there was no turning back now.","Soon, Zhu Silin had someone bring out the drafted document and placed it in front of him.","It was a standard betting agreement.","The terms were simple: within one year, both parties would assign ten billion in funds to be managed by their respective teams, and after a year, they would compare the rate of return. The loser would pay the winner ten billion in cash and also kneel publicly in front of the winner in a gesture of homage.","After reading the contract, Chu Junlin’s hands trembled slightly.","Ten billion!","Even though he had rallied seven people, eight counting himself, it still wasn’t easy to scrape together ten billion in cash.","But the words were already spoken. He was caught between a rock and a hard place—no choice but to sign.","Finally, biting the bullet, he picked up the pen and signed his name on the agreement.","Liu Yutong also signed. Then she picked up her copy, blew on the ink to dry it, and nodded with satisfaction.","“Young Master Chu, then we’re settled. We’ll see the outcome when the time comes.”","She paused and offered him a kindly reminder.","“By the way, Young Master Chu, you better manage your trading well. Don’t disappoint me, and don’t lose all that ten billion before the year is even up.”","Chu Junlin’s face turned ashen. With a cold snort, he turned and walked away.","The seven preparatory members who had sided with him could only steel themselves and follow him out.","As for that Zhou Zhao from the Zhou family, he was directly dragged out by two men in black, tossed aside like a piece of trash."]},{"number":784,"title":"Chapter 784: 785, Three Months, Gone with the Wind.","paragraphs":["As Chu Junlin and his group left in disgrace, the private room finally calmed down.","Liu Yutong turned to look at the four provisional members who had chosen to stand with the Cloud Mountain Society.","These four young people straightened up nervously as Miss Liu’s gaze swept over them.","After all, this woman seemed a bit too formidable—they couldn’t help but feel intimidated.","Liu Yutong reined in her imposing aura, a warm smile spreading across her face.","“The four of you were introduced so hastily earlier that I didn’t really remember much. How about we get to know each other again?”","The four quickly stood up and began introducing themselves one by one.","The first to step forward was a young man in his mid-twenties, slim and scholarly.","“Miss Liu, my name is Shen Cheng. I’m from the Shen family. My father works in XX. I’m a branch member, not of the main line, but I’ve always wanted to make something of myself.”","Liu Yutong nodded. “The Shen family, huh? Then Lin Yi is your cousin?”","Shen Cheng quickly nodded. “Yes, yes, Lin Yi is my cousin. She’s mentioned you, Miss Liu, saying you’re a rare extraordinary woman. She told me that if I ever had the chance to meet you, I should learn as much as I can from you.”","Liu Yutong smiled. “Sister Yi is too kind. But the fact that you stayed shows you have good judgment.”","Shen Cheng smiled shyly and scratched his head, a little embarrassed.","The second to step forward was a girl in her early twenties, with long hair flowing over her shoulders, a sweet face, and bright, clever eyes.","“Miss Liu, my name is Shangguan Ling’er. I’m from the Shangguan family. My father works in the XX department. I really love finance, but my family has never really supported it—they say girls are better off in steady government jobs. But I want to try. I don’t want to be a vase my whole life.”","Liu Yutong studied her for a moment.","This girl looked sweet on the surface, but there was a stubborn, determined streak in her bones—she liked that.","“Alright, now that you’ve joined Cloud Mountain Society, it’ll show your family that women can earn respect too.”","Shangguan Ling’er nodded firmly. “Mm! I’ll work hard!”","The third to step forward was a man around thirty, with a square face, thick eyebrows, and big eyes, standing tall and straight like a pine tree—clearly from a military family.","“Miss Liu, my name is Wei Xiao. I’m from the Wei family. My father works in XX. I run my own security company—it’s not big, just a few dozen people. I don’t know much about investing, but I trust your judgment, Miss Liu. I’m willing to follow you.”","As Liu Yutong looked at this young man named Wei Xiao, she suddenly thought of Chu Yang.","Both had military backgrounds, both were the practical, hardworking type.","“Wei Xiao, what exactly does your security company do?”","Wei Xiao answered honestly. “Mainly provides security services for businesses and individuals. We also take on some overseas projects. It’s not large in scale, but we have a good reputation.”","Liu Yutong’s interest peaked. This guy was impressive—he’d even managed to take his business abroad.","Most legitimate security companies in China focused on things like bank cash transport or corporate security—they rarely ever ventured overseas.","Companies doing international work usually registered abroad. Doing it from here was no small feat.","Liu Yutong said, “I actually have a security company under me too. We can exchange ideas sometime.”","Wei Xiao’s eyes lit up immediately. “I’d be thrilled.”","The fourth to step forward was a young man who looked barely over twenty, fair-skinned and clear-eyed, like a fresh graduate.","“Miss... Miss Liu, my name is Xu Ke. I’m from the Xu family. My family sent me out to gain experience. I... I’m not really sure what to do, but I knew that the ones who left were wrong—you were right—so I stayed.”","He spoke with a slight stutter but was very sincere.","Liu Yutong smiled. “Good. Work hard at Cloud Mountain Society in the future.”","After the introductions, Liu Yutong gestured to them. “Sit down, don’t just stand there. Once the contracts are signed, we can chat together.”","The four sat down cautiously.","Zhu Silin had new tea and snacks brought in.","With Chu Junlin’s annoying group gone, the atmosphere in the room had indeed become more relaxed.","As the conversation deepened, the four of them grew less tense.","After all, they’d officially signed on and become part of Cloud Mountain Society.","Now that they were part of the team, their mindset naturally shifted.","The clever-looking Shangguan Ling’er even sidled up beside Liu Yutong and asked a question she was dying to know.","“Sister Yutong, do we really think we can win the bet against Chu Junlin?”","As soon as she asked, the other three perked up their ears.","They all wanted to hear what Liu Yutong would say—whether she had simply bluffed and used the hundred billion figure to scare Chu Junlin, or if she really had absolute confidence in herself.","Before Liu Yutong could speak, the other founding members of Cloud Mountain Society couldn’t help laughing.","“Ling’er, your question... is a bit too underestimating our Sister Yutong.”","“Exactly. Do you know how much profit Sister Yutong has led us to make in the year since Cloud Mountain Society was founded?”","Shangguan Ling’er honestly shook her head.","Though rumors had spread about Cloud Mountain Society’s incredibly high returns, no one knew exactly how much initial capital had turned into that massive six-hundred-billion portfolio.","“A year ago, Sister Yutong and the rest of us pooled together about five billion in initial capital.”","“And now you’re wondering if we can beat that Chu Junlin?”","“Let me tell you—from the moment Sister Yutong took out that check, Chu Junlin had already lost.”","At that, Shangguan Ling’er and the others’ eyes went wide.","“How much?!”","“Five billion?!”","Five billion in initial capital, turned into six hundred billion in one year.","What kind of terrifying rate of return was that?","This wasn’t just making money anymore—this was printing it on a money press.","And a money press that could burn out from overuse.","No wonder Zhu Silin had said earlier that the core of Cloud Mountain Society was only one person—Liu Yutong.","If someone could turn five billion into six hundred billion in a year, who else would you put at the center?","What they didn’t know was that the six hundred billion only referred to the funds controlled by Cloud Mountain Capital, not the money Liu Yutong personally managed.","The subsidiaries under Liu Yutong, like Wanlong Capital and her offshore funds, were larger than that six hundred billion.","To say nothing of the more than six billion US dollars in overseas assets she had initially set aside, which after this year had grown to over ten billion US dollars.","And that number would only grow wildly in the future.","Because this year, she had already started sweeping up Bitcoin.","At this time, Bitcoin was almost worthless—not just worthless, but so obscure that no one would even take it for free.","As far as she could recall from her past life, it wasn’t until next year that a programmer overseas would first use Bitcoin to buy something, marking the cryptocurrency’s tradability milestone.","That programmer used ten thousand Bitcoin to buy two pizzas.","She wondered if that programmer ever regretted it later, since those two pizzas would one day be worth hundreds of millions of dollars.","It took Shangguan Ling'er and the others quite a while to calm the shock in their hearts.","At this moment, they felt incredibly fortunate to have chosen to stay behind instead of leaving with Chu Junlin.","They could well imagine that if Chu Junlin and his group learned that Yun Shan had made a six-hundred-billion-dollar plate with only five billion in capital, they'd probably have the urge to jump off a building.","Right now, Shangguan Ling'er was filled with confidence about the future. Following someone so brilliant in finance, how could they possibly lose?","\"Then... Sister Yutong, how long do you think it will take us to take them down?\"","Liu Yutong didn't beat around the bush either. \"The four of you chose to stay, which shows you're not the kind of fair-weather friends who shift with the wind. Since you're now part of the inner circle, I won't play games with you.\"","Then she held up three fingers and said a number that was both exhilarating and stunning:","\"Three months.\"","\"Three months will be enough to wipe out Chu Junlin's so-called business alliance into thin air.\"","................."]},{"number":785,"title":"Chapter 785: 786. Reflections on the Future.","paragraphs":["Three months?","Had they heard that correctly?","Chu Junlin alone could mobilize at least ten billion yuan in capital, and he was widely recognized as a business prodigy, leading a very strong team. Yet Liu Yutong claimed she could crush him within three months—wasn’t that a bit arrogant?","But when they looked at Liu Yutong’s cold, stunningly beautiful face, they swallowed their doubts.","She didn’t seem like the type to make jokes on a whim.","The three-month timeframe Liu Yutong mentioned wasn’t just a random number pulled out of thin air.","In fact, even three months felt too long to her.","That’s because she never intended to compete with Chu Junlin on rate of return.","If she really wanted to, she could easily beat him in that area too. As a reincarnator, she could just pick a few well-known stocks and outperform him effortlessly.","But she preferred a more “brutal” approach.","For instance—short selling.","Chu Junlin controlled three publicly traded companies: Star Shine Media, Origin Real Estate, and Color Glow Paper.","In Liu Yutong’s view, these industries were quite easy to short.","Take Color Glow Paper, for example. In 2009, environmental issues were already becoming a hot topic in society.","She could target the company’s environmental compliance problems. If they had even a single blemish, she could blow it out of proportion.","Then there was Star Shine Media.","This entertainment company was listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange and had signed many artists. Over the past few years, it had raked in substantial profits from talent shows and idol dramas.","But the entertainment world was full of secrets that couldn’t see the light of day. With some time, digging up scandals wouldn’t be hard.","The key point was that all of Chu Junlin’s listed companies were on the Hong Kong stock exchange, not mainland China, where there weren’t as many protective measures and short selling was legal.","Liu Yutong planned to use offshore account funds to short the stocks of these three companies at the right time.","The overseas assets she currently controlled amounted to over ten billion US dollars. Using just a portion of that to short three companies with a combined market cap of just over thirty billion Hong Kong dollars was like using a meat cleaver to kill a chicken.","Of course, she wasn’t going to completely destroy these companies—there was no need for that. She just needed to force Chu Junlin to step in and defend the stock prices.","If he dared to do so, he’d fall right into her trap.","Chu Junlin’s net worth was roughly ten billion yuan, but most of it was tied up in equity valuations. The actual liquid cash he could deploy was likely only a few billion.","Compared to Liu Yutong’s short-selling capital, that was nothing.","The only way for him to defend the stock prices was to use the newly raised ten billion yuan fund from his recently established business association.","But that money didn’t belong to him alone.","If he invested it in defending the stocks and still failed, what would happen then?","No doubt those eight other partners wouldn’t let it slide.","Of course, Liu Yutong knew her approach was a bit unscrupulous.","They had agreed to a competition on rate of return, and instead, she was directly targeting his listed companies—that was pretty underhanded.","But she didn’t care.","In business competition, the strong always make the rules.","She had money, people, resources, and twenty years of future knowledge. Why should she play fair?","She could fight however she wanted.","So her claim of three months wasn’t an exaggeration at all.","In that time, she could strip Chu Junlin down to nothing.","Then they moved on from the bet.","The group started discussing the prospects of the Cloud Mountain Society.","Alongside Liu Yutong and the other six founding members, four new members with deep backgrounds had joined, bringing the total past double digits.","That was a very good sign.","Even if the Cloud Mountain Society never expanded, it wouldn’t hurt their ability to make money—but making money was never the ultimate goal.","As the saying goes, “Eating alone won’t make you fat; sharing food lasts a long time.”","After Zhu Silin gave the four new members a detailed introduction to the deeper operations and profit-sharing rules of the Cloud Mountain Society, she raised a concern that had been weighing on her.","“Our Cloud Mountain Society is growing fast, and the capital we manage is expanding. But I’ve been thinking about something lately.”","“Right now, our model is basically a powerful capital alliance formed by pooling our resources. With our combined capital, doing financial investments in China is no problem—we could even bulldoze our way through. But what about expanding overseas in the long term? How will that play out?”","“Or more extreme, what if one day foreign powers decide to sanction us, freeze our funds, and seize our assets—do we have any cards to play in response?”","The Cloud Mountain Society’s investments were split between domestic and overseas, with the majority in China and a smaller portion abroad.","Why this split? First, because China was in a period of rapid growth with plenty of investment opportunities.","Second, there was the concern that funds overseas might run into trouble given the many unscrupulous players out there, so they placed more emphasis on domestic allocation.","Besides, the capital itself had been secretly accumulated through short selling abroad the previous year, and some parties had wanted to tear the behind-the-scenes operator apart back then.","So they had to be very careful when using funds overseas.","But focusing solely on the domestic market wasn’t a long-term solution either.","The vast overseas market—not going there to grab money like the Wall Street wolves would be a huge waste.","Yet if they grabbed too much, those wolves might get desperate and flip the table.","Zhu Silin raising this issue came not only from her deep understanding of international finance but also from a deeper reason—her father.","Uncle Zhu had more insight and sharper instincts.","For instance, he believed China would eventually face sanctions from foreign powers, and during such superpower clashes, the first to suffer would be rising capital like theirs.","So they needed to prepare for the worst.","After Zhu Silin posed the question, the private room fell silent. Everyone began pondering the problem.","Indeed, domestically, with their combined power, they didn’t have to worry about anyone daring to mess with them—they could act boldly.","But overseas was different.","That was someone else’s turf, and the rules were set by others.","Still, giving up the overseas market entirely didn’t seem realistic either.","Who didn’t want more money?","Who wouldn’t want to earn more foreign currency to help build their country?","Liu Yutong studied Zhu Silin carefully.","This CEO of Cloud Mountain Capital was very perceptive, spotting the danger so early.","According to her past life’s timeline, about five years from now, China would enter an all-out tug-of-war with foreign powers.","Especially after that [reliable] figure took office, sanction after sanction would rain down.","She had even mentally prepared herself to avoid traveling abroad after that point.","Given what she had done—shorting U.S. stocks, “acquiring” a lithography machine company, poaching top talent—if she went abroad, she’d almost certainly be monitored or even arrested.","But hiding away like that really irritated her.","Why should she have to lie low and let others have their way?","She would make sure she could go out whenever she wanted and come home whenever she felt like it, while making those thugs stare at her in frustration, unable to do a thing about her."]},{"number":786,"title":"Chapter 786: 787, Mystic Phoenix Society.","paragraphs":["\"Silin, please continue.\"","Zhu Silin nodded. \"Let me give you an example, Sister Yutong. Your company, Longxin, is working on chips. Once this project succeeds, it will even impact foreign chip giants. I can almost guarantee they'll unite to impose technology blockades, market blockades, or even use underhanded tactics to suppress Longxin.\"","\"Also, if we invest in real industries in the future, like ports or energy, what if they are forcibly taken back or even frozen by shady players?\"","\"And if that time comes, what can we, the Cloud Mountain Society, do?\"","\"Everyone, can you think of an answer?\"","After Zhu Silin finished speaking, the room fell into silence again—this time heavier and more suffocating than before.","To be honest, many of them had never thought about this layer, or simply dared not think about it. But now that they were pondering it carefully, it was truly chilling to consider.","In the past, they wouldn't have needed to think so far ahead. It was good enough to dominate the domestic market, let alone consider overseas markets. But then again, they had an incredibly strong leader at the helm.","No one doubted that if Liu Yutong let loose, she could achieve great things abroad. The founding members, in particular, believed this without a doubt. That was also the main reason Zhu Silin had considered this issue so early.","Liu Yutong was silent for a moment before speaking. \"Silin, I've actually thought about the problems you've raised too.\"","\"If the Cloud Mountain Society wants to expand overseas, no matter what we do, we'll step on other people's toes. It's indeed possible that we might face encirclement or sanctions. At that point, relying solely on the Cloud Mountain Society's strength simply wouldn't be enough.\"","Zhu Silin asked, \"Sister Yutong, do you already have an idea?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"I've been thinking about one thing lately.\"","Glancing at everyone in the room, she continued, \"I think we should establish a brand-new organization.\"","As soon as she said this, everyone in the room froze.","A brand-new organization?","What did that mean?","Were they disbanding the Cloud Mountain Society?","Liu Yutong explained, \"This organization is different from the Cloud Mountain Society. The Cloud Mountain Society is positioned as an investment platform—a way for us to pool resources and make money together. But this new organization's goal isn't to generate profit.\"","\"Then what is it?\" Shangguan Ling'er couldn't help asking.","Liu Yutong dipped her finger in tea from her cup and drew the shape of a net on the redwood table.","\"It's about building a net.\"","\"A super-relationship network that can cover the entire globe.\"","\"Simply put, this new organization doesn't distinguish by nationality, skin color, or industry. As long as someone holds enough capital, resources, or technology, or wields enough influence in global politics, business, tech, or finance—and they share our philosophy, willing to pursue mutual benefit and shared progress—they can join.\"","\"This organization isn't an ordinary chamber of commerce. It's a special alliance, an ultra-powerful community of interests...\"","\"Of course, this is just a rough idea of mine. I'm not sure if it's feasible, but I want to give it a try.\"","Although Liu Yutong's description was a bit vague, the others roughly understood that she wanted to create a global top-tier federation, similar to the legendary Illuminati. However, this organization would be purer than those secret societies—its ultimate goal was simply to band together and avoid being bullied by shady players.","But saying it was easy; doing it was extremely difficult.","\"Let me put it more bluntly: if one day someone tries to impose sanctions or blockades on us, we can mobilize everyone in this net, making them realize that locking us down or sanctioning us comes at a heavy price.\"","\"For example... bankrupt their companies, crash their stock markets!\"","Everyone's spirits were jolted by Liu Yutong's last sentence.","Gu Yebai stood up abruptly. \"Sister Yutong, count me in for this organization! I'll do it even if it means walking through fire and water!\"","Lu Hong also stood up. \"How could I miss out on something this good?\"","Zhu Silin, Shen Hao, Bai Shisui, Zhou Muchen, and others all expressed their agreement one after another.","The four new candidate members were also infected by this fervent atmosphere, a burst of excitement coursing through them.","Friends, who could understand? They had originally just wanted to invest with a big shot and make some money, and now they had the chance to become founding members of an organization that might become great in the future.","Without much hesitation, they joined in expressing their support, declaring their intent to join this new organization no matter what.","After all, they were all young people, at the peak of their ambition and passion. After hearing the massive vision Liu Yutong had painted, they were as hyped as if they'd been injected with adrenaline, eagerly buying into it.","Whether it could succeed or not, they didn't want to miss the chance.","\"Sister Yutong, what will we call this new organization?\" Shangguan Ling'er asked impatiently.","Liu Yutong shook her head. \"I haven't thought of a name yet. Any ideas?\"","The group immediately broke into a lively discussion.","\"How about the Dragon Abyss Society? 'Abyss' as in 'deep and unfathomable.'\"","\"That's too cheesy, sounds like something from a novel.\"","\"What about the Star Ocean Society? Our journey is the stars and seas!\"","\"Too cliché.\"","\"Maybe the Kunlun Society? Kunlun is the ancestor of all mountains, symbolizing supremacy.\"","\"Too flashy, it'll attract trouble.\"","Just then, Gu Yebai suddenly remembered something. \"Sister Yutong, wasn't your nickname abroad the Black Phoenix? How about incorporating the character 'Phoenix' into the name?\"","Liu Yutong: \"...\"","\"How did you find out about the Black Phoenix nickname?\"","Gu Yebai chuckled. \"Suisui told us. Who knew that in just one trip abroad, you got such a cool alias? I wish I'd gone with you—I might have snagged a badass nickname too.\"","Black Phoenix.","That was the alias the foreign gangs had given her, meaning a black phoenix—beautiful and deadly.","It was quite fitting.","Just then, Bai Shisui suddenly voiced the name she had thought of. \"What do you think of [Xuan Phoenix Society]?\"","\"Xuan Phoenix Society?\"","Everyone paused, savoring the name. Beyond its literal meaning, it seemed to carry a homophonic layer.","\"Xuan Phoenix Society...\"","Zhu Silin repeated it, his eyes growing brighter. \"That name is great. It sounds sophisticated without being too flashy.\"","The others nodded in agreement.","\"Xuan Phoenix Society—I like it too. It has a cool ring to it.\"","\"Since the core of our organization is Sister Yutong, and her nickname is Black Phoenix, this name fits perfectly.\"","\"Sister Yutong, let's go with Xuan Phoenix Society. That name is nice.\"","\"...\"","Seeing that everyone had embraced the name, Liu Yutong made the final decision.","\"Alright, then let it be Xuan Phoenix Society.\"","\"The positioning of the Black Phoenix Society is different from that of the Cloud Mountain Society. The Cloud Mountain Society is an overt investment platform, responsible for making money, executing projects, and building industries... The Black Phoenix Society operates in the shadows, responsible for constructing a global network of connections, integrating resources, and dealing with crises. Each side has its own duties, and they coordinate with each other.\"","\"Recruitment isn't limited to China, nor to the business world. As long as someone is influential enough—no matter what country they're from or what industry they're in—as long as they meet our standards, they can become a member of the Black Phoenix Society.\"","\"In short, we're going to turn the Black Phoenix Society into an organization powerful enough to shake the global order! An organization that will make those so-called old-money families and shadowy tycoons tremble!\"","Liu Yutong's speech stirred everyone present, sending chills down their spines and firing up their blood.","They had only thought of Liu Yutong as an investment genius and a ruthless woman before.","But now, they truly realized that this girl, who seemed to be barely twenty, possessed ambitions and a vision far, far greater than they had ever imagined.","\"Sister Yutong.\"","Gu Yebai stood up, his expression fervent, and said, \"I, Gu Yebai, will follow you for the rest of my life.\"","The others chimed in one after another.","\"Me too!\"","\"Me too!\"","\"... ...\"","Liu Yutong looked at these people who had chosen to follow her, and a wave of warmth surged in her heart.","I am not alone on this path!","\"Alright, don't publicize the Black Phoenix Society. Stay extremely low-key, as low as possible. And from now on, when we accept new members, we must be very cautious. Only the strictest vetting process will do.\"","Everyone responded in unison: \"Understood!\""]},{"number":787,"title":"Chapter 787: 788, New Project, Aerospace Technology","paragraphs":["After secretly establishing the Xuanfeng Society, Liu Yutong stayed in the imperial capital for another half month, tying up most of the loose ends.","First, she attended the ribbon-cutting ceremony for Rice Technology.","Seeing the modest office of just over 200 square meters, Liu Yutong couldn’t help but feel a mix of emotions. This was Lei Yun—despite being very wealthy, he chose to avoid wasting a single cent unnecessarily.","That was the mark of a real doer, someone truly responsible to investors—unlike some startup founders who, the moment they secure funding, indulge in reckless spending, eager to make everything as lavish as possible.","Lei Yun, of course, knew the current office was a bit shabby, but he confidently declared that one day, Rice Technology would have its own standalone office building, even a tech park.","The ribbon-cutting ceremony was simple—some might even say humble.","No flowers, no red carpet, no media reporters—just a few red banners hung in the office. They cut the ribbon at the entrance, and that was it.","For lunch, everyone had a steaming bowl of rice porridge.","After wrapping things up at Rice Technology, Liu Yutong visited the future-famous e-commerce company EastEast a few days later.","EastEast’s new round of funding had already been finalized.","It seemed to be the first e-commerce company to secure funding against the trend since the financial crisis.","In her previous life, EastEast’s funding round was led by JR Capital.","But this time, due to the butterfly effect from Liu Yutong’s series of moves in the imperial capital, the investment manager at JR Capital wavered at a critical moment, feeling that EastEast’s logistics model was too heavy and unlikely to show profits in the short term.","In the end, it was Chu Hai of AEG Capital who brokered the deal.","The founder of AEG Capital had a bit of a private agenda. With JR Capital backing out, he was also uncertain about whether to invest in EastEast—his risk control department was giving him a hard time.","Then it occurred to him that Liu Yutong was still in the capital, so he decided to test the waters.","Sure, the woman had a bit of a ruthless streak, but he had to admit her business instincts were razor-sharp. She seemed to succeed at everything she touched.","If she thought it was worth doing, that would be the reassurance he needed.","Over the phone, Chu Hai briefly explained EastEast’s situation to Liu Yutong.","Her reply was a single word.","“Invest.”","Hearing that, Chu Hai didn’t hesitate. He agreed on the spot.","Soon after, they met with Liu Dong, the founder of EastEast.","Liu Yutong had heard his name countless times in her previous life, but this was her first time meeting him in person.","“Miss Liu, EastEast’s model is different from those C-category e-commerce companies. The investment in logistics is enormous, and it’ll take time to see returns. I want to be upfront about that,” Liu Dong said.","He was essentially saying, “Let’s get the hard stuff out of the way first—if you’re looking for quick gains on a short-term financial report, don’t invest. I don’t want any bad blood later.”","To his credit, he was straightforward about it. He never tried to hide things from his investors.","As a reincarnator, Liu Yutong naturally knew EastEast’s future.","This man, called Brother Dong, would turn EastEast into one of the largest e-commerce platforms in China over the next decade or so, building a nationwide logistics network.","“President Liu, I trust your judgment. Building your own logistics is a solid move—I believe the core of future e-commerce lies in logistics,” she said.","Eventually, they finalized the funding: AEG Capital led with 500 million yuan, while Yunshan Capital, Mingzhu Capital, and Wanlong Capital followed with another 500 million, totaling one billion yuan.","That amount far exceeded Liu Dong’s expectations. He had originally planned to shop around and talk to more firms, but everything was settled fast.","With the EastEast deal done, Chu Hai found an opportunity to invite Liu Yutong out for tea privately.","They met at the Yunlu Club, with Qin Yunlu personally hosting, her demeanor notably deferential.","“Director Liu, I spent a fortune to get my hands on this Da Hong Pao tea. Please, have a taste,” Qin Yunlu said.","“Boss Qin, you’re too kind,” Liu Yutong replied.","“It’s the least I can do. I’ve been wanting a chance to apologize—I never expected Manager Han to be that kind of person. Thank goodness you exposed him, or my club might have gone under,” Qin Yunlu said.","Liu Yutong waved it off. “Let’s not dwell on the past.”","“Then I’ll leave you two to your tea—I won’t interrupt,” Qin Yunlu said, excusing herself.","After she left, Chu Hai rubbed his hands together nervously before speaking.","“Uh... Director Liu, there’s something I’d like to ask you.”","“President Chu, go ahead. No need to beat around the bush,” Liu Yutong said.","Chu Hai chuckled awkwardly. “I wanted to ask—when do you plan to push Wanhui Preferred and Weibo toward an IPO?”","He was getting anxious.","Both Wanhui Preferred and Weibo met the criteria for an IPO.","But this woman kept changing her tune. First, she said they could start the process, then she said to hold off.","He was confused. Should they move forward or not?","That’s why he was pressing.","An IPO meant cashing out—converting paper wealth into real money.","“President Chu, are you feeling impatient?” Liu Yutong asked.","Chu Hai quickly waved his hands. “No, no, just curious.”","“Really not impatient?”","“Really not.”","Liu Yutong nodded. “Then wait a bit longer.”","Chu Hai was speechless. That was the same vague answer he always got.","Unable to help himself, he added, “Director Liu, how about giving me a straight answer? How much longer?”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment, then held up one hand with all five fingers spread.","“Five months?”","“Five years?”","Liu Yutong shook her head. “I’ll tell you next time.”","Chu Hai nearly spat out his tea.","Next time?","Was she messing with him?","Frustrated though he was—even annoyed—he didn’t dare voice a single complaint. After all, this was Liu Yutong.","Forget about pushing her; even if she asked him to invest more, he wouldn’t dare refuse, afraid that offending this formidable woman might bring disaster.","He’d heard the recent rumors.","At the Jiang family’s birthday banquet, Liu Yutong had stormed into the Jiang compound with over a hundred men in black, humiliated the Zhou family, and ground the patriotic businessman Jiang Yuan into the dirt.","Something like that? Even with a hundred times the guts, he wouldn’t dare try it.","But she did.","“I’ll wait for your word, Director Liu. Whenever you say it’s time to push for the IPO, I’ll start,” he said.","Seeing his weepy expression, Liu Yutong couldn’t help but laugh.","“President Chu, rest assured—when it’s time to go public, we’ll go public. This just isn’t the best moment yet.”","Chu Hai nodded bitterly.","He believed her. He did.","He was just a little antsy.","After finishing the tea, Chu Hai was about to find an excuse to leave when Liu Yutong called him back.","“By the way, President Chu, I’m planning to start a new company soon. Interested in getting in on it again?”","Chu Hai was speechless.","Here it comes. Again.","He suddenly regretted inviting her for tea. Was he about to be bled dry again?","\"Director Liu, go ahead and tell me.\"","Liu Yutong took a document from her bag and slid it across to him.","\"I just registered an aerospace company.\"","Chu Hai froze, thinking he must have misheard.","\"Aerospace? You mean the kind that builds rockets?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Yes, building rockets, making satellites, exploring space.\"","Chu Hai's mind buzzed, and for a moment, he was completely stunned.","He looked down at the file. On the cover, bold letters read: \"Wanlong Aerospace Technology Business Plan.\"","Opening the first page, there was only one sentence.","\"Let human footsteps tread across the moon and Mars, let the sea of stars no longer be distant.\"","When Chu Hai read that line, the corner of his mouth twitched. Though it was brimming with teenage cringe, he couldn't bring himself to laugh.","He flipped through the rest of the pages, and the more he read, the more alarmed he became.","The company's business plans included: commercial rocket launches, satellite manufacturing, space tourism, asteroid mining, a Starlink-like project... and so on.","A Starlink-like project?","Covering the sky with satellites so that every corner of the globe could access the internet?","How many billions would that cost?","Chu Hai lifted his head and stared at Liu Yutong with a very complex expression.","\"Director Liu, are you serious?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Have you ever seen me joke?\""]},{"number":788,"title":"Chapter 788: 789. Sharing Blessings (Thanks to 'Yun Qin' for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong then began to introduce him to the blueprint of Wanlong Aerospace Technology Company.","“President Chu, as the first investor, I think it’s necessary for me to brief you on our plan.”","Upon hearing this, Chu Hai couldn’t help but grumble internally: “When did I ever agree to invest?”","But he only dared to complain to himself, not out loud.","“First, Wanlong Aerospace’s primary step is to develop private carrier rockets, breaking foreign technological monopolies to achieve low-cost, high-frequency satellite launches.”","“Second, we’ll deploy a satellite internet plan. Our goal is to launch thousands of low-orbit satellites within twenty years, building a global satellite internet network. In the future, no matter where you are on Earth, you’ll have high-speed internet access, completely replacing traditional ground base stations.”","“Third, we’ll venture into deep-space exploration, focusing on lunar mineral resource development and Mars rover R&D. We’ll pursue private space exploration, and eventually achieve manned space tourism...”","After listening to Liu Yutong’s “outrageous ramblings,” Chu Hai fell silent for a long time.","He suddenly recalled that when Liu Yutong had previously talked about making chips, he’d worn the exact same expression.","Back then, he thought a girl of eighteen or nineteen wanting to develop chips was pure nonsense.","But now?","The 90-nanometer production line for Longxin chips was running steadily, with a yield rate exceeding 90%, and small-scale mass production had already begun.","So when Liu Yutong proposed aerospace, Chu Hai’s first reaction wasn’t “impossible,” but rather “this woman has gone crazy,” “she’s talking nonsense,” and “she wants to drain my pockets.”","But what if she actually pulled it off?","That wouldn’t be a market of hundreds or thousands of billions—it would be a super blue ocean starting in the trillions.","Space mining, space tourism, global satellite internet... The more he thought about it, the more ridiculously dreamy it seemed.","Still, he probably wouldn’t live to see it in his lifetime.","Calm down! Calm down!","You’ve already invested in three of her projects!","Chu Hai frantically reminded himself.","Longxin, Wanhui Select, Weibo—three projects that were still just taking his money without paying back a single cent.","This damn aerospace venture? He might never see a return in his lifetime. Forget it.","“Um... Director Liu! Your project is indeed very promising, very imaginative, and has a great deal of... of vision. But AEG Capital is currently a bit tight on funds, so you see...”","“One word: are you investing or not?” Liu Yutong cut straight through his polite excuses.","Chu Hai jolted. “Yes! Yes! I’m very willing to invest! Director Liu, to be honest, my childhood dream was to become an astronaut and explore the stars. Thank you for giving me this opportunity to fulfill that dream.”","Liu Yutong immediately assured him, “President Chu, I promise, your childhood dream will come true.”","As she spoke, she noticed his eyes had suddenly grown bright and watery. “Hey, why are you crying?”","Chu Hai quickly wiped his face. “Emotion, it’s emotion! Tears of joy!”","Joy my ass!","He wanted to slap himself. He shouldn’t have invited her for tea today. He’d really screwed himself this time.","The three previous projects he’d invested in, though far from going public, were at least things he could wait for.","But this so-called aerospace tech company? He probably wouldn’t see a return in his whole life.","Chu Hai was smiling when he walked out of Yunlu Club, but the moment he got into his car, the smile vanished.","Seeing his grim expression, his driver Old Zhang couldn’t help but worry: “Boss, you look like you’ve been crying. Are you okay?”","Chu Hai waved a hand. “It’s nothing. I’m just happy because I might have a chance to meet my grandma someday.”","Old Zhang: “???”","Hadn’t his grandma already passed away?","How would he meet her? By going up to heaven?","He didn’t dare ask further and quickly handed his boss a bottle of water.","Chu Hai took it and chugged a big gulp.","Fifty billion!","A full fifty billion!","He’d thrown over ten billion into Longxin, over ten billion into Wanhui Select, several billion into Weibo, and now another aerospace company—another fifty billion.","Add it all up, and the money AEG Capital had poured into Liu Yutong’s projects had surpassed a hundred billion.","And he hadn’t seen a single cent in return.","Was this woman trying to drain him dry or what?","The more Chu Hai thought about it, the more it hurt. He clutched his chest, feeling his heart bleed.","“Boss, are you sure you’re okay?”","“Old Zhang.”","“Yes?”","“Do you think, at our age, we’ll ever see humans land on Mars?”","Old Zhang was taken aback, unsure why his boss would ask such a question, but he thought carefully: “That’s... a stretch, isn’t it? How many years would that take?”","Chu Hai nodded with a somber tone. “I think so too.”","He paused, then added, “But my money has already flown to Mars.”","Old Zhang: “???”","He had no idea what his boss was talking about, but it didn’t sound good.","Chu Hai pulled out his phone and made a call.","When it connected, he adjusted his emotions and made his voice sound cheerful and excited.","“Old Ji, where are you? I’ve got a huge project to share with you—a really, really good one. I just decided to invest fifty billion. Right, right... Only because we’re close. I wouldn’t bother with anyone else...”","On the other end was Ji Zhe, the head of Qixing Capital.","He had once gone to Mingzhu City with Chu Hai and had also invested in projects under Liu Yutong.","The two had an ironclad relationship.","As soon as Ji Zhe heard that Chu Hai had found a great project and invested fifty billion, he perked up.","“Brother, where are you? I’ll come find you right now!”","He’d known Chu Hai for years and understood his character. If Chu Hai praised a project that much and threw in fifty billion, it had to be a top-tier investment—maybe even a high-return, short-term goldmine.","So, without even asking for details, he was eager to meet.","“Sure, sure! I’ll be at our usual spot in the capital.”","“Great, see you in half an hour.”","After hanging up, Chu Hai immediately told the driver, “Old Zhang, to the usual place.”","“Yes, sir.”","Just imagining the look of disappointment on Ji Zhe’s face made Chu Hai’s mood improve. He couldn’t help but chuckle under his breath.","Old Ji, you’ve been my brother for all these years, so we’ve got to share both the good and the bad.","Now that I’m in a hole, it’s not right for you to stand up there on your own, is it?","Not right at all.","Absolutely not right.","So, brother, come on down.","Come keep me company.","Old Zhang caught sight of his boss’s expression in the rearview mirror and felt puzzled.","Hadn’t he been scowling just earlier?","Why was a phone call making him so happy?","Rich people sure are fickle!","Half an hour later, the two met at a barbecue joint.","After about five minutes of conversation...","Ji Zhe’s expression went from initial excitement, to gradually freezing, to red-hot—all in less than five minutes.","“Miss Liu said to find a like-minded partner to invest together, and I thought of you right away. Tell me, am I a good brother or what!”","“Let me warn you in advance—if you want to turn down the investment, you’ll have to tell Miss Liu yourself,” Chu Hai said.","Ji Zhe didn’t say a word, just kept his head down, searching for something under the table.","Chu Hai was puzzled. “What are you looking for?”","“A wine bottle,” Ji Zhe replied.","Chu Hai felt a sense of dread. “You... what are you looking for a wine bottle for?”","Ji Zhe finally found an empty bottle. He grabbed it, shot up from his seat with a ferocious expression, and roared, “Screw it, I’ll kill you first, you bastard!”"]},{"number":789,"title":"Chapter 789: 790, Zhou Yingpei.","paragraphs":["After the aerospace company's financing was finalized, Liu Yutong didn't rush to leave the capital.","The scale of Wanlong Aerospace Technology was far more complicated than any project she had managed before. The technical barriers, high-end talent, industry qualifications, and startup capital involved—each of these, taken individually, was something that ordinary people couldn't handle.","The initial planned investment was twenty billion yuan. She contributed ten billion personally, Chu Hai's AEG Capital claimed five billion, Ji Zhe's Qixing Capital followed with five billion. As for the state-owned portion, how much they would put in depended entirely on the higher-ups' mood.","After all, relying solely on private capital to go it alone in the aerospace sector was not feasible.","Policy support, technological accumulation, and talent reserves all required the backing of national power.","Aerospace involved national security—if a purely private company wanted to obtain rocket launch permits and satellite frequency resources, it was almost impossible without state-owned capital behind it.","So Liu Yutong had figured this out from the very beginning.","The equity structure of Wanlong Aerospace had to be a mixed-ownership model. She would hold a controlling stake personally, but state-owned capital also had to take a share—one that was neither too small nor too large to affect her decision-making.","This balance was difficult to strike.","But no matter how hard it was, it had to be done.","This was the price she had to pay to enter the aerospace field.","Over the next half month, Liu Yutong spent almost every day running around various government departments in the capital.","The National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, the State Administration of Science, Technology and Industry for National Defense... She went from one department to another, submitting one document after another.","If she had followed the normal procedures, getting everything done would have taken two or three years at the very least.","Rocket manufacturing permits, satellite launch licenses, radio frequency usage permits, export control qualifications—each of these required national-level approval, each needed layers of review, and the scrutiny was extremely strict.","But she was no longer who she used to be.","With her current network and connections, she could definitely take advantage of some fast tracks.","For example, Uncle Li, Uncle Zhu, and the Lin, Shen, and Jiang families, along with her relationships from the Yunshan Society.","Most importantly, she could mention it to the Madam.","With so many strong endorsements, getting the permits approved wouldn't take too long.","Apart from these connections, there was another thing that gave her confidence: Dragon Core.","The news that Dragon Core's 90-nanometer production line had successfully gone into mass production, though not yet publicly announced, had spread within the internal circles of the relevant ministries.","A twenty-year-old girl, in less than a year, had somehow managed to set up this entire operation and was about to start mass production.","This news had indeed surprised many people.","The first batch of chips was designated for supply to Shen Hao's Qiming Electrical Appliances.","Liu Yutong had already mentioned to Shen Hao that Qiming's electrical products, which were large appliances, were more than adequate with 90-nanometer chips.","In short, successfully pulling off Dragon Core carried much more weight than outsiders could imagine.","So when Liu Yutong went to the various departments to submit her materials, she still had to go through the formal procedures, but the efficiency was much faster.","A senior director from the State Administration of Science, Technology and Industry for National Defense, after reading her business plan, even took half an hour out of his schedule to have an in-depth conversation with her, expressing high praise for her boldness and ability to execute.","When someone so young was tackling such large, urgently needed national projects, it was hard not to hold them in high regard.","While she was handling the various permits, she was also simultaneously looking for talent.","In the aerospace field, having money alone wouldn't get a rocket built. You needed top experts in the industry to take the lead.","Although Liu Yutong had some knowledge of aerospace from her previous life, it was limited to knowing a few names and major events. Expecting her to personally draw blueprints and build rockets was absolutely out of the question.","So she needed to find a true industry heavyweight to steer the ship.","She eventually set her sights on the Capital University of Aeronautics and Astronautics.","This university was the cradle of domestic aerospace talent, with many chief and deputy chief engineers of aerospace systems having graduated from there.","Liu Yutong asked Lin Yi to use her connections to get in touch with a vice dean at the university, and she visited the campus under the guise of an inspection tour.","This university was quite different from her alma mater, the University of Finance and Economics, especially in terms of academic atmosphere.","That day, Liu Yutong wore a white shirt with her hair tied in a high ponytail, dressed much like an ordinary college student.","Soon, under the guidance of the university staff, she met the vice dean, whose surname was Fang.","\"Director Liu, our university has made quite a few achievements in the aerospace field over the years—rocket engines, aircraft design, satellite control—we've dabbled in many areas, and many projects have won National Science and Technology Progress Awards...\" Dean Fang briefly introduced the university's situation in a tone full of pride.","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Liu Yutong got straight to the point of her visit: \"Dean Fang, I'd like to meet with someone.\"","\"Who?\"","\"Professor Zhou Yingpei.\"","Dean Fang stopped in his tracks slightly, his expression turning a bit subtle.","\"Professor Zhou... How do you know his name?\"","Liu Yutong: \"I've done my homework.\"","Zhou Yingpei was a leading domestic expert in rocket engines. He had worked as a deputy chief engineer at the Aerospace Science and Technology Group and had led the research and development of several key national models.","However, because his personality was too straightforward, he had offended many people and was eventually transferred to teach at the university.","There was no doubt about his ability, but his temper was notoriously awful.","This kind of personality, however, wouldn't get far within the system.","But Liu Yutong needed exactly this kind of person.","Someone who truly understood technology, had high aspirations, and wouldn't easily compromise.","Dean Fang hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Director Liu, Professor Zhou has a bit of a difficult personality, and he's already turned down invitations from several well-known companies, including a few subsidiaries of state-owned enterprises.\"","Liu Yutong: \"It's all right. I want to give it a try.\"","Dean Fang sighed: \"Alright, I'll take you there, but whether he agrees to see you or not, I can't guarantee.\"","The two of them walked through several modern teaching buildings and arrived in front of an unremarkable old building.","Dean Fang pointed to a room on the second floor: \"Professor Zhou's lab is right up there. Go on up by yourself—I won't accompany you.\"","Liu Yutong thanked him and went upstairs alone.","When she reached the end of the hallway on the second floor, she saw a half-open door, from which came a loud roar of machinery.","She knocked on the door. No one answered.","She knocked a few more times. Still no response.","Finally, she simply pushed the door open and walked in.","The lab wasn't very large, filled with blueprints, parts, and various instruments she couldn't name.","An elderly man with mostly white hair was crouched in front of a piece of equipment, making adjustments, completely unaware that someone had entered.","Liu Yutong didn't disturb him. She just stood quietly to the side, watching.","About ten minutes later, the old man finally finished the work in his hands. He stood up and stretched his stiff body.","When he noticed the unfamiliar girl standing behind him, he immediately became angry.","\"Who are you? Who let you in here!\"","\"Don't you know this is a laboratory? Barging in here without permission—who’s going to take responsibility if there’s a safety accident? Get out!\""]},{"number":790,"title":"Chapter 790: 791, Is Aerospace Just for Retirement Travel","paragraphs":["“I’m sorry, Professor Zhou, for disturbing you.”","Liu Yutong quickly apologized, then introduced herself: “My name is Liu Yutong, Chairman of Wanlonghui Group. I’m here today because I’d like to talk with you.”","Zhou Yingpei waved his hand impatiently. “I have nothing to discuss with you. You’re not the first to come looking for me. None of you capitalists are reliable—you’re all just after quick money and government subsidies. Not a single one of you genuinely cares about technology.”","With that, he turned back to fiddle with the equipment in his hands, making it clear he had no intention of engaging with her further.","Liu Yutong: “Professor Zhou, I’m different from those people you’ve met before. I come with genuine sincerity.”","Zhou Yingpei, still tinkering with his device, said, “Are you done? If you’re done, you can leave.”","Seeing that the old man was unmoved by either soft or hard approaches, Liu Yutong decided to cut straight to the point. “Professor Zhou, I want to start a private aerospace company—build rockets, launch satellites, explore space—and I’d like to invite you to join me.”","Zhou Yingpei’s hands froze.","He slowly turned around and looked at Liu Yutong as if she were a swindler.","“What did you just say?”","“I said, I want to build rockets—rockets that can send people to Mars,” Liu Yutong repeated.","Zhou Yingpei looked her up and down before speaking. “Little girl, do you have any idea how much money it takes to build a single rocket? Do you know the technological accumulation required? Do you understand how high the barrier to entry is in this field? Even if your parents were billionaires, it still wouldn’t be enough. I suggest you give up that fantasy now.”","He clearly assumed Liu Yutong was just another spoiled rich kid with more money than sense, dreaming up a far-fetched aerospace venture.","Liu Yutong: “You don’t need to worry about that. I have more money than I could ever spend.”","Zhou Yingpei snorted, somewhat irritated. “Little girl, that’s quite a bold claim!”","Liu Yutong: “Let me answer your questions first, Professor. The R&D cost for a medium-lift launch vehicle is roughly between five and ten billion yuan. From design to maiden flight, it usually takes at least three to five years. Right now, only a handful of countries and organizations in the world have the capability to independently develop launch vehicles. As for private aerospace companies, there are only a few in the U.S., and they’re just getting started—their technology isn’t mature yet...”","After hearing her words, Zhou Yingpei’s expression shifted slightly.","This girl, who looked to be barely twenty, actually knew what she was talking about.","“You did your homework beforehand?”","Liu Yutong nodded. “If you’re going into aerospace, you have to do your homework. Professor Zhou, I own a chip company called Loongson. I’m sure you’ve heard of it.”","Zhou Yingpei paused, momentarily stunned.","He had certainly heard of Loongson—it was one of the few chip manufacturers in the country, and word had it that it took less than a year from project initiation to the mass production of its 90-nanometer process line, causing quite a stir in the industry.","Under normal circumstances, building such a factory would take at least two or three years before it could go into production, yet Loongson had managed it in less than a year. That was extraordinarily efficient.","It showed just how capable the owner of Loongson must be.","What he hadn’t expected was that the owner of that company would be this impossibly young woman standing before him.","“Did you really build Loongson?”","“Yes, I’m also the Chairman of Loongson.”","Liu Yutong didn’t downplay it. Being modest in front of someone like him would only come across as insincere—it was better to show her strength.","“Back when I started the chip company, a lot of people told me I was fantasizing and would likely fail. But as it turned out, I made it happen. Now I want to go into aerospace, and I’m hearing similar things again. I don’t care, because I’ll prove to everyone once more—I can do it again.”","“Professor Zhou, let me ask you something: What’s the biggest regret of your life?”","Zhou Yingpei fell into deep thought at her question.","His biggest regret was probably that, back when he was in the aerospace system, he never got to finish developing the new engine he had designed.","He had studied that project for ten years, run thousands of experiments, and was on the verge of a breakthrough when it was shut down due to various reasons.","Then he was transferred to the Aviation University to teach.","From that day on, he never touched that project again.","It was the greatest regret of his life and the deepest ache in his heart.","“Professor Zhou, what if I told you that I could let you finish that unfinished project?” Liu Yutong suddenly said.","Zhou Yingpei looked up sharply. “You don’t even know what project I was working on—how dare you make such a wild claim!”","But no sooner had he spoken than he realized something.","How did she know he had an unfinished project at all?","Liu Yutong pulled a document from her bag and handed it to him.","“Liquid oxygen and kerosene staged combustion cycle rocket engine, thrust-to-weight ratio design target of 320, specific impulse of 350 seconds. This was your ten-year project, wasn’t it?”","Zhou Yingpei took the document, his hands trembling.","He flipped open the first page and saw a line of text:","【Wanlong Aerospace Technology — New Liquid Oxygen Kerosene Rocket Engine R&D Plan】","As he read further, he found that the technical parameters, R&D roadmap, and timeline were startlingly similar to the plan in his own mind.","No, not just similar—some ideas were even more advanced than his.","“This... who wrote this?”","“I did.”","Liu Yutong didn’t hide it. “Of course, I’m not a technical person. These are just based on your original design, with some of my own ideas added in. Whether they can actually be realized depends on experts like you.”","This wasn’t a lie.","While she didn’t understand the core technologies behind rocket engines, in her past life, the hype around Elon Musk’s Starship had been so massive that it was impossible not to know something about it.","She had come across many videos and articles analyzing the pros and cons of the Raptor engine’s full-flow staged combustion cycle.","So after researching Zhou Yingpei’s background, she had incorporated some of the forward-looking concepts she remembered—like reusable rockets and high-efficiency engine designs—as inspiration and development directions.","These advanced ideas from the future were invaluable to a top rocket engine expert, potentially helping him bypass many dead ends.","Zhou Yingpei read that plan three times from cover to cover before finally confirming one thing:","This girl was not here to fool around.","She genuinely understood, she had genuinely thought it through, and she was genuinely ready to make it happen.","“Director... Director Liu, may I ask how much capital you can provide?” Zhou Yingpei addressed her with respect for the first time.","“Initial investment of twenty billion yuan. The funds will be in place soon, and we’ll add more as the project progresses,” Liu Yutong said.","“Twenty billion...”","Zhou Yingpei gasped.","In his decades in the aerospace system, the total project funds he had handled were probably less than half of that.","If this girl wasn’t exaggerating, then her family must own a printing press for money.","It was absolutely stunning.","Liu Yutong: “Beyond funding, I’ve already cleared things with various departments. Securing policy support shouldn’t be a major problem.”","Upon hearing her words, Zhou Yingpei was mostly convinced.","“Director Liu, I have a question.”","“Go ahead.”","“Why do you want to get into aerospace?”","He had asked the same question to some business owners who had approached him before, but none of their answers had satisfied him. He wanted to see how this young girl would respond.","Liu Yutong thought for a moment, then said, “Probably because I think I’ll get bored after retirement. I want to, while I’m still alive, travel to space, visit the moon and Mars, maybe check in for fun?”","Zhou Yingpei: “???”","Seriously, what kind of absurd reason was that? Were young people these days so restless that even Earth couldn’t contain them?"]},{"number":791,"title":"Chapter 791: 792, Feeling Disgusted.","paragraphs":["“Director Liu, if I may ask, how old are you this year?”","“Twenty.”","“And you’re already thinking about retiring at twenty?”","“Planning ahead. If I waited until I’m seventy or eighty to think about traveling to outer space, wouldn’t it be too late to start aerospace then? I call it being proactive.”","Zhou Yingpei: “...”","“Then... if you retire early, what happens to your company?”","“I’ll hand it over to someone else.”","“You can’t make all the money in the world, but life only lasts a few decades. You push hard when you’re young, and when you’ve done enough, you learn to enjoy yourself. Don’t you think so, Professor Zhou?”","Zhou Yingpei: “...”","Did he think so?","He thought this girl actually had a point somehow.","“Alright, alright, I’ll take your proposal. Let me think it over for a few days.”","Liu Yutong: “Great, I’ll wait to hear from you.”","Just as she reached the door, she suddenly turned back: “Oh, by the way, Professor Zhou, if you restart that engine project, how long would it take to produce a prototype?”","Zhou Yingpei answered instinctively: “If the funding and the team are in place, two years... no, a year and a half would be enough.”","Liu Yutong nodded: “Money isn’t an issue, and people aren’t either. If I can’t recruit domestically, I’ll go abroad. I hear the aerospace sector in the US has been laying off a lot of people—I’ll send someone to make contact.”","“In short, I’ll handle all the resources. You just do your job well!”","With that, she waved goodbye stylishly and walked away.","Zhou Yingpei stood there, stunned for a long moment.","“Wait, what does she mean by ‘doing my job well’?”","“Am I her employee?”","............","Not long after Liu Yutong left Hangda University, she received some bad news.","The permits for rocket manufacturing and satellite frequency usage had been stalled.","Everything had been going smoothly. They only needed to finalize the last steps, and the approvals would be stamped within a few days.","But now, at the final signing stage, someone had deliberately blocked them.","“Someone used connections to put pressure on things, saying that Wanlong Aerospace’s project involves national security and requires stricter review.”","“The exact source hasn’t been traced yet, but given the influence and our past conflicts, it can only be Chu Junlin,” Yun Cheng said.","Liu Yutong sneered upon hearing this: “Chu Junlin sure knows how to pick a time to be obnoxious.”","She had expected Chu Junlin to pull some small tricks.","After all, that day at the Imperial Club, she had embarrassed him in front of so many people and forced him into a ten-billion yuan bet.","Given how Young Master Chu’s ego worked, he was bound to try and get even.","She just hadn’t expected him to reach into aerospace approvals.","Quite impressive!","“The Young Lady, should we try pulling some strings? Lin Yi might be able to help.”","Liu Yutong shook her head: “No rush. I have my own plans for Lin Yi. For now, you find out what Chu Junlin is up to lately.”","Yun Cheng reported: “I’ve already had people look into it. He’s been busy lately—besides setting up a new chamber of commerce, he’s also working on a variety show.”","“A variety show?” Liu Yutong was slightly surprised.","“Yes, it’s called ‘China’s Best Music,’ meant to be the country’s first major music talent show. The mentor lineup is strong, and it feels like a direct challenge to our ‘China’s Best Voice.’”","Liu Yutong couldn’t help but laugh at the news.","“Interesting. He’s trying to go after me on all fronts.”","Yun Cheng: “That’s not all. Lin Muyang told me that some of the singers who signed up for our auditions have been poached by that show’s production team. We’ve already lost several standout contestants from Beijing to high-paying offers.”","“Let them go.”","Liu Yutong wasn’t too concerned: “There are plenty of good talents from the auditions. We don’t need those fence-sitters.”","Yun Cheng continued: “There’s one more thing. After our investigation, the person behind the delayed approval of our Longkan Vision platform—the capital behind it was Chu Junlin.”","Liu Yutong: “We hadn’t even fallen out by then, had we?”","“No, it was pure business competition. He owns a listed entertainment company that invested in several video platforms. Longkan Vision’s copyright strategy hurt those platforms, so they went to him for help, and he stepped in.”","Liu Yutong nodded and said nothing more.","She’d seen this kind of business maneuver plenty of times. It wasn’t anger, just a sense that Chu Junlin was small-minded.","Look at someone like Little Ma, for example—even when competing, he’d still call ahead to give you a heads up.","Chu Junlin, on the other hand, only knew how to use underhanded tricks behind the scenes.","“Yun Cheng, set up a meeting with Lin Yi for me. I’ll go see her tomorrow afternoon.”","“Got it.”","The next afternoon, Liu Yutong showed up on time at Lin Yi’s office.","Lin Yi’s office wasn’t large, but it was elegantly decorated. Several delicate orchids sat on the windowsill, and a calligraphy scroll hung on the wall with the words “Tranquility Leads to Far-reaching Ambition.”","“Yutong, you’re here.”","Lin Yi put down the documents in her hand and smiled as she invited her to sit: “What’s up? Did you suddenly miss me?”","Liu Yutong got straight to the point and explained the issue with the stalled aerospace approvals.","Lin Yi listened, her delicate brows furrowing slightly: “I’ll look into this for you later. But since you say it’s the Chu family, it’s almost certainly them.”","“Can you help smooth things over?” Liu Yutong asked.","Lin Yi: “It’ll take some time, but I’ll resolve it as soon as possible.”","Liu Yutong: “I’m not in a rush, as long as it gets approved in the end.”","Lin Yi nodded: “Sure, I’ll go talk to my uncle later and ask him to pull some strings.”","Liu Yutong: “Thank you, Sister Yi.”","“Don’t mention it. We’re family.”","Lin Yi waved her hand, then suddenly recalled something: “Oh, by the way, I heard someone’s been poaching talent from your ‘China’s Best Voice’?”","Liu Yutong: “News travels fast?”","Lin Yi: “Beijing is a small place. Any little stir gets around. Chu Junlin is setting up ‘China’s Best Music’ with a strong mentor lineup. I heard he shelled out big money to bring in A-list stars from Hong Kong and Taiwan.”","“Looks like you really offended him. He’s creating a whole show just to counter you.”","“So, do you think you can win?”","Liu Yutong: “Sister Yi, I never realized you were so gossipy.”","Lin Yi: “Gossip? No, this is me caring about my little sister.”","“I’ll keep an eye on the aerospace approval and let you know when I have news. But I don’t think it’ll be a big deal—he’s probably just trying to mess with you.”","“Well, he succeeded. I am annoyed.”","“But I’ll annoy him back. Fair’s fair.”","“Hearing you say that, I get the feeling he’s about to be in trouble.”"]},{"number":792,"title":"Chapter 792: 793, Encountering a Bar Singer.","paragraphs":["After leaving Lin Yi's company, Liu Yutong didn't go straight back to the hotel. Instead, she asked the driver to pull over by the roadside, wanting to take a walk and get some fresh air.","She strolled slowly along the sidewalk, and before she knew it, she had wandered near a commercial square.","The square was bustling with activity. Older women were dancing in groups, children were chasing each other around, and a few young people sat in a corner playing guitars and singing.","Just as Liu Yutong was about to head into the mall, a heated argument suddenly reached her ears.","\"Can you stop being so childish!\"","\"How am I being childish? I'm worried about you!\"","\"... \"","One of the voices sounded familiar.","Liu Yutong stopped in her tracks and turned to look.","Near an inflatable castle children's play area in the square, a young man carrying a guitar and a woman in elegant attire were arguing fiercely.","The man wore a denim jacket, and his bangs were a bit long, covering half his face—it was quite the edgy look.","But Liu Yutong recognized him at once.","It was the resident singer from the bar that night.","She only remembered his surname was Zhou; couldn't recall his exact name.","\"Zhou Ran, can you just wake up!\"","\"Do you have any idea what level of company Star Media is? Them being willing to sign me is my luck. Do you know how many people are dying to get in?\"","\"Xiaoya, listen to me. When I was competing, I overheard some staff talking about that company. They said... Star Media has problems.\"","\"What kind of problems?\"","\"They... they make newcomers drink with clients, attend social events, and—\"","\"Where did you hear such nonsense?\"","\"It's true!\"","The woman's expression shifted from anger to disappointment and impatience.","\"Zhou Ran, are you insane?\"","\"Xiaoya...\"","\"You actually believe what those people say? Who do they think they are? Just a few staff members gossiping about Star Media!\"","\"No, they were very specific. I think it's better to be safe than sorry—\"","\"Enough!\"","The woman exploded, yanking her hand out of his grasp.","\"Zhou Ran, do you know how much I've sacrificed for this opportunity? I've been studying singing for eight years, auditioning for talent shows for three years, getting rejected over and over again. Now, finally, someone is willing to sign me, guaranteeing I'll make it to the finals, and you're telling me not to go? All because you overheard some random staff talking about a so-called 'casting couch'?\"","\"Do you have any proof?\"","\"And you'd rather believe those unsubstantiated rumors than trust me? I honestly don't know what's going on in your head.\"","\"Or is it that you're afraid I'll get famous before you do?\"","Zhou Ran was left speechless, unable to find the words to defend himself.","He truly had no proof.","He had overheard those conversations in a bathroom stall during the second round of the competition.","Of course, he wasn't even sure if what those people said was true.","He just thought—what if?","What if it was true?","Xiaoya was so innocent, so beautiful. If she ended up in a place like that...","\"Xiaoya, just give me a little more time. Let me find out the truth—\"","\"Don't bother.\"","The woman's voice suddenly turned cold—eerily calm, with a tone of finality.","\"Zhou Ran, we're breaking up.\"","Zhou Ran froze.","\"What... what did you say?\"","\"I said we're breaking up!\"","\"We've been in the capital for almost five years now, haven't we? Back then, you said you'd make it soon, asked me to give you time. I waited—one year, two years, three years, four years, now almost five. And what's the result?\"","\"The result is we're still living in that dark, cramped basement, and sometimes you can't even afford the rent!\"","\"Zhou Ran, you can't even see your own future clearly. What right do you have to try and arrange mine?\"","\"This time, whether it's true or not, I'm going to take the chance. This is my opportunity, and no one is going to stop me!\"","With that, she turned and walked away, utterly resolute.","Zhou Ran reached out to grab her, his hand hovering in the air for a moment, then dropped limply to his side.","He just stood there silently, watching her figure grow distant until she disappeared into the crowd.","Then he slowly crouched down, burying his face in his knees.","The music from the square continued to play. The children in the play area kept laughing. The setting sun still cast its golden light over everything.","Everything was so lively.","Only him, as if forgotten by the world.","Liu Yutong stood nearby, quietly watching the scene.","She wasn't the type to meddle in other people's affairs.","But this young man surnamed Zhou had left a good impression on her before.","After a moment's thought, she walked over with Yun Cheng.","\"You okay?\"","Zhou Ran looked up, about to say \"I'm fine,\" but when he saw who it was, he froze.","\"You... you're the boss from the bar that night?\"","\"You remember me?\" Liu Yutong said.","Zhou Ran nodded, straightening up nervously. \"I've been performing at that bar for six months. You're the one who tipped me the most, so of course I remember.\"","Liu Yutong pulled a pack of tissues from her bag and handed them to him.","\"Here. A grown man crying doesn't look good.\"","Zhou Ran took the tissues, wiping his face awkwardly. \"Sorry you had to see that.\"","Liu Yutong added, \"You can't force these things.\"","Zhou Ran let out a bitter laugh. \"I know she's right. I really am useless—can't even support myself. Why should she have to suffer with me? I just... I just didn't want to see her walk into a trap.\"","\"You really think that company is shady?\"","\"I don't know.\"","Zhou Ran shook his head. \"I just heard it during the competition's second round. No proof. Maybe Xiaoya's right—I'm too naive, too idealistic, believe everything I hear.\"","\"What's the name of that company?\" Liu Yutong asked.","Zhou Ran thought for a moment. \"I think it's... Star Media.\"","Star Media.","Liu Yutong couldn't help but feel exasperated upon hearing that name.","How many times had she heard it today?","That Chu Junlin really was relentless.","\"What's your girlfriend's name?\" Liu Yutong asked again.","\"Lin Ya.\"","\"She's also a singer?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Liu Yutong nodded, making a mental note.","\"Zhou Ran.\"","Zhou Ran was startled. \"How do you know my name?\"","\"You just said it yourself.\"","\"Did I?\" Zhou Ran scratched his head, unsure.","Liu Yutong didn't dwell on it. \"What's the name of the competition you were in?\"","\"Show Me, but I was eliminated in the second round.\"","Zhou Ran felt even more dejected mentioning that. He thought it was probably the last straw that broke his and Lin Ya's relationship.","Liu Yutong asked, \"Since you're out, doesn't that mean you can sign up for other shows?\"","Zhou Ran replied, \"You mean The Voice of China? But the auditions are already over. I have no way to register, and I don't have any fame...\"","Liu Yutong pulled out her phone from her bag, scrolled through a contact number, wrote it down on a sticky note, and handed it to him. \"Keep this number. Call him later and just say Miss Liu recommended you. He should be able to arrange for you to go straight to the blind audition stage.\"","Zhou Ran was stunned, finding it hard to believe. \"You... you... who exactly are you?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Just an ordinary college student.\"","\"College student?\" Zhou Ran was baffled.","Were college students these days really this impressive?","With just one sentence, she could skip the preliminary rounds and get him directly into the main competition's blind auditions for The Voice of Dragon Kingdom.","That show was one of the hottest music competition shows being debated online recently.","Liu Yutong continued, \"I'm not helping you for nothing.\"","\"I'm helping you get into the main competition with a condition. In return, I need you to do something for me when the time is right.\"","Zhou Ran asked, \"What is it?\"","Liu Yutong replied, \"You'll find out when the time comes.\"","Zhou Ran wanted to ask more questions, but Liu Yutong turned and walked away without another word.","After taking a few steps, she stopped without turning back and added, \"Oh, and you might want to adjust your voice. There's no need to force that gravelly tone. Sure, that world-weary sound works well for folk songs, but I think you could try using your natural voice.\"","Zhou Ran was stunned by her words, standing still for a long time.","\"My natural voice... huh?\""]},{"number":793,"title":"Chapter 793: 794, Done, going home.","paragraphs":["Two more days passed.","The approval matter was finally resolved.","But Liu Yutong also had to pay some price.","In the afternoon, she was summoned to the National Defense Science, Technology, and Industry Bureau again. This time, it wasn’t the elderly director who met her, but a higher-level leader.","He wasn’t wearing a uniform, just an ordinary dark blue jacket. His face was stern, but when he spoke, his tone was quite gentle.","“Director Liu, we’ve carefully reviewed your application materials. Wanlong Aerospace’s plan is ambitious. The higher-ups intend to support private capital entering the aerospace sector—this is an inevitable trend. I estimate that within a few years, policies will fully open up. But some rules must be clarified in advance,” the leader said.","Liu Yutong caught the underlying meaning in his words. “Sir, whatever the conditions are, just tell me directly. I’m all ears.”","The leader smiled and handed her a document.","Liu Yutong took it, opened it, and read through each clause. Her expression gradually turned serious.","The conditions were simple but harsh.","The gist was this: all technological achievements from rocket-engine research and development by Wanlong Aerospace would belong to the state. She would only retain usage and operational rights. Throughout the entire R&D lifecycle, the project must accept full supervision and technical review by the National Defense Science, Technology, and Industry Bureau. Key technical personnel would need to pass the strictest national security background checks.","At the same time, all launch missions must prioritize national strategic needs, and civilian commercial launches would require advance reporting and approval.","To put it bluntly: she would fund and staff the R&D, but whatever came out of it would go to the state. She could only use it, not sell or transfer it to any third party. She would also have to sign an extremely strict confidentiality agreement with the state.","Moreover, she herself would be prohibited from emigrating.","Any other businessperson under these conditions would likely walk away without a second thought.","But Liu Yutong didn’t.","Because she understood better than anyone that aerospace was never a purely commercial game. It was a key pillar of national power—a blade of the nation. Every bit of technology in this field could be applied to intercontinental missiles, military satellites, or critical areas of national security.","For the state to entrust a private company with full control over technology of this level? That would only happen if the top brass got completely drunk.","So from the very beginning, she never expected to own these technologies outright.","What she wanted was usage rights, operational rights, and that legal license to launch rockets.","As for the more sensitive issues like technology ownership, she had already had private discussions with a few senior figures over the past few days. In particular, she had taken time yesterday to visit Madam and touched on the topic.","From that moment on, she had already made up her mind: no matter how much money she poured into developing those technologies, she would hand them over to the state.","Although it seemed like a loss, it was actually a good thing for her personally.","It was like adding a talisman of protection.","Beyond that, Wanlong Aerospace’s rockets could legitimately take on national missions, and even secure technical support and talent resources from the state level.","These were things money couldn’t buy.","“I agree.”","Liu Yutong closed the document without a moment’s hesitation.","The leader was slightly taken aback, clearly not expecting her to consent so quickly, without even bargaining.","“Director Liu, you don’t want to reconsider?”","“No need.”","Liu Yutong stood up and looked earnestly at the leader before her. “The aerospace industry has always been a national endeavor. For a private company like mine to be involved is already an exception. I’ll yield the profits I should yield, and I’ll follow the rules I’m meant to follow. As long as Longguo’s rockets can fly higher and farther, a little personal sacrifice means nothing.”","The leader stared for a long moment at this twenty-year-old woman, then suddenly smiled.","“Director Liu, what you’re saying puts an old-timer like me, who’s spent thirty years in this system, to shame.”","“Young people today should take you as a role model.”","“Thank you, sir, for the praise!”","The leader took a small red booklet from his drawer and pushed it across the desk to Liu Yutong.","“This is the launch vehicle manufacturing license you requested. It’s been approved at the top level. The satellite frequency approval will come through in the next couple of days, and I’ll have someone deliver it to you directly.”","Liu Yutong picked up the booklet, opened it, and flipped through it. The weight on her heart finally lifted.","“Thank you, sir.”","“Don’t thank me. You earned it yourself.”","The leader stood up and extended his right hand. “Director Liu, on behalf of all my colleagues in the aerospace system, I officially welcome Wanlong Aerospace into the family. If you run into any technical or policy difficulties in the future, don’t hesitate to come to me.”","Liu Yutong shook his hand. “I will.”","Stepping out of the Bureau, Liu Yutong stood on the steps and took a deep breath. She felt an incredible lightness throughout her body.","Now, she held two trump cards: Longxin and Wanlong Aerospace—her own talismans of protection.","And from the conversation with that leader, she had picked up something else: it seemed the top brass had truly begun to take notice of her.","Not the casual compliments from provincial visits last year in BS Province—you know, those polite, throwaway lines.","This was real entry into the vision of the highest authorities.","That feeling was more reassuring than making ten billion yuan.","After wrapping up Wanlong Aerospace matters, she turned her mind back to making money.","Aerospace was a bottomless pit—an enormous money furnace. You could pour hundreds of billions into it and not even hear a splash. So she needed to hustle, to build up plenty of ammunition for future R&D.","“Big Miss, heading back to the hotel?” Yun Cheng asked.","Liu Yutong nodded. “Yes, and book us tickets. We’re heading back tomorrow morning.”","“Understood.”","She had stayed in the capital long enough.","The things that needed doing were done. The people who needed seeing had been seen. The groundwork had been laid.","The rest was up to time to unfold.","The next morning, the plane landed at Danancheng Airport.","As Liu Yutong stepped off the aircraft, she couldn’t help grumbling, “When are they ever going to build an airport in Mingzhu City?”","That way, she wouldn’t have to go through all the transfer hassles. She could just land and be home.","But she knew perfectly well that, given the current pace of urban planning and economic development, it would be at least two decades before Mingzhu City had its own civilian airport.","Even with her push in this lifetime, it would likely take more than ten years.","Maybe she could find time to mention it to Uncle Li—see if he could bring it up with the higher-ups to get Mingzhu City an airport ahead of schedule.","“Yutong Jie! Over here!”","Before she even reached the exit, Li Xiaohui’s voice rang out.","That girl was wearing a bright purple T-shirt today, paired with a matching baseball cap. She looked like an eggplant that had wandered into the airport—very eye-catching.","Liu Yutong was surprised to see her. “What are you doing here?”","“I happened to be in Danancheng for a match. I knew you were coming back, so I specifically came to pick you up,” Li Xiaohui said, grinning as she linked her arm through Liu Yutong’s. “And I haven’t seen Yaya in a while. I’ll head back with you and mooch a meal.”","At the mention of Yaya, Liu Yutong’s heart softened.","It had been over a month since she’d seen that little girl.","“Alright, I’ll go buy some things first. I can’t go back empty-handed.”","The two of them first took a car to a shopping mall in the city, where they bought some clothes and gifts for the grandparents, as well as a bunch of snacks and toys for Yaya.","After about three or more hours, the convoy finally arrived at Liu Yutong’s hometown."]},{"number":794,"title":"Chapter 794: 795, Cute Yaya.","paragraphs":["About three hours later, the convoy arrived at Liu Yutong's hometown.","As they reached the old home, the air noticeably felt fresher.","The fields were bustling with activity—many villagers were planting rice seedlings. In the distance, the rice plants were a lush green, rippling like waves in the wind.","Liu Yutong rolled down the window and gazed at the vibrant scene outside, feeling an immense sense of relief.","Every time she returned to her hometown, she felt as if time moved slowly here.","So slow that she could hear the cicadas chirping, see the curling wisps of chimney smoke, and smell her grandmother’s old hen soup simmering on the stove.","Soon, the car pulled into the courtyard of a very grand rural villa.","“Grandpa! Grandma!”","“Ah, coming, coming!”","Grandma’s voice rang out from inside the house.","A moment later, an elderly woman with an apron tied around her waist and graying hair stepped out of the kitchen.","“Grandma, I’m home.”","Grandma took Liu Yutong’s hand, looked her over, and said with some concern: “It’s good you’re back, good you’re back. You look like you’ve lost a little weight—didn’t you eat well in the capital?”","“I ate well, but I got tired of it. I’ve been thinking about your cooking every day, Grandma.”","“Go wash your hands. Grandma’s made you chicken stew, your favorite bean-cake braised pork, and pork liver soup.”","Just as she finished speaking, Li Xiaohui suddenly popped her head out from behind Liu Yutong, grinning as she called out: “Grandma, I’m here too! Is there some for me?”","“Little Hui, you’re here too! Yes, yes, there’s plenty for everyone.”","Grandma beamed, unable to stop smiling. “Grandma’s made a lot of dishes. You look a bit thin too, dear—make sure to eat plenty later.”","“I’m not thin at all! I eat a ton, I just don’t seem to gain weight.”","“Grandma, I want to eat your sweet-and-sour fish—the same flavor as last time, with that tangy sweetness.”","“Yes, yes! They caught some big carp from the pond this morning. I’ll cook it for you right away.”","“Long live Grandma!”","Li Xiaohui cheered and turned back to wink at Liu Yutong. “Sister Yutong, did you hear that? Grandma’s making fish just for me!”","Liu Yutong ignored her and asked: “Where’s Grandpa?”","“He’s picking vegetables in the backyard with Yaya. That little girl is so hardworking—she follows Grandpa around every day helping out.” Grandma’s face lit up with wrinkles as she talked about Yaya.","In her mind, Liu Yutong quickly pictured the scene: a delicate, rosy-cheeked little girl holding up fruits and vegetables bigger than her own hands, toddling after her grandpa.","“I’ll go check on them in the back.”","“Me too, me too!” Li Xiaohui quickly followed.","They circled past the main hall and walked along a path paved with bluestone slabs. From a distance, they could hear a childish voice chatting away in the backyard vegetable garden.","“Grandpa, is this tomato the biggest of all? Sister will love it, right?”","“That’s right, that’s right—the one Yaya picked is the biggest and tastiest.”","“And this cucumber? Sister says eating cucumbers makes you prettier. I want to pick lots and lots of cucumbers for her, so she can become the prettiest person in the whole world!”","“Alright, alright, let’s pick a few more and fill up the basket.”","“Grandpa, look! There’s a little frog here. Ribbit, ribbit!”","“Don’t touch that—it’s a toad.”","“Eww, toads are so ugly! Will it eat our vegetables?”","“No, it eats pests. It’s a good friend helping protect our garden.”","“Then... then Yaya doesn’t hate it anymore. Good friends shouldn’t be hated—they should be cared for.”","Listening to this charmingly babyish conversation, Li Xiaohui felt her heart melt: “Sister Yutong, Yaya is way too adorable! I can’t take it!”","Liu Yutong’s heart was melting too.","In the garden, Grandpa was busy among the bean trellises, bent over. Beside him followed a tiny, cute figure—Yaya.","She wore a little pale pink dress and a pair of sandals that were clearly a few sizes too large, making her feet go pat-pat-pat like a little duck.","A few smudges of dirt were on her face, and her little skirt had gathered some mud stains. Right now, she was squatting on the ground, carefully poking a toad with a small twig and muttering to herself.","“Good friend, you be good, okay? Yaya won’t hurt you, and you don’t bite Yaya.”","The toad got annoyed from her poking and suddenly jumped into the grass.","Yaya let out an “Ah!” and plopped down onto the ground.","But she quickly propped herself up with her hands and stood up, patting herself clean, then turned around and saw Liu Yutong walking toward her.","The little girl’s eyes lit up instantly.","“Sister!”","Like a little butterfly, she fluttered over.","Liu Yutong crouched down and opened her arms, catching the flying little butterfly.","Yaya buried her head in Liu Yutong’s embrace, nuzzling her small face into her chest.","“Sister, Yaya missed you so, so, so much!”","Holding the soft little bundle in her arms, Liu Yutong said: “Sister missed you very much too, Yaya.”","Li Xiaohui, growing anxious from the sidelines, said: “Sister Yutong, let me hold her! Let me hold her! I want to get a dose of this little cutie too!”","Yaya only then noticed the person beside her and sweetly called out, “Hello, Sister Xiaohui!”","“Sister Xiaohui, your hair is so beautiful, just like a princess from a cartoon.”","Li Xiaohui was absolutely delighted by her compliment. “Haha... Yutong, did you hear that? She called me a princess! I’m taking her home with me! Nobody’s stopping me!”","With that, she reached out to take Yaya.","Yaya stretched out her little arms and let Li Xiaohui pick her up.","But after just a short while, Li Xiaohui started to struggle a bit. The kid might’ve looked skinny, but she was actually pretty solid and heavy.","“Sister Xiaohui, you’re holding me too tight. Yaya can barely breathe.”","“Ahh, sorry, sorry!”","Yaya giggled and reached out to touch Li Xiaohui’s purple hair. “Sister Xiaohui is so cute.”","Li Xiaohui was speechless for a moment.","She turned to look at Liu Yutong, her face dead serious. “Yutong, I hereby declare that from today onward, Yaya is my own little sister. Anyone who tries to take her from me is going to have to deal with me.”","Liu Yutong was equally speechless.","Are you saying... you want to fight me for her?","“Grandpa, dinner’s almost ready. Grandma said the chicken stew is done,” she called out.","Her grandfather had already noticed her. He straightened up, wiped the sweat off his forehead, and said, “Alright, after I pick these last few eggplants, I’ll head back.”","Just then, Yaya slipped out of Li Xiaohui’s arms and, once her feet hit the ground, ran right into the vegetable patch. She pulled out a tomato that was bigger than her own fist and held it up high with both hands.","“This is a tomato Yaya picked for you, sister! It’s super tasty! Really sweet!”","“Thank you, Yaya,” Liu Yutong said.","Yaya clapped her hands happily, then turned and ran back, bringing over all kinds of fruits and veggies.","“And this big melon—this one’s for you too, sister!”","“And green beans, and eggplants, and some baby bok choy...”","She ran back and forth like a busy little bee, carrying each item over, then looking up with her little face waiting for Liu Yutong’s praise. Every time she got it, she’d beam with joy—then turn around and race back to grab more.","Li Xiaohui stood nearby, watching in amazement. “Is this kid secretly a little hamster?”","Hearing that, Yaya corrected her seriously: “Yaya is not a hamster—Yaya is a little bunny! Grandpa said so. He says Yaya runs fast, just like a bunny!”","To show it, she even hopped a couple of times, her little skirt bouncing along with her, making her look exactly like a leaping white bunny.","Li Xiaohui immediately changed her tune: “Yaya’s right—you’re a bunny. The cutest little bunny in the whole wide world.”","Yaya thought for a moment then said, “Then Sister Xiaohui is a little purple bunny, because Sister Xiaohui’s hair is purple.”","“Alright, then I’m a little purple bunny! That makes us family!”","Li Xiaohui crouched down and pinched Yaya’s chubby cheeks. “Yaya, you really are just too adorable. Little Hui hereby declares that you are officially the cutest kid in the entire world—there is nobody cuter.”","Yaya replied, “Then Sister Xiaohui is the second cutest big person in the entire world.”","“Why second?” asked Li Xiaohui.","“Because the cutest is my sister,” Yaya said matter-of-factly.","Li Xiaohui clutched her chest dramatically, wearing an exaggerated expression of pain. “Wow, Yaya, you’ve wounded me. Little Hui’s heart is aching.”","Yaya immediately ran over, stood on tiptoe, and blew gently on Li Xiaohui’s chest. “Yaya will blow on it for you. Puff puff, all better now.”","Li Xiaohui was completely smitten. She hugged Yaya tightly and squealed: “I can’t!","I just can’t! You’re way too cute—I’m stealing you away! Right this second!”","“Try it,” Liu Yutong said, giving her a cool look.","“No, no, I’d never dare. Just kidding,” said Li Xiaohui, folding instantly.","The grandfather watched the girls fooling around with an even broader smile. He picked up his vegetable basket and walked over slowly.","“Alright, alright, enough fun. Time to head in for dinner.”","“Got it.”","Just as Liu Yutong was about to reach for Yaya, Li Xiaohui made a move first—she scooped Yaya up and swung her onto her shoulder. “Let’s gooo! Time to eat!”","Yaya grabbed onto Li Xiaohui’s purple hair with both little hands, giggling without stopping.","“Giddy up, giddy up! Little purple bunny, hurry! The big bad wolf is coming to get us!”","Liu Yutong: “...”","Who exactly is the big bad wolf?","..."]},{"number":795,"title":"Chapter 795: 796. Preparing to arrange a staff family trip.","paragraphs":["Lunch was served on the large round table in the main hall.","The table was covered with dishes—stewed chicken, sweet-and-sour fish, bean cake with braised pork, pork liver soup, stir-fried seasonal vegetables... an abundant spread, fragrant and inviting.","Yaya sat next to Liu Yutong, her little legs too short to reach the ground, swinging back and forth in the air, utterly adorable.","In the small bowl before her was piled a variety of delicious food, all of which Liu Yutong had placed there.","\"Sister, Yaya can't eat this much,\" Yaya said, looking a bit distressed.","\"Take your time, no rush,\" Liu Yutong said.","\"Then Sister should eat too.\" Yaya stretched out her tiny hand, scooped up a piece of chicken with her spoon, and placed it in Liu Yutong's bowl.","Liu Yutong smiled and said, \"Thank you, Yaya.\"","The little girl, encouraged by the praise, grew even more spirited and began eating heartily with her spoon.","Li Xiaohui, meanwhile, was also eating with relish and couldn't help but compliment, \"Grandma, your sweet-and-sour fish is the best in the world—even better than what they make in big restaurants!\"","Grandma chuckled and said, \"If it's good, eat as much as you like, dear.\"","The family chatted and ate together, the atmosphere warm and cozy, so much so that even the chirping of the cicadas outside didn't seem annoying.","Halfway through the meal, Grandpa suddenly put down his chopsticks, as if recalling something important, and said to Liu Yutong, \"Tongtong, Yaya said there's a parent-teacher meeting at kindergarten tomorrow. Are you going?\"","Liu Yutong was taken aback: \"Isn't it already on break? Why a parent-teacher meeting?\"","Yaya explained, \"The teacher said it's a parent meeting on summer safety. Can you come with me, Sister?\"","It then dawned on Liu Yutong that she hadn't really attended many of Yaya's parent-teacher meetings.","The main reason was that she'd been too busy—in fact, as a sophomore in college, she rarely even went to class anymore, almost as if she'd dropped out.","\"Sister will go with you tomorrow.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Really.\"","\"Pinky promise!\"","\"Pinky promise.\"","A large pinky and a small one hooked together.","\"Pinky swear, a hundred years no change, lying makes us puppies!\"","\"Alright, lying makes us puppies.\"","The next morning, Yaya woke up early.","She wore the little dress she had prepared the night before, spinning around in front of the mirror several times, and insisted that Liu Yutong put on nice clothes too.","\"Sister has to wear the prettiest outfit, so the other kids' parents will all envy Yaya.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Alright, Sister will wear the prettiest.\"","In the end, she changed into a white dress and dressed up meticulously, looking full of youthful vitality.","Yaya circled around her twice before nodding with satisfaction: \"Sister is the prettiest sister in the whole world.\"","\"Yaya is very pretty too.\"","After finishing the breakfast Grandma and Grandpa had prepared, Liu Yutong and Yaya took a car straight to the kindergarten in Pearl City.","The kindergarten Yaya attended was considered one of the best in Pearl City. The teaching building was new, the playground spacious, and the play facilities well-equipped.","But when Liu Yutong entered the classroom for the parent-teacher meeting, she saw something that made her feel a bit uneasy.","Looking around the room, she noticed that half of the parents present were middle-aged or elderly.","This kindergarten was already the best in Pearl City, and the families of the children who attended here were generally well-off.","Yet even so, so many children were still left in the care of grandparents.","Their parents either worked in other cities or were busy with business, rarely returning home.","There was no helping it—wages in Pearl City were relatively low. Apart from those in business or with stable jobs in the government system, most people chose to work elsewhere.","Thus, children being left behind was inevitable.","The situation was even more pronounced in rural areas, where the proportion of young parents attending parent-teacher meetings was even lower.","Not long after Liu Yutong sat down, she overheard a few elderly people chatting nearby.","\"Ah, the child's parents work in Shenzhen and only come back once or twice a year. We have to come to these meetings,\" one said.","\"Exactly. My grandson's parents run a business in Shanghai and are very busy. We take care of the child entirely.\"","\"Taking care of the child isn't the issue—it's that education nowadays is so different from when we were young. Things like parent-child reading, handicraft classes, parent interaction—we don't understand any of that.\"","\"And the teacher was just talking about summer vacation trips—how we should take the kids out to see the world and broaden their horizons. At my age, I can hardly take the child on a trip.\"","\"Don't even mention travel. I've barely left Pearl City myself. The farthest I've been is Danan City.\"","\"My old friend asked me to go south for a visit last year. I said I couldn't—I had to take care of the child. She said by the time the child is grown, you'll be too old to travel. Thinking about it... that's just how life goes.\"","They chatted on and on about family matters, their tone carrying a resigned, matter-of-fact weariness.","As Liu Yutong listened, something occurred to her.","A couple of years ago, when she founded Wanlonghui, she had promised the core members that their immediate family members—especially their parents—would be given at least one trip every year.","But now, almost two years had passed, and she hadn't organized a single one.","She truly had been too busy and forgotten, yet no one had reminded her. Could it be that others had also forgotten?","More likely, they had intentionally chosen not to remind her, not wanting to cause the company any trouble.","As the summer safety parent-teacher meeting ended, Liu Yutong led Yaya out and said to Yun Cheng, who had come to greet them,","\"Yun Cheng, arrange for someone to gather statistics. For all Wanlonghui Group's core members—no, for all employees, including those in subsidiaries—if they are regular staff, I need the ages of their parents, their health conditions, whether they've ever traveled far, and if they have any particular places they'd like to visit. Also, gather statistics on the employees' children—their age ranges and interests.\"","Yun Cheng was taken aback: \"The Young Lady, what are you planning?\"","Liu Yutong: \"I forgot—but how could you forget too?\"","\"When Wanlonghui was established, I said we would arrange trips for their families—at least once a year. I forgot, so let's make up for it during this holiday.\"","\"Understood. I'll have it done right away.\"","\"Also, since it's summer break, if the adults go on trips, the kids will need care. Hire more staff with experience in caring for toddlers and children, and arrange separate outings for the kids to some amusement parks for a few days.\"","The adults and children couldn't go on the same trip—the two age groups wanted to do different things, and bringing the kids along would ruin the travel experience for the adults.","It would be better to separate them: the adults enjoy their trips, while the children have their own fun, with plenty of professional caretakers looking after them.","\"Yes!\"","After giving the instructions to Yun Cheng, Liu Yutong's mood lifted considerably.","Some things—either you do them, or you don't.","She wasn't making excuses.","Since she had forgotten, she would make up for it twofold.","Originally, she had promised this benefit only to core members' immediate family, but the regular employees were also contributing to the company. And since she had more than enough money—this would just cost a few tens of millions—she decided to include everyone.","After leaving the kindergarten, Liu Yutong had Yun Cheng drive around Pearl City for a while, taking the chance to check out the newly built sports stadium there."]},{"number":796,"title":"Chapter 796: 797, Try to Build an Airport.","paragraphs":["About twenty minutes later, Liu Yutong arrived at her destination.","This stadium was being built to a standard capacity of sixty thousand people. The main structure was essentially complete, and it would certainly become a landmark building in a small city like Mingzhu City in the future.","Just as she was about to take a quick look around and leave, she suddenly spotted a man wearing a safety helmet, who looked like a secretary, running toward her.","\"Director Liu, I spotted your car from afar. The leader is inside inspecting the work.\"","Liu Yutong then noticed an Audi parked not far away, with the license plate number being 001.","\"Then I'll go see the leader.\"","Soon, Liu Yutong met Uncle Gao, who was chatting with the person in charge at the construction site.","When Uncle Gao saw her approaching, a smile immediately spread across his face.","\"Little girl, what brings you here?\"","\"I had a sudden urge to check on the progress of our stadium. Uncle Gao, this stadium is being built quite well.\"","\"Of course it is. This was built on your recommendation, with a sixty-thousand-person standard. It's more than enough to host a provincial sports meet. Look at the stands, the track, the roof design—all done by people from the provincial design institute, absolutely top-notch.\"","\"As for you, once this stadium is completed, you can't let it sit empty all the time, or that would be a huge waste.\"","\"Don't worry, Uncle Gao, I won't let it sit empty.\"","\"Do you know about the variety show my subsidiary is producing called 'The Voice of Dragon Country'?\"","Uncle Gao nodded: \"Of course I do. I've heard your show cost over a hundred million—a big investment! And I've seen how popular it is online. The blind audition is quite interesting, judging only by voice. That idea is really fresh. Even my daughter talked to me about it.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"Uncle Gao, the finals of 'The Voice of Dragon Country' are set for the National Day holiday in October. Given the influence of the several coaches and the show itself, I believe tickets will sell out quickly. Uncle Gao, you should know what that means, right?\"","Uncle Gao's eyes immediately lit up.","\"You mean you're planning to hold the finals right here in Mingzhu City?\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"But there's a condition. The stadium must be completed before October, and the quality must be guaranteed. I don't want tens of thousands of people sitting in a venue that's still under construction.\"","\"Don't worry about that!\"","Uncle Gao immediately assured her: \"It will be finished before October. I'll have the construction team work overtime to make sure nothing delays your finals.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Then I'll trouble you with that, Uncle Gao.\"","Uncle Gao waved his hand: \"No trouble at all. This is a good thing, a great thing.\"","He looked at Liu Yutong with emotion: \"Little girl, you're giving Mingzhu City a huge gift.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Uncle Gao, you're too kind. I just think holding it in Mingzhu City costs much less than in a big city. I'm trying to save on costs.\"","Uncle Gao laughed and shook his head: \"Oh, you.\"","He knew very well that these were just polite pleasantries.","Given this girl's capabilities, she could hold the event anywhere. Choosing to put the finals in Mingzhu City—wasn't that just to bring vitality to her hometown?","He had some understanding of how popular \"The Voice of Dragon Country\" was online now.","The several coaches were heavyweight figures in the music industry. Any one of them could easily fill a stadium for a concert.","If the finals were really held in Mingzhu City, fans, media, and industry professionals from all over the country would flood in.","Hotels, restaurants, transportation, tourism... the entire city's service industry would be driven.","This was a golden opportunity for Mingzhu City to shine in front of the entire nation.","For a small city to host the finals of a top national variety show—that in itself was the best publicity for the city.","The only drawback was that Mingzhu City didn't have an airport, which would be inconvenient for fans from far away.","Just as Uncle Gao was thinking this, Liu Yutong brought it up first: \"Uncle Gao, have you ever thought about when Mingzhu City might get an airport?\"","Uncle Gao was stunned for a moment, then gave a wry smile.","Was this girl a mind reader?","He had just thought about the lack of an airport, and now she mentioned it.","\"I've thought about building an airport too, but it's not something I can decide. Building an airport requires approval from higher authorities, and it involves so many departments. A small prefecture-level city like ours doesn't have that kind of power to build an airport.\"","\"To be honest with you, given Mingzhu City's current economic scale and population size, even if we applied to build an airport, the application would most likely be rejected.\"","\"What if I could help make the connections?\" Liu Yutong asked.","Gao Zhiyuan froze.","He looked at the young girl who seemed far too young for her power and suddenly realized she was no longer the little girl who used to sell lobsters.","Now, she was the leader of the Wanlonghui Group, the chairman of Longxin.","Her network might even be stronger than his.","\"Little girl, are you serious?\" — should this be considered the form of address \"Mr. Liu\"? The glossary only provides the correct name translations for known glossary terms; translate based on the characters. \"You weren't kidding me, were you?\"","\"I've never joked with you, Uncle Gao?\"","Liu Yutong said seriously: \"You can prepare the materials first, like site selection plans, environmental impact reports... Get everything ready. Once it's done, I'll go find Uncle Li and ask him to submit it to higher authorities.\"","Uncle Gao took a deep breath, suppressing his excitement.","Building an airport.","This was something he had only fantasized about occasionally, something he felt had little chance of being realized during his term of office.","If this girl really could push it forward, then there was a real possibility he might see it happen during his tenure.","Just like the high-speed rail station that was already in the planning and construction phase, an airport would boost the city's development across the board.","Investment attraction, tourism development, logistics and transportation... everything would reach a new level.","\"Alright, since you've said so, let's give it a try. I'll go back and have the materials prepared. Whether it succeeds or not, we'll try!\"","Liu Yutong: \"Then I'll leave it in your hands, Uncle Gao.\"","Uncle Gao was beaming with joy: \"No trouble at all. You're giving Mingzhu City a huge gift. I should be thanking you properly.\"","Liu Yutong exchanged a few more pleasantries with Uncle Gao, discussing details about the project progress, before taking her leave.","Back in the car, she immediately called Su Mansu and asked her to notify all senior executives of the group to return to the Mingzhu City headquarters for a meeting in two days.","The meeting was held in the large conference room of Shunchang Building.","The topic of this meeting was about the restructuring of the group.","Currently, the Wanlonghui Group operated with subsidiaries under a parent company framework. It had been fine in the early stages, but now that the scale was too large, the structure was no longer suitable.","So she planned a major restructuring.","After this restructuring, the next large group meeting would probably involve electing a new group CEO."]},{"number":797,"title":"Chapter 797: 798, Group Restructuring.","paragraphs":["Two days later, at Shunchang Tower.","The entire building had been under strict lockdown since early morning.","From the two-story underground parking garage all the way up to the forty-eighth-floor conference room, security personnel in black suits stood guard at every third step and every fifth post.","The scale of the operation rivaled—even surpassed—the pomp reserved for foreign dignitaries.","The plaza at the building’s entrance was packed with luxury cars.","There were local cars bearing Pearl City license plates, as well as numerous business vehicles arriving from the provincial capital.","In the first-floor lobby, attendees were gradually signing in and entering.","In the front were a group of young men and women in professional attire, carrying briefcases or laptops. They exchanged pleasantries and discussed business matters.","These individuals were professional managers and industry elites recruited by Wanlonghui Group through social hiring.","“General Manager Yao, long time no see! I hear your Wanlong Supermarket’s quarterly revenue hit another record high?”","“Not at all, not at all! General Manager Zhao, your Wanlong Plaza is the real beast. I heard the new city project in BS Province is progressing at lightning speed—almost ready for opening.”","“It’s mainly thanks to the group’s policy support. If the Chairwoman hadn’t poured major resources into BS Province back then, we wouldn’t have such a big operation today.”","“By the way, Manager Liu, that new squirrel-shaped mandarin fish dish from Yuyuefang is selling like crazy. I’ve got to try it sometime.”","“Haha, I’ll arrange it! I’ll save the best private room for you, General Manager Zhao...”","Behind them was a group with a completely different vibe.","These people were all uniformly dressed in black suits, each wearing a dragon-shaped badge on the left chest. Their aura was sharper and more intense than that of the professional managers ahead, and their gazes were keener.","“Old Sun, you came too?”","“No kidding. If The Young Lady summons a meeting, who dares not show up?”","“I heard there’s going to be a big shake-up this time—the group might restructure.”","“Whatever it is, we do whatever The Young Lady says. Even if it means risking my life, I’m in!”","“...”","Some among this group still carried a hint of a gangster atmosphere when they spoke.","These were the core executives of Wanlonghui’s inner circle, many of whom had once been brothers and sisters who helped Liu Yutong hustle lobster and seafood on the streets.","At the registration desk, Su Mansu was rapidly checking the attendance list with her secretarial team.","“Wanlong Supermarket, General Manager Yao, confirmed sign-in.”","“Yuyuefang Catering, Manager Zhou, confirmed sign-in.”","“Huangquan Internet Café, President Zhang, confirmed sign-in.”","“Group HR department...”","Su Mansu scanned the room until she spotted Ma Da waddling through the main door, his belly sticking out.","This head of Wanlong Group’s HR department had actually ditched his usual punk hairstyle today. He had slicked his hair back into a shiny, oiled pompadour, giving him a bit more of an executive look.","“President Ma, your look today is really something! Someone might think you’re going on a blind date.”","Ma Da grinned. “The Young Lady’s holding a big meeting. I had to look decent—can’t embarrass her.”","With that, he picked up the sign-in pen, scrawled his messy name on the list, and then joined the group in black suits, casually handing a cigarette to an old buddy nearby.","The sign-in process lasted a full half-hour.","At 9:50 AM, all attendees were in place.","In the large conference room, nearly a hundred seats were filled to capacity.","In the front row sat the core members of Wanlonghui, most of them founding veterans:","Yu Xin, Yang Xin, Li Xiaohui, Chu Yang, Zhao Tianyi, Zhang Tao, Zhang Dalong... and others.","In the middle row were the professional managers from various subsidiaries, including Wanlong Plaza’s Deputy General Manager Zhao, Wanlong Supermarket chain’s Deputy General Manager Yao Qianshan, Yuyuefang’s Operations Director, and more.","In the back row were department heads and key team members.","“Yu Xin, what do you think The Young Lady wants by gathering us so urgently?”","“I’m guessing she wants to integrate resources. Look at all these divisions now—supermarkets, real estate, catering, internet cafés—most of them are operating independently. There’s a lot of waste.”","“Makes sense. But no matter what changes, us old brothers will still be the core.”","“No doubt about it. When has The Young Lady ever shortchanged us? Back when we were hustling lobster with her, who’d have thought we’d get this big? She’s always had a sharp eye.”","“Sharp, my ass! It’s called ‘insightful’!”","“Right, right, insightful! Insightful! Haha...”","As the crowd chatted, the conference room door was pushed open from the outside.","Su Mansu walked in.","Everyone in the room immediately turned to look at her.","Su Mansu scanned the room, confirming everyone was present, and then said, “The Young Lady has arrived.”","At those words, the murmuring in the room instantly ceased.","In unison, everyone sat up straight, adjusted their clothes, and fixed their gazes on the door, waiting for the queenly figure to appear.","At exactly 10:00 AM—not a second more or less—the conference room door opened again.","First, two core members in black suits stepped in. After opening the door, they stood at attention on either side.","Then, a young woman everyone recognized walked in, flanked by a man and a woman.","It was Liu Yutong, with Yun Cheng and Lan Die.","Today, Liu Yutong was also dressed in a black suit, with a special crystal dragon-shaped badge pinned to her chest.","Her long hair was tied back, revealing a face so delicate it was nearly flawless.","The moment she stepped into the room, everyone shot to their feet.","“Greetings, The Young Lady!” dozens of voices rang out.","“Greetings, Chairwoman!” dozens more echoed.","Liu Yutong gave a slight nod to the crowd and walked straight to the front of the long conference table, stopping at the seat of honor.","“Sit.”","Everyone immediately sat down in unison.","Su Mansu took her seat beside her, opening her laptop to take meeting minutes.","Without any preamble, Liu Yutong addressed the room directly.","“Today, I’ve called you all back to make an announcement.”","“Wanlonghui Group will be restructured.”","At these words, the room began to buzz with whispers. Many had already guessed it—given the group’s size, change was inevitable. Still, some felt a pang of nostalgia. It had only been about a year since the last restructuring, hadn’t it? And now another one. The pace of growth was like a rocket.","“Our Wanlonghui Group is getting bigger and bigger. Similarly, our subsidiaries are multiplying—from the original Yuyuefang, to Wanlong Supermarket, Wanlong Plaza, Huangquan Internet Café... and the mobile phone division we’re currently setting up. Our business lines are incredibly fragmented, and most divisions are operating in silos.","If this continues, it will only waste enormous resources. Each subsidiary’s efficiency will keep dropping, and internal friction will only accelerate.","For example, the delivery services of Wanhui Select urgently need logistics support. However, even though the logistics company has idle vehicles, the cumbersome approval process prevents timely allocation, resulting in a rising order delay rate.","\"Furthermore, subsidiaries that have introduced external funding, such as Huangquan Internet Cafe, Wanhui Select, and Yuyue Fang, are essentially managing their own affairs. They lack a highly unified development direction and planning, which even impacts the Group's future growth strategy.\"","\"Based on the above circumstances, restructuring the Group is imperative!\""]},{"number":798,"title":"Chapter 798: 799, Ascended to Another Level.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong raised her hand to gesture.","Su Mansu immediately stood up, turned on the projector, and displayed the prepared PowerPoint on the large screen.","In the center of the screen, a line of large characters appeared—[Wanlong Group—Business Division Restructuring Plan]","Liu Yutong walked to the front of the projection screen, picked up a laser pointer, and used the red dot to indicate the structure chart on the screen.","\"The core of this restructuring is to break the existing independent subsidiary structure, resolve the situation of feudal lords ruling their own territories, and also to eliminate resource waste, enabling centralized resource allocation for better results. We will reorganize and integrate into six major business divisions based on business attributes.\"","\"First, the Commercial Consumer Retail Business Division.\"","\"Integrate Wanlong Plaza, Wanlong Commercial Street, Wanlong Supermarket Chain, Wanlong Convenience Store Chain, Yuyuefang Restaurant Chain, Huangquan Internet Cafe Chain, and the recently spun-off Qingyin Tea Beverage Chain, among others, into one business division.\"","This Qingyin milk tea brand name was changed later; it was originally spun off from the internet cafe business and then renamed, focusing on new-style Chinese fresh milk tea, with the signature product still being Bo Ya Jue Xian.","\"The Commercial Consumer Retail Business Division will be led by Yang Xin as President, with Zhang Tao and Yao Qianshan as Vice Presidents.\"","Yang Xin, Zhang Tao, and Yao Qianshan immediately stood up.","\"Thank you, The Young Lady!\"","\"Thank you, Chairwoman!\"","\"...\"","\"Let me briefly mention: for commercial real estate projects, we need unified planning, unified leasing, and unified operations. Over the next three years, we aim to open twenty more Wanlong Plazas in regions such as East China and South China, covering all second- and third-tier cities...\"","\"Also, Qingyin Tea Beverage must expand by at least three hundred stores, aiming to rank among the top three nationwide.\"","The three nodded again: \"Yes!\"","\"Second, the Technology Business Division.\"","\"This is the group's future, mainly including the mobile phone project team, hardware design center, chip design center, operating system R&D department, and related supply chains, working in vertical integration with Longxin Semiconductor.\"","\"This division will be led by Yu Xin as President, with XXX as Vice President.\"","Yu Xin and a professional manager stood up, expressed their gratitude, and sat down.","\"Over at Longxin, the 90-nanometer production line has achieved stable mass production. Next, they will continue to tackle the 65-nanometer and even 45-nanometer processes. The Wanlong mobile phone project is officially launched, with the brand name set as Longyao.\"","\"The first product of Longyao phones will target the mid-to-high-end market. For now, we won't produce low-end devices, directly competing with Fruit phones. The system will be deeply developed based on Android, named Long OS. For hardware, Longxin will collaborate with the team we just assembled to provide chip solutions. For appearance design, we'll first use our patented designs that were registered long ago.\"","\"I want to see samples by the end of this year, and a product launch by May next year.\"","\"Yu Xin, making phones will definitely be challenging. Are you sure you have no issues?\"","Yu Xin nodded: \"No problem! I will deliver a satisfactory result for you.\"","\"Good!\"","\"Third, the Digital Business Division.\"","\"Integrate Weibo, Longkan Vision, Wanhui Premium, and the under-development WeChat and Longpay projects to form a traffic-centric Digital Business Division.\"","\"The Digital Business Division will be led by Zhang Dalong as President, responsible for technical architecture, big data, software development, etc. Lin Muyang will serve as Vice President concurrently, and Xiao Bin as Vice President, responsible for daily operations and commercial monetization.\"","The three named also immediately stood up and made their declarations.","\"Fourth, the Entertainment and Media Business Division.\"","\"Integrate Longyu Media, Zilong E-sports, the Longguo Good Voice project team, artist management operations, etc. This division will be led by Lin Muyang as President, with Xue Qian and Li Xiaohui as Vice Presidents.\"","\"Huh? I'm also Vice President?\" Li Xiaohui pointed at her own nose, somewhat surprised.","She clearly had no interest in this Vice President title and even found it a burden, as it would interfere with her gaming and e-sports activities.","Liu Yutong was speechless: \"You'll just have a nominal role. You still do what you do.\"","Only then did Li Xiaohui breathe a sigh of relief: \"Don't worry, Yutong Jie. As long as I don't have to sit in the office every day writing reports, I'll work hard. I want to make Zilong E-sports the number one in the world!\"","Liu Yutong shook her head. Uncle Li probably never imagined back then that his daughter's ambition would be to take gaming to new heights.","\"Fifth, the Supply Chain and Logistics Business Division.\"","\"Integrate Wanlong Logistics, Wanlong Express, Wanhui Premium delivery network, group supply chain management center, warehousing center...\"","\"Temporarily, Xu Shishi will serve as President concurrently.\"","Xu Shishi was the only non-core member female president of a business division who rose quickly, a top-tier professional manager recruited by Liu Yutong with a high salary, possessing very strong capabilities.","\"Regarding logistics, Xu Shishi, I have set a goal for you: Within five years, build an intelligent logistics network covering core economic zones like East China, South China, and North China. Achieve same-day delivery within cities, next-day delivery between cities, and even day-after-next delivery for major cities.\"","Set in 2009, this goal was almost a fantasy, truly crazy.","But Liu Yutong was well aware that this kind of extreme logistics experience would, in about ten years, become the core competitiveness of e-commerce and even the industry norm.","Wasn't the Dongdong she invested in in the capital already doing this?","She also needed to lay the groundwork early.","Xu Shishi immediately stood up: \"I will not fail to live up to the Chairwoman's trust!\"","\"Mm!\"","\"Sixth, the Finance and Investment Business Division.\"","\"Integrate Wanlong Capital, the group's finance center, and strategic investment department.\"","\"This business division will only serve the group's internal fund management, financing, and strategic investments.\"","\"I will serve as President concurrently, with Su Mansu as Vice President.\"","\"Su Mansu will also hold the position of Chairwoman's Office Director, relieved of the special assistant position, which will be taken over jointly by Lan Die and Yun Cheng.\"","This appointment was indeed quite surprising.","Of course, they weren't surprised that Su Mansu was promoted to Vice President.","As Liu Yutong's special assistant, she had naturally been involved in the most core matters, and with her impressive resume, the promotion to Vice President was reasonable.","What truly surprised them was Yun Cheng.","This de facto number two figure of the group was actually going to become a special assistant. Clearly, The Young Lady had given him opportunities for experience.","In fact, this was Yun Cheng's own choice.","He could have easily become a business division president, but he ultimately decided to stay by Liu Yutong's side.","Lan Die was the same.","She had no interest in those empty titles.","Following that, Liu Yutong announced independent appointments for some special positions.","\"Head of the Wanlong Group Security Department: Yun Cheng and Chu Yang, dual-head system.\"","\"Personnel President of Wanlong Group: Ma Da.\"","\"COO (Chief Operating Officer) of Wanlong Group will be concurrently held by Yu Xin.\"","\"Chairwoman, CEO, and CFO (Chief Financial Officer) will still be held by me concurrently.\"","\"Longxin Semiconductor stands independently outside the group structure. The newly established Wanlong Aerospace Technology stands independently outside the group. Tianyi Law Firm stands independently outside the group, with Zhao Tianyi remaining as its head.\"","\"...........\"","Liu Yutong finished announcing everyone's appointments in one breath.","Finally, she dropped the laser pointer and swept her gaze across the room.","\"All of the above appointments take effect immediately.\"","After a few seconds of silence in the meeting room, Yun Cheng was the first to stand up.","He did not say a single word. He simply raised his right hand and clenched his fist high above his head.","But everyone understood the meaning of this gesture.","Chu Yang stood up, raising his fist.","Yu Xin stood up, raising her fist.","Ma Da stood up, raising his fist.","......","One after another.","All the founding members who had been with Liu Yutong from the start stood up, fists raised.","Then the professional managers, infected by the atmosphere, rose to their feet one by one, fists raised above their heads.","In the meeting room, nearly a hundred hands were raised, looking like a dark forest.","Then Yun Cheng led the chant, shouting three words.","\"Wanlong Society!\"","Everyone immediately echoed.","\"Invincible in battle!\"","\"Invincible in battle!\"","\"Invincible in battle!\"","Three shouts in succession, each louder than the last.","In this way, they declared that a future super business empire had stepped into a new level."]},{"number":799,"title":"Chapter 799: 800, Must Be Redeemed.","paragraphs":["The meeting started promptly at ten in the morning and didn’t end until two in the afternoon.","For four full hours, Liu Yutong laid out detailed plans for the six major business groups, covering specific strategies, annual targets, evaluation mechanisms, and resource allocation.","For example, the Commercial Consumer Retail Group was tasked with establishing twenty Wanlong Plazas nationwide within three years, covering all second- and third-tier cities in East and South China to build a scale advantage.","Qingyin Tea Drinks needed to expand to over 300 stores by the end of next year, aiming for the top three in the country.","Supermarkets were to proceed steadily while maintaining their reputation.","The Technology Group was under heavy pressure: they had to produce an engineering prototype of the Longyao phone by the end of the year, secure contracts with all core supply chain partners, and ensure the overseas launch of the first-generation Longyao phone took place before next May—no delays allowed, only earlier.","The Digital Group faced similar challenges.","Projects like WeChat and LongPay had only just launched, yet Liu Yutong demanded that the first version of these products be completed by the end of the year, with the ability to integrate with Wanhui Preferred’s offline scenarios for initial traffic sharing.","The Entertainment and Media Group had a relatively lighter load, basically focusing on the show \"The Voice of the Dragon Kingdom\" while coordinating with the stadium under construction to set up the stage early, ensuring the finals in October could be held smoothly in Pearl City.","Xu Shishi of the Supply Chain and Logistics Group received an incredibly challenging task: within five years, build a smart logistics network covering East, South, and North China, achieving same-day delivery within cities and next-day delivery between cities.","Logistics wasn’t just about efficiency—it was also the most cash-burning division in the group.","Liu Yutong personally took charge of the Finance and Investment Group, handling strategic direction herself while delegating execution to Su Mansu.","Although the targets set for everyone were incredibly high, no one complained or moaned about the hardship.","From this decisive series of reforms, everyone caught the same scent:","The Young Lady meant business. She wanted to push the Wanlong Group into the Fortune Global 500 in the shortest possible time.","Because this new organizational structure was built entirely to the standard of Fortune Global 500 companies.","As the meeting neared its end, Liu Yutong suddenly changed the subject, bringing up a topic that caught most people off guard.","“Everyone, before we close this meeting, I want to talk about something off-topic first.”","“A few days ago, I attended Yaya’s parent-teacher meeting. In the classroom, I noticed a detail—most of the people there for the kids were grandparents.”","“Where are the parents? Either working in other cities or running businesses in big cities, barely making it home a few times a year. The kids are basically being raised by these elderly folks.”","“Those grandparents—when they were young, they raised their own children. Now, in their middle and old age, they’re still helping out by raising their grandkids. Many of them have been trapped in their hometowns their whole lives, especially in small rural places. They might never have had the chance to see the outside world.”","“I thought to myself: How many of our 1,200-plus employees at Wanlong Group are in the same situation? Parents back home, kids back home, while they work their tails off here. Because work is busy, because they’re reluctant to spend money, because of all sorts of real-world reasons, their parents have hardly ever traveled far.”","“That parent-teacher meeting reminded me—when I first founded Wanlong Group, I promised some of you here that direct family members, especially parents, would get at least one trip arranged every year.”","“But over the past two years, I’ve been so busy that I completely forgot about it. If not for that parent-teacher meeting, I might have kept breaking that promise.”","As she said this, Liu Yutong’s gaze slowly swept over Yun Cheng, Yu Xin, and Ma Da—the veterans who had been with her since the beginning.","A few of them sheepishly lowered their heads.","They hadn’t forgotten—they just didn’t think it was necessary to trouble the company.","After all, core members already had high annual salaries and good benefits; they could easily pay for their parents to travel on their own. Why should the company foot the bill?","But Liu Yutong clearly saw it differently.","“Let me make this clear: if I, Liu Yutong, say something, I mean to keep my word!”","“I’ve decided: starting this year, Wanlong Group will hold its first-ever direct-family employee trip. Whether you’re a core member or a regular employee, whether you’re a president or a delivery driver or a service worker—if you have a formal contract, your direct family members will all be sent on a trip by the company!”","“All expenses will be covered by the company!”","“Five-star hotel accommodations, professional tour guides, and full medical support on site—everything will be in place!”","“What’s more, we’ll go into detail: based on the health and preferences of each employee’s direct family members, we’ll tailor different travel routes. Want to go to the capital to see the flag-raising at Tiananmen or the Great Wall? Want to head south or north for a seaside vacation? Want to visit the southwestern provinces to experience the unique ethnic customs and see the magnificent scenery? All options are available.”","“If they don’t want to travel far, they can choose nearby resorts—the company will arrange that too!”","As soon as she said this, the meeting room erupted with whispers.","“Chairman, this... this would cost an absolute fortune!” one professional manager couldn’t help but blurt out.","He knew that the group’s formal employees included full-time riders and delivery drivers, making the number immense.","Su Mansu had been prepared for this and immediately responded: “I’ve already calculated. The group currently has about 12,000 formal employees, including full-time riders and full-time delivery drivers and other blue-collar positions.”","“Even if we count only unmarried employees with just their parents—that’s between 200,000 and 300,000 people. Removing those unable to travel due to health or scheduling issues, the final number of participants is estimated at around 200,000. Factoring in five-star hotel accommodations, bus rentals, ticket costs, and discounts, the per-person budget is expected to be around 3,000 to 4,000 yuan, with a total budget no less than 600 million yuan. The final cost should fall between 600 and 800 million yuan.”","Hearing that number, many in the room felt their hearts skip a beat.","Six to eight hundred million!","That wasn’t a small sum—how many listed companies made that much profit in a year?","Some instinctively thought this was a wasteful expense; it would be better to just hand out cash.","Liu Yutong, guessing that some might think that way, continued:","“I know some of you think giving cash would be more practical. But have you considered this: if we give cash, would the parents of those ordinary employees actually spend it? Most likely, they’d save it—to buy their kids an apartment, to fund a wedding, for retirement nest eggs. So I won’t hand out cash. I’ll tell them: if you don’t go, you’ll be wasting this chance, and it expires! Only then will they truly step out and see the world.”","\"These employees' parents have worked hard their whole lives, giving their best years to their families and their children. They have poured themselves out, and they deserve to be treated with kindness.\"","\"Additionally, to prevent any situation where employees' parents go on vacation and leave their children unattended, arrangements will also be made for the employees' children. During the summer break, the company will hire professional childcare teams and instructors to take the kids to amusement parks, zoos, and science museums for educational trips. The adults will enjoy their time, and the children will enjoy theirs, each without interfering with the other—so employees have no worries.\"","\"Ma Da, your HR department will take the lead on this. Finance will coordinate, and each business unit will implement it. By July, we need to have collected all information on employees' parents—such as their details, health conditions, and travel preferences—so that the first tour groups can depart in July!\"","Ma Da immediately stood up. \"Yes, The Young Lady! I'll arrange for it right away!\"","Liu Yutong nodded, then swept her gaze across everyone in the room.","\"I know some of you might have doubts, but please remember this: Wanlong Corporation is not a company that only cares about profits. I want every person working with me to stand tall with pride! I want their parents to be looked up to—even proud—because their children work at Wanlong Corporation!\"","\"This is the corporate culture I want to build!\"","As her voice faded, thunderous applause erupted.","Those professional managers who had worked at big corporations now looked at Liu Yutong with more than just awe and respect.","There was also a genuine sense of emotion and belonging.","A boss who treated her employees' parents like her own—they had truly never seen such a thing before.","Some of the brothers and sisters who had been with Liu Yutong since the very beginning had tears welling up in their eyes.","They had followed The Young Lady for two years, from selling lobsters to building this business empire. No matter how big it grew, The Young Lady never forgot them.","The Young Lady—through fire and flood!","Yun Cheng watched the radiant girl on the stage, his eyes filled with pride.","This was the person he would devote his life to following."]},{"number":800,"title":"Chapter 800: 801, Zhang Erniu.","paragraphs":["After the meeting ended, Su Mansu returned to her office, and the first thing she did was draft an internal letter.","This letter was to be sent in Liu Yutong's name to all employees of Wanlonghui Group.","\"To All Wanlonghui Employees: United in Heart, United in Action, Toward the Future, Never Letting Any Effort Down!\"","The opening of the letter elaborated in detail on the upcoming restructuring of the Group into six major business divisions, along with Chairman Liu Yutong's gratitude and expectations for all employees.","It also included the announcement of the \"Wanlonghui Group Employee Parents' Annual Travel Plan\" and the \"Employee Children's Summer Camp Activity.\"","The details were thorough.","Starting this summer, all full-time employees of Wanlonghui Group — including grassroots positions such as full-time riders, couriers, and frontline service staff — could have their direct relatives (parents, children) enjoy one fully company-funded domestic trip.","Routes were optional, timing adjustable, and everything would be tailored to the needs of the employees' parents.","Travel standards: five-star hotel accommodation and meals throughout the trip, professional tour guides, and a dedicated medical support team accompanying the group, with round-trip transportation arranged uniformly by the company.","As for employees' children, the company would organize free summer camps during the summer break, covering outdoor team-building, science museum visits, interest development, and other programs — including marine parks, zoos, science and technology museums, and more.","Special note: All expenses would be covered by a special fund allocated by the Group, and would not deduct from employees' individual benefits.","The moment the email went out, the entire Group erupted.","\"Holy crap! For real? The company is paying for my parents to travel? Am I reading this right?\"","\"My parents have never left home their whole lives — never even been to the provincial capital. Now they can finally go see the capital city!\"","\"My daughter has always wanted to go to the marine park, but I never wanted to spend the ticket money. Now it's actually happening — and the company is renting the whole place!\"","\"Long live the Chairman! Long live The Young Lady! Long live Wanlonghui!\"","\"...\"","The comment section of the Group's internal forum was flooded with grateful messages.","...","Zhang Erniu had just turned thirty this year, and true to his name, he was built like an ox — sturdy and strong.","He didn't have much education; he'd dropped out in the fifth grade of elementary school. Now he'd been working at the Wanlong Logistics Center for almost a year.","His job was a simple package sorter: his work was straightforward but monotonous — taking parcels off the conveyor belt and sorting them into different zones based on their destination.","This kind of mechanical, repetitive work, in any other place, would drive a person insane.","But at Wanlong Logistics Center, Zhang Erniu worked with great enthusiasm.","Why?","Because the pay and treatment were so good, it felt like a dream.","His base salary plus monthly performance bonuses came to about four thousand yuan in hand — something he'd never even dared to imagine before.","Even more unbelievable, they actually had two days off every week.","He remembered that at other places, it was basically twelve-hour shifts with a two-shift rotation, and if you got one day off a month, you were lucky. The pay was only around two thousand, and they'd squeeze every drop of marrow out of you.","Zhang Erniu used to work at an electronics factory out of town — like that. Every day, he did nothing but work and sleep, with zero personal life — a pure human draft animal.","Then his wife called him, saying she'd seen the recruitment ad for Wanlong Logistics Center and insisted he come back and give it a try. Otherwise, he'd probably still be grinding away at some factory far from home, and he'd never have gotten a job this comfortable.","Three shifts, eight hours each, the legendary \"five insurances and one housing fund,\" rotating shifts weekly, with two days off each rotation. He took home around four thousand a month, plus a year-end bonus that existed only in legends.","Last year, even though he'd worked less than a full year, his year-end bonus alone was over ten thousand yuan.","His wife hadn't been hired, though — she worked as a cashier at a convenience store. Together, the two of them brought in about five thousand-plus a month.","In terms of total income, for ordinary people nowadays — especially in a small, low-cost city like this — that was absolutely considered a high salary.","Buying a house with just their wages wasn't even out of the question.","To put it in perspective, the average housing price in Mingzhu City — not in the prime downtown areas — was roughly around two thousand yuan per square meter. After covering their daily expenses for food, utilities, and the like, they could easily save enough for one square meter of house a month. Add Zhang Erniu's housing fund on top, and after a few years, they could buy a big house outright.","Sometimes, Zhang Erniu felt like all of this was a dream.","He was the only son in his family. His parents still farmed in the countryside. His wife worked at the convenience store. His six-year-old son lived with his grandparents back in the village. His biggest wish was to buy a big house in the city, bring his parents and child over, and have the whole family reunited under one roof.","At the rate he was saving now, that wish seemed like it could come true within the next few years.","The future looked nothing short of bright!","Today, Zhang Erniu was on the morning shift — starting at six in the morning and ending at two in the afternoon. And as luck would have it, his rotation gave him two consecutive days off. The moment he got off work, he hopped on the motorcycle he'd recently bought and rode, puttering puttering, all the way back to his hometown in the countryside.","As soon as he reached the front gate, he heard laughter coming from inside.","The family had guests.","\"Erniu's home!\"","Mom heard the sound of the motorcycle and called out toward the yard: \"Your Third Aunt is here, come in and say hello.\"","Third Aunt was the wife of a distant third uncle from the same village.","They usually had fairly frequent contact, since they lived close by after all.","But Zhang Erniu really didn't want to see this woman, because the moment she laid eyes on him, she would inevitably start comparing him with her own son—basically, she just wanted to show off on purpose.","Because her son was a college graduate, even if it was just a vocational college, that still counted as a college student. Compared to Erniu's elementary school education, her son was clearly the more accomplished one.","\"Third Aunt.\" Erniu greeted her politely when he saw her.","\"Oh, Erniu's back.\"","Third Aunt sat on a small stool, cracking sunflower seeds while sizing him up: \"I heard you're not working at the electronics factory in W City anymore. Did you go back to that logistics company in Pearl City?\"","\"So how much do you make in a month now? Is it enough to get by?\"","Erniu's head throbbed the moment she asked that question.","This old biddy was at it again, sure enough."]}]);
